Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:8;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:4:"Type";s:8:"longtext";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:9;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:4:"Type";s:8:"longtext";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:10;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:13:"prevention_en";s:4:"Type";s:8:"longtext";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:11;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:4:"Type";s:8:"longtext";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:12;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:4:"Type";s:4:"text";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:13;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:4:"Type";s:4:"text";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:14;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:10:"updated_at";s:4:"Type";s:8:"datetime";s:9:"Collation";N;s:4:"Null";s:2:"NO";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";s:19:"current_timestamp()";s:5:"Extra";s:29:"on update current_timestamp()";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}}s:4:"rows";a:400:{i:0;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:1;s:10:"disease_id";i:362;s:11:"overview_en";s:384:"Type 2 diabetes mellitus is a chronic metabolic disorder in which the body becomes resistant to insulin and, over time, may not produce enough insulin to maintain normal blood glucose levels. Persistent high blood sugar can damage blood vessels, nerves, kidneys, eyes, and other organs. The condition can often be managed through lifestyle measures, medicines, and regular monitoring.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:755:"टाइप 2 मधुमेह एक दीर्घकालिक चयापचय विकार है जिसमें शरीर इंसुलिन का सही उपयोग नहीं कर पाता या पर्याप्त इंसुलिन नहीं बना पाता। यह मधुमेह का सबसे सामान्य प्रकार है और धीरे-धीरे विकसित होता है। यदि इसे नियंत्रित न किया जाए तो यह हृदय, गुर्दे, आंखों, नसों और रक्त वाहिकाओं को प्रभावित कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:417:"Type 2 diabetes develops when cells become less responsive to insulin and the pancreas cannot produce enough insulin to compensate for this resistance. Excess body fat, particularly abdominal fat, physical inactivity, genetic susceptibility, aging, and certain metabolic conditions can contribute. The disease develops through interacting genetic, environmental, and metabolic factors rather than from a single cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:397:"इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध, मोटापा, शारीरिक निष्क्रियता, आनुवंशिक प्रवृत्ति, अस्वस्थ भोजन, तनाव, बढ़ती उम्र और हार्मोनल असंतुलन टाइप 2 मधुमेह के प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:408:"Risk factors for type 2 diabetes include overweight or obesity, physical inactivity, increasing age, family history, previous gestational diabetes, high blood pressure, abnormal cholesterol levels, and certain patterns of abdominal fat distribution. Risk also varies among populations because of genetic, social, and environmental factors. Having a risk factor does not mean diabetes will definitely develop.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:444:"मोटापा, परिवार में मधुमेह का इतिहास, 45 वर्ष से अधिक आयु, उच्च रक्तचाप, पीसीओएस, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल, धूम्रपान, व्यायाम की कमी और अस्वस्थ भोजन टाइप 2 मधुमेह का जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:445:"Type 2 diabetes is diagnosed using blood glucose testing. Common diagnostic methods include fasting plasma glucose, glycated hemoglobin, or an oral glucose tolerance test, with confirmation generally required when appropriate. A random glucose measurement may establish the diagnosis in a person with characteristic symptoms and markedly elevated glucose. Additional tests may be used to evaluate complications and cardiovascular or kidney risk.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:386:"निदान के लिए उपवास रक्त शर्करा जांच, HbA1c परीक्षण, ओरल ग्लूकोज टॉलरेंस टेस्ट, रैंडम ब्लड शुगर, किडनी फंक्शन टेस्ट और लिपिड प्रोफाइल की जांच की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:442:"The risk of type 2 diabetes can often be reduced through regular physical activity, maintaining a healthy body weight, eating a balanced diet rich in minimally processed foods, avoiding tobacco, and limiting excessive alcohol intake. People at increased risk may benefit from regular screening and structured lifestyle programs. Early identification of abnormal blood glucose can allow preventive measures before diabetes becomes established.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:388:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, नियमित व्यायाम करें, संतुलित आहार लें, धूम्रपान से बचें, शराब सीमित करें, तनाव नियंत्रित करें और नियमित स्वास्थ्य जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:459:"Type 2 diabetes mellitus requires ongoing medical management because prolonged high blood glucose can cause serious complications. Seek prompt care for persistent uncontrolled glucose, dehydration, recurrent infections, or worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for severe weakness, confusion, loss of consciousness, severe dehydration, chest pain, stroke symptoms, or symptoms suggesting diabetic ketoacidosis or hyperosmolar hyperglycemic state.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1397:"टाइप 2 डायबिटीज़ मेलिटस के लिए लगातार मेडिकल देखभाल की ज़रूरत होती है क्योंकि लंबे समय तक ब्लड ग्लूकोज़ का लेवल ज़्यादा रहने से गंभीर परेशानियाँ हो सकती हैं। अगर ग्लूकोज़ का लेवल लगातार कंट्रोल से बाहर रहता है, डिहाइड्रेशन होता है, बार-बार इन्फेक्शन होता है या लक्षण बिगड़ते हैं, तो तुरंत इलाज करवाएँ। बहुत ज़्यादा कमज़ोरी, कन्फ्यूज़न, बेहोशी, गंभीर डिहाइड्रेशन, सीने में दर्द, स्ट्रोक के लक्षण, या डायबिटिक कीटोएसिडोसिस या हाइपरऑस्मोलर हाइपरग्लाइसेमिक स्टेट का संकेत देने वाले लक्षणों के मामले में इमरजेंसी जाँच की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:02:46";}i:1;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:2;s:10:"disease_id";i:81;s:11:"overview_en";s:585:"Hypertension is a condition in which blood pressure remains higher than the recommended range over time. Because it often causes no noticeable symptoms, it may remain undetected for years. Persistent high blood pressure places increased strain on the heart and blood vessels and can contribute to complications involving the heart, brain, kidneys, and eyes. Blood pressure can vary between measurements, so diagnosis generally requires repeated or appropriately monitored readings. Early detection and long-term management can reduce the risk of cardiovascular and other complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:765:"उच्च रक्तचाप (हाइपरटेंशन) एक दीर्घकालिक स्थिति है जिसमें धमनियों की दीवारों पर रक्त का दबाव लगातार अधिक रहता है। लंबे समय तक अनियंत्रित रहने पर यह हृदय, मस्तिष्क, गुर्दे, आंखों और रक्त वाहिकाओं को नुकसान पहुंचा सकता है। इसके लक्षण अक्सर स्पष्ट नहीं होते, इसलिए इसे साइलेंट किलर भी कहा जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:582:"The causes of hypertension vary. Some people develop primary hypertension through a combination of genetic, environmental, and lifestyle factors without one identifiable underlying disease. Other cases are secondary hypertension caused or influenced by conditions such as kidney disease, hormonal disorders, sleep apnea, or certain medicines. High sodium intake, excess body weight, physical inactivity, alcohol use, and tobacco exposure can contribute to elevated blood pressure. Blood pressure also naturally changes with age and can be influenced by multiple interacting factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:474:"अक्सर इसका सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं होता। अधिक नमक का सेवन, मोटापा, शारीरिक निष्क्रियता, तनाव, धूम्रपान, शराब, हार्मोनल विकार, गुर्दे की बीमारी और आनुवंशिक कारण इसमें योगदान दे सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:526:"Risk factors for hypertension include increasing age, family history, excess body weight, high dietary sodium intake, low physical activity, tobacco exposure, excessive alcohol use, chronic stress, and certain sleep disorders. Kidney disease, diabetes, and some hormonal conditions can also increase risk. Certain medicines and substances may raise blood pressure. Risk generally reflects a combination of inherited susceptibility, health conditions, lifestyle factors, and environmental influences rather than a single cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:432:"40 वर्ष से अधिक आयु, मोटापा, मधुमेह, परिवार में उच्च रक्तचाप का इतिहास, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल, धूम्रपान, शराब का सेवन, खराब आहार और निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:583:"Hypertension is diagnosed by measuring blood pressure accurately and confirming that readings remain elevated over time. Measurements may be repeated during separate visits or obtained through home or ambulatory blood pressure monitoring. The clinician may review medical history, medicines, lifestyle factors, and family history and perform a physical examination. Blood and urine tests can help evaluate kidney function, cardiovascular risk, or possible secondary causes. Additional investigations may be required when the clinical history suggests an underlying medical condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:433:"निदान बार-बार रक्तचाप मापकर किया जाता है। साथ ही ईसीजी, इकोकार्डियोग्राफी, किडनी फंक्शन टेस्ट, मूत्र जांच, लिपिड प्रोफाइल, ब्लड शुगर और आंखों की जांच भी की जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:551:"Hypertension risk can be reduced by maintaining a healthy body weight, engaging in regular physical activity, limiting dietary sodium, eating a balanced diet, avoiding tobacco, and limiting excessive alcohol intake. Managing diabetes, kidney disease, sleep disorders, and other contributing conditions is also important. Regular blood pressure checks help identify elevated readings before complications develop. People already diagnosed with hypertension should follow their treatment plan and continue monitoring even when they do not have symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:379:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, नियमित व्यायाम करें, धूम्रपान से बचें, नमक कम करें, तनाव नियंत्रित करें, पर्याप्त नींद लें और नियमित स्वास्थ्य जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:353:"Hypertension often causes no symptoms and usually does not require emergency care solely because a blood pressure reading is elevated. Seek urgent medical attention for very high blood pressure accompanied by severe headache, chest pain, severe shortness of breath, confusion, weakness or numbness, vision changes, or other sudden neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:916:"हाई ब्लड प्रेशर (हाइपरटेंशन) के अक्सर कोई लक्षण नहीं दिखते और सिर्फ़ ब्लड प्रेशर बढ़ा हुआ होने पर आमतौर पर इमरजेंसी इलाज की ज़रूरत नहीं पड़ती। अगर बहुत ज़्यादा ब्लड प्रेशर के साथ तेज़ सिरदर्द, सीने में दर्द, सांस लेने में बहुत ज़्यादा तकलीफ़, उलझन, कमज़ोरी या सुन्नपन, देखने में बदलाव या अचानक कोई और न्यूरोलॉजिकल लक्षण दिखें, तो तुरंत डॉक्टर से मिलें।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:03:12";}i:2;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:3;s:10:"disease_id";i:181;s:11:"overview_en";s:581:"Polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS) is a common hormonal and metabolic disorder that can affect ovulation, menstrual cycles, androgen levels, and metabolism. People with PCOS may have irregular or absent periods, difficulty becoming pregnant, increased facial or body hair, acne, or thinning scalp hair. Some also have insulin resistance or increased risk of metabolic problems. The exact cause is not fully understood, but genetic and hormonal factors appear to contribute. Symptoms vary considerably, and diagnosis is based on the overall clinical picture rather than a single test.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:700:"पॉलीसिस्टिक ओवरी सिंड्रोम (PCOS) महिलाओं में पाया जाने वाला एक सामान्य हार्मोनल विकार है। इसमें अनियमित माहवारी, एंड्रोजन हार्मोन का बढ़ना और अंडाशय में कई छोटे सिस्ट बनना शामिल हो सकता है। यह प्रजनन क्षमता, वजन, त्वचा, चयापचय और मानसिक स्वास्थ्य को प्रभावित कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:523:"The exact cause of PCOS is not known. The condition appears to involve a combination of genetic, hormonal, and metabolic factors. Many people with PCOS have increased androgen activity or insulin resistance, which can interfere with normal ovarian function and ovulation. Family history may contribute to susceptibility. Hormonal signaling between the brain, ovaries, and adrenal glands can also be altered. PCOS is a complex condition, and the combination and severity of features differ substantially between individuals.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:447:"पीसीओएस का सटीक कारण पूरी तरह ज्ञात नहीं है। इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध, हार्मोनल असंतुलन, आनुवंशिक प्रवृत्ति, मोटापा, सूजन और एंड्रोजन हार्मोन की अधिकता इसमें योगदान दे सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:532:"Factors associated with PCOS include a family history of the condition, insulin resistance, excess body weight, and metabolic abnormalities, although PCOS can occur in people of different body sizes. The condition commonly becomes apparent around puberty or during the reproductive years. Some individuals have a higher risk of related metabolic problems, including impaired glucose regulation and abnormal cholesterol levels. Symptoms and risk factors vary, and the presence of one feature does not by itself establish a diagnosis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:390:"परिवार में पीसीओएस का इतिहास, मोटापा, इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध, टाइप 2 मधुमेह, निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली, अस्वस्थ आहार और मेटाबोलिक सिंड्रोम प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:570:"PCOS is diagnosed from the overall clinical picture because there is no single definitive test. Evaluation commonly includes a history of menstrual patterns, symptoms of androgen excess, physical examination, and selected blood tests. Pregnancy and other conditions that can cause irregular periods or androgen-related symptoms may need to be excluded. Pelvic ultrasound may be used to assess ovarian morphology when appropriate, but polycystic-appearing ovaries are not required for diagnosis in every diagnostic framework. Metabolic assessment may also be recommended.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:476:"निदान के लिए चिकित्सकीय इतिहास, शारीरिक परीक्षण, मासिक धर्म का इतिहास, पेल्विक अल्ट्रासाउंड, हार्मोन जांच, ब्लड शुगर, इंसुलिन स्तर, थायरॉयड जांच और लिपिड प्रोफाइल की जांच की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:591:"PCOS cannot currently be prevented in every individual because its underlying causes are complex and include genetic and hormonal factors. Maintaining regular physical activity, a balanced diet, and a healthy body weight where appropriate can support metabolic health and may improve some PCOS-related features. Early evaluation of persistent irregular periods, excessive hair growth, acne, or fertility difficulties can help identify the condition and associated metabolic risks. Regular monitoring can help address complications such as abnormal glucose regulation and cardiovascular risk.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:430:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखना, नियमित व्यायाम करना, संतुलित आहार लेना, तनाव नियंत्रित करना और नियमित स्वास्थ्य जांच करवाना पीसीओएस की जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:344:"Polycystic ovary syndrome usually requires ongoing medical evaluation rather than emergency care. Seek assessment for persistent menstrual irregularity, abnormal bleeding, fertility concerns, or worsening metabolic symptoms. Urgent evaluation is needed for very heavy bleeding, severe pelvic pain, fainting, or other sudden concerning symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1001:"पॉलीसिस्टिक ओवरी सिंड्रोम (PCOS) के लिए आमतौर पर इमरजेंसी केयर के बजाय लगातार मेडिकल जांच की ज़रूरत होती है। अगर पीरियड्स में लगातार अनियमितता, असामान्य ब्लीडिंग, फर्टिलिटी से जुड़ी चिंताएं या मेटाबोलिक लक्षण बिगड़ रहे हों, तो जांच करवाएं। बहुत ज़्यादा ब्लीडिंग, पेल्विक एरिया में तेज़ दर्द, बेहोशी या अचानक दिखने वाले अन्य चिंताजनक लक्षणों के मामले में तुरंत जांच की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:03:32";}i:3;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:4;s:10:"disease_id";i:106;s:11:"overview_en";s:395:"Fatty liver disease occurs when excess fat accumulates in liver cells. It is commonly associated with metabolic conditions such as obesity, insulin resistance, and type 2 diabetes, although alcohol and other causes can also lead to fatty liver. Many people have no symptoms, while some develop fatigue or discomfort in the upper right abdomen. Persistent liver inflammation can lead to scarring.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:794:"फैटी लिवर रोग में यकृत की कोशिकाओं में अत्यधिक वसा जमा हो जाती है। नॉन-अल्कोहोलिक फैटी लिवर डिजीज (NAFLD) में शराब का अधिक सेवन न करने के बावजूद लिवर में वसा जमा हो जाती है। यह रोग वर्षों तक बिना लक्षण के रह सकता है, लेकिन समय पर उपचार न मिलने पर लिवर में सूजन, फाइब्रोसिस, सिरोसिस और लिवर फेलियर तक पहुंच सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:432:"Fatty liver can result from excess fat storage associated with obesity, insulin resistance, type 2 diabetes, abnormal blood lipid levels, and other metabolic factors. Alcohol use can cause a separate form of fatty liver disease. Certain medicines, inherited disorders, rapid weight loss, and some medical conditions can also contribute. In some people, fat accumulation is accompanied by liver inflammation and progressive scarring.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:570:"मोटापा, इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध, टाइप 2 मधुमेह, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल, मेटाबोलिक सिंड्रोम, निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली, अधिक कैलोरी सेवन और अस्वस्थ भोजन इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं। कुछ लोगों में अत्यधिक शराब सेवन भी फैटी लिवर का कारण बन सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:384:"Risk factors include overweight or obesity, increased abdominal fat, insulin resistance, type 2 diabetes, abnormal cholesterol or triglyceride levels, metabolic syndrome, and physical inactivity. Alcohol consumption is a major risk factor for alcohol-related fatty liver disease. Certain medicines, rapid weight loss, and some inherited or endocrine conditions can also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:424:"मोटापा, पेट की चर्बी, मधुमेह, उच्च रक्तचाप, बढ़े हुए ट्राइग्लिसराइड्स, परिवार में लिवर रोग का इतिहास, निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली और बढ़ती उम्र इसके प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:408:"Diagnosis may begin with medical history, physical examination, blood tests, and imaging. Liver enzymes and other laboratory tests can help identify liver injury but cannot by themselves determine the cause. Ultrasound and other imaging can detect liver fat. Additional testing may be needed to assess fibrosis, exclude other liver diseases, or determine whether inflammation or advanced scarring is present.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:484:"निदान के लिए लिवर फंक्शन टेस्ट, अल्ट्रासाउंड, फाइब्रोस्कैन, सीटी स्कैन, एमआरआई, ब्लड शुगर और लिपिड प्रोफाइल की जांच की जा सकती है। कुछ मामलों में लिवर बायोप्सी की भी आवश्यकता हो सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:414:"Maintaining a healthy weight, regular physical activity, balanced nutrition, and good control of blood glucose and blood lipids can reduce the risk of metabolic fatty liver disease. Limiting or avoiding excessive alcohol can reduce alcohol-related liver injury. Medicines and supplements should be used appropriately. People with metabolic risk factors may benefit from periodic medical assessment of liver health.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:373:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, नियमित व्यायाम करें, मधुमेह और कोलेस्ट्रॉल नियंत्रित रखें, शराब का अत्यधिक सेवन न करें और नियमित स्वास्थ्य जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:299:"Fatty liver disease often causes few or no symptoms and is usually managed with routine medical care. Seek prompt assessment for jaundice, significant abdominal swelling or pain, persistent vomiting, confusion, unusual bleeding, or rapidly worsening symptoms, which may indicate liver complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:826:"फैटी लिवर की बीमारी में अक्सर बहुत कम या कोई लक्षण नहीं दिखते और आमतौर पर इसका इलाज रूटीन मेडिकल देखभाल से किया जाता है। पीलिया, पेट में ज़्यादा सूजन या दर्द, लगातार उल्टी, उलझन, असामान्य ब्लीडिंग या तेज़ी से बिगड़ते लक्षणों के मामले में तुरंत जांच करवाएं, क्योंकि ये लिवर से जुड़ी गंभीर समस्याओं का संकेत हो सकते हैं।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:03:53";}i:4;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:5;s:10:"disease_id";i:142;s:11:"overview_en";s:365:"Kidney stones are hard deposits that form inside the kidneys when substances in urine become concentrated and crystallize. Stones may remain in the kidney without causing symptoms or may move into the urinary tract and cause severe pain. Symptoms can include pain in the side or back, blood in the urine, nausea, vomiting, urinary discomfort, or frequent urination.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:800:"किडनी स्टोन या गुर्दे की पथरी खनिजों और लवणों के कठोर जमाव होते हैं जो गुर्दों में बनते हैं। इनका आकार छोटे क्रिस्टल से लेकर बड़ी पथरी तक हो सकता है। मूत्र मार्ग में चलते समय ये तीव्र दर्द पैदा कर सकते हैं। सामान्य प्रकारों में कैल्शियम स्टोन, यूरिक एसिड स्टोन, स्ट्रुवाइट स्टोन और सिस्टीन स्टोन शामिल हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:412:"Kidney stones form when urine contains high concentrations of substances such as calcium, oxalate, uric acid, or cystine. Low urine volume can increase crystal formation. Other contributors include dietary factors, dehydration, certain metabolic disorders, urinary tract abnormalities, some medicines, and a personal or family history of kidney stones. Different types of stones have different underlying causes.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:515:"जब मूत्र में कैल्शियम, ऑक्सालेट या यूरिक एसिड जैसे तत्व अधिक मात्रा में जमा हो जाते हैं तब पथरी बन सकती है। कम पानी पीना, आहार संबंधी कारण, चयापचय संबंधी विकार और कुछ बीमारियां इसका कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:399:"Risk factors include inadequate fluid intake, previous kidney stones, family history, high intake of sodium or certain animal proteins, obesity, some digestive disorders, recurrent urinary infections, and certain metabolic conditions. Some medicines can also increase stone risk. Hot climates and activities that cause substantial fluid loss may contribute when adequate hydration is not maintained.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:398:"निर्जलीकरण, परिवार में पथरी का इतिहास, मोटापा, अधिक नमक वाला भोजन, अत्यधिक मांसाहार, बार-बार मूत्र संक्रमण, गाउट, मधुमेह और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ा सकती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, urine testing, blood tests, and imaging when needed. Ultrasound or CT imaging can identify stones and assess obstruction. A stone that has been passed may be collected and analyzed to determine its composition. Testing can also help identify infection, kidney impairment, or metabolic factors that increase the likelihood of recurrence.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:438:"निदान के लिए मूत्र जांच, रक्त जांच, अल्ट्रासाउंड, सीटी स्कैन, एक्स-रे और पथरी की संरचना की जांच की जा सकती है। साथ ही गुर्दों की कार्यक्षमता का मूल्यांकन भी किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:411:"Drinking enough fluid to maintain adequate urine output is an important preventive measure. Depending on stone type and individual risk, reducing excessive sodium intake and making appropriate dietary changes may help. Maintaining a healthy weight and following medical advice for recurrent stones can reduce risk. People with repeated stones may benefit from metabolic evaluation and individualized prevention.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:435:"पर्याप्त पानी पिएं, नमक कम करें, स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, पथरी के प्रकार के अनुसार आहार लें, मूत्र संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार कराएं और बार-बार पथरी बनने पर नियमित जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:332:"Kidney stones can cause severe pain and may require urgent treatment. Seek prompt medical care for severe or persistent flank or abdominal pain, vomiting, fever or chills, blood in the urine, difficulty urinating, or worsening symptoms. Fever with urinary obstruction or inability to urinate requires urgent or emergency assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:917:"किडनी स्टोन की वजह से बहुत तेज़ दर्द हो सकता है और इसके लिए तुरंत इलाज की ज़रूरत पड़ सकती है। अगर कमर के किनारे या पेट में बहुत तेज़ या लगातार दर्द हो, उल्टी हो, बुखार या कंपकंपी हो, पेशाब में खून आए, पेशाब करने में दिक्कत हो या लक्षण और बिगड़ जाएं, तो तुरंत डॉक्टर को दिखाएं। अगर पेशाब रुकने या पेशाब न कर पाने के साथ बुखार हो, तो तुरंत जांच की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:04:10";}i:5;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:6;s:10:"disease_id";i:1;s:11:"overview_en";s:371:"Migraine is a neurological condition that causes recurring attacks, often with moderate to severe, throbbing headache that may worsen with routine activity. Nausea and sensitivity to light or sound are common. Some people have temporary visual, sensory, or speech symptoms called aura, which may occur with or without headache. Attacks can last for hours or several days.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:1204:"माइग्रेन एक न्यूरोलॉजिकल विकार है जिसमें बार-बार होने वाला सिरदर्द मध्यम से गंभीर स्तर का हो सकता है। यह दर्द अक्सर धड़कन जैसा महसूस होता है और आमतौर पर सिर के एक हिस्से में अधिक होता है, हालांकि दोनों तरफ भी हो सकता है। माइग्रेन का दौरा कुछ घंटों से लेकर कई दिनों तक रह सकता है और दैनिक गतिविधियों को प्रभावित कर सकता है। इसके साथ मतली, उल्टी, रोशनी और आवाज़ से परेशानी तथा चक्कर आना जैसे लक्षण हो सकते हैं। कुछ लोगों को सिरदर्द शुरू होने से पहले ऑरा महसूस होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:375:"The exact cause of migraine is not fully understood. It involves changes in brain activity and nerve signaling, with genetic factors contributing to susceptibility. Individual attacks may be triggered by hormonal changes, stress, disrupted sleep, missed meals, or particular sensory or dietary exposures. Triggers vary between people and are not universal causes of migraine.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:703:"माइग्रेन का कारण मस्तिष्क की रसायन प्रक्रिया, नसों और रक्त वाहिकाओं में होने वाले जटिल बदलावों से जुड़ा माना जाता है। तनाव, हार्मोनल परिवर्तन, नींद की कमी, निर्जलीकरण, भोजन छोड़ना, तेज रोशनी, तीव्र गंध, शराब, अधिक कैफीन और कुछ खाद्य पदार्थ माइग्रेन को ट्रिगर कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:272:"Migraine is more common in people with a family history of the condition and in women. Hormonal changes can influence attacks. Factors that trigger an attack in someone who already has migraine should be distinguished from factors associated with developing the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:344:"परिवार में माइग्रेन का इतिहास, महिला होना, हार्मोनल परिवर्तन, चिंता, अवसाद, मोटापा, अनियमित नींद और लगातार तनाव इसके जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:397:"Diagnosis usually relies on the pattern of headache and associated symptoms, medical history, and physical and neurological examination. There is no single laboratory test that confirms migraine; tests may help investigate other causes when appropriate. A sudden, extremely severe headache, new weakness, confusion, or a seizure requires urgent assessment rather than being assumed to be migraine.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:625:"निदान मुख्य रूप से रोगी के लक्षणों और चिकित्सकीय इतिहास के आधार पर किया जाता है। आवश्यकता होने पर न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, एमआरआई या सीटी स्कैन करवाया जा सकता है। माइग्रेन डायरी रखने से ट्रिगर और उपचार की प्रभावशीलता समझने में मदद मिलती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:224:"Attacks cannot always be prevented. Regular sleep and meals, adequate fluids, appropriate physical activity, and stress management may help reduce attacks. A headache diary can help identify patterns and individual triggers.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:355:"नियमित नींद लें, तनाव नियंत्रित करें, व्यायाम करें, पर्याप्त पानी पिएं, ज्ञात ट्रिगर्स से बचें और आवश्यकता होने पर चिकित्सकीय सलाह लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:231:"Seek urgent medical attention for a sudden, extremely severe headache, a new headache with weakness, numbness, confusion, fainting, seizures, vision loss, fever with a stiff neck, or a major change from your usual migraine pattern.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:573:"अगर अचानक बहुत तेज़ सिरदर्द हो, या नए सिरदर्द के साथ कमज़ोरी, सुन्नपन, उलझन, बेहोशी, दौरे पड़ना, दिखाई न देना, गर्दन में अकड़न के साथ बुख़ार हो, या आपके आम माइग्रेन के पैटर्न में कोई बड़ा बदलाव दिखे, तो तुरंत डॉक्टर से मिलें।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:04:29";}i:6;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:7;s:10:"disease_id";i:67;s:11:"overview_en";s:365:"Asthma is a chronic condition in which the airways become inflamed and can narrow or become more sensitive to triggers. This may cause repeated episodes of wheezing, coughing, chest tightness, or shortness of breath. Symptoms can vary over time and may become worse during an asthma attack. Asthma can begin in childhood or adulthood and affects people of all ages.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:813:"अस्थमा श्वसन मार्ग की एक दीर्घकालिक सूजन संबंधी बीमारी है जिसमें घरघराहट, खांसी, सीने में जकड़न और सांस लेने में कठिनाई होती है। वायुमार्ग सूज जाते हैं और धूल, एलर्जी, प्रदूषण, व्यायाम या संक्रमण जैसे कारकों के प्रति अधिक संवेदनशील हो जाते हैं। उचित उपचार और सावधानी के साथ अधिकांश लोग सामान्य जीवन जी सकते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:396:"The exact cause of asthma is not known. Genetic susceptibility and environmental exposures both appear to contribute. Triggers can include allergens such as dust mites, mold, pollen, and animal allergens, as well as tobacco smoke, air pollution, respiratory infections, cold air, exercise, and some medicines. Occupational exposure to chemicals or industrial dust can also cause or worsen asthma.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:518:"अस्थमा आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारणों के संयोजन से विकसित होता है। धूल, परागकण, पालतू जानवरों के बाल, फफूंदी, धुआं, प्रदूषण, श्वसन संक्रमण, ठंडी हवा, तीव्र गंध, तनाव और व्यायाम इसके सामान्य ट्रिगर हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:372:"Risk factors include a family history of asthma, allergies, exposure to tobacco smoke, certain workplace chemicals or dusts, repeated viral respiratory infections during childhood, and obesity. The likelihood of asthma may also be influenced by environmental conditions and individual sensitivity to allergens or irritants. Risk factors and triggers differ between people.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:446:"परिवार में अस्थमा का इतिहास, एलर्जी, एक्जिमा, धूम्रपान, मोटापा, प्रदूषण, बार-बार श्वसन संक्रमण, रासायनिक पदार्थों के संपर्क और परोक्ष धूम्रपान इसके प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:380:"Asthma is diagnosed using the pattern of symptoms, medical history, physical examination, and lung function testing. Spirometry can assess how much air a person can breathe out and how quickly it moves through the airways. Additional testing may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain or to identify allergic or other triggers. Symptoms and lung function are considered together.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:366:"निदान के लिए चिकित्सकीय इतिहास, शारीरिक परीक्षण, स्पाइरोमेट्री, पीक फ्लो टेस्ट, एलर्जी परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार अन्य जांचें की जाती हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:413:"Asthma cannot always be prevented, but attacks can often be reduced by identifying and avoiding personal triggers and following an individualized treatment plan. Avoiding tobacco smoke, reducing exposure to known allergens or irritants, managing respiratory infections, and taking prescribed medicines as directed can help control symptoms. Regular follow-up is important when symptoms are persistent or changing.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:408:"धूम्रपान से बचें, ट्रिगर्स की पहचान करें, स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, चिकित्सकीय उपचार का पालन करें, आवश्यक टीकाकरण करवाएं और श्वसन संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार कराएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:336:"Seek urgent medical attention for an asthma attack that is severe or worsening despite the person's usual reliever treatment, marked difficulty speaking or walking because of breathlessness, bluish lips or face, confusion, exhaustion, or severe breathing difficulty. Emergency care is needed when breathing becomes critically difficult.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1058:"अगर अस्थमा का दौरा गंभीर हो या व्यक्ति के सामान्य रिलीवर इलाज के बावजूद और बिगड़ रहा हो, तो तुरंत मेडिकल मदद लें। इसके अलावा, अगर सांस लेने में तकलीफ के कारण बोलने या चलने में बहुत मुश्किल हो रही हो, होंठ या चेहरा नीला पड़ रहा हो, उलझन या बहुत ज़्यादा थकान महसूस हो रही हो, या सांस लेने में बहुत ज़्यादा दिक्कत हो रही हो, तो भी तुरंत मदद लें। जब सांस लेना बहुत मुश्किल हो जाए, तो इमरजेंसी देखभाल की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:04:46";}i:7;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:8;s:10:"disease_id";i:101;s:11:"overview_en";s:574:"Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) is a chronic condition in which stomach contents repeatedly flow backward into the esophagus. This can cause heartburn, acid regurgitation, chest or upper abdominal discomfort, difficulty swallowing, or a sour taste in the mouth. Some people also experience cough, hoarseness, or other symptoms related to reflux. GERD commonly results from weakness or inappropriate relaxation of the lower esophageal sphincter. Persistent symptoms should be evaluated because long-term reflux can irritate the esophagus and may lead to complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:694:"गैस्ट्रोएसोफेगल रिफ्लक्स डिजीज (GERD) एक दीर्घकालिक पाचन विकार है जिसमें पेट का अम्ल बार-बार भोजन नली में वापस आ जाता है। इससे सीने में जलन, खट्टी डकार, सीने में असुविधा और निगलने में कठिनाई हो सकती है। लंबे समय तक अनुपचारित रहने पर यह गंभीर जटिलताएं उत्पन्न कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:531:"GERD develops when the barrier between the stomach and esophagus does not prevent stomach contents from repeatedly moving upward. Weakness or inappropriate relaxation of the lower esophageal sphincter is a major mechanism. A hiatal hernia can contribute in some people. Reflux may be worsened by factors such as excess body weight, large meals, lying down soon after eating, smoking, alcohol, and certain foods or medicines in susceptible individuals. Frequent reflux can cause inflammation and irritation of the esophageal lining.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:536:"GERD तब विकसित होता है जब भोजन नली और पेट के बीच का वाल्व कमजोर हो जाता है या सही ढंग से कार्य नहीं करता। मोटापा, अधिक भोजन, हायटल हर्निया, गर्भावस्था, धूम्रपान, शराब और कुछ खाद्य पदार्थ इसमें योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:523:"Risk factors for GERD include excess body weight, pregnancy, hiatal hernia, smoking, and certain eating or lifestyle patterns. Large meals, lying down soon after eating, and individual dietary triggers can worsen symptoms in susceptible people. Some medicines may also affect the lower esophageal sphincter or irritate the esophagus. Risk increases with age for some individuals. Persistent or severe symptoms require assessment because reflux can sometimes cause esophageal inflammation, narrowing, or other complications.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:350:"मोटापा, गर्भावस्था, धूम्रपान, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन, अधिक वसायुक्त भोजन, मसालेदार भोजन और निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली इसके प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:570:"GERD is often diagnosed from the pattern and frequency of symptoms, medical history, and response to appropriate treatment. Many people with typical heartburn and regurgitation do not initially need extensive testing. If symptoms are persistent, severe, atypical, or do not respond to treatment, upper endoscopy may be used to examine the esophagus and stomach. Ambulatory esophageal pH or impedance monitoring can measure reflux when the diagnosis remains uncertain. Additional testing may be considered when swallowing difficulty or other warning symptoms are present.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:387:"निदान के लिए एंडोस्कोपी, pH मॉनिटरिंग, इसोफेगल मैनोमेट्री तथा लक्षणों का मूल्यांकन किया जा सकता है। लगातार लक्षण होने पर चिकित्सकीय जांच आवश्यक है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:546:"GERD symptoms may be reduced by maintaining a healthy body weight, avoiding smoking, limiting alcohol when it worsens symptoms, and avoiding meals close to bedtime. Smaller meals and remaining upright after eating may also help some people. Individual trigger foods vary, so identifying personal triggers can be useful. Persistent symptoms should be medically evaluated rather than managed indefinitely without assessment. Appropriate treatment can reduce irritation and lower the likelihood of complications associated with long-standing reflux.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:299:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, भोजन के तुरंत बाद न लेटें, धूम्रपान छोड़ें, शराब सीमित करें और ट्रिगर खाद्य पदार्थों से बचें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:332:"GERD usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt medical assessment for difficulty or pain with swallowing, persistent vomiting, vomiting blood, black stools, unexplained weight loss, persistent chest pain, or symptoms that are new or significantly worsening. Severe or unexplained chest pain requires emergency evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:908:"GERD के लिए आमतौर पर इमरजेंसी इलाज की ज़रूरत नहीं होती है। अगर कुछ निगलने में परेशानी या दर्द हो, लगातार उल्टी हो, उल्टी में खून आए, मल का रंग काला हो, बिना किसी वजह के वज़न कम हो, सीने में लगातार दर्द हो, या कोई नया या तेज़ी से बिगड़ने वाला लक्षण दिखे, तो तुरंत डॉक्टर को दिखाएँ। सीने में तेज़ या बिना किसी वजह के दर्द होने पर इमरजेंसी जांच की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:05:25";}i:8;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:9;s:10:"disease_id";i:236;s:11:"overview_en";s:332:"Osteoarthritis is a common joint disorder in which the tissues within and around a joint gradually change and the joint cartilage can break down. It most often affects the knees, hips, hands, and spine. Symptoms may include joint pain, stiffness, swelling, and reduced movement, particularly after activity or periods of inactivity.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:922:"ऑस्टियोआर्थराइटिस गठिया का सबसे सामान्य प्रकार है। इसमें जोड़ों की हड्डियों के सिरों को ढकने वाली सुरक्षात्मक उपास्थि (कार्टिलेज) धीरे-धीरे घिसने लगती है। यह घुटनों, कूल्हों, हाथों, पैरों और रीढ़ की हड्डी को अधिक प्रभावित करता है। इसके लक्षण धीरे-धीरे विकसित होते हैं और इनमें दर्द, जकड़न, लचीलापन कम होना तथा दैनिक कार्यों में कठिनाई शामिल हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:334:"Osteoarthritis develops through changes and breakdown involving cartilage, bone, and other joint tissues. Aging is an important contributor, while previous joint injury, repeated joint stress, excess body weight, joint abnormalities, and certain metabolic or inflammatory conditions can increase the likelihood of developing symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:573:"ऑस्टियोआर्थराइटिस का मुख्य कारण उम्र के साथ जोड़ों की उपास्थि का घिसना है। इसके अलावा जोड़ों में चोट, मोटापा, बार-बार होने वाला दबाव, आनुवंशिक कारण, मांसपेशियों की कमजोरी और कुछ चयापचय विकार भी इसमें योगदान दे सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:382:"Risk factors include increasing age, excess body weight, previous joint injuries, repeated mechanical stress, joint abnormalities, and family history. Osteoarthritis is more common in certain joints and may be influenced by occupational or recreational activities that repeatedly load a joint. Having a risk factor does not necessarily mean that a person will develop the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:439:"बढ़ती उम्र, मोटापा, जोड़ों में पुरानी चोट, परिवार में बीमारी का इतिहास, कुछ प्रकार के शारीरिक कार्य, निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली और मांसपेशियों की कमजोरी प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:291:"Diagnosis is usually based on symptoms, medical history, and physical examination. A clinician assesses joint pain, stiffness, movement, swelling, and functional limitations. X-rays or other imaging may help identify joint changes or exclude other conditions when the diagnosis is uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:336:"निदान के लिए चिकित्सकीय इतिहास, शारीरिक परीक्षण, जोड़ों की गति का मूल्यांकन, एक्स-रे तथा आवश्यकता अनुसार एमआरआई किया जा सकता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:333:"Maintaining a healthy body weight, regular physical activity, strengthening muscles around vulnerable joints, avoiding joint injuries, and using appropriate techniques during repetitive activities may help reduce osteoarthritis risk or progression. Existing joint injuries and contributing conditions should be appropriately managed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:324:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, नियमित व्यायाम करें, मांसपेशियों को मजबूत रखें, जोड़ों पर अनावश्यक दबाव से बचें और समय पर उपचार कराएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:387:"Osteoarthritis is usually a chronic condition and is not generally an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent or worsening joint pain, swelling, stiffness, reduced mobility, or symptoms that interfere with normal activities. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for a suddenly hot, very swollen joint with fever because infection or another acute condition may need to be excluded.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1234:"ऑस्टियोआर्थराइटिस आमतौर पर एक लंबे समय तक चलने वाली बीमारी है और आमतौर पर यह कोई इमरजेंसी नहीं होती है। अगर जोड़ों में लगातार दर्द या दर्द का बढ़ना, सूजन, अकड़न, हिलने-डुलने में परेशानी हो, या ऐसे लक्षण हों जिनसे रोज़मर्रा के कामों में दिक्कत आए, तो डॉक्टर से जांच करवानी चाहिए। अगर जोड़ अचानक गर्म हो जाए, उसमें बहुत ज़्यादा सूजन हो और साथ में बुखार भी हो, तो तुरंत जांच करवाना सही रहता है, क्योंकि संक्रमण या किसी दूसरी गंभीर स्थिति की संभावना हो सकती है जिसे देखना ज़रूरी है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:05:42";}i:9;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:10;s:10:"disease_id";i:301;s:11:"overview_en";s:368:"Depression is a common mental health condition characterized by persistent low mood or loss of interest or pleasure that affects daily life. It may also involve changes in sleep, appetite, energy, concentration, motivation, and feelings about oneself. Depression can vary in severity and may result from an interaction of biological, psychological, and social factors.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:694:"अवसाद (डिप्रेशन) एक सामान्य मानसिक स्वास्थ्य विकार है जो व्यक्ति की भावनाओं, सोच और व्यवहार को प्रभावित करता है। यह केवल अस्थायी उदासी नहीं है बल्कि एक गंभीर चिकित्सीय स्थिति है जो कार्यक्षमता, रिश्तों, शारीरिक स्वास्थ्य और जीवन की गुणवत्ता को प्रभावित कर सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:316:"Depression can result from a combination of genetic, biological, psychological, and social factors. Stressful life events, trauma, chronic illness, certain medications, substance use, and family history may increase vulnerability. Changes involving brain signaling and other biological processes may also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:581:"डिप्रेशन जैविक, मनोवैज्ञानिक, सामाजिक और पर्यावरणीय कारकों के संयोजन से विकसित हो सकता है। आनुवंशिक कारण, मस्तिष्क के रासायनिक असंतुलन, तनाव, आघात, जीवन में बड़े परिवर्तन, बीमारियां और सामाजिक अलगाव इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:384:"Risk factors include personal or family history of depression, major or prolonged stress, trauma, social isolation, chronic medical conditions, certain medications, substance use, and major life changes. Some people may also have increased vulnerability because of genetic or biological factors. Having a risk factor does not necessarily mean that a person will develop the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:406:"परिवार में अवसाद का इतिहास, चिंता विकार, पुरानी बीमारियां, दर्दनाक अनुभव, नशे की आदत, अकेलापन, आर्थिक कठिनाइयां और सामाजिक सहयोग की कमी इसके जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:296:"Depression is diagnosed through a clinical assessment that considers mood, interest or pleasure, sleep, appetite, energy, concentration, thoughts, and daily functioning. A clinician may also review medical history, medications, substance use, and other conditions that can cause similar symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:380:"निदान के लिए विस्तृत मानसिक और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन किया जाता है। चिकित्सक लक्षणों, उनकी अवधि, गंभीरता और दैनिक जीवन पर प्रभाव का आकलन करते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:339:"Depression cannot always be prevented, but regular physical activity, adequate sleep, supportive relationships, stress management, avoidance of harmful substance use, and early attention to persistent mood changes may support mental health. People with recurrent depression may benefit from an individualized prevention and treatment plan.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:417:"सामाजिक संबंध बनाए रखें, तनाव नियंत्रित करें, नियमित व्यायाम करें, पर्याप्त नींद लें, मानसिक स्वास्थ्य संबंधी समस्याओं के लिए समय पर सहायता लें और नशे से बचें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:441:"Depression should be medically or professionally assessed when persistent low mood, loss of interest, sleep or appetite changes, hopelessness, or reduced functioning interferes with daily life. Seek prompt help when symptoms are worsening or daily functioning is substantially affected. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal thoughts, a plan to self-harm, inability to remain safe, severe confusion, or other immediate safety concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1198:"जब लगातार उदासी, किसी चीज़ में मन न लगना, नींद या भूख में बदलाव, निराशा या रोज़मर्रा के कामों में कमी आने से ज़िंदगी पर असर पड़े, तो डिप्रेशन की मेडिकल या प्रोफेशनल जांच करवानी चाहिए। अगर लक्षण बिगड़ रहे हों या रोज़मर्रा के कामों पर काफ़ी असर पड़ रहा हो, तो तुरंत मदद लें। आत्महत्या के विचार, खुद को नुकसान पहुँचाने की योजना, खुद को सुरक्षित न रख पाना, बहुत ज़्यादा उलझन या सुरक्षा से जुड़ी दूसरी तुरंत ध्यान देने वाली स्थितियों में इमरजेंसी मदद की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:06:02";}i:10;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:11;s:10:"disease_id";i:91;s:11:"overview_en";s:628:"Anemia occurs when the blood does not have enough healthy red blood cells or enough hemoglobin to carry oxygen effectively to body tissues. It is a common condition with many possible causes, including iron deficiency, vitamin deficiencies, blood loss, chronic diseases, inherited blood disorders, and problems affecting the production or destruction of red blood cells. Symptoms vary according to the cause and severity and may include tiredness, weakness, pale skin, dizziness, headaches, shortness of breath, or a rapid heartbeat. Identifying the underlying cause is important because treatment depends on the type of anemia.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:653:"एनीमिया एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें शरीर में पर्याप्त स्वस्थ लाल रक्त कोशिकाएं या हीमोग्लोबिन नहीं होता। इसके कारण शरीर के ऊतकों तक पर्याप्त ऑक्सीजन नहीं पहुंच पाती। इससे थकान, कमजोरी, चक्कर आना, त्वचा का पीला पड़ना और सांस फूलना जैसे लक्षण हो सकते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:567:"Anemia can result from blood loss, reduced production of red blood cells, or increased destruction of red blood cells. Iron deficiency is a common cause and may develop because of inadequate dietary iron, increased requirements, poor absorption, or chronic blood loss. Other causes include deficiencies of vitamin B12 or folate, chronic kidney or inflammatory conditions, inherited blood disorders, bone marrow problems, infections, and certain medicines. Identifying the specific mechanism is necessary because different forms of anemia require different treatments.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:359:"सामान्य कारणों में आयरन की कमी, विटामिन B12 की कमी, फोलेट की कमी, रक्तस्राव, दीर्घकालिक रोग, गुर्दा रोग, संक्रमण और आनुवंशिक विकार शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:553:"Risk factors for anemia vary according to its cause. They may include inadequate intake of iron, vitamin B12, or folate; heavy menstrual bleeding; pregnancy; gastrointestinal blood loss; chronic kidney or inflammatory disease; nutritional or absorption disorders; inherited blood conditions; and certain medicines. Infants, children, older adults, and people with chronic medical conditions may have increased risk of particular forms of anemia. Risk should therefore be assessed in relation to the individual's age, medical history, diet, and symptoms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:404:"जोखिम कारकों में खराब पोषण, गर्भावस्था, दीर्घकालिक बीमारी, अत्यधिक मासिक धर्म रक्तस्राव, बढ़ती उम्र और रक्त संबंधी विकारों का पारिवारिक इतिहास शामिल है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:552:"Diagnosis of anemia generally begins with a complete blood count to determine the hemoglobin level and assess the size and characteristics of red blood cells. Additional blood tests may evaluate iron stores, vitamin B12, folate, kidney function, inflammation, or other causes depending on the findings. The medical history may include diet, menstrual or other blood loss, digestive symptoms, chronic disease, medicines, and family history. Further investigation may be needed to identify an underlying source of blood loss or another medical condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:274:"निदान के लिए CBC, हीमोग्लोबिन जांच, आयरन प्रोफाइल, विटामिन B12, फोलेट स्तर तथा अन्य आवश्यक जांचें की जाती हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:583:"Prevention of anemia depends on its cause. A balanced diet containing adequate iron, vitamin B12, folate, and other nutrients can help prevent nutritional deficiencies. Pregnant people may require supplements according to medical guidance. Heavy menstrual bleeding, gastrointestinal blood loss, chronic disease, and absorption problems should be evaluated and treated when present. Iron or vitamin supplements should not be taken routinely in large amounts without identifying the cause of anemia, because unnecessary supplementation may be ineffective or harmful in some situations.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:325:"आयरन, फोलेट और विटामिन B12 युक्त संतुलित आहार लें। मूल कारणों का समय पर उपचार कराएं और लगातार थकान होने पर चिकित्सकीय सलाह लें.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:283:"Seek prompt medical assessment for severe weakness, shortness of breath at rest, chest pain, fainting, confusion, very rapid heartbeat, or symptoms that are rapidly worsening. Emergency assessment may be needed when severe anemia causes significant breathing or circulation problems.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:794:"अगर बहुत ज़्यादा कमज़ोरी, आराम करते समय भी सांस लेने में तकलीफ़, सीने में दर्द, बेहोशी, उलझन, दिल की धड़कन का बहुत तेज़ होना या तेज़ी से बिगड़ते लक्षण महसूस हों, तो तुरंत डॉक्टर से जाँच करवाएँ। जब गंभीर एनीमिया के कारण सांस लेने या ब्लड सर्कुलेशन में बड़ी समस्याएँ हों, तो इमरजेंसी जाँच की ज़रूरत पड़ सकती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:06:26";}i:11;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:12;s:10:"disease_id";i:92;s:11:"overview_en";s:595:"Iron deficiency anemia is the most common type of anemia and occurs when the body does not have enough iron to produce adequate hemoglobin. Hemoglobin is the protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout the body. As iron stores fall, the body may produce smaller or less effective red blood cells. Symptoms can include tiredness, weakness, pale skin, dizziness, headaches, shortness of breath, reduced concentration, and decreased ability to tolerate physical activity. The condition may develop gradually and can sometimes remain unnoticed until the deficiency becomes more severe.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:652:"आयरन की कमी से होने वाला एनीमिया एनीमिया का सबसे सामान्य प्रकार है। यह तब होता है जब शरीर में पर्याप्त आयरन नहीं होता जिससे पर्याप्त हीमोग्लोबिन नहीं बन पाता। इसके कारण थकान, कमजोरी, चक्कर आना, सांस फूलना और ध्यान केंद्रित करने में कठिनाई हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:551:"Iron deficiency anemia develops when the body does not have enough iron to make sufficient hemoglobin. Iron deficiency may result from inadequate dietary intake, increased requirements during childhood, adolescence, or pregnancy, reduced absorption from gastrointestinal disorders, or chronic blood loss. Menstrual blood loss is an important cause in some women, while gastrointestinal bleeding can be an important source in other adults. Conditions that interfere with digestion or absorption can also reduce the amount of iron available to the body.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:336:"यह रोग आयरन युक्त भोजन की कमी, रक्तस्राव, गर्भावस्था, पाचन तंत्र की समस्याओं या शरीर की बढ़ी हुई आयरन आवश्यकता के कारण हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:493:"Risk of iron deficiency anemia is increased by heavy menstrual bleeding, pregnancy, infancy and childhood growth, adolescence, diets that provide inadequate iron, and conditions that reduce iron absorption. People with chronic gastrointestinal disorders, recurrent blood loss, gastrointestinal bleeding, or certain dietary restrictions may also be at increased risk. The risk depends on the balance between iron intake, absorption, storage, and the amount of iron lost or required by the body.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:342:"अत्यधिक मासिक धर्म वाली महिलाएं, गर्भवती महिलाएं, बच्चे, किशोर, शाकाहारी और पाचन तंत्र संबंधी रोगियों में इसका जोखिम अधिक होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:570:"Diagnosis usually begins with a complete blood count to identify anemia and changes in red blood cell size and appearance. Ferritin testing is commonly used to assess iron stores, while serum iron, transferrin saturation, and related tests may help clarify iron status. When iron deficiency is confirmed, evaluation should also consider why it developed. Depending on age, sex, symptoms, and clinical circumstances, healthcare professionals may investigate menstrual blood loss, dietary factors, gastrointestinal bleeding, malabsorption, or another underlying condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:270:"निदान के लिए CBC, सीरम फेरिटिन, सीरम आयरन, ट्रांसफेरिन सैचुरेशन और रक्तस्राव के कारणों की जांच की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:525:"A balanced diet containing adequate iron can help maintain iron stores. Good dietary sources include meat, poultry, seafood, legumes, fortified grains, and leafy vegetables. Vitamin C can improve absorption of iron from plant foods. People with heavy menstrual bleeding, gastrointestinal disease, pregnancy, or other risk factors may need medical monitoring and, when appropriate, iron supplementation. Unexplained or persistent blood loss should be evaluated rather than treated only with iron without identifying its cause.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:358:"आयरन युक्त भोजन लें, विटामिन C युक्त खाद्य पदार्थ खाएं, रक्तस्राव संबंधी समस्याओं का समय पर उपचार कराएं और नियमित स्वास्थ्य जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:270:"Seek medical assessment for worsening fatigue, shortness of breath, dizziness, fainting, chest pain, rapid heartbeat, or evidence of significant bleeding. Emergency care is needed for severe weakness, fainting, major bleeding, chest pain, or severe difficulty breathing.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:763:"अगर थकान बढ़ रही हो, सांस लेने में दिक्कत हो, चक्कर आएं, बेहोशी छाए, सीने में दर्द हो, दिल की धड़कन तेज़ हो या ज़्यादा ब्लीडिंग हो, तो डॉक्टर को दिखाएं। बहुत ज़्यादा कमज़ोरी, बेहोशी, बहुत ज़्यादा ब्लीडिंग, सीने में दर्द या सांस लेने में बहुत ज़्यादा दिक्कत होने पर इमरजेंसी इलाज की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:06:42";}i:12;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:13;s:10:"disease_id";i:117;s:11:"overview_en";s:426:"Irritable bowel syndrome is a common disorder affecting the digestive system and causing recurrent abdominal pain associated with changes in bowel habits. Some people mainly have constipation, others mainly have diarrhea, and some alternate between both. Symptoms may also include bloating, gas, urgency, or a feeling of incomplete bowel movements. IBS does not cause the structural damage seen in inflammatory bowel diseases.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:642:"इरिटेबल बॉवेल सिंड्रोम (IBS) बड़ी आंत से संबंधित एक सामान्य कार्यात्मक विकार है। इसमें पेट दर्द, पेट फूलना, गैस, दस्त, कब्ज या दोनों का बारी-बारी से होना शामिल है। यह जीवन की गुणवत्ता को प्रभावित कर सकता है लेकिन आंतों को स्थायी नुकसान नहीं पहुंचाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:472:"The exact cause of irritable bowel syndrome is not fully understood. It may involve changes in communication between the brain and digestive tract, altered intestinal movement, increased sensitivity of the intestines, changes in the gut microbiome, and previous gastrointestinal infection. Food sensitivities, stress, and hormonal changes may influence symptoms in some people. IBS can develop through a combination of biological, psychological, and environmental factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:402:"इसका सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं है, लेकिन आंतों की असामान्य गतिविधि, तनाव, खाद्य संवेदनशीलता, संक्रमण और आंतों के बैक्टीरिया में बदलाव से इसका संबंध हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:472:"Risk may be increased by a history of gastrointestinal infection, changes in the gut microbiome, food-related triggers, and psychological stress. IBS is more common in women and often begins in younger adulthood. A family history may increase susceptibility. People with other functional gastrointestinal disorders or certain psychological stressors may also experience a greater burden of symptoms, although these factors do not necessarily cause IBS in every individual.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:272:"तनाव, चिंता, अवसाद, पारिवारिक इतिहास, खाद्य असहिष्णुता, महिला होना और पूर्व संक्रमण इसके जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:450:"Diagnosis is usually based on the pattern of abdominal pain and changes in bowel habits together with a medical history and physical examination. Healthcare professionals may use established symptom criteria and perform selected blood or stool tests to exclude other conditions. Additional testing, such as colonoscopy, may be recommended when warning signs, unusual symptoms, older age at onset, or other clinical concerns suggest another diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:387:"निदान लक्षणों, चिकित्सा इतिहास और अन्य रोगों को बाहर करने के आधार पर किया जाता है। आवश्यकता होने पर रक्त जांच, मल जांच और कोलोनोस्कोपी की जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:476:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent irritable bowel syndrome, but some people can reduce symptom flare-ups by identifying and managing individual triggers. Regular meals, adequate fluid intake, physical activity, sufficient sleep, and stress-management strategies may help. Dietary changes should be individualized because triggers differ. People with persistent or changing bowel symptoms should seek medical evaluation rather than assuming that symptoms are caused by IBS.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:309:"तनाव नियंत्रित रखें, संतुलित आहार लें, ट्रिगर खाद्य पदार्थों की पहचान करें, नियमित व्यायाम करें और पर्याप्त नींद लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:344:"Irritable bowel syndrome usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt medical assessment for new or persistent symptoms with unexplained weight loss, blood in the stool, fever, anemia, nighttime symptoms, persistent vomiting, or significant worsening. Severe abdominal pain, fainting, or significant bleeding requires urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1001:"इरिटेबल बाउल सिंड्रोम (IBS) के लिए आमतौर पर इमरजेंसी मेडिकल केयर की ज़रूरत नहीं होती है। अगर बिना किसी साफ़ वजह के वज़न कम होने, मल में खून आने, बुखार, एनीमिया, रात में लक्षण दिखने, लगातार उल्टी होने या हालत के काफ़ी बिगड़ने जैसे नए या लगातार बने रहने वाले लक्षण दिखें, तो तुरंत डॉक्टर से जाँच करवाएँ। पेट में तेज़ दर्द, बेहोशी या काफ़ी ज़्यादा ब्लीडिंग होने पर तुरंत जाँच की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:07:00";}i:13;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:14;s:10:"disease_id";i:143;s:11:"overview_en";s:395:"Chronic kidney disease is a long-term condition in which the kidneys become damaged or lose function over time. Healthy kidneys remove waste and excess fluid from the blood and help regulate blood pressure, electrolytes, and other important processes. Chronic kidney disease may progress gradually and can eventually lead to kidney failure. Early disease may cause few or no noticeable symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:693:"क्रॉनिक किडनी डिजीज (CKD) एक दीर्घकालिक रोग है जिसमें गुर्दे धीरे-धीरे रक्त को साफ करने की क्षमता खो देते हैं। शुरुआती चरणों में लक्षण कम हो सकते हैं, लेकिन आगे चलकर यह एनीमिया, उच्च रक्तचाप, हड्डियों की बीमारी, इलेक्ट्रोलाइट असंतुलन और किडनी फेलियर का कारण बन सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:421:"Diabetes and high blood pressure are the most common causes of chronic kidney disease. Other causes include inflammation of the kidney, inherited kidney disorders, repeated urinary obstruction, certain infections, autoimmune diseases, and long-term exposure to medicines or substances that can damage the kidneys. Some kidney diseases begin with direct injury to filtering structures and gradually reduce kidney function.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:346:"इसके सामान्य कारणों में मधुमेह, उच्च रक्तचाप, गुर्दों की सूजन, ऑटोइम्यून रोग, आनुवंशिक विकार और बार-बार होने वाले संक्रमण शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:407:"Risk is increased by diabetes, high blood pressure, heart disease, obesity, older age, smoking, and a family history of kidney disease. Previous acute kidney injury and certain inherited or inflammatory kidney disorders can also increase risk. Long-term use of some medicines or exposure to kidney-toxic substances may contribute. Risk is particularly important when several of these factors occur together.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:282:"जोखिम कारकों में मधुमेह, उच्च रक्तचाप, मोटापा, धूम्रपान, पारिवारिक इतिहास, हृदय रोग और बढ़ती उम्र शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:477:"Diagnosis uses blood and urine tests to assess kidney function and look for evidence of kidney damage. Blood creatinine is used to estimate the glomerular filtration rate, while urine testing can detect albumin or other abnormalities. Blood pressure measurement and review of medical history are also important. Ultrasound or other imaging may help identify structural abnormalities, obstruction, or other causes. Additional testing may be required when the cause is uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:249:"निदान के लिए रक्त जांच, सीरम क्रिएटिनिन, eGFR, मूत्र जांच, अल्ट्रासाउंड और अन्य जांचें की जाती हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:495:"Not all chronic kidney disease can be prevented, but controlling conditions that damage the kidneys can reduce risk or slow progression. Maintain healthy blood pressure and blood glucose levels, avoid smoking, stay physically active, and maintain a healthy weight. Use medicines as directed and avoid unnecessary use of medicines that can harm the kidneys. People at increased risk should follow recommended kidney-function and urine testing and seek medical advice for persistent abnormalities.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:326:"मधुमेह और रक्तचाप को नियंत्रित रखें, धूम्रपान से बचें, स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, पर्याप्त पानी पिएं और नियमित किडनी जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:389:"Chronic kidney disease usually requires ongoing medical monitoring rather than emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for rapidly worsening swelling, major changes in urination, persistent vomiting, severe weakness, confusion, chest pain, or worsening shortness of breath. Severe breathing difficulty, loss of consciousness, or other signs of a serious complication require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1025:"क्रोनिक किडनी की बीमारी में आमतौर पर इमरजेंसी केयर के बजाय लगातार मेडिकल निगरानी की ज़रूरत होती है। अगर तेज़ी से सूजन बढ़े, पेशाब में बड़े बदलाव हों, लगातार उल्टी हो, बहुत ज़्यादा कमज़ोरी महसूस हो, उलझन हो, सीने में दर्द हो या साँस लेने में तकलीफ़ बढ़े, तो तुरंत जाँच करवाएँ। साँस लेने में बहुत ज़्यादा तकलीफ़, बेहोशी या किसी गंभीर समस्या के दूसरे लक्षण दिखने पर इमरजेंसी केयर की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:07:18";}i:14;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:15;s:10:"disease_id";i:200;s:11:"overview_en";s:365:"Breast cancer develops when abnormal breast cells grow without normal control. Common invasive types begin in the milk ducts or milk-producing lobules and extend into surrounding tissue. It occurs mainly in women but can also affect men. Possible changes include a lump, thickening, altered breast shape, or nipple discharge; some cancers cause no obvious symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:521:"स्तन कैंसर एक ऐसी बीमारी है जिसमें स्तन की असामान्य कोशिकाएं अनियंत्रित रूप से बढ़ने लगती हैं और ट्यूमर बनाती हैं। यह महिलाओं में सबसे सामान्य कैंसरों में से एक है, हालांकि पुरुषों में भी हो सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:335:"Breast cancer involves genetic changes that disrupt normal control of cell growth. These changes can arise during life or be inherited. Inherited variants in genes such as BRCA1 and BRCA2 can increase susceptibility. A risk factor changes the likelihood of cancer; it does not necessarily identify why a particular person developed it.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:313:"स्तन कैंसर आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन, हार्मोनल प्रभाव, पर्यावरणीय कारणों और असामान्य कोशिका वृद्धि के कारण विकसित हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:392:"Risk increases with age. Other factors include a personal history of breast cancer or certain breast conditions, family history, inherited susceptibility, and dense breasts. Hormonal and reproductive history can influence risk. Alcohol use, excess weight after menopause, and physical inactivity are also associated with increased risk. Having a risk factor does not mean cancer will develop.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:311:"जोखिम कारकों में बढ़ती उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास, मोटापा, हार्मोनल प्रभाव, धूम्रपान, शराब और BRCA जीन उत्परिवर्तन शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:399:"Screening looks for cancer before symptoms appear; diagnostic evaluation investigates symptoms or an abnormal screening result. Evaluation may include examination, diagnostic mammography, ultrasound, or MRI when appropriate. A biopsy examines tissue to confirm cancer. After confirmation, tests assess tumor characteristics, including hormone receptors and HER2, and determine the extent of disease.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:217:"निदान के लिए मैमोग्राफी, अल्ट्रासाउंड, MRI, बायोप्सी और अन्य परीक्षण किए जा सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:398:"Risk reduction cannot guarantee prevention. Limiting alcohol, maintaining a healthy weight, and being physically active may reduce risk. People with a strong family history or known inherited susceptibility can discuss genetic assessment and appropriate risk-reduction options with a healthcare professional. Screening is intended to detect cancer early; it does not prevent cancer from developing.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:260:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, धूम्रपान और शराब से बचें, नियमित व्यायाम करें तथा समय-समय पर स्तन जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:391:"Breast cancer requires prompt medical evaluation for a new breast lump or other persistent breast or nipple changes. Seek assessment for a new or enlarging lump, nipple retraction, abnormal discharge, skin changes, or unexplained persistent breast symptoms. Emergency care is generally not required unless there is severe pain, significant bleeding, infection, or another acute complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:15;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:16;s:10:"disease_id";i:304;s:11:"overview_en";s:345:"Generalized anxiety disorder is a mental health condition characterized by excessive and persistent worry about everyday events or problems. The worry is difficult to control and may occur on most days for an extended period. Symptoms can include restlessness, irritability, muscle tension, fatigue, sleep problems, and difficulty concentrating.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:507:"जनरलाइज्ड एंग्जायटी डिसऑर्डर (GAD) एक मानसिक स्वास्थ्य विकार है जिसमें व्यक्ति सामान्य परिस्थितियों के बारे में अत्यधिक और लगातार चिंता करता रहता है। यह चिंता दैनिक जीवन को प्रभावित कर सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:359:"The exact cause of generalized anxiety disorder is not known. It is thought to result from a combination of genetic, biological, psychological, and environmental factors. Brain chemistry, inherited susceptibility, stressful life experiences, prolonged stress, trauma, and other mental health or medical conditions may contribute to persistent excessive worry.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:351:"इसका सटीक कारण पूरी तरह ज्ञात नहीं है। आनुवंशिक कारण, मस्तिष्क रसायन, लंबे समय का तनाव और जीवन की कठिन घटनाएं इसमें योगदान दे सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:374:"Risk may increase with a family history of anxiety or other mental health conditions, prolonged stress, traumatic experiences, certain personality or coping patterns, and other psychiatric conditions. Chronic medical problems and substance use may also contribute to persistent anxiety. Generalized anxiety disorder can develop even when no single risk factor is identified.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:301:"जोखिम कारकों में पारिवारिक इतिहास, लंबे समय का तनाव, जीवन की कठिन घटनाएं, नशा और कुछ चिकित्सीय स्थितियां शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:376:"Diagnosis is based on a clinical interview and assessment of excessive, difficult-to-control worry occurring on most days for at least six months, together with associated symptoms such as restlessness, fatigue, irritability, muscle tension, sleep problems, or difficulty concentrating. Clinicians may also assess for other mental health, medical, or substance-related causes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:264:"निदान मनोवैज्ञानिक मूल्यांकन, लक्षणों की समीक्षा और अन्य रोगों को बाहर करने के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:394:"Generalized anxiety disorder cannot always be prevented. Healthy sleep, regular physical activity, supportive relationships, stress-management skills, and avoiding excessive alcohol or drug use may support emotional well-being. People experiencing persistent or difficult-to-control worry should seek professional help early, particularly when anxiety begins to interfere with daily activities.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:284:"पर्याप्त नींद लें, नियमित व्यायाम करें, तनाव को नियंत्रित रखें और चिंता लगातार रहने पर विशेषज्ञ से सलाह लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:432:"Generalized anxiety disorder should be professionally assessed when excessive or persistent worry interferes with daily activities, sleep, work, relationships, or functioning. Seek prompt care when symptoms substantially worsen or become difficult to manage. Emergency assessment is appropriate for immediate safety concerns, severe inability to function, or physical symptoms that could represent another serious medical condition.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:16;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:17;s:10:"disease_id";i:361;s:11:"overview_en";s:350:"Type 1 diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition in which the immune system destroys the insulin-producing beta cells of the pancreas. As a result, the body produces little or no insulin, causing blood glucose levels to rise. Type 1 diabetes usually requires lifelong insulin treatment and regular monitoring of blood glucose to prevent complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:588:"टाइप 1 डायबिटीज मेलिटस एक दीर्घकालिक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जिसमें शरीर की प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली अग्न्याशय की इंसुलिन बनाने वाली कोशिकाओं को नष्ट कर देती है। इसके कारण शरीर पर्याप्त इंसुलिन नहीं बना पाता और रक्त शर्करा बढ़ जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:360:"Type 1 diabetes results from an autoimmune reaction in which the immune system mistakenly attacks and destroys pancreatic beta cells. The exact trigger is unknown. Genetic susceptibility appears to contribute, and certain environmental factors may help initiate the autoimmune process. The condition is not caused simply by eating sugar or by being overweight.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:418:"यह रोग मुख्य रूप से ऑटोइम्यून प्रक्रिया के कारण होता है जिसमें अग्न्याशय की बीटा कोशिकाएं नष्ट हो जाती हैं। आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारण भी योगदान दे सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:372:"Risk factors for type 1 diabetes include family history and genetic susceptibility. Having another autoimmune disease may also be associated with increased risk. The condition can develop at any age but often begins during childhood or adolescence. Environmental factors may influence development, but specific preventable lifestyle risk factors have not been established.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:249:"जोखिम कारकों में पारिवारिक इतिहास, आनुवंशिक कारक, ऑटोइम्यून रोग और पर्यावरणीय कारण शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:348:"Type 1 diabetes is diagnosed using blood glucose testing, including fasting glucose, random glucose, or an oral glucose tolerance test when appropriate. Hemoglobin A1c may help assess longer-term glucose levels. Autoantibody testing and measurement of C-peptide can help distinguish type 1 diabetes from other forms when the diagnosis is uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:245:"निदान के लिए फास्टिंग ब्लड शुगर, HbA1c, रैंडम ब्लड शुगर, ऑटोएंटीबॉडी और C-पेप्टाइड जांच की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:361:"There is currently no established lifestyle method that reliably prevents type 1 diabetes. Because the disease is caused by an autoimmune process, ordinary dietary habits or body weight do not directly prevent it. People with a strong family history or other risk factors may discuss research-based risk assessment and monitoring with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:292:"इसकी निश्चित रोकथाम नहीं है। समय पर निदान, इंसुलिन उपचार, संतुलित आहार और नियमित जांच जटिलताओं को कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:471:"Type 1 diabetes mellitus requires ongoing medical care and regular monitoring. Seek prompt assessment for persistent high or low blood glucose, repeated vomiting, dehydration, or unexplained worsening symptoms. Emergency medical attention is needed for diabetic ketoacidosis symptoms such as vomiting, abdominal pain, deep or rapid breathing, severe dehydration, confusion, or loss of consciousness, or for severe hypoglycemia with inability to safely take carbohydrates.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:17;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:18;s:10:"disease_id";i:59;s:11:"overview_en";s:356:"Hypothyroidism is a condition in which the thyroid gland does not produce enough thyroid hormone. Because thyroid hormones help regulate metabolism and many body functions, low levels can cause fatigue, feeling cold, constipation, weight gain, dry skin, muscle or joint symptoms, and a slower heart rate. It is more common with increasing age and in women.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:480:"हाइपोथायरॉइडिज्म एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें थायरॉयड ग्रंथि पर्याप्त थायरॉयड हार्मोन नहीं बनाती। इसके कारण थकान, वजन बढ़ना, कब्ज, त्वचा का सूखापन और ठंड अधिक लगना जैसे लक्षण हो सकते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:373:"The most common cause of hypothyroidism is thyroiditis, in which inflammation damages thyroid cells. Causes may include autoimmune attack, certain viral infections, pregnancy-related thyroiditis, medicines such as lithium or amiodarone, radiation treatment, radioactive iodine therapy, thyroid surgery, congenital abnormalities, and disorders affecting the pituitary gland.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:289:"सामान्य कारणों में ऑटोइम्यून थायरॉयड रोग, थायरॉयड सर्जरी, रेडियोथेरेपी, आयोडीन की कमी और कुछ दवाएं शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:320:"Risk of hypothyroidism is higher in women and people over age 50 and may increase with a personal or family history of thyroid disease or autoimmune disorders. Previous thyroid surgery, radiation treatment, radioactive iodine therapy, certain medicines, and some inherited or pituitary conditions can also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:274:"जोखिम कारकों में महिला होना, बढ़ती उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास, ऑटोइम्यून रोग और पूर्व थायरॉयड रोग शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:353:"Diagnosis of hypothyroidism usually involves blood tests measuring thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) and thyroid hormone levels such as free T4. Medical history and physical examination help identify symptoms and possible causes. Additional thyroid antibody or other testing may be used when an autoimmune cause or another thyroid disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:165:"निदान के लिए TSH, Free T4, थायरॉयड एंटीबॉडी और अन्य जांचें की जाती हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:362:"Some causes of hypothyroidism cannot be prevented. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to treatments or medicines that can affect thyroid function, following medical advice during thyroid treatment, and attending recommended follow-up can help reduce complications. People with thyroid or autoimmune conditions should follow appropriate monitoring and treatment plans.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:228:"पर्याप्त आयोडीन लें, जोखिम होने पर नियमित जांच करवाएं और चिकित्सकीय सलाह का पालन करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:297:"Hypothyroidism usually develops gradually and does not require emergency care. Seek urgent medical attention for severe drowsiness, confusion, very low body temperature, slow breathing, loss of consciousness, or rapidly worsening symptoms, particularly in someone with known severe hypothyroidism.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:18;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:19;s:10:"disease_id";i:60;s:11:"overview_en";s:389:"Hyperthyroidism occurs when the thyroid gland produces more thyroid hormone than the body needs. The excess hormone can increase metabolism and cause symptoms such as rapid or irregular heartbeat, nervousness, sweating, heat intolerance, weight loss, tremor, and difficulty sleeping. Some people have few noticeable symptoms, while severe untreated disease can cause serious complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:597:"हाइपरथायरॉइडिज्म एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें थायरॉयड ग्रंथि अत्यधिक मात्रा में थायरॉयड हार्मोन बनाती है। इससे शरीर का मेटाबॉलिज्म बढ़ जाता है और वजन कम होना, धड़कन तेज होना, घबराहट, कंपकंपी और अधिक पसीना आना जैसे लक्षण हो सकते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:425:"The most common cause of hyperthyroidism is Graves disease, an autoimmune disorder in which antibodies stimulate the thyroid to produce excess hormone. Other causes include toxic multinodular goiter, toxic thyroid nodules, thyroid inflammation, excessive iodine exposure, and excessive thyroid hormone medication. Rarely, pituitary or other disorders can contribute. The appropriate treatment depends on the underlying cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:282:"सामान्य कारणों में ग्रेव्स रोग, थायरॉयड नोड्यूल, थायरॉयडाइटिस, अत्यधिक आयोडीन सेवन और कुछ दवाएं शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:389:"Risk factors for hyperthyroidism depend on the underlying cause. Graves disease is more common in people with a family history of thyroid or autoimmune disorders and may be associated with other autoimmune conditions. Older age increases the likelihood of toxic thyroid nodules. Excess iodine exposure and certain medicines can also trigger thyroid overactivity in susceptible individuals.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:270:"जोखिम कारकों में महिला होना, पारिवारिक इतिहास, ऑटोइम्यून रोग, धूम्रपान और पूर्व थायरॉयड रोग शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:464:"Diagnosis of hyperthyroidism usually begins with a medical history and physical examination followed by thyroid blood tests. A low thyroid-stimulating hormone level with elevated thyroid hormone levels supports the diagnosis. Additional testing may include thyroid antibody tests, radioactive iodine uptake studies, or thyroid ultrasound to identify the cause. The choice of testing depends on symptoms, examination findings, and the suspected underlying disorder.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:177:"निदान के लिए TSH, Free T4, Free T3, थायरॉयड एंटीबॉडी तथा अन्य जांचें की जाती हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:454:"Some causes of hyperthyroidism cannot be prevented. Avoiding unnecessary excessive iodine exposure and taking thyroid medicines only as prescribed may reduce preventable causes. People with thyroid disease should attend recommended follow-up appointments and report new symptoms such as persistent palpitations, unexplained weight loss, tremor, or heat intolerance. Appropriate treatment of the underlying thyroid disorder can help prevent complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:243:"अनावश्यक आयोडीन सप्लीमेंट से बचें, धूम्रपान न करें और लक्षण होने पर चिकित्सकीय जांच करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:281:"Seek urgent medical attention for a very rapid or irregular heartbeat, severe chest pain, fainting, marked agitation or confusion, high fever, severe weakness, vomiting, or rapidly worsening symptoms. These may indicate a serious complication of excessive thyroid hormone activity.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:19;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:20;s:10:"disease_id";i:83;s:11:"overview_en";s:361:"A heart attack occurs when blood flow to part of the heart muscle becomes blocked, preventing the affected tissue from receiving enough oxygen. Without prompt treatment, the heart muscle can become permanently damaged. Symptoms may include chest pressure or discomfort, shortness of breath, sweating, nausea, or pain that spreads to the arm, back, neck, or jaw.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:460:"हार्ट अटैक (मायोकार्डियल इंफार्क्शन) तब होता है जब हृदय की मांसपेशियों तक रक्त प्रवाह अचानक रुक जाता है। समय पर उपचार न मिलने पर हृदय की मांसपेशियों को स्थायी क्षति हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:342:"Most heart attacks occur when a coronary artery becomes blocked by a blood clot that forms over a ruptured or damaged cholesterol-containing plaque. Less commonly, a heart attack can result from severe coronary artery spasm, a tear in a coronary artery, or other conditions that suddenly reduce blood flow and oxygen delivery to heart muscle.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:312:"सबसे सामान्य कारण कोरोनरी धमनियों में कोलेस्ट्रॉल जमा होना है। रक्त का थक्का बनकर रक्त प्रवाह को पूरी तरह रोक सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:343:"Risk of heart attack increases with smoking, high blood pressure, high cholesterol, diabetes, obesity, physical inactivity, increasing age, and a family history of coronary artery disease. Previous cardiovascular disease also increases risk. Some risk factors can be modified, while others, including age and family history, cannot be changed.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:330:"जोखिम कारकों में धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, उच्च रक्तचाप, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल, मोटापा, तनाव, पारिवारिक इतिहास और व्यायाम की कमी शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:362:"Diagnosis of a heart attack requires urgent clinical assessment. Doctors may use an electrocardiogram to look for changes in the heart's electrical activity and blood tests, especially cardiac troponin, to detect heart muscle injury. Echocardiography, coronary angiography, or other imaging may be used to determine the extent and location of blockage or damage.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:208:"निदान के लिए ECG, ट्रोपोनिन टेस्ट, इकोकार्डियोग्राफी और एंजियोग्राफी की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:379:"Heart attack risk can be reduced by not smoking, maintaining a healthy weight, exercising regularly, eating a heart-healthy diet, and controlling blood pressure, cholesterol, and diabetes. Taking prescribed cardiovascular medicines as directed and attending recommended medical follow-up can also reduce risk. Some risk factors, such as age and family history, cannot be changed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:241:"धूम्रपान से बचें, रक्तचाप और मधुमेह नियंत्रित रखें, स्वस्थ आहार लें और नियमित व्यायाम करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:296:"A heart attack is a medical emergency. Seek emergency medical care immediately for chest pressure or pain, shortness of breath, cold sweating, nausea, fainting, or pain spreading to the arm, shoulder, back, neck, or jaw. Do not delay emergency evaluation even if symptoms are mild or come and go.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:20;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:21;s:10:"disease_id";i:61;s:11:"overview_en";s:445:"Goiter is an enlargement of the thyroid gland, which is located at the front of the neck and produces hormones that regulate metabolism. A goiter may involve the entire thyroid gland or may occur with one or more thyroid nodules. Some people have no symptoms other than visible or palpable enlargement of the neck. A large goiter can sometimes press on the windpipe or esophagus and cause breathing, coughing, hoarseness, or swallowing problems.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:361:"उच्च रक्तचाप एक दीर्घकालिक स्थिति है जिसमें रक्तचाप लगातार बढ़ा रहता है। इससे हृदय रोग, स्ट्रोक और गुर्दे की बीमारी का जोखिम बढ़ जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:479:"Iodine deficiency is an important cause of simple goiter because the thyroid needs iodine to produce thyroid hormones. Other causes include autoimmune thyroid diseases, medicines such as lithium or amiodarone, certain infections, smoking, and thyroid nodules that produce excessive hormone. Goiter can also occur when the thyroid is underactive or overactive. The cause therefore needs to be evaluated rather than assuming that every enlarged thyroid is due to iodine deficiency.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:246:"कारणों में आनुवंशिकता, मोटापा, अधिक नमक, तनाव, गुर्दे की बीमारी और अस्वस्थ जीवनशैली शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:458:"Risk factors vary according to the underlying cause. Being over age 40, having a family history of goiter, and living or having grown up in an area where iodine deficiency occurs can increase risk of some types. Women are more frequently affected by simple goiter. Autoimmune thyroid disease, certain medicines, smoking, and conditions that cause thyroid nodules or abnormal thyroid hormone production can also increase the likelihood of thyroid enlargement.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:222:"जोखिम कारकों में मोटापा, धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, पारिवारिक इतिहास और बढ़ती उम्र शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:474:"Evaluation of a goiter begins with examination of the neck and thyroid gland. Blood tests can measure thyroid-stimulating hormone and thyroid hormones such as free T4. Thyroid ultrasound can identify enlargement and examine nodules or other structural changes. A thyroid scan and radioactive iodine uptake study may be used in selected cases to assess thyroid function. If a nodule has suspicious features, a biopsy may be recommended to determine whether cancer is present.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:141:"निदान रक्तचाप माप और अन्य जांचों द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:506:"Adequate iodine intake can prevent many cases of simple goiter caused by iodine deficiency. Using iodized salt appropriately is an established way to maintain adequate iodine intake in populations where deficiency is a concern. Other causes, such as autoimmune thyroid disease or genetic susceptibility, cannot always be prevented. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to factors that affect thyroid function and obtaining medical evaluation for persistent neck swelling can help identify thyroid disorders early.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:202:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, नमक कम करें, नियमित व्यायाम करें और तनाव नियंत्रित रखें.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:261:"Seek prompt medical assessment for a rapidly enlarging neck swelling, new difficulty swallowing or breathing, significant voice changes, or symptoms that develop suddenly. Severe breathing difficulty or inability to swallow requires emergency medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:21;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:22;s:10:"disease_id";i:62;s:11:"overview_en";s:413:"Hashimoto thyroiditis is an autoimmune disorder in which the immune system attacks the thyroid gland. The resulting inflammation can gradually damage thyroid tissue and reduce production of thyroid hormones, causing an underactive thyroid, or hypothyroidism. Symptoms may develop slowly and include tiredness, weight gain, feeling cold, dry skin, constipation, muscle or joint aches, and difficulty concentrating.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:226:"स्ट्रोक तब होता है जब मस्तिष्क के किसी भाग में रक्त प्रवाह रुक जाता है या कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:410:"Hashimoto thyroiditis occurs when the immune system mistakenly produces an inflammatory response against thyroid tissue. The exact reason this happens is not fully understood. Genetic factors and other environmental influences appear to contribute. The autoimmune process can cause antibodies to target proteins in the thyroid, gradually damaging the gland and reducing its ability to produce thyroid hormones.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:223:"अधिकांश स्ट्रोक धमनियों के अवरुद्ध होने या मस्तिष्क में रक्तस्राव के कारण होते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:385:"Hashimoto thyroiditis is more common in women and can occur at any age, although it is often diagnosed in adulthood. A family history of thyroid or other autoimmune diseases can increase risk. Having another autoimmune condition may also increase the likelihood. Certain genetic and environmental factors contribute, although most people cannot identify a single cause for the disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:204:"जोखिम कारकों में उच्च रक्तचाप, मधुमेह, धूम्रपान, मोटापा और हृदय रोग शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:405:"Hashimoto thyroiditis is diagnosed using symptoms, a physical examination, and blood tests that measure thyroid hormone levels and thyroid-stimulating hormone. Tests for thyroid antibodies, particularly thyroid peroxidase antibodies, can support the diagnosis. A thyroid ultrasound may sometimes be used to evaluate the gland, especially when there is enlargement, a nodule, or another structural concern.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:156:"निदान के लिए न्यूरोलॉजिकल जांच, CT स्कैन और MRI किए जा सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:413:"There is no reliable way to prevent Hashimoto thyroiditis because its exact cause is not known. Maintaining a balanced diet and avoiding unnecessary excessive iodine intake can support normal thyroid function. People with a family history of thyroid or autoimmune disease should discuss symptoms with a healthcare professional. Regular monitoring is important when thyroid dysfunction has already been identified.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:171:"रक्तचाप नियंत्रित रखें, धूम्रपान छोड़ें और नियमित व्यायाम करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:304:"Hashimoto thyroiditis usually develops gradually and does not require emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for significant neck swelling, difficulty swallowing or breathing, severe weakness, confusion, or rapidly worsening symptoms suggesting significant thyroid dysfunction or another acute condition.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:22;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:23;s:10:"disease_id";i:63;s:11:"overview_en";s:411:"Graves disease is an autoimmune disorder in which the immune system causes the thyroid gland to become overactive, producing excessive thyroid hormones. This condition is called hyperthyroidism. Symptoms may include weight loss, rapid or irregular heartbeat, nervousness, sweating, heat intolerance, increased appetite, and trouble sleeping. Some people also develop eye problems known as Graves ophthalmopathy.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:162:"अस्थमा श्वसन नलिकाओं की एक दीर्घकालिक सूजन संबंधी बीमारी है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:405:"Graves disease develops when the immune system produces antibodies that stimulate the thyroid gland to make excessive amounts of thyroid hormones. The exact reason this abnormal immune response develops is not fully understood. Genetic susceptibility and environmental factors appear to contribute. The same immune-system abnormalities can also affect tissues around the eyes and, less commonly, the skin.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"कारणों में एलर्जी, आनुवंशिकता और पर्यावरणीय कारक शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:366:"Graves disease is more common in women and often occurs in adulthood, although it can affect people at other ages. A family history of Graves disease or other autoimmune disorders may increase risk. Genetic susceptibility interacts with environmental influences. Factors affecting immune function may also contribute to the development or worsening of the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:169:"जोखिम कारकों में एलर्जी, पारिवारिक इतिहास और प्रदूषण शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:395:"Graves disease is diagnosed using symptoms, physical examination, and blood tests that measure thyroid hormone levels and thyroid-stimulating hormone. Tests for thyroid-related antibodies can support the diagnosis. Depending on the situation, thyroid imaging or a radioactive iodine uptake test may be used to evaluate thyroid activity. Eye findings may also help identify Graves ophthalmopathy.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:149:"निदान फेफड़ों की जांच और लक्षणों के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:438:"There is no proven way to completely prevent Graves disease because its exact cause is not known. Maintaining regular medical care can help identify thyroid overactivity early, particularly in people with symptoms or a family history of thyroid disease. Avoiding tobacco is especially important because smoking can worsen thyroid-related eye disease. People with diagnosed Graves disease should follow their treatment and monitoring plan.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:162:"ट्रिगर्स से बचें, धूम्रपान न करें और उपचार योजना का पालन करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:319:"Graves disease usually requires medical management but is not generally an emergency. Seek urgent medical attention for a very rapid or irregular heartbeat, severe chest pain, fainting, high fever, marked agitation or confusion, severe weakness, or rapidly worsening symptoms, which may indicate a serious complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:23;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:24;s:10:"disease_id";i:64;s:11:"overview_en";s:331:"A thyroid nodule is a growth or lump within the thyroid gland, which is located at the front of the neck. Thyroid nodules are common and may occur as a single growth or as several nodules. Most are benign rather than cancerous. Some nodules contain fluid, while others are solid, and a small number produce excess thyroid hormones.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:209:"सीओपीडी एक प्रगतिशील फेफड़ों की बीमारी है जो सांस लेने में कठिनाई पैदा करती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:353:"Thyroid nodules usually result from an overgrowth of thyroid cells. The exact cause is not always known. Nodules may be associated with conditions such as Hashimoto disease or inadequate iodine intake. They may be benign or malignant and can be fluid-filled or solid. Some nodules produce thyroid hormones, while others do not affect hormone production.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:187:"मुख्य कारण लंबे समय तक धूम्रपान और प्रदूषित वायु के संपर्क में रहना है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:386:"The chance of developing a thyroid nodule increases with age, and nodules are more common in women. Factors that may raise concern for thyroid cancer include radiation exposure to the head or neck, a family history of thyroid cancer, a hard or fixed nodule, certain voice changes, and being very young or older in age. Male sex is also associated with a higher likelihood of malignancy.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:157:"जोखिम कारकों में धूम्रपान, प्रदूषण और बढ़ती उम्र शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:411:"A thyroid nodule is usually evaluated with a physical examination and thyroid tests. Ultrasound can show the size and characteristics of the nodule and help determine whether further evaluation is needed. Depending on the findings, a healthcare provider may recommend a thyroid scan, blood tests, or fine-needle aspiration to obtain cells for examination and determine whether the nodule is benign or cancerous.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:133:"निदान में स्पाइरोमेट्री और अन्य जांचें शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:406:"There is no reliable way to prevent most thyroid nodules because their exact causes are often unknown. Maintaining adequate iodine intake can help prevent thyroid problems related to iodine deficiency. People with known thyroid disease or risk factors such as previous neck radiation should follow recommended medical evaluation. New or enlarging neck lumps should be assessed by a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:159:"धूम्रपान छोड़ें, प्रदूषण से बचें और सक्रिय जीवनशैली अपनाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:243:"Most thyroid nodules are not emergencies. Seek prompt medical assessment for a rapidly enlarging neck lump, new difficulty breathing or swallowing, persistent hoarseness, significant neck pain or swelling, or other rapidly developing symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:24;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:25;s:10:"disease_id";i:65;s:11:"overview_en";s:346:"Thyroid cancer is cancer that develops in the cells of the thyroid gland, a small gland in the front of the neck that produces hormones involved in metabolism. Several types of thyroid cancer exist, including papillary, follicular, medullary, and anaplastic thyroid cancer. Many thyroid cancers are detected early and can be treated successfully.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:182:"निमोनिया फेफड़ों का संक्रमण है जिसमें वायुकोषों में सूजन हो जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:413:"The exact cause of most thyroid cancers is not known. Thyroid cancer develops when genetic changes cause thyroid cells to grow and divide abnormally. Some inherited genetic changes increase the risk of particular types of thyroid cancer. Exposure to high levels of radiation, particularly during childhood, is an established risk factor. Family history and certain inherited syndromes can also contribute to risk.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:180:"कारणों में बैक्टीरिया, वायरस और फंगस से होने वाले संक्रमण शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:339:"Risk factors include previous exposure to high levels of ionizing radiation, especially during childhood, a family history of thyroid cancer, and certain inherited genetic syndromes. Some thyroid disorders and conditions affecting the thyroid may also be associated with increased risk. Risk varies according to the type of thyroid cancer.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:182:"जोखिम कारकों में कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, धूम्रपान और बढ़ती उम्र शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:462:"Diagnosis of thyroid cancer usually begins with a physical examination and assessment of a thyroid lump or other neck abnormality. Ultrasound can help evaluate thyroid nodules. Blood tests may assess thyroid function, although thyroid hormone levels are often normal in people with thyroid cancer. Fine-needle aspiration biopsy can be used to examine cells from a suspicious nodule. Additional imaging or testing may be needed to determine the extent of disease.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:157:"निदान के लिए एक्स-रे, रक्त जांच और अन्य परीक्षण किए जाते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:439:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent thyroid cancer. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to ionizing radiation and using appropriate protection when radiation is medically necessary can reduce avoidable exposure. People with certain inherited syndromes or strong family histories may benefit from genetic counseling and appropriate medical monitoring. Children should receive radiation involving the head and neck only when medically indicated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:186:"टीकाकरण, स्वच्छता और धूम्रपान से बचाव निमोनिया रोकने में मदद करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:271:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for a thyroid or neck lump that persists or enlarges, new difficulty swallowing or breathing, persistent hoarseness, unexplained neck swelling, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Severe difficulty breathing requires emergency medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:25;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:26;s:10:"disease_id";i:66;s:11:"overview_en";s:399:"Thyroiditis is inflammation of the thyroid gland. Different forms can cause temporary release of thyroid hormones followed by low thyroid hormone levels, while other forms may cause persistent changes in thyroid function. Symptoms therefore vary and may include neck pain or tenderness, fatigue, changes in heart rate, heat or cold intolerance, weight changes, or symptoms of an underactive thyroid.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:234:"क्षय रोग (टीबी) एक संक्रामक जीवाणु संक्रमण है जो मुख्य रूप से फेफड़ों को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:406:"Thyroiditis has several forms and causes. Some forms occur after a viral illness and can produce a painful, inflamed thyroid. Other forms are related to autoimmune processes in which the immune system attacks thyroid tissue. Silent or postpartum thyroiditis can occur without significant thyroid pain. Certain medicines and other medical conditions can also contribute to inflammation of the thyroid gland.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:182:"टीबी माइकोबैक्टीरियम ट्यूबरकुलोसिस जीवाणु से होने वाला संक्रमण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:382:"Risk factors depend on the type of thyroiditis. A recent viral illness may precede subacute thyroiditis, while autoimmune thyroid disorders are associated with other immune-related conditions and family history. Postpartum thyroiditis can occur after pregnancy. Some medicines and treatments can also affect the thyroid and contribute to inflammation or changes in thyroid function.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:223:"जोखिम कारकों में संक्रमित व्यक्ति के संपर्क, HIV, कुपोषण, मधुमेह और धूम्रपान शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:465:"Diagnosis begins with symptoms, medical history, and examination of the thyroid gland. Blood tests can measure thyroid-stimulating hormone and thyroid hormone levels and may include tests for thyroid antibodies. Depending on the suspected type, a healthcare provider may use an ultrasound or other thyroid imaging and, in selected cases, tests of thyroid hormone uptake. The pattern of thyroid function over time can help distinguish different forms of thyroiditis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:161:"निदान हेतु बलगम जांच, एक्स-रे, GeneXpert तथा अन्य जांचें की जाती हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:442:"Thyroiditis cannot always be prevented because many forms are related to autoimmune processes, viral illnesses, or other factors that cannot be controlled. Appropriate management of underlying autoimmune or medical conditions and review of medicines that may affect the thyroid can help reduce complications. People who develop persistent symptoms of abnormal thyroid function should seek medical evaluation and follow recommended monitoring.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:165:"शीघ्र पहचान, टीकाकरण और पूर्ण उपचार रोग नियंत्रण में सहायक हैं.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:256:"Thyroiditis usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for significant neck pain or swelling, difficulty swallowing or breathing, a very rapid or irregular heartbeat, fainting, severe weakness, confusion, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:26;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:28;s:10:"disease_id";i:68;s:11:"overview_en";s:403:"Bronchitis is inflammation of the bronchial tubes, the airways that carry air to and from the lungs. It commonly develops after a respiratory infection and may cause cough, mucus production, chest discomfort, tiredness, and sometimes wheezing. Acute bronchitis usually improves as the infection clears, while persistent or recurrent symptoms may require evaluation for another underlying lung condition.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:231:"ऑस्टियोआर्थराइटिस जोड़ों की एक अपक्षयी बीमारी है जिसमें कार्टिलेज धीरे-धीरे घिसता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:401:"Acute bronchitis is most often caused by viruses that also cause common colds and influenza-like illnesses. Less commonly, bacteria may contribute. Irritation from tobacco smoke, air pollution, dust, fumes, or other airborne substances can worsen airway inflammation. The cough may continue after the original infection has improved because the airways can remain sensitive and inflamed for some time.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:164:"यह उम्र, मोटापा, जोड़ों की चोट और आनुवंशिक कारणों से हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:464:"Risk factors include recent respiratory infection, exposure to tobacco smoke, air pollution, dust, chemical fumes, and other airway irritants. People with asthma or other chronic lung conditions may experience more prolonged or severe respiratory symptoms. Older adults and individuals with weakened immune systems may also have greater risk of complications. Repeated occupational exposure to airborne irritants can contribute to recurrent bronchial inflammation.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:165:"जोखिम कारकों में बढ़ती उम्र, मोटापा और जोड़ों की चोट शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:451:"Acute bronchitis is usually diagnosed from the history of illness and a physical examination. A healthcare professional may assess the cough, breathing, chest sounds, fever, and other symptoms. Tests are not routinely needed when the presentation is typical. Chest imaging or other testing may be considered when pneumonia, asthma, chronic lung disease, or another condition is suspected, particularly when symptoms are severe, prolonged, or atypical.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:130:"निदान के लिए शारीरिक जांच और एक्स-रे किए जाते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:472:"Reducing exposure to tobacco smoke, secondhand smoke, air pollution, dust, and chemical fumes can help protect the airways. Hand hygiene and avoiding close contact with people who have respiratory infections may reduce exposure to viruses. Staying appropriately vaccinated against respiratory infections can also reduce some causes of illness. People with persistent cough, breathing difficulty, recurrent bronchitis, or concerning symptoms should seek medical evaluation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:118:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें और नियमित गतिविधि करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:267:"Acute bronchitis is usually not an emergency. Seek prompt medical assessment for significant difficulty breathing, chest pain, coughing up blood, persistent high fever, severe weakness, dehydration, or symptoms that are rapidly worsening or not improving as expected.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:27;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:29;s:10:"disease_id";i:69;s:11:"overview_en";s:362:"Pneumonia is an infection that causes inflammation in the air sacs of one or both lungs. The air sacs may fill with fluid or pus, causing symptoms such as cough, fever, chills, chest discomfort, and difficulty breathing. Pneumonia can be caused by bacteria, viruses, fungi, or other infectious organisms, and its severity can range from mild to life-threatening.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:223:"रूमेटॉइड आर्थराइटिस एक दीर्घकालिक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जो जोड़ों में सूजन पैदा करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:367:"Pneumonia may result from bacteria, viruses, fungi, or other microorganisms entering the respiratory system. Common causes vary according to age, health status, location, and exposure. Pneumonia may develop after another respiratory infection or when organisms are inhaled into the lungs. Aspiration of food, liquid, vomit, or other material can also cause pneumonia.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:155:"यह तब होता है जब प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली जोड़ों पर हमला करती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:359:"Risk factors for pneumonia include older age, very young age, weakened immune function, chronic lung or heart disease, diabetes, smoking, poor nutrition, and prolonged hospitalization. Difficulty swallowing or impaired consciousness can increase the risk of aspiration. Exposure to certain infectious organisms and crowded environments may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:193:"जोखिम कारकों में आनुवंशिकता, धूम्रपान और ऑटोइम्यून प्रवृत्ति शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:413:"Pneumonia is diagnosed using symptoms, a physical examination, and medical history. A healthcare professional may listen to the lungs for abnormal sounds. A chest X-ray or other imaging may help identify inflammation in the lungs. Depending on severity, additional tests such as blood tests, oxygen measurements, sputum testing, or other investigations may be needed to identify the cause or assess complications.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:113:"निदान हेतु रक्त जांच और इमेजिंग की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:366:"Pneumonia risk can be reduced through recommended vaccinations, regular hand hygiene, avoiding tobacco smoke, managing chronic medical conditions, maintaining good nutrition, and reducing exposure to people with respiratory infections when appropriate. People at higher risk should discuss recommended vaccines and preventive measures with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:147:"शीघ्र निदान और उपचार से जोड़ों की क्षति कम की जा सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:297:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe difficulty breathing, bluish or gray lips or skin, chest pain, confusion, fainting, severe weakness, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Older adults and people with serious underlying conditions may need prompt assessment even when symptoms appear less severe.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:28;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:30;s:10:"disease_id";i:70;s:11:"overview_en";s:426:"Tuberculosis, or TB, is an infectious disease caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis. It most often affects the lungs but can also affect other parts of the body. TB can occur as a latent infection, in which the bacteria remain in the body without causing illness, or as active tuberculosis, which causes symptoms and can spread to others. Active lung TB commonly causes a persistent cough, fever, night sweats, and weight loss.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:142:"सोरायसिस त्वचा की एक दीर्घकालिक ऑटोइम्यून बीमारी है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:351:"Tuberculosis is caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis bacteria. The bacteria spread through the air when a person with active TB of the lungs or throat coughs, speaks, or sings. People nearby may breathe in the bacteria and become infected. Infection does not always lead to active disease because the immune system may keep the bacteria under control.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:231:"इसका सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं है, परंतु प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली और आनुवंशिकता की भूमिका होती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:401:"Risk of tuberculosis is higher after close or prolonged contact with someone who has active TB. People with weakened immune systems, including those with HIV infection, are at increased risk of developing active disease. Other factors include certain medical conditions, some medicines that suppress immunity, living or working in crowded settings, and residence or travel in areas where TB is common.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:186:"जोखिम कारकों में पारिवारिक इतिहास, तनाव, धूम्रपान और मोटापा शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"Tuberculosis is diagnosed using a medical history, physical examination, and tests for TB infection or disease. Skin tests and blood tests can identify immune responses to tuberculosis bacteria. If active TB is suspected, chest imaging and laboratory testing of respiratory samples may be used to detect the bacteria. Additional tests may be needed when TB affects organs outside the lungs.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:148:"निदान त्वचा परीक्षण और कभी-कभी बायोप्सी से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:412:"Tuberculosis can be prevented by identifying and treating TB infection before it progresses to active disease. People with active TB should follow treatment and infection-control advice to reduce transmission. Good ventilation and avoiding prolonged close exposure to infectious people can reduce airborne spread. In some countries, the BCG vaccine is used to help protect against severe forms of TB in children.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:165:"धूम्रपान से बचें, तनाव कम करें और चिकित्सकीय सलाह का पालन करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:343:"Tuberculosis requires medical evaluation and appropriate treatment. Seek urgent care for severe difficulty breathing, coughing up significant amounts of blood, chest pain, confusion, severe weakness, or rapidly worsening illness. People with suspected infectious tuberculosis should follow medical advice about reducing transmission to others.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:29;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:31;s:10:"disease_id";i:71;s:11:"overview_en";s:602:"COPD, or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, is a common long-term lung disease that makes it difficult to move air in and out of the lungs. It includes chronic bronchitis, which causes long-term inflammation and mucus production in the airways, and emphysema, which damages the air sacs of the lungs. Many people have features of both conditions. COPD can cause persistent cough, mucus production, wheezing, shortness of breath and reduced ability to stay active. Lung damage caused by COPD is usually permanent, although treatment and lifestyle changes can reduce symptoms and slow further damage.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:233:"एक्जिमा एक दीर्घकालिक त्वचा रोग है जिसमें खुजली, लालिमा, सूखापन और त्वचा में जलन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:569:"Smoking is the main cause of COPD. The risk increases with the amount and duration of smoking, although not every smoker develops COPD. Long-term exposure to secondhand smoke, air pollution, workplace gases, fumes, dust and other lung irritants can also contribute. Frequent exposure to smoke from cooking fires without adequate ventilation may increase risk. A rare inherited deficiency of alpha-1 antitrypsin can cause emphysema even in people who have never smoked. COPD generally develops after prolonged exposure to factors that damage the airways and lung tissue.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:275:"एक्जिमा आनुवंशिक कारणों, प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली की गड़बड़ी, एलर्जी और पर्यावरणीय कारकों के कारण हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:577:"Important risk factors for COPD include current or past cigarette smoking, long-term exposure to secondhand smoke, air pollution, workplace dusts and chemical fumes, and repeated exposure to smoke from poorly ventilated cooking fires. Increasing age also raises the likelihood of developing COPD because the condition usually develops during middle age or later. A family history of COPD or inherited alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency can also increase risk. Repeated respiratory problems and other factors that damage the lungs may contribute to disease development or worsening.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:221:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, एलर्जी, तनाव, शुष्क त्वचा और पर्यावरणीय उत्तेजक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:601:"COPD is diagnosed from a medical history, symptoms and physical examination together with tests of lung function. The healthcare provider will ask about smoking and other exposures, cough, mucus production, breathing difficulty and activity limitations. Pulmonary function testing, particularly spirometry, can measure how well air moves through the lungs and help determine the degree of airflow obstruction. Additional tests such as chest imaging, oxygen measurements and blood tests may be used when needed to assess the lungs, identify complications or look for other causes of breathing problems.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:231:"निदान शारीरिक जांच, रोग इतिहास और आवश्यकता पड़ने पर एलर्जी परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:608:"Not smoking prevents most cases of COPD. People who smoke should consider quitting and should avoid secondhand smoke. Reducing exposure to workplace dust, chemical fumes, indoor smoke and outdoor air pollution can also protect the lungs. Good ventilation is important when cooking with fuels that produce smoke. Vaccination against influenza, pneumococcal disease and COVID-19 can help reduce respiratory infections that may worsen COPD. People with COPD should also follow their healthcare provider’s treatment plan, remain appropriately active and avoid known triggers that make breathing symptoms worse.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:223:"त्वचा को नम रखें, ट्रिगर्स से बचें, तनाव कम करें और सौम्य त्वचा उत्पादों का उपयोग करें.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:343:"Seek urgent medical attention for a significant worsening of breathlessness, severe wheezing, inability to speak normally because of breathing difficulty, bluish lips or face, confusion, unusual drowsiness, chest pain, or symptoms that do not improve with the person's prescribed treatment. Severe breathing difficulty requires emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:30;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:32;s:10:"disease_id";i:72;s:11:"overview_en";s:404:"Pulmonary fibrosis is a condition in which lung tissue becomes scarred and stiff. The scarring makes it harder for oxygen to move from the lungs into the blood and can gradually make breathing more difficult. Symptoms often develop slowly and may include shortness of breath, a persistent dry cough, tiredness, weakness, and reduced ability to exercise. The course varies depending on the cause and type.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:280:"फैटी लिवर रोग में यकृत कोशिकाओं में अत्यधिक वसा जमा हो जाती है जिससे यकृत की कार्यक्षमता प्रभावित होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:393:"Pulmonary fibrosis can have many causes. Some cases result from long-term exposure to substances such as asbestos, silica dust, certain chemicals, or other environmental and occupational irritants. Certain medicines, radiation therapy, autoimmune diseases, and some infections can also damage the lungs. In many people, no specific cause is found; this is called idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:234:"मोटापा, इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध, मधुमेह, शराब सेवन और अस्वस्थ आहार फैटी लिवर का कारण बन सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:373:"Risk factors for pulmonary fibrosis include older age, smoking, exposure to occupational or environmental dusts and chemicals, and certain autoimmune diseases. Some medicines and previous radiation treatment can increase risk. A family history of pulmonary fibrosis may also be relevant in some cases. Risk depends on the specific type of fibrosis and its underlying cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:221:"मोटापा, मधुमेह, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल, निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली और शराब सेवन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:395:"Pulmonary fibrosis is diagnosed using symptoms, medical history, physical examination, and lung tests. High-resolution CT imaging can show characteristic patterns of lung scarring. Pulmonary function tests measure lung capacity and gas exchange. Blood tests may help identify autoimmune or other causes. In selected cases, additional procedures such as bronchoscopy or lung biopsy may be needed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:254:"निदान में लिवर फंक्शन टेस्ट, अल्ट्रासाउंड, फाइब्रोस्कैन, सीटी स्कैन या एमआरआई शामिल हो सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:429:"Not all cases of pulmonary fibrosis can be prevented, particularly when the cause is unknown or related to inherited factors. Avoiding cigarette smoke and occupational exposure to asbestos, silica, dust, fumes, and other lung irritants can reduce risk. Appropriate respiratory protection should be used in hazardous workplaces. People taking medicines associated with lung injury should follow medical monitoring recommendations.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:198:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, नियमित व्यायाम करें, शराब से बचें और संतुलित आहार लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:272:"Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening breathlessness, a significant decline in exercise tolerance, new or worsening chest pain, coughing up blood, fainting, or rapidly worsening respiratory symptoms. Severe difficulty breathing requires emergency medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:31;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:33;s:10:"disease_id";i:73;s:11:"overview_en";s:397:"Lung cancer is cancer that begins in the tissues of the lungs, usually in cells lining the air passages. The two main types are non-small cell lung cancer and small cell lung cancer. Early lung cancer may cause few or no symptoms. As it develops, symptoms may include persistent cough, coughing up blood, chest discomfort, breathing problems, fatigue, loss of appetite, or unexplained weight loss.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:272:"पित्ताशय की पथरी कठोर जमाव होते हैं जो पित्ताशय में बनते हैं और दर्द तथा पाचन समस्याएं पैदा कर सकते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:403:"The most important cause of lung cancer is tobacco smoking. Tobacco smoke contains cancer-causing substances that can damage lung cells over time. Lung cancer can also occur in people who have never smoked. Other contributors include secondhand smoke and exposure to substances such as asbestos, arsenic, chromium, beryllium, nickel, soot, and tar. Genetic and environmental factors can also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:258:"पित्ताशय की पथरी अधिक कोलेस्ट्रॉल, बिलीरुबिन असंतुलन या पित्ताशय के ठीक से खाली न होने से बनती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:394:"Smoking is the major risk factor for lung cancer, and risk increases with the number of years and amount of tobacco exposure. Secondhand smoke also increases risk. Other factors include occupational exposure to certain cancer-causing substances, a family history of lung cancer, and previous radiation exposure to the chest. Age is also associated with increased risk of developing the disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:218:"मोटापा, महिला लिंग, उम्र, गर्भावस्था, मधुमेह और उच्च वसा वाला आहार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:414:"Lung cancer is evaluated using symptoms, medical history, and physical examination followed by appropriate tests. Imaging such as chest X-rays or computed tomography scans can identify abnormal areas in the lungs. Additional tests may determine whether cancer has spread. A biopsy, in which a sample of abnormal tissue is examined, is generally needed to confirm the diagnosis and identify the type of lung cancer.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:205:"निदान आमतौर पर पेट के अल्ट्रासाउंड और अन्य इमेजिंग परीक्षणों से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:411:"The most effective way to reduce the risk of lung cancer is to avoid smoking or quit smoking if you currently smoke. Avoiding secondhand smoke can also reduce exposure. Workplace safety measures can reduce contact with asbestos and other cancer-causing substances. People with substantial smoking histories may be eligible for lung cancer screening with low-dose CT according to current medical recommendations.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:180:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, तेजी से वजन कम करने से बचें और संतुलित आहार लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:312:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for persistent or worsening cough, coughing up blood, unexplained weight loss, persistent chest pain, worsening breathlessness, or other concerning symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe difficulty breathing, significant bleeding, severe chest pain, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:32;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:34;s:10:"disease_id";i:74;s:11:"overview_en";s:417:"COVID-19 is an illness caused by the coronavirus SARS-CoV-2. It spreads mainly when an infected person breathes out respiratory droplets and very small particles containing the virus. Illness can range from mild to severe, and some people develop complications or longer-lasting symptoms after the initial infection. Testing, vaccination, and appropriate medical care are important parts of prevention and management.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:204:"गुर्दे की पथरी कठोर खनिज जमाव होते हैं जो गुर्दों और मूत्र मार्ग में बनते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:426:"COVID-19 is caused by infection with SARS-CoV-2, a coronavirus that primarily spreads through respiratory particles released by an infected person. Transmission is more likely during close contact and in situations where infected particles accumulate in indoor air. People may spread the virus before symptoms appear or when they have few symptoms, making transmission possible even when someone does not appear seriously ill.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:249:"निर्जलीकरण, अतिरिक्त खनिज, आहार संबंधी कारक और चयापचय विकार गुर्दे की पथरी का कारण बन सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:412:"The risk of severe COVID-19 increases with older age and certain underlying medical conditions. Risk can also be affected by immune-system problems and other factors that make it harder for the body to fight infection. Previous vaccination or infection can provide protection against severe disease, although protection changes over time. Exposure to an infected person increases the chance of becoming infected.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:225:"कम पानी पीना, मोटापा, अधिक नमक वाला आहार, पारिवारिक इतिहास और कुछ रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:411:"COVID-19 is diagnosed using tests that detect SARS-CoV-2 infection. Testing may be recommended when symptoms develop or after an appropriate exposure, depending on the situation. Common symptoms can include fever, cough, tiredness, sore throat, congestion, and changes in taste or smell, although symptoms vary. Healthcare providers consider symptoms, exposure history, and test results when evaluating illness.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:202:"निदान में मूत्र परीक्षण, रक्त परीक्षण, अल्ट्रासाउंड और सीटी स्कैन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:387:"COVID-19 risk can be reduced by staying up to date with recommended vaccines, improving indoor ventilation, and avoiding close contact with people known to be infected. Staying home when sick and following current public-health guidance can reduce transmission. People at higher risk of severe disease should discuss prevention and early treatment options with their healthcare provider.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:196:"पर्याप्त पानी पिएं, नमक कम करें और चिकित्सकीय आहार निर्देशों का पालन करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:320:"Seek urgent medical attention for significant difficulty breathing, persistent chest pain or pressure, new confusion, inability to stay awake, bluish or gray lips or face, severe dehydration, or rapidly worsening symptoms. People at higher risk of complications should seek medical advice promptly when symptoms develop.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:33;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:35;s:10:"disease_id";i:75;s:11:"overview_en";s:308:"Pleural effusion is an abnormal buildup of fluid between the layers of tissue surrounding the lungs. It may occur because of heart failure, infection, inflammation, cancer, liver or kidney disease, or other conditions. The amount of fluid and its underlying cause determine the symptoms and treatment needed.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:206:"जीईआरडी एक पाचन विकार है जिसमें पेट का अम्ल बार-बार भोजन नली में वापस आ जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:368:"Pleural effusion can occur when fluid leaks into the pleural space because of increased pressure in blood vessels or low blood protein levels, or when inflammation, infection, blocked vessels, lung injury, or tumors interfere with normal fluid balance. Heart failure is a common cause of transudative effusion, while infections and cancer can cause exudative effusion.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:256:"कमजोर निचला इसोफेजियल स्फिंक्टर, मोटापा, धूम्रपान और आहार संबंधी आदतें जीईआरडी का कारण बनती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:303:"Risk depends on the underlying cause. Factors associated with pleural effusion include heart, liver, or kidney disease, cancer, infections, lung injury, smoking, alcohol use, and previous exposure to asbestos. The presence of these factors does not necessarily mean that a pleural effusion will develop.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:184:"मोटापा, धूम्रपान, शराब सेवन, गर्भावस्था और भारी भोजन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:346:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, and imaging such as a chest X-ray or ultrasound. When the cause is uncertain, thoracentesis may be performed to remove and analyze pleural fluid. Laboratory testing of the fluid can help distinguish different causes, including infection, inflammation, heart-related fluid buildup, and cancer.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:221:"निदान में लक्षण मूल्यांकन, एंडोस्कोपी, पीएच मॉनिटरिंग और इमेजिंग शामिल हो सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:375:"Pleural effusion cannot always be prevented because it often results from another disease. Reducing the risk and complications of conditions that can cause fluid buildup may help. Avoiding tobacco, managing heart, liver, or kidney disease, treating infections appropriately, and seeking medical evaluation for persistent breathing symptoms can help address underlying causes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:240:"ट्रिगर खाद्य पदार्थों से बचें, स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, धूम्रपान छोड़ें और देर रात भोजन न करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:340:"Pleural effusion requires medical assessment because the underlying cause can vary. Seek urgent care for worsening shortness of breath, significant chest pain, fainting, severe weakness, fever with rapidly worsening illness, or other signs of serious infection or respiratory compromise. Severe breathing difficulty requires emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:34;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:36;s:10:"disease_id";i:76;s:11:"overview_en";s:454:"Sleep apnea is a disorder in which breathing repeatedly stops or becomes very shallow during sleep. The most common form is obstructive sleep apnea, which occurs when the upper airway becomes blocked or narrowed during sleep. Another form, central sleep apnea, occurs when the brain does not send appropriate signals to the muscles that control breathing. Symptoms may include loud snoring, pauses in breathing, daytime sleepiness, and morning headaches.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:241:"पेप्टिक अल्सर रोग एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें पेट या छोटी आंत की अंदरूनी परत में घाव बन जाते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:398:"Obstructive sleep apnea occurs when the muscles and tissues of the upper airway relax during sleep and block airflow. Enlarged tonsils or other anatomical features can contribute. Central sleep apnea results from problems with the brain signals that control breathing and may occur with certain medical conditions or medicines. Some people have a combination of obstructive and central sleep apnea.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:259:"अधिकांश अल्सर हेलिकोबैक्टर पाइलोरी संक्रमण या लंबे समय तक दर्द निवारक दवाओं के उपयोग से होते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:399:"Risk factors for obstructive sleep apnea include excess body weight, a larger neck circumference, certain facial or airway structures, older age, and a family history of the disorder. Alcohol and sedating medicines can worsen airway obstruction during sleep. Smoking may also increase risk. Central sleep apnea is associated with certain heart, brain, and medical conditions and with some medicines.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:275:"धूम्रपान, शराब सेवन, दीर्घकालिक तनाव, एच. पाइलोरी संक्रमण और दर्द निवारक दवाओं का उपयोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:383:"Sleep apnea is evaluated using symptoms, sleep history, and information from a sleep partner when available. A sleep study can monitor breathing, oxygen levels, heart rate, and other body functions during sleep. Testing may be performed in a sleep center or, for some people, at home. The results help determine whether apnea is present and what type and severity of disorder exists.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:230:"निदान में एंडोस्कोपी, एच. पाइलोरी परीक्षण, रक्त परीक्षण और मल परीक्षण शामिल हो सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:421:"Maintaining a healthy weight can reduce the risk of obstructive sleep apnea or lessen its severity. Avoiding alcohol and sedating medicines before sleep, when medically appropriate, can also help. Sleeping on the side may reduce airway obstruction in some people. Avoiding tobacco and treating nasal or other airway problems can support healthy breathing during sleep. People with symptoms should seek medical evaluation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:218:"धूम्रपान, अत्यधिक शराब, अनावश्यक दर्द निवारक दवाओं से बचें तथा स्वच्छता बनाए रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:276:"Sleep apnea generally requires medical evaluation but is not usually an emergency. Seek prompt assessment for severe daytime sleepiness causing safety problems, worsening breathing symptoms, chest pain, fainting, significant heart rhythm symptoms, or other concerning changes.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:35;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:37;s:10:"disease_id";i:77;s:11:"overview_en";s:389:"Emphysema is a chronic lung disease in which the air sacs, or alveoli, in the lungs become damaged. The damaged air sacs lose their ability to exchange air efficiently, making it difficult to breathe. Emphysema is a form of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, or COPD. Symptoms usually develop gradually and include shortness of breath, cough, wheezing, and reduced ability to exercise.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:281:"डेंगू मच्छरों से फैलने वाला वायरल संक्रमण है जो बुखार, शरीर दर्द और कभी-कभी गंभीर जटिलताएं उत्पन्न करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:381:"Long-term exposure to cigarette smoke is the most common cause of emphysema. Tobacco smoke damages the walls of the lung air sacs and causes ongoing inflammation. Long-term exposure to secondhand smoke, air pollution, and certain workplace dusts or chemicals can also contribute. A small number of people develop emphysema because of an inherited deficiency of alpha-1 antitrypsin.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:147:"डेंगू वायरस संक्रमित एडीज मच्छरों के काटने से फैलता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:387:"Smoking is the major risk factor for emphysema, and risk increases with the amount and duration of tobacco exposure. Long-term exposure to secondhand smoke, air pollution, chemical fumes, and dust can also increase risk. Older age is associated with greater risk because lung damage accumulates over time. An inherited alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency can cause emphysema at a younger age.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:253:"डेंगू प्रभावित क्षेत्रों में रहना, मच्छरों के संपर्क में आना और खराब नियंत्रण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:350:"Emphysema is evaluated using symptoms, medical history, and a physical examination. Doctors may perform pulmonary function tests to measure how well the lungs move air. Chest X-rays or CT scans can show structural changes in the lungs. Blood tests may be used to check oxygen levels or, in selected people, to look for alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:209:"निदान रक्त परीक्षण जैसे एनएस1 एंटीजन और डेंगू एंटीबॉडी परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:414:"The most effective way to prevent emphysema is not to smoke and to stop smoking as early as possible. Avoiding secondhand smoke and limiting exposure to workplace dust, fumes, and chemical irritants can also protect lung health. Good control of other respiratory conditions and maintaining physical activity can support lung function. People with occupational exposures should use recommended protective equipment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:188:"मच्छरों के काटने से बचें, रुके हुए पानी को हटाएं और सुरक्षा उपाय अपनाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:268:"Seek urgent medical attention for a significant worsening of breathlessness, severe wheezing, bluish lips or face, confusion, chest pain, coughing up blood, or symptoms that do not improve with prescribed treatment. Severe difficulty breathing requires emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:36;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:38;s:10:"disease_id";i:78;s:11:"overview_en";s:357:"Whooping cough, also called pertussis, is a highly contagious respiratory infection caused by bacteria. It is characterized by repeated, severe coughing fits that may make it difficult to breathe. After a coughing spell, a person may make a whooping sound when breathing in or may vomit. The infection can be especially serious in babies and young children.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:179:"मलेरिया एक मच्छरजनित रोग है जो प्लास्मोडियम परजीवी के कारण होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:394:"Whooping cough is caused by the bacterium Bordetella pertussis. The bacteria spread from an infected person through respiratory droplets released when coughing or sneezing. A person can spread the infection before the characteristic coughing fits become obvious. Close contact with an infected person increases the chance of transmission, particularly when vaccination protection has decreased.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:156:"मलेरिया संक्रमित मादा एनोफिलीज मच्छर के काटने से फैलता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:366:"People who have not received recommended pertussis vaccinations are at greater risk of developing whooping cough. Protection can also decrease over time after vaccination. Infants who are too young to have completed their vaccinations are particularly vulnerable to severe disease. Close household or community exposure to an infected person also increases the risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:253:"प्रभावित क्षेत्रों की यात्रा, मच्छर नियंत्रण की कमी और सुरक्षा उपायों का अभाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:372:"Whooping cough is diagnosed from the symptoms, medical history, and physical examination. The characteristic prolonged coughing fits can provide an important clue. A healthcare provider may collect a sample from the nose or throat for laboratory testing to detect Bordetella pertussis. Testing can help confirm the infection, especially during the early stages of illness.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:185:"निदान रक्त स्लाइड परीक्षण और रैपिड मलेरिया टेस्ट द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:390:"Vaccination is the main way to prevent whooping cough. Recommended pertussis-containing vaccines provide protection and are given according to age-based immunization schedules, with booster doses recommended at appropriate ages. Avoiding close contact with infected people and following medical advice when illness occurs can also reduce transmission. Early treatment may help limit spread.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:205:"मच्छरदानी, रिपेलेंट का उपयोग करें और मच्छरों के प्रजनन स्थलों को समाप्त करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:313:"Seek urgent medical attention for significant breathing difficulty, pauses in breathing, bluish lips or face, repeated vomiting with inability to maintain fluids, severe weakness, dehydration, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Infants and people at higher risk of complications may require prompt medical assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:37;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:39;s:10:"disease_id";i:79;s:11:"overview_en";s:312:"Acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) is a serious lung condition in which widespread inflammation and fluid buildup in the lungs make it difficult for oxygen to pass into the blood. It can develop rapidly after severe illness or injury and may cause severe breathing difficulty and low blood oxygen levels.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:251:"टाइफाइड साल्मोनेला टाइफी जीवाणु के कारण होने वाला संक्रमण है जो दूषित भोजन और पानी से फैलता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:377:"ARDS can develop when a serious illness or injury causes widespread inflammation and damage in the lungs. Common triggers include severe infections such as sepsis or pneumonia, major trauma, aspiration of stomach contents, and other conditions that injure lung tissue. The resulting inflammation increases leakage of fluid into the air sacs and interferes with oxygen exchange.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:120:"दूषित भोजन या पानी के सेवन से टाइफाइड होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:296:"Risk is increased by conditions that can severely injure or inflame the lungs, including sepsis, severe pneumonia, major trauma, aspiration, and other serious illnesses. The likelihood of ARDS is also influenced by the severity of the underlying condition and the extent of systemic inflammation.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:178:"खराब स्वच्छता, असुरक्षित पेयजल और अपर्याप्त सफाई जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:337:"Diagnosis of ARDS is based on severe breathing difficulty, low blood oxygen levels, clinical history, physical examination, and chest imaging. Chest X-rays or other imaging may show widespread lung abnormalities. Healthcare professionals also evaluate the underlying illness and exclude other causes of lung fluid or respiratory failure.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:173:"निदान में रक्त कल्चर, मल परीक्षण और सीरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:370:"ARDS cannot always be prevented because it can result from severe illness or injury. Prompt treatment of serious infections, careful management of conditions that can lead to severe lung injury, avoiding aspiration when possible, and appropriate medical care after major trauma may reduce risk or severity. Early recognition of worsening breathing problems is important.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:189:"सुरक्षित पानी पिएं, स्वच्छता बनाए रखें और आवश्यक होने पर टीकाकरण कराएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:290:"Acute respiratory distress syndrome is a medical emergency requiring hospital treatment. Seek emergency medical care for severe difficulty breathing, rapidly worsening breathlessness, bluish or gray skin or lips, confusion, extreme drowsiness, or inability to maintain adequate oxygenation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:38;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:40;s:10:"disease_id";i:80;s:11:"overview_en";s:400:"Bronchiectasis is a long-term lung condition in which the airways become permanently widened and damaged. Damaged airways do not clear mucus normally, allowing mucus and bacteria to accumulate and causing repeated lung infections. Symptoms may include a persistent cough, large amounts of mucus or phlegm, shortness of breath, wheezing, chest discomfort, fatigue, and repeated respiratory infections.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:277:"हेपेटाइटिस बी एक वायरल संक्रमण है जो यकृत को प्रभावित करता है और अनुपचारित रहने पर दीर्घकालिक हो सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:407:"Bronchiectasis can develop after repeated or severe lung infections or other conditions that damage the airways. Causes include certain childhood infections, cystic fibrosis, immune-system disorders, inflammatory diseases, and conditions that interfere with normal mucus clearance. Sometimes no specific cause is found. Inhaled foreign material or obstruction of an airway can also contribute in some cases.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:216:"हेपेटाइटिस बी वायरस संक्रमित रक्त, शारीरिक द्रवों और मां से बच्चे में फैल सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:423:"Risk factors for bronchiectasis include previous severe or repeated respiratory infections, cystic fibrosis, immune-system problems, inflammatory diseases, and conditions that interfere with airway clearance. Risk may also increase with certain structural lung abnormalities and long-term exposure to irritants. Older age can be associated with increased risk, particularly when other lung or immune conditions are present.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:245:"असुरक्षित यौन संबंध, सुई साझा करना, स्वास्थ्य सेवा संपर्क और टीकाकरण की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:387:"Bronchiectasis is evaluated using symptoms, medical history, and a physical examination. A chest CT scan is commonly used because it can show widening and structural damage of the airways. Lung function tests can measure breathing ability. Sputum may be tested to identify bacteria or other organisms causing infection. Additional blood tests may be used to look for an underlying cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:269:"निदान रक्त परीक्षणों द्वारा किया जाता है जो हेपेटाइटिस बी मार्कर और यकृत कार्य का मूल्यांकन करते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:443:"Preventing respiratory infections and treating them promptly can help reduce lung damage that may lead to bronchiectasis. Recommended vaccinations, including those against influenza and pneumococcal disease, can help protect against important infections. Avoiding tobacco smoke and other lung irritants is important. People with an underlying condition should follow treatment plans designed to maintain airway clearance and reduce infections.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:228:"टीकाकरण, सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार और संक्रमित रक्त से बचाव संक्रमण रोकने में मदद करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:308:"Seek prompt medical assessment for a significant increase in coughing or sputum, coughing up blood, worsening breathlessness, fever with deterioration, chest pain, or symptoms suggesting a serious infection. Large amounts of blood, severe breathing difficulty, or sudden deterioration require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:39;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:41;s:10:"disease_id";i:82;s:11:"overview_en";s:422:"Coronary artery disease is a condition in which the arteries supplying blood to the heart become narrowed or blocked, most commonly because of atherosclerosis. Reduced blood flow can cause chest discomfort or angina, especially during exertion. If a coronary artery becomes suddenly blocked, a heart attack can occur. Some people have coronary artery disease without noticeable symptoms until the disease becomes advanced.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:227:"कोरोनरी धमनी रोग में हृदय की धमनियां संकरी हो जाती हैं जिससे रक्त प्रवाह कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:437:"Coronary artery disease most commonly develops when cholesterol, fat, calcium, and other substances accumulate in the walls of the coronary arteries and form atherosclerotic plaques. These plaques can gradually narrow the arteries and restrict blood flow. A plaque can also rupture and form a blood clot that suddenly blocks an artery. Less common causes include coronary artery spasm and other conditions affecting the coronary vessels.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:147:"यह मुख्यतः धमनियों में कोलेस्ट्रॉल जमा होने से होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:379:"Risk factors include high blood pressure, high LDL cholesterol, diabetes, cigarette smoking, obesity, physical inactivity, unhealthy dietary patterns, increasing age, and a family history of premature heart disease. Chronic kidney disease and certain inflammatory conditions can also increase risk. The overall risk is influenced by the combination and duration of these factors.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:256:"धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, मोटापा, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल, उच्च रक्तचाप और निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:428:"Coronary artery disease is evaluated using medical history, symptoms, physical examination, and cardiovascular risk assessment. Tests may include an electrocardiogram, blood tests, echocardiography, exercise or pharmacologic stress testing, and coronary CT angiography. In selected patients, invasive coronary angiography may be used to directly assess the coronary arteries and determine the severity and location of blockages.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:206:"निदान में ईसीजी, स्ट्रेस टेस्ट, इकोकार्डियोग्राफी और एंजियोग्राफी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:457:"The risk of coronary artery disease can be reduced by not smoking, maintaining a healthy weight, exercising regularly, eating a heart-healthy diet, and controlling blood pressure, cholesterol, and blood glucose. Taking prescribed medicines consistently and attending recommended medical checkups are important when risk factors are present. Limiting tobacco exposure and maintaining healthy sleep and lifestyle habits can also support cardiovascular health.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:266:"नियमित व्यायाम करें, वजन नियंत्रित रखें, धूम्रपान से बचें तथा रक्तचाप और कोलेस्ट्रॉल नियंत्रित रखें.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:277:"Seek urgent medical attention for new or worsening chest pressure or pain, shortness of breath, sweating, nausea, fainting, or pain spreading to the arm, shoulder, back, neck, or jaw. Severe or persistent chest pain or symptoms suggesting a heart attack require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:18:42";}i:40;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:42;s:10:"disease_id";i:84;s:11:"overview_en";s:386:"Heart failure is a condition in which the heart cannot pump enough blood to meet the body’s needs. It does not mean that the heart has stopped working. Heart failure may develop suddenly or gradually and can affect one or both sides of the heart. Common symptoms include shortness of breath, tiredness, weakness, swelling of the legs or feet, and difficulty breathing when lying down.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:242:"हृदय विफलता एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें हृदय शरीर की आवश्यकताओं के अनुसार रक्त पंप नहीं कर पाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:361:"Heart failure can result from conditions that weaken or damage the heart or make it work harder. Common causes include coronary artery disease, previous heart attack, high blood pressure, heart valve disease, cardiomyopathy, and abnormal heart rhythms. Diabetes, obesity, and other conditions can also contribute. Sometimes the exact cause cannot be identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:220:"इसके प्रमुख कारण कोरोनरी धमनी रोग, उच्च रक्तचाप, हृदयाघात और कार्डियोमायोपैथी हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:376:"Risk factors for heart failure include coronary artery disease, high blood pressure, diabetes, obesity, smoking, excessive alcohol use, and a family history of heart disease. Risk also increases with age. Previous heart attack, heart valve disease, abnormal heart rhythms, and some diseases that damage the heart muscle can increase the likelihood of developing heart failure.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:194:"उच्च रक्तचाप, मधुमेह, मोटापा, धूम्रपान और पूर्व हृदय रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:374:"Heart failure is diagnosed using symptoms, medical history, and a physical examination. Doctors may check for abnormal heart sounds, swelling, or signs of fluid buildup. Tests can include blood tests, chest X-rays, an electrocardiogram, and echocardiography to assess heart structure and function. Other imaging or heart tests may be used to identify the cause and severity.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:206:"निदान में ईसीजी, इकोकार्डियोग्राफी, छाती का एक्स-रे और रक्त परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:421:"The risk of heart failure can be reduced by controlling conditions that damage the heart. This includes maintaining healthy blood pressure and cholesterol levels, managing diabetes, avoiding tobacco, limiting alcohol, maintaining a healthy weight, eating a heart-healthy diet, and getting regular physical activity. Treating heart disease and following prescribed treatment can also help prevent worsening heart function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:216:"रक्तचाप नियंत्रित रखें, स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाएं और हृदय रोगों का समय पर उपचार करें.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:275:"Seek urgent medical attention for sudden or rapidly worsening shortness of breath, severe difficulty breathing, chest pain, fainting, confusion, bluish lips or skin, or rapidly increasing swelling. Severe breathing difficulty or persistent chest pain requires emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:41;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:43;s:10:"disease_id";i:85;s:11:"overview_en";s:354:"Atrial fibrillation is an irregular and often rapid heart rhythm caused by disorganized electrical activity in the upper chambers of the heart. The irregular rhythm can reduce efficient heart function and increase the risk of blood clots and stroke. It may occur with heart or other medical conditions, although sometimes no specific cause is identified.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:163:"एट्रियल फिब्रिलेशन हृदय की अनियमित और तेज धड़कन की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:421:"Atrial fibrillation occurs when the electrical signals in the upper chambers of the heart become disorganized, producing an irregular and often rapid heartbeat. It may develop with increasing age or in association with high blood pressure, coronary artery disease, heart valve problems, heart failure, thyroid disorders, sleep apnea, obesity, diabetes, or excessive alcohol use. Sometimes no specific cause is identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:190:"यह हृदय रोग, उच्च रक्तचाप, थायरॉइड विकार या उम्र बढ़ने के कारण हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:415:"Risk of atrial fibrillation increases with age and with conditions that affect the heart or cardiovascular system. Important risk factors include high blood pressure, coronary artery disease, heart failure, heart valve disease, obesity, diabetes, thyroid disorders, and sleep apnea. Excessive alcohol use and other factors that affect heart rhythm may also increase the likelihood of developing atrial fibrillation.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:182:"उच्च रक्तचाप, हृदय रोग, मोटापा, मधुमेह और बढ़ती उम्र जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:421:"Atrial fibrillation is diagnosed by evaluating the heart rhythm and medical history. An electrocardiogram (ECG) can record the irregular rhythm and is commonly used for diagnosis. If episodes are intermittent, Holter monitoring or another ambulatory heart monitor may be used. Echocardiography can assess heart structure and function, while blood tests may help identify contributing conditions such as thyroid disorders.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:172:"निदान ईसीजी, होल्टर मॉनिटर और इकोकार्डियोग्राफी से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:413:"Maintaining cardiovascular health may help reduce the risk of atrial fibrillation and its complications. Control blood pressure, diabetes, and other cardiovascular conditions through appropriate medical care. Maintain a healthy weight, remain physically active, avoid smoking, and limit excessive alcohol use. Sleep disorders and thyroid conditions should also be appropriately evaluated and managed when present.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:195:"हृदय स्वास्थ्य बनाए रखें, रक्तचाप नियंत्रित रखें और अत्यधिक शराब से बचें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:269:"Seek urgent medical attention for a very rapid or irregular heartbeat accompanied by chest pain, severe shortness of breath, fainting, confusion, or severe weakness. Sudden weakness, facial drooping, difficulty speaking, or other signs of stroke require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:42;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:44;s:10:"disease_id";i:86;s:11:"overview_en";s:370:"Angina is chest pain or discomfort that occurs when the heart muscle does not receive enough oxygen-rich blood. It is most often related to narrowing of the coronary arteries, but can also occur because of coronary artery spasm or other conditions affecting blood flow. Symptoms may be triggered by physical activity, emotional stress, cold temperatures, or heavy meals.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:213:"एंजाइना हृदय की मांसपेशियों में रक्त प्रवाह कम होने से होने वाला सीने का दर्द है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:421:"Angina occurs when the heart muscle does not receive enough oxygen-rich blood to meet its needs. The most common cause is narrowing of the coronary arteries because of plaque buildup. Angina may also result from coronary artery spasm or other conditions that reduce blood flow or increase the heart muscle’s demand for oxygen. Physical exertion, emotional stress, cold temperatures, or heavy meals may trigger symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:145:"अधिकांश मामलों में यह कोरोनरी धमनी रोग के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:439:"Risk factors for angina include smoking, diabetes, high blood pressure, high cholesterol, obesity, increasing age, and a family history of cardiovascular disease. Conditions that narrow or affect the coronary arteries can reduce blood flow to the heart. Physical inactivity and other factors associated with cardiovascular disease may also increase the likelihood of developing symptoms related to reduced blood supply to the heart muscle.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:202:"धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, मोटापा, उच्च रक्तचाप और उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:416:"Diagnosis of angina begins with assessment of chest symptoms, medical history, and cardiovascular risk factors. An ECG may be performed to evaluate the heart’s electrical activity. Depending on the symptoms and suspected cause, additional tests may include exercise or other stress testing, echocardiography, blood tests, CT-based evaluation, or coronary angiography to assess blood flow and the coronary arteries.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:164:"निदान में ईसीजी, स्ट्रेस टेस्ट, इको और एंजियोग्राफी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:429:"Reducing cardiovascular risk factors can help lower the likelihood of angina caused by coronary artery disease. Do not smoke, maintain a healthy weight, exercise regularly as medically appropriate, and follow a heart-healthy eating pattern. Control high blood pressure, diabetes, and high cholesterol with lifestyle measures and prescribed treatment. Regular medical care can help identify and manage cardiovascular risk factors.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:189:"नियमित व्यायाम करें, स्वस्थ आहार लें और जोखिम कारकों को नियंत्रित रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:323:"Seek emergency medical care for new, severe, persistent, or worsening chest pressure or pain, particularly when accompanied by shortness of breath, sweating, nausea, fainting, or pain spreading to the arm, shoulder, back, neck, or jaw. Symptoms occurring at rest or becoming more frequent require prompt medical assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:43;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:45;s:10:"disease_id";i:87;s:11:"overview_en";s:329:"Cardiomyopathy refers to diseases of the heart muscle that can make the heart enlarged, thickened, stiff, or weakened and impair its ability to pump blood normally. Different types include dilated, hypertrophic, restrictive, and arrhythmogenic cardiomyopathies. Complications may include heart failure and abnormal heart rhythms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:226:"कार्डियोमायोपैथी हृदय की मांसपेशियों का रोग है जो पंपिंग क्षमता को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:390:"Causes vary according to the type of cardiomyopathy. Genetic changes can cause some forms, particularly hypertrophic and certain inherited cardiomyopathies. Other causes include coronary artery disease, previous heart attack, high blood pressure, infections, inflammation, metabolic disorders, alcohol or toxic exposures, and some medicines. In some people, no specific cause is identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:179:"यह आनुवंशिक कारणों, संक्रमण, उच्च रक्तचाप या शराब सेवन से हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:340:"Risk depends on the type and cause. Family history of cardiomyopathy or unexplained sudden cardiac death can increase risk. Other factors may include coronary artery disease, high blood pressure, previous heart attack, certain infections or inflammatory diseases, heavy alcohol use, and conditions or medicines that damage the heart muscle.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:183:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, उच्च रक्तचाप, मोटापा और शराब सेवन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:313:"Diagnosis may include medical and family history, physical examination, ECG, echocardiography, chest imaging, blood tests, and sometimes cardiac MRI. Additional testing may include exercise testing, heart rhythm monitoring, genetic testing, or cardiac catheterization depending on the suspected type and severity.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:155:"निदान में ईसीजी, इको, एमआरआई और आनुवंशिक परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:402:"Some forms of cardiomyopathy cannot be prevented, particularly inherited forms. Managing blood pressure, coronary artery disease, diabetes, and other conditions that affect the heart can reduce risk of acquired disease. Avoiding excessive alcohol and harmful substances, following prescribed treatment, and evaluating unexplained heart symptoms or a strong family history can help reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:169:"रक्तचाप नियंत्रित रखें, शराब से बचें और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:282:"Seek urgent medical attention for worsening shortness of breath, chest pain, fainting, a very rapid or irregular heartbeat, severe swelling, or sudden deterioration in exercise tolerance. Severe breathing difficulty, persistent chest pain, or fainting requires emergency assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:44;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:46;s:10:"disease_id";i:88;s:11:"overview_en";s:528:"Pericarditis is inflammation of the pericardium, the thin sac surrounding the heart. It can cause sharp chest pain that may become worse with deep breathing or lying down and improve when sitting forward. Viral infections are a common cause, but other infections, autoimmune diseases, medications, injury, and medical procedures can also contribute. Some cases resolve on their own, while others require treatment. Complications such as fluid accumulation around the heart can occur and may interfere with normal heart function.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:140:"पेरिकार्डाइटिस हृदय को घेरने वाली झिल्ली की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:481:"Pericarditis can be caused by viral infections and, less commonly, bacterial or other infections. It may also occur because of autoimmune diseases, inflammatory conditions, kidney failure, cancer, chest injury, radiation therapy, or certain medicines. Pericarditis can develop after a heart attack or heart surgery. In some cases, the cause remains unknown and is described as idiopathic. Identifying the underlying cause is important because treatment and risk of recurrence vary.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:187:"यह वायरल संक्रमण, ऑटोइम्यून विकार या हृदय शल्यक्रिया के बाद हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:416:"Risk factors for pericarditis include recent viral or other infections, autoimmune diseases, kidney failure, cancer, previous heart surgery, chest injury, radiation exposure, and certain medicines. A previous episode of pericarditis increases the chance of recurrence. People with systemic inflammatory diseases may be particularly susceptible. In many cases, however, no specific risk factor or cause is identified.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:138:"संक्रमण, ऑटोइम्यून रोग और हृदय चोट जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:496:"Pericarditis is diagnosed using the history, characteristic chest pain, physical examination, electrocardiogram, blood tests, and cardiac imaging. An electrocardiogram may show changes associated with inflammation, while blood tests can identify markers of inflammation or heart injury. Echocardiography can detect fluid around the heart and assess its effect on cardiac function. Chest imaging and additional tests may help identify an underlying infection, autoimmune condition, or other cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:165:"निदान में ईसीजी, इकोकार्डियोग्राफी और रक्त परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:498:"Some causes of pericarditis cannot be prevented, but managing underlying inflammatory or systemic conditions and following medical advice after infections or heart procedures may reduce risk in certain situations. People with a previous episode should follow recommendations intended to reduce recurrence. New or unexplained chest pain should be assessed promptly because pericarditis can resemble other serious heart and lung conditions. Preventive measures depend largely on the underlying cause.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:163:"संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार करें और ऑटोइम्यून रोग नियंत्रित रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:273:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe or persistent chest pain, significant shortness of breath, fainting, a very rapid heartbeat, high fever with worsening illness, or rapidly increasing symptoms. Severe chest pain or breathing difficulty requires emergency evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:45;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:47;s:10:"disease_id";i:89;s:11:"overview_en";s:555:"Endocarditis is an infection or inflammation of the inner lining of the heart and, most importantly, the heart valves. It is usually caused by bacteria that enter the bloodstream and attach to abnormal or damaged heart tissue, although fungi and other microorganisms can occasionally cause it. Symptoms may develop gradually or appear suddenly and can include fever, chills, fatigue, weakness, shortness of breath, and abnormal heart sounds. Endocarditis can damage heart valves and cause serious complications if it is not diagnosed and treated promptly.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:159:"एंडोकार्डाइटिस हृदय की आंतरिक परत और वाल्वों का संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:563:"Endocarditis usually occurs when microorganisms enter the bloodstream and travel to the heart, where they attach to the inner lining or heart valves. Bacteria are the most common cause, although fungi and other organisms can also be responsible. Damaged or artificial heart valves and certain congenital heart conditions can provide surfaces where microorganisms can attach more easily. Bacteria may enter the bloodstream through dental or medical procedures, skin infections, intravenous drug use, or other infections. The specific organism determines treatment.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:165:"यह रक्त के माध्यम से बैक्टीरिया के हृदय में पहुंचने से होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:572:"Risk factors for endocarditis include certain abnormal or artificial heart valves, previous endocarditis, some congenital heart conditions, injection of drugs with contaminated equipment, and infections that can enter the bloodstream. Certain invasive medical procedures may increase exposure to bacteria, although the absolute risk varies. People with damaged heart tissue or prosthetic valves are particularly susceptible because microorganisms can attach more easily to abnormal surfaces. Good dental and general health can reduce some sources of bloodstream infection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:241:"हृदय वाल्व रोग, इंजेक्शन द्वारा नशीली दवाओं का उपयोग और खराब दंत स्वच्छता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:550:"Diagnosis of endocarditis is based on symptoms, medical history, physical examination, blood cultures, and heart imaging. Multiple blood samples are usually collected to identify the responsible microorganism before antibiotics are started when possible. Echocardiography can detect abnormal growths on valves, valve damage, or other cardiac findings. Additional imaging and laboratory tests may be needed to identify complications or the source of infection. Diagnosis can be challenging when blood cultures are negative or symptoms are nonspecific.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:196:"निदान में रक्त कल्चर, इकोकार्डियोग्राफी और प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:559:"Not all cases of endocarditis can be prevented. Good oral hygiene and regular dental care can reduce some sources of bloodstream infection. People at particularly high risk may be advised to receive preventive antibiotics before certain dental procedures, according to current medical recommendations. Prompt treatment of skin infections and avoiding injection of drugs with shared or contaminated equipment can also reduce risk. People with prosthetic valves or previous endocarditis should follow individualized prevention advice from their healthcare team.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:145:"दंत स्वच्छता बनाए रखें और संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:311:"Endocarditis requires prompt medical treatment. Seek urgent care for persistent fever with worsening illness, new or worsening shortness of breath, chest pain, fainting, confusion, weakness, or other signs of serious infection. Sudden neurological symptoms or severe breathing difficulty require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:46;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:48;s:10:"disease_id";i:90;s:11:"overview_en";s:360:"Peripheral artery disease, or PAD, occurs when arteries outside the heart become narrowed or blocked, most often reducing blood flow to the legs and feet. Many people have few or no symptoms. When symptoms occur, they may include pain, aching, numbness, or heaviness in the legs during walking. Severe disease can cause poorly healing wounds and tissue damage.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:248:"पेरिफेरल आर्टरी डिजीज में धमनियां संकरी हो जाती हैं जिससे अंगों में रक्त प्रवाह कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:377:"The most common cause of peripheral artery disease is atherosclerosis, in which fatty material called plaque builds up inside the walls of arteries. The plaque makes the arteries narrower and can reduce blood flow to the muscles and tissues. Less commonly, PAD may result from other blood-vessel conditions, injury, or abnormal muscle or ligament structure affecting an artery.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:132:"यह मुख्यतः धमनियों में प्लाक जमने के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:396:"Smoking is the most important risk factor for peripheral artery disease. Risk also increases with older age and conditions such as diabetes, high blood pressure, high cholesterol, heart disease, and previous stroke. A family history of vascular disease and other factors associated with atherosclerosis can also increase risk. Having PAD is associated with a higher risk of cardiovascular events.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:202:"धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, मोटापा, उच्च रक्तचाप और उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"Doctors diagnose peripheral artery disease using a medical history and physical examination, including checking pulses and circulation in the legs and feet. The ankle-brachial index, which compares blood pressure in the ankle and arm, is commonly used. Additional vascular or imaging tests may be performed when needed to determine the location and severity of narrowed or blocked arteries.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:215:"निदान में एंकल-ब्रैकियल इंडेक्स, डॉप्लर अल्ट्रासाउंड और एंजियोग्राफी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:404:"Risk of peripheral artery disease can be reduced by avoiding tobacco and maintaining healthy blood pressure, cholesterol, blood sugar, body weight, and activity levels. Regular physical activity and a heart-healthy diet can help reduce atherosclerosis risk. People with diabetes or other cardiovascular risk factors should follow recommended treatment and monitoring plans to protect blood-vessel health.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:223:"धूम्रपान छोड़ें, नियमित व्यायाम करें और हृदय संबंधी जोखिम कारकों को नियंत्रित रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:262:"Seek prompt medical assessment for rapidly worsening leg pain, a suddenly cold or pale limb, new numbness or weakness, nonhealing wounds, or significant changes in skin color. Sudden severe limb pain with loss of circulation requires emergency medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:47;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:49;s:10:"disease_id";i:93;s:11:"overview_en";s:317:"Sickle cell disease is a group of inherited blood disorders in which abnormal hemoglobin causes red blood cells to become rigid and sickle-shaped. These cells can break down early, causing anemia, and can block small blood vessels, reducing oxygen delivery and causing episodes of severe pain and other complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:246:"सिकल सेल रोग एक आनुवंशिक रक्त विकार है जिसमें लाल रक्त कोशिकाएं दरांती के आकार की हो जाती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:324:"Sickle cell disease is caused by inherited changes in the HBB gene, which provides instructions for making part of hemoglobin. Abnormal hemoglobin, particularly hemoglobin S, can cause red blood cells to become sickle-shaped. The disease develops when a person inherits disease-causing hemoglobin variants from both parents.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:153:"यह हीमोग्लोबिन जीन में आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:354:"Because sickle cell disease is inherited, having parents who carry disease-causing hemoglobin variants increases risk. The condition is more common in people whose ancestry includes regions where malaria has historically been common. A family history of sickle cell disease or sickle cell trait also increases the likelihood of carrying an affected gene.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:164:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:341:"Diagnosis is made with blood tests that identify abnormal hemoglobin. Newborn screening can detect sickle cell disease early. Hemoglobin analysis and, when needed, genetic testing can distinguish sickle cell disease from sickle cell trait and other hemoglobin disorders. Additional blood tests may be used to assess anemia and complications.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:215:"निदान में रक्त परीक्षण, हीमोग्लोबिन इलेक्ट्रोफोरेसिस और आनुवंशिक जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:441:"Sickle cell disease itself cannot be prevented when the affected genetic variants have already been inherited. Carrier screening and genetic counseling can help people understand their reproductive risk. Newborn screening allows early diagnosis and treatment. For people with the disease, regular medical care, recommended vaccinations, infection prevention, adequate hydration, and avoidance of known triggers can help reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:123:"आनुवंशिक परामर्श और प्रारंभिक जांच सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:327:"Sickle cell disease can cause serious complications. Seek urgent medical attention for severe pain, fever, chest pain, difficulty breathing, sudden weakness or confusion, severe headache, vision changes, or symptoms that are rapidly worsening. Sudden neurological symptoms or severe breathing difficulty require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:48;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:50;s:10:"disease_id";i:94;s:11:"overview_en";s:422:"Thalassemia is a group of inherited blood disorders in which the body produces too little healthy hemoglobin. Hemoglobin is the protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout the body. Reduced hemoglobin production can lead to anemia, fatigue, weakness, and other complications. The severity varies widely, from mild forms with few symptoms to severe forms requiring regular medical care and blood transfusions.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:217:"थैलेसीमिया एक आनुवंशिक रक्त विकार है जिसमें हीमोग्लोबिन का निर्माण कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:420:"Thalassemia results from inherited changes in genes involved in making hemoglobin. The main forms are alpha thalassemia and beta thalassemia, depending on which globin protein is affected. These genetic changes reduce or alter hemoglobin production, causing red blood cells to carry less oxygen and making them more likely to break down. The condition is inherited from parents and can occur in several genetic patterns.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:219:"यह हीमोग्लोबिन निर्माण को प्रभावित करने वाले आनुवंशिक परिवर्तनों के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:419:"A family history of thalassemia is an important risk factor because the condition is inherited. The likelihood of carrying or developing a particular form varies among populations with ancestry from regions where thalassemia is more common, including parts of the Mediterranean, Middle East, South and Southeast Asia, China, and Africa. Genetic factors from both parents influence the type and severity of the disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:140:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और वाहक माता-पिता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:436:"Diagnosis of thalassemia usually involves blood testing to evaluate red blood cells and hemoglobin. A complete blood count can identify anemia and characteristic changes in red blood cells. Hemoglobin testing can help identify abnormal or reduced forms of hemoglobin. Depending on the situation, genetic testing may be used to identify variants responsible for alpha or beta thalassemia and to clarify the specific type of the disorder.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:211:"निदान में सीबीसी, हीमोग्लोबिन इलेक्ट्रोफोरेसिस और आनुवंशिक परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:484:"Because thalassemia is an inherited genetic disorder, it cannot usually be prevented after a person has inherited the responsible gene variants. However, people with a family history or ancestry associated with thalassemia can discuss carrier screening and genetic counseling before pregnancy. Identifying carrier status can help families understand inheritance patterns and reproductive risks. Appropriate medical follow-up can also help reduce complications in affected individuals.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:160:"विवाह या गर्भावस्था से पूर्व आनुवंशिक जांच सहायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:281:"Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening fatigue, shortness of breath, chest pain, fainting, significant paleness, rapid heartbeat, or symptoms suggesting severe anemia or another complication. Severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, or fainting requires emergency evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:49;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:51;s:10:"disease_id";i:95;s:11:"overview_en";s:376:"Hemophilia is an inherited bleeding disorder in which the blood does not clot normally because the body lacks or has too little of certain clotting factors. This can cause prolonged bleeding after injuries, surgery, or dental procedures and, in more severe cases, bleeding may occur spontaneously. Hemophilia most commonly affects males, although females can also be affected.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:224:"हीमोफीलिया एक आनुवंशिक रक्तस्राव विकार है जो क्लॉटिंग फैक्टर की कमी के कारण होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:393:"Hemophilia is usually caused by inherited changes in genes responsible for producing clotting factors. Hemophilia A results from insufficient factor VIII, while hemophilia B results from insufficient factor IX. These genes are located on the X chromosome, which explains why the disorder is more commonly diagnosed in males. Rarely, hemophilia can develop later in life as acquired hemophilia.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1042:"हीमोफीलिया आमतौर पर F8 जीन में वंशानुगत परिवर्तन के कारण होता है, जिससे क्लॉटिंग फैक्टर VIII की मात्रा कम या अनुपस्थित हो जाती है, या F9 जीन में परिवर्तन के कारण होता है, जिससे फैक्टर IX कम हो जाता है। ये जीन X गुणसूत्र पर होते हैं, इसलिए वंशानुगत हीमोफीलिया पुरुषों में अधिक गंभीर रूप से दिखाई देता है। दुर्लभ मामलों में बाद में acquired hemophilia हो सकता है, जिसमें एंटीबॉडी क्लॉटिंग फैक्टर के कार्य में बाधा डालती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:354:"Risk factors for hemophilia primarily involve inherited genetic changes and a family history of the condition. A person with a parent who carries a hemophilia-associated gene may have an increased likelihood of inheriting it. Acquired hemophilia can occur in association with autoimmune disorders, certain cancers, pregnancy, or other medical conditions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1297:"हीमोफीलिया के जोखिम कारक मुख्य रूप से रक्त के थक्के बनाने वाले कारकों के उत्पादन को प्रभावित करने वाले वंशानुगत आनुवंशिक बदलावों से जुड़े होते हैं। यह स्थिति अक्सर हीमोफीलिया के पारिवारिक इतिहास वाले लोगों में होती है और सामान्यतः X क्रोमोसोम से जुड़ी विरासत के कारण होती है। ज्ञात पारिवारिक इतिहास न होने पर भी नया आनुवंशिक बदलाव होने से हीमोफीलिया हो सकता है। रोग का प्रकार और गंभीरता इस बात पर निर्भर करती है कि कौन-सा क्लॉटिंग फैक्टर प्रभावित है और उसका कितना कार्यात्मक उत्पादन हो रहा है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:405:"Hemophilia is diagnosed using a medical and family history together with blood tests that measure clotting function and specific clotting-factor levels. Testing can determine whether factor VIII or factor IX is deficient and can help establish the severity of the disorder. Genetic testing may also be used in some circumstances, particularly for identifying carriers or clarifying an inherited diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:150:"निदान में क्लॉटिंग परीक्षण और फैक्टर स्तर जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:404:"Inherited hemophilia cannot generally be prevented, but genetic counseling can help families understand inheritance and reproductive options. People with hemophilia can reduce complications through regular medical care, appropriate replacement therapy when prescribed, avoidance of unnecessary injuries and certain medicines that increase bleeding, dental care, and prompt treatment of bleeding episodes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:166:"आनुवंशिक परामर्श जोखिम वाले परिवारों की पहचान में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:325:"Seek urgent medical attention for bleeding that does not stop, significant bleeding after an injury, severe headache, vomiting after head injury, sudden weakness or confusion, severe joint or muscle swelling, or blood in the urine or stool. Suspected bleeding inside the head or another critical area requires emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:50;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:52;s:10:"disease_id";i:96;s:11:"overview_en";s:434:"Leukemia is a group of cancers affecting blood-forming tissues, particularly the bone marrow and blood cells. Abnormal blood-forming cells multiply excessively and interfere with the production of normal red blood cells, white blood cells and platelets. Different types of leukemia progress at different rates and affect different blood-cell lines. Symptoms may include fatigue, frequent infections, fever, easy bruising and bleeding.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:115:"ल्यूकेमिया रक्त और अस्थि मज्जा का कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:379:"The exact cause of most leukemias is unknown. The disease develops when genetic changes cause blood-forming cells to grow and divide abnormally. Factors that may contribute include certain inherited genetic conditions, previous exposure to high doses of radiation, some cancer treatments and certain chemical exposures. In most people, however, no single cause can be identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:173:"यह श्वेत रक्त कोशिकाओं की असामान्य वृद्धि के कारण विकसित होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:393:"Risk factors vary by leukemia type and may include increasing age, certain inherited genetic disorders, previous chemotherapy or radiation therapy, high-dose radiation exposure and some occupational or environmental chemical exposures. Having certain blood disorders may also increase risk of particular leukemia types. Most people with leukemia do not have a clearly identifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:166:"विकिरण संपर्क, आनुवंशिक विकार और धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:401:"Leukemia is evaluated using a medical history, physical examination and blood tests. A complete blood count may show abnormal numbers of blood cells. Examination of blood cells can provide additional information. Bone marrow aspiration and biopsy are commonly used to confirm the diagnosis and determine the leukemia type. Genetic and molecular tests may help classify the disease and guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:161:"निदान में सीबीसी, बोन मैरो जांच और आनुवंशिक अध्ययन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:435:"Most cases of leukemia cannot be prevented because the causes are usually unknown. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to high levels of radiation and certain harmful chemicals may reduce the risk associated with known environmental factors. People who have received treatments that can increase leukemia risk should follow recommended medical follow-up. Early evaluation of persistent unexplained symptoms can help identify blood disorders.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:98:"अनावश्यक विकिरण और धूम्रपान से बचें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:302:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for persistent fever, recurrent infections, unusual bleeding or bruising, severe weakness, unexplained weight loss, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for severe bleeding, severe breathing difficulty, confusion, or sudden neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:51;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:53;s:10:"disease_id";i:97;s:11:"overview_en";s:403:"Lymphoma is a group of cancers that begin in lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell that is part of the immune system. Lymphoma can develop in lymph nodes or other tissues and is broadly classified into Hodgkin lymphoma and non-Hodgkin lymphoma. Symptoms may include painless swollen lymph nodes, fever, night sweats, unexplained weight loss, fatigue, itching, or symptoms related to an affected organ.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:152:"लिम्फोमा लसीका तंत्र और प्रतिरक्षा कोशिकाओं का कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:390:"Lymphoma develops when lymphocytes acquire genetic changes that cause them to grow or survive abnormally. The exact cause is often not known. Some infections, immune-system disorders, inherited susceptibility, and certain environmental or medical exposures can be associated with particular types of lymphoma. Different lymphoma subtypes have different biological features and risk factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:137:"यह लिम्फोसाइट्स की असामान्य वृद्धि के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:425:"Risk factors vary by lymphoma type and may include increasing age, a family history of lymphoma, weakened immune function, certain autoimmune diseases, and some infections. Previous treatment with certain medicines or radiation can be associated with increased risk in some circumstances. Having a risk factor does not mean that lymphoma will develop, and many people diagnosed with lymphoma have no identifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:178:"कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, संक्रमण और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:374:"Lymphoma is diagnosed through medical history, physical examination, blood tests, imaging, and usually a biopsy of an affected lymph node or tissue. The biopsy allows specialists to examine abnormal cells and determine the specific lymphoma type. Additional imaging and laboratory tests help determine how extensively the disease has spread and can guide treatment planning.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:170:"निदान में लिम्फ नोड बायोप्सी, इमेजिंग और रक्त परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:467:"Most lymphomas cannot be reliably prevented because their causes are often unknown and may involve genetic or biological changes that cannot be controlled. Reducing exposure to known infectious risks, following appropriate medical care for immune-system disorders, and avoiding unnecessary exposure to harmful substances may reduce the risk of some specific types. Persistent unexplained lymph-node swelling or other concerning symptoms should be medically evaluated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:139:"लगातार बढ़े हुए लिम्फ नोड्स की समय पर जांच आवश्यक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:298:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for persistent or enlarging lymph nodes, unexplained fever, night sweats, unexplained weight loss, severe fatigue, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe difficulty breathing, significant chest pressure, confusion, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:52;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:54;s:10:"disease_id";i:98;s:11:"overview_en";s:373:"Multiple myeloma is a cancer of plasma cells, a type of white blood cell found mainly in the bone marrow. Abnormal plasma cells multiply and produce an abnormal protein that can affect bones, blood, kidneys, and the immune system. The disease may cause bone pain, weakness, anemia, recurrent infections, or kidney problems, although some people have few symptoms initially.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:951:"मल्टीपल मायलोमा प्लाज़्मा कोशिकाओं का कैंसर है। प्लाज़्मा कोशिकाएँ श्वेत रक्त कोशिकाओं का एक प्रकार हैं जो सामान्यतः एंटीबॉडी बनाती हैं। असामान्य प्लाज़्मा कोशिकाएँ अस्थि-मज्जा में जमा होकर कई हड्डियों में ट्यूमर बना सकती हैं। रोग बढ़ने पर सामान्य रक्त कोशिकाओं के निर्माण में बाधा और हड्डियों की कमजोरी हो सकती है। इसे प्लाज़्मा सेल मायलोमा भी कहा जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:409:"Multiple myeloma develops when plasma cells acquire abnormal changes that allow them to grow and multiply uncontrollably in the bone marrow. The exact cause of these cellular changes is not known. Some cases develop from an earlier plasma-cell condition such as monoclonal gammopathy of undetermined significance (MGUS). The abnormal cells can crowd normal blood-forming cells and produce monoclonal proteins.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:929:"मल्टीपल मायलोमा तब विकसित होता है जब असामान्य प्लाज्मा कोशिकाएं अस्थि मज्जा में अनियंत्रित रूप से बढ़ने लगती हैं और असामान्य प्रोटीन बनाती हैं। इन कोशिकीय परिवर्तनों का सटीक कारण आमतौर पर ज्ञात नहीं होता। कुछ लोगों में पहले मोनोक्लोनल गैमोपैथी ऑफ अनडिटरमाइंड सिग्निफिकेंस (MGUS) जैसी पूर्ववर्ती स्थिति होती है, जो कुछ मामलों में मायलोमा में बदल सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:380:"Risk factors for multiple myeloma include increasing age, male sex, a personal history of certain plasma-cell disorders such as MGUS or plasmacytoma, and exposure to radiation or certain chemicals. Family and genetic factors may also contribute. Having a risk factor does not mean that a person will develop multiple myeloma, and the disease can occur without a known risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:176:"उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास और कुछ पर्यावरणीय कारक जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:420:"Diagnosis of multiple myeloma involves medical history, physical examination, and laboratory and imaging tests. Blood and urine tests can detect abnormal monoclonal proteins, free light chains, anemia, kidney problems, or abnormal calcium levels. Bone marrow examination may identify abnormal plasma cells. Imaging such as X-ray, CT, MRI, or PET-CT may be used to look for bone lesions and other disease-related changes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:167:"निदान में रक्त परीक्षण, बोन मैरो बायोप्सी और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:440:"There is no established way to completely prevent multiple myeloma because many of its causes are not known or cannot be changed. People with conditions associated with increased risk may benefit from appropriate medical follow-up. Reporting persistent bone pain, unusual fatigue, recurrent infections, or other concerning symptoms can support earlier evaluation. Management of identified plasma-cell disorders should follow medical advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:151:"कोई निश्चित रोकथाम नहीं है, लेकिन शीघ्र पहचान लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:318:"Seek prompt medical assessment for persistent or severe bone pain, unusual fractures, severe weakness, recurrent infections, unexplained bleeding, or symptoms suggesting kidney problems. Emergency care is needed for severe weakness, confusion, severe dehydration, difficulty breathing, or sudden neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:53;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:55;s:10:"disease_id";i:99;s:11:"overview_en";s:408:"HIV infection is caused by human immunodeficiency virus, which attacks cells of the immune system and can weaken the body's ability to fight infections and certain cancers. Early infection may cause flu-like symptoms or no noticeable symptoms. Without effective treatment, HIV can progress to AIDS, the most advanced stage of infection. Modern antiretroviral therapy can control HIV and reduce complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:189:"एचआईवी/एड्स एक वायरल संक्रमण है जो प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली को कमजोर करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:403:"HIV spreads when certain body fluids from a person with HIV enter another person's body. Transmission can occur through vaginal or anal sex, sharing needles or other injection equipment, exposure to infected blood, and from a mother to her baby during pregnancy, childbirth, or breastfeeding. HIV is not spread by ordinary casual contact such as hugging, sharing food, or being near someone who has HIV.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:169:"एचआईवी संक्रमित रक्त, यौन संपर्क और मां से बच्चे में फैल सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:412:"Risk is increased by sex without effective HIV prevention methods, having another sexually transmitted infection, sharing needles or injection equipment, and exposure to infected blood. Risk can also be affected by access to testing, prevention medicines, treatment, and healthcare. People with ongoing exposure risks may benefit from discussing HIV testing and prevention options with a healthcare professional.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:209:"असुरक्षित यौन संबंध, सुई साझा करना और संक्रमित रक्त का संपर्क जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:396:"HIV is diagnosed with laboratory testing or an approved home test that detects HIV infection. Testing may involve an antigen and antibody test, an antibody test, or a nucleic acid test depending on the situation and timing of exposure. A positive screening result generally requires follow-up testing. Additional tests such as viral load and CD4 testing help assess the infection after diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:189:"निदान एचआईवी एंटीबॉडी, एंटीजन और वायरल लोड परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:437:"HIV prevention includes using condoms or other effective prevention methods, getting tested, and treating sexually transmitted infections. People at substantial risk can discuss pre-exposure prophylaxis with a healthcare professional, while post-exposure prophylaxis is an emergency option that must be started promptly after a possible exposure. Avoiding shared needles and maintaining effective HIV treatment also reduces transmission.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:201:"सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार अपनाएं, सुई साझा न करें और जांचे हुए रक्त का उपयोग करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:358:"People with HIV should seek prompt medical assessment for persistent fever, severe or worsening infections, significant unexplained weight loss, severe diarrhea, breathing difficulty, confusion, or rapidly worsening illness. Emergency care is needed for severe breathing difficulty, altered consciousness, severe dehydration, or sudden neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:54;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:56;s:10:"disease_id";i:100;s:11:"overview_en";s:352:"Systemic lupus erythematosus, commonly called lupus, is a chronic autoimmune disease in which the immune system attacks the body’s own tissues. It can cause inflammation and damage in many parts of the body, including the skin, joints, kidneys, heart, lungs, blood cells, and nervous system. Symptoms and severity vary considerably among individuals.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:245:"सिस्टमिक ल्यूपस एरिथेमेटोसस एक दीर्घकालिक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जो कई अंगों को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:365:"The exact cause of systemic lupus erythematosus is unknown. It is believed to result from interactions among genetic susceptibility, immune-system abnormalities, hormones, and environmental triggers. Factors such as sunlight exposure, certain infections, medications, and other environmental influences may contribute to disease activity in susceptible individuals.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:171:"यह तब होता है जब प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली स्वस्थ ऊतकों पर हमला करती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:311:"Risk factors for systemic lupus erythematosus include genetic susceptibility, female sex, certain family histories, exposure to ultraviolet light, smoking, some infections, and particular medications. The disease is more common in women of childbearing age, although lupus can occur in people of any age or sex.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:186:"आनुवंशिकता, हार्मोनल प्रभाव और ऑटोइम्यून प्रवृत्ति जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:406:"Systemic lupus erythematosus is diagnosed using a combination of symptoms, physical examination, medical history, and laboratory tests. Blood tests may include antinuclear antibody testing and other tests for immune-system activity. Urine and kidney tests may be used to look for organ involvement. No single test can establish lupus in every person, so clinicians consider the overall pattern of findings.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:203:"निदान में एएनए परीक्षण, ऑटोइम्यून मार्कर और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:349:"Systemic lupus erythematosus cannot currently be prevented in every person. People with lupus can reduce disease flares by following prescribed treatment, protecting the skin from excessive ultraviolet exposure, avoiding smoking, maintaining regular medical follow-up, and learning to recognize symptoms that may indicate increased disease activity.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:164:"समय पर निदान और नियमित चिकित्सा देखभाल जटिलताओं को कम करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:258:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe chest pain or difficulty breathing, sudden neurological symptoms, seizures, confusion, severe swelling, markedly reduced urine output, or other rapidly worsening symptoms that could indicate serious organ involvement.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:55;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:57;s:10:"disease_id";i:102;s:11:"overview_en";s:565:"Gastritis is inflammation of the stomach lining. It may develop suddenly or persist for a long time. Common causes include infection with Helicobacter pylori, regular use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, alcohol use, and other conditions that irritate or damage the stomach lining. Some people have no symptoms, while others develop upper abdominal discomfort, nausea, vomiting, indigestion, or a feeling of fullness. Persistent symptoms or bleeding require medical evaluation because untreated gastritis may sometimes lead to ulcers or other complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:202:"गैस्ट्राइटिस पेट की अंदरूनी परत की सूजन है जिससे दर्द, मतली और अपच हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:529:"Gastritis has several possible causes. Helicobacter pylori infection is a common cause of chronic gastritis. Regular or prolonged use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs can weaken the stomach lining and promote inflammation. Heavy alcohol use can also irritate the stomach. Other causes include autoimmune gastritis, severe physical stress from serious illness or injury, bile reflux, and certain infections or medical treatments. In some cases, the exact cause is not immediately clear and additional testing may be needed.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:260:"एच. पाइलोरी संक्रमण, शराब, धूम्रपान और दर्द निवारक दवाओं का लंबे समय तक उपयोग इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:492:"Risk factors for gastritis include Helicobacter pylori infection, frequent or prolonged use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, heavy alcohol consumption, older age, autoimmune disorders, and severe physical stress from major illness or injury. Previous stomach problems and certain medical treatments may also increase risk. The likelihood depends on the underlying cause. Not everyone with a risk factor develops gastritis, and symptoms may be absent even when inflammation is present.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:156:"धूम्रपान, शराब, तनाव, संक्रमण और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:564:"Diagnosis of gastritis begins with a medical history and physical examination, including review of symptoms, medicines, alcohol use, and possible H. pylori exposure. Testing may include stool or breath tests for H. pylori and blood tests when appropriate. Upper gastrointestinal endoscopy may be recommended when symptoms are persistent, severe, recurrent, or associated with warning signs such as bleeding or unexplained weight loss. During endoscopy, tissue samples may be collected to examine the stomach lining and identify inflammation or other abnormalities.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:191:"निदान में एंडोस्कोपी, एच. पाइलोरी जांच और रक्त परीक्षण शामिल हो सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:557:"Some forms of gastritis can be prevented or their risk reduced by avoiding unnecessary use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs and discussing safer alternatives with a healthcare professional when long-term pain treatment is needed. Limiting heavy alcohol use can reduce stomach irritation. Good hygiene and appropriate food and water practices may reduce exposure to H. pylori in settings where infection is common. People with persistent digestive symptoms should seek evaluation rather than repeatedly treating symptoms without identifying the cause.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:141:"धूम्रपान, शराब और अनावश्यक दर्द निवारक दवाओं से बचें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:299:"Gastritis usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt medical assessment for persistent or severe abdominal pain, repeated vomiting, vomiting blood, black or bloody stools, dizziness, fainting, or symptoms suggesting significant bleeding. Heavy bleeding or fainting requires emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:56;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:58;s:10:"disease_id";i:104;s:11:"overview_en";s:360:"Stomach cancer is a malignant tumor arising from the lining of the stomach. It may develop gradually and can cause indigestion, abdominal discomfort, reduced appetite, nausea, vomiting, difficulty eating, or unexplained weight loss. Early disease may produce few or nonspecific symptoms, so persistent digestive symptoms require appropriate medical evaluation.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:153:"पेट का कैंसर पेट की परत से उत्पन्न होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:354:"Stomach cancer can develop through a combination of genetic and environmental factors that cause abnormal changes in stomach cells. Helicobacter pylori infection, chronic inflammation of the stomach lining, certain precancerous changes, inherited genetic conditions, smoking, and dietary factors can contribute to the development of some stomach cancers.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:239:"एच. पाइलोरी संक्रमण, धूम्रपान, आनुवंशिकता और दीर्घकालिक गैस्ट्राइटिस इसके जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:269:"Risk factors include Helicobacter pylori infection, chronic gastritis, smoking, family history, certain inherited cancer syndromes, increasing age, diets high in heavily salted or preserved foods, and previous stomach surgery or certain precancerous stomach conditions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:162:"धूम्रपान, पारिवारिक इतिहास और अस्वस्थ आहार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:331:"Diagnosis generally involves upper gastrointestinal endoscopy, during which the stomach lining can be examined directly and a biopsy can be taken for microscopic analysis. Imaging such as CT scans may be used to determine the extent of disease. Additional tests may be performed to assess tumor characteristics and possible spread.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:183:"निदान में एंडोस्कोपी, बायोप्सी, सीटी स्कैन और रक्त परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:362:"Risk reduction includes avoiding tobacco, maintaining a balanced diet with adequate fruits and vegetables, limiting heavily salted, smoked, or preserved foods, and identifying and treating Helicobacter pylori infection when appropriate. People with significant inherited or medical risk factors should follow individualized medical advice regarding surveillance.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1058:"पेट के कैंसर को हमेशा रोका नहीं जा सकता, लेकिन कुछ उपाय इसके जोखिम को कम कर सकते हैं। तंबाकू से बचना, शराब का सेवन सीमित करना और फलों तथा सब्जियों से भरपूर संतुलित आहार लेना लाभकारी हो सकता है। Helicobacter pylori संक्रमण की समय पर जांच और उपचार इस बैक्टीरिया से जुड़े जोखिम को कम कर सकते हैं। कुछ वंशानुगत स्थितियों या मजबूत पारिवारिक इतिहास वाले लोगों को विशेष चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन और निगरानी की आवश्यकता हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:346:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for persistent upper abdominal symptoms, unexplained weight loss, persistent vomiting, difficulty swallowing, anemia, blood in vomit or stool, or symptoms that progressively worsen. Emergency care is needed for significant bleeding, severe weakness or fainting, severe abdominal pain, or other sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:57;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:59;s:10:"disease_id";i:105;s:11:"overview_en";s:386:"Gastroenteritis is inflammation of the stomach and intestines that commonly causes diarrhea, vomiting, abdominal discomfort, nausea, and sometimes fever. It is often caused by an infection and may spread easily from person to person or through contaminated food and water. Most uncomplicated cases improve with supportive care, although severe dehydration can require medical attention.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:189:"गैस्ट्रोएंटेराइटिस पेट और आंतों की सूजन है जिससे दस्त और उल्टी होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:431:"Gastroenteritis can be caused by viruses, bacteria, or parasites. Common infectious causes can spread through contaminated food or water, contact with an infected person, or surfaces contaminated with infectious material. Certain medicines, toxins, and other noninfectious conditions can also cause inflammation of the digestive tract. The specific cause may depend on the person, exposure history, and local patterns of infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:160:"यह सामान्यतः वायरस, बैक्टीरिया या परजीवी संक्रमण से होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:385:"Risk increases with exposure to contaminated food or water, inadequate hand hygiene, close contact with an infected person, and poor sanitation. Young children, older adults, and people with weakened immune systems may be more vulnerable to complications such as dehydration. Travel to areas with unsafe water or food handling practices can also increase exposure to infectious causes.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:135:"दूषित भोजन, पानी और खराब स्वच्छता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:431:"Diagnosis is usually based on symptoms, medical history, recent food or water exposure, travel, and physical examination. Most mild cases do not require extensive testing. Stool testing may be recommended when diarrhea is severe or persistent, blood is present, an outbreak is suspected, or a specific bacterial or parasitic infection needs to be identified. Tests may also be used when dehydration or another illness is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:142:"निदान लक्षणों और कभी-कभी मल परीक्षण पर आधारित होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:452:"Careful handwashing with soap and water, safe food preparation, proper food storage, and drinking safe water can reduce the risk of infectious gastroenteritis. Avoid sharing food or utensils with people who are ill and clean surfaces contaminated by vomit or stool. People who are sick should avoid preparing food for others until the recommended recovery period has passed. Vaccination can prevent some causes, such as rotavirus infection in children.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1042:"संक्रामक गैस्ट्रोएंटेराइटिस से बचाव के लिए साबुन और पानी से अच्छी तरह हाथ धोना, भोजन को सुरक्षित तरीके से तैयार करना और मल या उल्टी से दूषित हो सकने वाली सतहों को साफ करना महत्वपूर्ण है। बीमार होने पर और लक्षण समाप्त होने के बाद अनुशंसित अवधि तक दूसरों के लिए भोजन तैयार करने से बचें। संक्रमण और आयु के अनुसार कुछ कारणों से बचाव के लिए टीकाकरण भी उपयोगी हो सकता है, जैसे बच्चों में रोटावायरस वैक्सीन।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:357:"Gastroenteritis usually improves with supportive care, but seek prompt medical assessment for severe or persistent vomiting or diarrhea, signs of dehydration, high fever, significant abdominal pain, blood in the stool or vomit, confusion, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care may be needed for severe dehydration, fainting, or significant bleeding.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:58;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:60;s:10:"disease_id";i:107;s:11:"overview_en";s:453:"Alcoholic liver disease is liver damage caused by prolonged or heavy alcohol use. It can range from fatty liver and inflammation to scarring and cirrhosis, in which liver function may become seriously impaired. Early disease may cause few or no symptoms. As damage progresses, symptoms can include fatigue, abdominal discomfort, jaundice, swelling, bleeding problems, or changes in mental status. Severe disease can cause life-threatening complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:173:"अल्कोहॉलिक लिवर रोग अत्यधिक शराब सेवन से होने वाली यकृत क्षति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:441:"Alcoholic liver disease develops when repeated or heavy alcohol exposure damages liver cells and causes inflammation and scarring. The likelihood of liver injury generally increases with the amount and duration of alcohol use, although not everyone who drinks heavily develops the same degree of disease. Individual susceptibility can also be influenced by genetic and biological factors and by other health conditions that affect the liver.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:180:"लंबे समय तक अधिक शराब पीने से यकृत कोशिकाएं क्षतिग्रस्त हो जाती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:410:"Risk increases with heavier and longer-term alcohol consumption. Women may develop alcohol-related liver injury after lower levels of exposure than men. Other factors may influence susceptibility, including genetic differences, nutritional status, obesity, and coexisting liver conditions. Continued alcohol use after liver injury can increase the risk of progression to fibrosis, cirrhosis, and complications.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:128:"अत्यधिक शराब सेवन और खराब पोषण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:406:"Diagnosis combines a history of alcohol use with symptoms, physical examination, blood tests, and assessment of liver function. Imaging may help evaluate the liver and detect fatty change, enlargement, or signs of advanced disease. Additional testing may be needed to exclude other causes of liver injury or assess the severity of fibrosis. In selected cases, further specialist evaluation may be required.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:188:"निदान में लिवर फंक्शन टेस्ट, अल्ट्रासाउंड और यकृत मूल्यांकन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:444:"The most effective way to prevent alcohol-related liver disease is to avoid harmful alcohol use. People who drink heavily should discuss their alcohol use with a healthcare professional, particularly if liver disease is suspected. If alcoholic liver disease has been diagnosed, stopping alcohol is an important part of care. Medical support may be needed to manage withdrawal safely and to address alcohol use disorder and nutritional problems.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"शराब पूरी तरह छोड़ें और पौष्टिक आहार लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:342:"Seek prompt medical assessment for jaundice, worsening abdominal swelling, persistent vomiting, significant abdominal pain, unusual bleeding or bruising, confusion, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for vomiting blood, black stools, severe confusion, loss of consciousness, or other signs of serious liver complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:59;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:61;s:10:"disease_id";i:108;s:11:"overview_en";s:347:"Hepatitis A is an infection of the liver caused by the hepatitis A virus. It is usually spread when a person ingests food or water contaminated with infected stool, or through close contact with an infected person. Symptoms can include tiredness, nausea, abdominal discomfort, dark urine, loss of appetite, and jaundice. Most people recover fully.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:188:"हेपेटाइटिस ए एक वायरल यकृत संक्रमण है जो दूषित भोजन और पानी से फैलता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:384:"Hepatitis A is caused by the hepatitis A virus. Infection usually occurs when contaminated food or water is swallowed, or when the virus is transferred from an infected person through poor hand hygiene. It can also spread through close personal contact and certain sexual practices involving oral-anal contact. The virus enters through the digestive system and then affects the liver.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:108:"हेपेटाइटिस ए वायरस संक्रमण इसका कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:351:"Risk of hepatitis A is higher with travel or residence in areas where the infection is more common, close contact with an infected person, poor sanitation, unsafe food or water, and certain sexual practices. People who use injection drugs and those working in settings involving food, healthcare, childcare, or sewage may also have increased exposure.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:121:"खराब स्वच्छता और दूषित भोजन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:375:"Hepatitis A is diagnosed using the symptoms, medical history, physical examination, and blood tests. Testing can identify antibodies associated with recent hepatitis A infection, while liver-function tests may show inflammation or impaired liver function. The clinician may also assess exposure history, travel, food or water exposure, and other possible causes of hepatitis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:105:"निदान रक्त परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:429:"Hepatitis A can often be prevented through vaccination, careful handwashing, safe food handling, and drinking safe water. Wash hands thoroughly after using the toilet and before preparing or eating food. Avoid contaminated food and water when traveling in areas where hepatitis A is common. People exposed to the virus who are not immune should promptly discuss vaccination or preventive treatment with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:121:"टीकाकरण और स्वच्छता संक्रमण से बचाव करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:330:"Hepatitis A usually resolves with supportive care, but seek prompt medical assessment for worsening jaundice, persistent vomiting, severe abdominal pain, dehydration, confusion, unusual bleeding, or rapidly worsening illness. Emergency care is needed for altered consciousness, severe dehydration, or signs of acute liver failure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:60;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:62;s:10:"disease_id";i:110;s:11:"overview_en";s:614:"Hepatitis C is a liver infection caused by the hepatitis C virus. It is transmitted primarily through contact with infected blood. Many people have few or no symptoms at first, but persistent infection can cause liver inflammation and, over time, serious complications such as cirrhosis or liver cancer. Acute hepatitis C may cause fatigue, nausea, abdominal discomfort, dark urine, or yellowing of the skin and eyes, although many people have no obvious symptoms. Some infections clear without treatment, while others become chronic. Chronic hepatitis C can progressively damage the liver if it remains untreated.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:164:"हेपेटाइटिस सी एक वायरल संक्रमण है जो यकृत को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:645:"Hepatitis C is caused by infection with the hepatitis C virus. The virus is primarily transmitted when infected blood enters another person's bloodstream. Transmission can occur through sharing contaminated needles or equipment, unsafe medical procedures, or less commonly through sexual contact or from an infected mother to her baby. The hepatitis C virus is an RNA virus that infects liver cells and can persist in the body. After exposure, the immune response may clear the virus or fail to eliminate it, resulting in chronic infection. Persistent viral replication and inflammation can progressively produce fibrosis and other liver damage.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:146:"हेपेटाइटिस सी वायरस मुख्यतः संक्रमित रक्त से फैलता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:665:"Risk factors include sharing needles or other injection equipment, receiving medical care with inadequately sterilized equipment, having a blood transfusion or organ transplant before modern screening was introduced, and other exposures to infected blood. Risk can also increase with certain sexual or occupational exposures. People who inject drugs or share injection equipment have an important risk of blood exposure. Other risks include accidental exposure to infected blood, nonsterile tattooing or piercing equipment, and certain healthcare exposures. People with previous transfusions or transplants before routine HCV screening may also have increased risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"असुरक्षित इंजेक्शन और संक्रमित रक्त जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:613:"Hepatitis C is diagnosed with blood tests. An antibody test can show whether a person has been exposed to the virus, while an HCV RNA test confirms whether active infection is present. Additional blood tests and liver assessment help evaluate liver health and the extent of disease. Testing generally begins with an HCV antibody blood test. If antibodies are detected, an HCV RNA test determines whether the virus is currently present. Further assessment may include liver enzyme tests, blood counts, fibrosis assessment, and imaging or other investigations when needed to evaluate liver damage and complications.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:150:"निदान में हेपेटाइटिस सी एंटीबॉडी और वायरल जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:614:"Hepatitis C can be prevented by avoiding contact with infected blood. Do not share needles, syringes, razors, or other items that may contain blood. Use properly sterilized medical and tattoo equipment and follow appropriate precautions when there is a risk of blood exposure. There is currently no widely available vaccine for hepatitis C. Prevention therefore depends on reducing blood exposure, using sterile injection and medical equipment, and ensuring appropriate infection-control practices. People with ongoing exposure risks should discuss testing and prevention strategies with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:106:"स्वच्छ सुई और जांचा हुआ रक्त उपयोग करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:359:"Hepatitis C requires medical evaluation because persistent infection can cause progressive liver disease. Seek prompt assessment for jaundice, significant abdominal swelling, severe abdominal pain, unusual bleeding, confusion, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe bleeding, altered consciousness, or signs of acute liver failure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:61;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:63;s:10:"disease_id";i:111;s:11:"overview_en";s:644:"Liver cirrhosis is advanced scarring of the liver that develops after long-term or repeated liver injury. Scar tissue gradually replaces healthy liver tissue and can interfere with blood flow and the liver's ability to perform important functions. Causes include chronic viral hepatitis, long-term alcohol-related liver injury, metabolic liver disease, and other conditions that produce persistent liver damage. Early cirrhosis may cause few symptoms, while advanced disease can lead to fluid accumulation, jaundice, bleeding problems, confusion, or other serious complications. Managing the underlying cause can help slow further liver damage.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:157:"लिवर सिरोसिस यकृत में उन्नत स्तर की क्षति और फाइब्रोसिस है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:536:"Cirrhosis develops when repeated or long-term liver injury causes inflammation and replacement of normal liver tissue with scar tissue. Common causes include chronic hepatitis B or C infection, long-term alcohol-related liver injury, metabolic dysfunction-associated fatty liver disease, and certain autoimmune, genetic, or bile-duct disorders. Some medicines and toxins can also cause chronic liver injury. When the underlying injury continues, progressive scarring can alter the structure of the liver and impair its normal functions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:185:"इसके प्रमुख कारण शराब, हेपेटाइटिस संक्रमण और दीर्घकालिक यकृत रोग हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:493:"Risk factors for cirrhosis include long-term alcohol misuse, chronic hepatitis B or C infection, metabolic dysfunction-associated fatty liver disease, obesity, diabetes, and conditions that cause persistent liver inflammation or injury. Certain inherited disorders, autoimmune diseases, and chronic bile-duct disorders can also increase risk. The likelihood of progression depends on the underlying cause, duration and severity of liver injury, and whether the cause is identified and treated.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:950:"सिरोसिस का जोखिम लंबे समय तक अधिक शराब के सेवन, लंबे समय तक रहने वाले हेपेटाइटिस बी या सी संक्रमण, फैटी लिवर रोग से जुड़ी मेटाबॉलिक स्थितियों तथा कुछ ऑटोइम्यून, आनुवंशिक या पित्त-नली संबंधी विकारों से बढ़ सकता है। मोटापा, मधुमेह और मेटाबॉलिक सिंड्रोम फैटी लिवर रोग में योगदान दे सकते हैं। जोखिम का स्तर मूल लिवर रोग और व्यक्ति के चिकित्सा इतिहास पर निर्भर करता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:514:"Diagnosis of cirrhosis may involve medical history, physical examination, blood tests, imaging, and sometimes specialized assessment of liver stiffness. Blood tests can evaluate liver function, blood-cell counts, clotting, and evidence of underlying causes. Ultrasound and other imaging methods can assess liver structure, blood flow, and complications. Elastography can estimate liver stiffness. In selected cases, additional testing or liver biopsy may be considered to clarify the diagnosis or underlying cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:188:"निदान में लिवर जांच, अल्ट्रासाउंड, फाइब्रोस्कैन और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:606:"Preventing cirrhosis involves preventing or treating the conditions that cause long-term liver injury. Avoiding excessive alcohol, preventing hepatitis B infection through vaccination when appropriate, reducing exposure to hepatitis C, maintaining a healthy weight, and managing diabetes and metabolic conditions can reduce liver-related risk. People with chronic hepatitis, fatty liver disease, autoimmune liver disease, or other liver disorders should follow medical advice and undergo appropriate monitoring. Avoiding unnecessary medicines or supplements that may injure the liver can also be important.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1119:"लिवर सिरोसिस की रोकथाम का उद्देश्य लिवर को होने वाली क्षति कम करना और उन रोगों का उपचार करना है जो धीरे-धीरे लिवर में निशान बना सकते हैं। यदि शराब लिवर को नुकसान पहुँचा रही है तो उससे बचें, डॉक्टर की सलाह के बिना अनावश्यक दवाएँ या सप्लीमेंट न लें और पुराने लिवर रोगों का उचित उपचार कराएँ। हेपेटाइटिस A और B के टीके, उचित परिस्थितियों में हेपेटाइटिस C की जाँच और संतुलित आहार भी आगे की क्षति तथा जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:306:"Seek urgent medical attention for vomiting blood, black or bloody stools, new or worsening confusion, severe abdominal swelling or pain, jaundice that is rapidly worsening, fainting, fever with significant deterioration, or rapidly worsening weakness. These may indicate serious complications of cirrhosis.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:62;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:64;s:10:"disease_id";i:112;s:11:"overview_en";s:333:"Liver cancer is cancer that begins in the cells of the liver. The most common primary liver cancer in adults is hepatocellular carcinoma. Liver cancer can develop in people with chronic liver disease, including cirrhosis and chronic infection with hepatitis B or hepatitis C. Symptoms may not appear until the disease has progressed.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:135:"यकृत कैंसर यकृत में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:394:"Liver cancer develops when liver cells acquire changes that cause uncontrolled growth. Several conditions can increase the likelihood of these changes. Chronic hepatitis B or hepatitis C infection, cirrhosis, heavy alcohol use, and certain inherited or metabolic conditions can increase risk. Some liver cancers can also arise from exposure to particular toxins or other chronic liver injuries.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:148:"दीर्घकालिक हेपेटाइटिस और सिरोसिस इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:282:"Risk factors include chronic hepatitis B or hepatitis C infection, cirrhosis, long-term heavy alcohol use, certain inherited metabolic diseases, exposure to some toxins, and chronic liver inflammation. The risk is also affected by the underlying cause and severity of liver disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:134:"हेपेटाइटिस, सिरोसिस और शराब सेवन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:419:"Diagnosis of liver cancer may involve blood tests, imaging studies, and examination of the liver. Ultrasound, computed tomography, or magnetic resonance imaging can identify suspicious lesions and help determine their size and location. Blood tests may include liver function tests and tumor markers such as alpha-fetoprotein. A biopsy may be performed in selected cases when imaging does not provide a clear diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान में इमेजिंग, एएफपी जांच और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:345:"Risk of liver cancer can be reduced by preventing or treating chronic hepatitis B and hepatitis C, limiting heavy alcohol use, maintaining a healthy body weight, and managing conditions that cause chronic liver disease. People with cirrhosis or other high-risk liver conditions should follow recommended medical surveillance and treatment plans.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:161:"हेपेटाइटिस की रोकथाम करें और यकृत रोगों का समय पर उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:227:"Seek urgent medical attention for vomiting blood, black or bloody stools, severe abdominal pain, sudden confusion or extreme drowsiness, severe swelling of the abdomen, fainting, or rapidly worsening jaundice or other symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:63;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:65;s:10:"disease_id";i:114;s:11:"overview_en";s:326:"Cholecystitis is inflammation of the gallbladder, most often caused by a gallstone blocking the cystic duct. It commonly produces persistent pain in the upper right or upper middle abdomen and may cause tenderness, fever, nausea, or vomiting. The inflammation can become serious if the blockage persists or infection develops.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:199:"कोलेसिस्टाइटिस पित्ताशय की सूजन है जो प्रायः पित्त की पथरी के कारण होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:395:"Cholecystitis most commonly occurs when a gallstone blocks the cystic duct, preventing normal drainage of bile from the gallbladder. Continued blockage can cause irritation and inflammation of the gallbladder wall and may lead to infection. Less commonly, inflammation occurs without gallstones, particularly during severe illness, trauma, prolonged fasting, or other serious medical conditions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:135:"पित्त नली में पथरी फंसना इसका सबसे सामान्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:328:"Risk factors for gallstones and cholecystitis include increasing age, obesity, rapid weight loss, pregnancy, a family history of gallstones, and certain metabolic conditions. Some dietary and hormonal factors may also contribute. People who have previously had gallstones are at increased risk of recurrent gallbladder problems.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:132:"पित्त की पथरी, मोटापा और संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:348:"Diagnosis is based on the history and pattern of abdominal pain, physical examination, blood tests, and imaging. Ultrasound is commonly used to detect gallstones, gallbladder wall thickening, fluid around the gallbladder, or other signs of inflammation. Additional imaging such as a HIDA scan or CT may be used when the diagnosis remains uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:156:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड, रक्त परीक्षण और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:370:"Reducing major weight fluctuations, maintaining a healthy body weight, staying physically active, and following a balanced diet may help reduce the risk of gallstones and related gallbladder problems. People with recurrent upper abdominal pain, especially after meals, should seek medical evaluation. Prompt treatment of gallstone disease may help prevent complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:130:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें और पथरी का समय पर उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:313:"Cholecystitis requires prompt medical assessment. Seek urgent care for persistent right upper abdominal pain, fever, repeated vomiting, jaundice, severe tenderness, or rapidly worsening illness. Severe abdominal pain with fainting, confusion, or other signs of serious deterioration requires emergency assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:64;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:66;s:10:"disease_id";i:115;s:11:"overview_en";s:379:"Pancreatitis is inflammation of the pancreas, an organ that produces digestive enzymes and hormones such as insulin. It may occur suddenly as acute pancreatitis or persist or recur as chronic pancreatitis. Symptoms commonly include upper abdominal pain that may spread to the back, nausea and vomiting. Severe disease can cause complications involving digestion and other organs.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:191:"पैंक्रियाटाइटिस अग्न्याशय की सूजन है जो अचानक या दीर्घकालिक हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:383:"Common causes of pancreatitis include gallstones and heavy alcohol use. Other causes include certain medicines, high levels of triglycerides or calcium in the blood, abdominal injury, infections, inherited conditions and abnormalities of the pancreatic or bile ducts. Some cases occur after medical procedures. Chronic pancreatitis may develop after repeated pancreatic inflammation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:163:"शराब, पित्त की पथरी, संक्रमण और कुछ दवाएं इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:323:"Risk factors include heavy alcohol consumption, gallstones, smoking, high blood triglyceride levels, certain genetic conditions and a family history of pancreatic disease. Previous episodes of pancreatitis can increase the risk of recurrence or chronic disease. Some medicines and medical conditions may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:149:"शराब, पित्त की पथरी, मोटापा और धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:382:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, blood tests and imaging. Blood tests commonly measure pancreatic enzymes such as lipase and may assess liver function and other abnormalities. Ultrasound, CT or MRI can help identify inflammation, gallstones or structural problems. Additional tests may be required when the cause is unclear or chronic pancreatitis is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:174:"निदान में रक्त जांच, सीटी स्कैन, अल्ट्रासाउंड और एमआरआई शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:373:"The risk of pancreatitis can sometimes be reduced by avoiding heavy alcohol use, not smoking and maintaining healthy blood triglyceride levels. Treatment of gallstones or other underlying conditions may prevent recurrent episodes. People who have previously had pancreatitis should follow medical advice about diet, alcohol, medicines and treatment of the underlying cause.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:127:"अत्यधिक शराब से बचें और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:336:"Pancreatitis can become serious and requires medical assessment. Seek urgent care for severe or persistent upper abdominal pain, repeated vomiting, fever, abdominal swelling, weakness, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe pain with fainting, confusion, severe breathing difficulty, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:65;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:67;s:10:"disease_id";i:116;s:11:"overview_en";s:348:"Pancreatic cancer is a malignant tumor arising from pancreatic tissue. It may develop in different parts of the pancreas and can affect digestion and other body functions as it progresses. Some cases are associated with smoking, chronic pancreatitis, genetic factors, diabetes, or other risk factors, while some occur without an identifiable cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:194:"अग्न्याशय कैंसर अग्न्याशय की कोशिकाओं से विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:393:"Pancreatic cancer develops when abnormal cells in pancreatic tissue grow uncontrollably and form a malignant tumor. The exact cause of most cases is not known. Factors associated with increased risk include smoking, chronic pancreatitis, obesity, diabetes, and certain inherited or genetic conditions. Some people develop pancreatic cancer without any clearly identifiable contributing factor.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:195:"धूम्रपान, दीर्घकालिक पैंक्रियाटाइटिस और आनुवंशिक कारक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:382:"Risk factors for pancreatic cancer include smoking, obesity, diabetes, chronic pancreatitis, increasing age, and a family history of pancreatic cancer. Certain inherited genetic conditions can also increase susceptibility. Having one or more risk factors does not mean that a person will develop pancreatic cancer, and some people develop the disease without any known risk factors.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:166:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा, मधुमेह और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:414:"Diagnosis of pancreatic cancer may involve imaging and laboratory evaluation to identify an abnormal growth and determine its extent. CT scanning and MRI can provide detailed images of the pancreas and surrounding structures. Endoscopic ultrasound may help examine the pancreas closely and obtain a tissue sample. Biopsy may be used to confirm cancer, particularly when tissue diagnosis is needed before treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:207:"निदान में सीटी स्कैन, एमआरआई, एंडोस्कोपिक अल्ट्रासाउंड और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:454:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent pancreatic cancer, and some risk factors cannot be changed. Avoiding tobacco use is an important preventive step because smoking increases risk. Maintaining a healthy weight, staying physically active, and managing long-term conditions such as diabetes may also help reduce risk. People with certain inherited conditions or a strong family history should discuss their individual risk with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1181:"पैंक्रियाटिक कैंसर को पूरी तरह रोकने का कोई निश्चित तरीका नहीं है और कुछ जोखिम कारकों को बदला नहीं जा सकता। फिर भी तंबाकू से बचना एक महत्वपूर्ण कदम है क्योंकि धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ाता है। स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखना, नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि करना और मधुमेह जैसी दीर्घकालिक स्थितियों को नियंत्रित करना भी जोखिम कम करने में मदद कर सकता है। कुछ आनुवंशिक स्थितियों या मजबूत पारिवारिक इतिहास वाले लोगों को स्वास्थ्यकर्मी से अपने जोखिम के बारे में चर्चा करनी चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:312:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for persistent upper abdominal or back pain, unexplained weight loss, jaundice, persistent vomiting, new digestive symptoms, or symptoms that progressively worsen. Emergency care is needed for significant bleeding, severe pain, severe weakness or fainting, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:66;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:68;s:10:"disease_id";i:118;s:11:"overview_en";s:543:"Crohn disease is a chronic inflammatory bowel disease that can cause inflammation anywhere along the digestive tract, although the small intestine and beginning of the large intestine are commonly affected. Symptoms may include persistent diarrhea, abdominal pain, weight loss, fatigue, reduced appetite, and sometimes fever. The disease can alternate between periods of active symptoms and remission. Inflammation may extend through the bowel wall and lead to complications such as narrowing, fistulas, abscesses, or nutritional deficiencies.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:262:"क्रोहन रोग एक दीर्घकालिक सूजनयुक्त आंत्र रोग है जो पाचन तंत्र के किसी भी भाग को प्रभावित कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:557:"The exact cause of Crohn disease is not fully understood. It is thought to result from an abnormal interaction between the immune system, intestinal microorganisms, genetic factors, and environmental influences. Family history can increase susceptibility, but most people with a family history do not necessarily develop the disease. Smoking is associated with increased risk and can worsen disease activity. Crohn disease is not caused simply by stress or by eating a particular food, although diet and stress can influence symptoms in individual patients.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:207:"यह प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली की असामान्य गतिविधि और आनुवंशिक कारकों के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:532:"Risk factors for Crohn disease include a family history of inflammatory bowel disease, certain genetic factors, smoking, and some environmental influences. The disease can occur at any age but is often diagnosed in adolescents and young adults. People with certain immune-related conditions may have increased susceptibility. Smoking is particularly important because it can increase disease activity and complications. Diet does not directly cause Crohn disease, although individual foods may worsen symptoms during active disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:183:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, धूम्रपान और ऑटोइम्यून प्रवृत्ति जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:527:"Crohn disease is diagnosed using a combination of medical history, physical examination, laboratory tests, stool testing, endoscopy, and imaging. Blood tests may identify anemia or inflammation, while stool tests can help assess intestinal inflammation and exclude infections. Colonoscopy with examination of the terminal ileum and biopsy is commonly important. Cross-sectional imaging such as MRI or CT enterography may evaluate the small intestine and complications. No single test establishes Crohn disease in every patient.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:182:"निदान में कोलोनोस्कोपी, इमेजिंग, बायोप्सी और रक्त परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:579:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent Crohn disease because its causes are complex and include genetic and immune factors. Not smoking is particularly important because smoking can increase disease activity and complications. People with Crohn disease can reduce complications through regular medical follow-up, appropriate treatment, nutritional support, and monitoring for deficiencies. Individual food triggers can be identified with professional guidance. Vaccination and preventive health care are also important for people receiving medicines that affect the immune system.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:131:"धूम्रपान से बचें और चिकित्सकीय सलाह का पालन करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:350:"Seek prompt medical assessment for severe or worsening abdominal pain, persistent vomiting or diarrhea, blood in the stool, fever, dehydration, significant weight loss, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe abdominal pain with marked swelling, persistent vomiting, heavy bleeding, fainting, or signs of bowel obstruction.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:67;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:69;s:10:"disease_id";i:119;s:11:"overview_en";s:422:"Ulcerative colitis is a chronic inflammatory bowel disease in which inflammation and ulcers develop in the lining of the rectum and colon. Symptoms commonly include abdominal pain, cramping, diarrhea, and blood or pus in the stool. Symptoms may range from mild to severe and often occur in periods of flares followed by remission. The disease can occur at any age but commonly begins during adolescence or early adulthood.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:159:"अल्सरेटिव कोलाइटिस बड़ी आंत और मलाशय की दीर्घकालिक सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:445:"The exact cause of ulcerative colitis is not known. The condition involves an abnormal immune response in the digestive tract, although it is not clear exactly what triggers that response. Genetic and environmental factors may contribute. A family history of ulcerative colitis or other autoimmune diseases can increase risk. Stress and certain foods may worsen symptoms in some people but are not considered the underlying cause of the disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:165:"प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली की गड़बड़ी और आनुवंशिक कारक इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:401:"Risk factors include having a family history of ulcerative colitis or other autoimmune diseases. The condition can occur at any age, with common periods of onset during adolescence and early adulthood and another peak later in life. Genetic susceptibility and other environmental or immune factors are thought to contribute. A person can develop ulcerative colitis even without a known family history.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और ऑटोइम्यून विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:506:"Diagnosis involves a medical history, physical examination, blood tests, stool tests, and examination of the colon. Colonoscopy with biopsy is commonly used to confirm the diagnosis and determine how much of the colon is affected. Tests such as complete blood count, C-reactive protein, erythrocyte sedimentation rate, and stool calprotectin or lactoferrin can help assess inflammation. Imaging or additional endoscopic tests may be used when needed to distinguish ulcerative colitis from other conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:168:"निदान में कोलोनोस्कोपी, बायोप्सी और प्रयोगशाला जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:275:"There is no known way to reliably prevent ulcerative colitis because its exact cause is not fully understood. Following medical advice, avoiding known personal triggers, not smoking, and maintaining regular medical care can help manage the condition and reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:130:"नियमित चिकित्सकीय देखभाल जटिलताओं को कम करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:314:"Seek prompt medical assessment for a significant increase in bloody diarrhea, severe abdominal pain, fever, dehydration, rapid worsening, or marked weakness. Emergency care may be required for heavy bleeding, severe abdominal swelling or pain, fainting, confusion, or other signs of a severe flare or complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:68;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:70;s:10:"disease_id";i:120;s:11:"overview_en";s:349:"Celiac disease is a chronic immune-mediated disorder in which gluten exposure damages the small intestine and can impair nutrient absorption. Symptoms vary and may include digestive problems, fatigue, or nutritional deficiencies; some people have few obvious symptoms. Celiac disease is distinct from wheat allergy and non-celiac gluten sensitivity.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:177:"सीलिएक रोग एक ऑटोइम्यून विकार है जो ग्लूटेन सेवन से सक्रिय होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:294:"Gluten in wheat, barley, and rye triggers an abnormal immune response in genetically susceptible people. Susceptibility commonly involves HLA-DQ2 or HLA-DQ8, but having these variants does not mean celiac disease will develop. Other factors influencing disease onset remain under investigation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:199:"ग्लूटेन प्रतिरक्षा प्रतिक्रिया उत्पन्न कर छोटी आंत को नुकसान पहुंचाता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:289:"Celiac disease is more likely in people with an affected close relative. It is also associated with conditions including type 1 diabetes, autoimmune thyroid disease, Down syndrome, and Turner syndrome. These associations do not mean that the other condition directly causes celiac disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और ऑटोइम्यून रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:444:"Evaluation generally includes celiac-related antibody blood tests and, when appropriate, upper endoscopy with small-intestinal biopsy. Results are interpreted alongside symptoms and medical history. Removing gluten before testing can affect results, so dietary changes should first be discussed with a healthcare professional. Genetic testing may help assess whether celiac disease is unlikely, but susceptibility genes alone do not confirm it.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान में एंटीबॉडी जांच और आंत की बायोप्सी शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:303:"Preventing further intestinal injury after diagnosis is different from preventing celiac disease from developing. For people with diagnosed celiac disease, gluten avoidance under medical and dietary guidance helps protect the intestine. Follow-up can identify nutritional deficiencies and complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:85:"सख्त ग्लूटेन-मुक्त आहार अपनाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:307:"Celiac disease usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for persistent diarrhea, significant weight loss, severe weakness, dehydration, anemia, or worsening symptoms. Emergency evaluation is needed for severe dehydration, fainting, significant bleeding, or another acute complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:69;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:71;s:10:"disease_id";i:121;s:11:"overview_en";s:372:"Diverticulitis occurs when small pouches that form in the wall of the colon become inflamed or otherwise develop complications. It commonly causes abdominal pain, often in the lower left abdomen, and may also cause fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, constipation, or diarrhea. Severe cases can lead to complications such as abscess, obstruction, perforation, or peritonitis.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:172:"डाइवर्टिकुलाइटिस बड़ी आंत की छोटी थैलियों की सूजन या संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:347:"The exact cause of diverticulitis is not fully understood. Diverticulitis occurs in people who have diverticula, or small pouches, in the colon wall. Factors that may contribute to diverticular disease include a diet low in fiber, higher intake of red meat, physical inactivity, obesity, smoking, and certain medicines such as NSAIDs and steroids.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:154:"डाइवर्टिकुला में अवरोध और सूजन संक्रमण का कारण बन सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:360:"Risk factors for diverticulitis include a diet low in fiber and high in red meat, physical inactivity, obesity, smoking, and use of certain medicines such as nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs and steroids. Having diverticula is the underlying condition in which diverticulitis occurs. Genetic and other biological factors may also influence individual risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:152:"कम फाइबर वाला आहार, मोटापा और बढ़ती उम्र जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:456:"Diagnosis of diverticulitis begins with a medical history and physical examination, including assessment of abdominal pain and tenderness. Blood tests may help identify inflammation or complications. CT scanning is commonly used to evaluate suspected diverticulitis and its complications, while ultrasound or MRI may also be used in appropriate situations. Colonoscopy may be recommended in selected cases to evaluate the colon or exclude other conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:139:"निदान में सीटी स्कैन, परीक्षण और रक्त जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:413:"Some lifestyle measures may lower the risk of diverticulitis. A diet higher in fiber and lower in red meat may be helpful, together with regular physical activity, maintaining a healthy weight, and avoiding smoking. People with diverticular disease should discuss medicines that may affect risk with a healthcare professional. Individual dietary recommendations may vary depending on symptoms and medical history.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:140:"पर्याप्त फाइबर लें और शरीर में पानी की कमी न होने दें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:373:"Diverticulitis requires prompt assessment when symptoms are significant. Seek urgent care for persistent or severe lower abdominal pain, fever, repeated vomiting, abdominal swelling, inability to pass stool or gas, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe pain with fainting, confusion, heavy bleeding, or signs of perforation or severe infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:70;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:72;s:10:"disease_id";i:122;s:11:"overview_en";s:353:"Appendicitis is inflammation of the appendix, a small pouch attached to the large intestine. It commonly causes pain that begins near the belly button and later moves toward the lower right abdomen. Loss of appetite, nausea, vomiting and fever may occur. If the appendix ruptures, infection can spread inside the abdomen and cause serious complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:204:"एपेंडिसाइटिस अपेंडिक्स की सूजन है और अक्सर तत्काल उपचार की आवश्यकता होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:348:"Appendicitis usually develops when the opening of the appendix becomes blocked. The blockage may result from hardened stool, swelling of lymphoid tissue or, less commonly, another obstruction. Bacteria can then multiply inside the appendix, causing inflammation and swelling. The condition can progress rapidly and may lead to rupture if untreated.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:145:"अपेंडिक्स में अवरोध संक्रमण और सूजन का कारण बन सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:313:"Appendicitis can occur at any age but is more common in children, teenagers and young adults. A family history may increase susceptibility in some people. Conditions that cause blockage or inflammation of the appendix may contribute, although many people who develop appendicitis have no identifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:92:"संक्रमण और अवरोध जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:370:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern of abdominal pain, medical history and physical examination. Blood tests may show signs of inflammation or infection. Urine testing can help exclude urinary causes of abdominal pain. Ultrasound or CT scanning may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain. Prompt evaluation is important because untreated appendicitis can lead to rupture.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:154:"निदान में शारीरिक परीक्षण, रक्त जांच और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:399:"There is no reliable way to prevent appendicitis because the exact reason the appendix becomes blocked is often unknown. Maintaining a balanced diet with adequate fiber may support normal bowel function, but it does not guarantee prevention. The most important measure is prompt medical assessment when symptoms suggest appendicitis, particularly worsening abdominal pain, fever, nausea or vomiting.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:172:"निश्चित रोकथाम नहीं है, लेकिन समय पर उपचार जटिलताओं को कम करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:363:"Appendicitis is a medical emergency requiring immediate medical assessment. Seek emergency care for worsening abdominal pain, particularly when pain moves to the lower right abdomen, fever, nausea or vomiting, abdominal swelling, inability to pass gas, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Prompt treatment reduces the risk of complications such as a ruptured appendix.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:71;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:73;s:10:"disease_id";i:123;s:11:"overview_en";s:356:"Constipation is a common digestive problem characterized by infrequent bowel movements, hard or dry stools, difficulty passing stool, or a feeling that the bowel has not completely emptied. It may be temporary or chronic and can result from diet, inadequate fluid intake, reduced activity, medications, changes in routine, or underlying medical conditions.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:866:"कब्ज एक सामान्य पाचन संबंधी समस्या है जिसमें सप्ताह में तीन से कम बार मल त्याग हो सकता है, मल कठोर, सूखा या गांठदार हो सकता है, या मल त्याग कठिन अथवा दर्दनाक हो सकता है। कुछ लोगों को यह भी महसूस होता है कि पूरा मल बाहर नहीं निकला। कब्ज थोड़े समय के लिए या लंबे समय तक रह सकता है और कभी-कभी किसी अन्य चिकित्सीय समस्या का लक्षण भी हो सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:316:"Constipation can result from insufficient dietary fiber, inadequate fluid intake, low physical activity, changes in routine, ignoring the urge to have a bowel movement, or changes in diet. Medications and medical conditions affecting the digestive tract, nerves, muscles, hormones, or metabolism can also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:155:"कम फाइबर, पानी की कमी और निष्क्रियता इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:398:"Risk factors include a low-fiber diet, inadequate fluid intake, physical inactivity, older age, changes in routine, pregnancy, frequent use of certain medicines, and conditions affecting the nervous system, muscles, hormones, or digestive tract. Previous episodes of constipation may also increase recurrence. Having a risk factor does not necessarily mean that a person will develop the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:161:"खराब आहार, पानी की कमी और निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली जोखिम बढ़ाती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:310:"Constipation is usually diagnosed from symptoms, bowel habits, diet, medications, and medical history. Physical examination may be performed, and additional blood tests, imaging, colon evaluation, or other tests may be considered when symptoms are persistent, severe, unusual, or associated with warning signs.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:165:"निदान सामान्यतः लक्षणों और चिकित्सा इतिहास पर आधारित होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:342:"Regular physical activity, adequate dietary fiber, sufficient fluids, and responding to the urge to have a bowel movement can help prevent constipation. Medication-related constipation may sometimes be reduced by reviewing medicines with a healthcare professional. People with persistent symptoms should seek evaluation for underlying causes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:154:"फाइबर युक्त भोजन करें, व्यायाम करें और पर्याप्त पानी पिएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:339:"Constipation usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for persistent symptoms, severe abdominal pain, vomiting, significant abdominal swelling, blood in the stool, unexplained weight loss, or a sudden change in bowel habits. Emergency evaluation is needed for severe pain with vomiting or signs of bowel obstruction.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:72;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:74;s:10:"disease_id";i:124;s:11:"overview_en";s:376:"Chronic constipation is a long-lasting problem involving infrequent bowel movements, hard or difficult-to-pass stools, excessive straining, or a feeling that the bowel has not emptied completely. Symptoms may persist for weeks or longer and can affect daily activities. Constipation may result from diet, lifestyle, medicines, medical conditions, or changes in bowel function.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:158:"दीर्घकालिक कब्ज लंबे समय तक बनी रहने वाली कब्ज की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:376:"Chronic constipation may result from inadequate fiber or fluid intake, low physical activity, ignoring the urge to have a bowel movement, or changes in daily routine. Medicines such as some pain relievers, iron supplements, and certain antacids can contribute. Medical conditions affecting the digestive system, nerves, hormones, or pelvic muscles may also cause constipation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:122:"यह आहार, दवाओं या अन्य रोगों के कारण हो सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:327:"Risk factors include a low-fiber diet, inadequate fluid intake, physical inactivity, older age, changes in routine, frequent use of certain medicines, and a history of constipation. Pregnancy and some neurological, hormonal, or digestive disorders can also increase the risk. Psychological stress may contribute in some people.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:152:"कम फाइबर, निष्क्रियता, उम्र और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:339:"Diagnosis is usually based on symptoms, bowel habits, diet, medication use, and medical history. A physical examination may be performed. Depending on the symptoms and risk factors, blood tests, imaging, colon evaluation, or specialized tests of bowel movement and pelvic muscle function may be recommended to identify an underlying cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:151:"निदान में शारीरिक परीक्षण और विशेष जांच शामिल हो सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:349:"Chronic constipation may be reduced by eating enough dietary fiber, drinking adequate fluids, staying physically active, and responding to the urge to have a bowel movement. Establishing a regular toilet routine may help. Medicines that contribute to constipation should be reviewed with a healthcare professional rather than stopped without advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:154:"स्वस्थ मल त्याग की आदतें और पर्याप्त फाइबर सेवन बनाए रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:360:"Chronic constipation should be assessed when persistent or changing. Seek prompt medical evaluation for blood in the stool, unexplained weight loss, persistent vomiting, severe abdominal pain, marked abdominal swelling, anemia, or a new significant change in bowel habits. Severe pain with vomiting or inability to pass stool or gas requires urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:73;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:75;s:10:"disease_id";i:125;s:11:"overview_en";s:386:"Diarrhea means passing loose or watery stools more often than is normal for a person. It can be sudden and short-lived or continue for several weeks. Common symptoms include frequent bowel movements, abdominal cramps, urgency, nausea, and sometimes fever or blood in the stool. The main concern with significant diarrhea is loss of water and electrolytes, which can lead to dehydration.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:167:"दस्त एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें बार-बार पतला या पानी जैसा मल आता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:435:"Diarrhea can be caused by infections from viruses, bacteria, or parasites, contaminated food or water, food intolerances, and side effects of medicines. It can also occur with conditions such as irritable bowel syndrome, inflammatory bowel disease, celiac disease, or other disorders that affect digestion and absorption. Some cases follow changes in diet or stress, while persistent diarrhea may have a more specific underlying cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:171:"यह सामान्यतः संक्रमण, दूषित भोजन या पाचन विकारों के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:429:"Risk factors include eating contaminated food, drinking unsafe water, traveling to areas where sanitation is limited, poor hand hygiene, and contact with someone who has an infectious illness. Antibiotic use can disturb normal intestinal bacteria and cause diarrhea. Certain digestive disorders, food intolerances, weakened immune function, and some medicines can also increase the likelihood of recurrent or persistent diarrhea.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:144:"खराब स्वच्छता, दूषित भोजन और संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:458:"Short-term diarrhea is often diagnosed from symptoms, medical history, and a physical examination. Healthcare professionals assess duration, frequency, recent food or travel exposures, medicines, and signs of dehydration. Stool tests may be needed when diarrhea is severe, persistent, bloody, associated with fever, or suspected to be caused by an infection. Blood tests or other investigations may be used when an underlying digestive disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:169:"निदान लक्षणों तथा आवश्यकता अनुसार मल परीक्षण पर आधारित होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:519:"Many infectious causes of diarrhea can be reduced through careful handwashing, safe preparation and storage of food, drinking treated or safe water, and avoiding contaminated food. Travelers should follow local food and water safety precautions. Appropriate vaccination can prevent some infections that cause diarrhea. Using antibiotics only when prescribed can also reduce certain medication-related complications. People with ongoing diarrhea should seek medical care when symptoms are severe or dehydration develops.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:160:"अच्छी स्वच्छता रखें और सुरक्षित भोजन तथा पानी का उपयोग करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:312:"Seek prompt medical assessment for persistent or severe diarrhea, blood or black stools, high fever, significant abdominal pain, repeated vomiting, signs of dehydration, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe dehydration, fainting, confusion, or significant gastrointestinal bleeding.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:74;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:76;s:10:"disease_id";i:126;s:11:"overview_en";s:270:"Chronic diarrhea means frequent loose or watery stools that continue for several weeks or longer. It can have many causes, including digestive disorders, infections, medicines, food intolerances, and conditions affecting how the intestine absorbs or processes nutrients.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:161:"दीर्घकालिक दस्त चार सप्ताह से अधिक समय तक रहने वाले दस्त हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:493:"Chronic diarrhea can have many causes because it may result from disorders affecting digestion, absorption, or movement through the gastrointestinal tract. Possible causes include persistent infections, food intolerances such as lactose intolerance, medication effects, irritable bowel syndrome, inflammatory bowel diseases such as Crohn disease and ulcerative colitis, and other diseases affecting the stomach, small intestine, or colon. Previous gastrointestinal surgery can also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:212:"यह दीर्घकालिक संक्रमण, सूजनयुक्त आंत्र रोग या अवशोषण विकारों के कारण हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:399:"Risk factors depend on the underlying cause. They may include exposure to contaminated food or water, use of medicines that can cause diarrhea, food intolerance, inflammatory or other chronic gastrointestinal disorders, and previous digestive tract surgery. A history of recurrent intestinal symptoms or diseases affecting nutrient absorption may also increase the likelihood of persistent diarrhea.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:109:"पाचन विकार और आंत्र रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:481:"Diagnosis of chronic diarrhea begins with a detailed history of the duration, frequency, appearance, and triggers of bowel movements, together with a physical examination. Healthcare providers may use blood tests, stool studies, tests for infection or inflammation, and other investigations depending on the suspected cause. Additional testing such as imaging, endoscopy, or specialized tests may be required when symptoms persist or an underlying intestinal disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:162:"निदान में मल जांच, रक्त जांच और कोलोनोस्कोपी शामिल हो सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:477:"Prevention depends on the underlying cause. Good hand hygiene, safe food preparation, and drinking safe water can reduce infectious causes. Avoiding foods that consistently trigger symptoms and using medicines only as directed can help prevent some episodes. People with chronic gastrointestinal disorders should follow their treatment plan and seek medical advice for persistent diarrhea, dehydration, blood in the stool, unexplained weight loss, or other concerning symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:114:"मूल कारणों का समय पर उपचार सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:357:"Chronic diarrhea should be medically assessed when persistent or recurrent. Seek prompt care for dehydration, blood or black stools, fever, significant abdominal pain, unexplained weight loss, persistent vomiting, or symptoms that are worsening. Emergency care is needed for severe dehydration, fainting, confusion, or significant gastrointestinal bleeding.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:75;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:77;s:10:"disease_id";i:127;s:11:"overview_en";s:356:"Hemorrhoids are swollen or enlarged veins in the lower rectum or around the anus. They may occur inside the rectum or beneath the skin around the anus and can cause bleeding, itching, irritation, swelling, discomfort, or pain. Hemorrhoids are common and may develop when increased pressure is placed on the veins during bowel movements or other activities.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:195:"बवासीर मलाशय या गुदा की सूजी हुई नसें हैं जो दर्द और रक्तस्राव कर सकती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:410:"Hemorrhoids commonly develop because of increased pressure on the veins around the anus and lower rectum. Constipation, repeated straining during bowel movements, prolonged sitting on the toilet, pregnancy, obesity, and heavy lifting can increase pressure. Persistent diarrhea may also contribute. Changes in the supporting tissues of the rectum and anus with aging can make hemorrhoids more likely to develop.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:158:"कब्ज, जोर लगाना, मोटापा और गर्भावस्था इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:424:"Risk factors include a low-fiber diet, chronic constipation or diarrhea, repeated straining during bowel movements, prolonged sitting, obesity, pregnancy, and increasing age. Activities that repeatedly increase abdominal pressure, including heavy lifting, may also contribute. People who spend long periods sitting on the toilet or have persistent bowel problems may have a higher risk of developing symptomatic hemorrhoids.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:156:"कम फाइबर आहार, मोटापा और लंबे समय तक बैठना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:373:"Diagnosis is usually based on symptoms and examination of the anus and rectum. External hemorrhoids may be visible during inspection, while internal hemorrhoids may require a digital rectal examination or anoscopy for evaluation. Additional testing may be recommended when bleeding is unexplained, symptoms are unusual, or another intestinal condition needs to be excluded.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:171:"निदान परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार एनोस्कोपी द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:434:"Hemorrhoids can often be prevented or reduced by keeping stools soft and avoiding straining during bowel movements. Eating enough fiber, drinking adequate fluids, exercising regularly, and treating constipation can help. Avoid sitting on the toilet for long periods and respond to the urge to have a bowel movement rather than repeatedly delaying it. Maintaining a healthy weight may also reduce pressure on the veins around the anus.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1015:"बवासीर की रोकथाम या कमी के लिए मल को नरम रखना और मल त्याग के समय अत्यधिक जोर लगाने से बचना महत्वपूर्ण है। पर्याप्त फाइबर लें, स्वास्थ्यकर्मी की सलाह के अनुसार पर्याप्त पानी और अन्य तरल पिएँ, नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि करें, जोर न लगाएँ और लंबे समय तक शौचालय पर न बैठें। कब्ज को नियंत्रित करना और नियमित रूप से भारी वजन उठाने से बचना गुदा तथा निचले मलाशय की नसों पर दबाव कम करने में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:313:"Hemorrhoids usually do not require emergency care. Seek medical assessment for persistent or significant rectal bleeding, severe pain, a rapidly enlarging or very painful lump, dizziness, weakness, or symptoms that do not improve. Heavy bleeding, fainting, or signs of unstable circulation require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:76;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:78;s:10:"disease_id";i:128;s:11:"overview_en";s:521:"An anal fissure is a small tear in the lining of the anus. It commonly causes sharp or burning pain during and after bowel movements and may produce a small amount of bright red blood on toilet paper or the surface of the stool. Anal fissures often develop when hard or large stools stretch the anal canal, although frequent diarrhea, childbirth, inflammatory bowel disease, or other conditions can also contribute. Most acute fissures improve with measures that keep stools soft and reduce strain during bowel movements.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:181:"गुदा विदर गुदा की परत में छोटा चीरा है जो मल त्याग के समय दर्द करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:570:"Anal fissures most commonly result from trauma to the anal canal when passing hard, dry, or unusually large stools. Repeated straining can increase the likelihood of a tear and may prevent it from healing. Frequent loose stools or prolonged diarrhea can also irritate the anal lining. Less commonly, fissures may be associated with inflammatory bowel disease, infections, previous anal surgery, childbirth, or other medical conditions. When a fissure is persistent, recurrent, or located in an unusual position, the clinician may investigate for an underlying condition.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:100:"कब्ज और कठोर मल इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:536:"Risk factors for anal fissure include chronic constipation, passing hard stools, repeated straining, and frequent diarrhea. Pregnancy and childbirth can increase risk because of pressure and changes affecting the pelvic and anal region. Inflammatory bowel disease and some infections or other anorectal conditions can also predispose to fissures. Previous anal procedures may occasionally contribute. A low-fiber diet can make stools harder and increase the likelihood of trauma, particularly when combined with inadequate fluid intake.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:121:"कम फाइबर और दीर्घकालिक कब्ज जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:583:"Anal fissure is usually diagnosed through the history of pain and bleeding together with examination of the anal area. A typical fissure may be visible as a small linear tear, often near the front or back of the anal opening. Examination can be uncomfortable, particularly during an acute episode, so it may be limited when pain is severe. Additional testing is generally unnecessary for a straightforward fissure. Persistent, recurrent, atypical, or multiple fissures may require further evaluation to identify inflammatory bowel disease, infection, or another underlying condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:526:"निदान आमतौर पर दर्दनाक मल त्याग, गुदा से रक्तस्राव और गुदा क्षेत्र की जांच के आधार पर किया जाता है। लंबे समय तक रहने या असामान्य फिशर में अंतर्निहित कारण की पहचान के लिए अतिरिक्त जांच आवश्यक हो सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:562:"Keeping stools soft and easy to pass is central to preventing anal fissures. Adequate dietary fiber and fluid intake can help maintain regular bowel movements, while avoiding unnecessary straining may reduce trauma to the anal canal. People prone to constipation may benefit from medical advice about appropriate stool-softening measures. Treating persistent diarrhea or underlying bowel disease can also reduce irritation. Good toilet habits and prompt attention to recurrent anal pain or bleeding may help prevent a short-term fissure from becoming persistent.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:95:"फाइबर और पानी से मल को नरम बनाए रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:307:"Anal fissures usually improve with appropriate care and are not emergencies. Seek medical assessment for persistent or severe pain, recurrent bleeding, a fissure that does not heal, or symptoms that are worsening. Significant bleeding, fainting, or severe unexplained rectal pain requires prompt evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:77;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:79;s:10:"disease_id";i:129;s:11:"overview_en";s:296:"An anal fistula is an abnormal tunnel that develops between the inside of the anus or rectum and the skin near the anus. It often develops after an infection or abscess in an anal gland. Symptoms may include persistent drainage, pain, swelling, irritation, or recurrent abscesses around the anus.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:158:"भगंदर गुदा नलिका और आसपास की त्वचा के बीच असामान्य मार्ग है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:379:"An anal fistula most commonly develops after an anal abscess, which is an infected cavity near the anus. When an abscess drains but the abnormal passage between the infected gland and the skin remains, a fistula may form. Other causes include inflammatory bowel disease, repeated infections, injury, previous surgery, and certain conditions affecting the tissues around the anus.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:992:"अधिकांश एनल फिस्टुला गुदा के पास संक्रमण के कारण बने एनल एब्सेस के बाद विकसित होते हैं। जब एब्सेस से मवाद निकल जाता है लेकिन घाव ठीक से नहीं भरता, तो आंत के अंतिम हिस्से और आसपास की त्वचा के बीच एक छोटी नली बनी रह सकती है। कम सामान्य कारणों में क्रोहन रोग, डायवर्टिकुलाइटिस, हिड्राडेनाइटिस सप्यूराटिवा, तपेदिक, HIV संक्रमण और गुदा के पास की सर्जरी के बाद होने वाली जटिलताएँ शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:306:"Risk factors include a previous anal abscess, inflammatory bowel disease such as Crohn disease, recurrent infections in the anal region, previous anal or rectal surgery, and conditions that interfere with normal healing or immunity. A history of an anal fistula also increases the likelihood of recurrence.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:115:"संक्रमण और आंत्र सूजन रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"An anal fistula is diagnosed through a medical history and examination of the anus and surrounding skin. The healthcare professional may look for an external opening, drainage, swelling, or tenderness. A digital rectal examination may help identify the tract. Imaging such as MRI or ultrasound may be used when the fistula is complex, recurrent, or difficult to identify during examination.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:105:"निदान में परीक्षण और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:361:"Preventing anal fistula mainly involves reducing the risk of anal abscesses and treating infections promptly. People with inflammatory bowel disease should follow appropriate medical treatment and monitoring. Persistent pain, swelling, drainage, or recurrent abscesses around the anus should be evaluated by a healthcare professional rather than left untreated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:100:"गुदा संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:329:"An anal fistula should be assessed by a healthcare professional because it may be associated with ongoing infection or an abscess. Seek prompt care for increasing pain, swelling, redness, fever, pus or drainage, or worsening symptoms. Severe pain with fever or rapidly spreading infection requires urgent or emergency assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:78;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:80;s:10:"disease_id";i:130;s:11:"overview_en";s:377:"Rectal prolapse occurs when part or all of the rectum protrudes through the anus. It may range from a small amount of tissue that appears during straining to a complete prolapse that remains outside the body. The condition is more common with increasing age and may be associated with chronic constipation, repeated straining, pelvic floor weakness, or previous pelvic surgery.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:155:"रेक्टल प्रोलैप्स में मलाशय का भाग गुदा से बाहर निकल आता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:358:"Rectal prolapse can develop when the tissues supporting the rectum become weakened or stretched. Chronic constipation and repeated straining, prolonged diarrhea, pelvic floor weakness, childbirth, aging, and previous pelvic or rectal surgery may contribute. Neurologic conditions and other disorders affecting pelvic support can also increase susceptibility.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:171:"लगातार जोर लगाना और कमजोर पेल्विक मांसपेशियां सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:318:"Risk factors include increasing age, chronic constipation, repeated straining during bowel movements, chronic diarrhea, pelvic floor weakness, previous pelvic or rectal surgery, childbirth, and certain neurologic or connective-tissue disorders. A history of rectal prolapse also increases the likelihood of recurrence.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:169:"कब्ज, बढ़ती उम्र और कमजोर पेल्विक मांसपेशियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:398:"Diagnosis is usually based on symptoms and physical examination, often including assessment while the patient strains or bears down. The clinician may examine the rectum and pelvic floor and determine whether the prolapse is partial or complete. Additional tests such as colonoscopy, imaging, or anorectal studies may be considered when symptoms or the clinical situation suggest another condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:142:"निदान सामान्यतः शारीरिक परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:381:"Preventive measures focus on maintaining regular, soft bowel movements and avoiding repeated straining. Adequate fiber and fluid intake, appropriate treatment of constipation, regular physical activity, and management of chronic diarrhea may help protect pelvic and rectal support tissues. Persistent rectal protrusion or difficulty controlling bowel movements should be evaluated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:143:"कब्ज का उपचार करें और पेल्विक मांसपेशियां मजबूत रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:358:"Rectal prolapse requires medical assessment. Seek prompt care when the rectum protrudes from the anus, especially if it cannot be gently reduced or is associated with significant bleeding or pain. Emergency assessment is needed if the prolapsed tissue becomes severely painful, dark or discolored, or if there is heavy bleeding or other sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:79;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:81;s:10:"disease_id";i:131;s:11:"overview_en";s:598:"Colon cancer is a malignant growth that develops in the lining of the colon, part of the large intestine. It often begins as a polyp or other abnormal growth that can gradually develop into cancer over time. Early colon cancer may cause few or no noticeable symptoms. Possible symptoms include changes in bowel habits, blood in the stool, abdominal discomfort, unexplained weight loss, weakness, or anemia caused by chronic blood loss. Screening can identify some precancerous polyps and cancers before symptoms appear, while diagnosis and staging help determine the appropriate treatment approach.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:145:"कोलन कैंसर बड़ी आंत में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:508:"Colon cancer develops when cells in the lining of the colon acquire changes that allow them to grow and divide abnormally. Many cases begin with adenomatous or other precancerous polyps that gradually acquire additional cellular changes. Genetic and inherited factors can contribute, while environmental and lifestyle factors may also influence risk. Chronic inflammation of the bowel and certain inherited conditions can increase susceptibility. The exact combination of factors differs between individuals.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:151:"आनुवंशिकता, धूम्रपान, मोटापा और आहार इसके जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:466:"Risk factors for colon cancer include increasing age, a personal or family history of colorectal cancer or certain polyps, inherited cancer syndromes, inflammatory bowel disease, smoking, heavy alcohol use, physical inactivity, and certain dietary patterns. Excess body weight and metabolic health factors may also be associated with increased risk. Risk is influenced by multiple factors, and colon cancer can occur in people who do not have an obvious risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:160:"उम्र, मोटापा, धूम्रपान और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:490:"Colon cancer may be detected through screening tests such as stool-based testing or colonoscopy, depending on age, risk, and applicable screening recommendations. When cancer is suspected, colonoscopy allows direct examination of the colon and removal or biopsy of abnormal tissue. A biopsy is used to establish the diagnosis of cancer. Additional imaging and laboratory evaluation may be performed to determine the stage of disease and whether it has spread to lymph nodes or other organs.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:146:"निदान में कोलोनोस्कोपी, बायोप्सी और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:559:"The risk of colon cancer may be reduced through recommended colorectal cancer screening, avoiding tobacco, limiting excessive alcohol use, maintaining a healthy body weight, staying physically active, and following a balanced dietary pattern. Screening is particularly important because precancerous polyps can sometimes be detected and removed before they become cancer. People with a family history, inherited cancer syndrome, inflammatory bowel disease, or other increased-risk conditions may require a different screening approach based on medical advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:130:"स्क्रीनिंग और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली जोखिम कम करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:387:"Colon cancer requires medical evaluation and ongoing treatment. Seek prompt assessment for blood in the stool, persistent changes in bowel habits, unexplained weight loss, significant abdominal pain, weakness, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe abdominal pain, inability to pass stool or gas with vomiting, significant bleeding, fainting, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:80;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:82;s:10:"disease_id";i:132;s:11:"overview_en";s:310:"Rectal cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the tissues of the rectum, the lower part of the large intestine. It often develops from abnormal growths in the lining of the colon or rectum. The disease may cause changes in bowel habits or bleeding, although some people have no symptoms in its early stages.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:131:"रेक्टल कैंसर मलाशय में विकसित होने वाला कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:377:"Rectal cancer develops when cells in the rectum acquire changes that cause them to grow and divide abnormally. These changes can accumulate over time and may be influenced by inherited factors, personal health history, environmental exposures, and lifestyle-related factors. Precancerous colorectal polyps can sometimes develop into cancer if they are not detected and removed.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:103:"इसके जोखिम कारक कोलन कैंसर के समान हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:407:"Risk factors include increasing age, a family history of colorectal cancer, a personal history of colorectal cancer or high-risk adenomas, inherited conditions such as Lynch syndrome or familial adenomatous polyposis, long-standing inflammatory bowel disease, smoking, obesity, physical inactivity, and higher alcohol consumption. Having a risk factor does not mean that a person will develop rectal cancer.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:160:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा, उम्र और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:352:"Evaluation may include a medical and family history, physical examination, and examination of the rectum and colon. Tests can include a digital rectal examination, colonoscopy, biopsy, and laboratory or molecular tests when appropriate. Imaging studies are commonly used after diagnosis to determine the extent of the disease and whether it has spread.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:146:"निदान में कोलोनोस्कोपी, बायोप्सी और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:383:"Risk may be reduced by avoiding tobacco, maintaining a healthy weight, staying physically active, and limiting excessive alcohol consumption. Regular colorectal cancer screening can detect some cancers early and can also identify and allow removal of precancerous polyps. People with increased risk may need an individualized screening plan based on their medical and family history.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:111:"नियमित जांच प्रारंभिक पहचान में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:382:"Rectal cancer requires prompt medical evaluation and treatment. Seek assessment for rectal bleeding, persistent changes in bowel habits, narrowing of the stool, unexplained weight loss, persistent pelvic or abdominal pain, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for significant bleeding, severe abdominal pain, bowel obstruction symptoms, fainting, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:81;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:83;s:10:"disease_id";i:133;s:11:"overview_en";s:343:"Food poisoning is an illness caused by eating or drinking food or water contaminated with bacteria, viruses, parasites, toxins, or other harmful substances. Symptoms commonly include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, abdominal cramps, fever, and weakness. Most cases are short-lived, but severe illness can cause dehydration and other complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:187:"फूड पॉइजनिंग दूषित भोजन या पेय पदार्थों के सेवन से होने वाली बीमारी है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:364:"Food poisoning occurs when contaminated food or water contains bacteria, viruses, parasites, toxins, or harmful chemicals. Contamination may occur during farming, processing, handling, preparation, cooking, storage, or serving. Common sources include undercooked meat or eggs, contaminated produce, unsafe water, raw seafood, and foods kept at unsafe temperatures.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:174:"बैक्टीरिया, वायरस, परजीवी और विषाक्त पदार्थ इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:361:"Anyone can develop food poisoning, but the risk of serious illness is higher in young children, older adults, pregnant people, and those with weakened immune systems or certain chronic medical conditions. Eating raw or undercooked foods, drinking unsafe water, poor food hygiene, and improper refrigeration or cooking can increase exposure to harmful organisms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:140:"अस्वच्छ भोजन प्रबंधन और दूषित भोजन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:383:"Food poisoning is usually assessed from the symptoms, medical history, possible food or water exposures, and physical examination, particularly for signs of dehydration. Stool testing may be performed when symptoms are severe, persistent, bloody, or when identifying the causative organism is important. In some outbreaks, testing of suspected food may also help identify the source.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान सामान्यतः लक्षणों और इतिहास पर आधारित होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:448:"Food poisoning can often be reduced by washing hands before preparing or eating food, keeping raw and cooked foods separate, cooking foods thoroughly, and refrigerating perishable foods promptly. Use safe drinking water and wash produce appropriately. Avoid unpasteurized products and foods that may be contaminated, and take extra precautions when preparing food for young children, older adults, pregnant people, or people with weakened immunity.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:106:"भोजन की स्वच्छता के नियमों का पालन करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:368:"Food poisoning usually improves within a short period, but seek prompt medical care for bloody or pus-containing stools, persistent vomiting that prevents fluid intake, high fever, significant dehydration, severe abdominal pain, or diarrhea that is persistent or worsening. Emergency care is needed for severe dehydration, fainting, confusion, or significant bleeding.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:82;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:84;s:10:"disease_id";i:134;s:11:"overview_en";s:539:"Lactose intolerance occurs when the small intestine does not produce enough lactase, the enzyme needed to digest lactose, the natural sugar in milk. Undigested lactose passes into the large intestine, where bacteria break it down and produce gas and other substances that can cause symptoms. Typical symptoms include bloating, abdominal discomfort, gas, and diarrhea after consuming lactose-containing foods. The severity varies between individuals and depends partly on the amount of lactose consumed and the degree of lactase deficiency.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:174:"लैक्टोज असहिष्णुता में शरीर दूध की शर्करा को ठीक से नहीं पचा पाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:524:"The main cause of lactose intolerance is reduced production or activity of the lactase enzyme in the small intestine. Primary lactose intolerance develops when lactase production naturally decreases after childhood. Secondary lactose intolerance can occur when an intestinal disorder or injury damages the intestinal lining, temporarily reducing lactase activity. It may occur with certain gastrointestinal conditions or infections. Rarely, congenital or developmental problems can result in lactase deficiency from infancy.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:584:"लैक्टोज असहिष्णुता छोटी आंत में लैक्टेज एंजाइम की कमी के कारण लैक्टोज के ठीक से न पचने से होती है। यह उम्र के साथ लैक्टेज में कमी, आनुवंशिक कमी, आंत की क्षति, संक्रमण या सीलिएक और क्रोहन रोग जैसी स्थितियों से जुड़ी हो सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:481:"Risk depends on the underlying type of lactose intolerance. Primary lactase reduction is common with increasing age in many populations. Secondary deficiency may occur after intestinal infections, inflammatory disorders, or other conditions that affect the small intestinal lining. Genetic background also influences lactase persistence into adulthood. The amount of lactose consumed, the food in which it occurs, and individual digestive tolerance affect whether symptoms develop.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:137:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और बढ़ती उम्र जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:510:"Diagnosis is based on the relationship between lactose consumption and digestive symptoms. A healthcare professional may review dietary history and may recommend a temporary reduction in lactose followed by controlled reintroduction. A hydrogen breath test can help confirm lactose malabsorption by measuring hydrogen produced after lactose is consumed. Other gastrointestinal conditions may cause similar symptoms, so persistent or severe digestive complaints may require evaluation for alternative diagnoses.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:166:"निदान में लैक्टोज परीक्षण और आहार मूल्यांकन शामिल हो सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:549:"Primary lactose intolerance related to genetically determined lactase reduction cannot generally be prevented. Secondary lactose intolerance may improve when the underlying intestinal condition is identified and treated. People who experience symptoms can often reduce discomfort by adjusting the amount and timing of lactose consumed rather than unnecessarily eliminating all dairy foods. Adequate calcium and vitamin D intake should be maintained through tolerated foods or appropriate alternatives, particularly when dairy consumption is reduced.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:118:"लक्षण होने पर लैक्टोज युक्त भोजन सीमित करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:316:"Lactose intolerance is generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment if symptoms are severe, persistent, unexplained, or associated with significant weight loss, blood in the stool, persistent vomiting, or another concerning change. Severe dehydration or significant bleeding requires urgent medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:83;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:85;s:10:"disease_id";i:135;s:11:"overview_en";s:373:"Esophagitis is inflammation, swelling, or irritation of the lining of the esophagus, the tube that carries food from the mouth to the stomach. It can cause painful or difficult swallowing, chest discomfort, heartburn, and sometimes vomiting. Reflux of stomach acid is a common cause, but infections, medicines, allergies, and other conditions can also injure the esophagus.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:197:"इसोफैजाइटिस भोजन नली की सूजन है जिससे निगलने में दर्द या कठिनाई हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:468:"Esophagitis may result from stomach acid repeatedly flowing into the esophagus, as occurs with gastroesophageal reflux disease. Other causes include eosinophilic esophagitis, infections caused by viruses, bacteria or fungi, and irritation from medicines that become lodged in the esophagus. Certain autoimmune or allergic conditions can also contribute. Repeated vomiting and some medical treatments, including radiation to the chest, may damage the esophageal lining.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:151:"एसिड रिफ्लक्स, संक्रमण और कुछ दवाएं इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:428:"Risk factors include gastroesophageal reflux, smoking, alcohol use, and taking certain medicines without enough water. Medicines such as alendronate, doxycycline, tetracycline, potassium tablets, and vitamin C can irritate the esophagus when they remain in contact with its lining. Vomiting, lying down soon after a large meal, chest radiation, and conditions associated with allergies or immune problems may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"जीईआरडी, धूम्रपान, शराब और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:267:"Esophagitis is diagnosed from symptoms, medical history, and a physical examination. Depending on the suspected cause and severity, tests such as upper endoscopy, imaging, or other studies may be used to look for inflammation, damage, infection, or another condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:145:"निदान में एंडोस्कोपी और चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:415:"Risk can be reduced by treating acid reflux and following measures that limit irritation of the esophagus. Take tablets and capsules with plenty of water and remain upright rather than lying down immediately after taking medicines. Avoid smoking and excessive alcohol use, and avoid lying down soon after large meals. People with recurrent symptoms should seek medical advice so the underlying cause can be treated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:168:"एसिड रिफ्लक्स का समय पर उपचार करें तथा धूम्रपान और शराब से बचें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:339:"Esophagitis usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for persistent or worsening difficulty swallowing, painful swallowing, persistent vomiting, vomiting blood, black stools, unexplained weight loss, or significant chest pain. Severe chest pain, major bleeding, or inability to swallow requires emergency evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:84;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:86;s:10:"disease_id";i:136;s:11:"overview_en";s:406:"Barrett esophagus is a condition in which the normal lining of the lower esophagus changes after prolonged exposure to stomach acid and other refluxed material. It is commonly associated with chronic gastroesophageal reflux disease. Many people have no specific symptoms beyond those caused by reflux. Barrett esophagus is important because it can increase the risk of developing esophageal adenocarcinoma.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:208:"बैरेट इसोफेगस में लंबे समय तक एसिड रिफ्लक्स के कारण भोजन नली की परत बदल जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:453:"Barrett esophagus usually develops after repeated exposure of the lower esophageal lining to stomach acid and other refluxed contents. Long-standing gastroesophageal reflux is the main associated condition. Repeated injury and healing can cause the normal squamous lining to be replaced by specialized glandular-type cells. The precise biological mechanisms behind this cellular change are complex and involve chronic inflammation and tissue adaptation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:132:"लंबे समय तक रहने वाला जीईआरडी इसका प्रमुख कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:424:"Risk factors include long-standing gastroesophageal reflux, male sex, increasing age, obesity, and central abdominal weight gain. Tobacco use may also contribute. The risk of progression to abnormal or precancerous cellular changes is influenced by the extent and duration of Barrett esophagus and other individual factors. Not everyone with Barrett esophagus develops cancer, but appropriate medical follow-up is important.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:152:"दीर्घकालिक जीईआरडी, मोटापा और धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:428:"Barrett esophagus is diagnosed by upper endoscopy with examination of the esophageal lining and biopsy of suspicious areas. Tissue samples are evaluated to confirm the characteristic cellular changes and determine whether dysplasia or cancer is present. The extent of the affected segment may also be documented. Continued endoscopic surveillance may be recommended for some patients depending on the findings and clinical risk.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1143:"बैरेट एसोफेगस का निदान ऊपरी एंडोस्कोपी द्वारा किया जाता है, जिसमें भोजन नली की अंदरूनी परत की जांच और असामान्य दिखने वाले ऊतक की बायोप्सी शामिल होती है। एंडोस्कोपी के दौरान डॉक्टर सामान्य परत में हुए बदलावों को देखते हैं और सूक्ष्मदर्शी जांच के लिए ऊतक के नमूने लेते हैं। पैथोलॉजी से यह पता लगाने में मदद मिलती है कि आंत जैसी कोशिकीय परिवर्तन मौजूद हैं या डिस्प्लेसिया या कैंसर है, जिससे आगे की निगरानी और उपचार तय करने में मदद मिलती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:450:"Reducing chronic acid reflux is an important part of managing risk. Maintaining a healthy weight, avoiding tobacco, and following medical advice for persistent reflux may help reduce ongoing irritation of the esophagus. People with diagnosed Barrett esophagus should follow recommended medical surveillance and treatment. Persistent swallowing difficulty, bleeding, unexplained weight loss, or worsening reflux symptoms should be medically evaluated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1077:"बैरेट एसोफैगस को पूरी तरह रोकने का कोई निश्चित तरीका नहीं है, लेकिन गैस्ट्रोएसोफेजियल रिफ्लक्स रोग को नियंत्रित करने से भोजन नली की परत को होने वाली लगातार क्षति कम हो सकती है। रिफ्लक्स के लिए चिकित्सकीय सलाह का पालन करें, लक्षण बढ़ाने वाले भोजन या पेय को पहचानकर सीमित करें, भोजन के तुरंत बाद न लेटें और सलाह मिलने पर स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें। लगातार रिफ्लक्स के लक्षण होने पर स्वास्थ्यकर्मी से परामर्श करना चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:383:"Barrett esophagus usually does not cause an immediate emergency but requires medical follow-up because it can increase the risk of esophageal cancer. Seek prompt assessment for new or worsening difficulty swallowing, persistent vomiting, unexplained weight loss, vomiting blood, black stools, or significant chest pain. Major bleeding or inability to swallow requires emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:85;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:87;s:10:"disease_id";i:137;s:11:"overview_en";s:322:"Esophageal cancer is a malignant tumor that develops in the esophagus, the muscular tube that carries food from the throat to the stomach. Early disease may cause few or no symptoms. As the tumor grows, people may develop difficulty swallowing, painful swallowing, weight loss, chest discomfort, or persistent indigestion.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:112:"इसोफेजियल कैंसर भोजन नली का घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:376:"Esophageal cancer develops when cells in the esophagus acquire changes that allow them to grow and divide abnormally. Important contributing factors include tobacco use, heavy alcohol exposure, chronic acid reflux, Barrett esophagus, obesity, and certain infections. The exact combination of factors varies between individuals and between different types of esophageal cancer.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:138:"धूम्रपान, शराब और बैरेट इसोफेगस इसके जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:349:"Risk factors include cigarette smoking, heavy alcohol use, chronic gastroesophageal reflux disease, Barrett esophagus, obesity, certain dietary patterns, and increasing age. Some inherited conditions, environmental exposures, and previous abnormalities of the esophagus may also increase risk. Risk varies according to the type of esophageal cancer.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:163:"तंबाकू, शराब, मोटापा और दीर्घकालिक रिफ्लक्स जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:358:"Diagnosis usually begins with evaluation of swallowing difficulty, chest or upper abdominal symptoms, weight loss, and other concerning findings. Upper endoscopy allows direct examination of the esophagus and collection of tissue for biopsy. CT, PET, or other imaging may then be used to assess the tumor, nearby structures, lymph nodes, and possible spread.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान में एंडोस्कोपी, बायोप्सी और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:396:"Avoiding tobacco, limiting alcohol, maintaining a healthy weight, and managing chronic acid reflux can help reduce several risk factors associated with esophageal cancer. People with Barrett esophagus should follow recommended medical surveillance and treatment. Persistent or progressive difficulty swallowing, unexplained weight loss, or other concerning symptoms should be medically evaluated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:132:"तंबाकू और शराब से बचें तथा रिफ्लक्स का उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:356:"Esophageal cancer requires prompt medical evaluation. Seek assessment for progressive difficulty swallowing, unexplained weight loss, persistent chest pain, vomiting, regurgitation, or other worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for inability to swallow, significant bleeding, severe chest pain, severe breathing difficulty, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:86;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:88;s:10:"disease_id";i:138;s:11:"overview_en";s:391:"Intestinal obstruction occurs when food, fluid or digestive contents cannot move normally through the intestine. The blockage may be partial or complete and can occur in the small or large intestine. It may cause abdominal pain or cramping, swelling, vomiting, constipation and inability to pass gas. A complete obstruction can become a medical emergency because it may damage the intestine.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:195:"आंत्र अवरोध वह स्थिति है जिसमें आंतों में भोजन या तरल का मार्ग रुक जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:419:"Common causes include scar tissue called adhesions, hernias, tumors, inflammatory bowel disease and twisting or telescoping of the intestine. In children, congenital abnormalities and other developmental problems may cause obstruction. Certain conditions can slow intestinal movement without a physical blockage. The cause depends on the location and type of obstruction and may require imaging or surgery to determine.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:142:"चिपकाव, हर्निया, ट्यूमर और सूजन इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:385:"Risk factors include previous abdominal or pelvic surgery, hernias, abdominal or intestinal tumors, inflammatory bowel disease and conditions that can cause abnormal intestinal movement. Older adults may have a higher risk of some forms of obstruction. A history of previous intestinal obstruction also increases the chance of recurrence. Risk varies according to the underlying cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:138:"पूर्व सर्जरी, हर्निया और आंत्र रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:368:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination and imaging. Healthcare professionals may listen for changes in bowel sounds and examine the abdomen for swelling or tenderness. Abdominal X-rays, CT scans or other imaging tests can help identify the location and cause of a blockage. Blood tests may be used to assess dehydration, infection or other complications.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:118:"निदान में परीक्षण और इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:462:"Not all intestinal obstructions can be prevented. Reducing the risk involves managing conditions that can cause blockage, following medical advice after abdominal surgery and seeking treatment for hernias or other structural problems when recommended. People with inflammatory bowel disease should follow their treatment plan. Prompt medical attention for severe abdominal pain, repeated vomiting or inability to pass stool or gas can help prevent complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:137:"पेट की बीमारियों का समय पर उपचार जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:340:"Intestinal obstruction can become life-threatening and requires urgent medical assessment. Seek emergency care for severe or worsening abdominal pain or cramping, repeated vomiting, significant abdominal swelling, inability to pass stool or gas, severe weakness, or rapidly worsening symptoms. A complete obstruction is a medical emergency.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:87;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:89;s:10:"disease_id";i:139;s:11:"overview_en";s:384:"Peritonitis is inflammation or infection of the peritoneum, the thin tissue lining the inside of the abdomen and covering many abdominal organs. It can cause severe abdominal pain, tenderness, swelling, fever, nausea and vomiting. Peritonitis can develop when bacteria or other substances enter the abdominal cavity. It is potentially serious and may require urgent medical treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:187:"पेरिटोनाइटिस पेट की अंदरूनी परत की सूजन है जो अक्सर संक्रमण से होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:401:"Peritonitis may occur when an abdominal organ becomes perforated or ruptures, allowing bacteria or digestive contents to enter the abdominal cavity. Causes include a burst appendix, perforated stomach or intestinal ulcer, bowel injury and severe abdominal infection. It can also develop as a complication in people receiving peritoneal dialysis. The underlying cause determines the treatment required.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:169:"बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण, अंग फटना और पेट की चोट इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:402:"Risk is increased by conditions that can cause abdominal perforation or infection, including appendicitis, diverticulitis, bowel disease, abdominal trauma and ulcers. People undergoing peritoneal dialysis have an increased risk of infection involving the peritoneum. Previous abdominal surgery and conditions that weaken immune defenses may also increase susceptibility to serious abdominal infections.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:129:"पेट के संक्रमण और अंगों का फटना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:388:"Diagnosis begins with symptoms, medical history and physical examination. The abdomen may be very tender or painful during examination. Blood tests can help identify inflammation or infection. Imaging such as abdominal CT scanning or ultrasound may help locate the source. In some cases, fluid from the abdominal cavity is collected and examined to identify infection and guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:145:"निदान में रक्त जांच, इमेजिंग और द्रव परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:419:"Some causes of peritonitis can be reduced by treating abdominal infections and conditions such as appendicitis promptly. People using peritoneal dialysis should carefully follow sterile technique and their treatment team instructions. Seek urgent medical care for severe or worsening abdominal pain, fever, persistent vomiting or abdominal swelling, particularly when an abdominal infection or perforation is suspected.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:107:"पेट के संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार आवश्यक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:332:"Peritonitis is a potentially life-threatening condition requiring immediate medical assessment. Seek emergency care for severe or worsening abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness or rigidity, fever, persistent vomiting, marked abdominal swelling, confusion, fainting, rapid deterioration, or other signs of serious infection or shock.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:88;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:90;s:10:"disease_id";i:140;s:11:"overview_en";s:388:"Short bowel syndrome occurs when the body cannot absorb enough nutrients, fluids, or electrolytes because part of the small intestine is missing or has been damaged. It commonly develops after extensive intestinal surgery, although some people are born with an unusually short or damaged intestine. The condition can lead to nutritional deficiencies, dehydration, and other complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:253:"शॉर्ट बाउल सिंड्रोम में छोटी आंत के हिस्से के नुकसान के कारण पोषक तत्वों का अवशोषण कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:422:"Short bowel syndrome usually develops after surgery removes a large part of the small intestine or when the intestine is damaged or missing from birth. Crohn disease, intestinal blockage, reduced blood supply, severe intestinal injury, or other conditions may require removal of part of the intestine. With less intestinal surface available, the remaining bowel may not absorb nutrients, fluids, and electrolytes normally.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:150:"यह प्रायः आंत की सर्जरी या गंभीर आंत्र रोग के बाद होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:425:"Extensive surgery involving removal of the small intestine is the major risk factor for short bowel syndrome. The risk also increases when intestinal disease or injury results in substantial loss of functioning bowel. Conditions such as Crohn disease, intestinal blockage, reduced blood supply, severe intestinal injury, or congenital absence of part of the intestine may therefore contribute to development of the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:111:"व्यापक आंत्र सर्जरी प्रमुख जोखिम कारक है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:442:"Diagnosis of short bowel syndrome involves assessing the person’s medical and surgical history together with symptoms and nutritional status. Healthcare professionals may evaluate weight, hydration, vitamin and mineral levels, and other laboratory measurements to identify deficiencies or electrolyte problems. Tests or imaging may also be used to assess the remaining intestine and help determine how much bowel function has been retained.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान में पोषण मूल्यांकन और आंत्र परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:464:"Short bowel syndrome cannot always be prevented because it may result from severe intestinal disease, injury, congenital conditions, or surgery that is medically necessary. When extensive intestinal surgery is required, careful surgical planning and preservation of healthy bowel when possible may help retain intestinal function. Appropriate nutritional support and follow-up after intestinal surgery can also help manage the consequences of reduced bowel length.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:115:"उचित सर्जिकल योजना और पोषण सहायता सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:335:"Short bowel syndrome requires ongoing medical management and monitoring. Seek prompt assessment for persistent diarrhea, dehydration, significant weight loss, weakness, nutritional problems, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care may be needed for severe dehydration, fainting, confusion, or inability to maintain adequate fluid intake.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:89;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:91;s:10:"disease_id";i:141;s:11:"overview_en";s:385:"A urinary tract infection is an infection affecting part of the urinary system, including the urethra, bladder, ureters, or kidneys. Most UTIs involve the bladder and may cause burning or pain during urination, frequent or urgent urination, lower abdominal pressure, or changes in urine. If infection reaches the kidneys, fever, chills, vomiting, or pain in the back or side may occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:175:"मूत्र मार्ग संक्रमण मूत्र तंत्र को प्रभावित करने वाला संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:436:"Most urinary tract infections are caused by bacteria that enter the urethra and multiply in the urinary tract. Infection commonly begins in the bladder but can spread to the kidneys. The shorter urethra and its location near the anus make UTIs more common in women. Bacteria may also enter the urinary tract in association with sexual activity, urinary catheters, or conditions that interfere with normal urine flow or bladder emptying.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:163:"यह सामान्यतः बैक्टीरिया के मूत्र मार्ग में प्रवेश से होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:396:"Risk factors include being female, sexual activity, menopause, diabetes, pregnancy, older age, urinary catheter use, incomplete bladder emptying, kidney stones, an enlarged prostate, urinary tract obstruction, and certain structural abnormalities. Previous UTIs can also increase the likelihood of recurrence. People with conditions affecting bladder control or mobility may have additional risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:161:"खराब स्वच्छता, मूत्र रुकना और महिलाओं में अधिक जोखिम होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:400:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history, and examination together with urine testing. Urinalysis can look for findings that suggest infection, while a urine culture can identify the bacteria and help guide antibiotic treatment. Additional testing or imaging may be considered when infections are recurrent, complicated, associated with obstruction, or suspected to have spread to the kidneys.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:115:"निदान में मूत्र परीक्षण और कल्चर शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:429:"Some UTIs may be prevented by maintaining good hydration, avoiding unnecessary urinary catheter use, and addressing conditions that interfere with complete bladder emptying. After menopause, vaginal estrogen may reduce recurrent UTIs in some women when prescribed by a healthcare professional. People with recurrent infections should be evaluated for underlying causes rather than repeatedly treating symptoms without assessment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:111:"पर्याप्त पानी पिएं और स्वच्छता बनाए रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:339:"A urinary tract infection should be assessed when symptoms are significant or persistent. Seek prompt care for fever, chills, flank or back pain, vomiting, blood in the urine, worsening symptoms, or symptoms during pregnancy. Emergency assessment is needed for severe illness, confusion, fainting, or signs of a serious systemic infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:90;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:93;s:10:"disease_id";i:144;s:11:"overview_en";s:368:"Acute kidney injury is a sudden decline in kidney function that develops over hours or days. The kidneys may temporarily lose their ability to remove waste products and maintain normal fluid, electrolyte, and acid balance. Causes include severe dehydration, infection, reduced blood flow, urinary obstruction, and certain medicines or other kidney-injuring substances.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:1191:"एक्यूट किडनी इंजरी यानी तीव्र गुर्दा क्षति में थोड़े समय के भीतर गुर्दों की कार्यक्षमता अचानक कम हो जाती है। जब गुर्दे सामान्य रूप से अपशिष्ट पदार्थों को छानने और शरीर में द्रव, लवण तथा अन्य पदार्थों का संतुलन बनाए रखने में सक्षम नहीं रहते, तो रक्त में अपशिष्ट जमा हो सकते हैं। यह गंभीर बीमारी, गुर्दों में रक्त प्रवाह कम होने, कुछ दवाओं या विषैले पदार्थों, संक्रमण, रुकावट या सीधे गुर्दे की चोट के बाद हो सकती है। समय पर चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन महत्वपूर्ण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:372:"Acute kidney injury may occur when blood flow to the kidneys falls, when kidney tissue is directly damaged, or when urine flow is obstructed. Severe dehydration, blood loss, shock, sepsis, heart problems, certain medicines, toxins, and contrast exposure can reduce kidney function. Kidney stones, enlarged prostate, tumors, or other blockages can cause obstructive injury.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:188:"निर्जलीकरण, संक्रमण, दवाएं और रक्त प्रवाह में कमी इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:385:"Risk is increased by older age, chronic kidney or heart disease, diabetes, severe infection, dehydration, major surgery, blood loss, low blood pressure, urinary obstruction, and exposure to medicines or substances that can injure the kidneys. Hospitalized and critically ill patients are particularly vulnerable. The risk depends on the severity and duration of the underlying problem.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:157:"गुर्दे के रोग, गंभीर बीमारी और निर्जलीकरण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:427:"Diagnosis involves identifying a sudden change in kidney function through blood and urine tests. Serum creatinine and urine output are important measures. Healthcare professionals may examine urine for blood, protein, infection, or other abnormalities and may use ultrasound or other imaging when obstruction is suspected. The medical history helps identify dehydration, infection, medicines, toxins, or other potential causes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:139:"निदान में रक्त जांच, मूत्र जांच और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:467:"Preventing dehydration, promptly treating serious infections, maintaining appropriate blood pressure and circulation, and avoiding unnecessary exposure to kidney-injuring medicines can reduce risk. People taking medicines that may affect kidney function may require monitoring, particularly during illness or dehydration. Urinary obstruction should be evaluated promptly. Individuals with chronic medical conditions should follow their treatment and monitoring plans.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:114:"मूल रोगों का समय पर उपचार बचाव में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:408:"Acute kidney injury requires prompt medical assessment because kidney function can deteriorate quickly. Seek urgent care for markedly reduced or absent urination, severe swelling, persistent vomiting, confusion, severe weakness, shortness of breath, chest pain, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Severe breathing difficulty, altered consciousness, or other signs of serious complications require emergency care.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:91;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:94;s:10:"disease_id";i:145;s:11:"overview_en";s:547:"Glomerulonephritis is inflammation or injury involving the glomeruli, the microscopic filtering structures of the kidneys. Damage can interfere with the kidneys’ ability to remove waste and regulate fluid and electrolytes. Depending on the cause and severity, it may produce blood or protein in the urine, swelling, high blood pressure, reduced urine output, or impaired kidney function. Glomerulonephritis may occur suddenly or develop gradually and can result from infections, immune-system disorders, medications, or other medical conditions.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:170:"ग्लोमेरुलोनेफ्राइटिस गुर्दों की छानने वाली इकाइयों की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:531:"Glomerulonephritis can result from immune-system activity directed against the kidney or from immune complexes deposited in the glomeruli. It may develop after certain infections, including some bacterial or viral infections, or as part of autoimmune diseases such as lupus or vasculitis. Other causes include inherited kidney disorders, medications, and diseases affecting small blood vessels. The precise mechanism differs between types, and determining the cause is important because treatment depends on the underlying process.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:978:"ग्लोमेरुलोनेफ्राइटिस तब हो सकता है जब गुर्दों की सूक्ष्म छनन इकाइयाँ, जिन्हें ग्लोमेरुली कहा जाता है, सूज जाएँ या क्षतिग्रस्त हो जाएँ। इसके कारणों में स्ट्रेप्टोकोकल संक्रमण, एंडोकार्डाइटिस, HIV, हेपेटाइटिस B या C जैसे संक्रमण; IgA नेफ्रोपैथी और anti-GBM रोग जैसे ऑटोइम्यून रोग; कुछ दवाएँ; तथा Alport syndrome या Fabry disease जैसे आनुवंशिक विकार शामिल हैं। कुछ मामलों में सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं हो पाता।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:506:"Risk factors depend on the specific form of glomerulonephritis and may include recent infections, autoimmune diseases, systemic inflammatory disorders, certain inherited conditions, and diseases affecting blood vessels. A family history of kidney disease can be relevant for some forms. Certain medications and chronic medical conditions may also contribute. Because different forms have different risk profiles, clinical history and appropriate testing are important when kidney inflammation is suspected.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:124:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और कुछ संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:514:"Evaluation begins with a medical history, physical examination, urine testing, blood tests, and assessment of kidney function. Urinalysis may show blood or protein, while blood tests can demonstrate impaired filtration or other abnormalities. Complement levels and tests for autoimmune or infectious causes may help identify the underlying process. Kidney ultrasound may assess kidney structure, while a kidney biopsy may be required in selected cases to determine the exact type and severity of glomerular injury.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:158:"निदान में मूत्र जांच, रक्त जांच और किडनी बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:535:"Not all forms of glomerulonephritis can be prevented because some are related to autoimmune or inherited conditions. Prompt treatment of certain infections and appropriate management of autoimmune, inflammatory, and systemic diseases may reduce kidney complications in susceptible people. Avoiding unnecessary medicines that may injure the kidneys and maintaining appropriate blood pressure and overall cardiovascular health can also support kidney function. People with known risk factors may benefit from periodic medical monitoring.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:148:"संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार करें और गुर्दों की निगरानी करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:428:"Glomerulonephritis requires medical assessment because kidney inflammation can impair kidney function. Seek prompt care for blood in the urine, significant swelling, reduced urination, high blood pressure with concerning symptoms, severe weakness, or rapidly worsening illness. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, confusion, markedly reduced urination, or other signs of serious kidney complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:29:39";}i:92;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:95;s:10:"disease_id";i:146;s:11:"overview_en";s:475:"Nephrotic syndrome is a group of findings caused by excessive loss of protein through the kidneys. It commonly includes large amounts of protein in the urine, low levels of protein in the blood, swelling, and increased levels of cholesterol or other blood fats. The condition can occur at any age and may result from several different kidney diseases or systemic conditions. The severity and long-term outcome depend largely on the underlying cause and response to treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:242:"नेफ्रोटिक सिंड्रोम एक गुर्दा विकार है जिसमें मूत्र के माध्यम से अत्यधिक प्रोटीन निकलता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:491:"Nephrotic syndrome develops when damage to the kidney glomeruli allows too much protein to pass from the blood into the urine. Different diseases can cause this damage. In children, minimal change disease is a common cause, while membranous kidney disease is an important cause in adults. Other causes include diabetes, lupus, amyloidosis, certain infections, genetic disorders, cancers, immune conditions, and some medicines. Identifying the underlying disorder is important for management.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:167:"गुर्दे के रोग, ऑटोइम्यून विकार और संक्रमण इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:502:"Risk factors for nephrotic syndrome are mainly related to conditions that can damage the kidney filters. Diabetes, systemic lupus erythematosus, certain infections, immune disorders, genetic kidney diseases, and some cancers can increase risk. A person may also develop nephrotic syndrome in association with specific glomerular diseases. Because causes differ between children and adults, age and the presence of an underlying medical condition can influence the likelihood of developing the syndrome.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:154:"मधुमेह, गुर्दे के रोग और ऑटोइम्यून विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:500:"Diagnosis involves identifying excessive protein loss and determining the condition responsible for kidney damage. Urinalysis and urine protein measurements can show abnormal protein levels. Blood tests may assess albumin, cholesterol, kidney function, and other abnormalities. Additional testing can investigate infections, autoimmune conditions, diabetes, or other possible causes. In some cases, a kidney biopsy is performed to examine kidney tissue and establish the specific underlying disorder.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:158:"निदान में मूत्र जांच, रक्त जांच और किडनी बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:476:"There is no single way to prevent all cases of nephrotic syndrome because it can result from many different diseases. Managing conditions that can damage the kidneys, such as diabetes and certain autoimmune disorders, may reduce risk. Appropriate treatment and monitoring of kidney disease can help identify protein loss and other abnormalities early. Regular medical follow-up is particularly important for people who already have a condition known to affect kidney function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:137:"गुर्दों के रोगों का समय पर उपचार जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:426:"Nephrotic syndrome requires medical evaluation and monitoring because it can cause significant swelling, blood clots, infections, and kidney problems. Seek prompt assessment for rapidly increasing swelling, reduced urination, shortness of breath, chest pain, fever, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, fainting, or symptoms suggesting a serious blood clot or infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:93;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:96;s:10:"disease_id";i:147;s:11:"overview_en";s:572:"Polycystic kidney disease is a group of inherited disorders in which numerous fluid-filled cysts develop in the kidneys. The cysts can enlarge the kidneys and, over time, interfere with normal kidney function. Some people have few symptoms for many years, while others develop high blood pressure, abdominal or back discomfort, blood in the urine, kidney stones, or recurrent urinary infections. The condition can progressively reduce kidney function in some individuals. It may also be associated with cysts in other organs and other complications, depending on the type.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:221:"पॉलीसिस्टिक किडनी रोग एक आनुवंशिक विकार है जिसमें गुर्दों में कई सिस्ट बन जाते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:567:"Polycystic kidney disease is primarily caused by inherited genetic changes. Autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease is commonly caused by changes in the PKD1 or PKD2 genes and often becomes apparent during adulthood. Autosomal recessive polycystic kidney disease is caused by changes in the PKHD1 gene and commonly presents earlier in life. These genetic changes disrupt proteins involved in normal kidney-cell function and lead to progressive formation and enlargement of cysts. The inheritance pattern and genetic cause influence the age of onset and severity.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:127:"यह मुख्यतः आनुवंशिक परिवर्तनों के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:510:"Risk depends largely on the inherited form of polycystic kidney disease and family history. People with an affected parent may have a substantial inherited risk in autosomal dominant disease. The condition can affect both sexes. High blood pressure, recurrent urinary problems, and increasing kidney cyst burden may accompany disease progression. Because symptoms may not appear early, individuals with a strong family history may require medical assessment and appropriate monitoring even when they feel well.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:117:"पारिवारिक इतिहास इसका प्रमुख जोखिम कारक है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:565:"Polycystic kidney disease can be evaluated with imaging studies that identify and characterize kidney cysts. Ultrasound is commonly used because it is noninvasive, while CT or MRI may provide more detailed assessment when necessary. A family history can provide important diagnostic information. Genetic testing may be considered when the diagnosis is uncertain, particularly in younger individuals or when family history is unavailable. Kidney function, blood pressure, urine findings, and possible complications are also monitored during evaluation and follow-up.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:175:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड, सीटी स्कैन और आनुवंशिक परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:599:"There is no established way to prevent inherited polycystic kidney disease in someone who carries a disease-causing genetic variant. However, early recognition and regular monitoring can help reduce complications. Controlling blood pressure, avoiding smoking, maintaining appropriate hydration as advised by a clinician, and managing cardiovascular risk factors support kidney health. People with a strong family history may benefit from genetic counseling and appropriate evaluation. Regular monitoring can identify changes in kidney function, cyst burden, or blood pressure that require attention.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1103:"पॉलीसिस्टिक किडनी डिजीज एक आनुवंशिक विकार है, इसलिए मूल रोग को रोकने का अभी कोई स्थापित तरीका नहीं है। हालांकि, रोग की जल्दी पहचान, रक्तचाप की निगरानी और नियंत्रण, उपयुक्त आहार एवं तरल सेवन, नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि, धूम्रपान से बचाव और चिकित्सकीय उपचार का पालन करके जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद मिल सकती है। पारिवारिक इतिहास के कारण जोखिम वाले लोगों को स्वास्थ्यकर्मी से जाँच और नियमित निगरानी के बारे में चर्चा करनी चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:456:"Polycystic kidney disease requires ongoing medical monitoring because it can cause high blood pressure, kidney infections, kidney stones, and progressive loss of kidney function. Seek prompt assessment for severe or persistent pain, fever, blood in the urine, markedly reduced urination, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe pain with fainting, severe breathing difficulty, confusion, or other signs of a serious complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:94;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:97;s:10:"disease_id";i:148;s:11:"overview_en";s:399:"Hydronephrosis is swelling of a kidney caused by urine building up because its normal drainage is blocked or impaired. It may affect one or both kidneys and can result from conditions such as kidney stones, narrowing of the urinary tract, an enlarged prostate, tumors, or urinary reflux. The condition may cause pain, urinary symptoms, infection, or reduced kidney function when severe or prolonged.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:215:"ओवरएक्टिव ब्लैडर ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें बार-बार अचानक पेशाब की तीव्र इच्छा होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:397:"Hydronephrosis occurs when urine cannot drain normally from a kidney to the bladder and therefore accumulates in the kidney. Causes can include kidney stones, narrowing or blockage of the ureter or urethra, enlarged prostate, tumors, blood clots, urinary tract abnormalities, and vesicoureteral reflux. In some newborns, temporary or developmental urinary tract narrowing may cause hydronephrosis.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:177:"मूत्राशय की मांसपेशियों की असामान्य गतिविधि इसका सामान्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:362:"Risk depends on the cause of urinary obstruction. Kidney stones, urinary tract abnormalities, enlarged prostate, tumors, blood clots, urinary tract infections, and conditions that cause urine to flow backward toward the kidneys can increase risk. Hydronephrosis may also occur during pregnancy or in infants with developmental abnormalities of the urinary tract.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:178:"उम्र, तंत्रिका संबंधी विकार और हार्मोनल परिवर्तन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:409:"Diagnosis of hydronephrosis usually involves a medical history, physical examination, and imaging to identify kidney swelling and determine its cause. Ultrasound is commonly used to visualize the kidneys and urinary tract. CT or other imaging may be needed to identify stones, tumors, or obstruction. Blood and urine tests can help assess kidney function and identify infection or other urinary abnormalities.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:134:"निदान में लक्षण मूल्यांकन और मूत्र जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:383:"Hydronephrosis itself is not always preventable because it can result from structural or medical conditions that cannot be avoided. Prompt evaluation of urinary symptoms, kidney stones, recurrent urinary infections, or difficulty passing urine may help identify obstruction early. Appropriate treatment of conditions that interfere with urinary flow can help protect kidney function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:143:"ब्लैडर प्रशिक्षण और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली सहायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:400:"Hydronephrosis should be assessed because prolonged blockage of urine flow can damage kidney function. Seek prompt medical care for significant flank or abdominal pain, fever, vomiting, blood in the urine, difficulty urinating, or worsening symptoms. Urgent or emergency assessment is particularly important when obstruction is accompanied by infection, severe pain, or markedly reduced urine output.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:95;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:98;s:10:"disease_id";i:149;s:11:"overview_en";s:615:"Interstitial cystitis, also called bladder pain syndrome, is a chronic condition associated with bladder discomfort, pressure, or pain together with urinary symptoms such as frequent or urgent urination. Symptoms can vary considerably between people and may come and go over time. Some people experience discomfort as the bladder fills and partial relief after urination, while others have persistent pelvic or bladder pain. The condition is diagnosed based on symptoms and by excluding other causes of similar urinary complaints, because there is no single test that confirms interstitial cystitis in every person.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:141:"मूत्र असंयम में अनियंत्रित रूप से मूत्र निकल जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:530:"The exact cause of interstitial cystitis is not fully understood. Possible contributing mechanisms include changes in the bladder lining, altered bladder signaling, inflammation, immune-system activity, or abnormal communication between bladder nerves and the nervous system. Some people may have symptoms associated with other chronic pain conditions. Urinary infection, bladder stones, and other disorders can cause similar symptoms, so these conditions generally need to be considered and excluded before the diagnosis is made.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:201:"कमजोर पेल्विक मांसपेशियां, उम्र और तंत्रिका समस्याएं इसके कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:574:"Factors associated with interstitial cystitis may include being female, having a history of chronic pelvic or bladder symptoms, and having certain other chronic pain or inflammatory conditions. Symptoms may be influenced by foods, beverages, stress, hormonal changes, sexual activity, or other individual triggers. These associations do not mean that a particular factor causes the condition. Because symptoms overlap with urinary infections and other bladder disorders, repeated urinary symptoms should be medically assessed rather than assumed to be interstitial cystitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:176:"गर्भावस्था, बढ़ती उम्र, मोटापा और तंत्रिका विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:562:"There is no single definitive test for interstitial cystitis. Diagnosis is generally based on the pattern and duration of bladder or pelvic symptoms while excluding conditions that can produce similar complaints. Evaluation may include medical history, physical examination, urinalysis, and urine culture to look for infection. Depending on symptoms, healthcare professionals may consider additional testing or procedures to evaluate the bladder and rule out other disorders. The diagnostic approach is individualized according to symptoms and clinical findings.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:132:"निदान में इतिहास, परीक्षण और ब्लैडर जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:559:"Because the exact cause of interstitial cystitis is not fully established, there is no proven method that completely prevents it. Some people find that identifying and avoiding individual symptom triggers, maintaining appropriate fluid intake, managing stress, and following an individualized treatment plan can reduce flare-ups. Prompt evaluation of urinary symptoms can also help identify infections or other treatable conditions. Keeping a record of foods, activities, and symptoms may help some people recognize factors associated with worsening symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:138:"पेल्विक फ्लोर व्यायाम जोखिम और लक्षण कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:374:"Interstitial cystitis is usually a chronic condition and is not generally an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent or worsening bladder pain, urinary symptoms that interfere with daily activities, blood in the urine, fever, or symptoms that suggest another urinary condition. Severe pain, significant bleeding, or inability to urinate requires prompt evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:96;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:99;s:10:"disease_id";i:150;s:11:"overview_en";s:316:"Pyelonephritis is a kidney infection that usually begins as an infection in the bladder or lower urinary tract and then spreads upward to one or both kidneys. It commonly causes fever, chills, painful or frequent urination, and pain in the back, side, or groin. Nausea, vomiting, and changes in urine may also occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"सौम्य प्रोस्टेट वृद्धि प्रोस्टेट ग्रंथि का गैर-कैंसरयुक्त बढ़ना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:390:"Pyelonephritis is most often caused by bacteria that enter the lower urinary tract and travel upward through the ureters to the kidneys. It commonly develops from an untreated or persistent bladder infection. Less commonly, infection may reach the kidneys through the bloodstream. Urinary obstruction, reflux, or other urinary tract problems can increase the likelihood of kidney infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:193:"उम्र से संबंधित हार्मोनल परिवर्तन प्रोस्टेट वृद्धि में योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:350:"Risk is higher in females, during pregnancy, and in people with a current or recent bladder infection. Urinary tract blockage from a kidney stone or enlarged prostate, vesicoureteral reflux, diabetes, and weakened immunity can increase risk. Structural or functional problems affecting normal urinary flow can also make kidney infections more likely.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:130:"उम्र और हार्मोनल परिवर्तन प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:410:"Diagnosis of pyelonephritis involves medical history, physical examination, and laboratory testing. Urinalysis can detect blood and white blood cells in the urine, while urine culture can identify bacteria and help guide antibiotic treatment. Blood tests may assess infection and kidney function. Ultrasound, CT, MRI, or other imaging may be used when obstruction, complications, or another cause is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:135:"निदान में परीक्षण, पीएसए जांच और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:410:"Prompt treatment of bladder infections can help reduce the chance of infection spreading to the kidneys. Drink adequate fluids unless a healthcare professional has advised otherwise, and seek medical care for symptoms such as fever, back or side pain, or painful urination. People with recurrent infections, urinary blockage, reflux, diabetes, or other risk factors should follow individualized medical advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:581:"गुर्दे के संक्रमण से बचाव के लिए मूत्र संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार, चिकित्सकीय रूप से उचित मात्रा में पर्याप्त पानी पीना, नियमित रूप से पेशाब करना तथा मूत्र मार्ग में रुकावट या अन्य जोखिमकारी स्थितियों का उपचार महत्वपूर्ण है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:361:"Pyelonephritis, or kidney infection, requires prompt medical treatment. Seek medical care right away for fever, chills, pain in the back or side, painful urination, nausea, or vomiting. Emergency assessment is needed for severe weakness, confusion, fainting, severe vomiting or dehydration, markedly worsening symptoms, or signs of a serious systemic infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:97;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:102;s:10:"disease_id";i:153;s:11:"overview_en";s:439:"Urinary incontinence is the involuntary leakage of urine. It may occur as stress incontinence, urge incontinence, overflow incontinence, functional incontinence, or a combination of types. Causes range from weakened pelvic floor muscles and bladder disorders to neurological conditions, medications, infections, prostate problems, or other medical conditions. Symptoms can range from occasional leakage to frequent loss of bladder control.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:168:"पुरुष बांझपन में साथी को गर्भधारण कराने की क्षमता कम हो जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:452:"Urinary incontinence can result from weakness or poor coordination of the pelvic floor and bladder muscles, overactive bladder activity, urinary tract problems, neurological disorders, prostate enlargement, constipation, medications, or impaired mobility. Temporary incontinence can occur with infections or certain medicines. Pregnancy and childbirth can affect pelvic floor function, while aging and some chronic diseases can increase susceptibility.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:168:"शुक्राणु विकार, हार्मोनल समस्याएं और आनुवंशिक कारण प्रमुख हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:402:"Risk factors for urinary incontinence include increasing age, pregnancy and childbirth, obesity, weakened pelvic floor muscles, menopause, prostate enlargement, neurological disorders, diabetes, recurrent urinary problems, constipation, and reduced mobility. Certain medicines and cognitive impairment can also contribute. Risk varies according to the type of incontinence and the underlying condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:172:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा, हार्मोनल विकार और आनुवंशिकता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:503:"Diagnosis begins with a detailed history of leakage, urinary urgency, frequency, nighttime urination, triggers, fluid intake, medications, bowel symptoms, and neurological or pelvic conditions. Physical examination may include assessment of the abdomen, pelvis, prostate, or nervous system. Urinalysis is often performed, while bladder diaries, post-void residual measurement, or specialized testing may be used when the diagnosis remains uncertain or treatment planning requires additional information.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:134:"निदान में वीर्य जांच और हार्मोन परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:504:"Maintaining a healthy weight, regular physical activity, and pelvic floor muscle training can reduce the risk of some forms of urinary incontinence. Preventing constipation, managing chronic cough, avoiding unnecessary bladder irritants, and controlling conditions such as diabetes may also help. During pregnancy and after childbirth, appropriate pelvic floor exercises can be beneficial. Persistent or worsening leakage should be medically assessed rather than accepted as an unavoidable part of aging.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1244:"मूत्र असंयम के कुछ कारणों को रोका नहीं जा सकता, लेकिन जीवनशैली के उपाय रिसाव का जोखिम कम करने या मूत्राशय नियंत्रण बनाए रखने में मदद कर सकते हैं। नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि करें और स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें। पर्याप्त फाइबर लेकर कब्ज से बचें। धूम्रपान न करें और यदि शराब या कैफीनयुक्त पेय लक्षण बढ़ाते हैं तो उन्हें सीमित करें। पेल्विक फ्लोर व्यायाम मूत्र नियंत्रण में मदद करने वाली मांसपेशियों को मजबूत कर सकते हैं। ब्लैडर ट्रेनिंग और सही समय पर तरल पदार्थ लेना भी मददगार हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:408:"Urinary incontinence is usually not an emergency but should be evaluated when persistent or bothersome. Seek medical assessment for new or worsening incontinence, blood in the urine, painful urination, fever, pelvic or back pain, or sudden neurological symptoms. Emergency care is needed for sudden loss of bladder control accompanied by new leg weakness, numbness, severe back pain, or inability to urinate.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:98;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:103;s:10:"disease_id";i:154;s:11:"overview_en";s:325:"Overactive bladder is a condition characterized by a sudden, difficult-to-control urge to urinate, often with frequent urination and nighttime urination. Some people also experience urge urinary incontinence, in which urine leaks before reaching a toilet. The condition may occur with or without a clearly identifiable cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:198:"महिला बांझपन नियमित असुरक्षित संबंधों के बाद गर्भधारण न होने की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:337:"Overactive bladder can be associated with abnormal bladder muscle activity, nerve problems, urinary tract conditions, excessive fluid intake, or substances such as caffeine. In some people, no specific cause is identified. Other conditions that affect the bladder or nervous system may produce similar symptoms and need to be considered.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:207:"ओव्यूलेशन विकार, हार्मोन असंतुलन और प्रजनन तंत्र की समस्याएं प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:340:"Risk may increase with increasing age, bladder or urinary tract problems, neurological disorders, diabetes, and conditions affecting bladder function. High intake of caffeine or other bladder-irritating beverages may worsen symptoms. Constipation and some medicines or medical conditions can also contribute to urinary urgency or frequency.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:158:"उम्र, हार्मोनल विकार, मोटापा और प्रजनन रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:416:"Diagnosis begins with medical history and physical examination. A healthcare professional may ask about urinary frequency, urgency, leakage, fluid intake, medicines, and other symptoms. A bladder or voiding diary can be useful. Urine testing may help exclude infection, while bladder imaging, cystoscopy, or urodynamic testing may be considered when the diagnosis is uncertain or symptoms require further evaluation.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:178:"निदान में हार्मोन जांच, अल्ट्रासाउंड और प्रजनन मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:354:"Not all cases of overactive bladder can be prevented. Maintaining healthy fluid habits, limiting caffeine and alcohol when they worsen symptoms, preventing constipation, staying physically active, and maintaining a healthy weight may help bladder function. Bladder training and pelvic floor exercises can also help some people manage urgency and leakage.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:157:"प्रजनन स्वास्थ्य समस्याओं का समय पर उपचार सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:320:"Overactive bladder is usually not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when urinary urgency, frequency, or leakage is persistent or worsening, particularly if symptoms are accompanied by blood in the urine, painful urination, fever, or pelvic pain. Inability to urinate or severe new symptoms require prompt evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:99;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:105;s:10:"disease_id";i:151;s:11:"overview_en";s:393:"Bladder stones are hard masses of minerals that form inside the urinary bladder. They may develop when urine remains in the bladder and becomes concentrated or when the bladder does not empty completely. Small stones may cause few symptoms, while larger stones can cause lower abdominal discomfort, painful urination, interrupted urine flow, blood in the urine, or repeated urinary infections.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:522:"मूत्राशय की पथरी कठोर खनिज जमाव होते हैं जो मूत्राशय के अंदर बनते हैं। इससे पेट के निचले हिस्से में असुविधा, पेशाब में दर्द, बार-बार पेशाब आना, पेशाब में खून या मूत्राशय खाली करने में कठिनाई हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:303:"Bladder stones commonly form when the bladder cannot empty completely. Conditions such as an enlarged prostate, nerve-related bladder dysfunction, urinary tract abnormalities, or other blockages can cause urine to remain in the bladder. Foreign objects or certain medical procedures may also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:507:"मूत्राशय पूरी तरह खाली न होने पर मूत्र में खनिज जमा होकर क्रिस्टल बना सकते हैं। मूत्र संक्रमण, बढ़ी हुई प्रोस्टेट ग्रंथि, तंत्रिका संबंधी मूत्राशय की समस्या या अन्य रुकावट इसके कारण बन सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:431:"Risk factors include incomplete bladder emptying, urinary obstruction, an enlarged prostate, nerve-related bladder problems, recurrent urinary infections, bladder abnormalities, and certain urinary devices or procedures. Older adults may have increased risk because conditions that interfere with bladder emptying become more common with age. Having a risk factor does not necessarily mean that a person will develop the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:482:"मूत्राशय के ठीक से खाली न होने, प्रोस्टेट बढ़ने, तंत्रिका या रीढ़ की समस्याओं, बार-बार मूत्र संक्रमण और लंबे समय तक कैथेटर के उपयोग से जोखिम बढ़ सकता है। निर्जलीकरण भी योगदान दे सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:283:"Diagnosis may involve a medical history, physical examination, urine testing, and imaging of the urinary tract. Ultrasound or other imaging can identify stones and evaluate the bladder. In some cases, examination of the bladder with a cystoscope is used to identify or remove stones.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:577:"निदान में चिकित्सीय इतिहास, शारीरिक जांच, मूत्र परीक्षण और अल्ट्रासाउंड या सीटी जैसी इमेजिंग शामिल हो सकती है। यह भी जांचा जाता है कि मूत्र रुकने, संक्रमण या किसी अन्य रुकावट के कारण मूत्राशय पूरी तरह खाली तो नहीं हो रहा।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:325:"Reducing the likelihood of bladder stones involves addressing conditions that prevent complete bladder emptying, maintaining appropriate fluid intake, and treating urinary obstruction or infections when present. People with recurrent stones may need evaluation for the underlying cause and individualized preventive measures.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:559:"पर्याप्त मात्रा में पानी पीने से मूत्र अधिक सघन होने से बच सकता है। मूत्र संक्रमण और मूत्र रुकने वाली समस्याओं का समय पर उपचार तथा बार-बार पथरी होने पर नियमित चिकित्सकीय फॉलो-अप आगे पथरी बनने का जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:377:"Bladder stones should be assessed when they cause persistent urinary symptoms or pain. Seek prompt medical care for severe or persistent lower abdominal pain, blood in the urine, difficulty urinating, fever, vomiting, or worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for inability to urinate, severe pain with fever, or signs of a serious urinary infection or obstruction.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:100;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:106;s:10:"disease_id";i:152;s:11:"overview_en";s:544:"Bladder cancer is a malignant growth that develops from cells lining the urinary bladder. The most common warning sign is blood in the urine, which may be visible or detected only by testing. Some people may also experience increased urinary frequency, urgency, burning, or discomfort. Bladder cancer can remain limited to the inner layers of the bladder or grow deeper into the bladder wall and surrounding tissues. Early evaluation of unexplained urinary bleeding is important because the disease may be easier to treat when detected earlier.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:176:"मूत्राशय कैंसर मूत्राशय की परत में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:520:"Bladder cancer develops when genetic changes cause cells lining the bladder to grow and divide abnormally. Tobacco smoke is a major avoidable contributor because cancer-causing chemicals can enter the bloodstream and become concentrated in urine. Occupational exposure to certain chemicals may also contribute. Other possible contributors include chronic irritation or inflammation of the bladder, previous radiation treatment involving the pelvis, certain chemotherapy medicines, and some inherited or cellular factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:134:"धूम्रपान और कुछ रसायनों का संपर्क प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:475:"Important risk factors include cigarette smoking, increasing age, certain occupational exposures to chemicals, previous pelvic radiation, exposure to some chemotherapy medicines, chronic bladder irritation, and certain inherited conditions. A history of bladder cancer also increases the likelihood of recurrence. Long-term exposure to some workplace chemicals may be relevant in occupations involving dyes, rubber, leather, textiles, paints, or related industrial materials.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:153:"धूम्रपान, रासायनिक संपर्क और बढ़ती उम्र जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:529:"Evaluation of suspected bladder cancer may include urinalysis and other urine-based tests, imaging of the urinary tract, and cystoscopy, in which the inside of the bladder is examined with a small camera. If a suspicious area is identified, tissue obtained during cystoscopy is examined by a pathologist to establish whether cancer is present and to determine its characteristics. Additional imaging may be used to assess the bladder wall, nearby structures, lymph nodes, or distant areas when more advanced disease is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:153:"निदान में सिस्टोस्कोपी, बायोप्सी और मूत्र जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:536:"Avoiding tobacco is one of the most important preventable measures for reducing bladder cancer risk. People who work with chemicals associated with bladder cancer should follow workplace exposure controls and use appropriate protective equipment. Adequate hydration may support normal urinary health, although it does not eliminate cancer risk. Persistent or unexplained blood in the urine should be evaluated promptly, even when it occurs without pain, because early investigation can help identify bladder disease at an earlier stage.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:127:"धूम्रपान और हानिकारक रसायनों के संपर्क से बचें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:392:"Bladder cancer requires prompt medical evaluation, particularly for blood in the urine or persistent urinary symptoms. Seek assessment for visible blood in the urine, painful or frequent urination, unexplained weight loss, persistent pelvic or back pain, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for heavy bleeding, inability to urinate, severe pain, fainting, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:101;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:107;s:10:"disease_id";i:155;s:11:"overview_en";s:485:"Urethritis is inflammation and irritation of the urethra, the tube that carries urine from the body. It may cause burning or pain during urination, urinary urgency or frequency, discharge, itching, or discomfort around the genital area. Urethritis can affect both men and women and may be caused by infections or by noninfectious irritation. Identifying the cause is important because untreated infectious urethritis can lead to complications and may be transmitted to sexual partners.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:182:"यूरेथ्राइटिस मूत्रमार्ग की सूजन है जो अक्सर संक्रमण के कारण होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:459:"Urethritis can be caused by bacteria or viruses. Bacterial causes include organisms associated with urinary tract infections and sexually transmitted infections, including chlamydia and gonorrhea. Viral causes can include herpes simplex virus and cytomegalovirus. Urethral injury and irritation from certain chemical products, such as some spermicides or contraceptive preparations, can also cause inflammation. In some cases, no specific cause is identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:155:"बैक्टीरियल तथा यौन संचारित संक्रमण इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:466:"Risk factors include a history of sexually transmitted infections, having multiple sexual partners, and sexual activity that increases exposure to infectious organisms. Urethritis can also occur after irritation or injury to the urethra. Some infections may occur more frequently in particular age or sex groups. Previous urethritis or other genitourinary infections may also be relevant. Appropriate sexual health practices can reduce exposure to infectious causes.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:130:"असुरक्षित यौन संबंध और संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:492:"Diagnosis involves a medical history, physical examination, and testing to identify infection or another cause of inflammation. Depending on the symptoms, healthcare professionals may examine the genital and abdominal areas and assess for discharge or tenderness. Urinalysis and urine cultures may be performed, along with specific tests for gonorrhea, chlamydia, and other sexually transmitted infections. A urethral swab or additional investigations may be used when clinically appropriate.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:134:"निदान में मूत्र जांच और संक्रमण परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:545:"Prevention of infectious urethritis includes reducing exposure to sexually transmitted infections through safer sexual practices, appropriate barrier protection, and testing when exposure or symptoms occur. Prompt evaluation of urinary or genital symptoms can help identify infections before complications develop. When urethritis is caused by an infection, appropriate evaluation and treatment of sexual partners may help prevent reinfection. Avoiding known chemical irritants or sources of urethral injury may help prevent noninfectious forms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:136:"सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार अपनाएं और स्वच्छता बनाए रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:360:"Urethritis should be medically assessed because infections can require specific treatment and may cause complications if untreated. Seek prompt care for painful urination, discharge, pelvic or genital pain, fever, blood in the urine, or worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for severe systemic illness, severe pain, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:102;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:108;s:10:"disease_id";i:156;s:11:"overview_en";s:536:"Urinary retention is the inability to empty the bladder completely or, in acute cases, the inability to urinate at all. It may develop suddenly or gradually. Symptoms can include difficulty starting urination, a weak or interrupted stream, frequent small amounts of urine, a feeling that the bladder has not emptied, lower abdominal discomfort, or an urgent inability to pass urine. Acute urinary retention can be painful and requires prompt medical evaluation because prolonged inability to empty the bladder can lead to complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"मूत्र अवरोध ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें मूत्राशय पूरी तरह खाली नहीं हो पाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:504:"Urinary retention can result from blockage of urine flow, impaired bladder muscle function, or problems with the nerves that control urination. Common causes include enlargement of the prostate, narrowing of the urethra, urinary stones, infections, pelvic conditions, neurological disorders, and certain medicines. Urinary retention may also develop after some surgical procedures or because of conditions affecting the bladder or surrounding structures. More than one contributing factor may be present.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:180:"प्रोस्टेट वृद्धि, तंत्रिका विकार और कुछ दवाएं इसके कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:423:"Risk factors include enlargement of the prostate, previous urinary tract procedures, urethral narrowing, urinary stones, neurological diseases, diabetes, pelvic disorders, certain medicines, and previous episodes of urinary retention. Risk may also increase after some operations or when conditions interfere with normal bladder muscle or nerve function. Older adults may have several contributing factors at the same time.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:144:"बीपीएच, तंत्रिका विकार और बढ़ती उम्र जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:485:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and physical examination, including assessment of urinary symptoms, medicines, previous procedures, and neurological or pelvic conditions. Measurement of the amount of urine remaining in the bladder after urination is commonly performed with a bladder scan or catheter. Urinalysis may identify infection or blood. Depending on the suspected cause, ultrasound, imaging, urine-flow testing, cystoscopy, or other urological studies may be required.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:125:"निदान में ब्लैडर स्कैन और मूत्र जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:548:"Prevention depends on the underlying cause. Conditions such as prostate enlargement, urinary infections, urinary stones, and neurological disorders should be appropriately evaluated and managed. Medicines that can interfere with urination should be reviewed with a healthcare professional when symptoms occur. Maintaining appropriate fluid intake and seeking care for worsening difficulty urinating may help prevent complications. Sudden inability to urinate, particularly with severe lower abdominal discomfort, requires prompt medical assessment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:106:"मूत्र संबंधी रोगों का समय पर उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:351:"Acute urinary retention is a medical emergency. Seek emergency medical treatment immediately if there is a sudden inability to urinate, particularly when accompanied by severe lower abdominal pain or swelling. Chronic or incomplete urinary retention also requires medical assessment because it can cause serious urinary tract and kidney complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:103;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:109;s:10:"disease_id";i:157;s:11:"overview_en";s:330:"Kidney cancer is a cancer that begins in the kidneys, usually in the cells lining the small tubes that filter blood and produce urine. Early kidney cancer may cause no symptoms. As it grows, it can cause blood in the urine, persistent pain in the side or back, a lump, unexplained weight loss, fatigue, or other changes in health.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:167:"किडनी कैंसर गुर्दे के ऊतकों में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:365:"The exact cause of kidney cancer is not always known. Cancer develops when abnormal kidney cells acquire changes that allow them to grow and divide uncontrollably. Factors associated with increased risk include tobacco exposure, obesity, high blood pressure, long-term dialysis, certain inherited conditions, family history, and some long-term medication exposures.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:137:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा और आनुवंशिक कारक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:336:"Risk factors for kidney cancer include smoking, excess body weight, high blood pressure, long-term dialysis, a family history of kidney cancer, and certain inherited disorders such as von Hippel-Lindau syndrome. Risk generally increases with age. Some long-term medication exposures and certain kidney conditions may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:159:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा और पारिवारिक इतिहास प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:352:"Kidney cancer is evaluated using the medical history, physical examination, and tests such as blood and urine studies and imaging. Ultrasound, CT, or MRI can help identify a kidney mass and assess its location and extent. A biopsy may be performed in selected cases when tissue confirmation is needed. Additional imaging may be used to look for spread.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:135:"निदान में सीटी स्कैन, एमआरआई और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:413:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent kidney cancer because some risk factors cannot be changed. Avoiding tobacco use is an important preventive measure. Maintaining a healthy body weight, managing blood pressure, and following appropriate medical care for kidney disease may also reduce risk. People with a strong family history or inherited risk may benefit from medical assessment and appropriate surveillance.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"धूम्रपान से बचें और स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:318:"Kidney cancer requires prompt medical evaluation for persistent blood in the urine, unexplained weight loss, persistent flank or abdominal pain, a mass, fever without an apparent cause, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for heavy bleeding, severe pain, fainting, severe weakness, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:104;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:110;s:10:"disease_id";i:158;s:11:"overview_en";s:392:"Renal artery stenosis is narrowing of one or both arteries that supply blood to the kidneys. Reduced blood flow can activate mechanisms that raise blood pressure and, in some cases, impair kidney function. The most common causes are atherosclerosis and fibromuscular dysplasia. Some people have no symptoms, while others develop difficult-to-control hypertension or declining kidney function.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:197:"रीनल आर्टरी स्टेनोसिस गुर्दों को रक्त पहुंचाने वाली धमनियों का संकुचन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:437:"Renal artery stenosis is most commonly caused by atherosclerosis, in which fatty deposits and arterial changes narrow the renal artery. It can also result from fibromuscular dysplasia, particularly in younger patients. Less common causes include inflammatory vascular disorders, trauma, compression, or other structural abnormalities. Narrowing reduces kidney blood flow and may activate hormonal mechanisms that increase blood pressure.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:119:"एथेरोस्क्लेरोसिस इसका सबसे सामान्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:403:"Risk factors for atherosclerotic renal artery stenosis include older age, smoking, high blood pressure, diabetes, high cholesterol, and other cardiovascular risk factors. Fibromuscular dysplasia is more often associated with women and may occur without the usual cardiovascular risk factors. A history of vascular disease elsewhere in the body can also increase the likelihood of renal artery narrowing.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:952:"रीनल आर्टरी स्टेनोसिस के जोखिम कारक इसके कारण पर निर्भर करते हैं। एथेरोस्क्लेरोटिक प्रकार उन लोगों में अधिक हो सकता है जिनमें उच्च रक्तचाप, मधुमेह, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल, धूम्रपान या पहले से हृदय-रक्तवाहिका रोग जैसे कारक हों। यह स्थिति फाइब्रोमस्कुलर डिस्प्लेसिया के कारण भी हो सकती है, जिसके जोखिम पैटर्न अलग होते हैं और जो केवल एथेरोस्क्लेरोसिस के कारण नहीं होता।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:527:"Diagnosis involves assessing blood pressure, kidney function, cardiovascular risk factors, and features suggesting renovascular disease. Imaging may include Doppler ultrasound, CT angiography, or magnetic resonance angiography to evaluate renal arteries. In selected circumstances, catheter-based angiography provides detailed visualization. Testing is generally considered when renal artery narrowing is clinically suspected, particularly with difficult-to-control hypertension or unexplained deterioration in kidney function.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:187:"निदान में डॉप्लर अल्ट्रासाउंड, सीटी एंजियोग्राफी और एमआरआई शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:487:"Atherosclerotic renal artery stenosis shares many risk factors with cardiovascular disease. Not smoking, maintaining healthy blood pressure and cholesterol levels, controlling diabetes, exercising regularly, maintaining a healthy weight, and following a heart-healthy diet can reduce vascular risk. People with established cardiovascular disease should follow recommended medical treatment and monitoring. Fibromuscular dysplasia cannot generally be prevented through lifestyle measures.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1152:"रीनल आर्टरी स्टेनोसिस को पूरी तरह रोकने का निश्चित तरीका नहीं है, लेकिन एथेरोस्क्लेरोसिस से जुड़े जोखिम को रक्तचाप, कोलेस्ट्रॉल और मधुमेह को नियंत्रित करके तथा तंबाकू से बचकर कम किया जा सकता है। हृदय के लिए स्वस्थ आहार, नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि, स्वस्थ वजन और निर्धारित दवाएं रक्त वाहिकाओं के जोखिम को कम करने में मदद कर सकती हैं। फाइब्रोमस्कुलर डिस्प्लेसिया या अन्य कारणों वाले लोगों को व्यक्तिगत चिकित्सा निगरानी की आवश्यकता हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:464:"Renal artery stenosis requires medical assessment because reduced blood flow to the kidneys can contribute to difficult-to-control high blood pressure and declining kidney function. Seek prompt care for rapidly worsening blood pressure, worsening kidney function, significant swelling, or reduced urination. Emergency care is needed for severe chest pain, severe breathing difficulty, neurological symptoms, or other signs of a serious cardiovascular complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:105;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:111;s:10:"disease_id";i:159;s:11:"overview_en";s:564:"Vesicoureteral reflux is a condition in which urine flows backward from the bladder toward one or both ureters and sometimes into the kidneys. Normally, the junction between the ureter and bladder helps prevent this backward flow. Reflux is often identified during childhood and may be associated with repeated urinary tract infections. In some children it improves as the urinary tract matures, while more significant reflux can increase the risk of kidney infections and kidney scarring. Evaluation and follow-up depend on the severity and associated infections.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:194:"वेसिकोयूरेटरल रिफ्लक्स में मूत्र मूत्राशय से वापस गुर्दों की ओर जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:590:"Vesicoureteral reflux usually occurs because the valve-like mechanism where the ureter enters the bladder does not prevent urine from flowing backward effectively. In primary reflux, this abnormality is generally present from birth and may improve as a child grows. Secondary reflux can develop when another condition increases pressure within the bladder or interferes with normal urinary drainage. Repeated urinary infections can occur because bacteria may travel upward toward the kidneys. The severity of reflux varies from mild backward flow to significant reflux reaching the kidneys.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:602:"वेसिकोयूरेटेरल रिफ्लक्स आमतौर पर मूत्रवाहिनी और मूत्राशय के बीच वाल्व जैसी व्यवस्था की जन्मजात असामान्यता के कारण होता है। मूत्र मार्ग की अन्य संरचनात्मक असामान्यताएं या मूत्राशय की कार्य संबंधी समस्या भी योगदान दे सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:591:"Risk of vesicoureteral reflux is increased by a family history of the condition because primary reflux can be inherited. It is more commonly identified in children and may occur with urinary tract abnormalities. Recurrent urinary tract infections are closely associated with reflux because backward urine flow can facilitate movement of bacteria toward the kidneys. Some children with bladder or urinary drainage problems may develop secondary reflux. The likelihood and clinical importance of reflux depend on its grade and whether kidney infections or structural abnormalities are present.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:517:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, जन्मजात मूत्र मार्ग की असामान्यताएं, बार-बार मूत्र संक्रमण और मूत्राशय या मूत्र प्रवाह में बाधा डालने वाली स्थितियां जोखिम बढ़ा सकती हैं। यह समस्या बच्चों में अधिक देखी जाती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:582:"Diagnosis of vesicoureteral reflux generally involves imaging of the urinary tract, particularly when a child has recurrent urinary tract infections or other findings that raise concern. A voiding cystourethrogram (VCUG) can show whether urine flows backward from the bladder toward the ureters and kidneys during urination. Ultrasound may assess kidney size and structure, while other imaging may be used when kidney damage or scarring is suspected. Urine testing and cultures are important when infection is present. The results help determine the severity and need for follow-up.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:606:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड और वॉइडिंग सिस्टोयूरेथ्रोग्राम शामिल हो सकते हैं, जिससे पेशाब के दौरान मूत्र के मूत्राशय से गुर्दों की ओर वापस जाने का पता चलता है। आवश्यकता होने पर गुर्दों की संरचना या कार्य की अतिरिक्त जांच की जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:609:"Primary vesicoureteral reflux cannot always be prevented because it may result from an inherited or developmental abnormality of the urinary tract. Preventing and promptly treating urinary tract infections can reduce the risk of kidney complications. Children with recurrent infections or known urinary abnormalities should receive appropriate medical follow-up. Good hydration, regular bladder emptying, and management of constipation may support healthy urinary function. Children diagnosed with reflux may require monitoring or treatment according to the severity of reflux and their history of infections.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1278:"वेसिकोयूरेटेरल रिफ्लक्स को हमेशा रोका नहीं जा सकता क्योंकि प्राथमिक रिफ्लक्स जन्म से मौजूद मूत्रमार्ग की संरचनात्मक असामान्यताओं के कारण होता है। हालांकि, मूत्र मार्ग के संक्रमण को कम करना और उनका समय पर उपचार करना गुर्दे की जटिलताओं को सीमित करने में मदद कर सकता है। पर्याप्त पानी पीना, मूत्राशय की उचित आदतें रखना और बार-बार होने वाले मूत्र संक्रमण की चिकित्सकीय जांच उपयोगी है। बार-बार संक्रमण या ज्ञात रिफ्लक्स वाले बच्चों को चिकित्सक की सलाह के अनुसार नियमित फॉलो-अप कराना चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:425:"Vesicoureteral reflux requires medical evaluation and monitoring because urine flowing backward toward the kidneys can contribute to recurrent urinary tract infections and kidney damage. Seek prompt care for fever, back or side pain, painful urination, vomiting, blood in the urine, or worsening urinary symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for severe illness, confusion, fainting, or signs of a serious kidney infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:106;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:112;s:10:"disease_id";i:160;s:11:"overview_en";s:571:"Diabetic nephropathy, also called diabetic kidney disease, is kidney damage that develops as a complication of diabetes. Persistently high blood glucose and elevated blood pressure can damage the small blood vessels and filtering structures of the kidneys over time. Early kidney disease may cause few or no symptoms, so urine and blood testing are important for people with diabetes. As kidney function declines, protein may appear in the urine and waste products can accumulate in the blood. Early detection and management can slow progression and reduce complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:172:"डायबिटिक नेफ्रोपैथी मधुमेह के कारण होने वाली गुर्दे की क्षति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:534:"Diabetic nephropathy develops through long-term effects of diabetes on the kidneys. Persistently elevated blood glucose can damage the tiny blood vessels and filtering units of the kidneys, while high blood pressure can accelerate this injury. Abnormal metabolic and inflammatory processes associated with diabetes may also contribute. Over time, the kidneys may become less effective at filtering waste and regulating fluid and electrolytes. The process usually develops gradually and may be present before noticeable symptoms occur.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:204:"अनियंत्रित मधुमेह समय के साथ गुर्दों की रक्त वाहिकाओं को नुकसान पहुंचाती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:526:"Risk of diabetic nephropathy increases with longer duration of diabetes and poor long-term blood glucose control. High blood pressure substantially increases the likelihood and progression of kidney damage. Other contributing factors include smoking, abnormal blood lipid levels, family history of diabetic kidney disease, and certain cardiovascular risk factors. Both type 1 and type 2 diabetes can cause kidney disease. Regular monitoring is particularly important because kidney damage may develop without obvious symptoms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"दीर्घकालिक मधुमेह और उच्च रक्तचाप जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:572:"Diabetic nephropathy is evaluated with tests that measure kidney function and detect albumin or other protein in the urine. Blood testing commonly includes serum creatinine and estimation of glomerular filtration rate. Urine albumin testing can identify early kidney damage before substantial loss of filtration occurs. Blood pressure measurement and assessment of diabetes control are also important. Repeated abnormal results may be needed to confirm persistent kidney involvement and distinguish diabetic kidney disease from temporary changes or other kidney disorders.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:147:"निदान में मूत्र प्रोटीन और किडनी फंक्शन जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:550:"The risk of diabetic kidney disease can be reduced by maintaining good long-term blood glucose control and managing blood pressure. Regular kidney screening with urine albumin and blood tests allows early changes to be detected. Avoiding smoking, maintaining a healthy weight, following an appropriate diet, and taking prescribed medicines consistently can support kidney health. People with diabetes should discuss kidney monitoring with their healthcare team and avoid unnecessary medicines or supplements that may adversely affect kidney function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:111:"रक्त शर्करा और रक्तचाप को नियंत्रित रखें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:433:"Diabetic nephropathy requires ongoing monitoring because kidney damage can progress gradually and may eventually lead to kidney failure. Seek prompt assessment for rapidly increasing swelling, major changes in urination, persistent vomiting, severe weakness, confusion, or worsening shortness of breath. Emergency care is needed for severe breathing difficulty, altered consciousness, or other signs of a serious kidney complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:107;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:113;s:10:"disease_id";i:162;s:11:"overview_en";s:415:"Premature ejaculation is a common sexual problem in which ejaculation occurs sooner than a person or their partner would like, often with limited control over ejaculation and associated distress. It may occur from the beginning of sexual activity or develop after a period of previously satisfactory sexual function. Causes can involve psychological, relationship, neurological, hormonal, or other physical factors.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:167:"शीघ्रपतन ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें अपेक्षा से पहले स्खलन हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:425:"Premature ejaculation can be associated with anxiety, stress, relationship difficulties, concerns about sexual performance, or previous sexual experiences. Physical factors may include changes in hormone levels, abnormalities involving brain chemicals, inflammation of the prostate or urethra, thyroid problems, erectile difficulties, or altered sensitivity. In many people, more than one factor contributes to the condition.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:124:"तनाव, चिंता और जैविक कारक इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:442:"Risk factors may include anxiety about sexual performance, relationship stress, depression, erectile difficulties, hormonal or thyroid problems, inflammation of the prostate or urethra, and previous sexual experiences associated with rapid ejaculation. Stress and concerns about sexual performance can reinforce the problem. The condition can affect people at different ages and does not necessarily result from a single physical abnormality.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:125:"तनाव, चिंता और संबंध समस्याएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:477:"Premature ejaculation is usually diagnosed from a detailed sexual and medical history. A healthcare professional asks about the timing of ejaculation, degree of control, how consistently the problem occurs, and the distress it causes. Questions about relationships, anxiety, erectile function, medicines, and other health conditions may help identify contributing factors. A physical examination or laboratory tests may be performed when another medical condition is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान सामान्यतः इतिहास और लक्षणों पर आधारित होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:424:"Premature ejaculation cannot always be prevented because it may result from a combination of psychological and physical factors. Managing stress and anxiety, maintaining open communication with a partner, addressing erectile or other health problems, and seeking help early can reduce the impact of symptoms. Healthy lifestyle habits and appropriate treatment of underlying medical conditions may also support sexual health.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:112:"तनाव प्रबंधन और परामर्श सहायक हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:332:"Premature ejaculation is generally not an emergency and can usually be addressed through routine medical care. Seek assessment if the problem is persistent, causes significant distress, or occurs with other sexual, urinary, hormonal, or neurological symptoms. Sudden severe genital pain or injury requires prompt medical evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:108;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:114;s:10:"disease_id";i:164;s:11:"overview_en";s:436:"Low testosterone, also called testosterone deficiency or hypogonadism when clinically significant, occurs when the body does not produce enough testosterone for normal needs. Testosterone is important for sexual development, reproductive function, muscle and bone health, and other body processes. Symptoms may include reduced sexual desire, erectile difficulties, fatigue, reduced muscle mass, mood changes, and decreased bone density.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:220:"कम टेस्टोस्टेरोन ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें टेस्टोस्टेरोन हार्मोन का स्तर कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:439:"Low testosterone can result from problems in the testes, which produce testosterone, or from disorders affecting the hypothalamus or pituitary gland, which regulate testosterone production. Causes may include certain genetic conditions, testicular injury or disease, pituitary disorders, some medicines, obesity, chronic illness, and aging-related hormonal changes. The underlying cause should be determined before treatment is considered.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:158:"उम्र, हार्मोनल विकार और कुछ बीमारियां इसके कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:392:"Risk factors include increasing age, obesity, chronic illnesses such as diabetes, disorders affecting the testes or pituitary gland, previous testicular injury, certain genetic conditions, and use of some medicines. Chronic severe illness and significant sleep problems can also be associated with reduced testosterone levels. Risk varies according to the underlying cause and overall health.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:150:"मोटापा, बढ़ती उम्र और पुरानी बीमारियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:435:"Low testosterone is diagnosed using symptoms and laboratory testing rather than a single symptom alone. Testosterone levels are usually measured with blood tests performed in the morning and may need to be repeated because levels fluctuate. Additional hormone tests can help determine whether the problem originates in the testes or in the hypothalamus or pituitary gland. Other tests may be performed according to the suspected cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:149:"निदान में रक्त टेस्टोस्टेरोन और हार्मोन जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:453:"Not all causes of low testosterone can be prevented, particularly genetic, testicular, or pituitary disorders. Maintaining a healthy weight, exercising regularly, managing chronic diseases, getting adequate sleep, avoiding unnecessary use of medicines that affect hormone production, and limiting harmful substance exposure may support normal hormonal health. Persistent symptoms should be evaluated rather than assuming that aging alone is responsible.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:126:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें और मूल रोगों का उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:373:"Low testosterone usually develops gradually and is evaluated through medical assessment and appropriate hormone testing. Seek prompt care for significant or rapidly changing symptoms, particularly when associated with severe weakness, neurological symptoms, testicular pain or swelling, or other concerning changes. Sudden severe testicular pain requires urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:109;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:115;s:10:"disease_id";i:165;s:11:"overview_en";s:399:"Prostatitis refers to inflammation or infection involving the prostate gland. It may cause pain in the pelvis or lower back, painful urination, difficulty urinating, frequent urination and pain during ejaculation. Some forms are caused by bacterial infection, while chronic prostatitis or chronic pelvic pain syndrome may occur without evidence of infection. Symptoms and severity vary considerably.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:245:"प्रोस्टेटाइटिस प्रोस्टेट ग्रंथि की सूजन है जिससे मूत्र और पेल्विक संबंधी लक्षण हो सकते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:382:"Acute and chronic bacterial prostatitis are caused by bacteria that enter or spread to the prostate. Bacteria may reach the prostate from the urinary tract or surrounding areas. Chronic pelvic pain syndrome has no single established cause and may involve inflammation, pelvic muscle dysfunction, nerve-related pain or other factors. Some cases remain unexplained despite evaluation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:161:"बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण और दीर्घकालिक सूजन इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:346:"Risk factors include previous urinary tract infections, prostatitis, urinary tract abnormalities, procedures involving the urinary tract and conditions that interfere with normal urine flow. Prostate problems and pelvic injury may also contribute. Some people develop chronic pelvic pain symptoms without an identifiable risk factor or infection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:136:"मूत्र संक्रमण और प्रोस्टेट विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:391:"Diagnosis involves medical history and physical examination, including assessment of urinary and pelvic symptoms. A healthcare professional may perform a digital rectal examination to assess the prostate. Urine tests and cultures can help identify bacterial infection. Blood tests or other investigations may be used when needed to evaluate complications or exclude other causes of symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:157:"निदान में मूत्र जांच, प्रोस्टेट परीक्षण और कल्चर शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:429:"Some bacterial forms of prostatitis may be reduced by promptly treating urinary infections and following medical advice for urinary tract procedures. Maintaining good hydration and avoiding behaviors that worsen urinary symptoms may help some people. There is no guaranteed way to prevent chronic prostatitis or chronic pelvic pain syndrome. Persistent urinary or pelvic symptoms should be evaluated by a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:130:"मूत्र संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:372:"Prostatitis should be medically assessed because some forms can be caused by infection and may require treatment. Seek prompt care for fever, chills, painful urination, pelvic or genital pain, difficulty urinating, or worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for inability to urinate, severe systemic illness, confusion, fainting, or rapidly worsening infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:110;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:116;s:10:"disease_id";i:168;s:11:"overview_en";s:354:"Testicular cancer is a cancer that develops in the tissues of a testicle. It most often affects younger and middle-aged men and may first appear as a painless lump, swelling, enlargement, heaviness, or change in the size or feel of a testicle. Most testicular cancers can be treated successfully, particularly when detected and treated at an early stage.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:141:"वृषण कैंसर अंडकोष में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:405:"The exact cause of testicular cancer is not known in most cases. It develops when cells in the testicle acquire abnormal changes that cause uncontrolled growth. Developmental and genetic factors can contribute to susceptibility. Some testicular cancers arise from abnormal germ cells that can develop into cancer over time. Most people with testicular cancer do not have an identifiable preventable cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:169:"आनुवंशिक कारण और वृषण विकास की असामान्यताएं योगदान कर सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:355:"Risk is increased by an undescended testicle, particularly when it was not corrected early, as well as a previous history of testicular cancer. A family history of testicular cancer and certain developmental or genetic conditions may also increase risk. Testicular cancer is most common in younger and middle-aged men, although it can occur at other ages.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:147:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और अवरोही न हुए वृषण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:465:"Evaluation usually begins with a medical history and examination of the testicles and scrotum. Scrotal ultrasound can help identify and characterize a testicular mass. Blood tests may measure tumor markers that can support diagnosis and help assess the disease. Additional imaging, such as CT scans, may be used to determine whether cancer has spread. Definitive diagnosis is generally established through surgical evaluation and examination of the affected tissue.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:162:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड, ट्यूमर मार्कर और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:402:"There is no reliable way to prevent most cases of testicular cancer because many risk factors cannot be changed. People with an undescended testicle or other known risk factors should follow appropriate medical advice. Being familiar with the normal appearance and feel of the testicles can help a person notice changes such as a new lump, swelling, or enlargement and seek medical evaluation promptly.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"समय पर पहचान उपचार परिणाम बेहतर बनाती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:332:"Testicular cancer requires prompt medical evaluation for a lump, swelling, enlargement, heaviness, or persistent change in a testicle. Seek assessment for persistent testicular discomfort or a new scrotal abnormality. Sudden severe testicular pain requires emergency assessment because testicular torsion can cause similar symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:111;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:117;s:10:"disease_id";i:169;s:11:"overview_en";s:384:"Testicular torsion is a medical emergency in which the spermatic cord twists and reduces or completely cuts off blood flow to a testicle. It usually causes sudden and severe pain and swelling in one side of the scrotum and may be accompanied by nausea or vomiting. Rapid diagnosis and treatment are important because prolonged loss of blood supply can permanently damage the testicle.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:232:"वृषण मरोड़ एक आपात स्थिति है जिसमें शुक्रवाहिनी मुड़ जाती है और रक्त प्रवाह रुक जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:429:"Testicular torsion usually occurs when a testicle is able to rotate too freely inside the scrotum because of an abnormal anatomical attachment. The testicle may twist spontaneously, sometimes during sleep, physical activity, or after minor trauma. It can also occur during puberty when rapid growth changes the position or mobility of the testicle. Once twisting begins, blood flow through the spermatic cord may become impaired.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:124:"अंडकोष की असामान्य संरचना इसका प्रमुख कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:403:"Testicular torsion is more common during adolescence, although it can occur at any age. An anatomical abnormality that allows the testicle to rotate freely is the main underlying risk factor. A previous episode of torsion or a family history of torsion may increase risk. Sudden movement, exercise, or minor injury may sometimes precede an episode, but torsion can also occur without an obvious trigger.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:156:"किशोरावस्था और संरचनात्मक असामान्यताएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:441:"Diagnosis is based on the sudden onset and characteristics of scrotal pain, medical history, and physical examination. The affected testicle may be swollen, tender, or positioned differently from the other testicle. Doppler ultrasound can assess blood flow and help distinguish torsion from other causes of acute scrotal pain. When torsion is strongly suspected, emergency surgical evaluation should not be unnecessarily delayed for testing.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:155:"निदान परीक्षण और डॉप्लर अल्ट्रासाउंड द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:445:"Many cases of testicular torsion cannot be prevented because the underlying anatomical abnormality is usually present from birth. People who have experienced torsion on one side may be advised to have the other testicle surgically secured to prevent future twisting. Any sudden or severe testicular or scrotal pain should be treated as an emergency because prompt treatment gives the best chance of preserving blood flow and testicular function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:83:"समय पर शल्य चिकित्सा आवश्यक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:336:"Testicular torsion is a medical emergency. Seek emergency medical attention immediately for sudden severe pain in one testicle, rapid scrotal swelling, a testicle that appears higher than usual, nausea, or vomiting. Treatment must be provided as soon as possible because prolonged loss of blood flow can permanently damage the testicle.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:112;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:118;s:10:"disease_id";i:170;s:11:"overview_en";s:457:"A hydrocele is a collection of fluid around a testicle that causes swelling of the scrotum. Hydroceles are common in newborn infants and often disappear on their own during the first months of life. In older children and adults, a hydrocele may develop because of fluid accumulation, inflammation, injury, or another condition affecting the testicle or surrounding tissues. It is often painless, although a large hydrocele can cause heaviness or discomfort.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:170:"हाइड्रोसील अंडकोष के आसपास तरल पदार्थ भरने से होने वाली सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:466:"In newborns, a hydrocele commonly develops when the channel between the abdomen and scrotum does not close completely after the testicle descends. Fluid can then pass from the abdomen into the scrotum and become trapped around the testicle. In older males, a hydrocele can result from increased fluid production or reduced drainage. Inflammation or injury of the testicle or epididymis can also contribute, and a hydrocele may occur together with an inguinal hernia.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"जन्मजात कारण, चोट या संक्रमण इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:451:"Hydroceles are particularly common in newborn boys, especially when the normal channel through which the testicle descends has not completely closed. In adults, factors that may increase risk include inflammation or infection involving the testicle or epididymis, injury to the scrotum, and conditions that interfere with normal fluid drainage. An associated inguinal hernia may also occur. Some hydroceles develop without an identifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:93:"संक्रमण और चोट जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:511:"Diagnosis usually begins with examination of the scrotum and surrounding structures. The healthcare professional may assess the size, tenderness, and consistency of the swelling and may use light transmission through the scrotum to help identify fluid. Ultrasound may be performed when the diagnosis is uncertain or when another condition such as a hernia, tumor, or testicular abnormality needs to be excluded. The medical history helps determine whether injury, inflammation, or another condition is involved.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:120:"निदान में परीक्षण और अल्ट्रासाउंड शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:470:"Many hydroceles, particularly those present at birth, cannot be prevented because they result from developmental changes before or shortly after birth. Protecting the testicles from injury and seeking appropriate treatment for infections or inflammation of the testicle or epididymis may reduce the risk of some acquired hydroceles. Newborns and adults with persistent or enlarging scrotal swelling should be evaluated so that other causes of swelling can be identified.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:126:"संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार जटिलताओं को रोक सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:304:"Hydrocele is usually not an emergency, but a new or persistent scrotal swelling should be medically assessed to determine its cause. Seek prompt care for increasing pain, redness, fever, significant swelling, or a sudden change in the scrotum. Sudden severe testicular pain requires emergency evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:113;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:119;s:10:"disease_id";i:171;s:11:"overview_en";s:495:"A varicocele is an enlargement of the veins within the scrotum, similar to varicose veins in other parts of the body. It most commonly occurs on the left side and may cause no symptoms. Some people experience a dull aching discomfort, a feeling of heaviness, or a noticeable enlargement of the scrotal veins. Varicoceles can be associated with impaired testicular development or abnormal sperm production in some individuals and are sometimes discovered during evaluation for fertility problems.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:124:"वैरिकोसील अंडकोश की नसों का असामान्य बढ़ना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:516:"A varicocele develops when blood is not efficiently returned from the veins of the testicle, allowing the veins to enlarge. Abnormal or ineffective functioning of the valves within these veins can contribute to backward blood flow and venous enlargement. The left-sided predominance is related partly to differences in the anatomy of the testicular veins. The exact mechanisms responsible for fertility effects are not completely established, but increased scrotal temperature and altered blood flow may play a role.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:119:"शिराओं के वाल्व की खराबी इसका प्रमुख कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:495:"Varicocele is most often identified during adolescence or early adulthood. The condition is more common on the left side because of differences in venous anatomy. Family or individual anatomical factors may influence susceptibility. A varicocele may be associated with abnormal testicular growth or fertility difficulties, although many people with varicoceles have normal fertility and no symptoms. A newly appearing varicocele later in adulthood may require evaluation for an underlying cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:117:"किशोरावस्था और शिरा विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:480:"A varicocele is often detected during a physical examination while standing and sometimes while performing a maneuver that increases abdominal pressure. The clinician may assess the size of the testicles and the degree of venous enlargement. Scrotal ultrasound can confirm the diagnosis and evaluate blood flow when the examination is uncertain. Semen analysis may be considered in people being evaluated for fertility, and adolescents may undergo monitoring of testicular growth.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:155:"निदान परीक्षण और डॉप्लर अल्ट्रासाउंड द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:483:"There is no established way to completely prevent varicocele because its development is largely related to individual venous anatomy. Regular medical assessment during adolescence can help identify changes in testicular size or development. People who notice scrotal swelling, persistent discomfort, or fertility concerns should seek evaluation. Early assessment is particularly useful when a varicocele is associated with reduced testicular growth or abnormal reproductive function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:141:"समय पर जांच प्रजनन क्षमता सुरक्षित रखने में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:358:"Varicocele is usually not an emergency and may cause a dull scrotal ache or no symptoms. Seek medical assessment for persistent pain, testicular size changes, swelling, or concerns about fertility. Sudden severe testicular pain or rapid swelling requires emergency evaluation because other conditions, including testicular torsion, may have similar symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:114;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:120;s:10:"disease_id";i:172;s:11:"overview_en";s:321:"Epididymitis is inflammation of the epididymis, the tube that carries sperm from the testicle toward the vas deferens. It commonly causes pain and swelling in the scrotum and may also cause urinary symptoms or fever. Infection is the most common cause, although medicines and other conditions can occasionally contribute.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:184:"एपिडिडिमाइटिस एपिडिडिमिस की सूजन है जो सामान्यतः संक्रमण से होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:400:"Epididymitis is most often caused by bacterial infection. In younger sexually active men, sexually transmitted infections such as chlamydia and gonorrhea are common causes. In older men or people with urinary tract problems, bacteria such as E. coli may be responsible. Less common causes include tuberculosis, urinary tract abnormalities, recent procedures, and certain medicines such as amiodarone.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:149:"बैक्टीरियल और यौन संचारित संक्रमण इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:295:"Risk increases with unprotected sexual activity and sexually transmitted infections, urinary tract infections, prostate or urinary tract abnormalities, recent urinary procedures, and regular use of a urinary catheter. Previous urinary tract surgery or structural problems may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:146:"असुरक्षित यौन संबंध और मूत्र संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:358:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms and physical examination, including assessment of the scrotum and testicles. Urine and blood tests may be used to identify infection, and testing for sexually transmitted infections may be appropriate. Ultrasound may be used when necessary, particularly to help distinguish epididymitis from other causes of acute scrotal pain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:127:"निदान में मूत्र जांच और अल्ट्रासाउंड शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:413:"Safer sexual practices, including appropriate condom use, can reduce the risk of sexually transmitted infections that cause epididymitis. Prompt diagnosis and treatment of urinary or sexually transmitted infections can reduce complications. People with urinary tract abnormalities or recurrent infections should follow appropriate medical management and seek evaluation for persistent urinary or scrotal symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:143:"सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार अपनाएं और संक्रमण का उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:373:"Epididymitis should be medically assessed because infection can spread to nearby structures and symptoms can resemble testicular torsion. Seek prompt care for testicular or scrotal pain, swelling, fever, urinary symptoms, or discharge. Emergency assessment is needed for sudden severe testicular pain, particularly with nausea or vomiting, because torsion must be excluded.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:115;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:121;s:10:"disease_id";i:173;s:11:"overview_en";s:320:"Orchitis is inflammation of one or both testicles. It may be caused by a viral or bacterial infection. Mumps is a well-known viral cause, while bacterial orchitis can occur with infections involving the urinary tract or reproductive system. Symptoms may include testicular pain, swelling, tenderness, fever, and fatigue.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:106:"ऑर्काइटिस एक या दोनों अंडकोष की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:367:"Orchitis may be caused by viruses or bacteria. Viral orchitis is commonly associated with mumps. Bacterial orchitis may develop when bacteria spread from an infection of the urinary tract, epididymis, or other nearby structures. Sexually transmitted infections can also cause infections involving the reproductive tract that may lead to inflammation of the testicles.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:130:"मम्प्स जैसे वायरल संक्रमण इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:289:"Risk factors include infections such as mumps, urinary or reproductive tract infections, sexually transmitted infections, and conditions that increase the likelihood of infection spreading to the testicles. Lack of vaccination against mumps can increase the risk of mumps-related orchitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:115:"टीकाकरण की कमी और संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:363:"Orchitis is diagnosed using symptoms, medical history, and examination of the scrotum and testicles. Tests may include urine testing, blood tests, and testing for sexually transmitted infections when appropriate. Ultrasound may help distinguish orchitis from other causes of acute testicular pain, particularly testicular torsion, which requires urgent treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:147:"निदान में परीक्षण, रक्त जांच और अल्ट्रासाउंड शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:360:"Vaccination against mumps is an important way to reduce the risk of mumps-related orchitis. Prompt evaluation and treatment of urinary, reproductive, and sexually transmitted infections can help prevent complications. Practicing safer sex and seeking medical care for symptoms of infection can also reduce the risk of infections that may involve the testicles.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:93:"टीकाकरण कुछ मामलों से बचाव करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:344:"Orchitis should be medically assessed, particularly when testicular pain or swelling develops. Seek prompt care for fever, significant swelling, persistent pain, or worsening symptoms. Emergency medical attention is needed for sudden severe testicular pain because testicular torsion can cause similar symptoms and requires immediate treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:116;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:122;s:10:"disease_id";i:174;s:11:"overview_en";s:633:"Balanitis is inflammation and swelling affecting the head of the penis and, often, the foreskin. It is more common in people who are not circumcised. The condition can result from irritation, infection, skin disorders, difficulty maintaining local hygiene, or conditions such as poorly controlled diabetes. Symptoms may include redness, swelling, soreness, itching, rash, pain, and discharge. The appearance and severity vary according to the underlying cause. Persistent or recurrent symptoms should be assessed by a healthcare professional because untreated inflammation can lead to scarring and difficulty retracting the foreskin.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:102:"बैलेनाइटिस लिंग के अग्रभाग की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:614:"Balanitis can have several causes. Poor hygiene may allow irritants, secretions, and microorganisms to accumulate beneath the foreskin. Bacterial or fungal infections can cause inflammation, while viral infections and sexually transmitted infections may also be considered in appropriate situations. Irritation from harsh soaps, chemicals, or inadequate rinsing can contribute. Skin conditions such as lichen sclerosus and inflammatory disorders may also affect the penis. Diabetes, particularly when blood glucose is poorly controlled, is associated with an increased risk of recurrent inflammation and infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:135:"खराब स्वच्छता, संक्रमण और जलन इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:536:"Risk factors include having an intact foreskin, difficulty keeping the area clean and dry, diabetes or persistently elevated blood glucose, recurrent infections, exposure to irritating soaps or chemicals, and underlying inflammatory or dermatologic conditions. Tight foreskin may make cleaning difficult and can contribute to recurrent episodes. Sexual exposure may be relevant when an infection is suspected. Repeated episodes should prompt evaluation for an underlying condition rather than relying only on repeated topical treatment.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:111:"मधुमेह और खराब स्वच्छता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:524:"Diagnosis is usually based on the medical history and examination of the penis and foreskin. The clinician looks for redness, swelling, rash, discharge, skin changes, or evidence of scarring. When infection is suspected, samples or skin tests may be used to look for bacterial, fungal, or viral causes. A biopsy may occasionally be needed when the diagnosis is uncertain or a persistent skin disorder is suspected. Evaluation may also consider conditions such as diabetes when symptoms are recurrent or difficult to control.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:134:"निदान परीक्षण और संक्रमण जांच द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:508:"Good genital hygiene can reduce the risk of balanitis. People with a foreskin should gently retract it when possible, wash the exposed area with water or a suitable mild cleanser, and dry the area afterward. Harsh soaps and irritating products should be avoided. Blood glucose should be appropriately controlled in people with diabetes. Recurrent or persistent inflammation should be medically assessed so that an infection, skin disorder, or difficulty retracting the foreskin can be identified and managed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:120:"उचित स्वच्छता रखें और मधुमेह नियंत्रित करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:327:"Balanitis is usually not an emergency but should be assessed when symptoms persist or recur. Seek medical care for significant swelling, pain, discharge, bleeding, difficulty urinating, fever, or worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed if severe swelling prevents urination or there are signs of a serious infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:117;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:123;s:10:"disease_id";i:175;s:11:"overview_en";s:354:"Phimosis is a condition in which the foreskin of the penis cannot be pulled back fully over the glans. Some degree of tightness is normal in young children and usually improves naturally with development. Persistent phimosis in older children or adults may cause pain, difficulty with hygiene, inflammation, painful erections, or problems with urination.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:192:"फाइमोसिस ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें अग्रचर्म पूरी तरह पीछे नहीं खींचा जा सकता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:430:"Phimosis may be a normal developmental condition in children when the foreskin has not yet separated naturally from the glans. In older children and adults, persistent tightness may result from repeated inflammation, infection, scarring, poor hygiene, skin disorders, or previous injury. Conditions such as balanitis and balanitis xerotica obliterans can produce scarring that makes the foreskin increasingly difficult to retract.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:130:"बार-बार संक्रमण और दाग बनना इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:416:"Risk factors for persistent phimosis include recurrent inflammation of the foreskin or glans, scarring, inadequate ability to maintain hygiene, certain skin disorders, diabetes, repeated forceful retraction, and previous injury. Adults with recurrent balanitis or conditions that cause foreskin scarring may be particularly susceptible. Normal childhood foreskin tightness should not be considered disease by itself.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:134:"खराब स्वच्छता और बार-बार संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:416:"Diagnosis is usually made through examination of the penis and assessment of whether the foreskin can be retracted without pain or injury. The clinician may look for inflammation, scarring, infection, or skin changes. Urinary symptoms, recurrent infections, painful erections, and other complications are also considered. Additional tests are generally unnecessary unless another condition or infection is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:142:"निदान सामान्यतः शारीरिक परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:473:"Normal childhood phimosis generally should not be forcibly retracted. Gentle hygiene and allowing the foreskin to separate naturally can prevent injury and scarring. Recurrent inflammation or infection should receive appropriate medical attention. People with persistent painful tightness, difficulty urinating, or repeated balanitis should seek evaluation. When treatment is required, medical guidance can help prevent complications and unnecessary trauma to the foreskin.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:93:"अच्छी स्वच्छता जोखिम कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:440:"Phimosis may often be managed routinely, but significant narrowing can interfere with urination or cause recurrent inflammation. Seek prompt medical assessment for painful or difficult urination, recurrent infections, bleeding, significant swelling, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed if the foreskin becomes trapped behind the glans and cannot be returned to its normal position, particularly with increasing swelling or pain.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:118;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:124;s:10:"disease_id";i:176;s:11:"overview_en";s:545:"Peyronie disease is a condition in which scar tissue, called a plaque, develops inside the penis and can cause curvature or changes in shape during an erection. The plaque may cause pain, shortening, narrowing, or difficulty with sexual activity. Some cases remain stable, while others change over time. The exact cause is not always clear, but injury or repeated minor trauma may contribute in susceptible individuals. Treatment depends on symptoms, degree of curvature, erectile function, and whether the condition is stable or still changing.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:186:"पेरोनी रोग में लिंग के भीतर दाग ऊतक बन जाते हैं जिससे टेढ़ापन आ सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:544:"The exact cause of Peyronie disease is uncertain. It is thought to involve abnormal wound healing and scar formation within the tissue of the penis. Repeated minor injuries or more significant trauma during sexual activity or other physical activity may contribute in some people. Genetic or connective-tissue factors may influence susceptibility. Some individuals develop the condition without recalling any injury. Other health conditions associated with abnormal scar formation or erectile problems may also occur alongside Peyronie disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:145:"बार-बार छोटी चोटें और आनुवंशिक कारण योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:429:"Risk factors for Peyronie disease include increasing age, previous injury to the penis, repeated minor trauma, and a family history of the condition. Certain connective-tissue disorders may also increase susceptibility. Erectile dysfunction can occur alongside Peyronie disease and may complicate symptoms. Not everyone with a possible risk factor develops the condition, and many affected people do not recall a specific injury.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:112:"उम्र और संयोजी ऊतक विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:510:"Peyronie disease is usually diagnosed from the medical history and physical examination. The clinician may ask about when curvature or pain began, whether it is changing, and whether erectile function has changed. Examination may identify the location and extent of plaque. Photographs of an erection or assessment of penile curvature during an induced erection may help determine severity when treatment is being considered. Ultrasound can evaluate plaque and blood flow when additional information is needed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:146:"निदान में परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार इमेजिंग शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:520:"Peyronie disease cannot reliably be prevented because the exact cause is uncertain. Avoiding unnecessary trauma to the penis and using appropriate care during sexual activity may reduce injury-related risk, although this does not guarantee prevention. People who notice persistent pain, new curvature, or a change in erectile function should seek evaluation rather than repeatedly traumatizing the affected area. Early assessment can help determine whether the condition is changing and whether treatment is appropriate.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:122:"समय पर चिकित्सकीय सलाह जटिलताएं कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:339:"Peyronie disease is generally not an emergency and is usually evaluated through routine medical care. Seek assessment for persistent or worsening penile curvature, pain, erectile difficulties, or problems with sexual function. Sudden severe penile pain, significant injury, or prolonged painful erection requires urgent medical evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:119;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:125;s:10:"disease_id";i:177;s:11:"overview_en";s:400:"Hypogonadism occurs when the body produces too little of the sex hormones needed for normal reproductive function and other body processes. In males, it usually involves low testosterone, while in females it may involve reduced estrogen production. It can affect sexual development, fertility, bone health, muscle mass, energy and mood. Hypogonadism may begin before puberty or develop later in life.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:199:"हाइपोगोनाडिज्म ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें शरीर पर्याप्त यौन हार्मोन नहीं बनाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:457:"Hypogonadism can result from problems in the testes or ovaries, called primary hypogonadism, or from disorders affecting the brain areas that control hormone production, called secondary hypogonadism. Causes may include genetic conditions, injury or infection of the reproductive organs, certain medicines, pituitary disorders, chronic illnesses, obesity, excessive exercise and some cancer treatments. Aging can also contribute to lower sex hormone levels.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:189:"हार्मोनल विकार, बढ़ती उम्र और आनुवंशिक स्थितियां इसका कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:378:"Risk factors depend on the underlying cause and may include genetic disorders, testicular or ovarian injury, infections, pituitary disease, obesity, chronic kidney or liver disease, diabetes, certain medicines and cancer treatment. A history of surgery or radiation involving reproductive organs or the brain may also increase risk. Some people have no identifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:165:"मोटापा, पुरानी बीमारियां और पिट्यूटरी विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:408:"Diagnosis usually begins with a medical history and physical examination, followed by blood tests measuring relevant sex hormone levels. Testosterone is commonly measured in males, while estrogen and related hormones may be assessed in females. Additional tests may evaluate pituitary hormones, thyroid function or other causes. Genetic testing, imaging or semen analysis may be recommended when appropriate.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान में हार्मोन जांच और शारीरिक परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:459:"Some causes of hypogonadism cannot be prevented, particularly genetic or developmental conditions. Risk may sometimes be reduced by protecting the reproductive organs from injury, avoiding unnecessary exposure to harmful substances and managing chronic illnesses. Regular medical care can help identify hormone-related problems early. People receiving treatments that may affect hormone production should discuss monitoring with their healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:126:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें और मूल रोगों का उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:364:"Hypogonadism usually develops gradually and requires medical evaluation to determine the underlying cause. Seek prompt assessment for significant or rapidly changing symptoms, particularly when accompanied by severe weakness, neurological symptoms, testicular pain or swelling, or other concerning changes. Sudden severe testicular pain requires urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:120;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:126;s:10:"disease_id";i:178;s:11:"overview_en";s:339:"Cryptorchidism, also called an undescended testicle, occurs when one or both testicles do not move into the scrotum before birth. It is most often identified in infancy or early childhood. The condition may affect fertility and can increase the risk of testicular cancer and other complications if the testicle remains outside the scrotum.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:171:"क्रिप्टॉर्किडिज्म में एक या दोनों अंडकोष अंडकोश में नहीं उतरते।";s:9:"causes_en";s:385:"Cryptorchidism occurs when a testicle fails to descend normally from the abdomen into the scrotum before birth. The process of descent is influenced by hormones, normal development of the testicle and supporting structures, and physical factors. Some cases are associated with genetic conditions, hormonal disorders, or abnormalities affecting the abdominal wall or reproductive tract.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:147:"यह सामान्यतः भ्रूण विकास की असामान्यता के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:378:"Cryptorchidism is more common in babies born prematurely or with low birth weight. Other risk factors include restricted fetal growth, conditions affecting normal hormone production, certain genetic or developmental disorders, and a family history of undescended testicles. The risk may be higher when other abnormalities of the reproductive or abdominal structures are present.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:147:"समय से पूर्व जन्म और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:386:"Cryptorchidism is usually identified during a physical examination of the newborn or child. The clinician checks whether each testicle can be felt in the scrotum and may determine whether it can be moved into the scrotum. Ultrasound or other imaging is not always necessary. Further evaluation may be required when the testicle cannot be located or when other abnormalities are present.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:143:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:392:"Cryptorchidism cannot usually be prevented because it is related to fetal development and factors that may not be controllable. Routine newborn and childhood examinations help identify an undescended testicle early. Children with cryptorchidism should receive appropriate medical follow-up so that treatment can be considered at the recommended age and potential complications can be reduced.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:104:"समय पर उपचार भविष्य के जोखिम कम करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:352:"Cryptorchidism requires medical evaluation because an undescended testicle can be associated with fertility problems and an increased risk of testicular cancer. Seek assessment when an undescended testicle is identified or when there is a new change in the scrotum. Sudden severe testicular pain requires emergency evaluation because torsion can occur.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:121;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:127;s:10:"disease_id";i:179;s:11:"overview_en";s:382:"Genital warts are sexually transmitted growths caused by certain types of human papillomavirus, or HPV. They may appear as small bumps or clusters around the genital or anal area and are often painless. HPV can be transmitted even when visible warts are absent. The HPV types that commonly cause genital warts are different from the types most strongly associated with some cancers.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:182:"जननांग मस्से एचपीवी संक्रमण के कारण होने वाले यौन संचारित मस्से हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:372:"Genital warts are caused by infection with certain types of human papillomavirus. HPV is usually transmitted through direct intimate or sexual skin-to-skin contact, including vaginal, anal, or oral sexual activity. A person can transmit HPV without having visible warts or knowing that they are infected. Infection may persist for some time before warts become noticeable.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:111:"ह्यूमन पैपिलोमा वायरस इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:399:"Risk is associated with sexual contact with a person who has HPV, including vaginal, anal, or oral sex. Having multiple sexual partners and not using barrier protection can increase exposure to HPV. A weakened immune system may make HPV infection more difficult to control. Genital warts can occur even when a person has had only one sexual partner and even when the partner has no visible symptoms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:101:"असुरक्षित यौन संबंध जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:430:"Genital warts are usually diagnosed by visual examination of the affected skin or mucosal areas. A healthcare professional may examine the size, shape, color, and distribution of the lesions. HPV testing is not generally required to diagnose typical visible genital warts. If a lesion has an unusual appearance, is pigmented, ulcerated, bleeding, or does not respond as expected, additional evaluation or biopsy may be considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:151:"निदान सामान्यतः चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:407:"HPV vaccination can help prevent infection with HPV types that cause genital warts and some cancers. Safer sexual practices, including condom or other barrier use, can reduce but do not completely eliminate HPV transmission because uncovered skin can also transmit the virus. Limiting the number of sexual partners and avoiding sexual contact when visible genital warts are present may also reduce exposure.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:153:"एचपीवी टीकाकरण और सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार जोखिम कम करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:364:"Genital warts are generally not an emergency but should be medically evaluated for diagnosis and appropriate management. Seek assessment for rapidly changing, bleeding, painful, ulcerated, or unusually appearing lesions, or when the diagnosis is uncertain. Severe pain, significant bleeding, or rapidly worsening genital swelling requires prompt medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:122;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:128;s:10:"disease_id";i:180;s:11:"overview_en";s:421:"Male breast cancer is a rare cancer that develops in breast tissue. Although breast cancer is much more common in women, men have breast tissue and can develop breast cancer. A persistent lump is a common presentation, and other possible signs include nipple discharge, nipple or skin changes, dimpling, puckering, redness, or scaling. Finding and evaluating a new breast change promptly can help establish the diagnosis.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:196:"पुरुष स्तन कैंसर पुरुषों के स्तन ऊतक में विकसित होने वाला दुर्लभ कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:423:"The exact cause of male breast cancer is not always known. Cancer develops when abnormal breast cells grow and divide uncontrollably. Factors that can alter risk include increased estrogen exposure, inherited genetic changes such as BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, certain genetic conditions, previous radiation exposure, and conditions that affect hormone balance. Most male breast cancers arise from cells lining the milk ducts.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन और हार्मोन असंतुलन इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:434:"Risk factors include increasing age, a family history of breast cancer, inherited BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, Klinefelter syndrome, previous chest radiation, and conditions that increase estrogen exposure. Cirrhosis, heavy alcohol use, obesity, and excess breast tissue may contribute to hormonal changes associated with risk. Men with concerning symptoms or substantial family history should discuss risk with a healthcare professional.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और हार्मोनल विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:423:"Evaluation usually begins with a clinical breast examination and assessment of the lump or other breast changes. Diagnostic imaging such as mammography or ultrasound may be used to examine the breast and nearby tissues. A biopsy is generally needed to determine whether abnormal tissue is cancerous. If cancer is confirmed, additional tests may assess hormone receptors, HER2 status, lymph nodes, and the extent of disease.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:108:"निदान में इमेजिंग और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:384:"There is no established way to completely prevent male breast cancer. Men can become familiar with their usual breast appearance and seek medical evaluation for a persistent lump, nipple discharge, skin changes, or other new symptoms. People with a strong family history or inherited cancer risk may benefit from genetic counseling and individualized surveillance or screening advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:90:"समय पर पहचान बेहतर परिणाम देती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:373:"Male breast cancer requires prompt medical evaluation for a new breast lump, nipple retraction, nipple discharge, skin changes, or persistent breast or nipple abnormality. Seek assessment for a new or enlarging lump or unexplained changes. Emergency care is generally not required unless there is severe pain, significant bleeding, infection, or another acute complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:123;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:130;s:10:"disease_id";i:182;s:11:"overview_en";s:339:"Endometriosis is a condition in which tissue similar to the lining of the uterus grows outside the uterus. It commonly affects the pelvic area and may cause painful periods, pelvic pain, pain during sexual activity, or difficulty becoming pregnant. Symptoms can vary widely, and some people may have endometriosis without obvious symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:184:"एंडोमेट्रियोसिस में गर्भाशय जैसी ऊतक वृद्धि गर्भाशय के बाहर होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:388:"The exact cause of endometriosis is not fully understood. Hormonal factors allow tissue similar to the uterine lining to grow and remain active outside the uterus. Genetic factors may also contribute, as the condition can occur more often in people with a family history. The development of endometriosis is likely influenced by a combination of biological, hormonal, and genetic factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:180:"सटीक कारण अज्ञात है, पर हार्मोनल और आनुवंशिक कारक भूमिका निभाते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:394:"Risk factors for endometriosis include having a family history of the condition and certain reproductive or menstrual characteristics that result in greater lifetime exposure to menstrual cycles. Symptoms may begin during the reproductive years. Having a close relative with endometriosis can increase susceptibility, although many people who develop the condition have no known family history.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और हार्मोन असंतुलन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:382:"Diagnosis of endometriosis is based on symptoms, medical history, and pelvic examination, together with imaging when appropriate. Ultrasound or MRI may identify some areas of endometriosis or related ovarian cysts, but normal imaging does not always exclude the condition. In selected cases, laparoscopy may be used to directly examine the pelvis and obtain tissue for confirmation.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1218:"एंडोमेट्रियोसिस का मूल्यांकन लक्षणों और चिकित्सकीय इतिहास से शुरू होता है, जिसके बाद पेल्विक परीक्षण और आवश्यकता होने पर इमेजिंग जाँच की जाती है। अल्ट्रासाउंड या अन्य इमेजिंग से अंडाशय की सिस्ट या अन्य बदलावों की पहचान में मदद मिल सकती है, लेकिन हर एंडोमेट्रियोसिस घाव दिखाई नहीं देता। लैप्रोस्कोपी वह सर्जिकल प्रक्रिया है जिससे एंडोमेट्रियोसिस को सीधे देखा जा सकता है। इसमें घावों का स्वरूप निदान में मदद करता है और ऊतक की जाँच के लिए बायोप्सी भी ली जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:398:"Endometriosis cannot always be prevented because its exact cause is not fully understood. Early evaluation of persistent pelvic pain, painful periods, or other concerning symptoms can help identify the condition and reduce delays in care. People with symptoms or a family history should discuss appropriate evaluation with a healthcare professional rather than relying on preventive measures alone.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"समय पर निदान लक्षण नियंत्रण में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:387:"Endometriosis is usually a chronic condition but can cause significant pelvic pain and other complications. Seek medical assessment for persistent or worsening pelvic pain, painful periods, abnormal bleeding, fertility concerns, or bowel or urinary symptoms. Urgent evaluation is needed for sudden severe pelvic or abdominal pain, fainting, heavy bleeding, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:124;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:131;s:10:"disease_id";i:183;s:11:"overview_en";s:418:"Uterine fibroids are noncancerous growths that develop in or around the uterus. They may occur as a single growth or as several fibroids and can vary greatly in size and location. Many cause no symptoms, but some can lead to heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding, pelvic pressure or pain, frequent urination, or discomfort during sexual activity. Fibroids may change in size over time and often shrink after menopause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:180:"गर्भाशय फाइब्रॉइड गर्भाशय में होने वाली गैर-कैंसरयुक्त गांठें हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:393:"The exact cause of uterine fibroids is not known. Their development appears to involve hormones such as estrogen and progesterone and genetic factors. Fibroids can grow in the muscle wall of the uterus, beneath the inner uterine lining, beneath the outer surface, or on a stalk. Their growth and symptoms can vary among individuals and may change during reproductive years and after menopause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"हार्मोनल प्रभाव और आनुवंशिक कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:372:"Risk is associated with factors such as reproductive age, family history of fibroids, and certain hormonal influences. Fibroids are more common during the childbearing years and are more frequently diagnosed in some racial and ethnic groups. Obesity may also be associated with increased risk. Having relatives with fibroids can increase the likelihood of developing them.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:134:"उम्र, मोटापा और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:378:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and pelvic examination. Ultrasound is commonly used to identify fibroids and assess their size and location. Depending on the symptoms and findings, MRI, hysterosonography, or hysteroscopy may provide additional information. An endometrial biopsy may be considered when abnormal uterine bleeding requires evaluation of the uterine lining.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:142:"निदान में पेल्विक परीक्षण और अल्ट्रासाउंड शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:410:"There is no proven way to completely prevent uterine fibroids because their exact cause is uncertain. Maintaining a healthy weight, being physically active, and having regular medical care may support overall reproductive health. People with heavy menstrual bleeding, persistent pelvic pressure, pelvic pain, or urinary symptoms should seek medical evaluation so that fibroids and other causes can be assessed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:85:"नियमित स्त्रीरोग जांच सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:338:"Uterine fibroids are usually benign and are not generally emergencies. Seek medical assessment for heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding, pelvic pressure or pain, anemia symptoms, urinary or bowel problems, or worsening symptoms. Urgent care is needed for very heavy bleeding, severe sudden pelvic pain, fainting, or significant weakness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:125;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:132;s:10:"disease_id";i:184;s:11:"overview_en";s:502:"An ovarian cyst is a fluid-filled sac or other tissue-filled structure that develops in or on an ovary. Many ovarian cysts are functional, occur as part of the normal menstrual cycle, and disappear without treatment. Others may develop because of conditions such as endometriosis or abnormal cell growth. Small cysts may cause no symptoms, while larger or complicated cysts can cause pelvic pain, pressure, bloating, or menstrual changes. Rarely, a cyst can rupture, bleed, or cause the ovary to twist.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:147:"ओवेरियन सिस्ट अंडाशय में बनने वाली तरल भरी थैलियां हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:482:"Ovarian cysts have several possible causes. Functional cysts develop as part of the normal menstrual cycle when a follicle does not release an egg normally or does not shrink as expected afterward. Other cysts may occur with endometriosis, pregnancy, hormonal stimulation, or abnormal growth of ovarian cells. Most are benign, but some tumors can form cystic structures. The cause cannot always be determined from symptoms alone, and ultrasound is often used to characterize a cyst.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:110:"हार्मोनल परिवर्तन इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:485:"Risk factors for ovarian cysts include being of reproductive age, having irregular menstrual cycles, certain hormonal treatments, pregnancy, endometriosis, and previous ovarian cysts. Some fertility treatments can increase the likelihood of developing ovarian cysts. The risk and significance depend on the type of cyst. After menopause, ovarian cysts are less common but may require more careful evaluation because the likelihood of a concerning underlying condition changes with age.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:124:"हार्मोनल विकार और प्रजनन आयु जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:498:"Ovarian cysts are commonly evaluated with a pelvic examination and ultrasound. Transvaginal ultrasound can show the size, location, and appearance of a cyst and help distinguish simple fluid-filled cysts from more complex structures. Pregnancy testing may be appropriate in people who could be pregnant. Blood tests or additional imaging may be recommended depending on age, symptoms, and ultrasound findings. In some cases, follow-up imaging is used to determine whether a cyst resolves over time.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:135:"निदान सामान्यतः अल्ट्रासाउंड द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:493:"Most ovarian cysts cannot be prevented because many develop as part of normal ovarian function. Regular medical care can help identify persistent or recurrent cysts and conditions such as endometriosis that may contribute to cyst formation. People receiving fertility medicines should follow monitoring recommendations. New or severe pelvic pain should be evaluated promptly, especially when accompanied by vomiting, fainting, or sudden symptoms that could indicate rupture or ovarian torsion.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"नियमित स्त्रीरोग जांच की सलाह दी जाती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:341:"Many ovarian cysts are benign and resolve without complications, but some can rupture or cause ovarian torsion. Seek prompt assessment for persistent pelvic pain, increasing abdominal swelling, or unusual bleeding. Emergency care is needed for sudden severe pelvic or abdominal pain, especially with nausea, vomiting, dizziness, or fainting.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:126;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:133;s:10:"disease_id";i:185;s:11:"overview_en";s:429:"Pelvic inflammatory disease is an infection and inflammation of the female reproductive organs, including the uterus, fallopian tubes, and ovaries. It can cause lower abdominal or pelvic pain, abnormal vaginal discharge, fever, pain during sex, or painful urination, although some people have few or no symptoms. Untreated PID can cause scarring that may lead to infertility, ectopic pregnancy, chronic pelvic pain, or abscesses.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:161:"पेल्विक इंफ्लेमेटरी डिजीज महिला प्रजनन अंगों का संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:393:"Pelvic inflammatory disease is usually caused by bacteria that move upward from the vagina or cervix into the upper reproductive tract. Sexually transmitted infections, especially chlamydia and gonorrhea, are common causes. Other bacteria normally present in the genital tract can also contribute. Untreated infections can spread and cause inflammation and scarring of the reproductive organs.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:111:"यौन संचारित संक्रमण इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:416:"Risk is higher in sexually active people, particularly those younger than 25, those with multiple sex partners, and people with a current or previous sexually transmitted infection. Having a previous episode of PID also increases risk. Douching may increase risk by disturbing normal vaginal bacteria and pushing bacteria upward. Failure to diagnose and treat an STI promptly can also increase the likelihood of PID.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:140:"अनेक यौन साथी और अनुपचारित संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:428:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history, pelvic examination, and laboratory testing. A healthcare professional may look for pelvic or cervical tenderness and abnormal discharge. Tests for sexually transmitted infections, pregnancy testing, urine testing, and other laboratory studies may be used. Ultrasound or other imaging may be considered when an abscess, ectopic pregnancy, or another pelvic condition is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:149:"निदान में पेल्विक परीक्षण और प्रयोगशाला जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:436:"Reducing exposure to sexually transmitted infections can lower the risk of pelvic inflammatory disease. Using condoms or other barrier protection, limiting the number of sexual partners, and getting recommended STI testing are important preventive measures. Chlamydia and gonorrhea should be treated promptly, and sexual partners may also need evaluation and treatment. Avoiding douching may help protect the normal vaginal environment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:105:"सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार जोखिम कम करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:504:"Pelvic inflammatory disease requires prompt medical assessment and treatment because untreated infection can cause abscesses, infertility, and other complications. Seek care for pelvic or lower abdominal pain, fever, abnormal vaginal discharge, pain during sex, painful urination, or worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for severe pelvic or abdominal pain, fainting, persistent vomiting, high fever with severe illness, pregnancy with significant symptoms, or signs of a serious infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:127;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:134;s:10:"disease_id";i:186;s:11:"overview_en";s:603:"Cervical cancer is a malignant growth that develops in the cells of the cervix, the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina. Many cervical cancers develop gradually from precancerous cellular changes caused by persistent infection with certain high-risk types of human papillomavirus (HPV). Early cervical cancer may cause no noticeable symptoms. As the disease progresses, symptoms can include abnormal vaginal bleeding, bleeding after sexual intercourse, unusual vaginal discharge, or pelvic pain. Regular cervical screening can identify precancerous changes before they become cancerous.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:211:"सर्वाइकल कैंसर गर्भाशय ग्रीवा में विकसित होता है और एचपीवी संक्रमण से जुड़ा है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:637:"Most cervical cancers are associated with persistent infection by high-risk types of human papillomavirus (HPV), a very common sexually transmitted infection. In many people, the immune system clears HPV without causing lasting problems. When high-risk HPV infection persists, however, it can produce abnormal changes in cervical cells that may gradually progress from precancerous lesions to invasive cancer. Other factors can influence this process, including smoking, impaired immune function, and certain reproductive or sexual health factors. Cervical cancer generally develops over a period of years rather than appearing suddenly.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:925:"लगभग सभी सर्वाइकल कैंसर उच्च जोखिम वाले ह्यूमन पैपिलोमावायरस (HPV) के लंबे समय तक बने रहने वाले संक्रमण से जुड़े होते हैं। HPV सामान्य है और अक्सर शरीर से स्वयं साफ हो जाता है, लेकिन लगातार संक्रमण गर्भाशय ग्रीवा की कोशिकाओं में असामान्य बदलाव पैदा कर सकता है जो समय के साथ कैंसर में बदल सकते हैं। धूम्रपान और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा तंत्र जोखिम को और बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:552:"Risk factors for cervical cancer include persistent infection with high-risk HPV, lack of regular cervical screening, smoking, weakened immune function, and certain reproductive or sexual health factors associated with greater exposure to HPV. A history of other sexually transmitted infections may also be associated with increased risk. People with impaired immunity may have greater difficulty clearing persistent HPV infection. Risk is also influenced by access to preventive vaccination, screening, and follow-up of abnormal cervical test results.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:120:"धूम्रपान और एचपीवी संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:602:"Cervical cancer is evaluated through cervical screening and follow-up of abnormal results. Screening may involve HPV testing, cervical cytology, or both, depending on age and local recommendations. If an abnormality is detected, colposcopy allows closer examination of the cervix and biopsy can determine whether precancerous or cancerous cells are present. If cancer is confirmed, additional examinations and imaging may be used to determine the tumor size, local involvement, lymph-node status, or spread to other parts of the body. The findings help establish the stage and guide treatment planning.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:942:"सर्वाइकल कैंसर के मूल्यांकन में चिकित्सा इतिहास, पेल्विक जांच और आवश्यकता के अनुसार गर्भाशय ग्रीवा की स्क्रीनिंग शामिल हो सकती है। यदि स्क्रीनिंग या जांच में असामान्य क्षेत्र मिलता है, तो कोल्पोस्कोपी और बायोप्सी जैसी जांचों से यह निर्धारित किया जा सकता है कि कैंसर मौजूद है या नहीं। निदान के बाद इमेजिंग जांच बीमारी के फैलाव का आकलन करने में मदद कर सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:611:"Cervical cancer prevention focuses on HPV vaccination, appropriate cervical screening, and timely follow-up of abnormal results. HPV vaccination reduces the risk of infection with several high-risk HPV types associated with cervical and other cancers. Avoiding tobacco use may also reduce risk. Screening can identify precancerous changes before invasive cancer develops, allowing them to be monitored or treated. Safer sexual practices can reduce exposure to HPV, although they cannot completely prevent transmission. Following recommended screening and vaccination guidance is an important part of prevention.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:131:"एचपीवी टीकाकरण और नियमित जांच बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:358:"Cervical cancer requires prompt medical evaluation and appropriate treatment. Seek assessment for abnormal vaginal bleeding, bleeding after sex, unusual vaginal discharge, pelvic pain, or symptoms that persist or worsen. Emergency care is needed for heavy uncontrolled bleeding, fainting, severe pelvic or abdominal pain, or sudden significant deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:128;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:135;s:10:"disease_id";i:187;s:11:"overview_en";s:491:"Ovarian cancer is a group of cancers that begin in or around the ovaries. It may not cause noticeable symptoms in its early stages, and symptoms can resemble common digestive or urinary problems. Possible symptoms include persistent abdominal or pelvic discomfort, bloating, feeling full quickly, changes in bowel or bladder habits, fatigue, and unexplained weight changes. Several types of ovarian cancer exist, and treatment depends on the cancer type, stage, and individual circumstances.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:150:"ओवेरियन कैंसर अंडाशय में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:538:"The exact cause of most ovarian cancers is not known. Cancer develops when cells acquire genetic changes that cause abnormal growth and survival. Risk is influenced by factors such as increasing age, inherited genetic changes including BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, family history, and certain reproductive or hormonal factors. Some ovarian cancers arise from cells in the fallopian tube or nearby tissues rather than directly from the ovarian surface. Different ovarian cancer types have different biological characteristics and risk factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:174:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन और पारिवारिक इतिहास इसके कारणों में शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:506:"Risk factors for ovarian cancer include increasing age, certain inherited genetic variants such as BRCA1 and BRCA2, a strong family history of ovarian, breast, or related cancers, and some reproductive or hormonal factors. Risk can also be influenced by personal medical history. Having a risk factor does not mean cancer will develop, and many people diagnosed with ovarian cancer have no strong identifiable risk factor. Genetic counseling may be appropriate for people with significant family histories.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:165:"उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास और आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:545:"Diagnosis of ovarian cancer generally involves a pelvic examination, review of symptoms and medical history, imaging, and laboratory evaluation. Ultrasound may help characterize an ovarian or pelvic mass, while CT or MRI may provide additional information about disease extent. Blood tests such as CA-125 can sometimes support evaluation but cannot by themselves diagnose ovarian cancer because levels may be abnormal for other reasons. Definitive diagnosis usually requires examination of tissue by a pathologist, often after surgery or biopsy.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:153:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड, सीटी स्कैन और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:602:"There is no certain way to prevent all ovarian cancers. People with a strong family history or known inherited cancer-related genetic variants should discuss individualized risk assessment and genetic counseling with a qualified healthcare professional. Some reproductive and hormonal factors are associated with risk, but preventive decisions depend on individual circumstances. Awareness of persistent abdominal or pelvic symptoms can support earlier medical evaluation. Routine screening is not recommended for average-risk people as a general method of preventing or detecting ovarian cancer early.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:120:"नियमित जांच समय पर पहचान में सहायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:412:"Ovarian cancer requires prompt medical evaluation when persistent or unexplained symptoms occur. Seek assessment for ongoing abdominal or pelvic pain, swelling or pressure, persistent bloating, difficulty eating or feeling full, urinary changes, unexplained weight loss, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for sudden severe abdominal or pelvic pain, fainting, heavy bleeding, or rapid deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:129;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:136;s:10:"disease_id";i:188;s:11:"overview_en";s:390:"Endometrial cancer is a cancer that begins in the lining of the uterus, called the endometrium. It is one of the most common cancers of the female reproductive system. Abnormal cells can grow uncontrollably and may invade nearby tissues or spread to other parts of the body. Abnormal vaginal bleeding, particularly bleeding after menopause, is an important symptom that should be evaluated.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:165:"एंडोमेट्रियल कैंसर गर्भाशय की अंदरूनी परत में विकसित होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:401:"Endometrial cancer develops when cells in the endometrium acquire changes that cause them to grow and divide abnormally. The exact cause is not always known. Hormonal factors, particularly prolonged exposure to estrogen without enough progesterone, can stimulate excessive growth of the uterine lining. Genetic changes and inherited conditions such as Lynch syndrome can also contribute to some cases.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:179:"हार्मोन असंतुलन और लंबे समय तक एस्ट्रोजन का प्रभाव प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:434:"Risk factors include increasing age, obesity, prolonged estrogen exposure, early menstruation, late menopause, never having been pregnant, certain hormone therapies, diabetes, and a family history of endometrial or colorectal cancer. Lynch syndrome and some other inherited genetic conditions can substantially increase risk. Risk varies among individuals and may depend on the combination of hormonal, metabolic, and genetic factors.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:134:"मोटापा, मधुमेह और हार्मोनल विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:465:"Diagnosis usually begins with evaluation of abnormal vaginal bleeding or other symptoms and a pelvic examination. Transvaginal ultrasound may be used to assess the thickness and appearance of the endometrium. A definitive diagnosis generally requires sampling the uterine lining, usually with an endometrial biopsy. Hysteroscopy or dilation and curettage may be used when additional tissue evaluation is needed. Imaging can help determine whether cancer has spread.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:146:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड, बायोप्सी और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:469:"Endometrial cancer cannot always be prevented, but maintaining a healthy weight, staying physically active, and managing conditions such as diabetes may reduce risk. Hormone therapy should be used according to medical advice, with appropriate consideration of whether estrogen is given with progesterone. People with Lynch syndrome or a strong family history should discuss appropriate risk assessment and screening or preventive options with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:145:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली और नियमित स्त्रीरोग जांच लाभकारी हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:378:"Endometrial cancer requires prompt medical evaluation, particularly for abnormal vaginal bleeding. Seek assessment for bleeding between periods, unusually heavy or prolonged bleeding, bleeding after menopause, or persistent pelvic pain or cramping. Emergency care is needed for heavy uncontrolled bleeding, fainting, severe weakness, severe pelvic pain, or sudden deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:130;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:137;s:10:"disease_id";i:189;s:11:"overview_en";s:365:"Vaginitis is inflammation or irritation of the vagina that may cause discharge, itching, burning, odor, soreness, or discomfort. It can result from bacterial vaginosis, yeast overgrowth, sexually transmitted infections, hormonal changes, irritants, or changes in the normal vaginal environment. The appropriate treatment depends on identifying the underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:102:"वैजिनाइटिस योनि की सूजन या संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:401:"Vaginitis can have several causes, including bacterial vaginosis, overgrowth of yeast, sexually transmitted infections, hormonal changes, irritants, and disruption of the normal vaginal environment. Antibiotic use can alter normal vaginal flora and contribute to some infections. The specific cause cannot always be determined from symptoms alone, so examination and appropriate testing may be needed.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:153:"बैक्टीरियल, फंगल या परजीवी संक्रमण इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:351:"Risk of vaginitis may increase with antibiotic use, hormonal changes, sexual activity, sexually transmitted infections, diabetes, and disruption of the normal vaginal flora. Exposure to scented products, douches, or other vaginal irritants may also contribute to irritation. The specific risk depends on the type of vaginitis and the underlying cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:190:"खराब स्वच्छता, एंटीबायोटिक उपयोग और हार्मोन परिवर्तन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:443:"Diagnosis of vaginitis begins with assessment of symptoms and medical history followed by examination when appropriate. A pelvic examination may identify inflammation or other abnormalities. Samples of vaginal discharge can be examined using microscopy or laboratory tests to identify bacterial, fungal, or sexually transmitted infections. Testing helps distinguish between causes because similar symptoms can result from different conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:127:"निदान में परीक्षण और प्रयोगशाला जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:441:"Prevention of vaginitis depends on its cause. Avoid unnecessary vaginal irritants such as scented products and douches, and use antibiotics only when medically appropriate. Safer sexual practices can reduce the risk of sexually transmitted infections. Maintaining appropriate hygiene without disrupting the normal vaginal environment may also help. Persistent, recurrent, or unusual symptoms should be evaluated by a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:138:"उचित स्वच्छता रखें और संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार कराएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:337:"Vaginitis is usually not an emergency but should be evaluated when symptoms persist or recur. Seek medical assessment for unusual discharge, itching, burning, pain, abnormal bleeding, fever, pelvic pain, or symptoms that worsen. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe pelvic pain, high fever, fainting, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:131;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:138;s:10:"disease_id";i:190;s:11:"overview_en";s:396:"Vulvodynia is a chronic pain disorder affecting the vulva, the external female genital area. It may cause burning, stinging, aching, itching, or sharp pain that lasts for months or longer. Pain may be localized to one area or affect a larger part of the vulva. Symptoms may be triggered or worsened by sexual activity, tampon insertion, sitting, exercise, tight clothing, or pressure on the area.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:193:"वल्वोडाइनिया वल्वा क्षेत्र में दीर्घकालिक दर्द या असुविधा की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:391:"The exact cause of vulvodynia is unknown. Possible contributing factors include irritation or injury of vulvar nerves, hormonal changes, abnormal responses to inflammation or infection, pelvic floor muscle problems, genetic susceptibility, or increased sensitivity of nerve fibers. Vulvodynia is not considered a sexually transmitted infection, and an STI does not itself cause the disorder.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:96:"इसका सटीक कारण अक्सर अज्ञात होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:404:"The factors that determine who develops vulvodynia are not fully understood. Possible contributors include previous vulvar irritation or injury, hormonal changes, pelvic floor muscle dysfunction, and increased sensitivity to inflammation or physical pressure. Symptoms may be aggravated by sexual activity, prolonged sitting, tight clothing, cycling, or other activities that place pressure on the vulva.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:176:"तंत्रिका क्षति, हार्मोन परिवर्तन और लगातार जलन योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:438:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern and duration of vulvar pain and requires evaluation for other possible causes. A healthcare professional may take a detailed medical history and perform a pelvic and vulvar examination. A cotton-swab test may be used to identify areas of tenderness. Urine tests, vaginal tests, or other investigations may be performed to exclude urinary infections, yeast infections, skin disorders, or other conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:145:"निदान लक्षणों और अन्य कारणों को बाहर करके किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:422:"Because the exact cause of vulvodynia is unknown, there is no reliable method to prevent it. Avoiding known irritants may help reduce symptoms in people who are sensitive to them. Wearing loose clothing, using gentle unscented products, avoiding unnecessary irritation, and addressing pelvic floor problems when present may be helpful. Persistent or unexplained vulvar pain should be assessed by a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:137:"समय पर चिकित्सकीय सलाह लक्षण नियंत्रण में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:340:"Vulvodynia is generally a chronic condition and is not usually an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent vulvar pain, burning, irritation, or pain that interferes with daily activities or sexual function. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for new sores, significant bleeding, marked swelling, fever, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:132;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:139;s:10:"disease_id";i:191;s:11:"overview_en";s:431:"Amenorrhea means the absence of menstrual periods. It may be primary, when menstruation has not started by the expected age, or secondary, when previously occurring periods stop for several months. Pregnancy is a common cause of secondary amenorrhea, while other causes include hormonal disorders, significant changes in weight or exercise, stress, medications, and conditions affecting the reproductive organs or endocrine system.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:86:"अमेनोरिया मासिक धर्म का अभाव है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:390:"Amenorrhea can result from pregnancy, hormonal changes, disorders of the hypothalamus or pituitary gland, ovarian dysfunction, thyroid disease, and other endocrine conditions. Significant weight loss, very low body fat, excessive exercise, severe stress, and some medications can suppress menstrual function. Structural abnormalities of the reproductive tract can also cause absent periods.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:164:"हार्मोन असंतुलन, गर्भावस्था और अन्य रोग इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:340:"Risk factors include pregnancy, significant weight loss or gain, excessive physical exercise, severe psychological stress, eating disorders, hormonal disorders, certain medications, and conditions affecting the ovaries, pituitary gland, thyroid, or reproductive tract. The likelihood and causes vary according to age and reproductive stage.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:153:"तनाव, अत्यधिक व्यायाम और हार्मोनल विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:399:"Evaluation includes a menstrual and reproductive history, physical examination, and pregnancy testing when appropriate. Blood tests may assess thyroid function, prolactin, ovarian hormones, or other endocrine causes. Pelvic ultrasound can evaluate the uterus and ovaries, while additional imaging or specialized testing may be required when a pituitary, ovarian, or structural disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:152:"निदान में हार्मोन जांच और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:427:"Amenorrhea caused by pregnancy is normal, but other forms may signal an underlying condition. Maintaining adequate nutrition, avoiding excessive exercise, managing significant stress, and seeking medical evaluation for persistent absence of periods can help identify and address potentially preventable contributors. People taking medicines that affect menstrual function should discuss concerns with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:158:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाएं और हार्मोनल समस्याओं का उपचार करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:345:"Amenorrhea should be medically assessed when periods stop unexpectedly or remain absent. Pregnancy should be considered when relevant, and other hormonal, reproductive, nutritional, or medical causes may need evaluation. Seek prompt care for severe pelvic pain, abnormal bleeding, fainting, severe weakness, or other rapidly developing symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:133;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:140;s:10:"disease_id";i:192;s:11:"overview_en";s:431:"Dysmenorrhea is painful menstruation, commonly causing cramping in the lower abdomen around the beginning of a menstrual period. Pain may also involve the lower back or thighs and may be accompanied by nausea, diarrhea, headache, dizziness, or fatigue. Primary dysmenorrhea occurs without another pelvic disease, while secondary dysmenorrhea results from an underlying condition and may develop later or become progressively worse.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:123:"डिसमेनोरिया दर्दयुक्त मासिक धर्म को कहते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:395:"Primary dysmenorrhea is commonly related to increased production and activity of prostaglandins in the uterus during menstruation. These substances cause uterine contractions that help shed the uterine lining but can also produce pain. Secondary dysmenorrhea can result from conditions such as endometriosis, uterine fibroids, adenomyosis, pelvic inflammatory disease, or other pelvic disorders.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:130:"गर्भाशय संकुचन और हार्मोनल कारक प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:379:"Risk factors for dysmenorrhea include younger age at menstruation, younger age at first menstrual periods, a family history of painful periods, heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding, and smoking. Secondary dysmenorrhea is more likely when an underlying gynecological condition is present. Symptoms may also be influenced by the timing and progression of the underlying condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"एंडोमेट्रियोसिस और पेल्विक विकार जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:448:"Diagnosis is based on a detailed menstrual history and the pattern, timing, severity, and duration of pain. A pelvic examination may be performed when secondary causes are suspected. Ultrasound or other investigations may be recommended when pain is severe, begins later than expected, persists despite usual treatment, becomes progressively worse, or is accompanied by abnormal bleeding or other symptoms suggesting an underlying pelvic condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:133:"निदान लक्षणों और चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:455:"Some cases of dysmenorrhea cannot be prevented because primary menstrual pain is related to normal biological processes and individual sensitivity. Regular physical activity, adequate sleep, balanced nutrition, stress management, and avoiding smoking may support overall health. Persistent, severe, or progressively worsening menstrual pain should be evaluated because identifying and treating an underlying pelvic condition can reduce recurrent symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:138:"नियमित व्यायाम और स्वस्थ आदतें लक्षण कम कर सकती हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:362:"Dysmenorrhea is usually not an emergency, but severe or worsening menstrual pain should be medically evaluated, particularly when it interferes with normal activities or develops later in life. Seek prompt assessment for sudden severe pelvic pain, unusually heavy bleeding, fever, fainting, or symptoms that are substantially different from usual menstrual pain.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:134;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:141;s:10:"disease_id";i:193;s:11:"overview_en";s:378:"Menorrhagia refers to unusually heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding that interferes with daily activities or may lead to anemia. Causes can include hormonal disturbances, uterine fibroids or polyps, adenomyosis, bleeding disorders, certain medicines, and other reproductive or medical conditions. Persistent heavy bleeding should be evaluated to identify the underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:169:"मेनोरेजिया अत्यधिक या लंबे समय तक मासिक रक्तस्राव की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:405:"Heavy menstrual bleeding may result from hormonal imbalances that prevent normal regulation of the menstrual cycle. Structural problems such as fibroids, polyps, or adenomyosis can cause excessive bleeding. Other causes include bleeding disorders, thyroid or other endocrine problems, certain medicines, complications of pregnancy, and, less commonly, cancers or other diseases of the reproductive system.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:165:"हार्मोन असंतुलन, फाइब्रॉइड और गर्भाशय विकार सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:315:"Risk factors depend on the underlying cause and may include uterine fibroids, adenomyosis, hormonal disorders, bleeding disorders, use of certain medicines, reproductive age, and some medical conditions. A family history of bleeding disorders or previous episodes of heavy menstrual bleeding may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:161:"हार्मोनल विकार और गर्भाशय की असामान्यताएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:409:"Evaluation begins with a detailed menstrual and medical history and a physical examination. Pregnancy testing is commonly performed when appropriate. Blood tests may assess anemia, thyroid function, or bleeding disorders, while pelvic ultrasound can identify fibroids, polyps, adenomyosis, or other structural abnormalities. Additional procedures may be needed depending on age, symptoms, and suspected cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:128:"निदान में रक्त जांच और पेल्विक इमेजिंग शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:373:"Not all causes of heavy menstrual bleeding can be prevented. Managing known hormonal or uterine conditions, taking medicines as directed, and seeking evaluation for persistent or unusually heavy bleeding can help reduce complications. Maintaining adequate iron intake and addressing iron deficiency when present may help prevent anemia associated with heavy menstrual loss.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:154:"नियमित स्त्रीरोग जांच कारणों की समय पर पहचान में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:433:"Menorrhagia, or very heavy menstrual bleeding, requires medical assessment because prolonged heavy bleeding can cause anemia and may have an underlying cause. Seek prompt care for bleeding that is unusually heavy or prolonged, significant weakness, dizziness, shortness of breath, or symptoms that are worsening. Emergency care is needed for uncontrolled heavy bleeding, fainting, severe weakness, or signs of significant blood loss.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:135;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:142;s:10:"disease_id";i:194;s:11:"overview_en";s:464:"Premenstrual syndrome (PMS) is a group of physical, emotional, and behavioral symptoms that occur during the days or weeks before menstruation and usually improve after menstrual bleeding begins. Symptoms can vary considerably between individuals and may include breast tenderness, bloating, headaches, fatigue, mood changes, irritability, food cravings, sleep changes, and difficulty concentrating. Symptoms may range from mild to severe and can change over time.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:245:"प्रीमेंस्ट्रुअल सिंड्रोम मासिक धर्म से पहले होने वाले शारीरिक और मानसिक लक्षणों का समूह है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:473:"The exact cause of premenstrual syndrome is not fully understood. Symptoms are believed to be related to sensitivity to normal hormonal changes that occur during the menstrual cycle rather than simply to abnormal hormone levels. Changes in estrogen and progesterone may influence brain chemicals and contribute to mood, physical, and behavioral symptoms. Stress, sleep problems, and other lifestyle factors may affect symptom severity but are not considered the sole cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:123:"हार्मोनल उतार-चढ़ाव प्रमुख भूमिका निभाते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:405:"Risk factors and factors associated with greater symptom burden include a personal or family history of PMS, sensitivity to normal hormonal changes, and certain mood disorders. Symptoms may also be influenced by stress, poor sleep, limited physical activity, and other lifestyle factors. PMS can occur during the reproductive years and its severity may change during different stages of reproductive life.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1203:"प्रीमेंस्ट्रुअल सिंड्रोम से जुड़े कारकों में मासिक चक्र के दौरान होने वाले सामान्य हार्मोनल बदलावों के प्रति संवेदनशीलता शामिल है। जिन लोगों को स्वयं या परिवार में PMS या कुछ मूड संबंधी विकारों का इतिहास है, उनमें लक्षण अधिक होने की संभावना हो सकती है। तनाव और जीवनशैली से जुड़े अन्य कारक लक्षणों की तीव्रता को प्रभावित कर सकते हैं, हालांकि इन्हें अकेला कारण नहीं माना जाता। लक्षण समय के साथ बदल सकते हैं और प्रजनन जीवन के कुछ चरणों में अधिक स्पष्ट हो सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:495:"Diagnosis of premenstrual syndrome is usually based on the recurring pattern of physical and emotional symptoms in the days before menstruation and improvement after menstruation begins. A symptom diary kept for several menstrual cycles can help establish the timing and severity of symptoms. There is no single laboratory test that confirms PMS. A healthcare professional may evaluate other conditions when symptoms are unusual, severe, persistent, or not clearly linked to the menstrual cycle.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:99:"निदान लक्षणों के पैटर्न पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:480:"PMS cannot always be prevented because it is related to normal menstrual-cycle changes and individual sensitivity to those changes. Regular physical activity, adequate sleep, balanced nutrition, limiting factors that worsen symptoms, and effective stress management may help reduce symptom burden. Keeping a menstrual and symptom record can help identify recurring triggers and support early discussion with a healthcare professional when symptoms interfere with daily activities.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:123:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली और तनाव नियंत्रण लाभकारी हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:361:"Premenstrual syndrome is generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when symptoms are severe, persistent, or substantially interfere with daily activities or quality of life, particularly when symptoms change significantly from usual patterns. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe physical symptoms, fainting, or other sudden concerning changes.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:136;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:143;s:10:"disease_id";i:195;s:11:"overview_en";s:513:"Premenstrual dysphoric disorder (PMDD) is a severe cyclical condition in which emotional, behavioral, and physical symptoms occur during the premenstrual phase and substantially interfere with daily functioning, relationships, work, or other activities. Symptoms typically improve after menstruation begins. PMDD is more severe than typical premenstrual symptoms and commonly includes marked mood changes, irritability, depression, anxiety, difficulty concentrating, fatigue, sleep changes, and physical symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:160:"प्रीमेंस्ट्रुअल डिस्फोरिक डिसऑर्डर पीएमएस का गंभीर रूप है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:428:"The exact cause of PMDD is not fully established. Symptoms appear to result from an increased sensitivity to normal hormonal fluctuations during the menstrual cycle rather than necessarily abnormal concentrations of reproductive hormones. Changes in ovarian hormones may influence neurotransmitter systems involved in mood and behavior. Genetic, biological, and psychological factors may contribute to individual susceptibility.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:229:"मस्तिष्क रसायन पर प्रभाव डालने वाले हार्मोनल परिवर्तन इसके लिए जिम्मेदार हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:402:"Risk may be increased by a personal or family history of mood disorders, previous significant premenstrual symptoms, and individual sensitivity to normal reproductive hormone changes. Some people may also have coexisting anxiety or depressive disorders. PMDD occurs in people who are biologically sensitive to cyclical hormonal changes, and symptoms may vary over different stages of reproductive life.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:109:"मूड विकारों का इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ा सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:429:"Diagnosis is based on the timing, number, severity, and cyclical recurrence of symptoms across menstrual cycles and the degree to which they interfere with daily functioning. Prospective symptom tracking over multiple cycles is often used to document the pattern. Evaluation also considers other psychiatric, medical, and gynecological conditions that can cause similar symptoms. There is no single blood test that confirms PMDD.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:168:"निदान लक्षणों के रिकॉर्ड और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:459:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent PMDD because it is associated with individual sensitivity to normal hormonal fluctuations. Regular sleep, physical activity, balanced nutrition, and effective stress management may help reduce the impact of symptoms. Tracking menstrual cycles and symptoms can help identify patterns and support early assessment when emotional or physical symptoms repeatedly interfere with work, relationships, or other daily activities.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:135:"समय पर पहचान और उपचार जीवन की गुणवत्ता सुधारते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:397:"Premenstrual dysphoric disorder requires medical evaluation when symptoms are severe or significantly interfere with daily functioning. Seek prompt assessment when mood or physical symptoms become substantially worse or difficult to manage. Any immediate risk of self-harm or inability to remain safe requires emergency help and immediate contact with local emergency services or a crisis service.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:137;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:144;s:10:"disease_id";i:196;s:11:"overview_en";s:606:"An ectopic pregnancy occurs when a fertilized egg implants outside the main cavity of the uterus, most often in a fallopian tube. Because these tissues cannot support a normally developing pregnancy, an ectopic pregnancy can cause serious internal bleeding if the pregnancy continues to grow and the affected structure ruptures. Symptoms may include a missed menstrual period, pelvic or abdominal pain, vaginal bleeding, dizziness, or shoulder pain. Some ectopic pregnancies are detected before severe symptoms develop, making early evaluation important when pregnancy occurs with unusual pain or bleeding.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:187:"एक्टोपिक प्रेग्नेंसी में निषेचित अंडा गर्भाशय के बाहर विकसित होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:513:"An ectopic pregnancy usually develops when the fertilized egg cannot travel normally through the fallopian tube and implants outside the uterine cavity. Previous damage or inflammation of the fallopian tubes can interfere with normal movement of the fertilized egg. Causes and contributing factors may include previous pelvic infections, previous ectopic pregnancy, certain fertility treatments, tubal surgery, or structural abnormalities of the reproductive tract. In some cases, no specific cause is identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:153:"फैलोपियन ट्यूब की क्षति और पूर्व संक्रमण प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:553:"Risk factors for ectopic pregnancy include a previous ectopic pregnancy, previous pelvic inflammatory disease, damage or surgery involving the fallopian tubes, certain fertility treatments, and some conditions affecting the reproductive tract. Pregnancy occurring with an intrauterine device in place is uncommon, but if pregnancy does occur, the relative likelihood of it being ectopic is higher. Smoking and increasing maternal age have also been associated with increased risk. An ectopic pregnancy can still occur without any recognized risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:198:"पेल्विक इंफ्लेमेटरी डिजीज और पूर्व एक्टोपिक गर्भावस्था जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:571:"Diagnosis of ectopic pregnancy usually involves a pregnancy test together with clinical assessment, blood testing for the pregnancy hormone hCG, and transvaginal ultrasound. The pattern of hCG levels over time can provide useful information but does not by itself establish the location of a pregnancy. Ultrasound may identify a pregnancy inside the uterus or findings suggesting an ectopic pregnancy. When the diagnosis remains uncertain, repeat testing and imaging may be required. Severe pain, fainting, or signs of internal bleeding require urgent medical assessment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:124:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड और रक्त जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:628:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent every ectopic pregnancy, but reducing the risk of pelvic infections, avoiding tobacco, and seeking appropriate care for sexually transmitted infections can help reduce some contributing factors. People with a previous ectopic pregnancy or conditions affecting the fallopian tubes may benefit from early medical evaluation when pregnancy occurs. Early confirmation of pregnancy location is particularly important when risk factors are present or when pain or bleeding develops. Any pregnancy accompanied by severe abdominal pain, fainting, or significant bleeding requires urgent assessment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:108:"समय पर चिकित्सा सहायता अत्यंत आवश्यक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:352:"Ectopic pregnancy is a medical emergency when rupture or significant internal bleeding occurs. Seek immediate medical care for abdominal or pelvic pain, vaginal bleeding, shoulder pain, dizziness, or fainting when pregnancy is possible. Sudden severe abdominal pain, fainting, marked weakness, or signs of internal bleeding require emergency treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:138;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:145;s:10:"disease_id";i:197;s:11:"overview_en";s:411:"Miscarriage is the unexpected loss of a pregnancy before the 20th week. It is common, especially early in pregnancy, and most miscarriages occur because the fetus does not develop normally. Symptoms may include vaginal bleeding, abdominal or lower-back cramping, or passage of fluid or tissue, although symptoms vary. A miscarriage can be physically and emotionally difficult and may require medical evaluation.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:186:"गर्भपात गर्भावस्था के 20 सप्ताह से पहले गर्भ का स्वतः समाप्त हो जाना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:459:"Most miscarriages occur because the developing fetus has a genetic or chromosome problem that prevents normal development. In many cases, the exact cause cannot be identified. Other possible contributors include problems involving the uterus or cervix, certain infections, hormone or immune problems, uncontrolled medical conditions, smoking, alcohol or drug use, and some environmental exposures. Miscarriage is not usually caused by normal daily activities.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:264:"क्रोमोसोमल असामान्यताएं, हार्मोनल विकार, संक्रमण और मातृ स्वास्थ्य समस्याएं इसका कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:434:"Factors associated with a higher chance of miscarriage include increasing maternal age, previous pregnancy problems, abnormalities of the uterus or cervix, certain chronic medical conditions, uncontrolled diabetes, some infections, smoking, alcohol or recreational drug use, and certain genetic problems. Some miscarriages occur without identifiable risk factors because chromosome abnormalities can arise randomly during development.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:197:"अधिक मातृ आयु, धूम्रपान, शराब, मोटापा और पुरानी बीमारियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:420:"A suspected miscarriage is evaluated using the symptoms and medical history along with a physical or pelvic examination. Blood tests may be used to assess pregnancy hormone levels and blood loss. Ultrasound can help determine whether the pregnancy is developing normally and whether pregnancy tissue remains in the uterus. The evaluation also helps distinguish miscarriage from other causes of bleeding during pregnancy.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:193:"निदान में अल्ट्रासाउंड, रक्त परीक्षण और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:458:"Many miscarriages cannot be prevented because the most common cause is a random genetic abnormality in the developing fetus. Early and regular prenatal care can help identify and manage conditions that may affect pregnancy. Avoiding alcohol, recreational drugs, smoking, and unnecessary harmful exposures is recommended. Managing chronic medical conditions before and during pregnancy and taking recommended prenatal vitamins can support a healthy pregnancy.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:212:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली, प्रसवपूर्व देखभाल और बीमारियों का नियंत्रण जोखिम कम कर सकता है.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:426:"Miscarriage requires medical assessment when bleeding or pain occurs during pregnancy because other causes, including ectopic pregnancy, may need to be excluded. Seek prompt care for vaginal bleeding, pelvic or abdominal pain, or passage of tissue. Emergency care is needed for heavy bleeding, severe abdominal or pelvic pain, fainting, severe weakness, fever with significant illness, or other signs of serious deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:139;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:146;s:10:"disease_id";i:198;s:11:"overview_en";s:427:"Female infertility is the inability to become pregnant after regular, unprotected sexual intercourse for a period of time. It can result from problems with ovulation, the fallopian tubes, the uterus, or other reproductive structures. Age is an important factor because fertility generally decreases with increasing age. Infertility may involve one partner or both partners and can sometimes remain unexplained after evaluation.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:225:"महिला बांझपन नियमित असुरक्षित संबंधों के एक वर्ष बाद गर्भधारण न कर पाने की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:402:"Female infertility can result from problems with ovulation, blocked or damaged fallopian tubes, endometriosis, uterine conditions, or problems affecting the reproductive organs. Hormonal disorders such as polycystic ovary syndrome can interfere with ovulation. Age-related changes in the ovaries and eggs can also reduce fertility. Sometimes no specific cause is identified despite appropriate testing.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:250:"ओव्यूलेशन विकार, फैलोपियन ट्यूब रुकावट, एंडोमेट्रियोसिस और हार्मोन असंतुलन सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:395:"Age is an important risk factor for female infertility because the number and quality of eggs decrease over time. Other factors include smoking, excessive alcohol use, significant weight problems, certain medical conditions, previous pelvic infections or surgery, endometriosis, and disorders affecting ovulation. Some treatments, including chemotherapy and radiation, can also affect fertility.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:159:"आयु, मोटापा, धूम्रपान, तनाव और प्रजनन विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:436:"Evaluation of female infertility includes a medical and reproductive history and physical examination. Tests may assess ovulation and hormone levels, ovarian reserve, and the structure of the uterus and fallopian tubes. Pelvic ultrasound is commonly used, and other procedures may be performed when indicated. Evaluation of both partners is generally important because infertility may have female, male, combined, or unexplained causes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:194:"निदान में हार्मोन जांच, अल्ट्रासाउंड और प्रजनन क्षमता परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:470:"Not all female infertility can be prevented, particularly infertility related to age, genetics, or some medical conditions. Avoiding smoking and recreational drugs, limiting alcohol, maintaining a healthy weight, and preventing sexually transmitted infections can help protect reproductive health. Prompt evaluation of menstrual or reproductive problems and appropriate treatment of conditions such as endometriosis or pelvic infections may also help preserve fertility.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:180:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखना, धूम्रपान से बचना और समय पर उपचार मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:397:"Female infertility generally requires planned medical evaluation rather than emergency care. Seek assessment when pregnancy has not occurred after an appropriate period of trying or when there are concerns about menstrual cycles, ovulation, reproductive anatomy, or previous pelvic conditions. Sudden severe pelvic pain, heavy bleeding, fainting, or other acute symptoms require prompt evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:140;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:147;s:10:"disease_id";i:199;s:11:"overview_en";s:346:"Genital warts are sexually transmitted growths caused by certain types of human papillomavirus (HPV). They may appear as small or larger bumps or groups of growths around the genitals or anal area. HPV can spread through direct sexual or intimate skin-to-skin contact, and transmission may occur even when an infected person has no visible warts.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:154:"जननांग मस्से HPV संक्रमण से होने वाले यौन संचारित मस्से हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:417:"Genital warts are caused by infection with certain types of human papillomavirus (HPV). The virus is usually spread through direct sexual or intimate skin-to-skin contact, including vaginal, anal, or oral sexual contact. A person can transmit HPV even when visible warts are not present. The HPV types that commonly cause genital warts are generally different from those more strongly associated with certain cancers.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:132:"ह्यूमन पैपिलोमावायरस संक्रमण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:377:"Risk of genital warts increases with sexual exposure to HPV, particularly with multiple sexual partners or unprotected sexual contact. Having a weakened immune system can also make HPV infection more likely to persist or cause visible warts. HPV can be transmitted even when a partner has no visible lesions, so absence of warts does not eliminate the possibility of infection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:192:"अनेक यौन साथी, असुरक्षित यौन संबंध और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:412:"Genital warts are usually diagnosed by examining the affected skin and identifying the characteristic appearance of the growths. A healthcare professional may ask about symptoms, sexual exposure, and the location and duration of the lesions. Testing is not always necessary, although additional evaluation may be considered when lesions are unusual, uncertain, or need to be distinguished from another condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:186:"निदान सामान्यतः शारीरिक परीक्षण तथा कभी-कभी HPV परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:429:"HPV vaccination can help prevent infection with HPV types that commonly cause genital warts and certain cancers. Safer sexual practices, including consistent condom or barrier use and limiting exposure to infected partners, can reduce but not completely eliminate transmission because HPV can infect skin not covered by a barrier. Avoiding sexual contact while visible genital warts are present can also reduce transmission risk.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:147:"HPV टीकाकरण और सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:364:"Genital warts are generally not an emergency but should be medically evaluated for diagnosis and appropriate management. Seek assessment for rapidly changing, bleeding, painful, ulcerated, or unusually appearing lesions, or when the diagnosis is uncertain. Severe pain, significant bleeding, or rapidly worsening genital swelling requires prompt medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:141;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:149;s:10:"disease_id";i:201;s:11:"overview_en";s:330:"Acne is a common skin condition that develops when hair follicles become blocked by oil and dead skin cells and become inflamed. It commonly affects the face, chest, shoulders, and back. Acne may produce blackheads, whiteheads, pimples, deeper nodules, or cysts and can sometimes lead to persistent scars or changes in skin color.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:190:"मुंहासे एक सामान्य त्वचा रोग है जिसमें दाने, ब्लैकहेड्स और सूजन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:247:"Acne involves blocked hair follicles, excess oil, retained dead skin cells, and inflammation. Bacteria normally present on the skin can multiply within blocked follicles. Hormonal changes can increase oil production and contribute to this process.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:199:"अधिक तेल उत्पादन, बंद रोमछिद्र, बैक्टीरिया और हार्मोनल बदलाव इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:297:"Acne is most common in teenagers and young adults but can persist into adulthood. Hormonal changes, family history, and certain medicines can contribute. Stress, pressure on the skin, harsh scrubbing, and picking can worsen existing acne; they should not be presented as its sole underlying cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:198:"हार्मोनल परिवर्तन, तैलीय त्वचा, तनाव और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:281:"Diagnosis usually involves examining the skin and asking about symptom duration, family history, medicines, and relevant hormonal history. The appearance of the lesions helps identify acne. Laboratory tests may be considered when another condition or medical disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:134:"निदान त्वचा के चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:337:"Skin care can reduce irritation but does not guarantee prevention of acne. Gentle cleansing and avoiding harsh scrubbing are appropriate. Products labelled non-comedogenic are intended not to block pores, although they may still worsen acne in some people. Avoid picking or squeezing lesions, which can contribute to scars or dark marks.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:179:"उचित त्वचा देखभाल और स्वस्थ आदतें मुंहासों की रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:299:"Acne usually does not require emergency care. Seek medical evaluation if lesions become rapidly painful, extensively inflamed, infected, or associated with significant swelling or fever. Prompt treatment may also be appropriate when severe acne is causing scarring or substantial emotional distress.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:142;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:150;s:10:"disease_id";i:202;s:11:"overview_en";s:327:"Eczema is a group of skin conditions that commonly cause itchy, dry, inflamed, or scaly skin. Atopic dermatitis is the most common type. Symptoms may come and go and can range from mild dryness and itching to more severe inflammation and skin changes. Eczema often begins in childhood, although it can affect people of any age.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:217:"एक्जिमा त्वचा की दीर्घकालिक सूजन संबंधी बीमारी है जिसमें खुजली और सूखापन होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:395:"Eczema results from a combination of skin-barrier problems, immune responses, and genetic factors. In atopic dermatitis, the skin may lack proteins that help maintain the normal barrier that keeps moisture inside the skin. This makes the skin more vulnerable to dryness and irritation. Environmental triggers, allergens, soaps, chemicals, heat, sweating, and other irritants can worsen symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:180:"आनुवंशिकता, प्रतिरक्षा असंतुलन और पर्यावरणीय कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:397:"Risk is higher in people with a personal or family history of eczema, asthma, or seasonal allergies. Atopic dermatitis commonly begins during infancy or childhood. People with a weakened skin barrier may be more sensitive to irritants and allergens. Dry environments, frequent exposure to irritating substances, sweating, and other individual triggers can make symptoms more likely or more severe.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:194:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, एलर्जी और उत्तेजक पदार्थों का संपर्क जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:277:"Eczema is usually diagnosed from the appearance and location of the skin changes, symptoms, and medical history. A healthcare professional may examine the skin and ask about triggers, allergies, and exposures. Additional testing may be used when another condition is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान रोग इतिहास और शारीरिक परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:476:"Eczema cannot always be prevented, but regular skin care can reduce irritation and flare-ups. Moisturizers help maintain the skin barrier and should be used regularly, especially after bathing. Avoiding known irritants, harsh soaps, excessive heat, and scratching can also help. Keeping fingernails short may reduce skin damage from scratching. People with recurrent or severe eczema should follow an individualized treatment and skin-care plan from a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:126:"त्वचा को नम रखना और ट्रिगर्स से बचना लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:364:"Eczema is usually not an emergency but should be assessed when symptoms are persistent, severe, or difficult to control. Seek medical care for rapidly worsening skin inflammation, extensive blistering, significant pain, fever, pus, or signs of skin infection. Urgent evaluation is appropriate when infection appears to be spreading or symptoms deteriorate rapidly.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:143;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:151;s:10:"disease_id";i:203;s:11:"overview_en";s:355:"Psoriasis is a chronic autoimmune skin disorder that causes skin cells to build up more rapidly than normal, producing areas of thickened, inflamed, scaly, or itchy skin. It can affect different parts of the body and may also involve the nails or joints. Symptoms often occur in episodes called flares, with periods when the condition becomes less active.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:201:"सोरायसिस एक ऑटोइम्यून त्वचा रोग है जिसमें त्वचा कोशिकाएं तेजी से बढ़ती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:395:"Psoriasis develops when the immune system becomes abnormally active and causes inflammation and rapid growth of skin cells. Genetic factors play an important role, and several genes are associated with susceptibility to the condition. Environmental or physical triggers can activate or worsen the abnormal immune response, although having a trigger does not necessarily mean it caused psoriasis.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:158:"प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली की गड़बड़ी और आनुवंशिक कारण प्रमुख हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:381:"Psoriasis can occur in anyone, but susceptibility is greater when there is a family history of the condition. Factors that may trigger or worsen flares include infections such as strep throat, injury or irritation of the skin, stress, smoking, certain medicines, and extremes of sun exposure. A weakened immune system may also be associated with more severe disease in some people.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1014:"सोरायसिस किसी भी व्यक्ति को हो सकता है, लेकिन पारिवारिक इतिहास से इसकी संवेदनशीलता बढ़ सकती है। स्ट्रेप थ्रोट जैसे संक्रमण, त्वचा का सूखना या चोट लगना, तनाव, धूम्रपान, कुछ दवाएँ और बहुत कम या बहुत अधिक धूप सोरायसिस को भड़का सकते हैं। HIV संक्रमण से जुड़ी कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा भी अधिक गंभीर बीमारी से संबंधित हो सकती है। ये कारक flare को बढ़ा सकते हैं, लेकिन हर व्यक्ति में सोरायसिस का कारण नहीं बनते।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:398:"Psoriasis is usually diagnosed clinically from the appearance and distribution of the skin lesions together with the medical history. A healthcare professional examines areas of affected skin and may ask about symptoms, previous episodes, family history, and possible triggers. A skin biopsy may sometimes be performed when the diagnosis is uncertain or another skin condition needs to be excluded.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:189:"निदान आमतौर पर चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण तथा कभी-कभी बायोप्सी से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:386:"Psoriasis cannot always be prevented because genetic and immune factors play an important role. Avoiding known personal triggers may help reduce flares. Protecting the skin from injury, managing stress, avoiding smoking, following prescribed treatment, and maintaining overall health may help control symptoms. Regular medical care can also help identify and manage associated problems.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:146:"ट्रिगर्स से बचना और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाना लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:357:"Psoriasis is usually a chronic condition and is not generally an emergency. Seek medical assessment when skin disease is extensive, painful, rapidly worsening, or interfering substantially with daily activities. Urgent care is appropriate for widespread redness with fever or severe illness, extensive blistering or skin loss, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:144;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:152;s:10:"disease_id";i:204;s:11:"overview_en";s:378:"Vitiligo is a condition in which areas of the skin lose their normal pigment, producing lighter or white patches. It occurs when pigment-producing cells called melanocytes are destroyed or stop functioning. The patches may appear on the face, hands, feet, around body openings or other areas and can gradually become more extensive. Hair in affected areas may also lose pigment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:180:"विटिलिगो में त्वचा का रंगद्रव्य नष्ट होने से सफेद धब्बे बन जाते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:426:"The exact cause of vitiligo is not fully understood. It is generally considered an autoimmune condition in which the immune system attacks melanocytes. Genetic factors may contribute to susceptibility. Vitiligo may occur along with other autoimmune disorders. In some people, skin injury, severe sunburn or other forms of skin damage may precede the appearance of new patches, although these factors do not explain every case.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:166:"रंग बनाने वाली कोशिकाओं का ऑटोइम्यून विनाश इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:320:"Having a family member with vitiligo can increase risk. Other risk factors include having certain autoimmune conditions and, in some people, a history of significant skin injury or severe sunburn. Vitiligo can develop at any age and affects people of all skin types. Many people who develop it have no known risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और ऑटोइम्यून रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:407:"Vitiligo is usually diagnosed from the appearance and distribution of depigmented skin during a physical examination. A Wood lamp may help a healthcare professional identify areas of pigment loss, particularly in lighter skin. Medical history and examination may be used to look for associated autoimmune conditions. A skin biopsy or blood tests may sometimes be recommended when the diagnosis is uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:160:"निदान त्वचा परीक्षण और विशेष प्रकाश परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:418:"There is no proven way to prevent vitiligo because its underlying causes are not completely understood. Protect depigmented skin from excessive sunlight because areas without pigment are more vulnerable to sunburn. Use appropriate sun protection and avoid unnecessary skin injury. People with vitiligo should seek medical advice if new or changing patches appear so that other causes of pigment loss can be considered.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:154:"शीघ्र उपचार और त्वचा की सुरक्षा रोग नियंत्रण में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:363:"Vitiligo is generally not an emergency and usually develops gradually. Seek medical assessment when skin changes are new, rapidly progressing, uncertain in diagnosis, or associated with other symptoms suggesting another condition. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for sudden widespread skin changes accompanied by significant illness or other concerning symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:145;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:153;s:10:"disease_id";i:205;s:11:"overview_en";s:359:"Rosacea is a chronic inflammatory skin disorder that commonly affects the central face. It may cause persistent redness, episodes of flushing, visible small blood vessels, burning or stinging, and acne-like bumps or pustules. Some people develop eye symptoms, including irritation or dryness. Symptoms may come and go and can become more persistent over time.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:179:"रोसैशिया एक दीर्घकालिक त्वचा रोग है जिसमें चेहरे पर लालिमा होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:398:"The exact cause of rosacea is not fully understood. Abnormal regulation of inflammation, blood-vessel activity, and the skin immune response may contribute. Genetic susceptibility and changes in the skin barrier may also play a role. Certain environmental or lifestyle triggers can cause flushing and worsen symptoms, but these triggers do not necessarily represent the underlying cause of rosacea.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:198:"सटीक कारण अज्ञात है, परंतु प्रतिरक्षा और रक्तवाहिकीय कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:359:"Risk factors include a family history of rosacea and skin that tends to flush easily. Sun exposure, heat, emotional stress, hot beverages, spicy foods, and alcohol can trigger or worsen symptoms in some people. Rosacea can occur in adults of different backgrounds and is often more noticeable in people with lighter skin, although it can affect any skin tone.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:186:"गोरी त्वचा, पारिवारिक इतिहास, गर्मी और मसालेदार भोजन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:420:"Rosacea is usually diagnosed clinically by examining the skin and reviewing the pattern of symptoms and triggers. A clinician looks for persistent facial redness, flushing, visible small blood vessels, and inflammatory bumps or pustules. There is no single laboratory test that confirms rosacea. If symptoms are unusual or overlap with another skin condition, additional evaluation may be needed to exclude other causes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1094:"रोसैशिया का निदान आमतौर पर चेहरे की त्वचा में होने वाले बदलावों के रूप और पैटर्न के आधार पर चिकित्सकीय रूप से किया जाता है। चिकित्सक चेहरे पर लगातार या बार-बार होने वाली लालिमा, फ्लशिंग, दिखाई देने वाली छोटी रक्त वाहिकाओं, दानों या पस्ट्यूल तथा अन्य विशिष्ट लक्षणों की जांच करते हैं। रोसैशिया की पुष्टि करने वाला कोई एक विशेष प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण नहीं है। अन्य त्वचा रोगों की संभावना होने पर अतिरिक्त जांच की जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:389:"Rosacea cannot always be prevented, but avoiding personal triggers may reduce flare-ups. Common measures include protecting the skin from sunlight with shade and sunscreen, avoiding excessive heat, identifying foods or drinks that trigger flushing, and using gentle skin-care products. Regular medical care can help control persistent symptoms and reduce the impact of recurrent flare-ups.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:122:"ट्रिगर्स से बचना और धूप से सुरक्षा लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:318:"Rosacea is usually not an emergency but should be assessed when persistent or worsening. Seek medical care if facial redness, swelling, pustules, or skin irritation becomes severe or difficult to manage. Eye pain, marked eye redness, blurred vision, or other significant eye symptoms require prompt medical assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:146;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:154;s:10:"disease_id";i:206;s:11:"overview_en";s:400:"Dermatitis refers to inflammation of the skin that commonly causes itching, redness, dryness, irritation, or a rash. Different types can develop because of allergens, irritants, genetic susceptibility, or immune reactions. Contact with substances such as soaps, detergents, chemicals, cosmetics, or metals may cause or worsen some forms, while other forms are associated with a weakened skin barrier.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:171:"डर्मेटाइटिस त्वचा की सूजन है जिसमें खुजली, लालिमा और जलन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:414:"Dermatitis can develop from allergens, irritants, genetic susceptibility, or immune reactions. Contact dermatitis may occur after exposure to substances such as soaps, detergents, chemicals, solvents, metals, cosmetics, or plants. Atopic dermatitis is associated with genetic and immune factors and a weakened skin barrier. Different forms of dermatitis can therefore have different underlying causes and triggers.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:216:"एलर्जी, उत्तेजक पदार्थ, आनुवंशिकता और प्रतिरक्षा प्रतिक्रियाएं कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:411:"Risk factors for dermatitis depend on the type. A personal or family history of allergies, asthma, or eczema can increase susceptibility to atopic dermatitis. Frequent exposure to soaps, detergents, chemicals, solvents, metals, cosmetics, plants, or other irritants can contribute to contact dermatitis. Dry skin, repeated hand washing, occupational exposure, and a weakened skin barrier may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:169:"एलर्जी, रसायनों का संपर्क और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:422:"Diagnosis of dermatitis generally involves a detailed medical history and examination of the skin. A healthcare professional may ask about symptoms, timing, exposures, products used on the skin, occupation, allergies, and previous skin conditions. Allergy testing or patch testing may be considered when allergic contact dermatitis is suspected. A skin biopsy may occasionally be used when the diagnosis remains uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:214:"निदान में रोग इतिहास, त्वचा परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार एलर्जी परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:434:"Avoiding known skin irritants and allergens can help reduce dermatitis flare-ups. Use gentle skin-care products, avoid unnecessary exposure to harsh soaps and chemicals, and maintain adequate skin hydration to support the skin barrier. Protective measures may be useful when occupational exposure to irritants is unavoidable. Identifying and avoiding personal triggers can be particularly helpful for people with recurrent dermatitis.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:146:"उत्तेजक पदार्थों से बचना और त्वचा को नम रखना लाभकारी है.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:338:"Dermatitis is usually not an emergency, but persistent or worsening inflammation should be evaluated. Seek medical care for extensive or rapidly worsening redness, significant pain, blistering, fever, pus, or other signs of infection. Urgent evaluation is appropriate when symptoms spread rapidly or there is significant systemic illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:34:53";}i:147;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:155;s:10:"disease_id";i:207;s:11:"overview_en";s:400:"Seborrheic dermatitis is a common inflammatory skin condition that usually affects areas rich in oil glands, including the scalp, face, eyebrows, ears, and upper chest. It may cause flaky or greasy scales, redness, itching, or irritation. Dandruff is a mild form affecting the scalp. Symptoms can come and go and may become more noticeable during periods of stress, illness, or environmental changes.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:275:"सेबोरिक डर्मेटाइटिस त्वचा की एक दीर्घकालिक सूजन वाली बीमारी है जिसमें त्वचा पर पपड़ी और लालिमा होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:440:"Seborrheic dermatitis is associated with an inflammatory response involving naturally occurring skin yeast, particularly Malassezia, together with skin oil production and individual susceptibility. The condition is not simply caused by poor hygiene. Factors such as stress, hormonal changes, neurological conditions, immune system problems, illness, cold or dry weather, and some medicines may contribute to flare-ups or increased severity.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:229:"मालासेज़िया फंगस की वृद्धि, अधिक तेल उत्पादन और प्रतिरक्षा प्रतिक्रिया इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:423:"Risk factors include personal or family tendency toward seborrheic dermatitis, oily skin, stress, cold or dry weather, and certain neurological or immune-related conditions. The condition is also more common in some adults with Parkinson disease or other neurological disorders and in people with weakened immune systems. Symptoms may fluctuate and can become more noticeable during periods of physical or emotional stress.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:181:"तैलीय त्वचा, तनाव, तंत्रिका संबंधी रोग और ठंडा मौसम जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:440:"Seborrheic dermatitis is usually diagnosed clinically from the characteristic appearance and distribution of affected skin. A healthcare professional examines areas such as the scalp, face, ears, eyebrows, and chest and reviews the pattern of symptoms. Laboratory testing is generally unnecessary. When the appearance is unusual or another skin condition is suspected, additional examination or testing may be used to clarify the diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:146:"निदान त्वचा के चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:453:"Seborrheic dermatitis cannot always be prevented because individual susceptibility and skin biology contribute to its development. Regular gentle cleansing and appropriate scalp care can help control symptoms. Avoiding known personal triggers and following an established treatment plan can reduce flare-ups. Stress management and treatment of associated medical conditions may also be helpful for people who experience recurrent or persistent symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:139:"नियमित सफाई और तनाव नियंत्रण से लक्षण कम हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:232:"Seborrheic dermatitis is usually not an emergency. Seek medical assessment if symptoms are persistent, severe, widespread, or difficult to control, or if there are signs of infection such as increasing pain, swelling, pus, or fever.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:148;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:156;s:10:"disease_id";i:208;s:11:"overview_en";s:359:"Contact dermatitis is inflammation of the skin that develops after contact with an irritating substance or an allergen. It may cause redness, itching, soreness, swelling, dryness, cracking, or a rash. Irritant contact dermatitis results from direct skin damage, while allergic contact dermatitis occurs when the immune system reacts to a particular substance.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:240:"कॉन्टैक्ट डर्मेटाइटिस त्वचा की सूजन है जो एलर्जी या उत्तेजक पदार्थों के संपर्क से होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:386:"Contact dermatitis develops when the skin reacts to a substance that directly irritates it or triggers an allergic response. Irritant causes include soaps, detergents, solvents, chemicals, frequent wet exposure, and friction. Allergic causes include substances such as metals, fragrances, cosmetics, hair dyes, rubber, plants, or other materials to which a person has become sensitized.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:152:"एलर्जन, रसायन, साबुन या कॉस्मेटिक्स इसका कारण बन सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:369:"Risk of contact dermatitis increases with repeated exposure to irritants or allergens, especially when the skin barrier is frequently damaged. People working with chemicals, detergents, solvents, metals, cosmetics, hair products, plants, or wet materials may have greater exposure. A history of atopic dermatitis can also increase susceptibility to irritant dermatitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:166:"रसायनों का संपर्क, एलर्जी और संवेदनशील त्वचा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:396:"Contact dermatitis is usually diagnosed from the appearance and distribution of the rash, symptoms, medical history, and possible exposure to irritants or allergens. The clinician may examine whether the rash corresponds to areas of contact. Patch testing can help identify an allergic trigger when allergic contact dermatitis is suspected or symptoms continue despite avoiding obvious exposures.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:165:"निदान इतिहास, परीक्षण और कभी-कभी पैच टेस्ट द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:398:"Contact dermatitis can often be prevented by identifying and avoiding substances that irritate the skin or trigger an allergy. Use protective gloves or other appropriate barriers when exposure cannot be avoided, and follow safe handling practices for chemicals and cleaning products. Gentle skin care and regular use of suitable moisturizers can help protect the skin barrier and reduce irritation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:115:"ज्ञात ट्रिगर्स से बचना रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:322:"Contact dermatitis is usually not an emergency. Seek medical care if the rash is severe, widespread, persistent, or worsening, or if there is significant swelling, blistering, pain, or signs of infection. Emergency care is needed for difficulty breathing or swelling of the face, lips, tongue, or throat after an exposure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:149;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:157;s:10:"disease_id";i:209;s:11:"overview_en";s:560:"Urticaria, commonly called hives, is a skin reaction characterized by raised, itchy areas called wheals. Individual hives may appear suddenly, change in size or shape, and disappear within hours while new lesions develop elsewhere. Urticaria may be acute and short-lived or may continue or recur over a longer period. Possible triggers include infections, medicines, foods, insect exposures, physical stimuli, and immune reactions, although a specific cause is not always identified. Swelling of deeper tissues, known as angioedema, can occur along with hives.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"अर्टिकेरिया (पित्ती) त्वचा पर खुजलीदार उभरे हुए चकत्तों की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:519:"Urticaria occurs when certain cells in the skin release substances such as histamine that cause small blood vessels to become more permeable. Triggers can include foods, medicines, infections, insect bites or stings, physical pressure, heat, cold, sunlight, exercise, or other physical stimuli. In many cases of chronic urticaria, no specific external trigger is identified. Some cases are associated with immune-system activity or other medical conditions. The cause may therefore remain unknown even after evaluation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:137:"एलर्जी, संक्रमण, दवाएं और तनाव इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:514:"Risk factors for urticaria depend on its type. People with allergies, certain infections, autoimmune conditions, or a personal tendency toward allergic or immune reactions may be more likely to develop particular forms. Physical urticaria can be triggered by pressure, cold, heat, sunlight, vibration, or exercise. Medicines and foods may trigger acute episodes in susceptible individuals. Chronic urticaria often has no identifiable trigger, and the presence of hives does not necessarily indicate a food allergy.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:134:"एलर्जी, ऑटोइम्यून रोग और संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:643:"Urticaria is usually diagnosed clinically by examining the skin and reviewing the timing, duration, appearance, possible triggers, medicines, infections, and associated symptoms. Individual hives typically change or disappear within a relatively short period, which helps distinguish them from some other skin conditions. Laboratory testing is not routinely necessary for uncomplicated acute hives. Additional evaluation may be considered when urticaria is persistent, recurrent, associated with systemic symptoms, or when another underlying condition is suspected. Assessment for angioedema and breathing difficulty is particularly important.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1168:"अर्टिकेरिया का निदान आमतौर पर त्वचा पर दिखाई देने वाले उभरे हुए चकत्तों और उनके इतिहास के आधार पर किया जाता है। स्वास्थ्यकर्मी पूछ सकते हैं कि पित्ती कब शुरू हुई, प्रत्येक उभरा हुआ दाना कितनी देर रहता है, क्या भोजन, दवा, संक्रमण या पर्यावरणीय कारण से संबंध है और क्या अन्य लक्षण मौजूद हैं। हर मामले में जाँच आवश्यक नहीं होती। बार-बार या लंबे समय तक पित्ती होने पर किसी अंतर्निहित कारण की तलाश के लिए चुनिंदा रक्त जाँच या अन्य परीक्षण किए जा सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:576:"Prevention of urticaria depends on whether a specific trigger can be identified. People with a known trigger may reduce episodes by avoiding that trigger when practical, while those with physical urticaria may need to limit the particular physical stimulus that causes symptoms. Medicines that have previously caused a reaction should be discussed with a healthcare professional before future use. Because chronic urticaria often has no identifiable cause, complete prevention may not be possible. Persistent or recurrent hives should be evaluated when the pattern is unclear.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:96:"ट्रिगर्स और एलर्जन से बचना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:298:"Urticaria is often temporary, but persistent, recurrent, or severe hives should be medically assessed. Emergency care is needed if hives occur with swelling of the lips, tongue, mouth, or throat, difficulty breathing or swallowing, dizziness, fainting, or other signs of a severe allergic reaction.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:150;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:158;s:10:"disease_id";i:210;s:11:"overview_en";s:314:"Cellulitis is a bacterial infection involving the deeper layers of the skin and underlying tissues. It commonly develops when bacteria enter through a break in the skin, such as a wound, cut, burn, bite, or ulcer. The affected area may become red, warm, swollen, painful, and tender, and fever or chills may occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:140:"सेलुलाइटिस त्वचा की गहरी परतों का जीवाणु संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:360:"Cellulitis is most commonly caused by bacteria such as Streptococcus or Staphylococcus species entering the skin through a break in its protective barrier. Entry can occur through cuts, wounds, burns, insect or animal bites, ulcers, surgical wounds, or cracks between the toes. Fungal infections and other conditions that damage the skin can make entry easier.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:157:"बैक्टीरिया कट, घाव या क्षतिग्रस्त त्वचा से प्रवेश करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:360:"Risk of cellulitis increases when the skin barrier is damaged by cuts, wounds, burns, insect or animal bites, surgery, ulcers, or chronic skin conditions. Cracked skin from fungal infections, diabetes, circulation problems, and medicines that suppress the immune system can also increase susceptibility. Previous episodes may increase the chance of recurrence.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:174:"मधुमेह, त्वचा की चोट, मोटापा और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:381:"Cellulitis is usually diagnosed by examining the affected skin and considering the pattern of redness, warmth, swelling, tenderness, and other symptoms. Blood tests or cultures may be used when infection is severe or when identifying the bacteria is important. A sample from an open wound or affected area may sometimes be tested, while imaging is reserved for selected situations.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:157:"निदान परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार रक्त जांच से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:380:"Cellulitis prevention focuses on protecting the skin and promptly caring for breaks in the skin. Clean cuts, wounds, and scratches with soap and water, keep them covered when appropriate, and watch for signs of infection. Keep skin moisturized to reduce cracking, protect the feet, and manage conditions such as diabetes or fungal foot infections that can damage the skin barrier.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:138:"घाव की उचित देखभाल और स्वच्छता रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:396:"Cellulitis requires prompt medical assessment and treatment because infection can spread into deeper tissues or the bloodstream. Seek care for painful, red, warm, swollen skin, especially when the area is expanding or accompanied by fever or chills. Emergency evaluation is needed for rapidly spreading infection, severe illness, confusion, fainting, or other signs of serious systemic infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:151;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:159;s:10:"disease_id";i:211;s:11:"overview_en";s:579:"Impetigo is a common and highly contagious bacterial infection of the skin. It usually causes red sores or blisters that break open and form a characteristic yellowish or honey-colored crust. It is particularly common among young children and can spread easily through direct contact. Impetigo most often affects exposed areas such as the face, hands, and limbs. There are two common forms: nonbullous impetigo, which produces crusted sores, and bullous impetigo, which produces larger fluid-filled blisters. Scratching can spread the infection to nearby skin or to other people.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:213:"इम्पेटिगो एक अत्यधिक संक्रामक जीवाणु त्वचा संक्रमण है जो बच्चों में सामान्य है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:627:"Impetigo is caused by bacteria, most commonly Staphylococcus aureus or Streptococcus pyogenes. The bacteria can enter through breaks in the skin caused by cuts, insect bites, eczema, or other irritation. The infection spreads readily through direct contact with infected skin or contaminated items. The bacteria responsible for impetigo can colonize the skin without causing disease and may enter through even very small breaks in the skin. Existing eczema, scabies, insect bites, abrasions, or other itchy conditions can create opportunities for infection. Warm conditions and close person-to-person contact facilitate spread.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:156:"स्टैफिलोकोकस या स्ट्रेप्टोकोकस बैक्टीरिया इसका कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:632:"Risk factors include close contact with an infected person, crowded living conditions, warm or humid environments, poor access to hygiene facilities, and existing skin conditions that cause breaks in the skin. Children commonly spread impetigo among classmates or family members. Children, people living in crowded settings, athletes involved in close-contact activities, and individuals with skin injuries or chronic skin conditions may have greater exposure or susceptibility. Poor hygiene and sharing personal items can facilitate transmission. Previous impetigo does not provide reliable lifelong protection against reinfection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:158:"खराब स्वच्छता, त्वचा की चोट और निकट संपर्क जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:616:"Impetigo is usually diagnosed by examining the characteristic sores and crusts. Laboratory testing is not always necessary, but a sample from an infected area may be cultured when the diagnosis is uncertain, treatment has failed, or antibiotic resistance is suspected. A clinician generally recognizes impetigo from the typical appearance of the lesions and their rapid spread. Bacterial culture can identify the organism when infection is recurrent, severe, atypical, or not responding to treatment. Examination can also distinguish impetigo from conditions such as herpes infections, dermatitis, or fungal disease.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1122:"इम्पेटिगो का निदान आमतौर पर त्वचा के विशिष्ट घावों की जांच से किया जाता है, विशेषकर नाक या मुंह के आसपास या खुली त्वचा पर बनने वाले पपड़ीदार घावों से। हर मामले में प्रयोगशाला जांच आवश्यक नहीं होती। यदि निदान स्पष्ट न हो, संक्रमण बार-बार हो या उपचार अपेक्षित रूप से काम न करे, तो चिकित्सक घाव से नमूना लेकर बैक्टीरियल कल्चर करा सकते हैं। जांच से इम्पेटिगो को समान दिखाई देने वाली अन्य त्वचा स्थितियों से अलग करने में भी मदद मिलती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:588:"Good hand and skin hygiene can reduce the spread of impetigo. Cuts, insect bites, and other skin injuries should be cleaned and covered. Avoiding close contact with infected lesions and not sharing towels, clothing, or personal items can help prevent transmission. Promptly cleaning minor skin injuries and treating underlying itchy skin conditions can reduce opportunities for bacterial infection. Hands should be washed regularly, especially after touching affected areas. During an active infection, personal towels, clothing, bedding, and other items should not be shared with others.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:153:"स्वच्छता और संक्रमित व्यक्ति से दूरी रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:317:"Impetigo is usually not an emergency but should be medically assessed because it is contagious and may require treatment. Seek care if lesions are spreading, persistent, painful, or associated with fever or significant swelling. Prompt assessment is appropriate if the infection is worsening or involves a large area.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:152;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:160;s:10:"disease_id";i:212;s:11:"overview_en";s:320:"Scabies is a contagious skin condition caused by infestation with the human itch mite. The mites burrow into the upper layer of the skin and lay eggs, causing an itchy rash. Severe itching is often worse at night. Scabies can affect people of any age and is commonly spread through prolonged, close skin-to-skin contact.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:189:"स्केबीज त्वचा का संक्रामक संक्रमण है जो सूक्ष्म माइट्स के कारण होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:418:"Scabies is caused by infestation with the human itch mite, Sarcoptes scabiei. The female mite burrows into the outer layer of skin and deposits eggs. The body reacts to the mites, eggs, and their waste, producing an itchy rash. Transmission usually occurs through prolonged direct skin-to-skin contact with an infected person. Less commonly, mites may spread through recently contaminated clothing, bedding, or towels.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:148:"सार्कोप्टिस स्केबीआई माइट्स त्वचा में सुरंग बनाते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:353:"Risk factors include close or prolonged contact with a person who has scabies, living in crowded conditions, and environments where close physical contact is common. Household members and sexual partners of an infected person have increased exposure. People with weakened immune systems may develop severe or crusted scabies, which is highly contagious.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:111:"भीड़भाड़ और निकट संपर्क जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:370:"Scabies is usually diagnosed from the characteristic itchy rash and the pattern and location of affected skin. A healthcare professional may examine the skin for burrows, which are small lines made by mites. A skin scraping may sometimes be examined under a microscope to look for mites, eggs, or mite waste. Diagnosis can also be based on symptoms and exposure history.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:166:"निदान त्वचा परीक्षण और कभी-कभी माइक्रोस्कोपिक जांच से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:477:"Scabies can be reduced by avoiding prolonged skin-to-skin contact with an infected person until treatment is completed. Household members and close contacts may need evaluation and treatment at the same time to prevent reinfection. Clothing, towels, and bedding used by an affected person should be appropriately washed or otherwise handled according to treatment guidance. People should follow the complete treatment plan even if itching continues temporarily after treatment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:150:"संक्रमित व्यक्तियों से बचाव और परिवार का उपचार सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:335:"Scabies is usually not an emergency but requires appropriate treatment to prevent continued spread and complications from scratching. Seek medical assessment if symptoms are severe, persistent after treatment, associated with extensive skin damage, or accompanied by signs of bacterial infection such as increasing pain, pus, or fever.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:153;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:161;s:10:"disease_id";i:213;s:11:"overview_en";s:525:"Ringworm is a common fungal infection of the skin, hair, or nails. Despite its name, it is not caused by a worm. The infection is produced by fungi called dermatophytes and can occur on different parts of the body, producing conditions such as athlete’s foot, jock itch, scalp ringworm, or ring-shaped skin infections. Symptoms commonly include itching, scaling, redness, cracking, or an expanding rash. Ringworm spreads through direct contact with an infected person or animal and through contaminated objects or surfaces.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:173:"दाद एक फंगल त्वचा संक्रमण है जिसमें गोल खुजलीदार चकत्ते बनते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:502:"Ringworm is caused by dermatophyte fungi that grow in the outer layers of the skin, hair, or nails. Different species can infect humans and animals. Infection occurs when fungal spores come into contact with susceptible skin and may spread through direct contact with an infected person or animal. It can also spread through contaminated clothing, towels, bedding, combs, sports equipment, floors, or other surfaces. Warm, moist environments can support fungal growth and make transmission more likely.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:160:"डर्माटोफाइट फंगस त्वचा, बाल या नाखूनों को संक्रमित करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:517:"Risk factors for ringworm include close contact with infected people or animals, living in warm and humid environments, participation in contact sports, sharing personal items, and frequent exposure to communal showers or locker rooms. Minor skin injuries can make infection easier. Conditions that weaken immune defenses can increase susceptibility. Wearing damp clothing or footwear for prolonged periods may encourage fungal growth. Children and people with frequent close-contact exposure may have increased risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:141:"पसीना, खराब स्वच्छता और निकट संपर्क जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:531:"Ringworm is often diagnosed by examining the characteristic appearance of the rash and considering exposure history. If the diagnosis is uncertain, a healthcare professional may collect skin scrapings, hair, or nail material for microscopic examination or fungal culture. A specialized examination may be useful for scalp or nail infections. Because several skin conditions can resemble ringworm, laboratory confirmation can be particularly useful when infection is extensive, recurrent, or not responding to appropriate treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:144:"निदान परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार फंगल जांच से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:503:"Ringworm can be reduced by avoiding direct contact with infected skin and by not sharing towels, clothing, bedding, combs, helmets, or sports equipment with an infected person. Keeping skin clean and dry, changing damp clothing, wearing appropriate footwear in communal wet areas, and treating infected pets can help reduce transmission. Contact sports facilities should maintain good hygiene. People with a suspected infection should seek treatment and avoid close contact that could spread the fungus.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:129:"त्वचा को सूखा और स्वच्छ रखना रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:307:"Ringworm is usually not an emergency. Seek medical assessment if the infection is widespread, involves the scalp or nails, persists despite treatment, or is rapidly worsening. Prompt care is appropriate if there is significant inflammation, pain, drainage, fever, or suspected secondary bacterial infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:154;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:162;s:10:"disease_id";i:214;s:11:"overview_en";s:374:"Athletes foot is a common fungal infection affecting the skin of the feet. It often causes itching, burning, redness, scaling and cracking, especially between the toes. The infection can spread to the soles or sides of the feet and may sometimes affect the toenails. It thrives in warm, damp environments and can spread through contact with contaminated surfaces or objects.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:195:"एथलीट फुट पैरों का फंगल संक्रमण है जो विशेष रूप से उंगलियों के बीच होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:343:"Athletes foot is caused by fungi known as dermatophytes. These fungi grow well in warm, moist areas such as locker rooms, communal showers, swimming-pool areas and inside damp footwear. Infection can occur when a person walks barefoot on contaminated surfaces or shares towels, shoes or other personal items with someone who has the infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:100:"फंगस गर्म और नम वातावरण में बढ़ते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:383:"Risk increases when the feet remain warm and moist for long periods. Wearing tight or poorly ventilated shoes, sweating heavily, walking barefoot in communal areas and sharing towels or footwear can increase exposure. People who have had athletes foot before may develop it again. Certain medical conditions or treatments that weaken immune defenses may also increase susceptibility.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:157:"अधिक पसीना, तंग जूते और सार्वजनिक स्नानघर जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:362:"Athletes foot is often diagnosed by examining the affected skin and recognizing its typical appearance. A healthcare professional may take a small skin scraping for microscopic examination or laboratory testing when the diagnosis is uncertain, the infection is severe or another skin condition could look similar. Nail involvement may require additional testing.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:157:"निदान परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार फंगल जांच से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:404:"Keep the feet clean and dry, especially between the toes. Change socks regularly and allow shoes to dry completely before wearing them again. Choose footwear that allows air circulation and avoid sharing shoes, socks or towels. Wear sandals or other protective footwear in communal showers, locker rooms and pool areas. Treating an infection promptly can also reduce spread to other people or body areas.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:129:"पैरों को सूखा रखना और हवादार जूते पहनना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:301:"Athlete’s foot is usually not an emergency. Seek medical care if symptoms persist despite treatment, spread extensively, become painful, or are accompanied by swelling, drainage, fever, or signs of bacterial infection. People with conditions that increase infection risk may need earlier assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:155;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:163;s:10:"disease_id";i:215;s:11:"overview_en";s:350:"Nail fungus, also called onychomycosis, is a fungal infection of a fingernail or toenail. The nail may become thickened, discolored, brittle, crumbly, or distorted. The infection commonly develops gradually and may affect one or several nails. Toenails are affected more often than fingernails, and infection can sometimes spread to surrounding skin.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:180:"नाखून फंगस नाखूनों का संक्रमण है जिसमें रंग बदलना और मोटापन होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:350:"Nail fungus is usually caused by fungi that infect the nail or the skin beneath it. Dermatophytes are the most common cause, although yeasts and other fungi can also be responsible. The infection may enter through small breaks in the skin or nail. It can spread through direct contact or contaminated floors, footwear, towels, or nail-care equipment.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:146:"डर्माटोफाइट और अन्य फंगस नाखूनों को संक्रमित करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:428:"Risk is increased by athlete’s foot, repeated exposure to moist environments, heavy sweating, tight footwear, minor nail injuries, diabetes, reduced circulation, weakened immunity, increasing age, and a previous history of nail fungus. Sharing nail clippers, towels, socks, or footwear can facilitate spread. Older adults are particularly susceptible because nail growth becomes slower and the nail structure changes with age.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:138:"अधिक आयु, मधुमेह और खराब रक्तसंचार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:406:"Diagnosis is usually based on examination of the affected nail and surrounding skin. A healthcare professional may take a nail clipping, scraping, or sample from beneath the nail for microscopic examination or laboratory testing. Testing is useful because other conditions, including psoriasis or nail trauma, can resemble fungal infection. Identifying the organism can help guide treatment when necessary.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:139:"निदान में नाखून परीक्षण और लैब जांच शामिल हो सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:376:"Keeping feet clean and dry, changing damp socks, wearing breathable footwear, treating athlete’s foot promptly, and avoiding shared nail-care equipment can reduce risk. Nails should be trimmed carefully and injuries should be avoided. People with diabetes or circulation problems should take particular care of their feet and seek medical advice for persistent nail changes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:135:"नाखूनों की स्वच्छता और पैरों को सूखा रखना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:345:"Nail fungus is usually not an emergency and often develops gradually. Seek medical assessment if the nail becomes painful, the infection spreads, the surrounding skin becomes inflamed, or treatment is unsuccessful. Prompt evaluation is appropriate when there is significant swelling, drainage, fever, or concern for another type of nail disease.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:156;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:164;s:10:"disease_id";i:216;s:11:"overview_en";s:375:"Folliculitis is inflammation of one or more hair follicles that can cause small red bumps, pimples, pustules, itching, tenderness, or discomfort. It can occur on many areas of the body, including the scalp, beard area, neck, groin, buttocks, and thighs. Folliculitis may result from irritation or blockage of follicles and may sometimes involve bacterial or fungal infection.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:134:"फॉलिकुलाइटिस बालों की जड़ों की सूजन या संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:390:"Folliculitis can develop when hair follicles are damaged, blocked, or irritated. Friction from clothing, shaving, sweating, and repeated skin irritation can damage follicles. Bacterial infection, particularly with staphylococci, is a common cause of infectious folliculitis. Fungal infections can cause some forms, while ingrown hairs may produce inflammation without a bacterial infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:152:"जीवाणु संक्रमण, जलन या फंगल संक्रमण इसका कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:360:"Risk increases with shaving, friction from clothing or equipment, sweating, prolonged moisture, and activities that repeatedly irritate the skin. People with curly hair may be more prone to ingrown hairs after shaving. Certain skin conditions, weakened immunity, or exposure to contaminated water can also increase the likelihood of some forms of folliculitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:116:"शेविंग, पसीना और तंग कपड़े जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:409:"Folliculitis is usually diagnosed by examining the skin and identifying the characteristic bumps or pustules around hair follicles. The healthcare professional may ask about shaving, friction, recent exposures, medicines, and previous episodes. When infection is suspected or symptoms are recurrent or severe, a sample from an affected follicle may be tested to identify bacteria or fungi and guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:108:"निदान त्वचा परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:419:"Reducing friction and avoiding unnecessary damage to hair follicles can help prevent folliculitis. Avoid shaving affected areas when possible; when shaving is necessary, use a clean razor and avoid cutting hairs excessively close to the skin. Wear breathable clothing, keep sweaty skin clean and dry, and avoid sharing razors or personal grooming items. Recurrent infections should be evaluated for an underlying cause.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:139:"स्वच्छता और त्वचा की जलन से बचाव रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:280:"Folliculitis is usually mild, but medical assessment is appropriate when bumps are widespread, painful, recurrent, or worsening. Seek prompt care for rapidly spreading redness, significant swelling, pus, fever, or increasing pain because a deeper skin infection may be developing.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:157;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:165;s:10:"disease_id";i:217;s:11:"overview_en";s:229:"A boil is a painful, pus-filled lump caused by an infection involving a hair follicle and nearby skin tissue. It may start as a tender, swollen area and enlarge as pus builds up. Several nearby boils can join to form a carbuncle.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:234:"फोड़े त्वचा के दर्दनाक मवादयुक्त संक्रमण हैं जो बालों की जड़ों के आसपास विकसित होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:247:"Boils are most often caused by Staphylococcus aureus. These bacteria can live on the skin or in the nose without causing illness. Infection can develop when bacteria enter through damaged skin or a hair follicle and spread into surrounding tissue.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:162:"आमतौर पर स्टैफिलोकोकस ऑरियस जीवाणु संक्रमण के कारण होते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:285:"Boils may be more likely with diabetes, conditions that weaken the immune system, certain skin conditions such as eczema, obesity, or close contact with someone who has boils. These factors affect susceptibility or exposure; a boil is not, by itself, evidence of poor personal hygiene.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:179:"खराब स्वच्छता, मधुमेह, मोटापा और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:275:"A healthcare professional can usually identify a boil by examining its appearance and asking about symptoms and previous episodes. A sample of fluid or pus may be cultured to identify the organism. Recurrent boils or signs of a wider infection may warrant further evaluation.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:158:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण और कभी-कभी कल्चर जांच से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:289:"Regular handwashing, keeping skin clean, and keeping cuts clean and covered can reduce infection risk and spread. Avoid sharing towels, washcloths, or razors. Cover draining areas with a clean dressing and wash hands after contact. These measures reduce risk but cannot prevent every boil.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:179:"अच्छी स्वच्छता और त्वचा संक्रमण का शीघ्र उपचार रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:337:"Boils should be medically assessed when they are large, painful, recurrent, or fail to improve. Seek prompt care if redness or swelling spreads, fever develops, multiple boils occur, or the lesion is on the face or near important structures. Emergency evaluation is appropriate for severe systemic illness or rapidly spreading infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:158;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:166;s:10:"disease_id";i:218;s:11:"overview_en";s:369:"A carbuncle is a group of interconnected boils caused by a deeper bacterial infection of the skin and tissues around several hair follicles. The area is usually painful, swollen, red, and filled with pus, and several openings may develop as the infection drains. Carbuncles commonly occur on the back, neck, thighs, or other areas where friction and sweating may occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:217:"कार्बंकल कई जुड़े हुए फोड़ों का समूह है जो त्वचा की गहरी परतों को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:414:"Carbuncles are most commonly caused by infection with Staphylococcus aureus bacteria. The infection often begins in a hair follicle and extends into nearby tissues, producing several connected boils and areas of pus. Bacteria can enter through small cuts, abrasions, or other breaks in the skin. Close contact with an infected person or sharing contaminated personal items can sometimes contribute to transmission.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:924:"कार्बंकल आमतौर पर कई पास-पास के बालों के रोमों में होने वाले जीवाणु संक्रमण के कारण बनता है। Staphylococcus aureus इसका सबसे सामान्य कारण है। जब बैक्टीरिया irritated या क्षतिग्रस्त त्वचा से अंदर प्रवेश करके ऊतकों में गहराई तक फैलते हैं, तो मवाद और मृत ऊतक से भरी फोड़ों की एक गुच्छेदार संरचना बन सकती है। बैक्टीरिया निकट संपर्क या दूषित वस्तुओं के माध्यम से भी फैल सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:397:"Diabetes and other conditions that weaken the immune system can increase the risk of developing carbuncles. Poor skin hygiene, repeated friction, sweating, and skin injuries may also contribute. People living in crowded conditions or those who have close contact with someone carrying the bacteria may have greater exposure. A history of recurrent skin infections can also increase susceptibility.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:160:"मधुमेह, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा और त्वचा का घर्षण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:441:"Diagnosis is usually based on the appearance of the affected skin and the symptoms. A healthcare professional may examine the size, depth, drainage, and surrounding redness of the infection. A sample of pus may be collected for bacterial culture when the infection is severe, recurrent, unusually located, or not responding to initial treatment. Additional assessment may be needed when an underlying condition such as diabetes is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:165:"निदान परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार बैक्टीरियल कल्चर से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:422:"Good skin hygiene can help reduce the spread of bacteria that cause carbuncles. Keep wounds clean and covered, wash hands regularly, and avoid sharing towels, razors, clothing, or other personal items with someone who has a skin infection. Managing diabetes and other chronic conditions can also reduce susceptibility. Recurrent infections should be evaluated by a healthcare professional to identify contributing factors.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:165:"स्वच्छता और पुरानी बीमारियों का नियंत्रण रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:367:"A carbuncle is a deeper cluster of infected boils and should receive prompt medical assessment because infection can spread into surrounding tissues. Seek care for increasing redness, swelling, pain, drainage, or fever. Emergency evaluation is needed for rapidly spreading infection, severe weakness, confusion, fainting, or other signs of serious systemic infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:159;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:167;s:10:"disease_id";i:219;s:11:"overview_en";s:438:"Warts are benign skin growths caused by infection with certain types of human papillomavirus (HPV). They may occur on the hands, feet, face, or other areas of the skin and can vary in size, shape, and surface texture. Some warts are painless, while others, particularly those on weight-bearing areas of the feet, can become uncomfortable or painful. Warts may resolve without treatment, although they can persist or spread to other areas.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:170:"मस्से HPV वायरस के कारण होने वाली गैर-कैंसरयुक्त त्वचा वृद्धि हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:410:"Warts develop when certain types of human papillomavirus infect the skin. The virus can enter through small breaks, cuts, or other minor damage in the skin and may spread through direct skin-to-skin contact or contact with contaminated surfaces. Autoinoculation can occur when the virus is transferred from one part of the body to another, particularly when a wart is picked, scratched, or otherwise irritated.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:132:"ह्यूमन पैपिलोमावायरस संक्रमण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:377:"Risk is increased by frequent skin-to-skin contact, sharing towels or personal items, walking barefoot in communal wet areas such as swimming-pool areas and locker rooms, and having damaged or irritated skin. Nail biting or picking around the nails can increase the likelihood of certain warts. Reduced immune function may make warts more likely to develop, persist, or spread.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:136:"त्वचा संपर्क और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:396:"Most warts are diagnosed clinically by examining their characteristic appearance, surface, and location. A healthcare professional may distinguish common warts from other skin lesions based on the examination. A biopsy or other testing may occasionally be required when a lesion is unusual, persistent, rapidly changing, painful, bleeding, or difficult to distinguish from another skin condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:139:"निदान सामान्यतः चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:439:"Warts cannot always be completely prevented, but reducing exposure to HPV can lower risk. Avoid picking, scratching, or biting warts and avoid sharing towels, razors, nail tools, or other personal items that contact affected skin. Wear footwear in communal wet areas, keep cuts and breaks in the skin clean and covered when appropriate, and wash hands after touching a wart. Avoid direct contact with another person’s wart when possible.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:151:"प्रत्यक्ष संपर्क से बचाव और स्वच्छता जोखिम कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:331:"Common warts are generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment if a wart changes rapidly, bleeds, becomes painful, spreads extensively, or does not respond to treatment, or if the diagnosis is uncertain. Prompt evaluation is especially appropriate for lesions in sensitive locations or in people with weakened immune systems.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:160;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:168;s:10:"disease_id";i:220;s:11:"overview_en";s:418:"Genital herpes is a sexually transmitted infection caused by herpes simplex virus, usually HSV-2 or HSV-1. It can cause painful blisters, sores, or ulcers around the genitals, anus, or nearby skin, although many infected people have mild or unrecognized symptoms. After infection, the virus remains in the body and can reactivate, causing recurrent outbreaks. Symptoms and recurrence patterns vary between individuals.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:211:"जननांग हर्पीज एक यौन संचारित संक्रमण है जो हर्पीज सिम्प्लेक्स वायरस से होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:419:"Genital herpes results from infection with herpes simplex virus, most commonly HSV-2 or HSV-1. The virus enters through mucous membranes or small breaks in the skin and can be transmitted through sexual or intimate skin-to-skin contact. Transmission can occur when sores are present and can also occur when the infected person has no visible lesions because the virus may be shed from the skin without obvious symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:128:"हर्पीज सिम्प्लेक्स वायरस टाइप 1 या 2 इसका कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:436:"Risk increases with sexual contact involving an infected partner, multiple sexual partners, inconsistent use of condoms or other barriers, and previous exposure to herpes simplex virus. Because transmission can occur without visible sores, a person may be exposed without knowing that a partner has an active infection. Other sexually transmitted infections or behaviors associated with increased sexual exposure can also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:134:"असुरक्षित यौन संबंध और अनेक साथी जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:441:"Diagnosis may be based on the appearance and location of characteristic genital lesions together with the person’s symptoms and sexual history. When lesions are present, a swab from a fresh lesion can be tested using molecular methods to detect herpes simplex virus. Blood tests may be useful in selected circumstances, particularly when there are no lesions but a specific clinical question about previous infection needs to be addressed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:117:"निदान में परीक्षण, PCR और वायरल जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:452:"Consistent condom or other barrier use can reduce, but does not completely eliminate, the risk of genital herpes transmission because uncovered skin can also transmit the virus. Avoid sexual contact when genital or oral lesions or other outbreak symptoms are present. People who know they have genital herpes should discuss the infection with partners and follow medical advice about antiviral treatment, including suppressive therapy when appropriate.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:130:"सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार संक्रमण रोकने में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:345:"Genital herpes usually does not require emergency care, but medical assessment can help confirm the diagnosis and guide treatment. Seek prompt care for severe or extensive outbreaks, significant pain, difficulty urinating, fever, or worsening symptoms. Urgent medical attention is appropriate during pregnancy when genital herpes symptoms occur.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:161;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:169;s:10:"disease_id";i:221;s:11:"overview_en";s:302:"Cold sores are small, painful, fluid-filled blisters that usually develop on or around the lips and mouth. They are caused by herpes simplex virus and often recur after the initial infection because the virus remains inactive in nerve tissue. Outbreaks commonly heal within several days to a few weeks.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:163:"कोल्ड सोर्स होंठों के आसपास होने वाले छोटे दर्दनाक फफोले हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:405:"Cold sores are caused by herpes simplex virus, most commonly HSV-1. After the initial infection, the virus remains in the body in an inactive state within nerve cells and can reactivate later. Illness, fever, emotional stress, fatigue, sunlight, hormonal changes, or irritation around the mouth may trigger recurrent outbreaks. The virus spreads through direct contact with infected secretions or lesions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1159:"कोल्ड सोर्स हर्पीस सिम्प्लेक्स वायरस के कारण होते हैं, जिनमें HSV-1 सबसे सामान्य है। पहली बार संक्रमण के बाद वायरस शरीर में निष्क्रिय अवस्था में रह सकता है और बाद में फिर सक्रिय होकर बार-बार घाव पैदा कर सकता है। बीमारी, तनाव, थकान, धूप, हार्मोनल बदलाव या त्वचा में स्थानीय जलन जैसे कारक इसे फिर सक्रिय कर सकते हैं। वायरस सक्रिय घाव या संक्रमित मुंह के स्राव के सीधे संपर्क से फैल सकता है, और कभी-कभी दिखाई देने वाले घाव न होने पर भी संक्रमण फैल सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:310:"Cold sore outbreaks may be more likely during periods of physical or emotional stress, fever, illness, fatigue, or hormonal changes. Sun exposure and local irritation around the lips can also trigger recurrence. People with weakened immune systems may experience more frequent, severe, or persistent outbreaks.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"तनाव, बुखार, धूप और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:380:"Cold sores are usually diagnosed clinically from their characteristic appearance and symptoms, particularly grouped fluid-filled blisters around the lips or mouth. A healthcare professional may examine the affected area and ask about previous episodes and possible triggers. A swab or laboratory test may be considered when the appearance is unusual or the diagnosis is uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:139:"निदान सामान्यतः चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:421:"Avoiding direct contact with active cold sores and not sharing items that contact the mouth can reduce transmission. During an outbreak, avoid kissing and oral contact with others until lesions have healed. Identifying and reducing personal triggers such as excessive sun exposure or fatigue may reduce recurrences. People with frequent or severe outbreaks should discuss treatment options with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:138:"ट्रिगर्स और प्रकोप के दौरान संपर्क से बचना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:295:"Cold sores are usually not an emergency and often heal without complications. Seek medical assessment if lesions are unusually severe, extensive, persistent, frequently recurrent, or involve the eye. Prompt evaluation is important for eye pain, eye redness, light sensitivity, or vision changes.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:162;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:170;s:10:"disease_id";i:222;s:11:"overview_en";s:348:"Melanoma is a type of cancer that begins in melanocytes, the cells that produce the pigment melanin. It commonly develops in the skin but can occur in other tissues containing pigment-producing cells. A melanoma may appear as a new unusual spot or as a change in an existing mole, including changes in its size, shape, border, color, or appearance.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:228:"मेलानोमा त्वचा कैंसर का गंभीर प्रकार है जो रंग बनाने वाली कोशिकाओं से उत्पन्न होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:357:"Melanoma develops when melanocytes acquire genetic changes that cause abnormal growth and survival. The exact cause of an individual melanoma is not always known. Ultraviolet radiation from sunlight or tanning devices can damage skin cells and contributes to melanoma risk. Melanoma can also arise from an existing mole or develop on apparently normal skin.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:148:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन और पराबैंगनी विकिरण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:372:"Risk factors include exposure to ultraviolet radiation, especially repeated sun exposure and severe blistering sunburns, use of tanning beds, fair skin that burns easily, many or atypical moles, and a personal or family history of melanoma. Certain inherited genetic conditions and weakened immunity can also increase risk. Melanoma can occur in people of all skin colors.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:154:"अधिक धूप, गोरी त्वचा और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:426:"Diagnosis of melanoma begins with examination of a suspicious skin lesion and assessment of changes in its appearance. Features such as asymmetry, an irregular border, uneven color, increasing size, or evolution over time may raise concern. The diagnosis is confirmed by removing all or part of the suspicious tissue and examining it under a microscope. Additional tests may be used to determine whether the cancer has spread.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:124:"निदान में त्वचा परीक्षण और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:387:"Limiting exposure to ultraviolet radiation can reduce melanoma risk. Avoid tanning beds, seek shade, use protective clothing, and take precautions when spending time in strong sunlight. People with many or atypical moles or a personal or family history of melanoma should discuss appropriate skin examinations with a healthcare professional. Report new or changing skin lesions promptly.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:132:"धूप से बचाव और प्रारंभिक जांच रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:381:"Melanoma requires prompt medical evaluation when a new or changing skin lesion is noticed. Seek assessment for a spot that is asymmetrical, has an irregular border, contains multiple colors, is changing in size or appearance, or bleeds or does not heal. Emergency care is generally not required unless there is an acute complication such as uncontrolled bleeding or severe illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:163;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:171;s:10:"disease_id";i:223;s:11:"overview_en";s:394:"Basal cell carcinoma is the most common type of skin cancer and develops from basal cells in the skin. It most often occurs on areas exposed to ultraviolet radiation, particularly the face, scalp, ears, neck, and arms. Lesions may appear as a pearly or shiny bump, a persistent sore, a scaly patch, or an area that repeatedly bleeds or heals and returns. Early evaluation helps guide treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:156:"बेसल सेल कार्सिनोमा त्वचा कैंसर का सबसे सामान्य प्रकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:479:"Basal cell carcinoma is primarily associated with cumulative ultraviolet radiation from sunlight or tanning devices. Repeated or prolonged exposure can cause DNA damage in basal cells and promote abnormal growth. Other contributing factors include previous radiation exposure, certain inherited conditions, a history of skin cancer, and reduced immune function. The cancer usually grows slowly and rarely spreads to distant organs, but untreated lesions can invade nearby tissue.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:142:"दीर्घकालिक पराबैंगनी किरणों का संपर्क मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:459:"Risk increases with cumulative ultraviolet exposure, frequent sunburns, use of tanning beds, fair skin, light-colored eyes, a tendency to burn rather than tan, and a history of significant sun exposure. Previous basal cell or other skin cancers increase future risk. Immunosuppression, previous radiation therapy, and certain inherited disorders can also increase susceptibility. Risk generally rises with age because ultraviolet damage accumulates over time.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:117:"गोरी त्वचा, धूप और अधिक आयु जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:493:"Basal cell carcinoma is usually suspected from the appearance of a persistent or changing skin lesion and confirmed by biopsy. A healthcare professional examines the lesion and surrounding skin and may use dermoscopy for additional visual assessment. A biopsy provides tissue for microscopic examination and establishes the diagnosis. Further imaging is generally reserved for lesions that are unusually large, deeply invasive, recurrent, or suspected of involving important nearby structures.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:114:"निदान बायोप्सी द्वारा पुष्टि किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:475:"The most important preventive measure is protection from ultraviolet radiation. Using broad-spectrum sunscreen, wearing protective clothing and hats, seeking shade, and avoiding tanning beds can reduce cumulative UV exposure. Regular awareness of changing or persistent skin lesions can promote early detection. People with previous skin cancer or substantial sun exposure may benefit from regular professional skin examinations and should report suspicious lesions promptly.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:103:"धूप से नियमित सुरक्षा जोखिम कम करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:380:"Basal cell carcinoma should be medically evaluated promptly when a new or changing skin growth, persistent sore, bleeding lesion, or non-healing area is present. Early assessment is important because untreated lesions can grow deeper and cause local tissue damage. Emergency care is generally not required unless there is severe bleeding, infection, or another acute complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:164;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:172;s:10:"disease_id";i:224;s:11:"overview_en";s:324:"Squamous cell carcinoma is a type of cancer that develops from squamous cells, which form part of the outer and inner lining of many parts of the body. Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma commonly develops on areas of skin exposed to sunlight. It may appear as a persistent scaly patch, sore, growth, or area of abnormal skin.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:162:"स्क्वैमस सेल कार्सिनोमा त्वचा कैंसर का एक सामान्य प्रकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:398:"Squamous cell carcinoma of the skin develops when squamous cells undergo abnormal genetic changes and begin multiplying uncontrollably. Ultraviolet radiation from sunlight or tanning devices is a major contributing factor. Other factors include previous radiation treatment, chronic wounds or scars, certain chemical exposures, weakened immune function, and some infections or inherited conditions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:137:"UV विकिरण और त्वचा की दीर्घकालिक क्षति इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:294:"Risk factors include substantial lifetime exposure to ultraviolet radiation, fair or easily sunburned skin, previous skin cancer, treatment with radiation, long-term immune suppression, chronic wounds or scars, and certain inherited conditions. Older age is also associated with increased risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:141:"धूप, गोरी त्वचा और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:366:"Squamous cell carcinoma is usually diagnosed by examining a suspicious skin lesion and performing a skin biopsy. During a biopsy, part or all of the abnormal area may be removed and examined under a microscope. The healthcare professional may also examine nearby lymph nodes or order additional tests when there is concern that the cancer has spread or is high risk.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:111:"निदान हेतु परीक्षण और बायोप्सी आवश्यक है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:383:"Reducing ultraviolet exposure can lower the risk of cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma. Protective measures include seeking shade, wearing protective clothing, using broad-spectrum sunscreen, and avoiding indoor tanning. People with previous skin cancer or other high-risk conditions should follow recommended skin examinations and report persistent or changing skin lesions promptly.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:96:"UV किरणों से सुरक्षा जोखिम कम करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:415:"Squamous cell carcinoma requires prompt medical evaluation for a persistent or changing skin lesion, especially a rough or scaly growth, sore that does not heal, bleeding lesion, or rapidly enlarging area. Early treatment is important because some squamous cell carcinomas can grow deeper or spread. Emergency care is generally not required unless there is severe bleeding, infection, or another acute complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:165;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:173;s:10:"disease_id";i:225;s:11:"overview_en";s:330:"Skin cancer is a group of cancers that begin in cells of the skin. The major types include basal cell carcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, and melanoma. Skin cancers may appear as a new or changing growth, sore, patch, or lesion. Early evaluation of suspicious skin changes can help identify cancer before it becomes more advanced.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:187:"त्वचा कैंसर त्वचा कोशिकाओं की असामान्य वृद्धि है जो DNA क्षति से होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:368:"Most skin cancers develop because abnormal skin cells acquire changes that allow uncontrolled growth. Ultraviolet radiation from sunlight and tanning devices is a major contributing factor. Other causes and contributing influences vary by cancer type and may include genetic changes, immune suppression, radiation exposure, certain chemicals, and previous skin injury.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:148:"पराबैंगनी विकिरण और आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:309:"Risk factors vary by skin cancer type but include cumulative ultraviolet exposure, frequent sunburns, tanning-bed use, fair skin, light eyes or hair, a history of previous skin cancer, increasing age, certain inherited conditions, chronic immune suppression, and exposure to particular radiation or chemicals.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:141:"धूप, गोरी त्वचा और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:330:"Skin cancer is usually evaluated through a skin examination followed by biopsy of a suspicious lesion. The biopsy allows a pathologist to determine the type of cancer and its characteristics. Additional imaging or lymph-node evaluation may be recommended for selected cancers when there is concern about deeper invasion or spread.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:143:"निदान में परीक्षण, डर्मोस्कोपी और बायोप्सी शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:347:"Regular protection from ultraviolet radiation can reduce skin cancer risk. Measures include seeking shade, wearing protective clothing and a broad-brimmed hat, using broad-spectrum sunscreen appropriately, avoiding tanning beds, and limiting intense sun exposure. Regular awareness of new or changing skin lesions can also support early detection.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:118:"धूप से सुरक्षा और शीघ्र पहचान महत्वपूर्ण है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:292:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for a new or changing skin lesion, a sore that does not heal, repeated bleeding or crusting, or a rapidly growing or changing mole or skin growth. Urgent assessment is appropriate if significant bleeding, rapidly worsening swelling, or signs of infection occur.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:166;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:174;s:10:"disease_id";i:226;s:11:"overview_en";s:463:"Alopecia areata is an autoimmune condition that causes the immune system to attack hair follicles, resulting in hair loss. It commonly produces one or more smooth, round patches of hair loss on the scalp or other areas of the body, although more extensive forms can affect much of the scalp or all body hair. Hair may regrow spontaneously, but the course is unpredictable and repeated episodes can occur. Changes to the nails may accompany more extensive disease.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:195:"एलोपेसिया एरियाटा एक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जिसमें बाल झड़ने के धब्बे बनते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:536:"Alopecia areata develops when the immune system mistakenly attacks structures associated with hair follicles. The exact reason this autoimmune response begins is not fully understood. Genetic susceptibility can increase risk, and environmental or other immune triggers may contribute. Alopecia areata is not caused by poor hygiene and is not simply a consequence of ordinary stress, although stressful events may coincide with onset or worsening in some people. Other autoimmune conditions may occur in association with alopecia areata.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:134:"प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली बालों की जड़ों पर हमला करती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:402:"Risk factors for alopecia areata include a family history of the condition and a personal or family history of autoimmune disease. It can occur at any age but often begins earlier in life. Certain immune-related conditions may increase susceptibility. The presence of a risk factor does not predict how extensive hair loss will become. Some people develop alopecia areata without any known risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:153:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, ऑटोइम्यून रोग और तनाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:507:"Alopecia areata is generally diagnosed through examination of the pattern of hair loss and the scalp, together with medical and family history. Dermoscopy can reveal characteristic changes in affected follicles. A scalp biopsy may be considered when the diagnosis is uncertain. Blood tests can be useful when there are signs of associated autoimmune, thyroid, nutritional, or other conditions. The clinician also considers other causes of patchy hair loss, including fungal infection and scarring disorders.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:131:"निदान स्कैल्प परीक्षण और रोग इतिहास पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:537:"There is no proven way to prevent alopecia areata because its autoimmune triggers are not fully understood. Maintaining general health and managing associated autoimmune conditions can support overall well-being but cannot guarantee prevention. People with sudden patchy hair loss should seek evaluation because some causes are treatable and early diagnosis can guide management. Avoiding unnecessary scalp trauma or harsh hair treatments can reduce additional hair damage, although these practices do not prevent the autoimmune process.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:104:"शीघ्र उपचार रोग की प्रगति कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:315:"Alopecia areata is generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment for sudden, extensive, rapidly progressing, or recurrent hair loss, or when the diagnosis is uncertain. Prompt evaluation is appropriate if hair loss is accompanied by significant skin inflammation, pain, scarring, or other concerning symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:167;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:175;s:10:"disease_id";i:227;s:11:"overview_en";s:557:"Androgenetic alopecia is a common form of hair loss caused by a combination of genetic susceptibility and the effects of androgen hormones on hair follicles. It can affect people of different sexes and usually develops gradually. Hair becomes progressively thinner because affected follicles produce shorter and finer hairs. The pattern varies between individuals, with thinning commonly occurring at the crown or hairline in men and more diffuse thinning over the top of the scalp in women. Early evaluation can help identify treatable causes of hair loss.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:164:"एंड्रोजेनेटिक एलोपेसिया बाल झड़ने का सबसे सामान्य प्रकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:581:"Androgenetic alopecia results from inherited sensitivity of hair follicles to androgen hormones, particularly dihydrotestosterone. In susceptible follicles, repeated hormone exposure gradually shortens the growth phase and causes progressive miniaturization. Genetic factors can come from either side of the family. Hormonal influences and age also affect how the condition develops. Although androgenetic alopecia is a major cause of patterned hair loss, other conditions can cause similar symptoms, so persistent or unusual hair loss should be assessed before assuming the cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:187:"आनुवंशिक कारण और एंड्रोजन हार्मोन के प्रति संवेदनशीलता इसका कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:481:"Risk of androgenetic alopecia is strongly influenced by family history and age. Hormonal sensitivity of hair follicles also plays an important role. The condition can affect people of different sexes, although the typical pattern differs. Hair loss may become more noticeable with increasing age. Other forms of hair loss can coexist, so sudden shedding, scalp inflammation, patchy loss, or rapidly changing symptoms should not automatically be attributed to androgenetic alopecia.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:150:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, आयु और हार्मोनल कारक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:557:"Androgenetic alopecia is usually diagnosed from the pattern and gradual progression of hair loss, medical history, family history, and examination of the scalp and hair. A clinician may use dermoscopy or other methods to examine follicle changes. Laboratory testing is not always necessary but may be considered when symptoms suggest another cause, such as nutritional deficiency, thyroid disease, hormonal abnormalities, or inflammatory scalp disease. Sudden, patchy, painful, or rapidly progressive hair loss warrants evaluation for alternative diagnoses.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:131:"निदान स्कैल्प परीक्षण और रोग इतिहास पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:556:"Androgenetic alopecia cannot always be prevented because genetic and hormonal factors are central to its development. Avoiding unnecessary traction, harsh chemical treatments, and practices that repeatedly damage hair may help prevent additional hair breakage or traction-related loss. A balanced diet supports normal hair growth, although supplements are not useful unless a deficiency is present. Early assessment of progressive hair thinning can help distinguish androgenetic alopecia from nutritional, hormonal, inflammatory, or other treatable causes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:117:"शीघ्र उपचार से रोग की प्रगति धीमी हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:316:"Androgenetic alopecia is usually gradual and is not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when hair loss is sudden, rapidly worsening, patchy, associated with scalp inflammation, or accompanied by other symptoms. Evaluation can help distinguish it from other causes of hair loss that may require different treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:36:39";}i:168;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:176;s:10:"disease_id";i:228;s:11:"overview_en";s:430:"Dandruff is a common scalp condition that causes visible flakes and itching. It may occur with an oily or dry scalp and is often associated with changes in the scalp skin and growth of a yeast that normally lives on the skin. Dandruff can be persistent or recurrent and may become more noticeable during periods of stress, cold weather, or changes in scalp care. Severe or persistent symptoms may indicate another scalp condition.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:181:"रूसी सिर की त्वचा की सामान्य समस्या है जिसमें पपड़ी और खुजली होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:406:"Dandruff is associated with increased shedding of scalp skin cells and may be influenced by excess oil production, irritation, and growth of the yeast Malassezia that normally lives on the scalp. Changes in the scalp environment can contribute to inflammation and flaking. Dandruff may overlap with or resemble seborrheic dermatitis and can sometimes be associated with other inflammatory scalp conditions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:134:"अधिक तेल, फंगल वृद्धि और त्वचा की जलन इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:335:"Risk may increase with an oily scalp, stress, cold or dry weather, infrequent scalp cleansing, and sensitivity to products used on the scalp. Some people with neurological or immune-related conditions may experience more persistent seborrheic-type scalp symptoms. Dandruff can occur at any age but is particularly common after puberty.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:132:"तैलीय स्कैल्प, तनाव और ठंडा मौसम जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:449:"Dandruff is usually diagnosed by examining the scalp and identifying characteristic flaking, scaling, and irritation. No specific laboratory test is normally required. When symptoms are severe, persistent, extensive, or atypical, a healthcare professional may assess for seborrheic dermatitis, psoriasis, eczema, contact dermatitis, fungal infection, or another scalp disorder. Further testing is generally guided by the findings of the examination.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:139:"निदान सामान्यतः चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:469:"Dandruff cannot always be completely prevented, but regular scalp care can help control recurrent flaking. Washing the hair regularly and using an appropriate anti-dandruff shampoo can reduce scaling and oil buildup. Depending on the individual, products containing ingredients such as ketoconazole, selenium sulfide, zinc pyrithione, or salicylic acid may be useful. Avoiding products that irritate the scalp and following product directions can help maintain control.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1277:"डैंड्रफ को हमेशा पूरी तरह रोका नहीं जा सकता, लेकिन नियमित स्कैल्प देखभाल से इसे नियंत्रित करने में मदद मिल सकती है। बालों को नियमित रूप से धोना और उपयुक्त एंटी-डैंड्रफ शैम्पू का उपयोग करना परत और अतिरिक्त तेल को कम कर सकता है। कुछ लोगों को केटोकोनाजोल, सेलेनियम सल्फाइड, जिंक पाइरिथियोन या सैलिसिलिक एसिड जैसे घटकों वाले शैम्पू से लाभ हो सकता है। स्कैल्प में जलन पैदा करने वाले उत्पादों से बचना और उत्पाद के निर्देशों का पालन करना लक्षण दोबारा आने पर नियंत्रण बनाए रखने में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:331:"Dandruff is usually a mild condition and is not an emergency. Seek medical assessment if scalp scaling is severe, persistent, painful, associated with significant redness or swelling, or does not improve with appropriate care. Prompt evaluation is appropriate if there are signs of infection such as pus, increasing pain, or fever.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:169;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:177;s:10:"disease_id";i:229;s:11:"overview_en";s:434:"Hyperhidrosis is a condition in which a person sweats excessively and unpredictably, even when the body does not need to cool itself. Sweating may be particularly noticeable on the hands, feet, underarms, face, or other areas. Primary hyperhidrosis often affects specific areas and may occur without another underlying disease. Excessive sweating can interfere with daily activities, work, social situations, and emotional well-being.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:129:"हाइपरहाइड्रोसिस अत्यधिक पसीना आने की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:439:"Primary hyperhidrosis is usually associated with overactive sweat glands, and in many cases no specific cause is identified. It may run in families. Secondary hyperhidrosis occurs when excessive sweating is related to another medical condition or a medicine. Possible associated conditions include infections, hormone disorders, neurologic conditions, low blood sugar, and other illnesses. Some medicines can also cause increased sweating.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:180:"अत्यधिक सक्रिय स्वेद ग्रंथियां और तंत्रिका उत्तेजना इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:464:"A family history of excessive sweating can increase the likelihood of primary hyperhidrosis. Primary focal hyperhidrosis commonly begins during childhood or adolescence, although it can occur later. Risk for secondary hyperhidrosis depends on the presence of an underlying medical condition or use of a medicine that affects sweating. Anxiety or emotional stress may worsen sweating, although they are not necessarily the underlying cause of primary hyperhidrosis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:144:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, मोटापा और चिंता जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:472:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern, location, duration, and severity of excessive sweating and whether it occurs without normal triggers such as heat or exercise. A physical examination and medical history can help distinguish primary from secondary hyperhidrosis. When another condition is suspected, blood or urine tests may be used to evaluate possible causes. In selected cases, tests that measure sweating may help document the amount and distribution of perspiration.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:133:"निदान लक्षणों और चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:528:"Primary hyperhidrosis cannot always be prevented because its exact cause is often unknown. Avoiding known triggers such as excessive heat, certain foods, or stressful situations may reduce episodes in some people. Good skin hygiene and breathable clothing can help manage moisture and reduce skin irritation. When excessive sweating begins suddenly or is accompanied by other symptoms, medical evaluation is important because treating an underlying condition or changing a causative medicine may address secondary hyperhidrosis.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"ट्रिगर्स का नियंत्रण लक्षण कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:397:"Hyperhidrosis is usually not an emergency but may require medical evaluation when excessive sweating is persistent or interferes substantially with daily activities. Seek assessment when sweating is new, unexplained, occurs during sleep, or is accompanied by other symptoms. Sudden heavy sweating with chest pain, shortness of breath, fainting, or severe illness requires urgent medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:170;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:178;s:10:"disease_id";i:230;s:11:"overview_en";s:362:"Hidradenitis suppurativa is a chronic skin condition that causes painful, recurrent lumps, nodules, and abscesses, usually in areas where skin rubs together such as the armpits, groin, buttocks, or under the breasts. Lesions may drain pus and heal with scars or tunnels under the skin. The condition often begins after puberty and may persist or recur over time.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:188:"हाइड्राडेनाइटिस सप्पुरेटिवा त्वचा की दीर्घकालिक सूजन वाली बीमारी है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:388:"Hidradenitis suppurativa develops when hair follicles become blocked and inflamed. The exact reason for the blockage is not fully understood. Genetic, hormonal, environmental, and immune-related factors may contribute. Some cases are associated with inherited changes in genes involved in skin and hair-follicle function. The condition is not caused by poor hygiene and is not contagious.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:163:"बालों की जड़ों का अवरोध और प्रतिरक्षा गड़बड़ी योगदान करती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:333:"Hidradenitis suppurativa is more common after puberty and occurs more often in women and people with a family history of the condition. Overweight or obesity and smoking are associated with increased risk and may also be linked with more severe disease. Friction, heat, and repeated skin injury may aggravate symptoms in some people.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:146:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:387:"Diagnosis is usually based on the medical history, the pattern and location of recurrent skin lesions, and physical examination. There is no single test that confirms hidradenitis suppurativa. A healthcare professional may examine nodules, abscesses, scars, and draining areas and may collect a sample of pus or affected tissue when another infection or diagnosis needs to be considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:123:"निदान चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:379:"Hidradenitis suppurativa cannot always be prevented, but some measures may reduce irritation and flare-ups. Maintaining a healthy weight when appropriate, avoiding smoking, wearing loose-fitting clothing, reducing friction, and avoiding unnecessary skin injury may help. Keeping regular medical follow-up is important when lesions recur or complications such as scarring develop.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:131:"वजन नियंत्रण और धूम्रपान छोड़ना सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:380:"Hidradenitis suppurativa can cause recurrent painful nodules, abscesses, drainage, and scarring and should be medically assessed when persistent or worsening. Seek prompt care for rapidly enlarging painful lesions, extensive inflammation, fever, spreading redness, or significant drainage. Urgent assessment is appropriate when there are signs of a serious or spreading infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:171;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:179;s:10:"disease_id";i:231;s:11:"overview_en";s:456:"A keloid is an area of raised, firm scar tissue that grows beyond the boundaries of an original wound. It develops because the body produces excess collagen during the healing process. Keloids can occur after surgery, cuts, burns, piercings, injections, acne, or other skin injuries, and sometimes develop after very minor trauma. They may be itchy, painful, or cosmetically noticeable. Keloids can continue growing over time and may recur after treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:142:"कीलॉइड घाव भरने के बाद बनने वाला अत्यधिक निशान ऊतक है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:498:"Keloids form when the normal wound-healing process produces excessive collagen and other scar tissue. The precise biological reason some people develop this response is not completely understood. Keloids may follow surgical wounds, burns, cuts, injections, piercings, acne, or other skin injuries. Some can develop after very minor trauma. Genetic and skin-related factors influence susceptibility, and keloids are more likely in people with a personal or family history of abnormal scar formation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:118:"घाव भरने की असामान्य प्रक्रिया इसका कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:471:"Risk factors for keloids include a personal or family history of keloid formation, certain genetic and skin characteristics, and injuries such as surgery, burns, acne, piercings, or injections. Keloids are more common in some populations and are particularly likely to occur during younger adulthood. The location of an injury also matters, with the chest, shoulders, upper back, neck, and ears being common sites. Not every scar in a susceptible person becomes a keloid.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:118:"आनुवंशिकता और त्वचा की चोट जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:513:"Keloids are usually diagnosed clinically by examining the scar and reviewing the history of the original injury. Their characteristic raised appearance and growth beyond the boundaries of the original wound often distinguish them from ordinary scars and hypertrophic scars. Biopsy is not routinely necessary but may be considered when the diagnosis is uncertain or another skin condition needs to be excluded. Assessment also considers symptoms such as itching, pain, tenderness, and the likelihood of recurrence.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:102:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:499:"Keloids cannot always be prevented in people who are genetically susceptible. When possible, unnecessary skin trauma and cosmetic procedures that create avoidable wounds should be considered carefully in people with a history of keloids. Proper wound care may support normal healing, although it cannot guarantee that a keloid will not develop. People with a strong history of keloids should inform healthcare professionals before planned surgery, piercing, or other procedures that injure the skin.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:96:"अनावश्यक त्वचा चोट से बचाव सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:330:"Keloids are generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when a scar is growing, painful, itchy, repeatedly irritated, or interfering with movement or function. Prompt evaluation is appropriate if there is significant redness, drainage, increasing pain, or another change suggesting infection or a different skin condition.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:172;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:180;s:10:"disease_id";i:232;s:11:"overview_en";s:631:"Lichen planus is an inflammatory condition that can affect the skin, mouth, nails, scalp, or genital areas. It often causes small, itchy, or painful lesions that may appear suddenly or develop gradually. The condition is not contagious and may persist for months or longer. The appearance of lichen planus varies depending on the body area involved. Skin lesions are often purplish, flat-topped, and intensely itchy, while lesions inside the mouth may appear as white lines or patches and can sometimes be painful. Nail, scalp, or genital involvement can require additional assessment. Symptoms may improve over time but can recur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:169:"लाइकेन प्लेनस त्वचा और श्लेष्म झिल्ली की सूजन संबंधी बीमारी है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:669:"The exact cause of lichen planus is not fully understood. It appears to involve an abnormal immune response in which immune cells attack cells in the skin or mucous membranes. Certain medicines, infections, allergens, or other triggers may cause similar lichen planus-like reactions in some people. Lichen planus is thought to result from immune-mediated damage to cells in the outer layers of the skin or mucous membranes. The reason this immune response begins is often unclear. Medication-related eruptions can resemble lichen planus, and infections or other immune triggers may be associated with some cases. Different affected sites may have different appearances.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:168:"प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली की सूजन प्रतिक्रिया इसका कारण मानी जाती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:672:"Risk factors for lichen planus may include certain medications, hepatitis C infection, immune-system abnormalities, and other triggers. It can occur at any age but is more common in adults. Some people may also develop the condition after exposure to specific substances or treatments. Some people with lichen planus have associated autoimmune or inflammatory conditions. Certain medicines can produce lichenoid reactions, and hepatitis C has been associated with the condition in some populations. Oral disease may be influenced by local irritation, dental materials, tobacco exposure, or other factors, although these associations do not mean that they cause every case.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:112:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और तनाव जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:585:"Diagnosis is based on the appearance and location of the lesions and the medical history. A healthcare professional may examine the skin, mouth, nails, or other affected areas. A skin biopsy may be performed when the diagnosis is uncertain or another condition needs to be excluded. A clinician may inspect the distribution, color, shape, and surface of lesions and ask about medications and associated symptoms. Oral lesions may require examination of the gums, cheeks, tongue, and other mucosal surfaces. Biopsy findings can support the diagnosis when clinical features are atypical.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:157:"निदान हेतु परीक्षण और कभी-कभी बायोप्सी की आवश्यकता होती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:656:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent lichen planus because its exact cause is uncertain. Avoiding known triggers or medicines that have previously caused reactions may reduce recurrence in some people. Regular dental care and avoidance of irritating oral products can help when the mouth is affected. Prevention is mainly focused on reducing known aggravating factors because the underlying cause is uncertain. People who develop lichenoid reactions after a medication should discuss alternatives with their healthcare professional rather than stopping prescribed treatment independently. Gentle skin and oral care can reduce irritation in affected areas.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:84:"शीघ्र उपचार लक्षण कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:343:"Lichen planus is usually not an emergency but should be assessed when symptoms persist or are extensive. Seek medical care for painful or widespread skin lesions, significant mouth or genital involvement, difficulty eating or drinking, or worsening symptoms. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for rapidly changing lesions or signs of infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:173;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:181;s:10:"disease_id";i:233;s:11:"overview_en";s:397:"Molluscum contagiosum is a contagious viral skin infection that causes small, firm, painless bumps, often with a central indentation. The lesions may appear on the face, neck, arms, hands, trunk, or other areas of the skin. In adults they may occur around the genitals. The infection is usually self-limited in people with healthy immune systems, although lesions can persist for months or longer.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:129:"मोलस्कम कॉन्टेजियोसम एक वायरल त्वचा संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:417:"Molluscum contagiosum is caused by a virus in the poxvirus family. It spreads through direct skin-to-skin contact with an infected person and can also spread through contaminated personal items such as towels, clothing, or toys. Sexual contact can transmit the infection in adults. Scratching or irritating lesions can spread the virus to nearby skin. People with weakened immunity may develop more extensive disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:124:"यह मोलस्कम कॉन्टेजियोसम वायरस के कारण होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:373:"Risk is higher in children who have close skin contact with other children, people who share contaminated personal items, and adults with sexual exposure to an infected partner. People with eczema may be more susceptible to extensive lesions, and those with weakened immune systems, including some people with HIV infection, may develop more numerous or persistent lesions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:133:"निकट संपर्क और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:406:"Diagnosis is usually based on the characteristic appearance of the skin lesions and a clinical examination. The typical bumps are small, flesh-colored or pearly, and often have a central dimple. Laboratory testing is not usually necessary. When lesions are unusual or the diagnosis is uncertain, a healthcare professional may examine a sample of a lesion under a microscope or use another appropriate test.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:126:"निदान सामान्यतः चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:430:"Avoid direct skin contact with visible molluscum lesions and do not share towels, clothing, razors, or other personal items that may contact affected skin. Covering lesions when practical can reduce contact with them, and people with genital lesions should discuss sexual precautions with a healthcare professional. Condoms may reduce but cannot completely prevent sexual transmission because uncovered skin can remain infectious.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:118:"प्रत्यक्ष संपर्क से बचना संक्रमण कम करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:333:"Molluscum contagiosum is usually mild and does not generally require emergency care. Seek medical assessment if lesions become painful, extensively inflamed, infected, unusually widespread, or persist longer than expected, or if the diagnosis is uncertain. Prompt evaluation may be appropriate in people with weakened immune systems.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:174;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:182;s:10:"disease_id";i:234;s:11:"overview_en";s:446:"Bed sores, also called pressure injuries or pressure ulcers, are areas of skin and underlying tissue damage caused by prolonged pressure or pressure combined with friction and shear. They commonly develop over bony areas such as the heels, hips, tailbone, elbows, and back of the head. Early pressure injuries may cause persistent redness or discoloration, while more severe injuries can involve deeper tissue and become complicated by infection.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:150:"बेड सोर लंबे समय तक दबाव के कारण होने वाली त्वचा क्षति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:423:"Pressure injuries develop when prolonged pressure compresses tissues against a firm surface and reduces blood flow and oxygen delivery. Friction can damage the outer skin, while shear can cause deeper tissue injury when skin and underlying tissues move in different directions. Moisture, poor nutrition, reduced sensation, impaired circulation, and inability to change position can increase tissue damage and delay healing.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:137:"लंबे समय तक दबाव ऊतकों में रक्त प्रवाह कम कर देता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:386:"Risk factors include limited mobility, prolonged bed or wheelchair use, older age, reduced sensation, paralysis, poor nutrition, dehydration, urinary or fecal incontinence, impaired circulation, and medical conditions that interfere with healing. People who cannot reposition themselves independently or who remain in the same position for prolonged periods are particularly vulnerable.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:137:"अचलता, कुपोषण और पुरानी बीमारियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:494:"Diagnosis is usually made by examining the skin and underlying tissues and determining the location, appearance, extent, and severity of the injury. Pressure injuries are classified according to the depth and characteristics of tissue damage. Healthcare professionals may assess nutrition, circulation, sensation, mobility, and other contributing factors. Laboratory tests, imaging, or other investigations may be required when infection, bone involvement, or deeper tissue damage is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:102:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:468:"Regular repositioning and reducing prolonged pressure are central to preventing pressure injuries. Pressure-relieving mattresses, cushions, and other support surfaces may help people at increased risk. Skin should be inspected regularly, kept clean and dry, and protected from excessive moisture. Adequate nutrition and hydration, maintaining mobility when possible, and using appropriate techniques when moving or transferring a person can further reduce injury risk.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:102:"स्थिति बदलते रहना रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:394:"Bed sores, or pressure ulcers, require medical assessment because they can deepen and become infected. Seek prompt care for increasing redness, swelling, drainage, foul odor, worsening pain, fever, or a wound that is enlarging or becoming deeper. Emergency evaluation is needed for rapidly spreading infection, severe weakness, confusion, fainting, or other signs of serious systemic infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:175;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:183;s:10:"disease_id";i:235;s:11:"overview_en";s:386:"Sunburn is skin damage caused by excessive exposure to ultraviolet radiation from sunlight or other UV sources. It causes red, warm, tender, or painful skin and may produce blisters followed by peeling. Symptoms can develop several hours after exposure and may become more noticeable during the following day. Repeated sunburn increases the risk of premature skin aging and skin cancer.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:169:"सनबर्न अत्यधिक पराबैंगनी किरणों के संपर्क से त्वचा की क्षति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:419:"Sunburn occurs when exposure to ultraviolet radiation exceeds the skin's ability to protect itself with melanin. Both UVA and UVB radiation can damage skin cells. Exposure may come from direct sunlight, reflected sunlight from surfaces such as water or snow, or artificial sources such as tanning lamps. Certain medicines and medical conditions that cause photosensitivity can make the skin more susceptible to sunburn.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:83:"अत्यधिक धूप इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:424:"Risk increases with prolonged or intense UV exposure, especially during periods when the sun is strongest. Infants and children are particularly susceptible, and people with lighter skin generally burn more easily, although darker skin can also develop sunburn and requires protection. High altitude, reflective surfaces, tanning devices, photosensitizing medicines, and conditions such as lupus can increase susceptibility.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:146:"गोरी त्वचा और लंबे समय तक धूप में रहना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:419:"Sunburn is usually diagnosed by examining the affected skin and reviewing the timing and amount of sun or ultraviolet exposure. A healthcare professional may assess redness, tenderness, swelling, blistering, and the extent of the affected area. Severe cases may require evaluation for dehydration, heat illness, infection, or other complications, particularly when extensive blistering or systemic symptoms are present.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:126:"निदान सामान्यतः चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:405:"Sunburn can be reduced by limiting direct sun exposure, especially when UV levels are high, and by seeking shade or wearing protective clothing, a wide-brimmed hat, and UV-protective sunglasses. Use a broad-spectrum sunscreen according to its label and reapply as directed, particularly after swimming or sweating. Avoid tanning beds and sunlamps, which also expose skin to damaging ultraviolet radiation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:142:"सनस्क्रीन और सुरक्षात्मक कपड़े रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:381:"Most sunburns are mild and can be managed with supportive care, but severe burns require medical assessment. Seek prompt care for extensive blistering, severe pain, significant swelling, fever, chills, dehydration, dizziness, or worsening symptoms. Emergency evaluation is needed for confusion, fainting, severe dehydration, difficulty breathing, or other signs of serious illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:176;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:185;s:10:"disease_id";i:237;s:11:"overview_en";s:394:"Rheumatoid arthritis is a chronic autoimmune disease that primarily causes inflammation of the joints. The immune system mistakenly attacks tissues around the joints, leading to pain, swelling, stiffness and reduced movement. It often affects the hands, wrists and feet symmetrically, but can involve other joints and organs. Persistent inflammation can damage joints and affect overall health.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:223:"रूमेटॉइड आर्थराइटिस एक दीर्घकालिक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जो जोड़ों में सूजन पैदा करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:354:"The exact cause of rheumatoid arthritis is unknown. It develops through a combination of genetic susceptibility and environmental influences that affect the immune system. Smoking and certain infections or environmental exposures may contribute to disease development in susceptible people. Hormonal and other immune-related factors may also play a role.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:143:"प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली की गड़बड़ी जोड़ों पर हमला करती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:306:"Risk factors include having certain genetic traits, being female, increasing age and having a family history of rheumatoid arthritis. Smoking is an important modifiable risk factor. Obesity and some environmental exposures may also contribute. The disease can occur in people without any known risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:165:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, धूम्रपान और ऑटोइम्यून रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:343:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, blood tests and imaging. Blood tests may measure rheumatoid factor and anti-CCP antibodies and assess inflammation. X-rays, ultrasound or MRI can show joint inflammation or damage. No single test confirms rheumatoid arthritis in every person, so the overall clinical picture is considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:163:"निदान में रक्त जांच, इमेजिंग और चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:418:"Rheumatoid arthritis cannot always be prevented because genetic and immune factors contribute to its development. Avoiding tobacco use is an important way to reduce risk. Maintaining a healthy weight and addressing other modifiable health factors may also be beneficial. Early medical evaluation of persistent joint swelling and stiffness allows appropriate treatment to begin before significant joint damage develops.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:136:"शीघ्र निदान और उपचार जोड़ों की क्षति कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:421:"Rheumatoid arthritis requires ongoing medical assessment because untreated inflammation can progressively damage joints and affect other organs. Seek prompt care for rapidly worsening joint swelling, severe pain, significant functional decline, or new systemic symptoms. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for chest pain, severe shortness of breath, sudden neurological symptoms, or other potentially serious complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:177;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:186;s:10:"disease_id";i:238;s:11:"overview_en";s:527:"Osteoporosis is a skeletal disorder characterized by reduced bone strength and increased susceptibility to fractures. Bone becomes less dense and its internal structure may deteriorate, making fractures more likely even after relatively minor falls or injuries. Common fracture sites include the hip, spine, and wrist. Osteoporosis can develop without symptoms for many years and may first become apparent when a fracture occurs. Early identification of increased fracture risk can help guide preventive measures and treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:208:"ऑस्टियोपोरोसिस में हड्डियां कमजोर हो जाती हैं और फ्रैक्चर का खतरा बढ़ जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:541:"Osteoporosis develops when bone breakdown occurs faster than new bone formation or when the amount and quality of newly formed bone are insufficient to maintain normal strength. Aging and hormonal changes contribute to bone loss, particularly after menopause. Other contributors include inadequate calcium or vitamin D, low physical activity, smoking, excessive alcohol use, prolonged corticosteroid treatment, and medical conditions that interfere with bone metabolism. Genetic factors also influence peak bone mass and later fracture risk.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:151:"बढ़ती उम्र, हार्मोन परिवर्तन और कैल्शियम की कमी कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:490:"Risk factors include increasing age, menopause and other states of reduced estrogen, a family history of osteoporosis or fragility fractures, low body weight, inadequate calcium or vitamin D, physical inactivity, smoking, excessive alcohol consumption, and prolonged use of medicines such as corticosteroids. Certain endocrine, gastrointestinal, kidney, liver, and inflammatory disorders can also increase risk. Previous fragility fracture is an important indicator of future fracture risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:172:"अधिक आयु, रजोनिवृत्ति, निष्क्रियता और धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:508:"Osteoporosis is commonly assessed using bone mineral density measurement with dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, commonly called a DXA or DEXA scan. The results are interpreted together with age, sex, fracture history, and other clinical risk factors. Blood and urine tests may be used to identify medical conditions that contribute to bone loss. Vertebral imaging may be considered when a spinal fracture is suspected or when clinical risk factors indicate a possibility of previously unrecognized fractures.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1279:"ऑस्टियोपोरोसिस का आकलन आमतौर पर हड्डियों के खनिज घनत्व की जांच से किया जाता है, जिसमें ड्यूल-एनर्जी एक्स-रे एब्जॉर्प्शियोमेट्री यानी DXA स्कैन का उपयोग किया जाता है। परिणाम की व्याख्या उम्र, लिंग, फ्रैक्चर के इतिहास और अन्य चिकित्सकीय कारकों के साथ की जाती है। स्वास्थ्य विशेषज्ञ भविष्य में फ्रैक्चर के जोखिम का भी आकलन कर सकते हैं और जरूरत पड़ने पर उन स्थितियों की जांच के लिए रक्त या मूत्र परीक्षण कर सकते हैं जो हड्डियों को कमजोर करती हैं। फ्रैक्चर की आशंका होने पर इमेजिंग की जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:528:"Bone health can be supported through adequate calcium and vitamin D, regular weight-bearing and muscle-strengthening activity, avoidance of smoking, and limiting excessive alcohol consumption. Maintaining appropriate nutrition and body weight is important, particularly during periods of rapid bone loss. People at increased risk should discuss fracture-risk assessment with a healthcare professional. Measures to reduce falls, such as improving balance and addressing hazards at home, are especially important for older adults.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:132:"पर्याप्त कैल्शियम, विटामिन D और व्यायाम सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:351:"Osteoporosis often has no symptoms until a fracture occurs and generally requires planned medical assessment and prevention. Seek medical care after a suspected fracture or significant new bone pain. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe sudden back pain, inability to bear weight, or symptoms suggesting a major fracture or spinal complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:178;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:187;s:10:"disease_id";i:239;s:11:"overview_en";s:402:"Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis caused by the buildup of uric acid crystals in and around joints. It commonly causes sudden episodes of severe joint pain, swelling, warmth, and redness, often beginning in the big toe but also affecting other joints. Repeated attacks can lead to persistent joint damage and deposits of urate crystals called tophi if the condition is not adequately controlled.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:172:"गाउट एक प्रकार का गठिया है जो यूरिक एसिड क्रिस्टल के कारण होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:453:"Gout develops when uric acid levels in the blood remain high enough for urate crystals to form. High uric acid can result from the body producing too much uric acid or the kidneys not removing enough of it. Diet, alcohol, obesity, kidney disease, certain medicines, and inherited factors can influence uric acid levels. The presence of high uric acid does not always result in gout, but sustained elevation increases the likelihood of crystal formation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:121:"उच्च यूरिक एसिड जोड़ों में क्रिस्टल बनाता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:442:"Risk factors include obesity, kidney disease, high blood pressure, diabetes, metabolic conditions, and a family history of gout. Regular consumption of alcohol, particularly beer, and foods high in purines can increase uric acid levels in susceptible people. Certain medicines, including some diuretics, may also increase risk. The likelihood of gout generally increases with age, particularly in people with persistent high uric acid levels.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:130:"मोटापा, शराब, गुर्दा रोग और आहार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:430:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern of joint symptoms, physical examination, medical history, and laboratory or imaging findings. Blood testing can measure uric acid levels, although a normal level during an acute attack does not completely exclude gout. Examination of joint fluid under a microscope can identify characteristic urate crystals and is an important way to confirm the diagnosis. Imaging may be used in selected cases.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:159:"निदान में यूरिक एसिड जांच और जोड़ों के द्रव की जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:446:"Gout attacks and complications can often be reduced by keeping uric acid levels under control. Maintaining a healthy weight, staying physically active, limiting alcohol, reducing sugary drinks, and moderating foods high in purines such as organ meats and some seafood may help. Adequate fluid intake can also support kidney function. People with recurrent or severe gout may need prescribed urate-lowering treatment and regular medical follow-up.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:715:"गाउट के दोबारा होने के जोखिम को कम करने के लिए स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखें, चिकित्सकीय सलाह के अनुसार शराब और अधिक प्यूरीन वाले खाद्य पदार्थों को सीमित करें, पर्याप्त पानी पिएं, संबंधित रोगों का नियंत्रण रखें और आवश्यकता होने पर निर्धारित यूरिक एसिड कम करने वाली दवाएं नियमित लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:378:"Gout can cause sudden severe joint pain and swelling and should be medically evaluated, particularly when the diagnosis is uncertain. Seek prompt care for a hot, swollen joint with fever because a joint infection can resemble gout and requires urgent treatment. Emergency evaluation is appropriate for severe systemic illness, confusion, fainting, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:179;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:188;s:10:"disease_id";i:240;s:11:"overview_en";s:404:"Osteomyelitis is an infection and inflammation of bone. It may develop when bacteria or other microorganisms reach bone through the bloodstream, spread from a nearby infection, or enter through an open wound or surgery. Symptoms can include localized bone pain, swelling, warmth, redness, fever, and reduced use of the affected area. Prompt diagnosis and treatment are important to prevent complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:103:"ऑस्टियोमायलाइटिस हड्डी का संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:440:"Osteomyelitis is usually caused by bacteria, although other microorganisms can occasionally be responsible. Infection may reach bone through the bloodstream, spread from nearby infected tissue, or enter directly after an open fracture, penetrating injury, surgery, or placement of medical hardware. Staphylococcus aureus is a common cause. The organisms involved and route of infection can vary according to the person and clinical setting.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:92:"जीवाणु संक्रमण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:430:"Risk factors include diabetes, poor circulation, weakened immunity, chronic kidney disease, recent surgery, open fractures, penetrating injuries, pressure sores, and infections near bone. People with implanted orthopedic hardware may also have increased risk when infection develops around the device. Recurrent bloodstream infections and conditions that impair wound healing can further increase susceptibility to bone infection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:131:"मधुमेह, चोट और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:458:"Diagnosis of osteomyelitis is based on symptoms, examination, blood tests, and imaging. Blood tests may show evidence of inflammation or infection. X-rays can identify bone changes, although early infection may not be visible. MRI is particularly useful for evaluating bone and surrounding soft tissues. In selected cases, a sample of bone or infected tissue may be obtained for microbiological testing to identify the causative organism and guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:126:"निदान में इमेजिंग, रक्त जांच और कल्चर शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:462:"Preventing osteomyelitis involves reducing infection and protecting wounds. Prompt cleaning and appropriate medical care of deep wounds, punctures, open fractures, and surgical sites can reduce the chance of infection reaching bone. Good control of diabetes and other chronic conditions can support healing. People with recurrent infections, poor circulation, or weakened immunity may require particular attention to wound care and early treatment of infections.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:115:"संक्रमण का शीघ्र उपचार रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:404:"Osteomyelitis is a bone infection that requires prompt medical assessment and treatment. Seek care for persistent bone pain, swelling, redness, drainage, fever, or a wound that is not healing, particularly when infection may have spread from nearby tissue. Emergency evaluation is needed for rapidly worsening infection, severe weakness, confusion, fainting, or other signs of serious systemic infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:180;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:189;s:10:"disease_id";i:241;s:11:"overview_en";s:401:"Paget disease of bone is a chronic disorder in which the normal process of bone breakdown and rebuilding becomes abnormal. Affected bones may become enlarged, misshapen, weaker, and more prone to fracture. The disease often affects one or a few bones and may cause no symptoms. When symptoms occur, they may include bone pain, arthritis, hearing problems, or deformity depending on the bones involved.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:195:"पेजेट डिजीज ऑफ बोन हड्डियों के पुनर्निर्माण को प्रभावित करने वाला रोग है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:427:"The exact cause of Paget disease of bone is not fully understood. Both genetic and environmental factors may contribute. Some people with the condition have close relatives with Paget disease, and variants in genes involved in bone remodeling have been associated with susceptibility. The disease results from abnormal activity of cells responsible for breaking down and rebuilding bone, leading to disorganized bone formation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:135:"सटीक कारण अज्ञात है, लेकिन आनुवंशिक कारण जुड़े हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:363:"Paget disease of bone is more common with increasing age and is more frequently reported in people of certain European ancestry. Having a close family member with Paget disease increases the likelihood of developing the condition. The disease can occur without a known family history, and many affected people have no obvious symptoms when it is first discovered.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:124:"अधिक आयु और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:430:"Diagnosis may involve a medical history, physical examination, blood tests, and imaging. An elevated alkaline phosphatase level can provide evidence of increased bone activity. X-rays are commonly used to identify characteristic changes in affected bones, while a bone scan can show which areas are involved. Additional imaging or biopsy may be considered when the diagnosis is uncertain or another bone disorder must be excluded.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:106:"निदान में रक्त जांच और इमेजिंग शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:535:"Paget disease of bone cannot currently be prevented because its underlying causes are not completely understood. Early detection and appropriate medical management can reduce the risk of complications in people who develop the condition. Maintaining adequate calcium and vitamin D intake when appropriate, staying physically active within safe limits, and avoiding excessive stress on affected bones can support overall bone health. Exercise plans should be discussed with a healthcare professional when bones are weakened or deformed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:100:"शीघ्र पहचान जटिलताओं को कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:335:"Paget disease of bone is usually chronic and is not generally an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent bone pain, deformity, changes in hearing, neurological symptoms, or other new problems. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe pain, inability to bear weight, new neurological deficits, or suspected fracture.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:181;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:190;s:10:"disease_id";i:242;s:11:"overview_en";s:512:"Bone cancer refers to malignant tumors that originate in bone tissue. Primary bone cancers are relatively uncommon and differ from cancers that begin elsewhere in the body and spread to bone. Symptoms may include persistent localized bone pain, swelling, tenderness, or reduced function, although early disease may not cause obvious symptoms. Different types have different biological behavior and commonly affect particular age groups and locations. Evaluation and treatment depend on the tumor type and extent.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:158:"बोन कैंसर हड्डी के ऊतकों में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:524:"Primary bone cancer results from abnormal genetic and cellular changes that cause bone cells to grow uncontrollably and form a malignant tumor. The exact initiating cause is often unknown. Different tumor types arise from different cell lineages and have distinct biological characteristics. Some inherited conditions, previous radiation exposure, and certain bone disorders are associated with increased risk for particular types of primary bone cancer. Cancer that spreads to bone from another organ is a separate process.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:145:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन और असामान्य कोशिका वृद्धि कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:516:"Risk factors depend on the specific type of bone cancer. Certain inherited cancer syndromes and genetic conditions are associated with increased risk of particular tumors. Previous radiation exposure can increase the risk of some bone cancers. Certain pre-existing bone disorders are also associated with particular tumor types. Most people who develop primary bone cancer do not have an identifiable preventable risk factor, and the condition is not generally caused by ordinary physical activity or minor injuries.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:117:"कुछ आनुवंशिक स्थितियां जोखिम बढ़ा सकती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:475:"Evaluation commonly begins with a history and physical examination followed by imaging of the affected area. X-rays can identify many bone tumors and may show changes in bone structure. Magnetic resonance imaging can define the local extent of a lesion and its relationship to nearby tissues. A biopsy is generally required to establish the specific diagnosis. Additional imaging or tests may be used to determine whether the tumor has spread and to guide treatment planning.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:105:"निदान में इमेजिंग और बायोप्सी शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:526:"There is no established way to prevent most primary bone cancers because their causes are often unknown and many recognized risk factors cannot be modified. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to ionizing radiation and appropriately managing medical conditions associated with specific bone tumors may reduce certain risks. People with known inherited cancer syndromes or relevant bone disorders may benefit from specialist monitoring. Persistent unexplained bone pain, swelling, or a growing mass should receive medical evaluation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:105:"शीघ्र निदान उपचार परिणाम बेहतर करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:355:"Bone cancer requires prompt medical evaluation when persistent or unexplained bone pain, swelling, a new lump, or an unexplained fracture occurs. Seek assessment for symptoms that persist or progressively worsen. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe new pain, rapidly enlarging swelling, inability to use an affected limb, or neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:182;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:191;s:10:"disease_id";i:243;s:11:"overview_en";s:330:"Osteosarcoma is a type of bone cancer that develops from cells involved in bone formation. It most often occurs in children, adolescents, and young adults and commonly affects the long bones near the knee or upper arm. Symptoms may include persistent bone pain, swelling, tenderness, or a weakened bone that fractures more easily.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:198:"ऑस्टियोसारकोमा एक प्राथमिक हड्डी कैंसर है जो युवाओं में अधिक पाया जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:396:"The exact cause of osteosarcoma is not known in most cases. Cancer develops when bone-forming cells acquire genetic changes that cause uncontrolled growth. Most cases occur without a clearly identifiable inherited cause. A small number are associated with inherited cancer-predisposition syndromes or previous exposure to radiation. Some genetic abnormalities have been identified in tumor cells.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1166:"ऑस्टियोसारकोमा तब विकसित होता है जब हड्डी की कोशिकाओं में ऐसे असामान्य परिवर्तन हो जाते हैं जिनसे उनकी अनियंत्रित वृद्धि होने लगती है। अधिकांश लोगों में इन परिवर्तनों का सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं होता। कुछ मामले वंशानुगत कैंसर-जोखिम वाली स्थितियों या पहले उच्च-खुराक विकिरण के संपर्क से जुड़े हो सकते हैं। ऑस्टियोसारकोमा सामान्यतः चोट या सामान्य शारीरिक गतिविधि के कारण नहीं होता और अधिकांश रोगियों में कोई स्पष्ट रोकथाम योग्य कारण नहीं मिलता।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:390:"Osteosarcoma is more common during periods of rapid bone growth, particularly in adolescence. Risk may be increased by certain inherited cancer syndromes, a family history of particular hereditary conditions, and previous radiation exposure. Most people who develop osteosarcoma do not have an identifiable risk factor, and ordinary injuries or physical activity are not established causes.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:144:"तेजी से हड्डी वृद्धि और आनुवंशिक रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:421:"Diagnosis generally involves imaging followed by biopsy when a bone tumor is suspected. X-rays may show characteristic changes, while MRI helps assess the local extent of the tumor. CT scans of the chest and other imaging may be used to look for spread. A biopsy provides tissue for microscopic examination and confirms the diagnosis. Specialist evaluation is important because biopsy planning can affect later treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:111:"निदान हेतु इमेजिंग और बायोप्सी आवश्यक है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:432:"There is no established way to prevent most cases of osteosarcoma because the cause is usually unknown. People with known hereditary cancer syndromes may benefit from appropriate genetic counseling and medical surveillance. Previous radiation exposure should be medically justified and minimized when possible. Persistent bone pain, swelling, or unexplained masses should receive timely medical evaluation rather than being ignored.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1149:"ऑस्टियोसारकोमा के अधिकांश मामलों से बचाव का कोई स्थापित तरीका नहीं है क्योंकि यह रोग आमतौर पर बिना किसी ज्ञात रोकथाम योग्य कारण के विकसित होता है। कुछ आनुवंशिक स्थितियां जोखिम बढ़ा सकती हैं, लेकिन उन्हें सामान्यतः रोका नहीं जा सकता। कुछ वंशानुगत कैंसर सिंड्रोम वाले लोगों को उचित आनुवंशिक परामर्श और चिकित्सकीय निगरानी से लाभ हो सकता है। अनावश्यक उच्च-खुराक विकिरण से बचना उचित है, हालांकि विकिरण से संबंधित ऑस्टियोसारकोमा दुर्लभ है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:380:"Osteosarcoma requires prompt specialist evaluation when persistent bone pain, swelling, or an unexplained mass is present, particularly in children and young adults. Seek medical assessment for symptoms that do not resolve or progressively worsen. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe pain, rapidly increasing swelling, inability to bear weight, or an unexplained fracture.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:183;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:192;s:10:"disease_id";i:244;s:11:"overview_en";s:379:"Ewing sarcoma is a rare cancer that develops in bone or soft tissue. It most often affects children, adolescents, and young adults and commonly occurs in the pelvis, thigh bones, ribs, or other bones. Symptoms may include localized pain, swelling, tenderness, or stiffness, and some tumors can cause a noticeable mass. The disease can also arise in soft tissues outside the bone.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:160:"ईविंग सारकोमा हड्डियों या आसपास के ऊतकों का दुर्लभ कैंसर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:382:"Ewing sarcoma is associated with acquired genetic changes in tumor cells. A characteristic abnormal rearrangement involving chromosome 11 and chromosome 22 can produce an EWSR1-related fusion gene, most commonly involving FLI1. These genetic changes develop during a person's lifetime and are generally not inherited from a parent. The exact reason these changes occur is not known.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:149:"आनुवंशिक असामान्यताएं रोग के विकास में योगदान करती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:338:"Ewing sarcoma most often occurs in children, adolescents, and young adults, with cases being more common in younger people than in older adults. It is somewhat more common in males. Unlike some other cancers, there are no well-established lifestyle-related risk factors that can be used to reliably predict who will develop Ewing sarcoma.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:102:"बच्चे और किशोर अधिक प्रभावित होते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:403:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and physical examination, followed by imaging of the suspected area. X-rays, MRI, CT, bone scans, or PET imaging may be used to evaluate the tumor and determine whether it has spread. A biopsy of the tumor is required to establish the diagnosis. Laboratory and molecular testing of tumor tissue can help confirm Ewing sarcoma and distinguish it from other tumors.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:105:"निदान में इमेजिंग और बायोप्सी शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:420:"There is no established way to prevent Ewing sarcoma because its known genetic changes usually arise spontaneously in tumor cells and are not linked to a preventable lifestyle exposure. Early evaluation of persistent or unexplained bone pain, swelling, or a growing mass can help identify serious conditions sooner. Follow-up and specialist assessment are important when symptoms persist or imaging shows an abnormality.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:89:"शीघ्र निदान बेहतर परिणाम देता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:379:"Ewing sarcoma requires prompt medical evaluation for persistent bone or soft-tissue pain, swelling, or an unexplained mass, particularly in children and young adults. Seek assessment when symptoms persist or worsen. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe pain, rapidly enlarging swelling, inability to use an affected limb, neurological symptoms, or an unexplained fracture.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:184;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:193;s:10:"disease_id";i:245;s:11:"overview_en";s:353:"Ankylosing spondylitis is a chronic inflammatory condition that mainly affects the spine and the joints connecting the spine and pelvis. It commonly causes lower back or hip pain and stiffness that may worsen after periods of rest and improve with movement. In some people, inflammation can also affect other joints, the eyes, skin, or digestive system.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:154:"एंकिलोसिंग स्पॉन्डिलाइटिस रीढ़ की सूजन संबंधी बीमारी है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:348:"The exact cause of ankylosing spondylitis is unknown. Genetic and environmental factors appear to contribute. The HLA-B27 gene is strongly associated with the condition, although many people who carry this gene never develop ankylosing spondylitis. Other genetic variations and environmental influences may also affect whether the disease develops.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:117:"ऑटोइम्यून और आनुवंशिक कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:332:"Risk factors include a family history of ankylosing spondylitis and genetic susceptibility, particularly the HLA-B27 gene. Symptoms commonly begin before age 45. People with inflammatory bowel diseases such as Crohn disease or ulcerative colitis, or with psoriasis, may also have increased risk of developing ankylosing spondylitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:109:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और HLA-B27 जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:365:"Diagnosis of ankylosing spondylitis is based on symptoms, physical examination, medical history, and imaging. X-rays may show changes in the sacroiliac joints or spine, while MRI can detect inflammation earlier in the disease. Blood tests may include markers such as C-reactive protein and testing for HLA-B27. No single test confirms the condition in every person.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:139:"निदान में इमेजिंग और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:415:"Ankylosing spondylitis cannot currently be prevented because its exact cause is unknown and genetic factors play an important role. People with a strong family history or persistent inflammatory back symptoms should seek medical evaluation. Early diagnosis and appropriate management, including regular physical activity and exercises recommended by healthcare professionals, can help maintain mobility and posture.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:127:"नियमित व्यायाम गतिशीलता बनाए रखने में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:380:"Ankylosing spondylitis is a chronic inflammatory condition that generally requires ongoing medical care rather than emergency treatment. Seek assessment for persistent inflammatory back pain, stiffness, reduced mobility, or worsening symptoms. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe pain, significant neurological symptoms, chest symptoms, or new eye pain and redness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:185;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:194;s:10:"disease_id";i:246;s:11:"overview_en";s:338:"Juvenile arthritis, commonly called juvenile idiopathic arthritis, is a group of chronic inflammatory disorders that begin during childhood. It can cause joint pain, swelling, stiffness, and reduced movement. Some forms may also cause fever, rash, growth problems, or inflammation of the eyes. The course and severity vary among children.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"जुवेनाइल आर्थराइटिस 16 वर्ष से कम आयु के बच्चों में होने वाला गठिया है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:376:"The cause of juvenile idiopathic arthritis is not fully understood. It is believed to involve an abnormal immune response in which the immune system attacks healthy tissues. Genetic susceptibility and environmental factors may contribute. Different forms affect different numbers of joints and may produce additional systemic symptoms such as fever, rash, or eye inflammation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:94:"ऑटोइम्यून गड़बड़ी सामान्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:357:"Juvenile idiopathic arthritis develops in children and adolescents, generally before age 16. A family history of autoimmune or inflammatory conditions may indicate increased susceptibility, although many affected children have no identifiable risk factor. The condition is not caused by a child being physically active or by ordinary injuries to the joints.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और ऑटोइम्यून रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"Juvenile idiopathic arthritis is diagnosed from persistent joint inflammation and symptoms beginning in childhood after other causes have been considered. Examination may show swollen, warm, or tender joints and reduced movement. Blood tests such as ESR, CRP, ANA, rheumatoid factor, and other studies may help assess inflammation or classify disease, but no single blood test confirms JIA.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:132:"निदान में परीक्षण, रक्त जांच और इमेजिंग शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:418:"There is no known way to prevent juvenile idiopathic arthritis. Early recognition of persistent joint swelling, stiffness, pain, or unexplained fever allows appropriate evaluation and management. Children with JIA benefit from maintaining suitable physical activity and joint mobility under medical guidance. Regular eye examinations may also be recommended because eye inflammation can occur without obvious symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:115:"शीघ्र उपचार जटिलताओं को रोकने में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:393:"Juvenile arthritis requires medical assessment and ongoing management because persistent inflammation can affect joints, growth, and other organs. Seek prompt care for worsening joint swelling, significant pain, reduced movement, fever, or functional decline. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe systemic illness, significant eye symptoms, or sudden neurological or breathing problems.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:186;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:195;s:10:"disease_id";i:247;s:11:"overview_en";s:426:"Psoriatic arthritis is an inflammatory form of arthritis associated with psoriasis, a condition that affects the skin and may also affect the nails. It can cause pain, stiffness, swelling, and reduced movement in affected joints. The disease may involve different joints and can affect the fingers, toes, spine, or other areas. Symptoms may vary over time, with periods of increased inflammation and periods of fewer symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:160:"सोरियाटिक आर्थराइटिस सोरायसिस से जुड़ा सूजनयुक्त गठिया है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:489:"Psoriatic arthritis is related to abnormal activity of the immune system, which causes inflammation in the joints and surrounding tissues. The exact reason this immune response develops is not fully understood. Genetic susceptibility may contribute, and environmental or other triggers may influence the development of the condition. Psoriatic arthritis can occur in people with psoriasis, although the severity of skin disease does not always correspond to the severity of joint symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"प्रतिरक्षा प्रणाली की गड़बड़ी जोड़ों में सूजन पैदा करती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:460:"Having psoriasis is an important risk factor for psoriatic arthritis. A family history of psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis may increase susceptibility because genetic factors can influence the immune response. Other autoimmune or inflammatory conditions may also be associated with increased risk. People with psoriasis who develop persistent joint pain, swelling, stiffness, or changes in movement should discuss these symptoms with a healthcare professional.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:165:"सोरायसिस, पारिवारिक इतिहास और ऑटोइम्यून रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:491:"Diagnosis of psoriatic arthritis is based on the pattern of joint symptoms, physical examination, medical history, and evidence of psoriasis or related skin and nail changes. Imaging studies such as X-rays, ultrasound, or magnetic resonance imaging may help identify inflammation and joint damage. Blood tests can help evaluate inflammation and may be used to help distinguish psoriatic arthritis from other types of arthritis. There is no single test that independently confirms every case.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:132:"निदान में परीक्षण, इमेजिंग और रक्त जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:513:"Psoriatic arthritis cannot always be prevented because its exact cause is not fully understood. Managing psoriasis and maintaining regular medical care may help identify joint symptoms at an early stage. Regular physical activity can help maintain joint movement and general fitness, while maintaining a healthy weight may reduce stress on weight-bearing joints. Protecting the joints from unnecessary injury and seeking medical evaluation for persistent pain, swelling, or stiffness can support early management.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:110:"शीघ्र उपचार जोड़ों की क्षति कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:410:"Psoriatic arthritis requires medical assessment and ongoing treatment because persistent inflammation can damage joints and affect function. Seek prompt care for worsening joint swelling, pain, stiffness, or reduced mobility. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for a suddenly hot and severely swollen joint, significant eye pain or redness, severe systemic symptoms, or sudden neurological or breathing problems.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:38:12";}i:187;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:196;s:10:"disease_id";i:248;s:11:"overview_en";s:334:"Reactive arthritis is a form of joint inflammation that develops after an infection elsewhere in the body, most often involving the digestive or urinary or genital tract. It can cause joint pain, swelling, and stiffness and may sometimes affect the eyes or urinary system. Symptoms may begin after the original infection has improved.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:182:"रिएक्टिव आर्थराइटिस शरीर में अन्य संक्रमण के बाद होने वाला गठिया है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:432:"Reactive arthritis usually develops after an infection, particularly an infection involving the gastrointestinal tract or the urinary or genital tract. The joint inflammation is thought to result from an abnormal immune response that continues after the original infection. Common triggering infections can include certain bacterial infections, although not everyone who develops one of these infections develops reactive arthritis.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:117:"आमतौर पर आंत या मूत्र संक्रमण के बाद होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:425:"Risk factors for reactive arthritis include a recent gastrointestinal or urinary or genital infection and genetic susceptibility. Certain inherited immune-system characteristics may make some people more likely to develop the condition after an infection. A history of infections that can trigger reactive arthritis may therefore increase risk, although most people with these infections do not necessarily develop arthritis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:148:"हालिया संक्रमण और आनुवंशिक प्रवृत्ति जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:375:"Diagnosis of reactive arthritis is based on the pattern of joint symptoms, physical examination, and evidence of a recent infection. Blood tests may help assess inflammation or identify other conditions that can cause similar symptoms. Testing for infections may be performed when appropriate, and imaging or examination of affected joints can provide additional information.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:135:"निदान लक्षणों, जांच और संक्रमण इतिहास पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:410:"Reactive arthritis cannot always be prevented, but reducing infections that can trigger it may lower risk. Practicing safer sex, including appropriate barrier protection, can help reduce sexually transmitted infections such as chlamydia. Good food safety and hand hygiene can reduce gastrointestinal infections. Prompt evaluation and appropriate treatment of suspected infections may also reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1307:"रिएक्टिव आर्थराइटिस अक्सर किसी संक्रमण के बाद होता है, इसलिए इसे ट्रिगर करने वाले संक्रमणों को कम करने से जोखिम घट सकता है। सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार और उचित barrier protection से क्लैमाइडिया जैसे यौन संचारित संक्रमणों का जोखिम कम किया जा सकता है। अच्छी खाद्य स्वच्छता और हाथों की स्वच्छता से रिएक्टिव आर्थराइटिस से जुड़े कुछ जठरांत्र संक्रमणों को कम किया जा सकता है। संदिग्ध संक्रमण का समय पर मूल्यांकन और उपचार जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकता है, हालांकि रिएक्टिव आर्थराइटिस के हर मामले को रोका नहीं जा सकता।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:412:"Reactive arthritis should be medically assessed when joint pain, swelling, stiffness, or inflammation persists or worsens, particularly when symptoms follow an infection. Seek prompt care for a severely swollen or painful joint, fever, significant difficulty walking, or worsening symptoms. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe eye symptoms, chest symptoms, or other signs of significant systemic illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:188;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:197;s:10:"disease_id";i:249;s:11:"overview_en";s:568:"Bursitis is inflammation or irritation of a bursa, a small fluid-filled sac that cushions tissues around joints and reduces friction during movement. It commonly affects the shoulder, elbow, hip, knee, or heel. Repetitive movement, prolonged pressure, injury, infection, or inflammatory conditions may contribute. Symptoms usually include localized pain, tenderness, swelling, and discomfort with movement or pressure. Treatment depends on the cause and may include activity modification, physical therapy, medicines, drainage, or treatment of an underlying condition.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:138:"बर्साइटिस जोड़ों के आसपास की तरल थैलियों की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:532:"Bursitis can result from repeated pressure, friction, or movement involving a joint. Activities that require frequent kneeling, leaning on the elbows, throwing, lifting, or repetitive shoulder movements can irritate a bursa. Direct trauma can also cause inflammation. Bursae may become inflamed in people with conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis or gout. In some cases, bacteria enter a bursa and cause septic bursitis, which requires prompt medical treatment. The underlying cause determines the appropriate treatment approach.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:114:"अधिक उपयोग, चोट या संक्रमण कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:544:"Risk factors for bursitis include repetitive joint movements, prolonged pressure on a joint, occupations or sports involving repetitive activity, direct trauma, increasing age, and inflammatory diseases such as rheumatoid arthritis or gout. Infection can cause septic bursitis, particularly when bacteria enter through damaged skin. Previous bursitis may increase the likelihood of recurrence if the activity or underlying condition continues. Proper technique, gradual conditioning, and protection from repeated pressure may reduce some risks.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:170:"बार-बार होने वाली गतिविधियां और जोड़ों पर दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:517:"Bursitis is usually diagnosed through history and physical examination. The location of pain, tenderness, swelling, movement-related symptoms, and recent activities help identify the affected bursa. Imaging such as ultrasound or MRI may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain or another injury is suspected. If the bursa is significantly swollen or infection is suspected, fluid may be removed with a needle for laboratory analysis. Fever, redness, warmth, or rapidly increasing swelling can suggest septic bursitis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:118:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण और इमेजिंग से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:571:"Bursitis risk can sometimes be reduced by avoiding prolonged pressure on joints, using protective padding when kneeling or leaning, taking breaks during repetitive activities, and gradually increasing exercise intensity. Proper technique and conditioning can reduce excessive stress on joints and surrounding tissues. Treating underlying inflammatory diseases may also reduce recurrence. Cuts or skin infections near a bursa should be managed appropriately because bacteria can enter the bursa. Persistent swelling, warmth, redness, or fever should be evaluated promptly.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:130:"अत्यधिक दोहराव वाली गतिविधियों से बचाव सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:320:"Bursitis is usually not an emergency and often improves with appropriate care. Seek medical assessment if pain or swelling persists, recurs, or worsens despite treatment. Prompt evaluation is important when a bursa becomes very red, hot, increasingly painful, or is accompanied by fever because infection may be present.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:189;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:198;s:10:"disease_id";i:250;s:11:"overview_en";s:346:"Synovitis is inflammation of the synovial lining of a joint, which can cause swelling, pain, warmth, stiffness, and reduced movement. It may develop after an injury or repeated joint stress, or as part of infection, autoimmune arthritis, crystal disease, or another inflammatory condition. Treatment and evaluation depend on the underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:136:"साइनोवाइटिस जोड़ों की साइनोवियल झिल्ली की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:448:"Synovitis may result from an injury, repetitive overuse, infection, autoimmune arthritis, crystal disease, or another inflammatory joint condition. These causes can irritate the synovial lining and lead to increased fluid production and inflammation inside the joint. Identifying the underlying cause is important because treatment differs depending on whether the inflammation is related to injury, infection, crystals, or an inflammatory disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:117:"चोट, गठिया और ऑटोइम्यून रोग कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:407:"Risk depends on the underlying cause of synovitis. Repetitive joint stress, previous joint injuries, inflammatory arthritis, infection, crystal disease, and some metabolic disorders can increase the likelihood of inflammation. People with conditions that affect the joints or immune system may therefore have a greater risk, while the specific risk factors vary according to the type and cause of synovitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:132:"जोड़ों की चोट और सूजन संबंधी रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:425:"Diagnosis of synovitis is based on symptoms and examination of the affected joint, including assessment of swelling, warmth, tenderness, stiffness, and movement. Imaging such as X-rays, ultrasound, or MRI may help identify structural or inflammatory changes. Blood tests may be useful when an inflammatory disease is suspected. Joint-fluid analysis may be performed when infection or crystal disease needs to be investigated.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:153:"निदान परीक्षण, इमेजिंग और प्रयोगशाला जांच द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:436:"Prevention of synovitis depends on its underlying cause. Protecting joints from repetitive strain, using appropriate techniques during physical activity, and allowing adequate recovery after strenuous activity may reduce irritation. Prompt and appropriate treatment of joint injuries and infections can also help. People with inflammatory or metabolic conditions should follow their treatment plans and maintain healthy activity levels.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:93:"शीघ्र उपचार जटिलताएं कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:334:"Synovitis should be medically assessed when joint swelling, pain, stiffness, or reduced movement persists or worsens. Seek prompt care for a suddenly hot, very swollen, or severely painful joint, especially when accompanied by fever, because joint infection may need to be excluded. Severe systemic illness requires urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:190;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:199;s:10:"disease_id";i:251;s:11:"overview_en";s:545:"Avascular necrosis, also called osteonecrosis, occurs when reduced blood supply causes bone tissue to die. It most often affects the hip but can involve other joints such as the knee, shoulder, or ankle. Early disease may cause no symptoms, while progressive damage can produce persistent pain, stiffness, reduced movement, and eventually collapse of the affected bone or joint surface. The condition may develop gradually and can be associated with injury, certain medicines, medical conditions, or other factors that impair blood flow to bone.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:227:"एवस्कुलर नेक्रोसिस में हड्डी को रक्त आपूर्ति कम होने से हड्डी क्षतिग्रस्त हो जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:528:"Avascular necrosis develops when the blood supply to a portion of bone is reduced or interrupted for a prolonged period. Without adequate oxygen and nutrients, bone cells can die and the affected area may gradually weaken and collapse. Causes include traumatic injury that damages blood vessels, prolonged or high-dose corticosteroid exposure, heavy alcohol use, and certain medical conditions affecting blood vessels or blood clotting. In some people, no definite cause is identified and the condition is considered idiopathic.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:116:"हड्डी में रक्त प्रवाह कम होना मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:500:"Risk factors include prolonged or high-dose corticosteroid use, heavy alcohol consumption, previous fractures or joint trauma, and certain medical conditions affecting blood vessels or blood clotting. Associations have also been reported with disorders such as sickle cell disease, lupus, certain metabolic disorders, and some organ-transplant or cancer-related conditions. The risk varies according to the underlying cause, duration of exposure, and the location and extent of impaired blood supply.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:124:"स्टेरॉयड, शराब, चोट और कुछ रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:497:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, medical history, and imaging of the affected bone. X-rays may appear normal in early disease, while magnetic resonance imaging can detect changes at an earlier stage. Additional imaging may help determine the extent of bone damage or joint collapse. Blood tests and other investigations may be used to identify an underlying condition or contributing cause, particularly when disease occurs at an unusual age or without an obvious risk factor.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:136:"निदान MRI, एक्स-रे और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:525:"Some cases of avascular necrosis cannot be prevented, particularly when an underlying medical condition is responsible. Risk may be reduced by avoiding excessive alcohol consumption, using corticosteroids only as medically indicated, and discussing long-term corticosteroid exposure with a healthcare professional. Prompt assessment after significant joint or bone injury may be appropriate. People with medical disorders associated with osteonecrosis may benefit from appropriate management and monitoring for complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1337:"एवैस्कुलर नेक्रोसिस को हमेशा रोका नहीं जा सकता, लेकिन ज्ञात जोखिम कारकों को कम करने से इसकी संभावना घट सकती है। अत्यधिक शराब के सेवन से बचना और धूम्रपान न करना उपयोगी हो सकता है। लंबे समय तक कॉर्टिकोस्टेरॉइड लेने वाले लोगों को चिकित्सकीय निगरानी में प्रभावी न्यूनतम खुराक का उपयोग करना चाहिए। रक्त प्रवाह या रक्त के थक्के बनने को प्रभावित करने वाली स्थितियों का उचित उपचार किया जाना चाहिए। जिन लोगों में महत्वपूर्ण जोखिम कारक हैं, उन्हें लक्षणों और निगरानी के बारे में स्वास्थ्य विशेषज्ञ से सलाह लेनी चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:370:"Avascular necrosis requires medical assessment because progressive loss of blood supply can damage bone and eventually impair joint function. Seek prompt care for persistent or worsening joint pain, reduced movement, or difficulty bearing weight. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe pain, inability to use the affected limb, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:191;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:200;s:10:"disease_id";i:252;s:11:"overview_en";s:305:"Osteopenia occurs when bone mineral density is lower than normal but not low enough to meet the definition of osteoporosis. It indicates reduced bone strength and may increase the risk of future bone loss and fractures. Bone density can decrease gradually without causing symptoms until a fracture occurs.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:163:"ऑस्टियोपेनिया में हड्डियों का घनत्व सामान्य से कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:380:"Osteopenia develops when bone breakdown exceeds new bone formation over time, causing bone mineral density to decrease. Aging and hormonal changes are common contributors. Inadequate calcium or vitamin D, physical inactivity, smoking, excessive alcohol use, certain medicines such as long-term corticosteroids, and medical conditions affecting bone metabolism can also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:135:"बढ़ती उम्र, खराब पोषण और हार्मोन परिवर्तन कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:326:"Risk increases with advancing age, menopause and other hormonal changes, family history of osteoporosis or fractures, low body weight, smoking, excessive alcohol use, physical inactivity, inadequate calcium or vitamin D, long-term corticosteroid use, and certain chronic diseases that affect bone formation or mineral balance.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:146:"कम कैल्शियम, निष्क्रियता और धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:391:"Osteopenia is generally identified using bone mineral density measurement, most commonly a dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry or DXA scan. The result is interpreted together with age, sex, medical history, and fracture risk. Blood or urine tests may be performed when there is concern about vitamin deficiencies, hormonal disorders, medication effects, or another secondary cause of bone loss.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:103:"निदान बोन डेंसिटी जांच से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:427:"Bone health can be supported through regular weight-bearing and muscle-strengthening exercise, adequate calcium and vitamin D, avoiding smoking, limiting excessive alcohol, and maintaining a healthy body weight. Preventing falls is also important, particularly in older adults. People taking medicines that affect bone health or who have other risk factors should discuss bone-density assessment with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:83:"उचित पोषण और व्यायाम सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:305:"Osteopenia is usually not an emergency and often causes no symptoms. Seek medical assessment for bone-health evaluation and fracture-risk assessment, particularly after a low-impact injury or unexplained fracture. Prompt care is appropriate for sudden severe bone or back pain or inability to bear weight.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:192;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:201;s:10:"disease_id";i:253;s:11:"overview_en";s:345:"Rickets is a disorder of growing bones in children caused by inadequate mineralization of developing bone. Vitamin D deficiency is a common cause, although inadequate calcium or phosphate and disorders affecting their absorption or metabolism can also contribute. Rickets may cause bone pain, weakness, growth problems, and skeletal deformities.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:186:"रिकेट्स बच्चों में होने वाला रोग है जिसमें हड्डियां कमजोर हो जाती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:355:"Rickets can result from insufficient vitamin D, which is needed for normal absorption and use of calcium and phosphate. Inadequate dietary calcium or phosphate can also contribute. Other causes include intestinal malabsorption, kidney disorders, certain medicines, and inherited conditions that interfere with vitamin D metabolism or phosphate regulation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:134:"विटामिन D, कैल्शियम या फॉस्फेट की कमी इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:374:"Risk factors include inadequate dietary vitamin D or calcium, limited sunlight exposure, poor nutrition, malabsorption disorders, darker skin pigmentation in settings with limited vitamin D availability, certain medicines, and medical conditions affecting the liver, kidneys, or mineral metabolism. Infants and children with inadequate nutrition are particularly vulnerable.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:107:"खराब पोषण और धूप की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:405:"Diagnosis is based on clinical findings together with laboratory and imaging studies. Blood tests may measure vitamin D, calcium, phosphate, alkaline phosphatase, and other markers of mineral metabolism. X-rays can show characteristic changes in affected bones. Additional testing may be needed when an inherited disorder, kidney problem, malabsorption condition, or another underlying cause is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:111:"निदान रक्त जांच और एक्स-रे से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:404:"Adequate vitamin D, calcium, and overall nutrition during childhood help support normal bone mineralization. Children should receive appropriate nutrition and vitamin D according to age and medical guidance. Children at increased risk because of malabsorption, limited dietary intake, or other medical conditions may need supplementation and monitoring under the supervision of a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:126:"पर्याप्त विटामिन D और पोषण रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:337:"Rickets requires medical evaluation because impaired bone mineralization can affect growth and skeletal strength. Seek prompt care for significant bone pain, weakness, difficulty walking, deformity, or worsening symptoms. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe pain, suspected fracture, seizures, or other significant complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:193;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:202;s:10:"disease_id";i:254;s:11:"overview_en";s:330:"Osteomalacia is a disorder in which bones become soft and weak because they do not mineralize normally. It is most often related to inadequate vitamin D, which is needed for the body to absorb calcium and maintain healthy bones. Osteomalacia can cause bone pain, muscle weakness, difficulty walking, and fractures in severe cases.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:120:"ऑस्टियोमलेशिया में हड्डियां नरम हो जाती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:422:"Osteomalacia most often results from vitamin D deficiency, which reduces calcium and phosphate absorption and interferes with normal bone mineralization. Causes may include inadequate sunlight exposure, insufficient dietary vitamin D, problems absorbing nutrients, certain kidney or liver disorders, and medicines that interfere with vitamin D metabolism. Rare inherited or metabolic disorders can also cause osteomalacia.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:85:"विटामिन D की कमी सामान्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:362:"Risk of osteomalacia increases with inadequate vitamin D intake or sunlight exposure, conditions that interfere with absorption of nutrients, chronic kidney or liver disease, and certain medicines that affect vitamin D metabolism. Older adults and people with limited outdoor activity may also be at increased risk. Risk varies according to the underlying cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:148:"कुपोषण, अवशोषण की समस्या और गुर्दा रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:360:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history, physical examination, and blood tests that assess vitamin D, calcium, phosphate, and related measures. X-rays or other bone imaging may show changes associated with poor mineralization. In selected cases, additional testing may be used to identify an underlying metabolic, kidney, liver, or intestinal disorder.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:112:"निदान रक्त जांच और इमेजिंग द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:372:"Some causes of osteomalacia can be prevented or reduced by getting adequate vitamin D, calcium, and other nutrients through diet or appropriate supplements. Safe exposure to sunlight may help the body produce vitamin D. People with conditions that interfere with absorption or vitamin D metabolism should follow medical advice and have deficiencies identified and treated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:97:"विटामिन D पूरकता रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:352:"Osteomalacia should be medically assessed because impaired bone mineralization can cause bone pain, weakness, and fractures. Seek prompt care for worsening bone pain, difficulty walking, muscle weakness, or suspected fracture. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for severe sudden pain, inability to bear weight, or symptoms suggesting a serious fracture.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:194;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:203;s:10:"disease_id";i:255;s:11:"overview_en";s:422:"Scoliosis is an abnormal sideways curvature of the spine. Instead of remaining relatively straight when viewed from the front or back, the spine may curve into a C or S shape and may also rotate. Scoliosis can develop during childhood or adolescence and may remain mild or become more pronounced during periods of rapid growth. Some forms occur because of known conditions, while the cause of many cases is not identified.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:129:"स्कोलियोसिस रीढ़ की असामान्य पार्श्व वक्रता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:446:"The most common form of scoliosis is idiopathic scoliosis, meaning that no specific cause can be identified. It is commonly recognized during childhood or adolescence. Other forms include congenital scoliosis, which results from abnormal development of the spinal bones before birth, and neuromuscular scoliosis, which occurs with conditions affecting the nervous system or muscles. The curvature may become more noticeable during a growth spurt.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:143:"कई मामलों का कारण अज्ञात होता है, कुछ जन्मजात होते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:464:"Risk factors depend on the type of scoliosis. Idiopathic scoliosis commonly appears during childhood or adolescence and is more frequently diagnosed in girls. A family history may increase susceptibility. Congenital abnormalities of the spine can increase the risk of congenital scoliosis, while conditions such as cerebral palsy, muscular dystrophy, and spina bifida can contribute to neuromuscular scoliosis. Rapid growth can allow an existing curve to progress.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:161:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और कुछ न्यूरोमस्कुलर रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:437:"Scoliosis is evaluated with a physical examination and assessment of the shape and alignment of the spine. A forward-bending examination can reveal differences in shoulder or hip height and spinal curvature. Spinal X-rays are commonly used to confirm the curve and measure its severity. Depending on the suspected cause and findings, additional imaging such as MRI or CT may be considered to examine the spine and surrounding structures.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:109:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:530:"Most cases of idiopathic scoliosis cannot be prevented because their exact cause is unknown. Early recognition during childhood and adolescence can help identify curves that may worsen during growth. Regular examinations when a spinal curvature is suspected allow healthcare professionals to monitor changes. Congenital and neuromuscular forms are related to underlying conditions and therefore cannot generally be prevented through lifestyle measures. Appropriate management of associated disorders may help reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:89:"शीघ्र पहचान बेहतर परिणाम देती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:347:"Scoliosis is usually not an emergency and many cases are monitored routinely. Seek medical assessment for progressive curvature, persistent pain, reduced mobility, or changes in posture or function. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for severe new back pain, significant weakness or numbness, breathing difficulties, or other neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:195;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:204;s:10:"disease_id";i:256;s:11:"overview_en";s:400:"Kyphosis is an excessive forward curvature of the upper spine that can produce a rounded or hunched appearance. Mild curvature may cause few symptoms, while more pronounced kyphosis can lead to back pain, stiffness, fatigue, or difficulty maintaining an upright posture. Causes vary with age and may include abnormal spinal development, vertebral fractures, degenerative changes, or certain diseases.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:130:"काइफोसिस में ऊपरी रीढ़ आगे की ओर अधिक झुक जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:365:"Kyphosis may result from abnormal development of the vertebrae, poor posture, vertebral fractures, osteoporosis, degenerative spinal changes, or certain diseases. In children and adolescents, structural conditions such as Scheuermann disease can cause a pronounced curve. In older adults, weakening of the bones and compression fractures are important contributors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:179:"गलत मुद्रा, कशेरुका फ्रैक्चर और जन्मजात स्थितियां कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:329:"Risk factors vary according to the cause and include increasing age, osteoporosis, vertebral fractures, poor posture, spinal degenerative disease, certain developmental disorders, and conditions that weaken bone or affect spinal structure. Prolonged abnormal posture may contribute to some forms of flexible or postural kyphosis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:138:"आयु, ऑस्टियोपोरोसिस और रीढ़ के रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:385:"Diagnosis involves a medical history and physical examination to assess posture, spinal alignment, pain, flexibility, and neurological function. Standing spinal X-rays can measure the degree of curvature and identify structural changes. Additional imaging or laboratory testing may be used when an underlying bone disorder, neurological problem, infection, or other cause is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:108:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:336:"Maintaining good posture, regular physical activity, appropriate muscle strength, and healthy bone density can reduce some preventable contributors to kyphosis. Adequate calcium and vitamin D, fall prevention, and evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis can help reduce the risk of vertebral fractures that may worsen spinal curvature.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:143:"अच्छी मुद्रा और हड्डी स्वास्थ्य रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:347:"Kyphosis is usually evaluated through routine medical care. Seek assessment when the curvature is progressive, painful, or associated with reduced mobility or functional problems. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe back pain, suspected fracture, weakness, numbness, breathing difficulty, or other significant neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:196;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:205;s:10:"disease_id";i:257;s:11:"overview_en";s:336:"Lordosis is an increased inward curvature of the spine, most commonly in the lower back. A certain degree of inward curvature is normal, but excessive curvature can alter posture and sometimes cause back discomfort or movement problems. The condition may be related to posture, body structure, muscle imbalance, or underlying disorders.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:162:"लॉर्डोसिस रीढ़ के निचले हिस्से की अत्यधिक अंदरूनी वक्रता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:334:"Lordosis can result from normal developmental changes or structural differences in the spine. Excessive curvature may also be associated with poor posture, obesity, muscle imbalance, hip problems, spinal abnormalities, or conditions affecting bone and muscle development. In some cases, the underlying cause is not clearly identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:149:"गलत मुद्रा, मोटापा और रीढ़ संबंधी विकार कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:352:"Risk depends largely on the underlying cause. Factors that may contribute include obesity, poor posture, weak or imbalanced trunk muscles, certain skeletal conditions, hip abnormalities, spinal disorders, and developmental problems. The likelihood of excessive curvature also depends on age and the condition affecting the spine or surrounding muscles.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:163:"मोटापा, मांसपेशियों की कमजोरी और रीढ़ विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:394:"Diagnosis involves a physical examination to assess posture, spinal alignment, range of movement, muscle strength, and symptoms. The clinician may evaluate possible underlying causes involving the hips, muscles, or spine. X-rays can measure the degree of curvature and identify structural abnormalities. Further imaging or testing may be considered when symptoms suggest an underlying disorder.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:121:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:391:"Maintaining a healthy body weight, regular physical activity, good posture, and appropriate strength and flexibility can support spinal health. Repetitive strain and prolonged poor posture should be addressed when possible. Conditions affecting the bones, hips, or muscles should receive appropriate medical care so that preventable contributors to excessive spinal curvature can be managed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:80:"सही मुद्रा बनाए रखना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:327:"Lordosis is generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when abnormal spinal curvature causes persistent pain, reduced mobility, or functional problems, or when the curvature is changing. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for severe new pain, weakness, numbness, bladder or bowel changes, or other neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:197;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:206;s:10:"disease_id";i:258;s:11:"overview_en";s:371:"A fracture is a break or crack in a bone. Fractures may occur after a fall, accident, sports injury, or other significant force, but weakened bones can fracture with relatively minor trauma. Symptoms commonly include pain, swelling, bruising, tenderness, and difficulty moving the affected area. Some fractures may also cause visible deformity or loss of normal function.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:103:"फ्रैक्चर हड्डी का टूटना या दरार आना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:454:"Fractures usually result from forces that exceed the strength of a bone, such as falls, collisions, twisting injuries, or direct blows. Repetitive stress can produce small cracks known as stress fractures. Bones weakened by osteoporosis, certain cancers, nutritional deficiencies, long-term use of some medicines, or other medical conditions may fracture after relatively minor trauma. The mechanism and severity of injury determine the fracture pattern.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:135:"चोट, गिरना और कमजोर हड्डियां इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:430:"Risk depends on the type and strength of injury as well as the condition of the bone. Older age, osteoporosis, low bone density, previous fractures, inadequate calcium or vitamin D, certain medical conditions, and long-term use of some medicines can weaken bones. Participation in high-impact sports, occupations involving physical hazards, poor balance, and fall-prone environments can increase the chance of traumatic fractures.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:155:"ऑस्टियोपोरोसिस, दुर्घटनाएं और खेल चोटें जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:459:"Fractures are diagnosed using the injury history, physical examination, and imaging. X-rays are commonly used to identify most fractures and determine their location and alignment. CT or MRI may be needed for complex injuries or fractures that are difficult to see on standard X-rays. The evaluation may also assess nearby blood vessels, nerves, joints, and soft tissues. Bone health may require additional assessment when fractures occur with minimal trauma.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:105:"निदान इमेजिंग जांच द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:455:"Not all fractures can be prevented, but maintaining strong bones and reducing injury risks can lower the likelihood. Adequate calcium and vitamin D, regular weight-bearing activity, avoidance of smoking, and moderation of alcohol support bone health. Fall prevention is especially important for older adults. Using appropriate protective equipment during sports and hazardous activities and following safe movement practices can reduce traumatic injuries.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:90:"सुरक्षा उपाय जोखिम कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:418:"A suspected fracture requires prompt medical assessment and appropriate immobilization. Seek urgent care for significant pain, swelling, deformity, inability to bear weight, or loss of normal function after an injury. Emergency medical attention is needed for an open fracture, severe bleeding, pale or blue skin beyond the injury, loss of circulation, severe neurological symptoms, or other signs of a serious injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:198;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:207;s:10:"disease_id";i:259;s:11:"overview_en";s:316:"A stress fracture is a small crack in a bone caused by repeated stress rather than a single major injury. It commonly affects the bones of the lower leg and foot, particularly in people who participate in running or other repetitive impact activities. Pain usually develops gradually and becomes worse with activity.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:164:"स्ट्रेस फ्रैक्चर बार-बार दबाव से होने वाली छोटी हड्डी दरार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:360:"Stress fractures develop when repeated physical stress causes microscopic damage to a bone faster than the body can repair it. A sudden increase in training intensity, running on hard surfaces, repetitive jumping, or prolonged physical activity can contribute. Reduced bone strength or inadequate nutrition can also make bones more vulnerable to stress injury.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:138:"बार-बार शारीरिक गतिविधि और अधिक उपयोग इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:372:"Stress-fracture risk increases with sudden increases in exercise duration, intensity, or frequency, especially running and other repetitive impact activities. Previous stress fractures, inadequate recovery, low energy intake, poor nutrition, reduced bone density, certain menstrual or hormonal problems, and inappropriate training surfaces or footwear may also contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"खिलाड़ी और कम हड्डी घनत्व वाले लोग अधिक जोखिम में हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:371:"A stress fracture is diagnosed from the history of gradually developing activity-related pain and a physical examination. Early X-rays may appear normal, so repeat imaging or MRI may be needed when suspicion remains high. Bone scans or other imaging can sometimes help identify the affected bone. The clinician may also assess training, nutrition, and other risk factors.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:96:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:383:"Stress fractures can often be reduced by increasing exercise gradually and allowing adequate recovery between demanding activities. Use appropriate footwear and vary training surfaces when possible. Adequate energy, calcium, vitamin D, and overall nutrition support bone health. Persistent or worsening pain during activity should be evaluated rather than ignored or trained through.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:121:"व्यायाम की तीव्रता धीरे-धीरे बढ़ाना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:352:"Stress fractures require medical assessment because continuing to place stress on the affected bone can worsen the injury. Seek care for persistent localized pain that increases with activity, swelling, or difficulty bearing weight. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for severe pain, inability to bear weight, or symptoms suggesting a complete fracture.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:199;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:208;s:10:"disease_id";i:260;s:11:"overview_en";s:381:"A dislocated joint occurs when the bones forming a joint are forced out of their normal position. It most often results from an injury such as a fall, collision, or sudden force, and commonly affects the shoulder, finger, elbow, hip, or knee. A dislocation can damage nearby ligaments, muscles, nerves, or blood vessels and usually requires prompt medical assessment and treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:190:"जोड़ खिसकना वह स्थिति है जब हड्डियां अपनी सामान्य स्थिति से हट जाती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:344:"A dislocated joint usually results from a sudden force that pushes the bones out of their normal alignment. Common causes include falls, sports injuries, motor vehicle collisions, and direct blows. Some people are more susceptible because of loose or previously injured ligaments, abnormal joint structure, or a history of earlier dislocations.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:100:"चोट और अचानक बल लगना सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:335:"Risk is increased by contact sports, activities involving falls or collisions, previous joint dislocation, joint instability, ligament laxity, and certain structural abnormalities. Older adults may be more vulnerable to dislocations associated with falls, while younger people may experience them during sports or high-impact injuries.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:96:"खेल चोटें और गिरना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:371:"Diagnosis is usually based on the mechanism of injury, symptoms, physical examination, and assessment of the affected joint. X-rays are commonly used to confirm the dislocation and identify fractures. Additional imaging such as CT or MRI may be needed when soft-tissue damage or a more complex injury is suspected. Nerve and blood-vessel function should also be assessed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:108:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:334:"Many traumatic dislocations cannot be completely prevented, but protective equipment, appropriate sports technique, physical conditioning, and attention to safe environments can reduce injury risk. Strengthening the muscles around an unstable joint and following rehabilitation after a previous dislocation may help reduce recurrence.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:105:"सुरक्षात्मक उपकरण जोखिम कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:327:"A dislocated joint is a medical emergency and requires immediate medical assessment. Do not attempt to force the joint back into position. Seek emergency care for a visibly displaced or severely painful joint, major swelling, numbness or tingling, pale or blue skin, loss of circulation, or inability to move the affected limb.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:200;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:209;s:10:"disease_id";i:261;s:11:"overview_en";s:325:"Temporomandibular joint disorder refers to conditions affecting the temporomandibular joints, jaw muscles, or structures involved in jaw movement. It may cause jaw pain, difficulty chewing, clicking or popping sounds, stiffness, headaches, or difficulty opening and closing the mouth. Symptoms can be temporary or persistent.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:247:"टेम्पोरोमैंडिबुलर जॉइंट डिसऑर्डर जबड़े के जोड़ और आसपास की मांसपेशियों को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:360:"Temporomandibular joint disorders can have several contributing causes. Jaw injury, arthritis, inflammation, problems involving the jaw muscles, and excessive strain on the joint can contribute. Teeth grinding or clenching may increase stress on the jaw. Some people develop symptoms without a single identifiable cause, and several factors may occur together.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:128:"जबड़े की चोट, दांत पीसना और तनाव कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:333:"Risk factors can include jaw injury, arthritis, teeth grinding or clenching, prolonged stress on the jaw, repetitive chewing, and habits that place strain on the temporomandibular joints. Some people may have anatomical or structural factors that contribute. Symptoms are also more common in some people with chronic pain conditions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:117:"तनाव, गठिया और जबड़े की चोट जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:379:"Diagnosis is based primarily on symptoms, medical history, and examination of the jaw and surrounding muscles. The healthcare professional may assess jaw movement, tenderness, clicking or popping sounds, and the ability to open the mouth. Dental or imaging examinations may be used when needed to identify arthritis, structural abnormalities, injury, or other causes of symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:102:"निदान लक्षणों और परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:378:"Temporomandibular joint symptoms may be reduced by avoiding excessive chewing, very hard foods, prolonged gum chewing, and activities that strain the jaw. Maintaining good jaw posture and addressing teeth grinding or clenching may help. People with persistent or recurrent symptoms should seek appropriate dental or medical assessment rather than repeatedly stressing the joint.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:126:"तनाव नियंत्रण और जबड़े पर दबाव कम करना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:388:"Temporomandibular joint disorder is usually not an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent jaw pain, clicking with functional problems, difficulty chewing, limited jaw movement, or symptoms that interfere with daily activities. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for a jaw that becomes locked, severe swelling, significant trauma, or inability to open or close the mouth normally.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:201;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:210;s:10:"disease_id";i:262;s:11:"overview_en";s:327:"Chondromalacia patella refers to damage or softening of the cartilage on the underside of the kneecap. It can cause pain around or behind the kneecap, especially when climbing stairs, squatting, kneeling, running, or sitting for a long time. Symptoms may be related to irritation where the kneecap moves against the thigh bone.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:179:"कॉन्ड्रोमलेशिया पटेला घुटने की टोपी के नीचे की उपास्थि की क्षति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:388:"Chondromalacia patella can develop when the kneecap does not move smoothly over the lower end of the thigh bone, placing abnormal stress on the cartilage underneath it. Repetitive activity, muscle imbalance or weakness, previous injury, abnormal alignment, and increased pressure on the knee may contribute. The condition is often associated with activities that repeatedly load the knee.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:144:"अधिक उपयोग, चोट और घुटने की गलत स्थिति कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:365:"Risk may increase with repeated activities that place stress on the kneecap, including running, jumping, squatting, and climbing stairs. Muscle weakness or imbalance, abnormal kneecap tracking, previous knee injury, changes in lower-limb alignment, and increased pressure on the knee can contribute. The condition may be more noticeable in physically active people.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:157:"घुटने पर बार-बार दबाव और मांसपेशी असंतुलन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, and assessment of how the kneecap moves. The clinician may evaluate pain during squatting, stair climbing, or other knee movements and check strength and alignment of the leg. X-rays may help assess bone alignment and other causes of pain. MRI may be used when cartilage damage or another internal knee problem needs further evaluation.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:96:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:423:"Risk may be reduced by maintaining balanced strength and flexibility around the hip, thigh, and knee and by increasing physical activity gradually. Use proper technique during running, jumping, squatting, and other repetitive activities. Supportive footwear and appropriate training can help reduce excessive knee stress. Treating previous injuries and addressing persistent knee pain early may also help prevent worsening.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:100:"सही व्यायाम तकनीक जोखिम कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:354:"Chondromalacia patella is generally not an emergency and is often managed through planned medical care. Seek assessment for persistent or worsening knee pain, swelling, instability, or difficulty with normal activities. Prompt evaluation is appropriate after significant trauma, sudden inability to bear weight, marked swelling, or severe worsening pain.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:202;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:211;s:10:"disease_id";i:263;s:11:"overview_en";s:364:"Septic arthritis is a serious infection of a joint caused by bacteria, viruses, fungi, or other microorganisms. The infection can cause sudden joint pain, swelling, warmth, redness, and difficulty moving the affected joint. Septic arthritis requires prompt medical evaluation and treatment because infection can rapidly damage cartilage and other joint structures.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:126:"सेप्टिक आर्थराइटिस जोड़ों का गंभीर संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:341:"Septic arthritis occurs when microorganisms enter a joint and multiply within the joint fluid or tissues. Bacteria are the most common cause. Infection can reach a joint through the bloodstream, from an injury or surgery, or by spreading from nearby infected tissue. Existing joint disease or an artificial joint can increase susceptibility.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:92:"जीवाणु संक्रमण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:371:"Risk factors for septic arthritis include an artificial joint, recent joint surgery, injection drug use, bloodstream infection, weakened immunity, diabetes, rheumatoid arthritis, and other chronic illnesses. Older age and existing joint damage can also increase susceptibility. Any condition that allows microorganisms to enter the bloodstream can potentially contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:157:"कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, मधुमेह और जोड़ों के रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:379:"Septic arthritis is diagnosed urgently using symptoms, physical examination, blood tests, imaging when appropriate, and analysis of joint fluid. A needle may be used to remove fluid from the affected joint for laboratory testing, including examination for microorganisms and inflammatory cells. Blood cultures may also help identify an infection that has entered the bloodstream.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:116:"निदान में जोड़ द्रव जांच और कल्चर शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:337:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent septic arthritis, but prompt treatment of skin and other infections, good wound care, appropriate management of chronic illnesses, and proper care around joint surgery can reduce risk. People with artificial joints or weakened immunity should seek prompt medical attention for symptoms of infection.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:115:"संक्रमण का शीघ्र उपचार रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:264:"Septic arthritis can damage a joint quickly and requires urgent medical assessment. Seek immediate care for sudden severe joint pain, swelling, warmth, restricted movement, fever, chills, or feeling acutely unwell, particularly when these symptoms develop rapidly.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:203;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:212;s:10:"disease_id";i:264;s:11:"overview_en";s:380:"Fibrous dysplasia is a bone disorder in which normal bone is replaced by abnormal fibrous tissue. The affected bone may become weaker, causing pain, deformity, or fractures. It can affect one bone or several bones and may vary considerably in severity. The genetic change responsible usually develops in affected cells after conception and is generally not inherited from parents.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:185:"फाइब्रस डिस्प्लेसिया में सामान्य हड्डी की जगह रेशेदार ऊतक बन जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:368:"Fibrous dysplasia results from a genetic change occurring in affected bone-forming cells, usually after conception. The change causes abnormal bone development, with normal bone being replaced by fibrous tissue. The condition is generally not inherited from parents. It may affect a single bone or multiple bones, and the extent of involvement can vary between people.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:175:"हड्डी विकास को प्रभावित करने वाला आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन इसका कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:432:"There are no well-established lifestyle risk factors that reliably cause fibrous dysplasia. The condition results mainly from a genetic change in affected bone cells rather than from a person’s diet, exercise, or daily habits. The severity depends largely on which bones are affected and how much abnormal tissue is present. Because the genetic change usually develops after conception, it is generally not inherited from parents.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:97:"यह रोग अक्सर बचपन में विकसित होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:401:"Diagnosis of fibrous dysplasia may involve a physical examination together with imaging studies such as X-rays, CT scans, or MRI. Blood tests may be used to assess bone-related abnormalities or complications. The characteristic appearance on imaging can often support the diagnosis. A biopsy may occasionally be performed when the findings are uncertain or another bone condition needs to be excluded.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:150:"निदान में इमेजिंग और आवश्यकता होने पर बायोप्सी शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:385:"Fibrous dysplasia cannot usually be prevented because it results from a genetic change that develops in affected bone cells. However, monitoring affected bones can help identify changes and complications early. Appropriate medical follow-up, treatment of pain or other complications, and measures to reduce injury or fracture risk may help protect affected bones and maintain function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:99:"शीघ्र निगरानी जटिलताएं कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:375:"Fibrous dysplasia is usually a chronic bone condition but should be medically assessed when pain, deformity, or functional problems develop. Seek prompt care for persistent or worsening bone pain, changes in limb function, or recurrent fractures. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe pain, inability to bear weight, neurological symptoms, or suspected fracture.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:204;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:213;s:10:"disease_id";i:265;s:11:"overview_en";s:386:"A bone spur is a bony projection that develops along the edge of a bone, often near joints. Bone spurs may form gradually in response to aging, joint wear, arthritis, or long-term stress on bones and connective tissues. Many cause no symptoms, but a spur can produce pain, stiffness, restricted movement, or irritation of nearby nerves or tendons when it affects surrounding structures.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:179:"बोन स्पर हड्डियों के किनारों पर बनने वाली अतिरिक्त हड्डी वृद्धि है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:461:"Bone spurs commonly develop as part of the body’s response to long-term joint wear and tissue stress. Osteoarthritis can stimulate additional bone formation around affected joints. Repetitive pressure, previous injury, tendon or ligament changes, and aging may also contribute. The spur itself may not cause symptoms; problems generally occur when the additional bone interferes with joint movement or presses against nearby nerves, tendons, or other tissues.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:118:"जोड़ों का घिसाव और दीर्घकालिक सूजन कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:441:"Risk factors include increasing age, osteoarthritis, previous joint injury, repetitive stress, prolonged mechanical loading, and activities that place repeated pressure on joints or tendons. Bone spurs may develop in the spine, hips, knees, shoulders, hands, or feet depending on the underlying condition. Some people develop spurs without symptoms, while others are more likely to experience discomfort when the spur affects nearby tissues.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:169:"बढ़ती उम्र, ऑस्टियोआर्थराइटिस और बार-बार दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:453:"Bone spurs may be suspected from symptoms and physical examination, but imaging is generally required to demonstrate the bony growth. X-rays can usually identify the spur and associated joint changes. CT or MRI may be used when more detailed information about surrounding structures, nerves, cartilage, tendons, or other soft tissues is needed. The findings are interpreted together with symptoms because an incidental bone spur may cause no discomfort.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:118:"निदान सामान्यतः एक्स-रे द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:434:"Bone spurs cannot always be prevented, particularly when they develop as part of aging or osteoarthritis. Maintaining a healthy weight, regular physical activity, joint-friendly exercise, and avoiding repeated excessive stress on joints may help reduce contributing mechanical strain. Proper treatment of underlying arthritis or previous joint injuries may also help manage symptoms and functional problems associated with bone spurs.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:105:"जोड़ों का स्वास्थ्य बनाए रखना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:307:"Bone spurs are usually not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when pain, stiffness, reduced movement, nerve symptoms, or functional problems persist or worsen. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for significant weakness, numbness, inability to use the affected area, or severe symptoms following an injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:205;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:214;s:10:"disease_id";i:266;s:11:"overview_en";s:350:"A muscle strain is an injury in which a muscle or tendon is stretched or torn. It commonly occurs during sports, physical work, lifting, or sudden movements and may cause pain, tenderness, swelling, weakness, or difficulty moving the affected area. Strains can range from mild overstretching to partial or complete tearing of muscle or tendon tissue.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:185:"मांसपेशी खिंचाव मांसपेशी तंतुओं के अत्यधिक खिंचने या फटने से होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:430:"Muscle strains commonly occur when a muscle is suddenly stretched beyond its normal range or is forced to contract strongly. Sudden acceleration, jumping, lifting, twisting, or direct trauma can cause injury. Repetitive overuse can also produce microscopic damage and eventually lead to a strain. Inadequate warm-up, fatigue, poor conditioning, or returning to strenuous activity too quickly can increase the likelihood of injury.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"अधिक उपयोग, अचानक गतिविधि और गलत तरीके से वजन उठाना कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:418:"Risk increases with intense or sudden physical activity, inadequate conditioning, muscle fatigue, previous muscle injury, poor flexibility, and sudden increases in training intensity. Repetitive occupational activities and sports involving sprinting, jumping, or rapid changes in direction can also increase risk. Insufficient recovery between demanding activities may contribute to fatigue and reduced muscle control.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"कम शारीरिक तैयारी और वार्म-अप की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:449:"Diagnosis is usually based on the history of injury, symptoms, and physical examination. The clinician assesses pain, swelling, tenderness, strength, range of motion, and the circumstances in which the injury occurred. Imaging is not always necessary for a straightforward strain but may be used when a severe tear, fracture, tendon injury, or another condition is suspected. Ultrasound or MRI can help evaluate soft-tissue damage in selected cases.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:114:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:494:"Gradual conditioning, appropriate warm-up, adequate recovery, and regular flexibility and strengthening exercises can reduce the risk of muscle strains. Use proper technique during sports, lifting, and physical work, and increase training intensity gradually rather than making sudden changes. Avoid strenuous activity when muscles are significantly fatigued or already injured. Returning to full activity should be gradual after an injury and guided by symptoms and appropriate medical advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:124:"उचित स्ट्रेचिंग और तैयारी रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:378:"Most muscle strains are not emergencies and improve with appropriate rest and care. Seek medical assessment when pain is severe, swelling or bruising is substantial, function is significantly reduced, or symptoms do not improve. Prompt evaluation is appropriate when there is inability to use the affected limb, major weakness, or concern for a complete muscle or tendon injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:206;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:215;s:10:"disease_id";i:267;s:11:"overview_en";s:492:"Tendinitis is a condition involving irritation or structural changes in a tendon, the strong connective tissue that attaches muscle to bone. It commonly affects tendons subjected to repetitive loading, including those around the shoulder, elbow, wrist, knee, or ankle. Symptoms usually include localized pain, tenderness, and discomfort that may worsen with movement or activity. The condition can develop gradually after repeated use or sometimes follow a sudden increase in physical demand.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:99:"टेंडिनाइटिस कण्डरा की सूजन या जलन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:502:"Tendinitis commonly develops when a tendon is subjected to repeated mechanical stress that exceeds its ability to recover. Repetitive sports, manual work, prolonged gripping, lifting, running, or other movements can gradually produce tendon changes. A sudden increase in activity, inadequate conditioning, poor technique, or repetitive loading in an unfamiliar activity can increase stress. Tendon degeneration, rather than acute inflammation alone, may contribute to persistent symptoms in many cases.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:125:"बार-बार गतिविधि और अधिक उपयोग सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:508:"Risk increases with repetitive physical activity, sudden increases in workload, insufficient recovery, and activities requiring repeated forceful movement. Sports, manual occupations, prolonged computer or tool use, and other repetitive tasks can increase tendon loading depending on the affected body region. Age-related tendon changes, reduced muscle conditioning, previous tendon problems, and poor movement mechanics may also contribute. The relevant risk factors differ according to the tendon involved.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"खेल, दोहराव वाला कार्य और बढ़ती उम्र जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:467:"Diagnosis is generally based on the location and pattern of pain, the activities that provoke symptoms, and physical examination. The affected tendon may be tender and pain may be reproduced with resisted movement or stretching. Imaging is not always necessary for straightforward cases. Ultrasound or magnetic resonance imaging may be considered when symptoms persist, the diagnosis is uncertain, or a significant tendon injury or alternative condition is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:121:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:492:"Gradual increases in physical workload, adequate recovery, appropriate conditioning, and good technique can reduce excessive tendon stress. Repetitive activities should include suitable rest periods, particularly when performed for long periods. Strengthening and flexibility programs may help prepare the muscles and tendons for activity. Persistent pain should not simply be ignored or repeatedly aggravated, as early evaluation can help identify contributing factors and prevent worsening.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:125:"उचित स्ट्रेचिंग और अधिक उपयोग से बचाव सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:374:"Tendinitis is usually not an emergency and often develops from repetitive use or overloading. Seek medical assessment when pain persists, worsens, or interferes with normal activities despite appropriate rest and care. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe pain, a popping sensation, marked weakness, significant swelling, or inability to use the affected area.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:207;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:216;s:10:"disease_id";i:268;s:11:"overview_en";s:341:"Tennis elbow is a condition involving pain and tenderness around the outside of the elbow, usually caused by repeated use of the muscles and tendons of the forearm. Despite its name, it can affect anyone whose activities involve repetitive gripping or wrist and forearm movements. Pain may worsen when gripping, lifting, or moving the wrist.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:163:"टेनिस एल्बो कोहनी के बाहरी हिस्से की कण्डरा संबंधी समस्या है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:377:"Tennis elbow usually results from repeated contraction and overuse of the forearm muscles that attach to the outside of the elbow. Repetitive gripping, lifting, throwing, typing, or other activities involving the wrist and forearm can place repeated stress on the tendon. Small areas of tendon damage and degeneration may develop over time rather than from one specific injury.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:139:"कलाई और हाथ की बार-बार गतिविधियां इसका कारण बनती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:311:"Risk factors include repetitive gripping or wrist movements, occupations involving manual work, sports that require repeated arm use, poor technique, sudden increases in activity, and inadequate recovery between activities. Increasing age may also contribute because tendons can become less resilient over time.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:155:"दोहराव वाला कार्य, रैकेट खेल और गलत तकनीक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:376:"Tennis elbow is usually diagnosed through a medical history and physical examination. The healthcare professional may assess pain and tenderness around the outside of the elbow and test wrist and forearm movements. Imaging is not usually necessary for straightforward cases but may be used when symptoms are unusual, severe, persistent, or suggest another condition or injury.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:102:"निदान लक्षणों और परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:388:"The risk of tennis elbow may be reduced by using proper technique during sports and work activities, taking breaks from repetitive movements, gradually increasing activity, and allowing adequate recovery. Strengthening and stretching the forearm muscles may help people who perform repetitive activities. Ergonomic adjustments and appropriate equipment can also reduce unnecessary strain.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:112:"सही तकनीक और व्यायाम रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:323:"Tennis elbow is generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when persistent outer-elbow pain interferes with normal activities or does not improve with appropriate care. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for significant weakness, numbness, major swelling, severe pain after an injury, or sudden loss of arm function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:41:09";}i:208;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:217;s:10:"disease_id";i:269;s:11:"overview_en";s:313:"Golfer elbow, also called medial epicondylitis, is an overuse condition affecting the tendons that attach muscles of the forearm to the inner side of the elbow. It commonly causes pain and tenderness around the inner elbow, particularly during gripping, lifting, throwing, or repeated wrist and forearm movements.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:153:"गोल्फर एल्बो कोहनी के अंदरूनी हिस्से की कण्डरा समस्या है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:371:"Golfer elbow usually develops from repeated stress on the muscles and tendons that attach to the inner side of the elbow. Repetitive gripping, wrist bending, throwing, lifting, or forceful forearm movements can cause small tendon injuries and inflammation or degeneration. The condition may occur during sports or occupational activities that repeatedly load the forearm.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:122:"बार-बार पकड़ने और कलाई की गतिविधियां कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:372:"Risk increases with activities involving repeated gripping, wrist flexion, throwing, lifting, or forceful forearm use. Athletes who play golf or participate in throwing sports may be affected, as may people whose jobs require repetitive hand and wrist movements. Previous elbow or forearm problems and inadequate recovery between repetitive activities may also contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:112:"खेल और दोहराव वाले कार्य जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:389:"Golfer elbow is usually diagnosed from the symptoms, medical history, and physical examination. The clinician may examine the inner elbow and assess pain or tenderness while the patient moves the wrist or forearm against resistance. Imaging such as X-rays, ultrasound, or MRI may be considered when symptoms are persistent, severe, or when another injury or condition needs to be excluded.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:121:"निदान परीक्षण और गतिविधि इतिहास पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:415:"Prevention focuses on reducing repeated stress on the forearm and elbow. Warm up before sports, use appropriate technique and equipment, avoid sudden increases in training or workload, and take breaks during repetitive activities. Strengthening and stretching the forearm muscles may help maintain conditioning. Persistent inner-elbow pain should be evaluated rather than continuing activities that worsen symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:137:"सही एर्गोनॉमिक्स और स्ट्रेचिंग जोखिम कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:352:"Golfer elbow is usually not an emergency and often develops from repetitive strain. Seek medical assessment if pain persists, worsens, or interferes with normal activities despite appropriate rest and care. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for significant weakness, numbness, major swelling, severe pain after an injury, or sudden loss of arm function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:209;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:218;s:10:"disease_id";i:270;s:11:"overview_en";s:551:"Fibromyalgia is a chronic condition characterized by widespread musculoskeletal pain accompanied by other symptoms such as fatigue, nonrestorative sleep, difficulty concentrating, and increased sensitivity to sensory or physical stimuli. Symptoms can fluctuate over time and may be influenced by stress, sleep disruption, illness, or changes in activity. There is no single laboratory test that establishes the diagnosis. Evaluation generally focuses on the overall symptom pattern and helps exclude other conditions that can cause similar complaints.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:564:"फाइब्रोमायल्जिया एक दीर्घकालिक स्थिति है जिसमें पूरे शरीर में दर्द, थकान, नींद की समस्या और दर्द के प्रति बढ़ी हुई संवेदनशीलता हो सकती है। लक्षण समय के साथ बदल सकते हैं और अकड़न तथा एकाग्रता में कठिनाई भी हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:481:"The precise cause of fibromyalgia is not known. Research suggests that changes in how the nervous system processes and regulates pain may increase sensitivity to normally nonpainful or mildly painful stimuli. Genetic susceptibility may contribute, and symptoms can develop or worsen after physical injury, infection, prolonged stress, or other significant events in some individuals. Sleep disturbance and other factors affecting pain regulation may interact with these mechanisms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:691:"फाइब्रोमायल्जिया का सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं है। शोध से पता चलता है कि तंत्रिका तंत्र में दर्द के संकेतों की प्रक्रिया बदल सकती है। आनुवंशिक कारक भूमिका निभा सकते हैं और कुछ लोगों में अन्य दर्दनाक रोगों, तनाव या मनोदशा संबंधी समस्याओं के साथ लक्षण विकसित हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:505:"Fibromyalgia is more commonly reported in women and often begins during adulthood, although it can affect people of any sex or age. A family history may increase susceptibility. Physical trauma, surgery, infection, prolonged stress, sleep disturbance, and other significant physical or psychological stressors may precede symptom onset in some individuals. Having another chronic pain condition or certain rheumatic disorders may also be associated with increased likelihood of developing widespread pain.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:605:"फाइब्रोमायल्जिया किसी भी उम्र में हो सकता है, लेकिन यह महिलाओं में अधिक देखा जाता है और अक्सर मध्य आयु में शुरू होता है। पारिवारिक इतिहास तथा लंबे समय के दर्द, रूमेटिक रोग, चिंता या मनोदशा संबंधी समस्याएं संवेदनशीलता बढ़ा सकती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:515:"There is no single laboratory or imaging test that confirms fibromyalgia. Diagnosis generally involves a detailed history and physical examination to identify widespread pain and associated symptoms and to assess how long they have been present. Clinicians may use established symptom criteria and may order selected blood tests to evaluate other possible causes of fatigue, pain, or sleep problems. The evaluation should consider coexisting conditions without assuming that every symptom is caused by fibromyalgia.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:663:"फाइब्रोमायल्जिया की पुष्टि के लिए कोई एक विशेष रक्त या इमेजिंग जांच नहीं है। निदान मुख्यतः पूरे शरीर के दर्द और संबंधित लक्षणों, चिकित्सीय इतिहास तथा शारीरिक जांच पर आधारित होता है। समान लक्षण देने वाले अन्य रोगों को बाहर करने के लिए जांच की जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:560:"There is no established way to completely prevent fibromyalgia. Maintaining regular sleep habits, appropriate physical activity, gradual conditioning, stress-management strategies, and balanced daily routines may help support overall symptom control and physical function. Avoiding prolonged periods of inactivity and managing associated health conditions can also be useful. When persistent widespread pain, fatigue, or sleep problems develop, appropriate medical evaluation can help identify treatable conditions and establish a suitable management approach.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:671:"सटीक कारण ज्ञात न होने के कारण फाइब्रोमायल्जिया को निश्चित रूप से रोकने का कोई तरीका नहीं है। नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि, धीरे-धीरे बढ़ाया गया व्यायाम, पर्याप्त नींद, तनाव प्रबंधन और संबंधित रोगों की उचित देखभाल लक्षणों को नियंत्रित करने में सहायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:367:"Fibromyalgia is a chronic condition that generally requires planned medical assessment rather than emergency care. Seek medical evaluation for persistent widespread pain, fatigue, sleep problems, or symptoms that significantly interfere with daily activities. Prompt assessment is appropriate for new or rapidly worsening symptoms that may indicate another condition.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:210;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:219;s:10:"disease_id";i:271;s:11:"overview_en";s:454:"Muscular dystrophy is a group of inherited disorders characterized by progressive muscle weakness and loss of muscle tissue. More than 30 types are recognized, and they differ in the muscles affected, age at onset, rate of progression, and involvement of other organs. Some forms begin in childhood while others become apparent later in life. Depending on the type, weakness can affect walking, daily activities, breathing, swallowing, or heart function.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:207:"मस्कुलर डिस्ट्रॉफी आनुवंशिक रोगों का समूह है जो मांसपेशियों को कमजोर करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:475:"Muscular dystrophies are caused by inherited genetic changes that interfere with proteins needed for normal muscle structure and function. Different forms involve different genes and inheritance patterns. Examples include Duchenne, Becker, facioscapulohumeral, limb-girdle, myotonic, and oculopharyngeal muscular dystrophies. A person may inherit the condition from a parent, or in some circumstances a genetic change may arise without a previously recognized family history.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:138:"वंशानुगत आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन इसके लिए जिम्मेदार हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:473:"The principal risk factor is having a genetic change associated with a muscular dystrophy. Risk therefore depends on the specific type and its inheritance pattern. A family history of muscular dystrophy or unexplained progressive muscle weakness can be important when assessing risk. Because some forms have sex-linked inheritance while others follow different patterns, genetic counseling may be useful for affected individuals and families considering future pregnancies.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:101:"पारिवारिक इतिहास मुख्य जोखिम कारक है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:522:"Diagnosis begins with the pattern of muscle weakness, age at onset, family history, and physical examination. Blood tests may identify increased muscle enzymes. Genetic testing can identify disease-causing variants and may establish the specific type. Electromyography and nerve studies can help distinguish muscle disorders from nerve disorders. Imaging such as MRI can assess muscle quality and fatty replacement. Depending on the suspected disorder, additional heart, breathing, or swallowing assessments may be needed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:146:"निदान में आनुवंशिक जांच और मांसपेशी परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:545:"Most muscular dystrophies cannot be prevented because they result from inherited genetic changes. Families with a known history may benefit from genetic counseling to understand inheritance and reproductive options. Early recognition is important because treatment and supportive care can reduce complications and maintain function. Physical and occupational therapy, respiratory monitoring, appropriate exercise, assistive devices, and management of heart or other organ involvement can help people remain as active and independent as possible.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:118:"आनुवंशिक रोगों की पूर्ण रोकथाम संभव नहीं है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:391:"Muscular dystrophy requires ongoing medical care because muscle weakness can gradually progress and some forms can affect breathing, swallowing, or the heart. Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening weakness, falls, swallowing difficulty, or reduced mobility. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for significant breathing difficulty, choking, chest symptoms, or sudden major deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:211;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:220;s:10:"disease_id";i:272;s:11:"overview_en";s:564:"Myositis refers to inflammation of muscles involved in movement. It is a group of inflammatory muscle disorders rather than a single disease. Myositis may cause muscle weakness, fatigue, difficulty with activities such as walking or climbing stairs, and in some forms a characteristic skin rash. Polymyositis and dermatomyositis are examples of inflammatory myopathies. Some people can also develop difficulty swallowing or breathing when muscles involved in these functions are affected. Diagnosis and treatment depend on the particular type and underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:169:"मायोसाइटिस मांसपेशियों की सूजन है जिससे कमजोरी और दर्द होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:593:"Myositis may develop after an injury or infection, as a reaction to certain medicines, or because of an autoimmune process in which the immune system attacks muscle tissue. Different inflammatory myopathies have different mechanisms and clinical patterns. Dermatomyositis combines muscle inflammation and weakness with characteristic skin findings, while polymyositis primarily affects muscle strength. Identifying the underlying cause is important because treatment differs according to whether inflammation is autoimmune, infectious, medication-related, or associated with another condition.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:125:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और संक्रमण इसका कारण बन सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:558:"Risk varies according to the type of myositis and its cause. Factors that may be relevant include autoimmune disease, certain infections, previous muscle injury, and exposure to medicines associated with muscle inflammation or injury. The specific age, sex, and pattern of risk also differ among inflammatory muscle disorders. A history of progressive weakness, difficulty rising or climbing stairs, repeated falls, swallowing problems, or breathing difficulty warrants medical evaluation rather than assuming the symptoms are due to ordinary muscle fatigue.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:114:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:556:"Evaluation usually begins with a medical history and physical examination focused on muscle strength and the pattern of weakness. Blood tests may identify elevated muscle enzymes or evidence of autoimmune activity. Imaging can help assess affected muscles, and electromyography may provide additional information about muscle function. In selected cases, a muscle biopsy is performed to identify the type of inflammatory muscle disorder. The combination of clinical findings, laboratory testing, imaging, and sometimes biopsy helps establish the diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:143:"निदान रक्त जांच और मांसपेशी मूल्यांकन द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:540:"There is no established way to prevent all forms of myositis because autoimmune and genetic factors can play an important role. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to known muscle-injuring medicines and promptly addressing infections or other medical conditions may reduce some risks, but prevention depends on the underlying cause. For people who already have myositis, appropriate treatment, physical therapy, safe exercise, adequate rest, and monitoring for swallowing or breathing problems can help reduce complications and preserve function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:93:"शीघ्र उपचार जटिलताएं कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:378:"Myositis requires medical assessment because muscle inflammation can cause progressive weakness and may affect swallowing or breathing. Seek prompt care for worsening weakness, difficulty walking, falling, or significant muscle pain. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for difficulty breathing, difficulty swallowing, rapidly worsening weakness, or other signs of serious illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:212;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:221;s:10:"disease_id";i:273;s:11:"overview_en";s:444:"Rhabdomyolysis is a condition in which damaged skeletal muscles break down and release their contents into the bloodstream. The released substances, including myoglobin, can injure the kidneys and cause dangerous changes in electrolytes. Symptoms may include severe muscle pain, weakness, swelling, or dark-colored urine, although the full combination is not always present. Severe cases can lead to acute kidney injury and other complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:204:"रैब्डोमायोलिसिस में मांसपेशियां टूटकर हानिकारक पदार्थ रक्त में छोड़ती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:459:"Rhabdomyolysis can result from severe or prolonged muscle injury, strenuous exercise, crush injuries, prolonged immobilization, seizures, or very high body temperatures. Other causes include certain medicines or drugs, alcohol and other toxic exposures, infections, metabolic disorders, and inherited muscle conditions. The condition may occur when muscle cells are damaged directly or when the blood supply or normal metabolism of muscle tissue is disrupted.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:177:"गंभीर मांसपेशी चोट, अत्यधिक परिश्रम या दवाएं इसका कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:439:"Risk increases with severe physical exertion, especially when exercise is unusually intense or performed in hot conditions, traumatic muscle injury, prolonged immobilization, seizures, and extreme heat exposure. Certain medicines, recreational drugs, heavy alcohol use, infections, and metabolic or inherited muscle disorders can also increase risk. Dehydration may worsen the consequences of muscle injury and contribute to complications.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:140:"अत्यधिक व्यायाम, चोट और निर्जलीकरण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:485:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, and laboratory testing. A blood test measuring creatine kinase is commonly used to detect significant muscle breakdown and may be repeated to follow the condition. Blood tests also assess kidney function and electrolyte levels. Urine testing may show evidence of myoglobin-related muscle injury. Additional tests may be performed when an underlying drug exposure, infection, metabolic disorder, or inherited condition is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:106:"निदान रक्त और मूत्र जांच द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:499:"Risk can be reduced by increasing strenuous exercise gradually, staying adequately hydrated, avoiding excessive heat exposure, and taking medicines only as prescribed. People should use appropriate safety measures during physically demanding work or activities and seek medical care after major muscle injury. Avoiding harmful drug or alcohol exposures can also reduce risk. Prompt evaluation of severe muscle pain, weakness, swelling, or unusually dark urine may help prevent serious complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:147:"अत्यधिक परिश्रम से बचना और पर्याप्त पानी पीना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:487:"Rhabdomyolysis requires prompt medical assessment because breakdown of muscle tissue can cause kidney injury and dangerous changes in blood chemistry. Seek urgent care for severe muscle pain or swelling, marked weakness, or dark or cola-colored urine, particularly after intense exercise, trauma, prolonged immobilization, or another known trigger. Emergency evaluation is appropriate for severe weakness, fainting, confusion, very low urine output, or signs of serious systemic illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:213;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:222;s:10:"disease_id";i:274;s:11:"overview_en";s:447:"A rotator cuff tear is a partial or complete tear of one or more tendons that stabilize the shoulder and help lift and rotate the arm. Tears may develop gradually through tendon degeneration or occur suddenly after an injury such as a fall or forceful lifting movement. Symptoms can include shoulder pain, weakness, difficulty raising the arm, and discomfort at night. The severity of symptoms depends on the size, location, and cause of the tear.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:110:"रोटेटर कफ टियर कंधे की कण्डरा में फटना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:484:"Rotator cuff tears may result from gradual tendon degeneration associated with aging and repeated shoulder use or from an acute injury. Repetitive overhead activity can place repeated stress on the tendons. A fall, sudden lifting force, or other traumatic event can produce a tear in a previously healthy or already weakened tendon. Degenerative changes, reduced blood supply in certain tendon regions, and bone changes around the shoulder may contribute to progressive tendon damage.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:93:"चोट और घिसाव इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:455:"Risk increases with advancing age, repetitive overhead activity, occupations or sports requiring frequent shoulder use, and previous shoulder injury. Tendon degeneration can make the rotator cuff more susceptible to tearing. Activities involving repeated throwing, lifting, or overhead work may increase mechanical stress. Some anatomical changes around the shoulder can reduce the available space for tendon movement and contribute to progressive damage.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:152:"बार-बार सिर के ऊपर की गतिविधियां और उम्र जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:514:"Diagnosis is based on the history of shoulder symptoms, physical examination, and assessment of strength and range of motion. Specific examination maneuvers can help identify rotator cuff involvement. X-rays may assess bone changes and other structural causes of shoulder pain, while ultrasound or magnetic resonance imaging can visualize the tendons and determine the size and extent of a tear. Imaging findings are interpreted together with symptoms because structural tears do not always cause significant pain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:103:"निदान परीक्षण और MRI द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:516:"Some rotator cuff tears cannot be prevented, particularly age-related degenerative tears. Risk may be reduced by maintaining shoulder and upper-body strength, using appropriate technique during overhead activities, and increasing training or occupational workload gradually. Repetitive tasks should include adequate recovery. Proper ergonomics and attention to persistent shoulder pain may help reduce continued tendon overload and allow underlying problems to be addressed before a more significant injury develops.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:104:"कंधे की उचित मजबूती जोखिम कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:293:"A rotator cuff tear should be medically assessed when shoulder pain, weakness, or loss of movement persists, particularly after an injury. Seek prompt evaluation for sudden severe pain, significant weakness, inability to raise the arm, or a traumatic injury followed by major loss of function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:214;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:223;s:10:"disease_id";i:275;s:11:"overview_en";s:525:"Achilles tendinitis is an overuse condition affecting the Achilles tendon, the strong tendon connecting the calf muscles to the heel. The tendon is heavily involved in walking, running, jumping, and pushing the foot downward. Repetitive loading can cause pain, tenderness, and swelling near the heel. Symptoms often develop gradually rather than after one major injury. Although most cases can be managed without surgery, recovery may take several weeks or months, particularly when the tendon has been repeatedly overloaded.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:120:"अकिलीस टेंडिनाइटिस अकिलीस कण्डरा की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:488:"The most common cause is repeated or excessive loading of the Achilles tendon. A sudden increase in running, walking, jumping, or other physical activity can exceed the tendon’s ability to adapt. Tight calf muscles can increase strain on the tendon, and running on hard surfaces may contribute. Less commonly, an acute injury can damage the tendon. Repeated stress without adequate recovery can maintain inflammation and pain and may increase the risk of more significant tendon damage.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:131:"अधिक उपयोग और अचानक गतिविधि बढ़ाना इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:554:"Risk factors include a sudden increase in exercise intensity or duration, frequent running or jumping, tight calf muscles, and activities performed on hard surfaces. Athletes and physically active people may be particularly affected. Inadequate recovery between strenuous activities can also contribute to repeated tendon loading. Previous Achilles tendon problems may increase the likelihood of recurrent symptoms. Appropriate progression of activity and attention to calf flexibility and tendon conditioning can help reduce excessive mechanical stress.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:110:"दौड़ना, खेल और खराब जूते जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:499:"Diagnosis is generally based on the symptoms and physical examination. A healthcare professional may assess the location of pain, tenderness, swelling, tendon function, calf strength, and the ability to walk or push off the foot. Imaging is not always required, but ultrasound or MRI may be considered when the diagnosis is uncertain, when a tendon tear is suspected, or when surgery is being considered. Imaging can help distinguish tendinitis or tendinopathy from a more significant tendon injury.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:102:"निदान लक्षणों और परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:552:"Gradually increase the amount and intensity of physical activity rather than making sudden changes. Allow adequate recovery after strenuous exercise and address tight calf muscles with an appropriate stretching or conditioning program. Choosing suitable footwear and reducing repeated high-impact activity when symptoms begin may help prevent worsening. Alternating high-impact exercise with lower-impact activities such as cycling or swimming can reduce tendon loading. Persistent pain should be assessed before returning to intense sport or exercise.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:121:"व्यायाम धीरे-धीरे बढ़ाना रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:367:"Achilles tendinitis is usually not an emergency, but persistent pain should be assessed to prevent worsening injury. Seek medical evaluation for increasing pain, swelling, or difficulty walking. Prompt assessment is important after a sudden pop or snap, sudden severe pain, or inability to push off or bear weight because an Achilles tendon rupture may have occurred.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:215;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:224;s:10:"disease_id";i:276;s:11:"overview_en";s:349:"Carpal tunnel syndrome occurs when the median nerve is compressed as it passes through a narrow passage in the wrist called the carpal tunnel. It can cause numbness, tingling, burning, pain, or weakness in the hand and fingers, especially the thumb, index, and middle fingers. Symptoms may be worse at night or during activities involving the wrist.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:145:"कार्पल टनल सिंड्रोम कलाई में मेडियन नस दबने से होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:365:"Carpal tunnel syndrome develops when pressure builds around the median nerve inside the carpal tunnel. Swelling may result from a wrist injury, arthritis, diabetes, rheumatoid arthritis, pregnancy, menopause, or other conditions. Repeated hand and wrist movements and use of vibrating tools may also contribute. In some people, the exact cause cannot be identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"बार-बार हाथ की गतिविधियां और कलाई पर दबाव कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:315:"Risk is increased by repeated hand and wrist movements, wrist injuries, diabetes, rheumatoid arthritis, obesity, pregnancy, menopause, hypothyroidism, and certain structural problems of the wrist. Carpal tunnel syndrome is more common in women and in adults. A close family history may also increase susceptibility.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:141:"दोहराव वाला कार्य, मधुमेह और मोटापा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history, and examination of the hand and wrist. A healthcare professional may assess sensation, strength, and movement and may perform specific wrist and hand tests. Nerve conduction studies and electromyography can evaluate median nerve function. Ultrasound or X-rays may be used when needed to assess the nerve or look for other causes of symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:119:"निदान परीक्षण और नसों की जांच द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:406:"Carpal tunnel syndrome cannot always be prevented, but reducing strain on the wrists may help lower risk. Keep the wrists in a neutral position during work, use appropriately designed tools and equipment, take regular breaks, and vary repetitive tasks. Avoid prolonged pressure or extreme wrist positions, and address conditions such as diabetes or inflammatory joint disease with appropriate medical care.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:97:"सही कार्य मुद्रा जोखिम कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:338:"Carpal tunnel syndrome is generally not an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent numbness, tingling, pain, or weakness in the hand, particularly when symptoms interfere with sleep or daily activities. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for progressive weakness, loss of hand function, or rapidly worsening neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:216;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:225;s:10:"disease_id";i:277;s:11:"overview_en";s:364:"Trigger finger is a condition in which a finger catches, locks, or becomes difficult to straighten after being bent. It occurs when movement of a tendon through its surrounding sheath becomes restricted, often causing pain, stiffness, or a clicking sensation. Symptoms may be more noticeable after periods of hand use and can interfere with normal finger movement.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:200:"ट्रिगर फिंगर एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें उंगली मुड़ी हुई स्थिति में फंस जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:385:"Trigger finger commonly develops when a tendon and its surrounding sheath become irritated or swollen, making smooth tendon movement difficult. Repetitive hand use, forceful gripping, and activities that repeatedly stress the fingers may contribute. The resulting inflammation can cause the tendon to catch as the finger bends or straightens, producing clicking, stiffness, or locking.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:136:"हाथों का अधिक उपयोग और कण्डरा की सूजन इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:380:"Risk of trigger finger may increase with repetitive gripping, forceful hand use, or activities that place repeated stress on the fingers and palm. Diabetes is also associated with a higher likelihood of developing the condition. Other factors that may contribute include repeated hand strain and occupations or activities requiring frequent gripping or prolonged use of the hands.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:172:"मधुमेह, बार-बार पकड़ने का कार्य और हाथों पर दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:375:"Trigger finger is usually diagnosed from the person’s symptoms and a physical examination of the affected hand. A healthcare professional may observe the finger while it bends and straightens and may feel for tenderness or thickening near the base of the finger. Imaging is not usually required, but additional testing may be considered when another condition is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:124:"निदान लक्षणों और शारीरिक परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:459:"Trigger finger may not always be preventable, but reducing repeated gripping and forceful hand movements may lower irritation of the tendon. Taking breaks during repetitive activities, using appropriate tools and hand positions, and avoiding prolonged pressure on the palm can help. Conditions associated with trigger finger, such as diabetes, should be managed with appropriate medical care. Persistent locking or painful finger movement should be evaluated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:513:"ट्रिगर फिंगर के जोखिम को कम करने के लिए बार-बार जोर से पकड़ने वाले काम को सीमित करें, हाथ को पर्याप्त आराम दें, सही हाथ की कार्यप्रणाली अपनाएं और मधुमेह जैसी संबंधित स्थितियों का उचित प्रबंधन करें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:324:"Trigger finger is usually not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when finger catching, locking, pain, or stiffness persists or interferes with normal hand function. Prompt evaluation is appropriate if the finger becomes completely locked, develops significant swelling or redness, or symptoms follow a substantial injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:217;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:226;s:10:"disease_id";i:278;s:11:"overview_en";s:378:"Compartment syndrome occurs when pressure builds up within a closed group of muscles and surrounding tissues, reducing blood flow and potentially damaging muscles and nerves. Acute compartment syndrome usually develops after a significant injury, fracture, crush injury, or bleeding into a muscle compartment and is a medical emergency requiring prompt assessment and treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:171:"कम्पार्टमेंट सिंड्रोम में मांसपेशियों के भीतर दबाव बढ़ जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:386:"Acute compartment syndrome commonly follows fractures, crush injuries, severe muscle injury, bleeding, or swelling within a confined tissue compartment. It can also occur after reperfusion of an injured limb, tight casts or dressings, burns, or prolonged compression. Chronic exertional compartment syndrome develops during repetitive exercise and usually improves after activity stops.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:110:"चोट, फ्रैक्चर और गंभीर सूजन इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:346:"Risk is increased by major fractures, crush injuries, severe limb trauma, bleeding disorders or anticoagulant use, tight casts or dressings, burns, and situations that cause substantial swelling within a confined body compartment. Athletes involved in repetitive high-intensity activity may be at risk for chronic exertional compartment syndrome.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:124:"गंभीर चोट और अत्यधिक व्यायाम जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:473:"Acute compartment syndrome is diagnosed primarily from the symptoms, physical examination, and the circumstances of the injury. Severe or progressively worsening pain, pain with passive stretching, swelling, altered sensation, or weakness can be important findings. When the diagnosis is uncertain, pressure measurements within the compartment may help confirm elevated tissue pressure. Treatment should not be delayed when clinical findings strongly suggest the condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:122:"निदान परीक्षण और दबाव माप द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:379:"Acute compartment syndrome is not always preventable after major trauma, but prompt treatment of fractures and other serious injuries can reduce complications. Casts, dressings, and splints should be appropriately fitted and monitored for increasing pain, swelling, numbness, or weakness. People undergoing high-risk procedures or treatment should be monitored for warning signs.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:112:"चोटों का शीघ्र उपचार जटिलताओं से बचाता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:375:"Acute compartment syndrome is a medical emergency. Seek emergency medical attention immediately for severe or rapidly increasing pain, marked swelling, pain that is greater than expected from the injury, numbness, weakness, or increasing tightness of an affected limb. Do not wait for symptoms to resolve because delayed treatment can cause permanent tissue and nerve damage.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:218;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:227;s:10:"disease_id";i:279;s:11:"overview_en";s:349:"Polymyalgia rheumatica is an inflammatory disorder that causes pain and stiffness, especially in the shoulders, neck, and hips. Symptoms are often worse in the morning or after periods of rest. It mainly affects adults over 50 and may occur together with giant cell arteritis, which can cause headaches, vision problems, and other vascular symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:192:"पॉलीमायल्जिया रूमेटिका सूजन संबंधी रोग है जो दर्द और जकड़न पैदा करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:348:"The exact cause of polymyalgia rheumatica is unknown. It is thought to involve inflammation related to the immune system and may result from a combination of genetic and environmental influences. The condition is strongly associated with older age and can occur alongside giant cell arteritis, another inflammatory disorder affecting blood vessels.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:198:"सटीक कारण अज्ञात है लेकिन प्रतिरक्षा तंत्र की गड़बड़ी भूमिका निभा सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:359:"Polymyalgia rheumatica occurs almost exclusively in adults over 50 and is more common in women. Risk may also be influenced by genetic and geographic factors. Having giant cell arteritis is closely associated with PMR, and people with PMR may develop symptoms of giant cell arteritis. There are no established lifestyle measures known to prevent the disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:125:"बढ़ती उम्र और सूजन संबंधी रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:389:"Polymyalgia rheumatica is diagnosed from the pattern of pain and stiffness, medical history, and physical examination. There is no single test that confirms the condition. Blood tests such as erythrocyte sedimentation rate and C-reactive protein may show inflammation. Additional testing may be used to exclude rheumatoid arthritis, other inflammatory disorders, infections, or malignancy.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:106:"निदान लक्षणों और रक्त जांच पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:371:"There is no known way to prevent polymyalgia rheumatica. Because the condition is associated with giant cell arteritis, people diagnosed with PMR should be aware of new headaches, scalp tenderness, jaw pain while chewing, or visual changes and seek prompt medical evaluation if these occur. Regular follow-up can help monitor symptoms and treatment-related complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:108:"शीघ्र निदान लक्षण नियंत्रण में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:349:"Polymyalgia rheumatica requires prompt medical assessment because it can occur together with giant cell arteritis, which can threaten vision. Seek medical care for new severe headache, scalp tenderness, jaw pain when chewing, visual changes, or other symptoms suggesting giant cell arteritis. Sudden vision loss requires emergency medical attention.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:219;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:228;s:10:"disease_id";i:280;s:11:"overview_en";s:400:"Muscle cramps are sudden, involuntary contractions in one or more muscles that do not relax immediately. They commonly affect the calves, thighs, feet, hands, arms, or abdomen and may occur during exercise or at night. A cramp can be painful and may last from a few seconds to several minutes. Most cramps are temporary, but frequent or severe episodes may require evaluation for an underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:152:"मांसपेशियों में ऐंठन अचानक होने वाला अनैच्छिक संकुचन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:449:"Muscle cramps can result from muscle strain or overuse, dehydration, or low levels of electrolytes such as potassium, calcium, or magnesium. Other possible causes include nerve compression, reduced blood flow to muscles, pregnancy, certain medicines, dialysis, thyroid disorders, and other medical conditions. Cramps may also occur without an identifiable cause. During exercise, inadequate fluid replacement and excessive muscle use can contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:155:"निर्जलीकरण, अधिक उपयोग और इलेक्ट्रोलाइट असंतुलन कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:406:"Cramps are more common in older adults, athletes, people who are overweight, pregnant people, and individuals with certain thyroid, nerve, kidney, or circulation disorders. Prolonged or strenuous exercise, exercising in hot conditions, dehydration, and medicines that affect fluid or electrolyte balance can also increase risk. Individual risk depends on activity level, health conditions, and medications.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:131:"अत्यधिक व्यायाम और कम पानी पीना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:439:"Most occasional muscle cramps can be identified from their typical symptoms and do not require extensive testing. A healthcare professional may ask about exercise, hydration, medicines, medical conditions, and the timing and frequency of cramps. If cramps are severe, recurrent, prolonged, or accompanied by weakness, swelling, redness, or other symptoms, examination and blood or other tests may be used to identify an underlying problem.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:101:"निदान सामान्यतः लक्षणों पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:446:"Regular stretching, gradual increases in exercise, adequate fluid intake, and appropriate recovery can help reduce muscle cramps. Stretching before exercise and before bed may be useful for people who experience recurrent leg cramps. During prolonged or intense exercise, replacing fluids and electrolytes may be appropriate. Persistent or severe cramps should be assessed rather than relying on supplements or medicines without medical guidance.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:105:"पर्याप्त पानी पीना रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:347:"Most muscle cramps are mild and are not emergencies. Seek medical assessment when cramps are frequent, severe, persistent, or associated with weakness, swelling, or other unexplained symptoms. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for severe generalized cramps, fainting, significant weakness, or symptoms occurring with serious illness or dehydration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:220;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:229;s:10:"disease_id";i:281;s:11:"overview_en";s:297:"A herniated disc occurs when part of a spinal disc pushes through a weakened area and may press on nearby nerves. It most often affects the lower back but can also occur in the neck. Symptoms may include back or neck pain, pain spreading into an arm or leg, numbness, tingling, or muscle weakness.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"हर्नियेटेड डिस्क में रीढ़ की डिस्क बाहर निकलकर नसों पर दबाव डालती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:347:"A herniated disc develops when a spinal disc becomes weakened and part of its inner material pushes through the outer layer. Disc degeneration with age is common, while injury, strenuous activity, heavy lifting, repetitive bending or twisting, and sudden strain may contribute. The displaced material can irritate or compress nearby spinal nerves.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:108:"उम्र, चोट और डिस्क का घिसाव इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:352:"Risk factors for a herniated disc include increasing age, because spinal discs gradually lose flexibility, as well as heavy lifting, repetitive bending or twisting, prolonged sitting or standing, physical inactivity, excess body weight, smoking, and strenuous activity. Jobs or activities that place repeated stress on the spine may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:138:"भारी वजन उठाना, मोटापा और धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:383:"A herniated disc is usually diagnosed through the medical history and physical examination, including assessment of pain, sensation, muscle strength, and reflexes. Imaging is not always required initially. If symptoms are severe, persistent, or associated with concerning neurological findings, MRI or other spinal imaging may be used to identify disc problems and nerve compression.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:103:"निदान परीक्षण और MRI द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:399:"Back injury risk can be reduced by using proper lifting techniques, keeping the back and core muscles strong, maintaining a healthy body weight, and staying physically active. Avoid lifting objects that are too heavy or twisting while lifting. Reducing prolonged inactivity and avoiding tobacco use may also support spinal health. Proper workplace ergonomics can reduce repeated strain on the spine.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:111:"सही तरीके से वजन उठाना जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:393:"Most herniated discs are not emergencies and improve with appropriate treatment, but medical assessment is important when pain, numbness, or weakness persists or worsens. Seek prompt care for progressive weakness or significant neurological symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for new loss of bladder or bowel control, numbness around the groin or buttocks, or rapidly worsening weakness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:221;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:230;s:10:"disease_id";i:282;s:11:"overview_en";s:314:"Sciatica describes pain, numbness, tingling, or weakness that travels along the path of the sciatic nerve, usually from the lower back through the buttock and into the leg. It is a symptom rather than a disease itself and may result from a herniated disc, spinal stenosis, or another condition affecting the nerve.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:123:"सायटिका सायटिक नस में जलन से होने वाला दर्द है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:326:"Sciatica occurs when the sciatic nerve or one of its roots is irritated, compressed, or injured. Common causes include a herniated disc and narrowing of the spinal canal from spinal stenosis. Less common causes include piriformis syndrome, spinal injury, vertebral displacement, or a tumor affecting structures near the nerve.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:143:"हर्नियेटेड डिस्क और रीढ़ विकार इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:341:"Risk of sciatica is influenced by conditions that affect the lower spine or sciatic nerve. Age-related spinal changes, herniated discs, spinal stenosis, prolonged sitting, physically demanding work, heavy lifting, and activities involving repeated bending or twisting may increase risk. Some spinal injuries or disorders can also contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:143:"मोटापा, लंबे समय तक बैठना और रीढ़ रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:374:"Sciatica is usually diagnosed from the pattern of pain and symptoms together with a physical and neurological examination. The clinician may check muscle strength, sensation, reflexes, walking, and pain produced by leg movement. Imaging such as MRI or X-ray is generally considered when symptoms are severe, persistent, recurrent, or when another serious cause is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान लक्षणों और आवश्यकता अनुसार इमेजिंग से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:427:"Sciatica cannot always be prevented because it may result from age-related spinal changes or other conditions. Maintaining regular physical activity, strengthening the core and back, using proper lifting techniques, maintaining a healthy weight, and avoiding prolonged sitting may reduce strain on the spine. Work activities involving repeated bending, twisting, or heavy lifting should be performed with appropriate technique.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:80:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:398:"Sciatica often improves with conservative treatment but should be medically assessed when symptoms are severe, persistent, or worsening. Seek prompt care for increasing weakness or numbness, severe uncontrolled pain, fever with back pain, or symptoms following significant trauma. Emergency evaluation is needed for new loss of bladder or bowel control or rapidly progressive neurological problems.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:222;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:231;s:10:"disease_id";i:283;s:11:"overview_en";s:490:"Spinal stenosis occurs when spaces within the spine become narrowed and place pressure on the spinal cord or nearby nerves. It most often develops gradually because of age-related changes such as arthritis, thickened ligaments, or enlargement of spinal joints. Some people have no symptoms, while others develop back or neck pain, numbness, weakness, or pain that travels into the arms or legs. Symptoms may become worse with standing or walking and improve with sitting or bending forward.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:147:"स्पाइनल स्टेनोसिस रीढ़ की नलिका के संकुचन की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:556:"Spinal stenosis most commonly develops because of degenerative changes associated with aging. Arthritis can cause bone spurs and enlargement of spinal joints, while thickened ligaments may reduce the available space for nerves. Bulging or herniated discs can also contribute. Some people are born with a narrower spinal canal. Previous spinal injury, certain bone disorders, and abnormal spinal development may increase the likelihood of narrowing. Symptoms occur when the narrowing affects the spinal cord or nerve roots sufficiently to cause compression.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:118:"उम्र संबंधी परिवर्तन और गठिया इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:481:"Risk factors for spinal stenosis include increasing age, osteoarthritis, degenerative disc disease, previous spinal injury or surgery, certain congenital spinal conditions, and disorders affecting bone or connective tissue. Excessive mechanical stress may contribute to degenerative changes. Symptoms are more common when structural narrowing becomes significant enough to affect nerves. Having spinal narrowing on an imaging study does not always mean a person will have symptoms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:119:"बढ़ती उम्र और रीढ़ का घिसाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:545:"Diagnosis of spinal stenosis begins with a history and neurological examination assessing pain, sensation, strength, reflexes, and walking ability. Imaging is used when symptoms suggest significant narrowing or nerve compression. MRI can show the spinal cord, nerve roots, discs, and soft tissues, while CT can provide detailed information about bone structures. X-rays may identify alignment or degenerative changes. Imaging findings must be interpreted together with symptoms because narrowing can be present without causing clinical problems.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:97:"निदान MRI जैसी इमेजिंग जांच से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:549:"Spinal stenosis cannot always be prevented because aging and inherited anatomy play important roles. Maintaining regular physical activity, healthy body weight, and good muscle strength can support spinal function. Safe lifting techniques and appropriate management of injuries may reduce additional strain. Treating conditions such as osteoarthritis and maintaining mobility can help preserve function. People with persistent back pain, weakness, numbness, walking difficulty, or changes in bladder or bowel function should seek medical assessment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:117:"नियमित व्यायाम रीढ़ स्वास्थ्य में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:381:"Spinal stenosis is usually a chronic condition requiring medical assessment rather than emergency treatment. Seek care for persistent or worsening pain, numbness, weakness, walking difficulty, or reduced function. Prompt or emergency evaluation is needed for worsening weakness, significant balance problems, new bladder or bowel dysfunction, or inability to urinate or pass stool.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:223;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:232;s:10:"disease_id";i:284;s:11:"overview_en";s:628:"Degenerative disc disease refers to changes in the spinal discs that occur as they lose water, flexibility, and structural strength over time. These changes can sometimes cause back or neck pain, stiffness, or other symptoms. Disc degeneration can occur with aging and may also be influenced by injury or repeated stress. Degenerative disc disease does not necessarily cause symptoms, and disc changes seen on imaging are common as people age. When symptoms occur, they may include localized back or neck pain, stiffness, or pain that extends into an arm or leg when nearby nerves are affected. Symptoms can fluctuate over time.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:163:"डिजेनरेटिव डिस्क डिजीज में रीढ़ की डिस्क धीरे-धीरे घिसती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:620:"Degenerative disc changes occur partly because spinal discs naturally lose water and elasticity with age. Repeated physical stress, injury, heavy lifting, smoking, and other factors may accelerate disc wear. Changes in the discs can sometimes lead to inflammation or irritation of nearby spinal structures. Intervertebral discs contain a soft inner portion and a tougher outer ring. With degeneration, the discs can lose hydration and height and develop structural changes. Reduced disc height can alter the mechanics of the spine and may contribute to inflammation, abnormal movement, or narrowing around spinal nerves.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:111:"उम्र और रीढ़ पर बार-बार दबाव इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:563:"Risk increases with aging, repeated spinal stress, physically demanding work, heavy lifting, previous spinal injury, smoking, and excess body weight. Certain activities or occupations that place repeated strain on the spine may accelerate disc degeneration. Risk may be greater with advancing age and repeated loading of the spine. Heavy physical work, repetitive bending or lifting, prolonged vibration, previous spinal trauma, smoking, and excess body weight can contribute. Genetic differences may also influence how quickly discs undergo degenerative changes.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:125:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा और भारी श्रम जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:632:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history, and a physical examination. Imaging such as X-rays or magnetic resonance imaging may show disc-space narrowing, changes in the discs, or other spinal abnormalities. Imaging findings do not always correspond directly to the severity of pain. Imaging findings can include disc-space narrowing, changes in disc shape, bone spurs, or other degenerative changes. MRI can provide more information about discs and nerves when neurological symptoms are present. A careful clinical examination remains important because degenerative findings may occur even in people without significant pain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:108:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:650:"Disc degeneration cannot always be prevented because aging is a major contributor. Regular physical activity, maintaining a healthy weight, using safe lifting techniques, avoiding smoking, and protecting the back from repeated injury may help reduce strain on the spine. Regular strengthening and flexibility exercises can support the muscles surrounding the spine. Proper lifting technique, ergonomic work practices, maintaining a healthy weight, and avoiding tobacco can reduce modifiable stress on spinal structures. People with recurring symptoms should address contributing physical activities rather than repeatedly working through severe pain.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:96:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली जोखिम कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:389:"Degenerative disc disease is generally managed through planned medical care and is not usually an emergency. Seek assessment for persistent or worsening back or neck pain, reduced mobility, numbness, or weakness. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for significant neurological symptoms, and emergency assessment is needed for new bladder or bowel dysfunction or rapidly progressive weakness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:224;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:233;s:10:"disease_id";i:285;s:11:"overview_en";s:329:"Chronic low back pain is persistent pain in the lower back that continues for several months or longer. It may result from problems involving the discs, joints, muscles, or other structures of the spine. Pain may remain localized to the lower back or sometimes extend into the buttocks or legs, depending on the underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:140:"क्रॉनिक लो बैक पेन कई महीनों तक रहने वाला कमर दर्द है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:367:"Chronic low back pain can have many causes. Disc disease, arthritis, muscle strain, and other problems affecting the structures of the spine may contribute. Pain can also persist after an earlier injury or episode of back pain. In some people, no single structural cause can be identified, and several physical or lifestyle factors may contribute to ongoing symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:132:"डिस्क रोग, गठिया और मांसपेशी खिंचाव इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:387:"Risk factors for chronic low back pain include previous back injury, repeated physical strain, poor posture, and activities that place repeated stress on the spine. Physical inactivity or weak back and abdominal muscles may contribute. Increasing age, certain spinal conditions, excess body weight, and some chronic illnesses can also increase the likelihood that back pain will persist.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:137:"मोटापा, गलत मुद्रा और निष्क्रियता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:407:"Diagnosis of chronic low back pain is based primarily on the medical history and physical examination. The clinician assesses the location and duration of pain, movement, strength, sensation, and other symptoms that may suggest a particular cause. Imaging such as X-rays or MRI may be used when clinically necessary, particularly when symptoms are persistent, severe, or associated with concerning findings.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:166:"निदान इतिहास, परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार इमेजिंग पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:396:"Some episodes of chronic low back pain cannot be prevented, but regular physical activity can help maintain strength and flexibility. Maintaining a healthy weight may reduce strain on the back. Use safe lifting techniques by bending at the knees, keeping objects close to the body, and avoiding twisting while lifting. Avoid smoking and use supportive sitting and working positions when possible.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1094:"कमर के निचले हिस्से के दर्द के सभी मामलों को रोका नहीं जा सकता, लेकिन नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि पीठ की मांसपेशियों को मजबूत और लचीला रखकर जोखिम कम करने में मदद कर सकती है। स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखने से पीठ पर पड़ने वाला दबाव कम हो सकता है। सुरक्षित तरीके से उठाना और झुकना सीखें: घुटनों से झुकें, वस्तु को शरीर के पास रखें और उठाते समय शरीर को मोड़ने से बचें। धूम्रपान से बचें और संभव हो तो बैठने तथा काम करने की सहायक मुद्रा अपनाएँ।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:415:"Chronic low back pain usually requires planned medical assessment rather than emergency care. Seek evaluation when pain persists, worsens, or interferes with normal activities. Prompt assessment is important for fever, unexplained weight loss, significant trauma, progressive weakness or numbness, and emergency evaluation is needed for new bladder or bowel dysfunction or other signs of serious spinal involvement.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:225;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:234;s:10:"disease_id";i:286;s:11:"overview_en";s:504:"Cervical spondylosis refers to age-related wear and structural changes affecting the bones, discs, and joints of the neck. Changes may include loss of disc height, bone spurs, and degeneration of the joints between the vertebrae. Many people have these changes without symptoms, while others develop neck pain, stiffness, headaches, or reduced movement. If nerves or the spinal cord become compressed, symptoms such as arm pain, numbness, weakness, balance problems, or changes in coordination may occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:165:"सर्वाइकल स्पॉन्डिलोसिस गर्दन की रीढ़ का उम्र संबंधी घिसाव है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:513:"Cervical spondylosis primarily results from gradual age-related degeneration of the structures of the cervical spine. Intervertebral discs may lose water and height, while the vertebral joints and surrounding bone can develop degenerative changes and bone spurs. Previous neck injury, repetitive mechanical stress, and certain occupational activities may contribute. Structural changes can narrow the spaces through which nerves or the spinal cord pass, potentially producing neurological symptoms in some people.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:97:"उम्र और रीढ़ का घिसाव मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:508:"Risk increases with advancing age and is associated with the cumulative effects of spinal wear and tear. Previous neck injuries, repetitive occupational loading, prolonged poor posture, and activities that place repeated stress on the cervical spine may contribute. Some people have more extensive structural changes because of individual anatomy or genetic factors. Neurological complications are more likely when degenerative changes substantially narrow the spaces around spinal nerves or the spinal cord.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"बढ़ती उम्र और गर्दन पर बार-बार दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:545:"Diagnosis is usually based on the history of neck symptoms and a physical and neurological examination. X-rays can demonstrate degenerative changes such as reduced disc space or bone spurs. Magnetic resonance imaging provides more detailed information about discs, nerves, and the spinal cord and may be used when neurological symptoms or significant compression is suspected. Computed tomography may provide additional information about bone structures. The degree of imaging abnormality does not always correspond directly to symptom severity.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:121:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग जांच द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:504:"Age-related cervical spine changes cannot always be prevented. Regular physical activity, maintaining neck and upper-body strength, using appropriate posture, and avoiding prolonged positions that place unnecessary strain on the neck may support spinal function. Safe lifting techniques and appropriate ergonomics at work can reduce repetitive mechanical stress. Preventing neck injuries through appropriate safety measures during sports and other activities may also reduce additional structural damage.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:80:"सही मुद्रा बनाए रखना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:336:"Cervical spondylosis is generally a chronic condition and is not usually an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent neck pain, stiffness, numbness, weakness, or changes in coordination. Prompt evaluation is important for progressive weakness, difficulty walking, significant balance problems, or new bladder or bowel symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:226;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:235;s:10:"disease_id";i:287;s:11:"overview_en";s:530:"Lumbar spondylosis refers to degenerative changes involving the bones, discs, joints, and other structures of the lower spine. These changes are commonly associated with aging and long-term mechanical wear. Some people have degenerative findings without significant symptoms, while others develop chronic low back pain, stiffness, reduced mobility, or symptoms related to irritation or compression of spinal nerves. The clinical importance depends on the structures involved and whether there are associated neurological findings.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:150:"लम्बर स्पॉन्डिलोसिस कमर की रीढ़ का उम्र संबंधी घिसाव है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:487:"Lumbar spondylosis develops from age-related and long-term degenerative changes in the lower spine. Repeated mechanical stress can contribute to wear of the intervertebral discs, facet joints, and other spinal structures. Previous spinal injury, physically demanding activities, prolonged or repetitive loading, and other factors that increase mechanical stress may contribute to degeneration. The degree of structural degeneration does not always correspond to the severity of symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:97:"उम्र और रीढ़ का घिसाव मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:537:"Increasing age is the main risk factor for degenerative changes of the spine. Other factors may include repetitive physical stress, physically demanding work, previous spinal injury, prolonged mechanical loading, and conditions that accelerate degeneration. Being physically active does not by itself mean a person will develop symptomatic disease, and imaging abnormalities may occur without significant symptoms. Risk assessment should therefore consider both structural findings and the person’s symptoms and functional limitations.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:120:"उम्र, मोटापा और बार-बार दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:559:"Diagnosis begins with a history and physical examination, including assessment of back pain, movement, strength, sensation, reflexes, and neurological symptoms. Imaging may be used when symptoms persist, neurological findings are present, or another spinal problem needs to be excluded. X-rays can demonstrate degenerative changes, while MRI provides more detailed information about discs, nerves, the spinal canal, and surrounding structures. Imaging findings need to be interpreted together with symptoms because degenerative changes can occur without pain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:121:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:539:"Degenerative changes related to aging cannot be completely prevented, but maintaining general physical conditioning can help support spinal function. Regular appropriate exercise, maintaining healthy body weight, using safe techniques when lifting, and avoiding unnecessary repetitive strain may reduce mechanical stress on the lower back. People with persistent or worsening symptoms should seek evaluation rather than relying only on self-treatment. New weakness, numbness, or bladder or bowel problems require prompt medical assessment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:103:"सही मुद्रा और नियमित व्यायाम सहायक हैं.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:423:"Lumbar spondylosis is generally a chronic condition and is not usually an emergency. Seek medical assessment for persistent or worsening back pain, stiffness, reduced mobility, numbness, or weakness. Prompt evaluation is important for progressive neurological symptoms, and emergency assessment is needed for new bladder or bowel dysfunction, severe weakness, or other signs of significant spinal nerve or cord compression.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:227;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:236;s:10:"disease_id";i:288;s:11:"overview_en";s:518:"Spinal cord injury is damage to the spinal cord that can interfere with movement, sensation, or normal control of body functions below the level of the injury. The severity depends on the location and extent of damage and whether the injury is complete or incomplete. Traumatic injuries may cause weakness, paralysis, altered sensation, pain, or problems with bladder and bowel function. Nontraumatic injuries can produce similar effects when disease or another medical condition damages or compresses the spinal cord.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:152:"स्पाइनल कॉर्ड इंजरी रीढ़ की हड्डी की नसों की गंभीर चोट है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:503:"Spinal cord injury can result from traumatic damage when the spinal cord is bruised, stretched, compressed, or torn. Common traumatic causes include motor-vehicle crashes, falls, sports injuries, and acts of violence. Fractures or dislocations of the spine can compress or damage the cord. Nontraumatic spinal cord injury can occur because of tumors, infections, inflammation, reduced blood supply, degenerative changes, or other medical conditions that affect the spinal cord or surrounding structures.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1041:"स्पाइनल कॉर्ड इंजरी तब हो सकती है जब रीढ़ की हड्डी पर चोट लगने से वह दब जाए, खिंच जाए, कुचल जाए या फट जाए। सामान्य दर्दनाक कारणों में सड़क दुर्घटनाएं, गिरना, खेल की चोटें और हिंसक घटनाएं शामिल हैं। रीढ़ की हड्डी में फ्रैक्चर या डिसलोकेशन होने पर भी कॉर्ड पर दबाव पड़ सकता है। गैर-दर्दनाक स्पाइनल कॉर्ड इंजरी ट्यूमर, संक्रमण, सूजन, रक्त की आपूर्ति कम होने या अन्य चिकित्सकीय स्थितियों के कारण हो सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:500:"Risk is increased by activities or circumstances associated with severe trauma, including high-speed vehicle crashes, falls from heights, contact or high-impact sports, violence, and unsafe diving or water activities. Older adults may have increased risk of spinal injury from falls, particularly when bone or balance problems are present. Failure to use seat belts, protective equipment, or appropriate workplace and recreational safety measures can also increase the likelihood of traumatic injury.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"गंभीर चोट और जोखिमपूर्ण गतिविधियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:502:"Diagnosis requires an urgent assessment of neurological function, including strength, sensation, reflexes, and other signs of spinal cord involvement. Imaging is used to identify damage to the spine and spinal cord. CT scans can show fractures or other structural injuries, while MRI can provide detailed information about the spinal cord, discs, ligaments, compression, bleeding, or soft-tissue damage. The neurological examination and imaging findings help determine the level and severity of injury.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:133:"निदान न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण और इमेजिंग से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:528:"Many traumatic spinal cord injuries can be reduced by preventing serious accidents. Use seat belts and appropriate child restraints in vehicles, follow workplace safety procedures, and use suitable protective equipment during sports and recreational activities. Avoid diving into unfamiliar or shallow water. Reduce fall hazards at home, particularly for people at increased risk of falls. Never drive under the influence of alcohol or drugs, and follow established safety practices when using vehicles, machinery, or equipment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:90:"सुरक्षा उपाय जोखिम कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:375:"Spinal cord injury is a medical emergency and requires immediate medical assessment. Do not move a person with a suspected spinal injury unless necessary for immediate safety. Seek emergency care for loss of sensation or movement, severe neck or back pain after trauma, weakness, difficulty breathing, loss of bladder or bowel control, or any significant neurological change.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:42:32";}i:228;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:237;s:10:"disease_id";i:289;s:11:"overview_en";s:505:"Cauda equina syndrome occurs when the bundle of nerve roots at the lower end of the spinal cord becomes compressed or damaged. These nerve roots control sensation and movement in the legs and help control bladder and bowel function. The condition can develop from a severe disc problem, spinal narrowing, tumor, infection, bleeding or other causes of pressure on the nerve roots. Because permanent nerve damage can occur, suspected cauda equina syndrome is a medical emergency requiring prompt assessment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"कॉडा इक्वाइना सिंड्रोम निचली रीढ़ की नसों पर दबाव की गंभीर स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:431:"Cauda equina syndrome is most often caused by severe compression of the nerve roots in the lower spinal canal. A large herniated disc can compress the nerves, while spinal stenosis, tumors, infections, bleeding or traumatic injury can also produce pressure. Other structural conditions affecting the lower spine may contribute. The underlying problem determines how quickly symptoms develop and how much nerve function is affected.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:123:"बड़ी डिस्क समस्या और रीढ़ की चोट इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:445:"Risk factors depend on the condition causing nerve compression and may include severe or recurrent lumbar disc disease, narrowing of the spinal canal, spinal tumors, infection, bleeding around the spine and significant lower-back trauma. Previous spinal disorders or procedures may also be relevant. People with new severe lower-back symptoms accompanied by changes in bladder, bowel, leg strength or sensation require urgent medical evaluation.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:495:"जोखिम कारकों में बड़ी लम्बर डिस्क हर्निएशन, स्पाइनल कैनाल का संकुचन, ट्यूमर, संक्रमण, चोट, रक्तस्राव या ऐसी अन्य स्थितियां शामिल हैं जो निचली रीढ़ की तंत्रिका जड़ों पर गंभीर दबाव डालती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:533:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern of neurological symptoms and a physical examination, followed by urgent imaging when cauda equina syndrome is suspected. The healthcare provider will assess leg strength, sensation, reflexes and bladder or bowel function. MRI is commonly used to identify compression of the nerve roots and determine the underlying cause. Other imaging or tests may be needed depending on the suspected cause. Prompt diagnosis is important because prolonged compression can result in permanent neurological problems.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:127:"निदान हेतु तत्काल इमेजिंग और परीक्षण आवश्यक है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:506:"Cauda equina syndrome cannot always be prevented because some causes, such as tumors or sudden severe disc herniation, are not predictable. Reducing the risk of spinal injury through safe lifting practices, appropriate protective equipment and safer driving and recreational activities may help prevent some spinal conditions. People with known spinal disease should follow medical advice and seek prompt evaluation for rapidly worsening back pain, leg weakness, numbness or new bladder and bowel problems.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:113:"रीढ़ रोगों का शीघ्र उपचार सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:431:"Cauda equina syndrome is a medical emergency caused by severe compression of the nerves at the lower end of the spinal canal. Seek emergency medical attention immediately for new loss of bladder or bowel control, inability to urinate, numbness around the groin or buttocks, rapidly worsening leg weakness, or major changes in sensation or movement. Prompt treatment is important to reduce the risk of permanent neurological damage.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:229;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:238;s:10:"disease_id";i:290;s:11:"overview_en";s:519:"Spondylolisthesis occurs when one vertebra slips forward or backward in relation to another vertebra. The condition can range from mild and symptom-free to more significant displacement associated with back pain, stiffness, muscle tightness, or symptoms caused by irritation of nearby nerves. It may occur in children, adolescents, or adults depending on the underlying cause. Some cases are associated with a stress fracture or defect in part of a vertebra, while others develop from degenerative changes in the spine.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:155:"स्पॉन्डिलोलीस्थीसिस में एक कशेरुका दूसरी पर खिसक जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:497:"Spondylolisthesis has several possible causes. A stress fracture or defect in a vertebral structure can allow one vertebra to shift relative to another. Degenerative changes affecting spinal discs and joints can also lead to vertebral slippage, particularly in adults. Less common causes include congenital spinal abnormalities, significant trauma, or diseases that weaken bone or spinal structures. The underlying mechanism helps determine the expected course and the most appropriate management.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:102:"घिसाव, दोष या चोट इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:494:"Risk factors depend on the type of spondylolisthesis. Repetitive activities involving spinal extension and loading may contribute to stress-related forms, particularly in young athletes. Age-related degeneration can increase risk of degenerative spondylolisthesis in adults. Certain congenital or structural differences of the spine can also predispose a person to vertebral slippage. A history of spinal injury or conditions that weaken the vertebrae may increase risk in selected individuals.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:127:"उम्र, खेल चोटें और रीढ़ पर दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:516:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and examination of the spine and lower-limb function. The clinician may assess pain, stiffness, muscle tightness, strength, sensation, reflexes, and signs of nerve involvement. Spinal X-rays can demonstrate vertebral displacement and may show associated bone abnormalities. Additional imaging such as MRI may be used when nerve compression or other soft-tissue abnormalities are suspected. The severity of symptoms and degree of vertebral displacement are considered together.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:108:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:542:"Not all cases of spondylolisthesis can be prevented, particularly those related to congenital structure or age-related degeneration. Reducing repetitive excessive spinal loading and using appropriate technique during physical activity may help lower the risk of stress-related injury. Gradual conditioning and appropriate training are especially important for athletes involved in activities that repeatedly extend the lower back. Persistent back pain, weakness, numbness, or changes in bladder or bowel control should be medically evaluated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:100:"उचित व्यायाम और चोट से बचाव सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:377:"Spondylolisthesis is usually managed through planned medical assessment, but symptoms may worsen when spinal nerves are affected. Seek medical care for persistent or worsening back pain, leg pain, numbness, weakness, or difficulty walking. Urgent evaluation is needed for rapidly progressive weakness, new bladder or bowel dysfunction, or numbness around the groin or buttocks.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:230;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:239;s:10:"disease_id";i:291;s:11:"overview_en";s:322:"Plantar fasciitis is a common cause of pain around the heel and bottom of the foot. It involves irritation or degeneration of the plantar fascia, a strong band of tissue that connects the heel bone with the toes and supports the arch of the foot. Pain is often most noticeable with the first steps after waking or resting.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:122:"प्लांटर फेशियाइटिस पैर के तलवे की ऊतक सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:381:"Plantar fasciitis is associated with repeated stress on the plantar fascia. Repetitive walking, running, standing, or other weight-bearing activities can contribute. Tight calf muscles, changes in foot structure, flat feet or high arches, inappropriate footwear, and increased body weight may increase stress on the plantar fascia. Sudden increases in activity can also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:118:"अधिक उपयोग, पैर पर दबाव और खराब जूते कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:368:"Risk factors include activities involving prolonged standing, walking, running, or other repetitive weight-bearing exercise. Flat feet, high arches, tight calf muscles, increased body weight, inappropriate footwear, and sudden increases in physical activity may increase stress on the plantar fascia. Occupations requiring long periods of standing may also contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:149:"मोटापा, लंबे समय तक खड़े रहना और दौड़ना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:372:"Plantar fasciitis is usually diagnosed from the pattern of foot pain and a physical examination. The healthcare professional may examine the heel and plantar fascia and assess foot movement, walking pattern, and calf flexibility. Imaging is not usually required for typical cases but may be used when symptoms are persistent, severe, or suggest another cause of heel pain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:102:"निदान लक्षणों और परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:382:"Plantar fasciitis risk may be reduced by maintaining a healthy body weight, wearing supportive footwear, avoiding sudden increases in exercise, and gradually building activity levels. Regular stretching of the calf and plantar fascia may be useful for people at risk. Replacing worn-out athletic shoes and modifying activities that repeatedly cause heel pain can also reduce strain.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:83:"उचित जूते रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:339:"Plantar fasciitis is usually not an emergency. Seek medical assessment when heel pain persists, worsens, or interferes with walking or daily activities despite appropriate care. Prompt evaluation is appropriate when pain follows significant trauma, walking becomes very difficult, or another cause of severe heel pain needs to be excluded.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:231;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:240;s:10:"disease_id";i:292;s:11:"overview_en";s:323:"A bunion is a structural deformity in which the joint at the base of the big toe becomes displaced, causing the toe to angle toward the other toes and a prominent bump to develop on the side of the foot. Bunions may cause pain, swelling, redness, pressure from footwear, and difficulty walking or finding comfortable shoes.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:163:"बनियन बड़े पैर के अंगूठे के जोड़ पर बनने वाली हड्डी की उभार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:269:"Bunions develop when the bones forming the big-toe joint become misaligned. Genetic foot structure can contribute, and factors such as abnormal foot mechanics, certain types of footwear, joint conditions, and repeated pressure on the foot may contribute to progression.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"आनुवंशिकता, पैर की संरचना और जूते कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:360:"Risk factors include family history, inherited foot structure, abnormal foot mechanics, certain joint conditions, and repeated pressure on the big-toe joint. Footwear that places pressure on the toes may worsen discomfort or contribute to progression in susceptible feet. Having a risk factor does not necessarily mean that a person will develop the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:124:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और तंग जूते जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:275:"Diagnosis is usually based on examination of the foot and assessment of the position and movement of the big-toe joint. X-rays may be used to evaluate bone alignment and the severity of the deformity, particularly when symptoms are significant or surgery is being considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार एक्स-रे से होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:329:"Bunions cannot always be prevented, particularly when inherited foot structure contributes. Wearing comfortable footwear with adequate room for the toes, avoiding persistent pressure on the big-toe joint, maintaining appropriate foot mechanics, and addressing painful foot problems early may help reduce symptoms and progression.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:93:"आरामदायक जूते जोखिम कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:330:"Bunions are usually not emergencies and can often be managed with planned medical care. Seek assessment when pain, swelling, difficulty walking, skin problems, or footwear problems persist or worsen. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for severe pain, significant inflammation, skin breakdown, or sudden changes following an injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:232;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:241;s:10:"disease_id";i:293;s:11:"overview_en";s:439:"Flat feet, or pes planus, occur when the arches of the feet are reduced or appear flattened when standing. Flat arches can be a normal variation, particularly in young children, and many people have no symptoms. In some individuals, changes in the arch can contribute to foot pain, ankle discomfort, altered walking mechanics, or problems higher in the legs. Flat feet may be flexible or associated with structural or tendon abnormalities.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:128:"फ्लैट फीट में पैर का आर्च कम या समाप्त हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:466:"Flat feet may result from normal developmental variation, particularly because the foot arches may not fully develop during early childhood. In other people, the arches may become flatter because of ligament or tendon problems, injury, arthritis, obesity, aging, or structural differences in the bones and joints of the foot. Flexible flat feet maintain an arch when the foot is unloaded, whereas more rigid flattening may reflect an underlying structural condition.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:135:"आनुवंशिकता, चोट और टेंडन समस्याएं कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:401:"Many cases of flat feet are simply a normal anatomical variation. Risk of symptomatic or acquired flat feet may increase with age, obesity, injury, arthritis, tendon dysfunction, and certain neuromuscular or connective-tissue conditions. Family patterns and individual foot structure may also influence arch shape. Having flat arches alone does not necessarily indicate disease or predict future pain.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:120:"मोटापा और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:505:"Diagnosis is usually based on examination of the feet while sitting and standing and observation of walking mechanics. The clinician may assess whether an arch appears when the person stands on the toes, which can help distinguish flexible from more rigid flat feet. Imaging is often unnecessary when symptoms are mild and the examination is typical. X-rays or other imaging may be considered when there is persistent pain, stiffness, deformity, injury, or concern about an underlying structural disorder.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:100:"निदान पैर की जांच द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:467:"Flexible flat feet without symptoms generally do not require prevention. Maintaining a healthy body weight, wearing comfortable and appropriately supportive footwear when needed, staying physically active, and addressing injuries or conditions affecting the foot and ankle can support normal function. Children with persistent pain, stiffness, weakness, or unusual gait patterns should be evaluated rather than assuming that flat arches are simply a normal variation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:96:"सहायक जूते जटिलताओं से बचा सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:317:"Flat feet are usually not an emergency, particularly when painless. Seek medical assessment when persistent pain, weakness, swelling, balance problems, or difficulty walking develops. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe pain, inability to bear weight, or a significant change in foot shape or function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:233;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:242;s:10:"disease_id";i:294;s:11:"overview_en";s:582:"A heel spur is a bony growth that develops on the underside or back of the heel. It may occur when repeated stress causes changes where tendons or ligaments attach to the bone. Heel spurs can occur with conditions such as plantar fasciitis and may or may not cause pain. A heel spur may be discovered incidentally during an X-ray performed for another foot problem. Pain is generally related more closely to inflammation or irritation of surrounding tissues than to the bony spur itself. Symptoms may be worse with the first steps after rest or after prolonged standing and walking.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:168:"हील स्पर एड़ी पर कैल्शियम जमा होने से बनने वाली हड्डी वृद्धि है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:661:"Heel spurs develop when repeated stress or pressure on the tissues attached to the heel causes bone to form gradually in response. Factors associated with their development include plantar fasciitis, prolonged standing or walking, repeated impact, certain foot structures, and excessive stress on the heel. Repeated pulling of the plantar fascia or other structures attached to the heel can stimulate gradual bone formation. Mechanical stress may produce small tears and inflammation in the surrounding tissues. Abnormal walking patterns, flat feet, high arches, tight calf muscles, and unsuitable footwear can increase the mechanical forces placed on the heel.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:131:"लगातार दबाव और प्लांटर फेशिया तनाव इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:605:"Risk factors include repeated stress on the feet, prolonged standing or walking, running and other high-impact activities, being overweight, abnormal foot mechanics, and wearing poorly supportive footwear. Age-related changes and conditions such as plantar fasciitis may also increase risk. People who spend long periods on their feet, participate in running or jumping activities, or have occupations involving repetitive walking may experience greater heel stress. Increased body weight, limited ankle flexibility, altered gait, and structural foot abnormalities can further increase mechanical loading.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:129:"मोटापा और लंबे समय तक खड़े रहना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:622:"Heel spurs are diagnosed using a medical history and physical examination. X-rays can show the bony growth and may help identify other structural changes in the foot. The presence of a heel spur does not always explain pain, so other causes of heel discomfort may also be evaluated. The clinician may examine the heel, assess tenderness, walking mechanics, ankle flexibility, and the range of motion of the foot. Imaging is considered when symptoms persist, the diagnosis is uncertain, or another structural problem is suspected. Other causes of heel pain should be considered before attributing symptoms solely to a spur.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:109:"निदान एक्स-रे द्वारा पुष्टि किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:628:"Heel spurs may be reduced by limiting repeated excessive stress on the feet, maintaining a healthy body weight, wearing supportive footwear, and using appropriate techniques during physical activity. Treating conditions such as plantar fasciitis may also reduce ongoing strain on the heel. Gradual increases in physical activity, appropriate footwear, stretching of tight calf and foot muscles, and attention to walking or running technique can reduce excessive stress. Maintaining a healthy weight can also reduce the load transmitted through the heel. Persistent heel pain should be assessed rather than repeatedly aggravated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:96:"उचित जूते और वजन नियंत्रण सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:342:"Heel spurs are generally not an emergency and may cause pain related to surrounding soft tissues. Seek medical assessment for persistent or worsening heel pain or difficulty walking. Prompt evaluation is appropriate when pain is severe, follows significant trauma, or is associated with swelling, redness, or other signs of another condition.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:234;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:243;s:10:"disease_id";i:295;s:11:"overview_en";s:547:"An Achilles tendon rupture is a partial or complete tear of the strong tendon connecting the calf muscles to the heel bone. It often occurs during sudden forceful activity such as jumping, running, or changing direction, but degeneration of the tendon can increase vulnerability. A person may feel or hear a sudden pop followed by pain, swelling, difficulty walking, and inability to push off normally with the affected foot. Prompt medical assessment is important because treatment decisions depend on the extent of the injury and the individual.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:157:"अकिलीस टेंडन रप्चर अकिलीस कण्डरा का आंशिक या पूर्ण फटना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:530:"Achilles tendon rupture can occur when the tendon is suddenly subjected to a force greater than it can withstand. Common situations include pushing off forcefully, jumping, sprinting, or suddenly changing direction. A tendon weakened by age, repeated stress, inflammation, or certain medical conditions may be more vulnerable. Previous Achilles tendon problems can increase risk. Some medicines have also been associated with tendon injury. The rupture may occur in a previously symptomatic tendon or unexpectedly during activity.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:119:"अचानक जोरदार गतिविधि या खेल चोट इसका कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:522:"Risk factors for Achilles tendon rupture include participation in sports involving running or jumping, sudden increases in activity, inadequate conditioning, previous tendon problems, increasing age, and certain medicines or medical conditions associated with tendon weakness. Men in middle age who participate in recreational sports are commonly affected. Tight or weak calf muscles and repeated tendon stress may contribute. A gradual training program and appropriate conditioning can reduce some activity-related risks.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:137:"खेल गतिविधियां और पूर्व टेंडन चोट जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:491:"Achilles tendon rupture is usually diagnosed from the history and physical examination. The clinician may assess the ability to walk and push off and perform the Thompson test, in which compression of the calf normally produces movement of the foot. Ultrasound can help identify the location and extent of a tear, while MRI may be used when the diagnosis or degree of injury remains uncertain. Prompt diagnosis helps determine whether nonsurgical treatment or surgical repair is appropriate.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:121:"निदान परीक्षण और इमेजिंग द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:535:"Achilles tendon rupture cannot always be prevented, but risk may be reduced by gradual increases in training, adequate warm-up, regular calf and lower-limb conditioning, and avoiding sudden large increases in exercise intensity. Proper footwear and appropriate recovery between demanding activities may also help. People with previous tendon problems should discuss safe progression of activity with a healthcare professional. Sudden Achilles pain or a popping sensation during activity should be assessed promptly rather than ignored.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:134:"उचित प्रशिक्षण और स्ट्रेचिंग जोखिम कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:366:"An Achilles tendon rupture requires prompt medical assessment. Seek urgent care after a sudden pop or snapping sensation, sudden severe pain near the heel, swelling, or difficulty pushing off the foot or walking. Emergency assessment is appropriate when the injury is associated with major trauma, an open wound, severe bleeding, or loss of circulation or sensation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:235;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:244;s:10:"disease_id";i:296;s:11:"overview_en";s:499:"Ankle sprain is an injury in which one or more ligaments supporting the ankle are stretched or torn. It commonly occurs when the foot twists inward, producing an inversion injury that affects the ligaments on the outer side of the ankle. Sprains range from mild stretching to complete ligament tears. Typical symptoms include pain, swelling, bruising, tenderness, and difficulty bearing weight. Recovery varies with severity, and some severe injuries may require immobilization or further treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:135:"एंकल स्प्रेन टखने के लिगामेंट का खिंचाव या फटना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:445:"An ankle sprain usually occurs when the ankle is forced beyond its normal range of motion. A sudden inward twisting movement is a common mechanism, especially during running, jumping, sports, or an unexpected step on an uneven surface. The supporting ligaments may be stretched, partially torn, or completely torn. Previous ankle injury can also contribute to recurrent sprains because weakness or instability may remain after an earlier injury.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:131:"मुड़ने वाली चोटें और गिरना इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:492:"Risk factors include sports and activities involving running, jumping, rapid changes of direction, or uneven surfaces. Previous ankle sprains can increase the risk of another injury when strength and stability have not fully recovered. Poorly fitting footwear, inadequate conditioning, and returning to demanding activity before rehabilitation is complete may also increase risk. Reduced ankle strength, balance, or flexibility can make it harder to control the joint during sudden movements.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:90:"खेल और असमतल सतह जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:497:"Diagnosis is usually based on the injury mechanism, symptoms, and physical examination. The clinician checks swelling, bruising, tenderness, range of motion, joint stability, and the ability to bear weight. X-rays may be needed when a fracture is suspected. MRI or other imaging may be considered when a significant ligament injury, persistent symptoms, or another structural problem is suspected. The severity of the sprain is assessed to guide protection, rehabilitation, and return to activity.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:152:"निदान परीक्षण और आवश्यकता अनुसार इमेजिंग द्वारा होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:561:"Proper footwear and gradual conditioning can reduce the likelihood of ankle sprains. Warming up before sports, strengthening the muscles around the ankle, and improving balance and coordination can improve joint control. Activities should be increased progressively rather than suddenly. After an ankle injury, completing rehabilitation and restoring strength and stability before returning to demanding sports can reduce recurrence. People with repeated sprains may benefit from additional support such as bracing when recommended by a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:108:"उचित जूते और संतुलन प्रशिक्षण सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:360:"Most ankle sprains are not emergencies and improve with appropriate treatment. Seek medical assessment when swelling, pain, or difficulty bearing weight is significant or does not improve. Prompt evaluation is important when there is severe deformity, inability to bear weight, numbness, loss of circulation, or concern for a fracture or major ligament injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:236;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:245;s:10:"disease_id";i:297;s:11:"overview_en";s:377:"An ACL tear is an injury to the anterior cruciate ligament, one of the major ligaments that stabilizes the knee. It commonly occurs during sports or activities involving sudden stopping, changing direction, landing from a jump, or a direct blow to the knee. A tear may cause a popping sensation, pain, swelling, reduced range of motion, and a feeling that the knee is unstable.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:153:"एसीएल टियर घुटने के एंटीरियर क्रूसिएट लिगामेंट की चोट है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:395:"An ACL tear usually results from a sudden force or movement that overstretches the ligament. Common mechanisms include rapidly changing direction, stopping suddenly, landing awkwardly from a jump, or pivoting while the foot remains planted. A direct blow to the knee can also damage the ACL. The injury may occur alone or together with damage to other knee ligaments, cartilage, or the meniscus.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:122:"अचानक मुड़ना और खेल चोट इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:383:"Risk factors include participation in sports involving cutting, pivoting, jumping, or rapid changes in direction, such as football, basketball, soccer, and skiing. Previous knee injury, inadequate conditioning, poor landing or movement mechanics, and muscle weakness may increase risk. Differences in anatomy and neuromuscular control can also influence susceptibility to ACL injury.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:144:"खेल गतिविधियां और पूर्व घुटने की चोट जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:371:"An ACL tear is diagnosed using the injury history and a physical examination of the knee. Tests such as the Lachman test and other stability maneuvers can indicate ligament injury. MRI may be used to confirm the diagnosis and identify associated damage to the meniscus, cartilage, or other ligaments. X-rays may be performed to check for fractures or other bone injuries.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:580:"निदान चोट के इतिहास, घुटने की शारीरिक जांच और लिगामेंट की स्थिरता जांचने वाले परीक्षणों पर आधारित होता है। ACL फटने की पुष्टि तथा मेनिस्कस, कार्टिलेज या घुटने की अन्य संरचनाओं की संबंधित चोट पहचानने के लिए MRI किया जा सकता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:418:"ACL injuries may be reduced through structured injury-prevention programs that include strength training, balance exercises, agility work, and instruction in safe jumping and landing techniques. Proper warm-up and conditioning are important before sports. Training that improves control of the hips, knees, and core may help reduce excessive forces on the knee during cutting, landing, and sudden changes in direction.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:144:"उचित प्रशिक्षण और व्यायाम चोटों से बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:359:"An ACL tear requires medical assessment, particularly after a twisting injury with a popping sensation, rapid swelling, instability, or difficulty bearing weight. Seek prompt orthopedic evaluation when significant instability or loss of function persists. Urgent assessment is appropriate when severe swelling, deformity, numbness, or major trauma is present.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:237;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:246;s:10:"disease_id";i:298;s:11:"overview_en";s:338:"A meniscus tear is an injury to one of the two pieces of cartilage that cushion and stabilize the knee joint. It may occur during twisting or pivoting movements, particularly during sports, or develop gradually as the cartilage becomes less resilient with age. Pain, swelling, stiffness, catching, or difficulty moving the knee can occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:115:"मेनिस्कस टियर घुटने के कार्टिलेज की चोट है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:388:"A meniscus tear can occur when the knee is forcefully twisted, rotated, or loaded while the foot is planted. Sports involving sudden changes of direction can cause acute tears. In older adults, the meniscus can become weaker and less flexible, allowing relatively minor movements to produce a degenerative tear. The pattern and severity depend on the force and condition of the cartilage.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:144:"मुड़ने वाली चोट और उम्र संबंधी घिसाव सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:377:"Risk increases with activities involving twisting, pivoting, squatting, or sudden changes of direction. Athletes participating in football, basketball, soccer, skiing, and similar sports may be more exposed. Increasing age also raises risk because the meniscus becomes less resilient. Previous knee injury, joint degeneration, and repetitive occupational stress can contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1041:"मेनिस्कस टियर के जोखिम कारकों में ऐसे खेल या गतिविधियां शामिल हैं जिनमें घुटने को अचानक मोड़ना या दिशा बदलना पड़ता है। दिशा में तेज बदलाव, बैठना, घुटने टेकना या घुटने को जोर से घुमाना चोट का जोखिम बढ़ा सकता है। उम्र बढ़ने के साथ मेनिस्कस कम लचीला हो जाता है, इसलिए बड़े वयस्कों में क्षयी प्रकार के टियर अधिक हो सकते हैं। घुटने की पिछली चोट या लंबे समय से चली आ रही घुटने की समस्या भी जोखिम बढ़ा सकती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:410:"Diagnosis is usually based on the history of injury, symptoms, and a physical examination of the knee. Specific movements and tests can help identify meniscal injury. X-rays may be used to assess bone problems or arthritis but do not directly show most meniscus tears. MRI can provide detailed images of the meniscus and surrounding structures when the diagnosis is uncertain or treatment planning requires it.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:103:"निदान परीक्षण और MRI द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:423:"Using proper technique, strengthening the muscles around the knee and hips, maintaining flexibility, and gradually increasing training intensity may reduce injury risk. Appropriate sports equipment and conditioning can help. Avoiding sudden increases in activity and using care during movements involving twisting or pivoting may also reduce risk. Previous knee injuries should be appropriately evaluated and rehabilitated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1219:"मेनिस्कस टियर को हमेशा रोका नहीं जा सकता, विशेषकर जब यह अचानक खेल की चोट या उम्र से संबंधित क्षय के कारण हो। सही खेल तकनीक अपनाना, गतिविधि से पहले वार्म-अप करना, घुटने के आसपास की मांसपेशियों को मजबूत करना और संतुलन सुधारना चोट के जोखिम को कम करने में मदद कर सकता है। प्रशिक्षण की तीव्रता धीरे-धीरे बढ़ाना और उपयुक्त जूते पहनना भी उपयोगी हो सकता है। जिन लोगों को पहले घुटने की चोट हो चुकी है, उन्हें कठिन गतिविधि शुरू करने से पहले पुनर्वास संबंधी सलाह का पालन करना चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:345:"A meniscus tear should be medically assessed when knee pain, swelling, catching, locking, or instability persists after an injury. Seek prompt care when the knee cannot fully straighten or bear weight, or when symptoms are worsening. Urgent evaluation is appropriate for major trauma, severe swelling, deformity, or significant loss of function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:238;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:247;s:10:"disease_id";i:299;s:11:"overview_en";s:518:"Patellar tendinitis is an overuse injury affecting the tendon that connects the kneecap to the shinbone. It is commonly associated with activities involving repeated jumping, running, or forceful contraction of the thigh muscles. Pain is usually felt at the front of the knee, particularly near the lower edge of the kneecap, and may initially occur during activity before becoming more persistent. Continued repetitive stress without adequate recovery can contribute to ongoing tendon irritation and reduced function.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:121:"पटेलर टेंडिनाइटिस घुटने की कण्डरा की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:541:"Patellar tendinitis usually results from repeated mechanical loading of the patellar tendon without sufficient recovery. Jumping sports, running, repeated squatting, and other activities that place substantial force through the knee can contribute. Sudden increases in training intensity, inadequate conditioning, muscle weakness or imbalance, and poor movement mechanics may increase tendon stress. Repeated microscopic injury can lead to changes within the tendon and persistent pain rather than a simple short-lived inflammatory response.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:135:"अधिक उपयोग और बार-बार कूदने की गतिविधियां कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:496:"Risk is increased by repetitive jumping or running, sudden increases in training volume or intensity, frequent high-impact activity, inadequate recovery, and reduced lower-limb conditioning. Muscle weakness or imbalance and movement patterns that place excessive load on the patellar tendon may also contribute. Athletes involved in sports requiring repeated jumping are commonly affected. Age, body composition, and previous tendon problems can further influence mechanical stress on the tendon.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:141:"खिलाड़ियों और घुटने पर बार-बार दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:493:"Diagnosis is generally clinical and based on the location and pattern of knee pain, activity history, and physical examination. Tenderness over the patellar tendon and pain with activities that load the tendon are characteristic findings. Ultrasound or magnetic resonance imaging may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain, symptoms persist despite treatment, or a significant tendon injury is suspected. Imaging can also help distinguish tendinopathy from other causes of anterior knee pain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:102:"निदान लक्षणों और परीक्षण पर आधारित है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:493:"Gradual increases in training load, adequate recovery between demanding activities, appropriate strength and conditioning, and proper exercise technique can reduce excessive stress on the patellar tendon. Athletes should avoid sudden large increases in jumping or running volume. Addressing lower-limb strength or movement problems and using suitable footwear and equipment may also help. Persistent tendon pain should be evaluated rather than repeatedly training through significant symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:99:"उचित वार्म-अप और प्रशिक्षण सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:329:"Patellar tendinitis is usually not an emergency and often relates to repetitive stress. Seek medical assessment when persistent pain, swelling, or weakness interferes with activity. Prompt evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe pain, a popping sensation, marked weakness, or inability to straighten the knee after an injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:239;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:248;s:10:"disease_id";i:300;s:11:"overview_en";s:468:"Deep vein thrombosis is a blood clot that forms in a deep vein, most commonly in the leg. It can cause swelling, pain, warmth, tenderness, or a change in the appearance of the affected limb, although some people have few or no noticeable symptoms. A major concern is pulmonary embolism, which can occur when part of the clot breaks away and travels to the lungs. Sudden shortness of breath, chest pain, coughing up blood, or fainting requires urgent medical attention.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:168:"डीप वेन थ्रोम्बोसिस गहरी नस में रक्त का थक्का बनने की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:491:"Deep vein thrombosis develops when conditions favor formation of a blood clot inside a deep vein. Reduced blood flow from prolonged immobility, increased tendency of the blood to clot, or injury to the inner lining of a blood vessel can all contribute. Surgery, hospitalization, serious illness, cancer, pregnancy, certain medicines, inherited clotting disorders, and prolonged travel can increase the likelihood of clot formation. Several risk factors may occur together in the same person.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:165:"लंबे समय तक निष्क्रियता, सर्जरी और रक्त जमने के विकार कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:451:"Risk increases with prolonged immobility, recent surgery, hospitalization, serious illness, cancer, pregnancy, use of estrogen-containing medicines, previous DVT or pulmonary embolism, inherited clotting disorders, obesity, and increasing age. Long-distance travel involving prolonged sitting can contribute, particularly when other risk factors are present. Smoking and certain chronic medical conditions may also contribute to overall clotting risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:162:"धूम्रपान, मोटापा, सर्जरी और लंबे समय तक आराम जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:444:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical findings, and assessment of the likelihood of DVT. Compression ultrasonography is commonly used to examine blood flow and detect a clot in the deep veins. A D-dimer blood test may help exclude DVT in selected people when the clinical probability is low or intermediate. If DVT is strongly suspected, treatment decisions and further testing are guided by the clinical assessment and initial test results.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान अल्ट्रासाउंड और रक्त जांच द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:525:"Regular movement can help reduce blood stasis during prolonged sitting or bed rest. During long journeys, periodically walk or move the legs when it is safe to do so. After surgery or serious illness, early mobilization should follow the healthcare team's recommendations. People with a high risk of thrombosis may be prescribed preventive anticoagulant treatment or mechanical measures. Maintaining a healthy weight, avoiding smoking, and managing medical conditions can also reduce overall cardiovascular and clotting risk.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:120:"नियमित गतिविधि और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:389:"Deep vein thrombosis requires prompt medical assessment because a blood clot can potentially travel to the lungs. Seek urgent care for new swelling, pain, warmth, or redness in one leg, especially when symptoms are unexplained. Emergency medical attention is required for sudden shortness of breath, chest pain, coughing up blood, fainting, severe dizziness, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:240;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:250;s:10:"disease_id";i:302;s:11:"overview_en";s:344:"Major depressive disorder is a mood disorder characterized by persistent depressed mood or loss of interest that interferes with daily life. Symptoms may affect sleep, appetite, energy, concentration, and functioning and generally persist for at least two weeks. Depression can affect people of different ages and may require ongoing treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:124:"मेजर डिप्रेसिव डिसऑर्डर अवसाद का गंभीर रूप है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:367:"The exact cause of major depression is not known. It is thought to result from a combination of biological, genetic, psychological, and environmental factors. Changes in brain function and genetic susceptibility may contribute, while stressful life events, certain medical conditions, alcohol or drug use, and long-term pain may trigger or worsen depressive symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:137:"आनुवंशिक, जैविक और पर्यावरणीय कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:331:"Risk of major depressive disorder may increase with family history, previous episodes of depression, stressful or traumatic life events, certain chronic medical conditions, long-term pain, substance or alcohol use, and other mental health conditions. Depression can occur even without an identifiable risk factor or family history.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:128:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, तनाव और आघात जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:377:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, their duration, their effect on daily functioning, medical history, and clinical assessment. Major depression generally involves depressed mood or loss of interest lasting at least two weeks along with other symptoms. Healthcare professionals may also assess for medical conditions, medicines, or substance use that could contribute to symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:372:"Major depressive disorder cannot always be prevented. Maintaining supportive social connections, regular physical activity, adequate sleep, healthy routines, and appropriate management of chronic medical conditions may support mental well-being. Recognizing persistent changes in mood or functioning and seeking professional help early may reduce the impact of depression.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:112:"शीघ्र सहायता और उपचार लाभकारी हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:457:"Major depressive disorder requires professional assessment and treatment when symptoms persist and interfere with daily functioning. Seek prompt care for worsening depression, severe withdrawal, inability to perform essential daily activities, or significant changes in sleep, appetite, or behavior. Emergency help is needed for suicidal thoughts or plans, inability to stay safe, severe self-neglect, psychotic symptoms, or other immediate safety concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:241;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:251;s:10:"disease_id";i:303;s:11:"overview_en";s:519:"Persistent depressive disorder is a chronic form of depression in which a person has a persistently low or depressed mood over a prolonged period. It was previously called dysthymia. In addition to depressed mood, people may experience low energy, poor concentration, changes in sleep or appetite, low self-esteem, or feelings of hopelessness. Symptoms can interfere with work, relationships, self-care, and daily activities. Some people with persistent depressive disorder also experience episodes of major depression.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:165:"परसिस्टेंट डिप्रेसिव डिसऑर्डर लंबे समय तक रहने वाला अवसाद है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:493:"The exact cause of persistent depressive disorder is not fully understood. Genetic and biological factors may contribute, and the condition can occur in families. Psychological and environmental influences may also affect vulnerability and persistence of depressive symptoms. The disorder is not caused by a single event in every person. A healthcare professional may consider medical conditions, medicines, substance use, and other mental health disorders when evaluating persistent low mood.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:127:"आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारक योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:542:"Risk may be influenced by family history of depression, previous depressive episodes, prolonged stress, social difficulties, and other mental health or medical conditions. Persistent depressive disorder can occur at different ages, and symptoms may appear differently in children, adolescents, and adults. Older adults may experience additional difficulties with self-care, isolation, or cognitive symptoms. Having another form of depression or a history of significant psychological stress may increase the likelihood of persistent symptoms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और दीर्घकालिक तनाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:486:"Diagnosis is based on the history and pattern of depressive symptoms over time. A clinician evaluates mood, sleep, appetite, energy, concentration, self-esteem, hopelessness, functioning, and any associated mental health symptoms. The duration and persistence of symptoms are important because persistent depressive disorder is characterized by a long-standing course. Blood or urine tests may sometimes be used to look for medical conditions that can contribute to depressive symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:145:"निदान मानसिक स्वास्थ्य मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:548:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent persistent depressive disorder, but early recognition of depressive symptoms and timely professional support may reduce their impact. Maintaining regular sleep, physical activity, healthy nutrition, supportive relationships, and meaningful daily activities can support overall mental health. People with a history of depression can work with their healthcare provider to recognize early signs of worsening and develop a plan for responding to them. Avoiding harmful substance use may also reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:95:"शीघ्र हस्तक्षेप लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:405:"Persistent depressive disorder can cause long-lasting depressive symptoms and should be medically or professionally assessed when they interfere with daily life. Seek prompt care when symptoms worsen, functioning declines, or hopelessness becomes significant. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal thoughts or plans, inability to remain safe, severe self-neglect, or other immediate safety concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:242;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:253;s:10:"disease_id";i:305;s:11:"overview_en";s:461:"Panic disorder is characterized by recurrent, unexpected panic attacks together with persistent concern about having additional attacks or significant changes in behavior related to them. A panic attack can cause sudden intense fear accompanied by symptoms such as a racing heartbeat, sweating, trembling, shortness of breath, dizziness, chest discomfort, or a feeling of losing control. The condition can interfere with daily activities and social functioning.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:148:"पैनिक डिसऑर्डर में बार-बार अचानक घबराहट के दौरे आते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:458:"The exact cause of panic disorder is uncertain. A combination of genetic, biological, psychological, and environmental factors may contribute. Some people may have increased sensitivity to bodily sensations associated with anxiety, while stressful life events or major changes can contribute to onset. Certain substances, medicines, stimulants, or medical conditions can produce panic-like symptoms and should be considered when evaluating recurrent attacks.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:126:"आनुवंशिक और मनोवैज्ञानिक कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:462:"Risk may be increased by a family history of panic disorder or other anxiety conditions, major life stress, traumatic experiences, and prolonged psychological strain. Other anxiety disorders, depression, or substance use may coexist with panic symptoms. Caffeine and other stimulants can worsen symptoms in susceptible individuals. Certain medical conditions can produce similar physical sensations, so recurrent unexplained attacks should be medically assessed.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:114:"तनाव और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:476:"Panic disorder is diagnosed through a clinical assessment of recurrent panic attacks, persistent concern about further attacks, behavioral changes, and their effect on daily life. The clinician also considers whether symptoms are better explained by another mental health condition, medication, substance, or medical disorder. Physical symptoms such as chest pain, faintness, or breathing difficulty may require appropriate medical evaluation before being attributed to panic.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:145:"निदान मानसिक स्वास्थ्य मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:464:"Panic disorder cannot always be prevented, but recognizing and addressing persistent anxiety or severe stress may help reduce the impact of symptoms. Regular sleep, physical activity, stress-management strategies, and limiting excessive caffeine or stimulant use may be useful. People experiencing recurrent panic attacks should seek professional assessment so that contributing medical, psychological, or substance-related factors can be identified and addressed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:84:"शीघ्र उपचार लक्षण कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:483:"Panic disorder should be professionally assessed when recurrent panic attacks or fear of further attacks interfere with daily life. Seek prompt evaluation when attacks are frequent, worsening, or causing major avoidance or functional impairment. Because panic symptoms can resemble serious medical conditions, emergency assessment is appropriate for new or severe chest pain, significant breathing difficulty, fainting, or other symptoms that could indicate an acute medical problem.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:243;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:254;s:10:"disease_id";i:306;s:11:"overview_en";s:481:"Social anxiety disorder is a persistent fear of situations in which a person may be observed, evaluated, or judged by others. It is more than ordinary shyness because the fear can substantially interfere with work, education, relationships, and routine activities. People may worry extensively before social situations and may avoid them altogether. Physical symptoms can include sweating, trembling, nausea, blushing, difficulty speaking, and a strong sense of self-consciousness.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:152:"सामाजिक चिंता विकार सामाजिक परिस्थितियों का तीव्र भय है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:471:"The exact cause of social anxiety disorder is not known. It may develop through a combination of biological, psychological, and environmental influences. The disorder can begin during adolescence. Experiences involving criticism, limited social opportunities, or highly protective environments may contribute in some people, although they do not explain every case. Genetic vulnerability and differences in how a person responds to social evaluation may also play a role.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:127:"आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारक योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:536:"Risk may be influenced by family history, temperament, previous negative social experiences, limited opportunities for social interaction, and certain environmental circumstances. The disorder often begins during the teenage years, although symptoms can occur at other ages. People with severe social anxiety may avoid situations that could otherwise provide education, employment, relationships, or social support. Some affected individuals may also develop problematic use of alcohol or other substances in attempts to reduce anxiety.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और नकारात्मक अनुभव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:547:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern and severity of social fear, avoidance, and interference with everyday functioning. A clinician asks about situations that trigger anxiety, the person’s thoughts and physical symptoms, avoidance behavior, duration of symptoms, and effects on work, school, and relationships. Information from family members or other trusted people may sometimes help describe the behavior. The clinician also considers other anxiety disorders, depression, substance use, and medical conditions that may produce similar symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:568:"There is no guaranteed method for preventing social anxiety disorder. Early recognition of persistent social fear and avoidance can allow treatment before the problem becomes more disabling. Maintaining supportive relationships and gradually engaging in appropriate social activities may help build confidence and coping skills. People who notice that anxiety is causing significant avoidance or interfering with education, employment, or relationships should seek professional assessment rather than relying on alcohol or other substances to manage social situations.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:104:"शीघ्र सहायता आत्मविश्वास बढ़ा सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:388:"Social anxiety disorder should be professionally assessed when fear of social or performance situations significantly interferes with work, education, relationships, or daily activities. Seek prompt care when avoidance or anxiety becomes substantially worse or limits essential activities. Emergency assistance is appropriate for immediate safety concerns or severe inability to function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:244;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:255;s:10:"disease_id";i:307;s:11:"overview_en";s:340:"Specific phobia is an anxiety disorder involving an intense and persistent fear of a particular object, situation, or activity. The fear is excessive in relation to the actual danger and commonly leads a person to avoid the feared situation. Examples include fears of animals, heights, flying, injections, blood, storms, or enclosed spaces.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:161:"विशिष्ट फोबिया किसी वस्तु या स्थिति का तीव्र और लगातार भय है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:334:"Specific phobias may develop through a combination of genetic, biological, psychological, and environmental factors. A frightening or traumatic experience involving the feared object or situation can contribute. Some fears may also be learned by observing another person’s fearful response. The exact cause varies among individuals.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:145:"आनुवंशिक, पर्यावरणीय और सीखे गए अनुभव कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:317:"Risk factors for specific phobia may include a family history of anxiety disorders or phobias, a highly sensitive or anxious temperament, traumatic experiences, stressful childhood experiences, and learning fear responses from others. The disorder can begin during childhood or adolescence but may develop at any age.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और आघातपूर्ण अनुभव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:349:"Specific phobia is diagnosed through a clinical interview and assessment of symptoms. A healthcare professional considers whether the fear is persistent, excessive, causes significant distress or impairment, and leads to avoidance. The clinician also considers whether another mental health condition or medical problem better explains the symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:327:"Specific phobia cannot always be prevented. Supportive childhood environments, healthy coping skills, early attention to persistent anxiety, and professional help after traumatic experiences may reduce the impact of fear and avoidance. Early treatment can also help prevent a phobia from becoming more disruptive to daily life.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:103:"शीघ्र परामर्श से गंभीरता कम हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:397:"Specific phobia is usually not an emergency, but professional assessment can be helpful when fear causes substantial avoidance or interferes with normal activities. Seek care when the phobia significantly affects work, education, relationships, travel, medical care, or other essential activities. Emergency assistance is appropriate for an immediate safety crisis or severe inability to function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:44:25";}i:245;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:256;s:10:"disease_id";i:308;s:11:"overview_en";s:405:"Obsessive-compulsive disorder is a mental health condition characterized by recurring unwanted thoughts, images, or urges called obsessions and repetitive behaviors or mental acts called compulsions. These symptoms can consume substantial time, cause distress, and interfere with daily life. People often recognize that the symptoms are excessive or difficult to control, although this awareness can vary.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:233:"ऑब्सेसिव कम्पल्सिव डिसऑर्डर में अनचाहे विचार और बार-बार किए जाने वाले व्यवहार होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:441:"The exact cause of obsessive-compulsive disorder is not known. Research suggests that genetic vulnerability, differences in brain circuits and neurotransmitter systems, temperament, and environmental influences may contribute. Stressful life events can worsen symptoms in susceptible people. OCD is not caused simply by poor discipline or a lack of willpower, and unwanted obsessive thoughts do not mean that a person intends to act on them.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:165:"आनुवंशिक, तंत्रिका संबंधी और पर्यावरणीय कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:438:"Risk factors for obsessive-compulsive disorder include a family history of OCD, certain genetic vulnerabilities, childhood adversity or trauma, and particular patterns of temperament. Symptoms may begin or worsen during periods of significant stress. Some people experience symptom onset or worsening around major life transitions. OCD can occur at any age, although symptoms often begin during childhood, adolescence, or early adulthood.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:114:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और तनाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:445:"Diagnosis is based on a detailed mental health assessment identifying obsessions, compulsions, their frequency and duration, the distress they cause, and their impact on functioning. Clinicians also assess whether symptoms could be explained by another mental health condition, substance use, medication, or a medical disorder. Structured questionnaires may assist assessment, but there is no single laboratory or imaging test that confirms OCD.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1214:"ऑब्सेसिव कम्पल्सिव डिसऑर्डर का निदान लगातार होने वाले ऑब्सेशन, कंपल्शन या दोनों तथा उनसे होने वाले तनाव या दैनिक जीवन में बाधा के चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन से किया जाता है। चिकित्सक लक्षणों के प्रकार, आवृत्ति और अवधि का आकलन करते हैं तथा आवश्यकता होने पर संरचित प्रश्नावली या इंटरव्यू का उपयोग कर सकते हैं। OCD की पुष्टि करने वाली कोई विशेष रक्त जांच या मस्तिष्क स्कैन नहीं है, हालांकि जरूरत पड़ने पर अन्य कारणों को अलग करने के लिए चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन किया जा सकता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:468:"OCD cannot reliably be prevented because its exact causes are not fully understood. Early recognition of persistent intrusive thoughts and compulsive behaviors can allow timely treatment and may reduce their impact on daily life. Supportive environments, stress management, and appropriate mental health care may be beneficial. Parents and caregivers should seek professional assessment when repetitive behaviors or fears become persistent, distressing, or disruptive.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:83:"शीघ्र उपचार लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:433:"Obsessive compulsive disorder should be professionally assessed when obsessions or compulsions are difficult to control, consume substantial time, or interfere with daily life. Seek prompt care when symptoms are worsening or significantly impairing functioning. Emergency assistance is appropriate for immediate safety concerns, suicidal thoughts, severe inability to care for oneself, or other acute psychiatric or medical concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1331:"जब ऑब्सेशन (बार-बार आने वाले विचार) या कंपल्शन (बार-बार किए जाने वाले काम) को कंट्रोल करना मुश्किल हो, उनमें बहुत ज़्यादा समय लगता हो, या वे रोज़मर्रा की ज़िंदगी में रुकावट डालते हों, तो ऑब्सेसिव-कंपल्सिव डिसऑर्डर (OCD) की प्रोफेशनल जांच करवानी चाहिए। अगर लक्षण बिगड़ रहे हों या रोज़मर्रा के कामों पर बुरा असर डाल रहे हों, तो तुरंत मदद लें। सुरक्षा से जुड़ी तत्काल चिंताओं, आत्महत्या के विचारों, खुद की देखभाल करने में गंभीर अक्षमता, या अन्य गंभीर मानसिक या मेडिकल समस्याओं के मामले में इमरजेंसी मदद लेना सही रहता है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:07:56";}i:246;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:257;s:10:"disease_id";i:309;s:11:"overview_en";s:455:"Post-traumatic stress disorder is a mental health condition that can develop after experiencing or witnessing a traumatic event involving serious injury, death, abuse, violence, disaster, or another extreme threat. Symptoms may include intrusive memories or nightmares, avoidance of reminders, negative changes in thoughts or mood, and increased alertness or startle responses. Symptoms can interfere with relationships, work, sleep, and daily activities.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:203:"पोस्ट ट्रॉमेटिक स्ट्रेस डिसऑर्डर किसी आघातपूर्ण घटना के बाद विकसित होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:445:"PTSD can occur after a traumatic event, but not everyone who experiences trauma develops the disorder. The reasons for this difference are not fully understood. Genetic factors, previous emotional trauma, individual responses to stress, family circumstances, and the nature or severity of the traumatic experience may all influence vulnerability. PTSD can occur after events such as assault, accidents, abuse, disasters, war, or sexual violence.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:80:"गंभीर आघात इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:402:"Risk may be influenced by previous trauma, earlier emotional difficulties, repeated or severe traumatic experiences, limited social support, and personal or family factors affecting responses to stress. Certain traumatic events may carry greater risk than others. Having symptoms soon after trauma does not necessarily mean PTSD will develop, because normal distress after trauma can improve with time.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1038:"PTSD किसी दर्दनाक घटना का अनुभव करने या उसे देखने के बाद विकसित हो सकता है, लेकिन आघात का अनुभव करने वाले हर व्यक्ति में यह विकार नहीं होता। बार-बार या गंभीर आघात, पहले के दर्दनाक अनुभव, कम सामाजिक सहयोग, लगातार तनाव या कुछ मानसिक स्वास्थ्य समस्याओं के इतिहास से जोखिम बढ़ सकता है। आघात के प्रति हर व्यक्ति की प्रतिक्रिया अलग होती है और जोखिम कारक यह निश्चित नहीं करते कि किसी व्यक्ति में PTSD विकसित होगा।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:435:"Diagnosis is based on a detailed clinical assessment of symptoms, their duration, their relationship to a traumatic event, and their effect on daily life. A mental health professional may ask about intrusive memories, avoidance, changes in mood and thinking, sleep, alertness, and functioning. PTSD is generally considered when the required symptom pattern persists for at least one month and causes significant distress or impairment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:791:"PTSD का निदान योग्य मानसिक स्वास्थ्य विशेषज्ञ द्वारा चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन के आधार पर किया जाता है। मूल्यांकन में आघात का अनुभव, लक्षणों का प्रकार और अवधि, दैनिक जीवन पर उनका प्रभाव तथा यह देखा जाता है कि लक्षण कम से कम एक महीने से बने हुए हैं या नहीं। PTSD की पुष्टि करने वाली कोई एक रक्त जांच या स्कैन नहीं है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:423:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent PTSD after trauma. Early access to supportive care, safe surroundings, practical assistance, and appropriate mental health support may help people cope after a traumatic event. People whose symptoms persist, worsen, or interfere substantially with daily life should seek professional evaluation. Avoiding alcohol and recreational drugs can also reduce factors that may worsen symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:123:"शीघ्र मनोवैज्ञानिक सहायता लाभकारी हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:451:"Post-traumatic stress disorder should be professionally assessed when symptoms persist, become very distressing, or interfere with daily functioning. Seek prompt care when symptoms worsen, sleep and functioning are substantially affected, or the person is struggling to control behavior. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal thoughts, thoughts of harming others, severe loss of behavioral control, severe confusion, or inability to remain safe.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1306:"जब पोस्ट-ट्रॉमेटिक स्ट्रेस डिसऑर्डर (PTSD) के लक्षण बने रहें, बहुत ज़्यादा परेशानी पैदा करें या रोज़मर्रा के कामों में रुकावट डालें, तो किसी प्रोफेशनल से इसकी जांच करवानी चाहिए। अगर लक्षण बिगड़ जाएं, नींद और रोज़मर्रा के कामों पर बुरा असर पड़े, या व्यक्ति को अपने व्यवहार पर काबू पाने में मुश्किल हो, तो तुरंत मदद लें। आत्महत्या के विचार, दूसरों को नुकसान पहुंचाने के विचार, व्यवहार पर काबू पूरी तरह खो देना, बहुत ज़्यादा उलझन या खुद को सुरक्षित न रख पाना जैसी स्थितियों में इमरजेंसी मदद की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:08:14";}i:247;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:258;s:10:"disease_id";i:310;s:11:"overview_en";s:379:"Acute stress disorder (ASD) is a trauma- and stressor-related mental health condition that can develop after experiencing or witnessing a traumatic event. Symptoms may include intrusive memories, avoidance, heightened arousal, and dissociation. ASD is diagnosed when significant symptoms occur from 3 days to 1 month after the trauma and cause substantial distress or impairment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:194:"एक्यूट स्ट्रेस डिसऑर्डर आघात के बाद होने वाला अल्पकालिक मानसिक विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:293:"Acute stress disorder occurs following exposure to a traumatic event. Trauma can include experiences involving actual or threatened death, serious injury, or sexual violence. Not everyone who experiences trauma develops ASD, and individual responses to traumatic events can vary substantially.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:95:"आघातपूर्ण अनुभव इसका कारण बनते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:324:"Risk may be increased by previous traumatic experiences, a history of post-traumatic stress disorder or other mental health conditions, and certain types of traumatic exposure, including interpersonal violence. However, it is difficult to predict which individuals will develop acute stress disorder after a traumatic event.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:96:"गंभीर तनाव और आघात जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:433:"Diagnosis requires a clinical assessment of the traumatic event, symptoms, their duration, and their effect on daily functioning. A qualified mental health professional may assess symptoms such as intrusion, avoidance, arousal, and dissociation while also considering other medical or psychological explanations. ASD is distinguished from PTSD partly by the timing of symptoms, with ASD occurring from 3 days to 1 month after trauma.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:127:"निदान लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:374:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent acute stress disorder after a traumatic event. After trauma, ensuring safety, obtaining appropriate support, and seeking professional help when distress is severe or interferes with daily life may support recovery. People with persistent or significant trauma-related symptoms should be evaluated by a qualified healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:108:"शीघ्र हस्तक्षेप जटिलताओं को रोक सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:444:"Acute stress disorder should be assessed when severe stress symptoms persist after a traumatic event or significantly interfere with daily functioning. Seek prompt professional care when symptoms are worsening, overwhelming, or preventing normal activities. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal thoughts, thoughts of harming others, severe behavioral disturbance, inability to remain safe, or other acute psychiatric or medical concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1434:"जब किसी दर्दनाक घटना के बाद गंभीर तनाव के लक्षण बने रहें या रोज़मर्रा के कामों में बहुत ज़्यादा रुकावट डालें, तो 'एक्यूट स्ट्रेस डिसऑर्डर' (अचानक होने वाला गंभीर तनाव विकार) की जाँच करवानी चाहिए। अगर लक्षण बिगड़ रहे हों, बहुत ज़्यादा परेशान करने वाले हों या सामान्य काम-काज में बाधा डाल रहे हों, तो तुरंत किसी प्रोफेशनल से मदद लें। आत्महत्या के विचार, दूसरों को नुकसान पहुँचाने के विचार, व्यवहार में गंभीर गड़बड़ी, खुद को सुरक्षित न रख पाना, या मानसिक या शारीरिक स्वास्थ्य से जुड़ी अन्य गंभीर समस्याओं के मामले में तुरंत इमरजेंसी मदद की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:08:29";}i:248;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:259;s:10:"disease_id";i:311;s:11:"overview_en";s:531:"Bipolar disorder is a mental health condition characterized by episodes of unusually elevated or irritable mood and episodes of depression. Mood episodes can affect energy, sleep, activity, concentration, judgment, and daily functioning. The pattern and severity vary between individuals, and periods of relatively stable mood may occur between episodes. Bipolar disorder includes different forms, including bipolar I and bipolar II. Accurate diagnosis is important because symptoms can overlap with other mental health conditions.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:150:"बाइपोलर डिसऑर्डर में अवसाद और उन्माद के एपिसोड होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:516:"Bipolar disorder is thought to result from an interaction of genetic, biological, and environmental factors. Having a close relative with bipolar disorder increases risk, but genes alone do not determine whether the condition develops. Differences in brain signaling and regulation of mood may contribute. Major stress, trauma, disrupted sleep, substance use, and other environmental factors can influence the timing or severity of episodes in susceptible people. These factors are not single causes of the disorder.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:142:"आनुवंशिक और जैविक कारक महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:501:"Risk factors for bipolar disorder include a family history of bipolar disorder or other mood disorders, genetic susceptibility, and certain environmental or psychological stresses. Major disruptions in sleep can affect people who are vulnerable to mood episodes. Substance use may worsen symptoms or complicate the course. The disorder can begin during adolescence or adulthood, although onset can occur at other ages. Having a risk factor does not mean that bipolar disorder will necessarily develop.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:91:"पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:543:"Bipolar disorder is diagnosed through a comprehensive psychiatric assessment that reviews current symptoms, previous mood episodes, duration and severity of changes, sleep, energy, behavior, functioning, substance use, and medical history. Information from family members may sometimes help clarify past episodes. There is no blood test or brain scan that independently confirms bipolar disorder. Clinicians also evaluate for conditions such as major depression, substance-induced symptoms, anxiety disorders, and other causes of mood changes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:543:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent bipolar disorder because genetic and biological factors contribute substantially. Maintaining regular sleep, avoiding substance misuse, managing stress, and obtaining early professional help for significant mood changes may help reduce triggers or complications in people who are vulnerable. People already diagnosed should follow their treatment plan and seek help if warning signs of a mood episode appear. Support from family, mental health professionals, and a stable daily routine can also be useful.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:127:"शीघ्र उपचार दीर्घकालिक परिणाम बेहतर कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:456:"Bipolar disorder requires ongoing professional assessment and treatment because mood episodes can substantially affect judgment, functioning, and safety. Seek prompt care for rapidly worsening depression, unusually elevated or irritable mood, markedly reduced need for sleep, impulsive behavior, or major functional changes. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal behavior, severe confusion, dangerous behavior, psychosis, or inability to remain safe.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1251:"बाइपोलर डिसऑर्डर के लिए लगातार प्रोफेशनल जांच और इलाज की ज़रूरत होती है क्योंकि मूड एपिसोड सोचने-समझने की क्षमता, कामकाज और सुरक्षा पर काफ़ी असर डाल सकते हैं। तेज़ी से बिगड़ते डिप्रेशन, असामान्य रूप से बहुत ज़्यादा या चिड़चिड़े मूड, नींद की ज़रूरत में बहुत कमी, बिना सोचे-समझे काम करने या कामकाज में बड़े बदलाव दिखने पर तुरंत मदद लें। आत्महत्या की कोशिश, बहुत ज़्यादा कन्फ्यूज़न, खतरनाक व्यवहार, साइकोसिस या खुद को सुरक्षित न रख पाने की स्थिति में इमरजेंसी मदद की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:08:51";}i:249;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:260;s:10:"disease_id";i:312;s:11:"overview_en";s:341:"Cyclothymic disorder is a mood disorder involving repeated periods of hypomanic symptoms and depressive symptoms that are less severe than full episodes of mania or major depression. These mood changes persist over an extended period and may affect relationships, work, school, and daily activities. Symptoms can vary in intensity over time.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:166:"साइक्लोथाइमिक डिसऑर्डर में बार-बार मूड में उतार-चढ़ाव होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:312:"The exact cause of cyclothymic disorder is not fully understood. Genetic factors, differences in brain function, temperament, and environmental or psychological influences may contribute. The disorder likely results from interactions among several biological and environmental factors rather than a single cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:105:"आनुवंशिक और जैविक कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:415:"Possible risk factors include a family history of mood disorders, inherited temperament, stressful life circumstances, and other psychological or environmental influences. Cyclothymic disorder may occur alongside other mental health conditions, although the exact factors determining individual risk are not fully established. Having a risk factor does not necessarily mean that a person will develop the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:130:"मूड विकारों का पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:330:"Diagnosis requires a detailed mental health assessment and review of mood symptoms over time. A clinician considers the duration, frequency, and pattern of hypomanic and depressive symptoms and determines whether they meet criteria for another mood disorder or are better explained by substances, medicines, or medical conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:311:"There is no established way to completely prevent cyclothymic disorder. Recognizing mood changes early, maintaining regular sleep and daily routines, reducing avoidable stress, avoiding substance misuse, and seeking professional support for persistent mood symptoms may help reduce disruption and complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"शीघ्र पहचान प्रबंधन में सहायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:387:"Cyclothymic disorder should be professionally assessed when recurring mood changes interfere with daily functioning, relationships, sleep, or work. Seek prompt care when symptoms become more severe or begin to resemble a major depressive or manic episode. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal thoughts, severe confusion, psychosis, dangerous behavior, or inability to remain safe.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:993:"जब बार-बार होने वाले मूड में बदलाव रोज़मर्रा के कामकाज, रिश्तों, नींद या काम में रुकावट डालें, तो साइक्लोथाइमिक डिसऑर्डर की पेशेवर जांच करवानी चाहिए। जब ​​लक्षण गंभीर हो जाएं या मेजर डिप्रेशन या मैनिक एपिसोड जैसे लगने लगें, तो तुरंत इलाज लें। आत्महत्या के विचार, बहुत ज़्यादा उलझन, साइकोसिस, खतरनाक व्यवहार या खुद को सुरक्षित न रख पाने की स्थिति में इमरजेंसी मदद की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:09:09";}i:250;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:261;s:10:"disease_id";i:313;s:11:"overview_en";s:376:"Schizophrenia is a serious mental health disorder that can affect thinking, perception, emotions, behavior, and the ability to function in daily life. Symptoms may include hallucinations, delusions, disorganized thinking, reduced emotional expression, social withdrawal, and difficulties with attention or decision-making. Symptoms and their severity vary between individuals.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:232:"सिज़ोफ्रेनिया एक दीर्घकालिक मानसिक विकार है जो विचारों और व्यवहार को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:319:"The exact cause of schizophrenia is not fully understood. Research indicates that genetic susceptibility interacts with environmental and developmental factors. Differences in brain development and signaling may also contribute. No single gene, life event, or personal characteristic is sufficient to explain all cases.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"आनुवंशिक और मस्तिष्क संबंधी कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:308:"Risk is influenced by genetic factors and may also be affected by certain complications during pregnancy or birth, exposure to some maternal infections, severe childhood stress or trauma, and certain patterns of substance exposure. Having a risk factor does not mean that a person will develop schizophrenia.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:111:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और नशा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:332:"There is no single laboratory test that establishes schizophrenia. Diagnosis requires a comprehensive psychiatric assessment of symptoms, their duration, and their effect on functioning. Medical tests, blood tests, imaging, and assessment for substance use may be used to rule out other conditions that can produce similar symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:353:"There is no established way to completely prevent schizophrenia. Because several genetic and environmental factors contribute to risk, prevention is complex. Early recognition of significant changes in thinking, perception, behavior, or functioning and timely professional assessment can support earlier care and reduce the impact of untreated symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:83:"शीघ्र उपचार लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:298:"Seek urgent help for thoughts or plans of suicide or serious self-harm, threats or plans to harm another person, severe agitation or confusion, inability to care for basic needs, or behavior that creates an immediate safety risk. Emergency assessment may be needed when safety cannot be maintained.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:903:"अगर आत्महत्या या खुद को गंभीर नुकसान पहुँचाने के विचार या योजनाएँ हों, किसी और को नुकसान पहुँचाने की धमकी या योजना हो, बहुत ज़्यादा बेचैनी या उलझन हो, अपनी बुनियादी ज़रूरतों का ध्यान न रख पा रहे हों, या ऐसा व्यवहार हो जिससे तुरंत सुरक्षा का ख़तरा पैदा हो, तो तुरंत मदद लें। जब सुरक्षा बनाए रखना मुमकिन न हो, तो इमरजेंसी में जाँच की ज़रूरत पड़ सकती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:09:33";}i:251;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:262;s:10:"disease_id";i:314;s:11:"overview_en";s:661:"Schizoaffective disorder is a mental health condition in which symptoms of psychosis occur together with significant mood episodes. A person may experience hallucinations, delusions, disorganized thinking, depression, or periods of unusually elevated or irritable mood. Symptoms and their severity vary among individuals. Schizoaffective disorder may involve periods in which psychotic symptoms occur with mood symptoms and periods in which psychosis occurs independently of a major mood episode. The pattern over time is important in distinguishing the disorder from schizophrenia, bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder, and substance-related conditions.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:215:"स्किजोअफेक्टिव डिसऑर्डर में सिज़ोफ्रेनिया और मूड विकार दोनों के लक्षण होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:632:"The exact cause of schizoaffective disorder is unknown. Researchers believe that genetic, brain, and environmental factors may contribute. Family history of psychotic or mood disorders may increase susceptibility, while stressful experiences or other environmental factors may influence when symptoms appear. The biological mechanisms underlying schizoaffective disorder are not completely established. Researchers have studied genetic susceptibility, neurotransmitter systems, brain development, and environmental influences. The disorder may represent an interaction among multiple factors rather than a single identifiable cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:105:"आनुवंशिक और जैविक कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:620:"Risk factors may include a family history of schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder, bipolar disorder, or other psychotic or mood conditions. Genetic susceptibility, stressful life experiences, and certain environmental or developmental factors may also influence risk. Having a close relative with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder, or related conditions may increase susceptibility. Other possible contributors include prenatal or developmental complications, severe stress, trauma, and exposure to certain substances. These factors are not sufficient by themselves to establish that a person will develop the disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:133:"मानसिक रोगों का पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:668:"Diagnosis requires a detailed psychiatric assessment and evaluation of the timing and pattern of psychotic and mood symptoms. Clinicians consider hallucinations, delusions, disorganized thinking, depression, and manic or other mood episodes while also excluding substance use, medical conditions, and other psychiatric disorders. Clinicians review the duration, frequency, and relationship between psychotic and mood symptoms. Information from family members may be useful when appropriate because insight can be affected during episodes. Assessment also considers medication effects, substance use, neurological disorders, and other causes before a diagnosis is made.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:652:"There is no established way to completely prevent schizoaffective disorder. Early recognition of psychotic or significant mood symptoms and timely professional care may reduce complications. Avoiding harmful substance use and maintaining supportive routines may also help overall mental health. Because the causes are multifactorial and incompletely understood, there is no established prevention strategy. Early attention to persistent hallucinations, delusions, severe mood changes, or major changes in functioning can facilitate timely assessment. Avoiding illicit substances that can provoke psychotic symptoms may reduce some preventable episodes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:104:"शीघ्र उपचार और निगरानी महत्वपूर्ण हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:457:"Schizoaffective disorder requires ongoing specialist mental-health care because it involves both mood and psychotic symptoms. Seek prompt professional assessment for worsening hallucinations, delusions, severe mood changes, disorganized behavior, or declining ability to care for oneself. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal or violent thoughts, severe confusion, dangerous behavior, inability to remain safe, or severe loss of contact with reality.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1197:"स्किज़ोअफेक्टिव डिसऑर्डर में मूड और मनोविकार दोनों तरह के लक्षण शामिल होते हैं, इसलिए इसमें निरंतर विशेषज्ञ मानसिक स्वास्थ्य देखभाल की आवश्यकता होती है। मतिभ्रम, भ्रम, गंभीर मनोदशा परिवर्तन, अव्यवस्थित व्यवहार या स्वयं की देखभाल करने की क्षमता में कमी आने पर तुरंत पेशेवर मूल्यांकन करवाएं। आत्महत्या या हिंसक विचार, गंभीर भ्रम, खतरनाक व्यवहार, सुरक्षित रहने में असमर्थता या वास्तविकता से पूरी तरह संपर्क टूटने की स्थिति में आपातकालीन सहायता आवश्यक है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:10:18";}i:252;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:263;s:10:"disease_id";i:315;s:11:"overview_en";s:402:"Delusional disorder is a mental health condition characterized by one or more firmly held false beliefs that persist for at least one month. The beliefs may concern subjects such as persecution, jealousy, relationships, or physical health. Unlike some other psychotic disorders, prominent hallucinations, disorganized speech, and other major psychotic symptoms are not typical features of the disorder.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:175:"डिल्यूशनल डिसऑर्डर में प्रमाण के बावजूद गलत विश्वास बने रहते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:349:"The exact cause of delusional disorder is not fully understood. Psychotic disorders can arise from a complex combination of biological, genetic, psychological, and environmental factors. Delusions can also occur as a result of certain medical conditions, medications, or substance use, so these possibilities need to be considered during evaluation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:124:"जैविक और मनोवैज्ञानिक कारक योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:340:"The factors associated with delusional disorder are not completely understood. It generally develops in adulthood and may occur more often in middle-aged or older adults. A history of certain personality traits or other psychiatric or medical conditions may be relevant, but no single factor reliably predicts who will develop the disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:114:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और तनाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:337:"Diagnosis requires a comprehensive psychiatric assessment and review of the person's history and symptoms. A healthcare professional evaluates the nature and duration of the beliefs and assesses whether other psychotic disorders, mood disorders, substance use, neurological conditions, or other medical causes could explain the symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:329:"There is no established method for reliably preventing delusional disorder. Early evaluation of persistent or unusual beliefs, particularly when they cause significant distress, conflict, or changes in behavior, can help identify possible mental health or medical causes and connect the person with appropriate professional care.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:104:"शीघ्र उपचार कार्यक्षमता सुधार सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:474:"Delusional disorder requires professional mental-health assessment when persistent false beliefs interfere with functioning or relationships. Seek prompt care when beliefs become increasingly distressing, behavior changes significantly, or the person becomes increasingly detached from reality. Emergency assistance is needed for dangerous behavior, severe confusion, hallucinations with loss of behavioral control, suicidal or violent thoughts, or inability to remain safe.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1305:"जब लगातार गलत सोच-विचार की वजह से रोज़मर्रा के कामों या रिश्तों पर बुरा असर पड़ने लगे, तो डिल्यूज़नल डिसऑर्डर के लिए किसी प्रोफेशनल मेंटल-हेल्थ एक्सपर्ट से जांच करवानी चाहिए। अगर ये सोच-विचार बहुत ज़्यादा परेशान करने वाले हो जाएं, व्यवहार में बड़ा बदलाव आए, या व्यक्ति असलियत से दूर होता जाए, तो तुरंत मदद लें। खतरनाक व्यवहार, बहुत ज़्यादा कन्फ्यूज़न, व्यवहार पर काबू खोने के साथ मतिभ्रम (hallucinations), आत्महत्या या हिंसा के विचार आने, या खुद को सुरक्षित न रख पाने की स्थिति में इमरजेंसी मदद की ज़रूरत होती है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:10:05";}i:253;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:264;s:10:"disease_id";i:316;s:11:"overview_en";s:419:"Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) is a neurodevelopmental condition involving persistent patterns of inattention, hyperactivity, and impulsivity that interfere with daily functioning. Symptoms can affect school, work, relationships, organization, and time management. ADHD commonly begins during childhood, although some people are diagnosed later when demands increase or symptoms become more noticeable.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"एडीएचडी ध्यान की कमी और अतिसक्रियता वाला न्यूरोडेवलपमेंटल विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:462:"The exact cause of ADHD is not completely understood. Research indicates that genetic factors play an important role, while differences in brain development and function may also contribute. Factors affecting development before or around birth may influence risk in some individuals. ADHD is not caused simply by poor parenting, lack of discipline, or inadequate motivation, although environmental circumstances can affect how symptoms are expressed and managed.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1052:"अटेंशन डेफिसिट हाइपरएक्टिविटी डिसऑर्डर का सटीक कारण पूरी तरह ज्ञात नहीं है। शोध से पता चलता है कि आनुवंशिक कारकों की महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका होती है और मस्तिष्क के विकास तथा कार्य में कुछ अंतर भी योगदान कर सकते हैं। समय से पहले जन्म, कम जन्म वजन और गर्भावस्था के दौरान कुछ प्रकार के संपर्क जैसे कारक जोखिम को प्रभावित कर सकते हैं। ADHD केवल खराब पालन-पोषण, अनुशासन की कमी या अधिक स्क्रीन उपयोग के कारण नहीं होता।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:494:"Risk factors and associated features include a family history of ADHD, childhood developmental differences, and certain prenatal or early-life factors. Symptoms may become more noticeable when academic, occupational, or organizational demands increase. Coexisting learning, behavioral, emotional, or sleep difficulties can complicate the presentation. Having one risk factor does not mean that a person will develop ADHD, and the condition can occur without an obvious identifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1248:"अटेंशन डेफिसिट हाइपरएक्टिविटी डिसऑर्डर के जोखिम से ADHD का पारिवारिक इतिहास और कुछ आनुवंशिक प्रभाव जुड़े हैं। समय से पहले जन्म, कम जन्म वजन और गर्भावस्था के दौरान कुछ प्रकार के संपर्क भी बढ़े हुए जोखिम से जुड़े पाए गए हैं, हालांकि इनमें से कोई कारक अकेले यह निर्धारित नहीं करता कि किसी व्यक्ति को ADHD होगा या नहीं। मस्तिष्क के विकास और पर्यावरणीय प्रभाव जटिल तरीके से एक-दूसरे से प्रभावित हो सकते हैं। ADHD केवल खराब परवरिश, अनुशासन की कमी या सामान्य बचपन के व्यवहार के कारण नहीं होता।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:449:"Diagnosis of ADHD involves a comprehensive assessment rather than a single laboratory or imaging test. A clinician considers the pattern, duration, severity, and impact of symptoms and determines whether they occur in more than one setting. Information from the individual, family members, teachers, or other relevant observers may be useful, especially for children. The assessment also considers alternative explanations and coexisting conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:164:"निदान व्यवहारिक और चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:519:"There is no established way to completely prevent ADHD because genetic and developmental factors play important roles. Supporting healthy pregnancy and early childhood development and reducing avoidable prenatal risks are generally beneficial for child health. Early recognition of persistent difficulties can allow appropriate educational, behavioral, and clinical support. Establishing predictable routines, sleep habits, organizational strategies, and supportive environments can help reduce functional difficulties.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:101:"शीघ्र हस्तक्षेप और सहयोग लाभकारी हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:394:"Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder generally requires planned professional assessment and management rather than emergency care. Seek evaluation when inattention, hyperactivity, or impulsivity significantly interferes with school, work, relationships, or daily activities. Prompt assessment is appropriate when behavior creates substantial safety risks or severe functional deterioration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1048:"ध्यान अभाव अतिसक्रियता विकार (ADHD) के लिए आमतौर पर आपातकालीन देखभाल के बजाय सुनियोजित पेशेवर मूल्यांकन और प्रबंधन की आवश्यकता होती है। जब ध्यान की कमी, अतिसक्रियता या आवेगशीलता स्कूल, काम, रिश्तों या दैनिक गतिविधियों में महत्वपूर्ण रूप से बाधा उत्पन्न करती है, तो मूल्यांकन करवाएं। जब व्यवहार से सुरक्षा संबंधी गंभीर जोखिम या गंभीर कार्यात्मक गिरावट उत्पन्न होती है, तो शीघ्र मूल्यांकन करना उचित है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:10:34";}i:254;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:265;s:10:"disease_id";i:317;s:11:"overview_en";s:550:"Autism spectrum disorder is a neurodevelopmental condition associated with differences in social communication and interaction together with restricted, repetitive, or unusually focused patterns of behavior, interests, or activities. The characteristics and degree of support needed vary widely between individuals. Some people may also have differences in sensory processing, learning, language, attention, or motor development. Autism begins during early development, although recognition may occur later when social or functional demands increase.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:252:"ऑटिज्म स्पेक्ट्रम डिसऑर्डर संचार और व्यवहार को प्रभावित करने वाला न्यूरोडेवलपमेंटल विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:494:"The causes of autism spectrum disorder are complex and involve genetic and developmental factors. Research supports a substantial genetic contribution, with many different genetic variants potentially influencing brain development. Environmental and biological factors may also interact with genetic susceptibility during prenatal or early development. Autism does not have one single cause, and the presence of an associated factor does not determine whether an individual will develop autism.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:861:"ऑटिज्म स्पेक्ट्रम डिसऑर्डर मस्तिष्क के विकास में अंतर से जुड़ी एक विकासात्मक स्थिति है। इसका कोई एक कारण नहीं है। शोध से पता चलता है कि कई आनुवंशिक, जैविक और पर्यावरणीय कारक ASD की संभावना में योगदान कर सकते हैं। कुछ लोगों में यह ज्ञात आनुवंशिक या क्रोमोसोमल स्थिति से जुड़ा होता है, जबकि कई लोगों में विशिष्ट कारण ज्ञात नहीं होता।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:500:"Autism spectrum disorder can occur in people with or without identifiable risk factors. Genetic susceptibility and certain developmental or biological factors are associated with increased likelihood. A family history of autism or certain genetic conditions may be relevant. Some prenatal or early developmental circumstances have been associated with increased risk, although associations vary and do not establish a direct cause. Autism occurs across all socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic groups.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:98:"पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ा सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:562:"Diagnosis involves a developmental assessment focused on social communication, interaction, repetitive behaviors, restricted interests, sensory characteristics, and the way these features affect daily functioning. Clinicians may gather information from caregivers, teachers, or other people familiar with the individual’s development. Developmental history is important because characteristics begin early in life, although they may become more noticeable later. Hearing, language, cognitive, neurological, and other developmental factors may also be assessed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1076:"ऑटिज्म स्पेक्ट्रम डिसऑर्डर का निदान विकासात्मक और व्यवहार संबंधी मूल्यांकन से किया जाता है; इसके लिए कोई एक रक्त जांच या इमेजिंग स्कैन पर्याप्त नहीं है। चिकित्सक संचार, सामाजिक संपर्क, दोहराव वाले या सीमित व्यवहार, विकास के इतिहास और दैनिक जीवन पर प्रभाव का आकलन करते हैं। स्क्रीनिंग टूल उन बच्चों की पहचान में मदद कर सकते हैं जिन्हें आगे मूल्यांकन की आवश्यकता है, लेकिन निदान के लिए व्यापक जांच जरूरी होती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:531:"There is no known method that can completely prevent autism spectrum disorder, and autism should not be viewed as a condition caused by parenting or ordinary childhood experiences. Appropriate prenatal care and management of maternal health are important for general developmental health. Early recognition of developmental differences allows timely access to educational, behavioral, communication, and other supports. Developmental surveillance during childhood can help identify children who may benefit from further assessment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:95:"शीघ्र हस्तक्षेप लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:418:"Autism spectrum disorder is a developmental condition that generally requires individualized, ongoing support rather than emergency treatment. Seek professional assessment when developmental, communication, behavioral, sensory, or functional difficulties require additional support. Prompt assistance is appropriate for severe behavioral changes, inability to meet basic needs, self-injury, or an acute safety concern.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1152:"ऑटिज़्म स्पेक्ट्रम डिसऑर्डर विकास से जुड़ी एक स्थिति है, जिसमें आमतौर पर इमरजेंसी इलाज के बजाय हर व्यक्ति की ज़रूरतों के हिसाब से लगातार मदद की ज़रूरत होती है। जब विकास, बातचीत, व्यवहार, सेंसरी या कामकाज से जुड़ी मुश्किलों के लिए अतिरिक्त मदद की ज़रूरत हो, तो किसी एक्सपर्ट से जांच करवाएं। व्यवहार में गंभीर बदलाव, बुनियादी ज़रूरतों को पूरा न कर पाना, खुद को नुकसान पहुंचाना या सुरक्षा से जुड़ी गंभीर चिंता होने पर तुरंत मदद लेना सही रहता है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:10:50";}i:255;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:266;s:10:"disease_id";i:318;s:11:"overview_en";s:615:"Conduct disorder is a behavioral and emotional condition in which a child or adolescent repeatedly violates the rights of others or important age-appropriate social rules. Behaviors may include aggression, destruction of property, deceitfulness, theft, or serious rule violations. The pattern is generally persistent rather than an isolated incident and can interfere with family life, education, friendships, and later functioning. The presentation can vary considerably, and assessment should consider the person’s developmental stage, environment, relationships, and other emotional or behavioral difficulties.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:154:"कंडक्ट डिसऑर्डर लगातार व्यवहारिक समस्याओं वाला विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:599:"The exact causes of conduct disorder are not fully understood. Development is thought to involve an interaction between individual characteristics and environmental influences. Possible contributors include temperament, difficulties with emotional regulation, adverse childhood experiences, family conflict, inconsistent discipline, exposure to violence, peer influences, and social circumstances. Attention-deficit or other behavioral difficulties may coexist. No single factor causes the disorder, and the presence of a particular risk factor does not mean that a child will develop the condition.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:143:"आनुवंशिक, पर्यावरणीय और सामाजिक कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:589:"Risk may be associated with a combination of individual, family, and environmental factors. These can include a history of significant behavioral difficulties, impulsivity, poor emotional regulation, family conflict, inconsistent supervision or discipline, exposure to violence or abuse, academic difficulties, problematic peer relationships, and environments in which aggressive or antisocial behavior is frequently observed. Other behavioral or developmental conditions may also occur at the same time. These factors increase vulnerability but do not determine an individual’s outcome.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:154:"पारिवारिक संघर्ष और व्यवहारिक समस्याएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:590:"Diagnosis requires a comprehensive assessment of persistent behavioral patterns rather than a single laboratory or imaging test. Clinicians consider the nature, frequency, duration, and circumstances of behaviors such as aggression, property destruction, deceitfulness, theft, and serious rule violations. Information from parents, caregivers, teachers, and the young person may be useful. The assessment also considers developmental history, family and social environment, education, substance exposure, and other mental or behavioral conditions that may explain or accompany the symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1344:"कंडक्ट डिसऑर्डर का निदान बच्चे या किशोर के व्यवहार, विकास और सामाजिक कार्यप्रणाली के व्यापक मूल्यांकन से किया जाता है। चिकित्सक ऐसे लगातार व्यवहार के पैटर्न की जांच करते हैं जिसमें दूसरों के अधिकारों या उम्र के अनुरूप महत्वपूर्ण सामाजिक नियमों का उल्लंघन होता है। माता-पिता, देखभाल करने वालों, शिक्षकों या अन्य विश्वसनीय स्रोतों से मिली जानकारी यह समझने में मदद करती है कि व्यवहार कितनी बार और किन परिस्थितियों में होता है। अन्य विकासात्मक, मानसिक स्वास्थ्य और पर्यावरणीय कारकों का भी मूल्यांकन किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:614:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent conduct disorder, but supportive environments may reduce the likelihood of persistent behavioral problems. Consistent and appropriate boundaries, positive parent-child relationships, stable supervision, early recognition of significant behavioral difficulties, and timely psychological or behavioral support can be helpful. Addressing family conflict, school difficulties, exposure to violence, and other environmental stressors may also reduce contributing influences. Early assessment is particularly important when aggressive or seriously disruptive behavior is persistent.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:115:"शीघ्र परामर्श और सहयोग लाभकारी हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:398:"Conduct disorder requires professional assessment because persistent behavioral problems can affect safety, relationships, education, and functioning. Seek prompt care when aggression, serious rule-breaking, self-harm, or dangerous behavior is escalating. Emergency assistance is appropriate for immediate threats of serious harm to the person or others, severe violence, or an acute safety crisis.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1042:"कंडक्ट डिसऑर्डर के लिए प्रोफेशनल जांच की ज़रूरत होती है क्योंकि लगातार व्यवहार संबंधी समस्याएं सुरक्षा, रिश्तों, पढ़ाई और कामकाज पर असर डाल सकती हैं। जब आक्रामकता, नियमों का गंभीर उल्लंघन, खुद को नुकसान पहुंचाना या खतरनाक व्यवहार बढ़ रहा हो, तो तुरंत मदद लें। अगर व्यक्ति या दूसरों को गंभीर नुकसान का तुरंत खतरा हो, बहुत ज़्यादा हिंसा हो या सुरक्षा का गंभीर संकट हो, तो इमरजेंसी मदद लेना सही रहता है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:11:05";}i:256;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:267;s:10:"disease_id";i:319;s:11:"overview_en";s:443:"Oppositional Defiant Disorder is a behavioral condition characterized by a persistent pattern of angry or irritable mood, argumentative or defiant behavior, and sometimes vindictiveness. The behavior is more frequent and severe than expected for the person’s age and can interfere with family, school, social, or other daily activities. Symptoms usually occur in interactions with authority figures or other people the individual knows well.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:158:"विपरीत अवज्ञाकारी विकार में लगातार विरोधी व्यवहार होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:423:"The exact cause of oppositional defiant disorder is not known. Researchers believe that a combination of biological, psychological, and environmental factors may contribute. Differences in temperament, difficulties with emotional regulation, family conflict, inconsistent discipline, stressful life circumstances, and certain developmental or mental health conditions may increase the likelihood of developing the disorder.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:120:"आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:351:"Risk factors for oppositional defiant disorder may include a difficult temperament, problems with emotional regulation, family conflict, inconsistent or harsh discipline, exposure to significant stress, and a family history of behavioral or mental health conditions. Other developmental or psychiatric conditions may also occur alongside the disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"पारिवारिक तनाव और व्यवहारिक विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:471:"Oppositional defiant disorder is diagnosed through a clinical assessment of behavior, emotions, and relationships. A healthcare professional considers the frequency, persistence, and severity of symptoms and whether they cause significant problems at home, school, work, or in social settings. Information from parents, caregivers, teachers, or other people may help establish the pattern of behavior. Other conditions that can cause similar symptoms are also considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:129:"निदान चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:427:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent oppositional defiant disorder. Early recognition of persistent behavioral difficulties, consistent and age-appropriate discipline, positive parent-child communication, predictable routines, and support for emotional regulation may help reduce problems. Early professional assessment can also help identify associated difficulties and provide appropriate behavioral or family-based support.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:123:"शीघ्र व्यवहारिक हस्तक्षेप लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:406:"Oppositional defiant disorder generally requires planned behavioral and mental-health assessment rather than emergency care. Seek professional evaluation when persistent defiance, irritability, or argumentative behavior significantly interferes with home, school, relationships, or daily functioning. Prompt assistance is appropriate when behavior becomes dangerous or there is an immediate safety concern.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";s:1033:"'ऑपोज़िशनल डिफायेंट डिसऑर्डर' (ODD) के लिए आम तौर पर इमरजेंसी केयर के बजाय, व्यवहार और मानसिक स्वास्थ्य की योजनाबद्ध जांच की ज़रूरत होती है। अगर लगातार बात न मानना, चिड़चिड़ापन या बहस करने वाला व्यवहार घर, स्कूल, रिश्तों या रोज़मर्रा के कामों में काफ़ी रुकावट डालता है, तो किसी एक्सपर्ट से जांच करवानी चाहिए। जब ​​व्यवहार खतरनाक हो जाए या सुरक्षा को लेकर तुरंत चिंता हो, तो फ़ौरन मदद लेना सही रहता है।";s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-12 03:11:24";}i:257;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:268;s:10:"disease_id";i:320;s:11:"overview_en";s:439:"Insomnia is a common sleep disorder involving persistent difficulty falling asleep, staying asleep, or obtaining restorative sleep despite having an adequate opportunity to sleep. It can cause daytime tiredness, poor concentration, irritability, reduced performance, and other difficulties. Insomnia may be short term or chronic and can occur on its own or alongside medical, psychological, medication-related, or sleep-related conditions.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:139:"अनिद्रा नींद आने या बनाए रखने में कठिनाई का विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:495:"Insomnia may result from stress, changes in schedule, travel, an uncomfortable sleep environment, or ongoing worries. Chronic insomnia can be associated with anxiety, depression, chronic pain, breathing problems, reflux, hormonal changes, or other medical conditions. Caffeine, nicotine, alcohol, some medicines, and irregular sleep schedules can also interfere with sleep. In some cases, behavioral patterns develop that maintain sleep difficulties even after the original trigger has resolved.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:143:"तनाव, चिंता और चिकित्सकीय स्थितियां सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:444:"Risk increases with ongoing stress, irregular sleep schedules, shift work, travel across time zones, older age, and certain medical or mental health conditions. Caffeine, nicotine, alcohol, some medicines, and poor sleep habits can contribute. A previous episode of insomnia may increase the likelihood of recurrence. People who experience persistent pain, breathing problems during sleep, or other sleep disorders may also have increased risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:125:"तनाव और अनियमित नींद की आदतें जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:498:"Diagnosis is based mainly on a detailed history of sleep patterns, daytime symptoms, health conditions, medicines, and lifestyle factors. A sleep diary may help identify patterns and triggers. Healthcare professionals may use questionnaires to assess insomnia and daytime sleepiness. A physical examination or laboratory testing may be used when an underlying condition is suspected. Sleep studies are generally reserved for cases in which another sleep disorder, such as sleep apnea, is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:144:"निदान नींद के इतिहास और मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:475:"Consistent sleep and wake times, a comfortable dark and quiet bedroom, regular physical activity, and limiting caffeine and nicotine later in the day can support healthy sleep. Avoiding heavy meals and excessive alcohol close to bedtime may also help. Limiting stimulating activities and bright screens before bed can be useful for some people. Persistent insomnia should be evaluated, particularly when it causes significant daytime impairment or occurs with other symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:100:"अच्छी नींद की आदतें सहायक हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:357:"Insomnia is usually not an emergency and can often be managed through planned medical assessment and appropriate sleep treatment. Seek care when persistent sleep problems interfere with daytime functioning, mood, concentration, or safety. Prompt assessment is important when severe daytime sleepiness creates a risk of accidents, particularly while driving.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:258;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:269;s:10:"disease_id";i:321;s:11:"overview_en";s:387:"Hypersomnia refers to excessive sleepiness or an excessive need for sleep that interferes with normal daytime functioning. Affected people may have difficulty staying awake during the day, sleep for unusually long periods, or experience prolonged sleep without feeling adequately refreshed. Hypersomnia can occur as a symptom of another condition or as part of a specific sleep disorder.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:158:"हाइपरसोम्निया पर्याप्त नींद के बावजूद अत्यधिक नींद आना है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:372:"Possible causes include insufficient or disrupted nighttime sleep, sleep apnea and other sleep disorders, depression and other medical conditions, certain medicines or substances, neurological disorders, and disturbances of the body clock. Some people have central disorders of hypersomnolence in which excessive sleepiness persists despite adequate opportunity for sleep.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"तंत्रिका संबंधी, मानसिक और चिकित्सकीय कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:257:"Risk depends on the underlying cause and may include chronic sleep deprivation, irregular work schedules, sleep disorders, certain medicines, alcohol or other substances, neurological or psychiatric conditions, and family history of sleep-related disorders.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:121:"नींद विकार और कुछ बीमारियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:354:"Diagnosis begins with a detailed sleep history, assessment of daytime sleepiness, medication and substance review, and evaluation for medical or psychological causes. A sleep diary, sleep questionnaires, overnight polysomnography, multiple sleep latency testing, or other specialized investigations may be used when a primary sleep disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:131:"निदान स्लीप स्टडी और परीक्षण द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:412:"Maintaining a regular sleep schedule, allowing adequate time for nighttime sleep, limiting substances that disrupt sleep, treating sleep apnea and other underlying conditions, and reviewing medicines that cause excessive sleepiness may reduce preventable daytime sleepiness. Persistent or severe sleepiness should be medically evaluated, particularly when it affects driving or other safety-sensitive activities.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:109:"शीघ्र निदान प्रबंधन में सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:406:"Hypersomnia should be medically assessed when excessive daytime sleepiness persists, interferes with daily functioning, or causes unintended sleep episodes. Seek prompt evaluation when sleepiness is worsening or creates safety problems. Urgent assessment is appropriate when sudden severe sleepiness is accompanied by confusion, neurological symptoms, difficulty staying awake, or other concerning changes.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:259;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:270;s:10:"disease_id";i:322;s:11:"overview_en";s:387:"Narcolepsy is a chronic neurological disorder that causes excessive daytime sleepiness and an uncontrollable tendency to fall asleep during the day. Some people also experience cataplexy, a sudden temporary loss of muscle control triggered by emotions. Other features may include sleep paralysis, vivid dream-like experiences when falling asleep or waking, and disrupted nighttime sleep.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:184:"नार्कोलेप्सी अत्यधिक दिन में नींद आने वाला तंत्रिका संबंधी विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:430:"Narcolepsy is associated with abnormalities in the brain systems that regulate sleep and wakefulness. Narcolepsy with cataplexy is commonly linked to a major loss of neurons that produce hypocretin, also called orexin, a chemical involved in maintaining wakefulness. Genetic susceptibility and immune-system factors may contribute. In some cases, narcolepsy can occur after certain brain injuries or other neurological conditions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:165:"नींद नियंत्रित करने वाली मस्तिष्क क्रियाओं की समस्या कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:445:"Risk may be influenced by family history and genetic susceptibility. Having a close relative with narcolepsy may increase the likelihood of developing the disorder, although most people with narcolepsy do not have an affected close family member. Certain neurological injuries or diseases may also be associated with secondary forms of narcolepsy. The condition can begin at different ages but often starts during adolescence or young adulthood.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:136:"आनुवंशिक और तंत्रिका संबंधी कारक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:503:"Diagnosis requires assessment of daytime sleepiness, nighttime sleep patterns, cataplexy and other symptoms. A healthcare professional may use sleep diaries and standardized sleepiness questionnaires. Overnight polysomnography can evaluate nighttime sleep and exclude other sleep disorders. A multiple sleep latency test performed during the following day can measure how quickly a person falls asleep and whether REM sleep occurs unusually early. Hypocretin testing may be considered in selected cases.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:162:"निदान स्लीप स्टडी और विशेषज्ञ मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:503:"There is no established way to prevent most cases of narcolepsy because its underlying causes are not fully understood. Recognizing persistent excessive daytime sleepiness and seeking evaluation can help identify the disorder and reduce associated problems. People with narcolepsy should follow their treatment plan, maintain regular sleep schedules, use planned naps when advised, and take appropriate precautions around driving, operating machinery, and other activities affected by sudden sleepiness.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:108:"शीघ्र उपचार जीवन गुणवत्ता सुधार सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:396:"Narcolepsy requires medical assessment because sudden sleep episodes and related symptoms can affect safety and daily functioning. Seek prompt evaluation when excessive daytime sleepiness or sudden loss of muscle control interferes with normal activities. Urgent care is appropriate when symptoms result in injury, dangerous sleep episodes, or significant sudden changes in neurological function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:260;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:271;s:10:"disease_id";i:323;s:11:"overview_en";s:398:"Sleepwalking, also called somnambulism, is a sleep disorder in which a person gets out of bed or performs other activities while remaining asleep. Episodes usually occur during deep non-REM sleep early in the night. A person may walk, talk, sit up, or perform simple activities and often has little or no memory of the episode after waking. Sleepwalking is more common in children and young adults.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:183:"नींद में चलना एक विकार है जिसमें व्यक्ति नींद में गतिविधियां करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:364:"Sleepwalking is associated with arousal from deep non-REM sleep before the brain is fully awake. It tends to run in families and may be associated with fatigue, sleep deprivation, anxiety, or disrupted sleep. In adults, alcohol, some medicines, seizures, and other medical or mental health conditions can contribute. The exact cause may vary from person to person.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:97:"नींद की कमी और तनाव सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:396:"Risk factors include a family history of sleepwalking, insufficient sleep, irregular sleep schedules, stress or anxiety, and some medicines or substances. Children and young adults are more likely to experience episodes because they spend more time in deep sleep. In adults, recurrent episodes may warrant evaluation for sleep disorders, medication effects, seizures, or other medical conditions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:127:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और खराब नींद जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:467:"Sleepwalking is usually diagnosed from the history of episodes and information from the person or someone who has observed them. A physical examination and additional testing are not usually required when the pattern is typical. If episodes are frequent, unusual, dangerous, or associated with other symptoms, a healthcare professional may evaluate for conditions such as seizures or other sleep disorders and may consider a mental health assessment when appropriate.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:140:"निदान इतिहास और स्लीप मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:462:"Adequate regular sleep and a consistent bedtime routine may reduce sleepwalking episodes. Avoiding sleep deprivation, limiting alcohol when it triggers episodes, and addressing stress or anxiety can also help. The sleeping environment should be made safer by removing trip hazards, securing windows and doors when necessary, and blocking access to dangerous areas such as stairs. Frequent or dangerous episodes should be discussed with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:113:"स्वस्थ नींद की आदतें एपिसोड कम कर सकती हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:395:"Sleepwalking is usually not an emergency, but recurrent episodes can cause falls, injuries, or unsafe behavior. Seek medical assessment when episodes are frequent, begin suddenly in adulthood, cause injury, or significantly disrupt sleep. Prompt evaluation is appropriate when episodes involve dangerous behavior, confusion that persists after waking, or another concerning neurological symptom.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:261;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:272;s:10:"disease_id";i:324;s:11:"overview_en";s:454:"Nightmare disorder involves repeated, disturbing dreams that cause significant distress or interfere with sleep and daytime functioning. Nightmares may lead to repeated awakenings, difficulty returning to sleep, fear of going to bed, daytime fatigue, or anxiety about sleep. Occasional nightmares are common, but frequent or persistent episodes may warrant evaluation for contributing psychological, medical, medication-related, or sleep-related factors.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:154:"दुःस्वप्न विकार में बार-बार परेशान करने वाले सपने आते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:475:"Nightmares can be associated with stress, anxiety, trauma, major life changes, sleep deprivation, irregular sleep schedules, and other emotional or psychological factors. Certain medicines and substances can also influence dreaming. Sleep disorders and other medical conditions may contribute in some cases. In children, nightmares may occur as part of normal development, while persistent severe nightmares can be associated with traumatic experiences or other difficulties.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:108:"तनाव, आघात और नींद विकार कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:465:"Risk factors include frequent stress or anxiety, traumatic experiences, disrupted sleep schedules, sleep deprivation, and some medicines or substances. Children commonly experience nightmares, and episodes can increase during periods of developmental or emotional change. People with post-traumatic stress disorder or other psychological conditions may experience recurrent distressing dreams. Persistent nightmares can also occur alongside certain sleep disorders.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:114:"चिंता और आघातपूर्ण अनुभव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:419:"Nightmare disorder is diagnosed primarily from the history and pattern of recurrent disturbing dreams, awakenings, distress, and daytime impairment. A clinician may ask about sleep schedules, medications, substances, trauma, stress, mental health, and other sleep symptoms. A sleep diary can help document patterns. A sleep study is not routinely required but may be considered when another sleep disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:109:"निदान नींद के इतिहास द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:450:"Occasional nightmares are common and cannot always be prevented. Maintaining a consistent sleep schedule, getting adequate sleep, managing stress, and avoiding excessive stimulation before bedtime may help promote healthier sleep. Addressing trauma, anxiety, or other psychological difficulties can be important when nightmares are recurrent. Reviewing medicines or substances that may affect dreams with a healthcare professional can also be useful.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:86:"तनाव प्रबंधन लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:348:"Nightmare disorder is generally not an emergency. Seek professional assessment when recurrent nightmares significantly disrupt sleep, daytime functioning, or emotional well-being. Prompt care is appropriate when nightmares are associated with severe distress, trauma-related symptoms, suicidal thoughts, or other significant mental-health concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:262;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:273;s:10:"disease_id";i:325;s:11:"overview_en";s:464:"Anorexia nervosa is a serious eating disorder characterized by restriction of food intake, significantly low body weight, an intense fear of gaining weight, and a disturbed perception of body weight or shape. People with anorexia may severely limit food, exercise excessively, or use other behaviors to lose weight. The disorder can affect nutrition, bones, the heart, hormones, and other body systems, and it can occur in people of different ages and backgrounds.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:173:"एनोरेक्सिया नर्वोसा भोजन सीमित करने और कम वजन वाला भोजन विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:488:"The exact cause of anorexia nervosa is not fully understood. Genetic, biological, psychological, and social factors may all contribute. Differences in brain and hormone function may play a role, while attitudes about body shape and weight can influence risk. Certain personality traits, anxiety, negative self-image, perfectionism, and earlier eating difficulties may also contribute. Anorexia can develop through an interaction of several factors rather than from one identifiable cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:149:"मनोवैज्ञानिक, आनुवंशिक और सामाजिक कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:492:"Risk factors include a strong concern about body weight or shape, negative self-image, perfectionistic or highly rule-focused behavior, anxiety disorders, and certain social or cultural pressures related to appearance. Eating difficulties during childhood or adolescence may also be associated with increased risk. Anorexia commonly begins during the preteen or teenage years or young adulthood and is more frequently diagnosed in females, although it can affect males and people of all ages.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:156:"शारीरिक छवि की चिंता और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:556:"Diagnosis involves assessment of eating behavior, weight changes, thoughts about food and body image, and physical health. A healthcare professional may perform a physical examination and order tests to identify complications of inadequate nutrition or other causes of weight loss. Blood counts, electrolyte and kidney tests, liver and thyroid tests, protein measurements, urinalysis, electrocardiography, and bone-density testing may be used when appropriate. Psychological assessment also helps identify the characteristic eating and body-image concerns.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:173:"निदान चिकित्सकीय और मनोवैज्ञानिक मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:601:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent anorexia nervosa, but early recognition of unhealthy eating behaviors and excessive concern about weight may allow treatment before severe complications develop. Healthy attitudes toward food, body image, and physical activity can be encouraged in families, schools, and healthcare settings. Avoiding harmful dieting practices and discussing persistent concerns about weight, eating, or body image with a qualified professional can support early identification. People recovering from an eating disorder benefit from continued medical and psychological follow-up.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:95:"शीघ्र हस्तक्षेप लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:478:"Anorexia nervosa requires prompt medical and mental-health assessment because severe restriction and malnutrition can cause serious medical complications. Seek urgent care for significant weakness, fainting, dehydration, very slow or irregular heartbeat, chest symptoms, confusion, or inability to maintain adequate nutrition or fluids. Emergency evaluation is needed for loss of consciousness, severe cardiac symptoms, severe dehydration, or other signs of medical instability.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:263;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:274;s:10:"disease_id";i:326;s:11:"overview_en";s:571:"Bulimia nervosa is an eating disorder characterized by repeated episodes of binge eating followed by behaviors intended to prevent weight gain, such as self-induced vomiting or misuse of laxatives. People may feel a loss of control during binge episodes and experience intense concern about body weight or shape. The disorder can occur at any body size and may not be obvious to others. Repeated compensatory behaviors can cause serious physical complications, including electrolyte disturbances, dental damage, gastrointestinal problems, and heart-related abnormalities.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:242:"बुलिमिया नर्वोसा भोजन विकार है जिसमें अत्यधिक भोजन और बाद में क्षतिपूर्ति व्यवहार होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:541:"Bulimia nervosa develops through a combination of biological, psychological, social, and environmental factors rather than a single cause. Genetic and biological factors may increase vulnerability, while concerns about body weight and shape can contribute to disordered eating patterns. Dieting, pressure to achieve a particular appearance, stressful life experiences, and certain personality or emotional factors may play a role. The condition can become reinforced by a cycle of binge eating, guilt or distress, and compensatory behaviors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1158:"बुलिमिया नर्वोसा का सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं है। यह संभवतः आनुवंशिक, जैविक, मनोवैज्ञानिक और सामाजिक कारकों के संयोजन से विकसित होता है। वजन या शरीर की बनावट को लेकर अत्यधिक चिंता, कम आत्मसम्मान, भावनात्मक तनाव और बार-बार डाइटिंग इसका योगदान कर सकते हैं। ईटिंग डिसऑर्डर या कुछ मानसिक स्वास्थ्य स्थितियों का पारिवारिक इतिहास भी संवेदनशीलता बढ़ा सकता है। शरीर की छवि को लेकर सामाजिक और सांस्कृतिक दबाव भी इस विकार के विकास को प्रभावित कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:498:"Risk factors for bulimia nervosa include a history of dieting, strong concerns about body weight or shape, pressure related to appearance, family or personal vulnerability to eating disorders, and certain psychological or emotional difficulties. Adolescence and young adulthood are common periods for onset, although the disorder can occur at any age. Social pressures, stressful experiences, and environments that emphasize weight or appearance may contribute, but no single factor causes bulimia.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:819:"बुलिमिया नर्वोसा का जोखिम आनुवंशिक, जैविक, मनोवैज्ञानिक, व्यवहारिक और सामाजिक कारकों के संयोजन से प्रभावित हो सकता है। वजन या शरीर के आकार को लेकर चिंता, बार-बार डाइटिंग, शरीर की छवि से असंतोष और अन्य मानसिक स्वास्थ्य समस्याएं जोखिम बढ़ा सकती हैं। ईटिंग डिसऑर्डर का पारिवारिक इतिहास भी संवेदनशीलता बढ़ा सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:586:"Diagnosis of bulimia nervosa involves a detailed assessment of eating patterns, binge episodes, compensatory behaviors, body-image concerns, mental health, and physical health. Clinicians may use established diagnostic criteria together with interviews and questionnaires. Physical examination and laboratory tests can identify complications such as dehydration or electrolyte abnormalities. An electrocardiogram may be needed when purging or electrolyte disturbance creates a risk of heart rhythm problems. Assessment should also consider other eating disorders and medical conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1060:"बुलिमिया नर्वोसा का निदान भोजन संबंधी व्यवहार, बार-बार अधिक मात्रा में भोजन करने के एपिसोड, स्वयं उल्टी कराने या लैक्सेटिव के गलत उपयोग जैसे प्रतिपूरक व्यवहार और वजन या शरीर के आकार को लेकर अत्यधिक चिंता के चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन से किया जाता है। चिकित्सक शारीरिक स्वास्थ्य, पोषण, इलेक्ट्रोलाइट और अन्य जटिलताओं का भी आकलन कर सकते हैं। बुलिमिया नर्वोसा की पुष्टि करने वाली कोई एक प्रयोगशाला जांच नहीं है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:581:"Bulimia nervosa cannot always be prevented, but early recognition of unhealthy eating patterns and body-image concerns may help reduce progression. Avoiding repeated restrictive dieting and promoting balanced eating habits can be helpful. Families, schools, and healthcare professionals can encourage healthy attitudes toward food, weight, and appearance. People showing recurrent binge eating, vomiting, laxative misuse, or intense fear of weight gain should receive professional assessment. Early treatment can reduce the risk of serious physical and psychological complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:106:"शीघ्र उपचार रिकवरी में सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:436:"Bulimia nervosa requires professional assessment because recurrent bingeing and purging can cause dehydration and dangerous electrolyte or heart problems. Seek prompt care for persistent vomiting, weakness, dizziness, fainting, dehydration, or symptoms suggesting an electrolyte disturbance. Emergency evaluation is needed for fainting, severe chest symptoms, confusion, seizures, severe weakness, or other signs of medical instability.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:264;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:275;s:10:"disease_id";i:327;s:11:"overview_en";s:542:"Binge eating disorder is an eating disorder characterized by repeated episodes of eating unusually large amounts of food while feeling unable to control the eating. Episodes may involve eating rapidly, eating when not physically hungry, continuing until uncomfortably full, or eating alone because of embarrassment. Unlike bulimia nervosa, binge eating is not routinely followed by behaviors such as self-induced vomiting or misuse of laxatives to compensate for eating. The disorder is treatable and can affect physical and emotional health.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:158:"अत्यधिक भोजन विकार में बार-बार बहुत अधिक भोजन करना शामिल है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:498:"The exact cause of binge eating disorder is not known. Genetic factors and differences in brain chemicals may contribute, and having close relatives with an eating disorder can increase susceptibility. Emotional distress such as depression, anxiety, stress, or other difficult feelings may contribute to episodes. Unhealthy dieting, severe food restriction, or regularly skipping meals can also contribute to cycles of overeating. Several biological, psychological, and social factors may interact.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:158:"मनोवैज्ञानिक, आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:541:"Risk factors include a family history of eating disorders, emotional distress, depression or anxiety, and patterns of restrictive or irregular eating. Experiences that contribute to negative emotions or difficulty managing stress may increase vulnerability. Binge eating can occur in people of different ages and backgrounds and may occur with other mental health or eating-related conditions. Body weight alone does not establish whether a person has binge eating disorder, so assessment should focus on eating behavior and loss of control.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:841:"बिंज ईटिंग डिसऑर्डर के जोखिम कारकों में खाने के विकारों का पारिवारिक इतिहास, आनुवंशिक या जैविक प्रभाव, तनाव या अवसाद जैसी कठिन भावनाएँ और अस्वास्थ्यकर डाइटिंग की आदतें, जैसे भोजन छोड़ना या बहुत कम खाना, शामिल हो सकते हैं। यह विकार अलग-अलग शरीर के आकार वाले लोगों में हो सकता है और इसे केवल इच्छाशक्ति की कमी नहीं माना जाता।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:526:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern and frequency of binge-eating episodes, the sense of loss of control, associated behaviors and emotions, and the absence of regular compensatory behaviors characteristic of bulimia. A healthcare professional will ask about eating habits and symptoms and may perform a physical examination. Blood tests or other medical assessments may be used to identify health effects or related conditions. Psychological evaluation can help identify emotional factors and coexisting mental health problems.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:173:"निदान चिकित्सकीय और मनोवैज्ञानिक मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:549:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent binge eating disorder, but regular and balanced eating patterns may help avoid cycles of severe restriction followed by overeating. Developing healthy ways to manage stress and emotional distress can also be useful. Avoiding extreme dieting and seeking help for persistent concerns about eating, body image, or loss of control may allow earlier intervention. Treatment commonly includes psychological and nutrition counseling, which can help reduce binge episodes and address factors that maintain the disorder.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:150:"स्वस्थ भोजन और मानसिक स्वास्थ्य सहयोग सहायक हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:403:"Binge eating disorder should be professionally assessed when recurrent episodes cause distress or interfere with health and daily functioning. Seek prompt care when eating behavior is escalating, significant medical problems are developing, or severe emotional distress is present. Emergency assistance is appropriate for suicidal thoughts, severe psychiatric distress, or an acute medical complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:265;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:276;s:10:"disease_id";i:328;s:11:"overview_en";s:361:"Substance use disorder is a medical condition involving continued use of alcohol or drugs despite harmful effects or difficulty controlling use. It can affect health, relationships, work, and daily functioning. The disorder may involve craving, loss of control, increasing tolerance, withdrawal symptoms, or repeated unsuccessful attempts to reduce or stop use.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:195:"नशीले पदार्थ उपयोग विकार में हानिकारक पदार्थों का बार-बार उपयोग शामिल है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:407:"Substance use disorder develops through a combination of biological, psychological, and social factors. Repeated exposure to a substance can alter brain reward and stress systems and contribute to craving and loss of control. Genetic susceptibility, mental health conditions, trauma, social environment, and the properties and availability of the substance can all contribute to development of the disorder.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:149:"आनुवंशिक, मनोवैज्ञानिक और सामाजिक कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:356:"Risk factors include family history of substance use disorder, early exposure to alcohol or drugs, trauma, chronic stress, certain mental health conditions, social environments where substance use is common, and easy access to addictive substances. Risk varies according to the substance, pattern of use, individual vulnerability, and social circumstances.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:163:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, तनाव और साथियों का प्रभाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:367:"Diagnosis is based on a clinical assessment of substance use and its effects on health and daily functioning. Healthcare professionals consider patterns of use, inability to control use, craving, continued use despite harm, tolerance, withdrawal, and related problems. Screening questionnaires and assessment for medical or psychiatric complications may also be used.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:129:"निदान चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:373:"Substance use disorder cannot always be prevented, but risk may be reduced by delaying or avoiding harmful substance use, using prescribed medicines only as directed, building healthy coping strategies, and addressing stress or trauma appropriately. Early recognition of problematic use and timely professional support can help prevent progression and reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:157:"नशीले पदार्थों से बचाव और शीघ्र हस्तक्षेप सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:424:"Substance use disorder requires professional assessment and treatment, particularly when substance use is causing health, work, school, relationship, or safety problems. Seek prompt medical help when stopping a substance may cause withdrawal or when use is escalating. Emergency assistance is needed for overdose, severe confusion, loss of consciousness, seizures, severe breathing problems, poisoning, or suicidal behavior.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:266;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:277;s:10:"disease_id";i:329;s:11:"overview_en";s:380:"Alcohol use disorder is a medical condition in which a person has difficulty controlling alcohol use despite harmful consequences. It may involve strong cravings, increasing tolerance, withdrawal symptoms, and continued drinking that interferes with health, relationships, work, or daily activities. The condition can range from mild to severe and may develop gradually over time.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:158:"मद्यपान विकार में शराब सेवन को नियंत्रित न कर पाना शामिल है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:468:"Alcohol use disorder develops through a combination of biological, psychological, and social factors. Repeated alcohol exposure can change brain reward and stress systems, increasing craving and reducing control over drinking. Genetic susceptibility, early exposure to alcohol, mental health conditions, chronic stress, trauma, social environment, and patterns of heavy or frequent drinking can all contribute. Over time, tolerance and physical dependence may develop.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:120:"आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:470:"Risk factors for alcohol use disorder include a family history of problematic alcohol use, early initiation of drinking, frequent or heavy alcohol consumption, and exposure to environments where heavy drinking is common. Mental health conditions, trauma, chronic stress, social isolation, and certain personality or behavioral factors may increase vulnerability. Risk reflects the interaction of biological susceptibility with drinking patterns and social circumstances.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:150:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, तनाव और सामाजिक कारण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:423:"Diagnosis is based on a clinical assessment of alcohol use, drinking patterns, loss of control, cravings, continued use despite problems, tolerance, withdrawal, and effects on daily functioning. Clinicians may use standardized screening questionnaires and ask about medical, psychological, and social consequences. Blood tests can help assess alcohol-related health effects but cannot by themselves establish the diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:129:"निदान चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:468:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent alcohol use disorder, but reducing alcohol exposure can lower risk. Avoiding heavy or frequent drinking, following recommended drinking limits where applicable, and having alcohol-free periods can help. Early support for problematic drinking, treatment of anxiety or depression, healthy coping strategies, supportive relationships, and avoiding alcohol in situations where it creates harm can reduce progression and complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:116:"शराब सीमित करना और परामर्श सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:409:"Alcohol use disorder requires professional assessment and treatment. Seek prompt medical care when alcohol use is causing significant health or functional problems or when withdrawal may occur after stopping or reducing heavy use. Emergency assistance is needed for severe confusion, seizures, loss of consciousness, severe breathing difficulty, significant bleeding, suspected overdose, or suicidal behavior.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:46:12";}i:267;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:278;s:10:"disease_id";i:330;s:11:"overview_en";s:543:"Gaming disorder is a pattern of persistent or recurrent gaming behavior in which gaming becomes difficult to control and takes increasing priority over other activities and responsibilities. Affected individuals may continue gaming despite negative consequences involving education, work, relationships, sleep, or physical health. The severity and presentation can vary, and occasional heavy gaming by itself does not establish the disorder. Assessment considers the overall pattern, duration, loss of control, and impact on daily functioning.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:176:"गेमिंग विकार में अत्यधिक गेम खेलना दैनिक जीवन को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:520:"The exact causes of gaming disorder are not fully established. It may involve interactions between psychological, behavioral, social, and environmental factors. Gaming can provide rewards, social connection, achievement, or escape from distress, which may reinforce repeated use in susceptible individuals. Difficulties with impulse control, emotional regulation, stress, social relationships, or other mental health problems may coexist. These associations do not mean that gaming itself inevitably causes the disorder.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:129:"मनोवैज्ञानिक और व्यवहारिक कारक योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:517:"Factors associated with increased vulnerability may include frequent or prolonged gaming, using gaming as a primary way to cope with stress or negative emotions, social isolation, family or relationship difficulties, and problems with school or work functioning. Depression, anxiety, attention difficulties, sleep problems, and other behavioral or mental health conditions may coexist. These associations vary between individuals and should not be interpreted as proof that a particular factor causes gaming disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:137:"सामाजिक अलगाव और अधिक स्क्रीन समय जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:566:"Diagnosis is based on a detailed assessment of gaming behavior and its impact on daily life. Clinicians consider loss of control over gaming, increasing priority given to gaming, continuation despite negative consequences, duration of the pattern, and impairment in personal, family, educational, occupational, or social functioning. Information from the individual and, when appropriate, family members can help clarify the pattern. Assessment should also consider depression, anxiety, substance use, sleep problems, and other conditions that may require attention.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1339:"गेमिंग डिसऑर्डर का निदान लगातार या बार-बार होने वाले ऐसे गेमिंग व्यवहार के चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन से किया जाता है जो महत्वपूर्ण परेशानी या दैनिक जीवन में बाधा पैदा करता है। चिकित्सक गेमिंग पर नियंत्रण कम होना, अन्य गतिविधियों की तुलना में गेमिंग को बढ़ती प्राथमिकता देना और हानिकारक परिणामों के बावजूद गेमिंग जारी रखना जैसे पैटर्न का आकलन करते हैं। इसे अस्थायी रूप से अधिक गेम खेलने या सामान्य मनोरंजन से अलग करना आवश्यक है और अन्य मानसिक स्वास्थ्य या व्यवहार संबंधी स्थितियों का भी मूल्यांकन किया जा सकता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:500:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent gaming disorder. Maintaining balanced routines that include sleep, physical activity, education or work, relationships, and non-gaming interests can help reduce excessive reliance on gaming. Families can establish appropriate boundaries around gaming and encourage healthy coping strategies for stress and emotional difficulties. Persistent loss of control or significant impairment should prompt early discussion with a healthcare or mental health professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:112:"स्वस्थ स्क्रीन आदतें जोखिम कम कर सकती हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:402:"Gaming disorder is usually managed through planned professional assessment and behavioral support rather than emergency care. Seek help when gaming becomes difficult to control and significantly interferes with sleep, education, work, relationships, or other daily activities. Prompt assessment is appropriate when severe functional decline, self-neglect, or significant mental-health symptoms develop.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:268;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:279;s:10:"disease_id";i:331;s:11:"overview_en";s:546:"Adjustment disorder is a stress-related condition in which emotional or physical symptoms develop after a significant stressful life event. Symptoms may include anxiety, sadness, hopelessness, irritability, nervousness, withdrawal, or physical complaints. The reaction is more severe than would normally be expected and can interfere with work, school, relationships, or everyday functioning. Symptoms commonly begin within several months of the stressful event and often improve when the stressor is resolved and appropriate support is provided.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:148:"समायोजन विकार तनावपूर्ण जीवन घटनाओं की प्रतिक्रिया है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:535:"Adjustment disorder can follow many types of stressful events. Examples include the death of a loved one, relationship problems or divorce, moving, illness affecting oneself or someone close, financial difficulties, major life changes, unexpected disasters, and family or school problems. The same event does not affect everyone in the same way. Individual coping skills, previous experiences, available social support, and the circumstances surrounding the stressful event may influence whether a person develops significant symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:107:"तनावपूर्ण जीवन परिवर्तन मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:496:"There is no single factor that predicts who will develop adjustment disorder after a stressful event. Risk may be influenced by previous experiences with stress, coping strategies, social support, family or relationship difficulties, and the severity or persistence of the stressor. Children, adolescents, and adults can all develop the condition, although the types of stressors may differ by age. A history of mental health difficulties may also influence how a person responds to major stress.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:163:"जीवन की बड़ी घटनाएं और कमजोर अनुकूलन क्षमता जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:510:"Diagnosis is based primarily on the relationship between the stressful event and the symptoms. A clinician considers when symptoms began, how severe they are, how they affect daily functioning, and whether another mental or medical disorder better explains them. Adjustment disorder generally involves symptoms that occur after an identifiable stressor and are more intense than expected. The clinician also considers whether the reaction represents normal grief or another established mental health condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:129:"निदान चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:554:"Adjustment disorder cannot always be prevented because stressful events are part of life. Developing healthy coping strategies, maintaining supportive relationships, addressing problems early, and seeking help after a major stressful event may reduce the risk of prolonged distress. Adequate sleep, regular physical activity, and structured daily routines can support overall resilience. When symptoms significantly interfere with daily life, early professional support can help prevent worsening and identify other conditions that may require treatment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:106:"तनाव प्रबंधन और सहयोग सहायक हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:442:"Adjustment disorder should be professionally assessed when emotional or behavioral symptoms following a stressful event become persistent or interfere significantly with daily functioning. Seek prompt care when symptoms are worsening, functioning is substantially impaired, or severe anxiety or depression develops. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal thoughts, self-harm, inability to remain safe, or other immediate safety concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:269;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:280;s:10:"disease_id";i:332;s:11:"overview_en";s:348:"Personality disorders are long-lasting patterns of thoughts, feelings, and behaviors that differ significantly from cultural expectations and can cause difficulties in relationships, work, or other areas of life. Different personality disorders have different characteristic patterns, and symptoms generally begin by adolescence or early adulthood.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:203:"व्यक्तित्व विकार में व्यवहार और सोच के दीर्घकालिक असामान्य पैटर्न होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:302:"The causes of personality disorders are not completely understood. A combination of inherited characteristics, temperament, brain-related factors, childhood experiences, relationships, and environmental influences may contribute. Different personality disorders may have different contributing factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1086:"पर्सनैलिटी डिसऑर्डर के विकास में आनुवंशिक, जैविक, मनोवैज्ञानिक और पर्यावरणीय कारकों की जटिल परस्पर क्रिया की भूमिका मानी जाती है। विरासत में मिले स्वभाव और अन्य जैविक विशेषताएं संवेदनशीलता को प्रभावित कर सकती हैं, जबकि शुरुआती संबंध, बचपन के अनुभव और लंबे समय तक बना तनाव भी योगदान दे सकते हैं। अलग-अलग पर्सनैलिटी डिसऑर्डर में योगदान देने वाले कारक अलग हो सकते हैं और सभी मामलों को समझाने वाला कोई एक कारण नहीं है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:279:"Risk may be influenced by family history, inherited personality traits, childhood experiences, trauma, unstable relationships, and environmental circumstances. Risk factors vary among the different personality disorders and do not mean that a person will necessarily develop one.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:158:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और बचपन की प्रतिकूलताएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:360:"Diagnosis involves a comprehensive psychological or psychiatric assessment of long-term patterns of thinking, feeling, and behavior. The clinician considers relationships, functioning, developmental history, and the persistence of symptoms across situations while also evaluating other mental health conditions and possible medical or substance-related causes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:315:"There is no established method to prevent all personality disorders. Stable and supportive relationships, healthy childhood environments, early attention to persistent behavioral or interpersonal difficulties, and appropriate mental health care may help reduce associated problems and improve long-term functioning.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:130:"शीघ्र मानसिक स्वास्थ्य सहयोग लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:425:"Personality disorders generally require planned professional assessment and longer-term mental-health care. Seek prompt evaluation when personality-related patterns cause substantial impairment, severe relationship problems, dangerous behavior, or major deterioration in functioning. Emergency assistance is appropriate for suicidal behavior, severe self-harm, violent behavior, psychosis, or another immediate safety crisis.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:270;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:281;s:10:"disease_id";i:333;s:11:"overview_en";s:383:"Borderline personality disorder is a mental health condition involving a long-term pattern of instability in emotions, relationships, self-image, and behavior. People may experience intense emotions, fear of abandonment, impulsive behavior, rapidly changing relationships, and recurrent thoughts or behaviors related to self-harm. Symptoms can vary substantially between individuals.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:177:"बॉर्डरलाइन व्यक्तित्व विकार में अस्थिर भावनाएं और संबंध होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:373:"The exact cause of borderline personality disorder is uncertain. It is believed to arise from an interaction of genetic vulnerability, emotional and behavioral traits, brain and biological factors, and environmental experiences. Difficult or unstable early relationships and traumatic experiences may contribute in some individuals, but no single factor explains all cases.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:120:"आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:315:"Risk may be increased by family history of personality disorders or other mental health conditions, childhood adversity, unstable relationships, traumatic experiences, and certain biological or temperamental characteristics. Substance use and ongoing environmental stress can worsen symptoms and impair functioning.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:114:"आघात और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:337:"Diagnosis involves a comprehensive psychiatric assessment of long-term patterns of emotional instability, relationships, self-image, impulsivity, and behavior. Clinicians assess the timing and severity of symptoms and consider other psychiatric conditions, substance use, trauma, and medical causes that can produce overlapping symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:382:"There is no guaranteed method of preventing borderline personality disorder. Supportive and stable relationships, early recognition of significant emotional or behavioral difficulties, appropriate mental health care, and treatment of trauma or substance-related problems may help reduce impairment. Seeking professional help for persistent symptoms can support earlier intervention.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:86:"शीघ्र थेरेपी लाभकारी हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:460:"Borderline personality disorder requires professional mental-health assessment and ongoing support because emotional instability and impulsive behavior can significantly affect safety and functioning. Seek prompt care when self-harm, suicidal thoughts, severe mood changes, or impulsive behavior are worsening. Emergency assistance is needed for a suicide attempt, imminent risk of self-harm, serious self-injury, violent behavior, or inability to remain safe.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:271;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:282;s:10:"disease_id";i:334;s:11:"overview_en";s:379:"Antisocial personality disorder is a mental health condition characterized by a persistent pattern of disregard for and violation of the rights of other people. Behaviors may include repeated rule breaking, deceitfulness, impulsivity, aggression, irresponsibility, and limited concern about the consequences of actions. Symptoms begin earlier in life and continue into adulthood.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:181:"असामाजिक व्यक्तित्व विकार में दूसरों के अधिकारों की अनदेखी होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:361:"The exact cause of antisocial personality disorder is not known. Development is thought to involve a combination of inherited characteristics, differences in temperament and brain function, childhood experiences, and environmental influences. Adverse childhood experiences and persistent behavioral problems during childhood may contribute to later development.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:120:"आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:368:"Risk factors may include a family history of antisocial or other personality disorders, persistent behavioral problems during childhood, conduct-related difficulties, adverse childhood experiences, unstable family environments, and certain biological or temperamental characteristics. Substance use and social adversity may further complicate behavior and functioning.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:120:"बचपन की व्यवहारिक समस्याएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:378:"Diagnosis requires a detailed mental health assessment and review of long-term patterns of behavior. Clinicians consider disregard for others, deceitfulness, impulsivity, aggression, irresponsibility, and other characteristic behaviors, as well as evidence of conduct-related problems earlier in life. Other mental health or substance-related conditions must also be considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:366:"There is no established way to completely prevent antisocial personality disorder. Stable and supportive childhood environments, early recognition of persistent conduct problems, appropriate psychological or behavioral intervention, and attention to substance use and family difficulties may help reduce harmful behavioral patterns and improve long-term functioning.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:123:"शीघ्र व्यवहारिक हस्तक्षेप लाभकारी हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:352:"Antisocial personality disorder should be assessed and managed through appropriate professional and behavioral support. Seek prompt care when dangerous, aggressive, impulsive, or unlawful behavior is escalating or causing substantial harm. Emergency assistance is appropriate when there is an immediate threat of serious injury to the person or others.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:272;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:283;s:10:"disease_id";i:335;s:11:"overview_en";s:412:"Dependent personality disorder is a long-term pattern of excessive reliance on other people for emotional support, decision-making, and care. A person may have difficulty making everyday decisions independently, fear being alone, and feel unable to manage without close support. The pattern can interfere with relationships, work, and personal functioning and is generally persistent across different situations.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:168:"निर्भर व्यक्तित्व विकार में अत्यधिक सहारे की आवश्यकता होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:482:"The exact causes of dependent personality disorder are not fully established. Development may involve a combination of inherited temperament, personality characteristics, childhood experiences, family relationships, and environmental influences. Experiences that limit opportunities for independence or reinforce excessive dependence may contribute in some individuals. Other psychological conditions may occur alongside the disorder and can influence its development or expression.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:126:"आनुवंशिक और मनोवैज्ञानिक कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:451:"Possible risk factors include family history of personality disorders or other mental health conditions, childhood experiences involving overprotection or limited independence, unstable family environments, and certain temperament characteristics. Chronic medical conditions or stressful experiences may also influence dependence in some individuals. These factors are not sufficient by themselves to establish that a person will develop the disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:136:"अत्यधिक संरक्षणात्मक पालन-पोषण जोखिम बढ़ा सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:489:"Diagnosis requires a detailed mental health assessment by a qualified professional. The clinician evaluates long-standing patterns of dependence, difficulty making decisions, fear of separation, need for reassurance, and behavior across different relationships and situations. The assessment also considers cultural and social context and evaluates whether symptoms are better explained by another mental health condition, substance use, medical condition, or temporary life circumstances.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:499:"There is no established method that completely prevents dependent personality disorder. Supportive relationships that encourage age-appropriate independence, healthy decision-making, and development of coping skills may be beneficial during childhood and adolescence. Early attention to persistent difficulties with independence, boundaries, anxiety, or relationships may help prevent worsening impairment. Professional psychological support can help address patterns that interfere with daily life.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:153:"आत्मविश्वास और अनुकूलन कौशल विकसित करना सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:445:"Dependent personality disorder generally requires planned professional assessment and psychological treatment when excessive reliance on others significantly interferes with daily functioning or relationships. Seek prompt care when severe anxiety, inability to function independently, or major deterioration develops. Emergency assistance is appropriate for an immediate safety crisis, suicidal behavior, or severe inability to care for oneself.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:273;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:284;s:10:"disease_id";i:336;s:11:"overview_en";s:353:"Paranoid personality disorder is characterized by a long-standing pattern of distrust and suspicion toward other people. Affected individuals may frequently question the motives of others, interpret harmless actions as threatening, or have difficulty trusting people. The pattern is persistent and can interfere with relationships and daily functioning.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:174:"पैरानॉयड व्यक्तित्व विकार में दूसरों पर लगातार अविश्वास होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:345:"The exact cause of paranoid personality disorder is not known. It may result from a combination of inherited characteristics, temperament, biological influences, childhood experiences, and environmental or social factors. Difficult early relationships or experiences may contribute in some individuals, but no single cause explains the disorder.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:120:"आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारण योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:358:"Possible risk factors include a family history of personality disorders or other mental health conditions, certain inherited personality traits, adverse childhood experiences, unstable or difficult relationships, and social or environmental difficulties. These factors do not necessarily cause the disorder, and many people exposed to them do not develop it.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और प्रतिकूल अनुभव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:430:"Diagnosis requires a detailed mental health assessment focusing on a persistent pattern of suspiciousness and distrust across different situations. A clinician considers relationships, behavior, interpretation of other peoples actions, personal history, and the duration and impact of symptoms. The assessment also helps distinguish the condition from other psychiatric disorders or temporary reactions to stressful circumstances.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"निदान मनोचिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन द्वारा किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:416:"There is no established method that completely prevents paranoid personality disorder. Supportive and stable relationships, healthy communication, early attention to persistent interpersonal difficulties, and access to appropriate psychological care may be beneficial. Early evaluation of significant behavioral or relationship problems can help identify other conditions and provide appropriate support when needed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:159:"मानसिक स्वास्थ्य सहयोग लक्षण नियंत्रण में सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:451:"Paranoid personality disorder generally requires planned professional mental-health assessment when persistent mistrust or suspiciousness interferes with relationships or functioning. Seek prompt care when suspicious beliefs become substantially worse or lead to severe isolation or dangerous behavior. Emergency assessment is appropriate for severe loss of contact with reality, threats of violence, suicidal behavior, or an immediate safety concern.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:274;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:285;s:10:"disease_id";i:337;s:11:"overview_en";s:387:"Dissociative identity disorder is a mental health condition involving disruption of identity characterized by two or more distinct personality states or experiences of identity. It may be associated with gaps in memory that are greater than ordinary forgetfulness. Symptoms can interfere with daily functioning and may occur together with anxiety, depression, or trauma-related symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:310:"डिसोसिएटिव आइडेंटिटी डिसऑर्डर एक मानसिक विकार है जिसमें व्यक्ति में दो या अधिक अलग-अलग पहचान या व्यक्तित्व होते हैं。";s:9:"causes_en";s:358:"The exact cause of dissociative identity disorder is not fully established. It is commonly associated with severe or repeated trauma during childhood, particularly when traumatic experiences are overwhelming or prolonged. Dissociation may develop as a way of coping with traumatic experiences. Not everyone exposed to trauma develops a dissociative disorder.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:163:"यह आमतौर पर बचपन के गंभीर आघात और मानसिक तनाव से जुड़ा होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:404:"Risk is associated particularly with severe or repeated childhood trauma, abuse, neglect, and other overwhelming experiences. A history of prolonged traumatic events may increase vulnerability to dissociative symptoms. Other mental health conditions and ongoing stressful circumstances may coexist with the disorder, although exposure to trauma does not inevitably lead to dissociative identity disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:143:"आघात, दुर्व्यवहार और भावनात्मक तनाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:396:"Diagnosis is based on a detailed mental health assessment that considers symptoms, identity disruption, memory gaps, distress, and effects on daily functioning. A clinician may review personal and trauma history and assess for other psychiatric or medical conditions that could explain symptoms. Diagnosis requires careful evaluation because dissociative symptoms can occur in several conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1349:"डिसोसिएटिव आइडेंटिटी डिसऑर्डर का निदान किसी एक प्रयोगशाला या इमेजिंग जांच से नहीं, बल्कि विस्तृत मानसिक स्वास्थ्य मूल्यांकन से किया जाता है। चिकित्सक पहचान, स्मृति, जागरूकता और संबंधित कार्यक्षमता में लगातार होने वाले व्यवधानों का आकलन करते हैं तथा व्यक्ति के इतिहास और वर्तमान लक्षणों को देखते हैं। मूल्यांकन में अन्य मानसिक, न्यूरोलॉजिकल, पदार्थ-संबंधी और चिकित्सकीय स्थितियों पर भी विचार किया जाता है जो लक्षणों को बेहतर ढंग से समझा सकती हैं। निदान योग्य मानसिक स्वास्थ्य विशेषज्ञ द्वारा किया जाना चाहिए।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:383:"There is no established way to completely prevent dissociative identity disorder. Reducing exposure to abuse and neglect, protecting children from traumatic environments, and providing appropriate support after traumatic experiences may reduce the impact of trauma. Early professional support for trauma-related symptoms may help prevent worsening distress and functional impairment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:134:"समय पर मानसिक स्वास्थ्य सहायता लाभदायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:445:"Dissociative identity disorder should be professionally assessed when dissociation, memory gaps, identity disruption, or related symptoms interfere with daily life. Seek prompt care when symptoms worsen, functioning declines, or significant self-harm or trauma-related symptoms occur. Emergency assistance is needed for suicidal behavior, severe self-harm, dangerous disorientation, inability to remain safe, or another acute psychiatric crisis.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:275;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:286;s:10:"disease_id";i:338;s:11:"overview_en";s:396:"Somatic symptom disorder involves persistent physical symptoms that are associated with significant distress, excessive concern, or disproportionate thoughts and behaviors related to the symptoms. The symptoms are real and can affect daily functioning. The condition may occur with or without an identifiable medical disease and often involves repeated health-related worry or healthcare seeking.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:203:"सोमैटिक सिम्पटम डिसऑर्डर में शारीरिक लक्षणों को लेकर अत्यधिक चिंता होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:474:"The exact cause of somatic symptom disorder is not fully understood. The condition may involve interactions between biological sensitivity to bodily sensations, psychological factors, learned responses, stress, and previous experiences with illness. Anxiety, depression, trauma, chronic stress, and heightened attention to physical sensations may contribute. Symptoms may also become more distressing when ordinary bodily changes are interpreted as signs of serious disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:144:"मानसिक कारक, तनाव और भावनात्मक समस्याएं कारण बनती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:388:"Risk factors may include a history of anxiety or depression, previous trauma, chronic stress, persistent attention to bodily sensations, and previous experiences with serious illness. A family history of certain mental health conditions may also contribute. Some people develop the disorder after a period of physical illness, although the presence of a medical condition is not required.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:920:"सोमैटिक सिम्पटम डिसऑर्डर की संभावना बढ़ाने वाले कारकों में नकारात्मक दृष्टिकोण, दर्द या अन्य शारीरिक संवेदनाओं के प्रति अधिक संवेदनशीलता, पारिवारिक इतिहास या पालन-पोषण से जुड़े प्रभाव और आनुवंशिक कारक शामिल हो सकते हैं। शारीरिक या यौन दुर्व्यवहार का इतिहास भी अधिक जोखिम से जुड़ा हो सकता है, हालांकि इस विकार वाले कई लोगों में ऐसा इतिहास नहीं होता।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:467:"Diagnosis involves a comprehensive clinical assessment of physical symptoms, associated thoughts and worries, behaviors, duration, and effects on daily life. The clinician reviews the medical history and may perform appropriate examinations or investigations to identify or exclude relevant medical conditions. The diagnosis is based on the pattern of excessive health-related thoughts, anxiety, or behaviors rather than on whether symptoms are medically unexplained.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:148:"चिकित्सीय कारणों को बाहर करने के बाद निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:513:"There is no established method that completely prevents somatic symptom disorder. Maintaining healthy coping strategies, managing chronic stress, addressing anxiety or depression early, and developing a balanced approach to health information may be helpful. Regular care with an appropriate healthcare professional can reduce fragmented medical evaluations. People with persistent physical symptoms should receive appropriate medical assessment while also addressing associated distress and health-related worry.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:128:"तनाव नियंत्रण और मानसिक देखभाल सहायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:446:"Somatic symptom disorder should be professionally assessed when persistent physical symptoms and health concerns cause significant distress or interfere with daily functioning. Seek prompt medical evaluation for new, severe, or changing physical symptoms rather than assuming they are caused by the disorder. Emergency assessment is appropriate for symptoms suggesting a serious acute medical condition or an immediate psychiatric safety concern.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:276;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:287;s:10:"disease_id";i:339;s:11:"overview_en";s:643:"Health anxiety disorder involves persistent and excessive worry about having or developing a serious illness. A person may closely monitor normal bodily sensations, frequently seek medical reassurance, repeatedly check the body for signs of disease, or remain concerned even after appropriate medical evaluation has not found a serious condition. Physical symptoms may still be experienced, but the central problem is the ongoing fear and preoccupation with illness. Symptoms can interfere with daily activities, relationships, work, and quality of life. Recognition of the pattern can help guide appropriate psychological and medical support.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:192:"हेल्थ एंग्जायटी डिसऑर्डर में गंभीर बीमारी होने का लगातार डर बना रहता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:552:"The exact cause of health anxiety disorder is not established. It may develop through an interaction of psychological, behavioral, biological, and environmental factors. Previous experiences with serious illness, illness in a family member, stressful life events, increased attention to bodily sensations, or repeated exposure to health-related information may contribute in some people. Anxiety can also lead to repeated checking and reassurance seeking, which may temporarily reduce fear but can reinforce the cycle of health-related worry over time.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:156:"चिंता विकार, तनाव और पूर्व बीमारी के अनुभव कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:564:"Possible risk factors for health anxiety disorder include a personal or family history of anxiety or other mental health conditions, previous experiences with significant illness, serious illness affecting someone close, stressful life events, and a tendency to closely monitor bodily sensations. Repeated reassurance seeking and frequent checking of symptoms can maintain health-related fears. Access to large amounts of alarming or misunderstood health information may also increase worry in some people, particularly when it encourages repeated self-monitoring.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:131:"चिंता, पारिवारिक इतिहास और तनाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:576:"Diagnosis of health anxiety disorder involves a detailed assessment of persistent illness-related worry, the person's interpretation of bodily sensations, reassurance-seeking or checking behaviors, and the degree to which these concerns interfere with daily life. A healthcare professional may also review medical history and perform appropriate examinations to address genuine physical symptoms and rule out important medical causes. The diagnosis focuses on the persistent pattern of health-related anxiety rather than on whether the person has any physical symptoms at all.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1304:"हेल्थ एंग्जायटी डिसऑर्डर का निदान लगातार स्वास्थ्य संबंधी चिंता और उसके दैनिक जीवन पर प्रभाव के चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन से किया जाता है। चिकित्सक गंभीर बीमारी होने या विकसित होने की चिंता, चिंता की तीव्रता, बार-बार शरीर की जांच करने या आश्वासन मांगने तथा यह व्यवहार कितने समय से बना हुआ है, इसका आकलन करते हैं। वास्तविक शारीरिक लक्षणों का उचित चिकित्सकीय मूल्यांकन किया जाता है, जबकि अनावश्यक जांच से बचने का प्रयास किया जाता है। अन्य चिंता, मनोदशा और संबंधित स्थितियों का भी मूल्यांकन किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:610:"Health anxiety may be managed by recognizing repeated checking and reassurance-seeking patterns and obtaining appropriate professional support when worry becomes persistent or disruptive. Reliable health information and regular medical care can help reduce unnecessary uncertainty, while repeated self-testing or searching for serious diseases may reinforce anxiety in some people. Psychological therapies can help people change unhelpful interpretations of bodily sensations and reduce behaviors that maintain health-related fear. Genuine physical symptoms should still receive appropriate medical evaluation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:137:"मानसिक स्वास्थ्य सहायता और तनाव कम करना लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:448:"Health anxiety is generally managed through planned medical and psychological care. Seek professional assessment when persistent fear of serious illness causes repeated checking, reassurance seeking, avoidance, or substantial interference with daily life. Prompt medical evaluation remains appropriate for new or severe physical symptoms, while emergency care is needed for symptoms indicating an acute medical condition or immediate safety crisis.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:277;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:288;s:10:"disease_id";i:340;s:11:"overview_en";s:336:"Selective mutism is an anxiety-related condition in which a person who is able to speak normally in comfortable situations consistently does not speak in particular social settings where speaking is expected. It is most often recognized in childhood and may interfere with education, friendships, communication, and everyday activities.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:260:"सेलेक्टिव म्यूटिज्म एक चिंता विकार है जिसमें व्यक्ति कुछ सामाजिक परिस्थितियों में बोल नहीं पाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:354:"The exact cause is not known. Selective mutism is commonly associated with anxiety and may involve a combination of inherited temperament, social anxiety, developmental factors, environmental experiences, and learned responses to stressful communication situations. It is not simply a refusal to speak or a sign that a child does not understand language.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:534:"सेलेक्टिव म्यूटिज्म का संबंध चिंता, विशेषकर सामाजिक चिंता, से होता है। आनुवंशिक संवेदनशीलता, अत्यधिक संकोची स्वभाव, तनावपूर्ण सामाजिक अनुभव और संचार संबंधी कठिनाइयां इसके विकास में योगदान दे सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:416:"Risk may be increased by a family history of anxiety or related conditions, an anxious or behaviorally inhibited temperament, significant social stress, communication difficulties, and experiences that make speaking in certain environments particularly stressful. Bilingual or multilingual children may require careful assessment so that normal language development differences are not mistaken for selective mutism.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:550:"सेलेक्टिव म्यूटिज्म का संबंध चिंता से होता है और यह सामाजिक चिंता, चिंता विकारों के पारिवारिक इतिहास, व्यवहार में अधिक संकोच या सामाजिक एवं संचार संबंधी तनावपूर्ण अनुभवों वाले बच्चों में अधिक देखा जा सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:365:"Diagnosis is based on a detailed developmental and behavioral assessment. Clinicians consider where and when the person speaks, how long the pattern has persisted, its effect on daily functioning, language development, hearing, anxiety symptoms, and other possible explanations. Information from parents, teachers, and other caregivers may be important in children.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:719:"निदान विस्तृत इतिहास और व्यवहारिक मूल्यांकन पर आधारित होता है, जिसमें व्यक्ति कुछ सामाजिक परिस्थितियों में लगातार बोल नहीं पाता जबकि अन्य परिस्थितियों में बोल सकता है। मूल्यांकन से भाषा, सुनने, विकास या अन्य मानसिक स्वास्थ्य संबंधी स्थितियों को अलग करने में मदद मिलती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:378:"Early recognition and supportive management of anxiety may help reduce the impact of selective mutism. Children should not be pressured, punished, or repeatedly forced to speak in stressful situations. A supportive environment, gradual exposure under professional guidance, and appropriate treatment of anxiety or communication difficulties may help prevent worsening avoidance.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:579:"सेलेक्टिव म्यूटिज्म को निश्चित रूप से रोकने का कोई तरीका नहीं है। चिंता की जल्दी पहचान, सहयोगी संचार, बोलने के लिए दबाव न डालना और समय पर विशेषज्ञ मूल्यांकन कार्यात्मक कठिनाइयों को कम करने तथा सुधार में सहायक हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:444:"Selective mutism is usually managed through planned developmental, psychological, educational, or speech-language support rather than emergency treatment. Seek professional assessment when inability to speak in specific settings interferes with education, relationships, or essential activities. Prompt evaluation is appropriate when severe functional impairment, developmental concerns, or another significant mental-health problem is present.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:278;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:289;s:10:"disease_id";i:341;s:11:"overview_en";s:336:"Aplastic anemia is a rare disorder in which the bone marrow does not produce enough new blood cells. Because red cells, white cells, and platelets may all be reduced, the condition can cause tiredness, frequent infections, easy bruising, or bleeding. Severity varies, and severe disease requires prompt medical evaluation and treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:196:"एप्लास्टिक एनीमिया में अस्थि मज्जा पर्याप्त रक्त कोशिकाएं नहीं बना पाती।";s:9:"causes_en";s:374:"Aplastic anemia develops when blood-forming stem cells in the bone marrow are damaged or destroyed. Possible causes include certain medicines, toxic chemicals such as benzene, radiation, chemotherapy, autoimmune disorders, pregnancy, and some viral infections. In many people, no specific cause can be identified, and the condition is then called idiopathic aplastic anemia.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:173:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग, संक्रमण और पुरानी बीमारियां इसका कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:312:"Risk of aplastic anemia may increase with exposure to certain toxic chemicals or medicines, radiation or chemotherapy, some viral infections, autoimmune disorders, and pregnancy. However, many cases have no identifiable cause. The presence of a risk factor does not mean that a person will develop the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:178:"विषाक्त पदार्थों, संक्रमण और प्रतिरक्षा विकारों से जोखिम बढ़ता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:377:"Diagnosis of aplastic anemia involves blood tests showing reduced numbers of blood cells and evaluation of the bone marrow. A complete blood count and examination of blood cells can identify low red cells, white cells, and platelets. Bone marrow examination may be performed to assess blood-cell production and distinguish aplastic anemia from other causes of low blood counts.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:148:"रक्त परीक्षण और बोन मैरो जांच द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:426:"Aplastic anemia cannot always be prevented because many cases have no identifiable cause. When possible, avoid unnecessary exposure to toxic chemicals known to damage bone marrow and follow appropriate safety precautions at work. Medicines that can affect blood-cell production should be used only as directed by a healthcare professional. Prompt evaluation of unexplained bleeding, infections, or severe fatigue is important.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:150:"विषाक्त पदार्थों से बचाव और संक्रमण का उपचार लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:442:"Aplastic anemia requires prompt medical assessment because reduced blood-cell production can lead to serious infection, bleeding, and anemia. Seek urgent care for fever, signs of infection, unusual or persistent bleeding, severe weakness, dizziness, shortness of breath, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for severe bleeding, difficulty breathing, fainting, severe infection, or other signs of medical instability.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:279;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:290;s:10:"disease_id";i:342;s:11:"overview_en";s:350:"Megaloblastic anemia is a type of anemia in which the bone marrow produces unusually large and abnormal red blood cells. It commonly develops when the body does not have enough vitamin B12 or folate, nutrients required for normal DNA production. The condition can cause fatigue, weakness, pale skin, shortness of breath, and other symptoms of anemia.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:213:"मेगालोब्लास्टिक एनीमिया में लाल रक्त कोशिकाएं असामान्य रूप से बड़ी हो जाती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:389:"Megaloblastic anemia is commonly caused by vitamin B12 or folate deficiency. Vitamin B12 deficiency may result from inadequate intake, poor absorption, certain stomach or intestinal disorders, or autoimmune conditions that interfere with B12 absorption. Folate deficiency may result from poor nutrition, malabsorption, increased nutritional requirements, alcohol use, or certain medicines.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:110:"विटामिन B12 और फोलेट की कमी प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:363:"Risk depends on the cause of vitamin B12 or folate deficiency. Poor nutrition, malabsorption disorders, gastrointestinal surgery, heavy alcohol use, pregnancy, and certain medicines can increase risk. Older adults may also be at increased risk of B12 deficiency because absorption can become less efficient with age or because of medical conditions and medicines.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1458:"मेगालोब्लास्टिक एनीमिया के जोखिम कारकों में विटामिन B12 या फोलेट का पर्याप्त सेवन न होना या शरीर द्वारा उनका ठीक से अवशोषण न कर पाना शामिल है। इन पोषक तत्वों की कमी वाला आहार, पेट या छोटी आंत को प्रभावित करने वाली स्थितियां और कुछ दवाएं अवशोषण में बाधा डाल सकती हैं। अत्यधिक शराब का सेवन फोलेट की कमी में योगदान कर सकता है। गर्भावस्था और पोषण की अधिक आवश्यकता वाली अन्य अवस्थाओं में भी फोलेट की जरूरत बढ़ सकती है। मूल जोखिम कारक इस बात पर निर्भर करता है कि एनीमिया विटामिन की कमी या लाल रक्त कोशिकाओं के निर्माण को प्रभावित करने वाली किसी अन्य स्थिति के कारण है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:353:"Diagnosis involves a complete blood count and examination of red blood cells, which may show large abnormal cells. Blood tests can measure vitamin B12 and folate levels and may include additional tests when the cause is uncertain. Further evaluation may look for malabsorption, nutritional deficiency, medication effects, or other underlying conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:126:"रक्त जांच और विटामिन स्तर जांच से निदान होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:373:"Megaloblastic anemia can often be prevented when it results from nutritional deficiency. Eating a balanced diet containing adequate vitamin B12 and folate and taking recommended supplements during periods of increased need can help. People with malabsorption disorders or medicines that affect these vitamins should follow medical advice and undergo appropriate monitoring.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:137:"संतुलित आहार और विटामिन पूरकता रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:411:"Megaloblastic anemia should be medically assessed to identify and treat the underlying nutritional or other cause. Seek prompt care when anemia is severe or symptoms such as marked weakness, shortness of breath, dizziness, or palpitations are worsening. Emergency assessment is appropriate for fainting, severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, significant bleeding, or other signs of acute medical instability.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:280;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:291;s:10:"disease_id";i:343;s:11:"overview_en";s:360:"Vitamin B12 deficiency occurs when the body does not have enough vitamin B12 to support normal red blood cell formation, nerve function, and DNA production. It may develop gradually and can cause tiredness, weakness, pale skin, numbness, tingling, balance problems, or changes in concentration and memory. Severe or prolonged deficiency can cause nerve damage.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:187:"विटामिन B12 की कमी शरीर में इस विटामिन की अपर्याप्त मात्रा को दर्शाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:428:"Vitamin B12 deficiency can result from inadequate dietary intake, especially in people who consume little or no animal-derived food without appropriate supplementation. It can also occur when the body cannot absorb B12 properly because of pernicious anemia, stomach or intestinal disorders, previous gastrointestinal surgery, or certain medicines. Reduced absorption can be more important than dietary deficiency in some people.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:515:"विटामिन B12 की कमी अपर्याप्त आहार या शरीर द्वारा B12 के खराब अवशोषण के कारण हो सकती है। कारणों में परनिशियस एनीमिया, पेट या आंत के रोग, जठरांत्र संबंधी सर्जरी और कुछ दवाओं का लंबे समय तक उपयोग शामिल हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:403:"Risk factors include a diet low in vitamin B12, strict vegan diets without supplementation, pernicious anemia, disorders affecting the stomach or small intestine, previous gastrointestinal surgery, and prolonged use of certain medicines that interfere with absorption. Older adults may also have impaired absorption. Alcohol misuse and some chronic gastrointestinal conditions can further increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:584:"बुजुर्गों, परनिशियस एनीमिया या पाचन तंत्र के रोगों वाले लोगों, जठरांत्र सर्जरी करा चुके लोगों तथा बहुत कम या बिना पशु-आधारित खाद्य पदार्थ खाने वालों में जोखिम अधिक हो सकता है। कुछ दवाओं के लंबे उपयोग से भी जोखिम बढ़ सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:396:"Diagnosis usually involves a medical history, physical examination, and blood testing. A complete blood count may show anemia or enlarged red blood cells, while a serum vitamin B12 measurement can help assess deficiency. Additional tests such as methylmalonic acid, homocysteine, folate, or tests for pernicious anemia may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain or the cause needs clarification.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:848:"विटामिन B12 की कमी का निदान चिकित्सा इतिहास, शारीरिक जांच और रक्त परीक्षणों से किया जाता है। जांच में पूर्ण रक्त गणना और विटामिन B12 का स्तर शामिल हो सकता है। यदि परिणाम स्पष्ट न हो, तो मेथिलमैलोनिक एसिड जैसी अतिरिक्त जांच कमी की पुष्टि में मदद कर सकती है। डॉक्टर भोजन, दवाओं, अवशोषण की समस्या या अन्य कारणों की भी जांच कर सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:433:"A balanced diet containing reliable sources of vitamin B12 can help prevent nutritional deficiency. People who follow a strict vegan diet may need fortified foods or a vitamin B12 supplement. Individuals with conditions or medicines that reduce B12 absorption may require periodic monitoring and supplementation under medical guidance. Early evaluation of unexplained anemia or neurological symptoms can prevent prolonged deficiency.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:706:"विटामिन B12 के विश्वसनीय स्रोतों वाला संतुलित आहार आहार संबंधी कमी को रोकने में मदद करता है। अवशोषण में समस्या या अधिक जोखिम वाले लोगों को चिकित्सकीय सलाह के अनुसार फोर्टिफाइड खाद्य पदार्थ या सप्लीमेंट की आवश्यकता हो सकती है और जरूरत पड़ने पर स्तर की निगरानी की जाती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:456:"Vitamin B12 deficiency should be medically assessed because prolonged deficiency can cause anemia and potentially persistent neurological problems. Seek prompt evaluation for progressive numbness, weakness, balance problems, difficulty walking, cognitive changes, or significant anemia symptoms. Emergency assessment is appropriate for sudden severe neurological symptoms, chest pain, severe breathing difficulty, fainting, or other acute medical concerns.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:281;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:292;s:10:"disease_id";i:344;s:11:"overview_en";s:615:"Folate deficiency occurs when the body does not have enough folate, a B vitamin needed for DNA production, cell division, and normal formation of red blood cells. Deficiency can develop gradually when dietary intake is inadequate, the body cannot absorb enough folate, or the body requires more folate than usual. It may lead to a type of anemia in which red blood cells become unusually large and may cause fatigue, weakness, pale skin, shortness of breath, or other symptoms. Folate deficiency is particularly important to recognize during pregnancy because adequate folate is needed for normal fetal development.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:174:"फोलेट की कमी में शरीर में फोलिक एसिड की पर्याप्त मात्रा नहीं होती।";s:9:"causes_en";s:544:"Folate deficiency may result from inadequate intake of folate-rich foods, poor absorption in the digestive tract, increased nutritional requirements, or conditions that interfere with folate metabolism. Pregnancy increases the body's need for folate. Alcohol use can contribute through poor nutrition and impaired absorption or metabolism. Certain medicines can also interfere with folate availability or metabolism. Digestive disorders that affect absorption may increase the risk, particularly when they are prolonged or inadequately treated.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:148:"खराब आहार, गर्भावस्था और अवशोषण की समस्या इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:499:"Risk of folate deficiency may increase with a diet low in folate-rich foods, heavy alcohol use, disorders that interfere with intestinal absorption, pregnancy, and other situations in which the body requires more folate. Older adults and people with certain chronic digestive conditions may also be at increased risk. Some medicines can interfere with folate metabolism or absorption. Risk depends on the combination of dietary intake, medical conditions, nutritional requirements, and medicine use.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:131:"गर्भावस्था, शराब सेवन और कुपोषण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:542:"Diagnosis of folate deficiency may involve a complete blood count and examination of blood-cell characteristics, followed by measurement of folate when appropriate. Healthcare professionals may also assess vitamin B12 levels because the two deficiencies can produce similar types of anemia and require different management. Medical history may include diet, alcohol use, pregnancy, digestive symptoms, and medicines. Additional testing may be needed when poor absorption, chronic disease, or another nutritional or medical cause is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:113:"रक्त जांच से फोलेट स्तर ज्ञात किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:603:"Folate deficiency can often be reduced by eating a balanced diet containing folate-rich foods such as leafy green vegetables, legumes, citrus fruits, and fortified grain products. People with increased requirements, including those who are pregnant or planning pregnancy, may need folic acid supplementation according to medical guidance. Treating digestive disorders that interfere with absorption and reviewing medicines that affect folate metabolism can also help. Persistent fatigue or symptoms of anemia should be evaluated rather than treated solely with supplements without identifying the cause.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:125:"फोलेट युक्त भोजन और पूरकता रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:378:"Folate deficiency should be medically assessed to identify the cause and correct the deficiency. Seek prompt care when significant anemia symptoms, weakness, shortness of breath, dizziness, or nutritional problems are present. Emergency assessment is appropriate for fainting, severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, major bleeding, or other signs of acute medical instability.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:282;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:293;s:10:"disease_id";i:345;s:11:"overview_en";s:464:"Neutropenia is a condition in which the number of neutrophils, a type of white blood cell that helps fight infections, is lower than normal. It can be temporary or persistent and may occur as a result of infection, medicines, cancer treatment, immune disorders, nutritional problems, bone marrow conditions, or inherited factors. Mild neutropenia may cause no symptoms, while more severe neutropenia can increase the risk of serious bacterial or fungal infections.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:193:"न्यूट्रोपेनिया में न्यूट्रोफिल नामक श्वेत रक्त कोशिकाओं की कमी होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:471:"Neutropenia can develop when the bone marrow does not produce enough neutrophils, when neutrophils are destroyed or removed from the bloodstream too quickly, or when they are used up during severe infection. Medicines and cancer treatments can suppress bone marrow production. Viral and other infections, autoimmune disorders, nutritional deficiencies, bone marrow diseases, and inherited conditions can also cause neutropenia. In some people, no specific cause is found.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:179:"ऑटोइम्यून विकार, संक्रमण और पुरानी बीमारियां इसके कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:481:"Risk depends on the underlying cause. People receiving chemotherapy, radiation, or medicines that suppress bone marrow or immune function may be at increased risk. Certain infections, autoimmune diseases, nutritional deficiencies, blood or bone marrow disorders, and inherited conditions can also increase risk. Severe illness may cause neutrophils to be consumed faster than the body can replace them. Some individuals have persistent mild neutropenia without frequent infections.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:156:"कैंसर उपचार, संक्रमण और प्रतिरक्षा विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:502:"Diagnosis is based on a complete blood count with a differential to determine the number and proportion of neutrophils and other blood cells. The healthcare professional may review medicines, recent infections, medical conditions, and family history to identify a possible cause. Depending on the findings, additional blood tests, antibody testing, nutritional studies, or a bone marrow examination may be needed. Repeated blood counts can help determine whether neutropenia is temporary or persistent.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:100:"पूर्ण रक्त गणना से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:530:"Neutropenia itself cannot always be prevented because many causes are unavoidable or related to underlying medical conditions. When a medicine or cancer treatment can lower neutrophil counts, healthcare professionals may monitor blood counts and adjust treatment when necessary. Treating infections and managing underlying conditions can reduce complications. People known to have significant neutropenia may receive individualized advice about infection prevention and should seek prompt medical attention for signs of infection.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:121:"संक्रमण का शीघ्र उपचार और निगरानी लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:421:"Neutropenia requires medical assessment because a low neutrophil count can increase the risk of serious infection. Seek urgent medical attention for fever, chills, sore throat, new cough, painful urination, skin infection, or other signs of infection, particularly when neutrophil counts are very low. Emergency care is needed for severe infection, difficulty breathing, confusion, fainting, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:283;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:294;s:10:"disease_id";i:346;s:11:"overview_en";s:389:"Polycythemia vera is a chronic blood disorder in which the bone marrow produces too many red blood cells. The increased number of blood cells can make the blood thicker and increase the risk of blood clots. Some people also have increased white blood cells or platelets. Symptoms may include headache, dizziness, itching after a warm bath, fatigue, or a feeling of fullness in the abdomen.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:184:"पॉलीसाइथीमिया वेरा में लाल रक्त कोशिकाओं का अत्यधिक उत्पादन होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:463:"Polycythemia vera is usually caused by an acquired genetic change in blood-forming cells, most commonly a mutation affecting the JAK2 gene. The mutation causes the bone marrow to produce blood cells excessively. It is generally not inherited from parents. The abnormal blood-cell production develops during a person's lifetime and is different from secondary polycythemia, in which another condition or low oxygen level causes increased red blood cell production.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:171:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन और अस्थि मज्जा की असामान्यताएं इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:447:"The risk of polycythemia vera increases with age and is uncommon in children and young adults. It occurs somewhat more often in men than women. Having certain blood disorders or related genetic changes may be associated with increased risk. Unlike secondary polycythemia, lifestyle factors such as smoking or living at high altitude are not the direct cause of polycythemia vera, although they can increase red blood cell counts for other reasons.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:130:"बढ़ती उम्र और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:471:"Diagnosis involves a complete blood count showing an increased red blood cell level and may also show increased white blood cells or platelets. Healthcare professionals may measure erythropoietin levels and test blood cells for JAK2 mutations. Additional evaluation may include examination of the bone marrow and assessment for other causes of an elevated red blood cell count. The diagnosis is based on laboratory findings together with the clinical and medical history.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1020:"पॉलीसाइथीमिया वेरा का मूल्यांकन रक्त जाँच से किया जाता है, जिसमें लाल रक्त कोशिकाओं की मात्रा या सांद्रता बढ़ी हुई दिखाई दे सकती है और श्वेत रक्त कोशिकाएँ या प्लेटलेट्स भी बढ़े हो सकते हैं। डॉक्टर erythropoietin का स्तर और JAK2 जीन में परिवर्तन की जाँच कर सकते हैं, जो अधिकांश रोगियों में पाया जाता है। जरूरत के अनुसार बोन मैरो की जाँच और बढ़ी हुई तिल्ली या अन्य जटिलताओं का मूल्यांकन भी किया जा सकता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:482:"There is no established way to prevent polycythemia vera because it usually results from acquired genetic changes that cannot be predicted or avoided. Early evaluation of persistent abnormal blood counts can help identify the disorder and reduce complications. People with the condition should follow medical treatment and recommendations aimed at reducing blood clot risk, avoid tobacco exposure, and seek urgent care for symptoms that may indicate a serious clotting complication.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:123:"नियमित निगरानी और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली लाभकारी है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:464:"Polycythemia vera requires ongoing medical care because increased blood-cell production can raise the risk of blood clots and bleeding. Seek prompt assessment for new headaches, visual changes, unusual bleeding, or worsening symptoms. Emergency medical attention is needed for sudden weakness or numbness, difficulty speaking, severe chest pain, sudden shortness of breath, severe abdominal pain, or other symptoms suggesting a stroke, heart attack, or major clot.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:284;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:295;s:10:"disease_id";i:347;s:11:"overview_en";s:568:"Idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura, also called immune thrombocytopenia, is a disorder in which the immune system mistakenly destroys platelets or interferes with their production. Platelets help blood clot, so a low platelet count can increase the tendency to bruise or bleed. Some people have no symptoms and are diagnosed after a routine blood test, while others develop pinpoint skin spots, easy bruising, nosebleeds, or heavier menstrual bleeding. The condition may be short-lived or persistent and requires monitoring based on platelet levels and bleeding risk.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:189:"आईटीपी एक ऑटोइम्यून विकार है जिसमें प्लेटलेट्स की संख्या कम हो जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:577:"Idiopathic immune thrombocytopenia occurs when the immune system mistakenly targets platelets for destruction and may also interfere with platelet production. In many cases, no specific trigger can be identified. The condition may develop after an infection, vaccination, or exposure to certain medicines, particularly in children, although these associations do not occur in every case. Other medical conditions can cause low platelet counts and must be distinguished from immune thrombocytopenia. The term idiopathic reflects cases in which no underlying cause is identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"प्लेटलेट्स का ऑटोइम्यून विनाश इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:495:"Risk factors for immune thrombocytopenia vary and may include a recent infection, certain autoimmune disorders, and some medicines or medical conditions that affect platelet production or destruction. In children, the condition can follow a viral illness and may be temporary. Adults may develop persistent disease more often. A previous episode can also be relevant. Because many other disorders can cause thrombocytopenia, a low platelet count alone does not establish immune thrombocytopenia.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:162:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग, संक्रमण और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:543:"Diagnosis of immune thrombocytopenia begins with a complete blood count showing a low platelet count and an assessment for bleeding or other abnormalities. A medical history and physical examination help identify medicines, infections, autoimmune conditions, liver disease, or other causes of thrombocytopenia. A blood smear may be examined to assess platelet appearance and exclude other disorders. There is no single definitive test for immune thrombocytopenia, so diagnosis generally requires excluding other causes of a low platelet count.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:129:"रक्त जांच और प्लेटलेट गणना से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:574:"There is no established way to prevent every case of immune thrombocytopenia because its triggers are not always known. Avoiding medicines that affect platelet function or count unless medically necessary may reduce bleeding risk, but medicines should not be stopped without professional advice. People diagnosed with thrombocytopenia should follow monitoring recommendations and report unusual bleeding promptly. Protecting against injuries may be important when platelet counts are low. Treatment of underlying conditions can reduce secondary forms of low platelet counts.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:155:"संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार और नियमित निगरानी सहायक हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:456:"Immune thrombocytopenic purpura requires medical assessment because a low platelet count can increase bleeding risk. Seek urgent care for persistent or heavy bleeding, blood in the urine or stool, vomiting blood, large unexplained bruises, or numerous new pinpoint skin spots. Emergency assessment is needed for uncontrolled bleeding, severe headache with neurological symptoms, confusion, fainting, or other signs of potentially serious internal bleeding.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:285;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:296;s:10:"disease_id";i:348;s:11:"overview_en";s:467:"Von Willebrand disease is an inherited bleeding disorder caused by reduced amounts or abnormal function of von Willebrand factor, a protein that helps blood clot properly. People with the condition may bruise easily or experience prolonged nosebleeds, bleeding after injuries, or excessive bleeding after surgery or dental procedures. Menstrual bleeding may also be unusually heavy or prolonged. Severity varies considerably among the different types of the disorder.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:136:"वॉन विलेब्रांड रोग एक आनुवंशिक रक्तस्राव विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:462:"Von Willebrand disease is usually caused by inherited variants affecting the VWF gene, which provides instructions for making von Willebrand factor. This protein helps platelets attach to damaged blood vessels and supports normal clot formation. Type 1 generally involves reduced amounts of the factor, while type 2 involves impaired function. Type 3 causes a severe deficiency. A rare acquired form can develop later in life in association with other disorders.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:156:"रक्त के थक्के बनने की आनुवंशिक असामान्यताएं इसका कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:443:"A family history of von Willebrand disease or another inherited bleeding disorder is an important risk factor. The condition can be inherited in different patterns depending on the specific type. People with affected relatives may therefore have an increased likelihood of carrying a disease-causing genetic variant. Symptoms can vary even among family members, so a person with a relatively mild bleeding history may still have the condition.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:101:"पारिवारिक इतिहास मुख्य जोखिम कारक है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:471:"Diagnosis can be challenging because von Willebrand factor levels and bleeding symptoms can vary over time. Evaluation usually includes a personal and family bleeding history together with blood tests. Testing may measure von Willebrand factor amount and activity, factor VIII levels, platelet function, and related clotting measures. Repeated or specialized testing may sometimes be necessary to distinguish von Willebrand disease from other causes of abnormal bleeding.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:112:"रक्त जमावट जांच द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:518:"Inherited von Willebrand disease cannot currently be prevented because it results from genetic changes passed through families. People with a family history can discuss genetic counseling and appropriate testing with healthcare professionals. Individuals who have been diagnosed should inform healthcare providers before surgery, dental procedures, or other invasive procedures so bleeding risk can be considered. Recognizing abnormal bleeding early can help reduce complications and improve planning for medical care.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:141:"आनुवंशिक परामर्श और चिकित्सकीय निगरानी लाभकारी हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:440:"Von Willebrand disease should be medically assessed when abnormal or recurrent bleeding occurs. Seek prompt care for prolonged bleeding after injuries or procedures, frequent significant nosebleeds, unusually heavy menstrual bleeding, or unexplained bruising. Emergency assessment is needed for uncontrolled bleeding, signs of significant blood loss, severe weakness or fainting, blood in vomit or stool, or bleeding that cannot be stopped.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:286;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:297;s:10:"disease_id";i:349;s:11:"overview_en";s:414:"Deep immune deficiency refers to a condition in which the immune system is significantly weakened or unable to protect the body adequately from infections and other diseases. It may result from inherited disorders, certain infections, medical treatments, or conditions that damage immune cells or their function. The severity and type of immune deficiency determine the infections and complications that may occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:192:"गंभीर प्रतिरक्षा कमी में शरीर संक्रमणों से प्रभावी रूप से नहीं लड़ पाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:384:"Deep immune deficiency may be caused by inherited abnormalities affecting immune cells, antibodies, or other parts of the immune system. It can also develop from conditions such as HIV infection, cancers affecting immune cells, severe malnutrition, or treatments that suppress immunity, including some chemotherapy, immunosuppressive medicines, and stem cell or organ transplantation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:157:"आनुवंशिक दोष, संक्रमण और पुरानी बीमारियां कारण हो सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:365:"Risk factors include a family history of inherited immune disorders, HIV infection, certain cancers, prolonged or intensive immune-suppressing treatment, organ or stem cell transplantation, severe nutritional deficiencies, and other illnesses that impair immune function. The specific risks depend on the underlying cause and the part of the immune system affected.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:143:"बार-बार संक्रमण और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:378:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and examination, including the pattern, frequency, and severity of infections. Blood tests may measure white blood cells, lymphocyte populations, immunoglobulins, and other immune markers. Additional specialized tests, genetic testing, or tests for infections may be performed when an inherited or acquired immune deficiency is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:144:"प्रतिरक्षा परीक्षण और रक्त जांच से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:411:"Some immune deficiencies cannot be prevented, particularly inherited disorders. Risk of acquired immune deficiency may be reduced by preventing HIV infection, maintaining adequate nutrition, receiving recommended vaccinations when appropriate, and avoiding unnecessary exposure to infections. People receiving immune-suppressing treatment should follow their healthcare provider's infection-prevention guidance.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:140:"टीकाकरण, स्वच्छता और संक्रमण से बचाव महत्वपूर्ण हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:519:"Deep immune deficiency requires specialist medical assessment because impaired immune function can lead to recurrent or severe infections. Seek prompt care for persistent fever, recurrent infections, worsening cough, breathing difficulty, significant diarrhea, dehydration, or infections that are unusually severe or difficult to treat. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, confusion, fainting, severe dehydration, rapidly worsening infection, or other signs of sepsis or medical instability.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:47:44";}i:287;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:298;s:10:"disease_id";i:350;s:11:"overview_en";s:325:"Sjogren syndrome is an autoimmune disorder in which the immune system attacks moisture-producing glands, particularly those responsible for tears and saliva. This can cause persistent dry eyes and dry mouth. The condition may also affect other parts of the body and can occur alone or together with other autoimmune diseases.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:239:"स्जोग्रेन सिंड्रोम एक ऑटोइम्यून विकार है जो नमी बनाने वाली ग्रंथियों को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:398:"The exact cause of Sjogren syndrome is not known. It is an autoimmune disorder in which the immune system mistakenly attacks healthy tissues, especially glands that produce tears and saliva. A combination of genetic susceptibility and environmental factors may contribute. An environmental trigger, such as a previous infection, may help activate the abnormal immune response in susceptible people.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1163:"स्जोग्रेन सिंड्रोम का सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं है। यह एक ऑटोइम्यून विकार है जिसमें प्रतिरक्षा तंत्र गलती से स्वस्थ ऊतकों पर हमला करता है, विशेष रूप से आँसू और लार बनाने वाली ग्रंथियों पर। शोधकर्ताओं का मानना है कि आनुवंशिक और पर्यावरणीय कारकों का संयोजन इसमें योगदान कर सकता है। कई जीनों में बदलाव संवेदनशीलता बढ़ा सकते हैं, जबकि किसी पिछले वायरल या बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण जैसा पर्यावरणीय कारक असामान्य प्रतिरक्षा प्रतिक्रिया को सक्रिय कर सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:355:"Risk factors for Sjogren syndrome include female sex, a family history of autoimmune disease, and having another autoimmune disorder. The condition can occur alongside diseases such as rheumatoid arthritis or lupus. Genetic susceptibility may contribute, although having a risk factor does not mean that a person will necessarily develop Sjogren syndrome.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:173:"महिलाओं में, ऑटोइम्यून रोग और पारिवारिक इतिहास से जोखिम बढ़ता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:404:"Diagnosis of Sjogren syndrome involves a clinical evaluation of symptoms such as dry eyes and dry mouth together with medical history and examination. Blood tests may look for antibodies associated with autoimmune disease. Depending on the symptoms and findings, tests of tear or saliva production, eye examination, or other investigations may be used to support the diagnosis and assess affected organs.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:137:"क्लिनिकल जांच और एंटीबॉडी परीक्षण से निदान होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:359:"Sjogren syndrome cannot currently be reliably prevented because its exact cause is not known and genetic and immune factors play important roles. Early recognition of persistent dry eyes, dry mouth, or other symptoms can support timely medical evaluation. Regular follow-up and appropriate management may help reduce complications and protect affected organs.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:140:"समय पर उपचार और नियमित जांच जटिलताओं को कम कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:453:"Sjögren syndrome usually requires planned medical assessment and ongoing management rather than emergency care. Seek prompt evaluation when dryness, fatigue, joint symptoms, or other problems are persistent or worsening, or when symptoms suggest involvement of the lungs, kidneys, nerves, or other organs. Urgent assessment is appropriate for significant breathing difficulty, severe neurological symptoms, or other rapidly worsening systemic symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:288;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:299;s:10:"disease_id";i:351;s:11:"overview_en";s:544:"Scleroderma is a group of autoimmune diseases characterized by abnormal hardening and thickening of the skin and, in some forms, changes affecting connective tissues and internal organs. The disease can vary considerably between individuals. Some forms mainly affect the skin, while systemic forms may involve the digestive tract, lungs, kidneys, heart, or blood vessels. Symptoms may include skin tightening, changes in skin color, joint stiffness, cold-sensitive fingers, digestive problems, or symptoms related to internal-organ involvement.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:200:"स्क्लेरोडर्मा एक दीर्घकालिक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जिसमें त्वचा कठोर हो जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:526:"Scleroderma develops through abnormal immune activity that promotes inflammation and excessive production or accumulation of collagen and other fibrous tissue. The precise cause is not known. Genetic susceptibility may influence who develops the disease, while environmental or occupational exposures may contribute in some people. Different forms of scleroderma involve different patterns of immune activity and tissue changes, and the reasons why internal organs become affected in systemic disease are not fully understood.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1014:"स्क्लेरोडर्मा एक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जिसमें प्रतिरक्षा तंत्र गलती से स्वस्थ ऊतकों पर हमला करता है। इससे सूजन और कोलेजन तथा अन्य रेशेदार ऊतक के अत्यधिक निर्माण या जमाव को बढ़ावा मिल सकता है, जिससे त्वचा मोटी हो जाती है और systemic disease में आंतरिक अंग भी प्रभावित हो सकते हैं। इसका सटीक कारण ज्ञात नहीं है। कुछ लोगों में आनुवंशिक संवेदनशीलता और सिलिका धूल जैसे पर्यावरणीय संपर्क योगदान दे सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:409:"Risk varies according to the type of scleroderma. Factors that may be associated with increased risk include family history, other autoimmune disorders, genetic susceptibility, and certain environmental or occupational exposures. The disease is more common in women than men. Having an associated autoimmune condition or possible environmental exposure does not mean that scleroderma will necessarily develop.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और ऑटोइम्यून रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:551:"Diagnosis is based on the medical history, physical examination, characteristic skin findings, and assessment for internal-organ involvement. Blood tests may identify autoimmune markers that support the diagnosis but do not establish it by themselves. Depending on symptoms, doctors may use lung function testing, chest imaging, heart evaluation, gastrointestinal studies, kidney tests, or other investigations. In selected cases, a skin biopsy or another tissue examination may help distinguish scleroderma from other disorders with similar features.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:146:"क्लिनिकल और प्रयोगशाला जांच द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:551:"There is no established way to completely prevent scleroderma because its exact cause is unknown. Early recognition of symptoms and regular medical follow-up can help identify organ involvement before complications become severe. People with relevant occupational exposures should follow appropriate safety measures. Avoiding smoking and managing associated cardiovascular, pulmonary, kidney, and other health problems may support overall health. Patients with established disease should follow individualized monitoring and treatment recommendations.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:122:"शीघ्र निदान और उपचार से परिणाम बेहतर होते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:471:"Scleroderma requires specialist medical assessment because it can affect the skin, blood vessels, digestive tract, lungs, kidneys, and heart. Seek prompt care for worsening shortness of breath, chest symptoms, significant swallowing problems, new severe high blood pressure, or reduced urine output. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, sudden neurological symptoms, severe hypertension, or rapidly worsening organ-related symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:289;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:300;s:10:"disease_id";i:352;s:11:"overview_en";s:508:"Vasculitis is a group of disorders characterized by inflammation of blood vessel walls. Inflammation can cause blood vessels to become narrowed, weakened, blocked, or scarred, reducing blood flow to tissues and organs. Symptoms vary widely according to the vessels and organs affected and may include fever, fatigue, weight loss, skin changes, joint or muscle symptoms, nerve problems, kidney abnormalities, or organ-specific symptoms. Some forms affect small areas, while others can involve multiple organs.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:193:"वास्कुलाइटिस रक्त वाहिकाओं की सूजन है जो कई अंगों को प्रभावित कर सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:519:"Vasculitis occurs when abnormal immune activity causes inflammation of blood vessel walls. Some forms are primary disorders in which no single underlying cause is identified. Other forms may occur in association with infections, medicines, autoimmune diseases, or other inflammatory conditions. The inflammation can damage the vessel wall and interfere with normal blood flow. Different forms of vasculitis affect different sizes and types of blood vessels and therefore produce different patterns of organ involvement.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:124:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और संक्रमण इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:463:"Risk factors vary substantially according to the type of vasculitis. They may include autoimmune diseases, certain infections, exposure to particular medicines, smoking, family history, and other underlying inflammatory or medical conditions. Some forms occur more frequently in particular age groups or populations. Having a risk factor does not mean that vasculitis will develop, and many people with vasculitis have no clearly identifiable preventable trigger.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:105:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और सूजन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:549:"Diagnosis depends on the suspected type of vasculitis and the organs involved. Evaluation may include a complete blood count, inflammatory markers, kidney and liver tests, urine testing, and selected antibody or infection studies. Imaging may be used to examine affected blood vessels or organs. In some cases, biopsy of affected skin, kidney, nerve, muscle, lung, or another tissue is needed to confirm inflammation and determine the specific pattern. The diagnostic approach is individualized according to symptoms and suspected organ involvement.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:142:"रक्त जांच, इमेजिंग और बायोप्सी की आवश्यकता हो सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:536:"Many forms of vasculitis cannot be prevented because their causes are unknown or involve abnormal immune activity. When a specific trigger is identified, avoiding that trigger may reduce the risk of recurrence. Not smoking, managing associated autoimmune or other medical conditions, taking prescribed medicines as directed, and attending recommended follow-up can help reduce complications. New or worsening symptoms should be assessed promptly because inflammation affecting major organs or blood vessels may require timely treatment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:101:"मूल रोगों का उपचार जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:461:"Vasculitis requires medical assessment because inflammation of blood vessels can affect multiple organs. Seek prompt care for persistent fever, unexplained weight loss, worsening weakness, new rash, joint symptoms, blood in the urine, breathing problems, or neurological changes. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, sudden weakness or confusion, major bleeding, severe abdominal pain, or rapidly worsening organ function.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:290;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:301;s:10:"disease_id";i:353;s:11:"overview_en";s:511:"Antiphospholipid syndrome is an autoimmune disorder in which persistent antiphospholipid antibodies increase the tendency of the blood to clot abnormally. The condition can cause blood clots in veins or arteries and is also associated with certain pregnancy complications. Clots may affect the legs, lungs, brain, or other organs. Some people have antiphospholipid antibodies without developing clinical complications, so diagnosis requires both appropriate clinical findings and persistent laboratory evidence.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:185:"एंटीफॉस्फोलिपिड सिंड्रोम में रक्त के थक्के बनने का जोखिम बढ़ जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:555:"Antiphospholipid syndrome is associated with persistent antibodies directed against phospholipid-associated proteins. These antibodies can interfere with normal blood-clotting regulation and increase the tendency to form clots. The condition may occur on its own or alongside another autoimmune disease, particularly systemic lupus erythematosus. The presence of antiphospholipid antibodies alone does not necessarily mean that a person has the clinical syndrome; relevant clinical complications and persistent laboratory findings are considered together.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:139:"ऑटोइम्यून एंटीबॉडी रक्त घटकों को प्रभावित करती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:431:"Risk is influenced by persistent antiphospholipid antibodies, a previous blood clot, pregnancy-related complications, and associated autoimmune disease such as systemic lupus erythematosus. Additional factors such as smoking, prolonged immobility, surgery, estrogen exposure, and other inherited or acquired clotting risks can further increase the likelihood of thrombosis. The overall risk varies considerably between individuals.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:167:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और गर्भावस्था संबंधी जटिलताएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:561:"Diagnosis requires appropriate clinical findings together with persistent laboratory evidence of antiphospholipid antibodies. Relevant clinical findings include objectively confirmed thrombosis or specific pregnancy complications recognized as part of the syndrome. Laboratory evaluation may test for lupus anticoagulant, anticardiolipin antibodies, and anti-beta-2 glycoprotein I antibodies. Positive antibody findings generally need to remain present on repeat testing performed at the appropriate interval rather than being based on a single isolated result.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:119:"रक्त में एंटीबॉडी जांच से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:580:"Risk reduction depends on the person's history and whether antiphospholipid syndrome has already caused thrombosis or pregnancy complications. Avoiding smoking, maintaining regular movement, managing blood pressure and other cardiovascular risk factors, and following prescribed preventive treatment can reduce clotting risk. During periods of increased risk such as surgery, prolonged immobility, or pregnancy, medical advice should be followed carefully. People with confirmed antiphospholipid syndrome may require individualized anticoagulation or pregnancy-related management.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:120:"नियमित निगरानी और जोखिम नियंत्रण आवश्यक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:467:"Antiphospholipid syndrome requires medical assessment because it can cause blood clots and pregnancy complications. Seek prompt care for new unexplained leg swelling, pain, redness, recurrent pregnancy loss, or other possible clotting symptoms. Emergency medical attention is needed for sudden shortness of breath, chest pain, coughing blood, sudden weakness or speech difficulty, severe limb pain or discoloration, fainting, or other signs of a major clot or stroke.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:291;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:302;s:10:"disease_id";i:354;s:11:"overview_en";s:374:"Infectious mononucleosis, often called mono, is a contagious viral infection. It commonly causes extreme tiredness, fever, sore throat, swollen lymph nodes, and sometimes an enlarged spleen or liver. Most cases are caused by Epstein-Barr virus. Symptoms often develop gradually and most people recover, although fatigue can continue for several weeks or occasionally longer.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:207:"मोनोन्यूक्लियोसिस एक वायरल संक्रमण है जो प्रायः एपस्टीन-बार वायरस से होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:293:"Mononucleosis is most commonly caused by Epstein-Barr virus, which spreads through contact with infected saliva. Less commonly, similar symptoms can be caused by other infections. The virus may spread through activities involving saliva, including kissing or sharing drinks or eating utensils.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:91:"यह वायरस लार के माध्यम से फैलता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:429:"Mononucleosis is particularly common among teenagers and young adults, although infection can occur at any age. Risk increases with close contact with an infected person because the virus is commonly spread through saliva. Sharing drinks, food, utensils, or personal items that contact saliva can also transmit the infection. Previous lack of exposure to Epstein-Barr virus may make a person susceptible to symptomatic infection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:134:"संक्रमित व्यक्ति के निकट संपर्क से जोखिम बढ़ता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:426:"Diagnosis is based on the symptoms and physical examination, including examination of the throat and lymph nodes and checking for enlargement of the liver or spleen. A healthcare provider may order blood tests to look for changes associated with mononucleosis or antibodies to Epstein-Barr virus. A rapid mono test may be used in appropriate circumstances, although additional testing may be needed when the result is unclear.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:125:"क्लिनिकल जांच और रक्त परीक्षण से निदान होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:403:"There is no vaccine that prevents infectious mononucleosis. The risk of spreading the infection can be reduced by avoiding kissing and by not sharing food, drinks, utensils, or lip balm with someone who has mono. Good hand hygiene is also useful. Because the virus may remain in saliva after symptoms improve, people should follow appropriate precautions during recovery and according to medical advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:152:"स्वच्छता और बर्तनों को साझा न करना संक्रमण से बचा सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:415:"Mononucleosis is usually managed with supportive care, but medical assessment is appropriate when symptoms are severe or persistent. Seek prompt care for significant dehydration, worsening weakness, severe abdominal pain, or difficulty swallowing. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, inability to swallow fluids, fainting, severe abdominal pain, or other signs of a serious complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:292;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:303;s:10:"disease_id";i:355;s:11:"overview_en";s:451:"Sepsis is a life-threatening condition in which the body has an extreme response to an infection, leading to widespread inflammation, impaired blood flow, and organ dysfunction. It can progress rapidly and may cause changes in blood pressure, breathing, mental status, kidney function, or other vital organ functions. Sepsis requires urgent medical assessment and treatment because severe cases can progress to septic shock and multiple-organ failure.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:228:"सेप्सिस संक्रमण के प्रति शरीर की गंभीर प्रतिक्रिया है जो अंगों को प्रभावित कर सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:387:"Sepsis develops when an infection triggers an extreme and dysregulated immune response that damages the body rather than remaining limited to the original site of infection. Bacterial infections are common causes, but viral, fungal, and other infections can also lead to sepsis. Common sources include infections of the lungs, urinary tract, abdomen, bloodstream, skin, or other tissues.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:96:"गंभीर संक्रमण से सेप्सिस हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:404:"Risk is higher in people with severe or untreated infections, chronic medical conditions, weakened immunity, advanced age or very young age, recent hospitalization or surgery, invasive medical devices, or conditions requiring prolonged medical care. People with conditions that impair the body’s ability to fight infection or maintain normal organ function may also have a higher risk of severe sepsis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:178:"पुरानी बीमारी, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा और गंभीर संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:422:"Diagnosis of sepsis is based on the overall clinical picture, evidence of infection, and signs of organ dysfunction. Healthcare professionals may assess vital signs, mental status, urine output, blood oxygenation, and other indicators of organ function. Blood tests, blood cultures, urine tests, imaging, and tests from suspected sites of infection may be used to identify the source and determine the severity of illness.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:119:"रक्त जांच और कल्चर द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:471:"Sepsis cannot always be prevented, but reducing infections and treating infections promptly can lower risk. Recommended measures include staying up to date with appropriate vaccinations, practicing good hand hygiene, caring for wounds properly, following infection-control measures, and seeking medical attention for serious or worsening infections. Managing chronic medical conditions and following prescribed treatment can also reduce vulnerability to severe infection.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1100:"सेप्सिस को हमेशा रोका नहीं जा सकता, लेकिन संक्रमणों को कम करना और उनका समय पर उपचार करना जोखिम घटा सकता है। नियमित टीकाकरण पूरा रखें, हाथों की अच्छी स्वच्छता बनाए रखें, घावों की उचित देखभाल करें और स्वास्थ्य संस्थानों में संक्रमण नियंत्रण संबंधी सलाह का पालन करें। पुरानी बीमारियों वाले लोगों को अपनी उपचार योजना का पालन करना चाहिए। संक्रमण बिगड़ने या गंभीर संक्रमण के संकेत दिखाई देने पर समय पर चिकित्सकीय सहायता लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:418:"Sepsis is a medical emergency requiring immediate assessment and treatment. Seek emergency medical attention for suspected infection accompanied by confusion, very rapid breathing, severe weakness, fainting, very low blood pressure, rapidly worsening illness, bluish or mottled skin, or other signs of poor circulation or organ dysfunction. Do not delay emergency care while waiting for symptoms to become more severe.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:293;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:304;s:10:"disease_id";i:356;s:11:"overview_en";s:477:"Dengue fever is a viral infection transmitted mainly through the bites of infected mosquitoes. It is common in tropical and subtropical regions and is more frequently reported during periods favorable to mosquito breeding. Many infections cause no symptoms or produce a short illness with fever, headache, nausea, rash, and muscle or joint pain. A smaller proportion of infections can progress to severe dengue, which may cause bleeding, shock, and other serious complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:137:"डेंगू बुखार मच्छरों से फैलने वाला वायरल संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:479:"Dengue fever is caused by dengue viruses, which are transmitted primarily through infected Aedes mosquitoes. There are four related dengue virus types, and infection with one type does not necessarily provide protection against the others. The virus enters the bloodstream after the bite of an infected mosquito and can cause a range of illness from mild dengue fever to severe dengue. Rare transmission can also occur through blood exposure and from a pregnant person to a baby.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:108:"संक्रमित एडीज मच्छरों से वायरस फैलता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:492:"Living in or traveling to areas where dengue transmission occurs increases the likelihood of infection because infected mosquitoes may be present. Exposure to mosquito bites is the main risk factor. A previous dengue infection can increase the risk of severe dengue during a later infection. Infants, pregnancy, and certain other circumstances may also increase concern for severe disease. Mosquito exposure is particularly important in warm and wet environments where transmission is common.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:195:"संक्रमित क्षेत्रों में रहना और मच्छरों के संपर्क में आना जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:477:"Dengue is diagnosed using the medical history, symptoms, physical examination, and laboratory testing. Blood tests can detect evidence of dengue infection and may be selected according to the stage of illness. Testing may include molecular tests such as polymerase chain reaction, antibody testing, and other laboratory investigations. A complete blood count and liver-related tests may also help healthcare professionals assess the illness and identify possible complications.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:104:"रक्त जांच से डेंगू की पुष्टि की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:477:"Preventing mosquito bites is an important way to reduce the risk of dengue. Measures include using appropriate insect repellent, wearing clothing that covers the arms and legs, using window screens or other barriers, and sleeping under mosquito nets when appropriate. Reducing standing water around homes can limit mosquito breeding sites. People traveling to areas where dengue occurs should learn about local transmission and take practical precautions throughout their stay.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:129:"मच्छर नियंत्रण और व्यक्तिगत सुरक्षा आवश्यक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:422:"Dengue requires medical monitoring because some infections can progress to severe dengue. Seek prompt medical care for persistent high fever or worsening symptoms. Immediate medical attention is needed for severe abdominal pain, repeated vomiting, bleeding from the nose or gums, vomiting blood, blood in the stool, marked restlessness or weakness, breathing difficulty, fainting, or other signs of shock or severe dengue.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:294;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:305;s:10:"disease_id";i:357;s:11:"overview_en";s:364:"Malaria is a potentially serious disease caused by Plasmodium parasites and transmitted primarily through the bites of infected female Anopheles mosquitoes. It commonly causes fever, chills, sweating, headache, weakness, and body aches. Some forms of malaria can progress rapidly and cause severe complications affecting the brain, blood, kidneys, or other organs.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:190:"मलेरिया मच्छरों से फैलने वाला परजीवी रोग है जिसमें बुखार और ठंड लगती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:371:"Malaria is caused by Plasmodium parasites. An infected Anopheles mosquito introduces parasites into the bloodstream during a bite. The parasites travel to the liver and subsequently infect red blood cells, where they multiply and cause recurring illness. Rarely, transmission can occur through infected blood, contaminated needles, or from an infected mother to her baby.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:187:"यह संक्रमित मच्छरों द्वारा फैलने वाले प्लास्मोडियम परजीवी से होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:374:"Risk depends strongly on geographic exposure to malaria transmission. Travel or residence in areas where malaria is common increases risk, particularly without effective mosquito precautions or preventive medicines when indicated. Young children, pregnant people, older adults, and people with weakened immunity may be more likely to develop severe disease or complications.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:195:"संक्रमित क्षेत्रों में रहना और मच्छरों के संपर्क में आना जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:394:"Malaria should be considered in a person with fever who has recently lived in or traveled to an area where malaria occurs. Diagnosis requires testing for Plasmodium parasites, commonly through blood smears or rapid diagnostic tests. Molecular testing may be used in some settings. Repeated testing can sometimes be necessary when initial testing is negative but clinical suspicion remains high.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:131:"रक्त परीक्षण द्वारा मलेरिया की पुष्टि की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:453:"Prevention focuses on avoiding mosquito bites and using recommended malaria prevention measures when traveling to affected areas. Protective clothing, insect repellent, screened or air-conditioned sleeping areas, and insecticide-treated bed nets can reduce exposure. Depending on destination and individual circumstances, preventive antimalarial medicines may be recommended. Travelers should seek medical advice before visiting malaria-endemic regions.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:136:"मच्छर नियंत्रण और बचाव के उपाय रोकथाम में सहायक हैं.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:438:"Malaria requires prompt medical assessment and treatment because some forms can progress rapidly to severe disease. Seek urgent care for fever with chills or other symptoms after possible mosquito exposure in a malaria-risk area. Emergency assessment is needed for confusion, seizures, severe weakness, difficulty breathing, jaundice with severe illness, repeated vomiting, fainting, or other signs of severe malaria or organ dysfunction.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:295;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:306;s:10:"disease_id";i:358;s:11:"overview_en";s:342:"Typhoid fever is a systemic bacterial infection caused by Salmonella Typhi. It can cause persistent fever, headache, weakness, and abdominal symptoms, including constipation or diarrhoea. The related illness paratyphoid fever is caused by Salmonella Paratyphi. Their symptoms can resemble other infections, so laboratory testing is important.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:187:"टाइफाइड एक जीवाणु संक्रमण है जो पाचन तंत्र और रक्त को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:283:"Typhoid fever occurs when Salmonella Typhi is swallowed in contaminated food or water. The bacteria are shed in the stools of infected people, including some people who no longer have symptoms. Sewage contamination and food handling without adequate handwashing can spread infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1005:"टाइफाइड बुखार साल्मोनेला टाइफी नामक बैक्टीरिया के संक्रमण से होता है। पैराटाइफाइड बुखार संबंधित साल्मोनेला पैराटाइफी बैक्टीरिया के कारण होता है। ये बैक्टीरिया आमतौर पर तब फैलते हैं जब संक्रमित व्यक्ति या वाहक के मल से भोजन या पानी दूषित हो जाता है। खराब स्वच्छता और असुरक्षित पेयजल से संक्रमण फैलने की संभावना बढ़ जाती है, विशेषकर उन क्षेत्रों में जहां टाइफाइड अधिक पाया जाता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:340:"Risk is higher where typhoid is common and safe drinking water, sanitation, or food hygiene are inadequate. Residence or travel in these settings, including parts of South Asia, can increase exposure. Consuming contaminated food or water increases risk; absence of appropriate vaccination leaves a person without vaccine-derived protection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:121:"खराब स्वच्छता और दूषित भोजन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:392:"Assessment considers symptoms and travel or exposure history, but symptoms alone cannot reliably distinguish typhoid from other infections. Blood culture is the main diagnostic test, and more than one culture may be needed. Other specimen cultures may contribute. Serological tests alone can produce misleading results and should not replace appropriate clinical and culture-based assessment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:119:"रक्त जांच और कल्चर द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:356:"Prevention combines safe drinking water, sanitation, handwashing after using the toilet and before preparing food or eating, and careful food preparation. Vaccination can reduce typhoid risk where recommended, but protection is incomplete and does not replace food and water precautions. Available typhoid vaccines do not protect against paratyphoid fever.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:136:"स्वच्छ भोजन, साफ पानी और टीकाकरण बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:431:"Typhoid fever requires medical assessment and appropriate treatment because untreated infection can cause serious complications. Seek prompt care for persistent fever, worsening weakness, dehydration, abdominal symptoms, or inability to maintain fluids. Emergency assessment is needed for severe abdominal pain, gastrointestinal bleeding, confusion, fainting, severe dehydration, difficulty breathing, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:296;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:307;s:10:"disease_id";i:359;s:11:"overview_en";s:599:"Chikungunya is a viral infection transmitted primarily by infected Aedes mosquitoes. It commonly causes sudden fever and severe joint pain, often accompanied by headache, muscle pain, joint swelling, rash, or fatigue. Most people recover, but joint pain can persist for weeks or months in some cases. The illness can resemble other mosquito-borne infections, so clinical evaluation may be important when symptoms occur after exposure in an area where chikungunya is circulating. Treatment is generally focused on relieving symptoms and maintaining adequate fluids while monitoring for complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:124:"चिकनगुनिया मच्छरों से फैलने वाला वायरल रोग है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:509:"Chikungunya is caused by chikungunya virus, which is transmitted mainly through the bites of infected Aedes mosquitoes. A mosquito becomes infected after feeding on a person who has the virus and can later transmit it to another person. Transmission is therefore closely associated with the presence of infected mosquitoes. The virus does not usually spread through ordinary casual contact between people. Infected mosquitoes can transmit the virus during periods when the virus is circulating in a community.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:153:"यह मच्छरों द्वारा फैलने वाले चिकनगुनिया वायरस से होता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:523:"Risk of chikungunya is greatest in places where infected Aedes mosquitoes are present and the virus is circulating. Living in or traveling to an affected area increases the opportunity for mosquito exposure. Risk may also increase where mosquitoes can breed around homes because of standing water in suitable containers or other locations. People of any age can become infected, while older adults, very young children, pregnant people, and individuals with certain chronic illnesses may have greater risk of complications.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:96:"मच्छरों के संपर्क से जोखिम बढ़ता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:577:"Diagnosis of chikungunya is based on symptoms, exposure history, and laboratory testing when confirmation is required. Blood tests can detect viral genetic material during the early phase of illness, while antibody testing may become useful later in the infection. Because chikungunya can resemble dengue and other infections that cause fever and joint pain, the healthcare professional may consider the local pattern of disease and the patient's travel or mosquito exposure. Testing may be especially important when the diagnosis affects management or public-health decisions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:138:"क्लिनिकल जांच और रक्त परीक्षण से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:607:"Preventing mosquito bites is an important way to reduce the risk of chikungunya. Use appropriate insect repellent, wear clothing that reduces exposed skin, and use screens or air conditioning where available. Mosquitoes can breed in standing water, so removing or covering water-holding containers around homes can reduce breeding sites. During outbreaks or travel to affected areas, additional mosquito precautions are especially important. People who develop symptoms should take measures to avoid further mosquito exposure during the early illness period so mosquitoes do not acquire the virus from them.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:118:"मच्छर नियंत्रण संक्रमण से बचाव में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:393:"Chikungunya usually causes a self-limited illness, but medical assessment is appropriate when symptoms are severe or persistent. Seek care for prolonged or severe joint pain, dehydration, persistent fever, or worsening symptoms. Prompt or emergency evaluation is appropriate for breathing difficulty, confusion, fainting, severe neurological symptoms, or other signs of a serious complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:297;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:308;s:10:"disease_id";i:360;s:11:"overview_en";s:442:"Leptospirosis is an infectious disease caused by Leptospira bacteria. The bacteria can be present in water or soil contaminated with urine from infected animals. People may become infected when contaminated water or soil contacts broken skin or mucous membranes. Illness can range from a mild febrile infection to a severe disease affecting the kidneys, liver, lungs, or other organs. Symptoms may appear several days to weeks after exposure.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:190:"लेप्टोस्पायरोसिस दूषित पानी या मिट्टी से फैलने वाला जीवाणु संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:436:"Leptospirosis is caused by infection with Leptospira bacteria. The bacteria are shed in the urine of infected animals and can contaminate freshwater, wet soil, and other environments. Infection can occur when a person has direct contact with contaminated water, soil, animals, or materials. Exposure may occur through occupational, household, or recreational activities. Person-to-person transmission is uncommon and occurs only rarely.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"लेप्टोस्पाइरा जीवाणु इस रोग के लिए जिम्मेदार हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:513:"Risk increases with exposure to freshwater or soil that may be contaminated with animal urine, particularly in warm climates. Occupational risk can occur among farmers, ranchers, veterinarians, sewage workers, agricultural workers, animal handlers, and others who work around animals or contaminated environments. Recreational activities such as swimming, canoeing, kayaking, or biking in potentially contaminated areas can also increase exposure. Contact with infected pets, livestock, or rodents may contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:126:"दूषित पानी और पशुओं के संपर्क से जोखिम बढ़ता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:496:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, exposure history, physical examination, and laboratory testing. Because early symptoms can resemble other infections, information about recent contact with contaminated water, soil, or animals is important. Blood or urine tests can detect evidence of Leptospira infection, and additional laboratory testing may be performed depending on the stage of illness. Kidney and liver function tests and other blood tests may help assess disease severity and complications.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:116:"रक्त और मूत्र परीक्षण से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:556:"Reducing contact with potentially contaminated water and soil is an important way to prevent leptospirosis. People working or participating in recreational activities in areas where exposure is possible should use appropriate protective clothing and footwear and cover cuts or abrasions. Avoiding contact with potentially contaminated water and controlling rodents around homes can reduce exposure. Pets and livestock should receive appropriate veterinary care, and people with high-risk occupational exposure should follow recommended protective measures.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:138:"दूषित पानी से बचाव और स्वच्छता रोकथाम में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:465:"Leptospirosis requires prompt medical assessment because severe infection can affect the kidneys, liver, lungs, and other organs. Seek urgent care for persistent fever with severe headache, muscle pain, vomiting, or jaundice after possible exposure to contaminated water or animals. Emergency assessment is needed for difficulty breathing, confusion, reduced urine output, severe bleeding, jaundice with worsening illness, fainting, or other signs of organ failure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:298;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:311;s:10:"disease_id";i:363;s:11:"overview_en";s:535:"Prediabetes means blood glucose levels are higher than normal but not yet in the range used to diagnose type 2 diabetes. It often develops because the body becomes less responsive to insulin, causing glucose to remain elevated in the blood. Prediabetes may have no obvious symptoms and is often discovered through blood testing. Without appropriate lifestyle changes and follow-up, some people progress to type 2 diabetes. Early identification provides an opportunity to address modifiable risk factors and reduce future complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:233:"प्रीडायबिटीज में रक्त शर्करा सामान्य से अधिक होती है लेकिन मधुमेह स्तर तक नहीं पहुंचती।";s:9:"causes_en";s:578:"Prediabetes usually develops when the body becomes resistant to insulin or does not produce enough insulin to maintain normal blood glucose levels. Risk is influenced by excess body weight, physical inactivity, increasing age, family history of diabetes, and previous gestational diabetes. Certain ethnic and genetic backgrounds also influence risk. Conditions associated with insulin resistance can contribute. Prediabetes is not caused by eating one particular food, but long-term dietary patterns, inactivity, and excess body fat can increase the likelihood of developing it.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:98:"इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:511:"Risk factors for prediabetes include overweight or obesity, increased waist circumference, physical inactivity, family history of type 2 diabetes, increasing age, previous gestational diabetes, high blood pressure, abnormal cholesterol levels, and certain ethnic or genetic backgrounds. Polycystic ovary syndrome and other conditions associated with insulin resistance can also increase risk. Risk rises when several factors occur together, but prediabetes can develop even without every recognized risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1185:"प्रीडायबिटीज के जोखिम कारकों में अधिक वजन या मोटापा, कम शारीरिक गतिविधि, बढ़ती उम्र और टाइप 2 मधुमेह का पारिवारिक इतिहास शामिल हैं। गर्भावस्था के दौरान मधुमेह का पिछला इतिहास और कुछ मेटाबॉलिक स्थितियां भी जोखिम बढ़ा सकती हैं। अलग-अलग लोगों में जोखिम अलग हो सकता है और रक्तचाप, कोलेस्ट्रॉल, भोजन, नींद तथा अन्य स्वास्थ्य कारकों से प्रभावित हो सकता है। अधिक जोखिम वाले लोगों में नियमित जांच से असामान्य ग्लूकोज स्तर का जल्दी पता लगाने में मदद मिल सकती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:530:"Prediabetes is diagnosed with blood glucose testing rather than symptoms alone. Common tests include fasting plasma glucose, hemoglobin A1C, and an oral glucose tolerance test. Results are interpreted according to established diagnostic thresholds and may need confirmation depending on the circumstances. A clinician may also assess blood pressure, cholesterol, weight, waist circumference, family history, and other diabetes risk factors. Regular follow-up testing may be recommended because glucose levels can change over time.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1009:"प्रीडायबिटीज का निदान रक्त में ग्लूकोज की जांच से किया जाता है। सामान्य जांचों में फास्टिंग प्लाज्मा ग्लूकोज, A1C और ओरल ग्लूकोज टॉलरेंस टेस्ट शामिल हैं। परिणामों की व्याख्या स्थापित प्रयोगशाला सीमाओं के अनुसार की जाती है और आवश्यकता होने पर पुष्टि के लिए दोबारा जांच की जा सकती है। प्रीडायबिटीज का अर्थ है कि रक्त ग्लूकोज सामान्य से अधिक है लेकिन अभी मधुमेह की सीमा तक नहीं पहुंचा है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:555:"Prediabetes can often be managed and, in many people, progression to type 2 diabetes can be delayed or prevented through sustained lifestyle changes. Regular physical activity, a balanced eating pattern, maintaining or reaching a healthy weight when appropriate, and avoiding tobacco can reduce metabolic risk. People at increased risk should undergo recommended glucose screening. Follow-up testing is important because prediabetes can progress over time. A healthcare professional can help create an individualized prevention plan based on overall risk.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1134:"प्रीडायबिटीज से टाइप 2 मधुमेह की ओर बढ़ने के जोखिम को स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाकर अक्सर कम किया जा सकता है। नियमित शारीरिक गतिविधि, आवश्यकता होने पर धीरे-धीरे वजन कम करना और संतुलित भोजन रक्त ग्लूकोज नियंत्रण में सुधार कर सकते हैं। तंबाकू से बचना और अत्यधिक कैलोरी का सेवन सीमित करना भी मेटाबॉलिक स्वास्थ्य के लिए उपयोगी है। प्रीडायबिटीज वाले लोगों को व्यक्तिगत निगरानी और रोकथाम की रणनीति के लिए स्वास्थ्य विशेषज्ञ से सलाह लेनी चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:332:"Prediabetes usually does not cause an emergency by itself. Seek prompt medical evaluation for symptoms suggesting markedly elevated blood glucose, such as excessive thirst and urination, unexplained weakness, vomiting, confusion, or rapidly worsening illness, particularly in someone with known diabetes or other metabolic problems.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:299;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:312;s:10:"disease_id";i:364;s:11:"overview_en";s:451:"Diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA, is a life-threatening diabetes complication in which insufficient insulin leads to ketone accumulation and increased blood acidity. It occurs most often in type 1 diabetes but can also occur in type 2 diabetes. Warning signs include thirst, frequent urination, vomiting, abdominal pain, deep or rapid breathing, fruity-smelling breath, and increasing drowsiness or confusion. Suspected DKA requires emergency assessment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:132:"डायबिटिक कीटोएसिडोसिस मधुमेह की गंभीर जटिलता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:287:"When effective insulin is insufficient, the body breaks down fat and produces ketones that can accumulate in the blood. Infection or another illness, missed insulin, and problems with insulin delivery can precipitate DKA. It can also be the first sign of previously undiagnosed diabetes.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1091:"DKA तब होता है जब शरीर में पर्याप्त प्रभावी इंसुलिन नहीं होता और ग्लूकोज का सही उपयोग नहीं हो पाता। इसके बाद शरीर ऊर्जा के लिए वसा को तोड़ता है, जिससे कीटोन नामक अम्लीय पदार्थ बनते हैं और रक्त में जमा हो सकते हैं। इंसुलिन की खुराक छूटना या कम होना, संक्रमण या अन्य बीमारी, नए मधुमेह का पता चलना और कुछ दवाएं या चिकित्सकीय परिस्थितियां इसके कारण बन सकती हैं। यह टाइप 1 मधुमेह में अधिक सामान्य है, लेकिन टाइप 2 में भी हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:251:"Risk is greater when diabetes is accompanied by insufficient insulin, acute illness, or disrupted insulin delivery. Some medicines, including SGLT2 inhibitors, can increase DKA risk. DKA is not restricted to people who already know they have diabetes.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:108:"मधुमेह का खराब नियंत्रण जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:310:"Clinicians assess glucose, ketones—particularly blood beta-hydroxybutyrate—and blood acidity using pH or bicarbonate. Electrolytes, kidney function, and possible precipitants are also evaluated. Diagnosis depends on the combined findings, not glucose alone: DKA can occur without markedly elevated glucose.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:150:"रक्त शर्करा, कीटोन और रक्त गैस जांच से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:264:"People with diabetes can reduce risk by following their existing prescribed care plan, monitoring glucose as advised, and having an agreed plan for illness. That plan should explain when to check ketones and when to contact the healthcare team or seek urgent help.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:907:"डायबिटिक कीटोएसिडोसिस से बचाव के लिए मधुमेह की उपचार योजना का पालन करें, निर्धारित इंसुलिन लें और रक्त शर्करा की नियमित जांच करें। बीमारी के दौरान या रक्त शर्करा अधिक होने पर चिकित्सकीय सलाह के अनुसार कीटोन की जांच करें। चिकित्सकीय सलाह के बिना इंसुलिन बंद न करें। डायबिटीज टीम से व्यक्तिगत sick-day योजना और चेतावनी संकेतों के बारे में जानकारी लें।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:376:"Diabetic ketoacidosis is a medical emergency requiring immediate treatment. Seek emergency medical attention for high blood glucose with repeated vomiting, abdominal pain, deep or rapid breathing, fruity-smelling breath, severe dehydration, marked weakness, confusion, drowsiness, or loss of consciousness. Do not delay care while attempting to manage severe symptoms at home.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:300;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:313;s:10:"disease_id";i:365;s:11:"overview_en";s:372:"Metabolic syndrome is a group of conditions that occur together and increase the risk of cardiovascular disease, stroke, and type 2 diabetes. It commonly involves increased waist circumference, high blood pressure, abnormal blood glucose, high triglycerides, and low HDL cholesterol. Having several of these abnormalities together is more concerning than having one alone.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:222:"मेटाबोलिक सिंड्रोम कई स्थितियों का समूह है जो हृदय रोग और मधुमेह का जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:422:"Metabolic syndrome develops through interacting metabolic abnormalities rather than a single cause. Abdominal obesity, insulin resistance, physical inactivity, unhealthy dietary patterns, aging, and genetic factors can contribute. Conditions such as high blood pressure and abnormal cholesterol or triglyceride levels may occur as part of the syndrome. The underlying metabolic changes can reinforce one another over time.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"मोटापा, इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध और उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:380:"Risk factors include excess abdominal weight, physical inactivity, increasing age, insulin resistance, unhealthy dietary patterns, family history, and certain hormonal or metabolic conditions. The likelihood is also influenced by high blood pressure, abnormal blood lipids, and elevated blood glucose. Risk generally increases as more components of metabolic syndrome are present.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:142:"निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली और अस्वस्थ आहार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:432:"Diagnosis is based on measurement of the metabolic abnormalities that make up the syndrome. Healthcare professionals may assess waist circumference, blood pressure, fasting glucose or other measures of blood sugar, triglycerides, and HDL cholesterol. Medical history and physical examination help identify associated conditions. Different clinical guidelines use slightly different thresholds for defining the individual components.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:125:"रक्तचाप, शर्करा और कोलेस्ट्रॉल जांच की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:414:"Regular physical activity, a balanced diet, maintaining a healthy weight, avoiding tobacco, and limiting excessive alcohol can help reduce metabolic risk. Managing blood pressure, blood glucose, and cholesterol is also important. Reducing excess abdominal weight when appropriate can improve several metabolic abnormalities. People with multiple risk factors should have appropriate health screening and follow-up.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:105:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाने से बचाव संभव है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:431:"Metabolic syndrome generally requires planned medical assessment and long-term management of blood pressure, blood glucose, cholesterol, weight, and other cardiovascular risk factors. Seek prompt care when these conditions become poorly controlled or new symptoms develop. Emergency assessment is appropriate for chest pain, sudden neurological symptoms, severe shortness of breath, or other signs of an acute cardiovascular event.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:301;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:314;s:10:"disease_id";i:366;s:11:"overview_en";s:422:"Obesity is a chronic disease involving excess body fat that can affect health and increase the risk of other conditions. Body mass index, or BMI, is commonly used as one measure of weight relative to height, although it does not directly measure body fat and has limitations for individuals with high muscle mass or reduced muscle mass. Obesity can affect children and adults and results from multiple interacting factors.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:132:"मोटापा शरीर में अत्यधिक वसा जमा होने की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:436:"Obesity develops when energy intake and energy use remain out of balance over time, but the causes are more complex than food intake and exercise alone. Genetic, biological, environmental, social, behavioral, and economic factors can influence body weight. Certain medicines and medical conditions may contribute. Sleep, stress, eating patterns, physical activity, and the availability of healthy foods can also affect long-term weight.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:157:"अधिक कैलोरी सेवन और कम शारीरिक गतिविधि इसके मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:407:"Risk factors include a family history of obesity, limited physical activity, eating patterns that provide more energy than the body uses, inadequate sleep, chronic stress, certain medicines, and some medical conditions. Environmental and social factors can influence access to nutritious foods and opportunities for physical activity. Risk also varies with age, life stage, genetics, and individual biology.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:147:"निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली, तनाव और खराब आहार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:464:"Diagnosis involves assessment of weight, height, BMI, waist size, health history, and physical activity. A healthcare professional may review previous weight changes, eating patterns, medicines, and medical conditions. Blood tests or other investigations may be used to identify obesity-related conditions or possible contributors. BMI is useful for population and clinical assessment but does not distinguish fat from muscle or show where body fat is distributed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:149:"बीएमआई और क्लिनिकल मूल्यांकन द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:500:"Healthy eating patterns, regular physical activity, adequate sleep, and long-term attention to weight can help reduce the risk of obesity. Prevention strategies work best when they are realistic and sustainable rather than based on rapid weight loss. Children and adults benefit from supportive environments that make nutritious foods, movement, sleep, and healthy routines easier to maintain. People with medical or medication-related contributors should discuss them with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:137:"संतुलित आहार और नियमित व्यायाम मोटापे से बचाते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:401:"Obesity generally requires planned medical assessment and long-term management rather than emergency treatment. Seek professional care when weight is associated with diabetes, high blood pressure, sleep apnea, mobility problems, or other health complications. Urgent assessment is appropriate for severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, sudden neurological symptoms, or another acute medical problem.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:302;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:315;s:10:"disease_id";i:367;s:11:"overview_en";s:362:"Cushing syndrome occurs when the body is exposed to excessive levels of cortisol for a prolonged period. It can result from long-term use of corticosteroid medicines or from conditions that cause the body to produce too much cortisol. Symptoms may include weight gain, changes in skin appearance, muscle weakness, high blood pressure, and changes in blood sugar.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:232:"कुशिंग सिंड्रोम एक हार्मोनल विकार है जो लंबे समय तक उच्च कॉर्टिसोल स्तर के कारण होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:385:"Cushing syndrome can result from taking corticosteroid medicines for a long period or at high doses. It can also occur when the body produces excessive cortisol because of a tumor or other abnormality involving the pituitary gland, adrenal glands, or, less commonly, another part of the body. Pituitary tumors that produce excess ACTH are a common cause of endogenous Cushing syndrome.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:210:"अत्यधिक कॉर्टिसोल उत्पादन या लंबे समय तक स्टेरॉयड उपयोग इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:346:"Risk factors depend on the cause. Long-term or high-dose corticosteroid treatment is an important risk factor for medication-related Cushing syndrome. Conditions that cause abnormal ACTH or cortisol production can lead to endogenous disease. A family history of certain endocrine tumors or inherited syndromes may increase the risk of some forms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:166:"हार्मोनल विकार और लंबे समय तक स्टेरॉयड उपयोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:418:"Diagnosis of Cushing syndrome involves determining whether cortisol levels are abnormally high and then identifying the source of excess cortisol. Tests may include measurement of cortisol in urine, saliva, or blood and suppression testing. Once excess cortisol is confirmed, additional blood tests and imaging may be used to determine whether the cause involves the pituitary gland, adrenal glands, or another source.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:143:"रक्त जांच, मूत्र जांच और इमेजिंग से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:378:"Cushing syndrome related to corticosteroid medicines may be reduced by using these medicines only as prescribed and at the lowest effective dose for the appropriate duration. Corticosteroids should not be stopped suddenly without medical guidance. People with conditions that can cause excess cortisol should receive appropriate monitoring and treatment to reduce complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:179:"स्टेरॉयड का चिकित्सकीय निगरानी में उपयोग बचाव में सहायक हो सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:443:"Cushing syndrome requires medical assessment because prolonged excess cortisol can affect blood pressure, blood glucose, bones, muscles, and cardiovascular health. Seek prompt evaluation for worsening weakness, uncontrolled blood pressure or diabetes, significant infection, or other progressive symptoms. Emergency assessment is appropriate for severe chest pain, severe shortness of breath, confusion, fainting, or other acute complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:303;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:316;s:10:"disease_id";i:368;s:11:"overview_en";s:373:"Addison disease is a disorder in which the adrenal glands do not produce enough of certain hormones, particularly cortisol and, in many cases, aldosterone. The condition can develop when the adrenal glands are damaged, most commonly through an autoimmune process. Symptoms may develop gradually and can include fatigue, weakness, weight loss, and changes in blood pressure.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:177:"एडिसन रोग में अधिवृक्क ग्रंथियां पर्याप्त हार्मोन नहीं बनाती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:378:"Addison disease most commonly develops when the immune system attacks and damages the adrenal glands. Other causes can include infections such as tuberculosis, bleeding into the adrenal glands, tumors, certain inherited conditions, and other forms of adrenal damage. The underlying cause determines how much adrenal hormone production is affected and how the condition develops.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:171:"ऑटोइम्यून क्षति और अधिवृक्क ग्रंथि विकार इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:365:"Risk factors for Addison disease depend on the underlying cause. The autoimmune form is more likely in people who have other autoimmune conditions, including autoimmune thyroid disease, type 1 diabetes, vitiligo, pernicious anemia, or hypoparathyroidism. Other forms may be associated with infections, adrenal bleeding, tumors, or certain rare inherited conditions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1191:"एडिसन रोग के जोखिम कारक उसके कारण पर निर्भर करते हैं। इसका ऑटोइम्यून रूप उन लोगों में अधिक देखा जा सकता है जिन्हें थायरॉइड रोग, टाइप 1 मधुमेह, विटिलिगो, परनिशियस एनीमिया, हाइपोपैराथायरॉइडिज्म या मायस्थीनिया ग्रेविस जैसी अन्य ऑटोइम्यून स्थितियाँ हों। अन्य रूपों का संबंध तपेदिक, HIV या फंगल संक्रमण, एड्रिनल ग्रंथियों में रक्तस्राव, ट्यूमर या कुछ दुर्लभ वंशानुगत स्थितियों से हो सकता है। इन कारकों का होना यह निश्चित नहीं करता कि व्यक्ति को एडिसन रोग होगा।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:382:"Diagnosis of Addison disease involves assessment of symptoms, medical history, and hormone testing. Blood tests may show low cortisol levels and abnormalities in sodium or potassium. An ACTH stimulation test is commonly used to assess how well the adrenal glands respond to stimulation. Additional hormone tests, antibody testing, and imaging may help identify the underlying cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:134:"हार्मोन जांच और इमेजिंग द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:426:"Addison disease cannot always be prevented because autoimmune and other underlying causes may not be avoidable. Early recognition of symptoms and appropriate medical evaluation can help identify adrenal hormone deficiency before serious complications develop. People with known adrenal insufficiency should follow prescribed treatment and medical advice to reduce the risk of severe hormone deficiency and related emergencies.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:120:"समय पर निदान और उपचार जटिलताओं को कम करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:457:"Addison disease requires ongoing hormone replacement and medical follow-up. Seek prompt medical attention for worsening weakness, vomiting, diarrhea, dehydration, dizziness, low blood pressure, or inability to take prescribed steroid medication. Emergency assessment is required for suspected adrenal crisis with severe abdominal pain, repeated vomiting, severe weakness, confusion, loss of consciousness, difficulty breathing, or severe low blood pressure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:304;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:317;s:10:"disease_id";i:369;s:11:"overview_en";s:373:"Hyperparathyroidism occurs when one or more parathyroid glands produce too much parathyroid hormone. This hormone regulates calcium levels in the blood and bones. Excess hormone can raise blood calcium and cause calcium to be released from bones. Some people have no symptoms, while others may develop kidney stones, bone problems, weakness, fatigue, or digestive symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:200:"हाइपरपैराथायरायडिज्म में पैराथायरॉयड हार्मोन का अत्यधिक उत्पादन होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:421:"Hyperparathyroidism most often occurs because one or more parathyroid glands become overactive. Primary hyperparathyroidism is commonly caused by a benign enlargement or adenoma of a parathyroid gland and less commonly by multiple-gland enlargement or cancer. Secondary hyperparathyroidism develops when another condition, such as chronic kidney disease or vitamin D deficiency, causes persistent low calcium stimulation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:151:"पैराथायरॉयड ग्रंथि की असामान्यताएं इसका मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:358:"Risk depends on the type of hyperparathyroidism. Primary disease is more common with increasing age and may be associated with certain inherited endocrine disorders or previous radiation exposure to the neck. Secondary hyperparathyroidism is more likely with chronic kidney disease, vitamin D deficiency, or conditions that interfere with calcium absorption.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:130:"बढ़ती उम्र और अंतःस्रावी विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:351:"Diagnosis is usually based on blood tests showing elevated calcium and parathyroid hormone levels in primary disease. Additional tests may measure phosphate, vitamin D, kidney function, and urinary calcium. Bone density testing and imaging may be used to assess complications. In secondary disease, testing focuses on identifying the underlying cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:125:"रक्त कैल्शियम और हार्मोन जांच से निदान होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:359:"Some forms of hyperparathyroidism cannot be prevented. Maintaining adequate vitamin D and calcium, managing kidney disease appropriately, and treating conditions that cause chronic disturbances in calcium balance may reduce the risk of secondary disease. People with known parathyroid or endocrine disorders should follow recommended monitoring and treatment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:93:"नियमित जांच से शीघ्र पहचान संभव है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:457:"Hyperparathyroidism generally requires medical evaluation and monitoring because prolonged excess parathyroid hormone can affect bones and kidneys. Seek prompt care for recurrent kidney stones, significant weakness, worsening bone pain, dehydration, or symptoms suggesting high calcium levels. Emergency assessment is appropriate for severe confusion, persistent vomiting, severe dehydration, abnormal heart symptoms, or other signs of severe hypercalcemia.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:305;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:318;s:10:"disease_id";i:370;s:11:"overview_en";s:354:"Hypoparathyroidism is a condition in which the parathyroid glands produce too little parathyroid hormone. This can lead to low levels of calcium and increased phosphorus levels in the blood and may affect muscles, nerves, and other body functions. It can develop after neck surgery, from autoimmune disease, or from inherited or other less common causes.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:166:"हाइपोपैराथायरायडिज्म में पैराथायरॉयड हार्मोन की कमी होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:370:"Hypoparathyroidism occurs when the parathyroid glands produce too little parathyroid hormone. The most common cause is damage to or removal of the glands during thyroid or other neck surgery. Other causes include autoimmune destruction of the glands, very low magnesium levels, inherited conditions, and rare developmental abnormalities affecting the parathyroid glands.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1364:"हाइपोपैराथायरॉइडिज्म तब होता है जब पैराथायरॉइड ग्रंथियाँ पर्याप्त पैराथायरॉइड हार्मोन नहीं बनातीं, जिससे रक्त में कैल्शियम कम और फॉस्फोरस अधिक हो जाता है। इसका सबसे सामान्य कारण थायरॉइड या गर्दन की सर्जरी के दौरान इन ग्रंथियों को चोट लगना है। अन्य कारणों में पैराथायरॉइड ग्रंथियों पर ऑटोइम्यून हमला, रक्त में बहुत कम मैग्नीशियम और दुर्लभ रूप से रेडियोधर्मी आयोडीन उपचार शामिल हैं। कुछ लोग जन्म से ही इन ग्रंथियों के असामान्य विकास के साथ होते हैं या उन्हें अन्य अंतःस्रावी विकारों से जुड़ा वंशानुगत रूप हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:366:"Risk factors for hypoparathyroidism include previous thyroid or neck surgery, autoimmune disorders, inherited conditions affecting the parathyroid glands, and disorders that cause very low magnesium levels. A history of conditions affecting the parathyroid glands or nearby tissues can increase the likelihood of developing inadequate parathyroid hormone production.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:140:"गर्दन की सर्जरी और ऑटोइम्यून विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:378:"Diagnosis of hypoparathyroidism is based on blood tests showing low calcium and inappropriately low parathyroid hormone levels, often together with increased phosphorus. Doctors may also assess magnesium and other laboratory values to identify contributing factors. Medical history, including previous neck surgery or autoimmune disease, can help determine the underlying cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:150:"रक्त कैल्शियम और हार्मोन जांच द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:370:"Hypoparathyroidism cannot always be prevented because it may result from autoimmune, inherited, or other causes. Careful monitoring of calcium and parathyroid function after thyroid or neck surgery may help identify problems early. Appropriate treatment and regular follow-up can help maintain calcium levels and reduce complications in people who develop the condition.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:119:"उचित उपचार और निगरानी जटिलताओं को कम करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:427:"Hypoparathyroidism requires medical assessment and monitoring because low parathyroid hormone can cause low calcium levels and related symptoms. Seek prompt care for increasing muscle cramps, tingling, weakness, or other symptoms suggesting worsening calcium imbalance. Emergency assessment is needed for severe muscle spasms, seizures, difficulty breathing, abnormal heart rhythm symptoms, confusion, or loss of consciousness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:49:35";}i:306;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:319;s:10:"disease_id";i:371;s:11:"overview_en";s:356:"Acromegaly is a hormonal disorder in adults caused by excessive production of growth hormone, usually from a benign pituitary tumor. The excess hormone increases insulin-like growth factor 1, leading over time to enlargement of bones and soft tissues and potentially causing changes in appearance, joint problems, headaches, and other health complications.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:194:"एक्रोमेगली वयस्कों में अत्यधिक ग्रोथ हार्मोन के कारण होने वाला विकार है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:383:"Acromegaly is usually caused by a benign tumor of the pituitary gland that produces too much growth hormone. The excess growth hormone increases production of insulin-like growth factor 1, which drives enlargement of bones and soft tissues. Rarely, tumors outside the pituitary gland can stimulate excessive growth hormone or related hormone production. Most cases are not inherited.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1015:"एक्रोमेगाली आमतौर पर पिट्यूटरी ग्रंथि के एक सौम्य ट्यूमर के कारण होती है, जो बहुत अधिक ग्रोथ हार्मोन बनाता है। अतिरिक्त ग्रोथ हार्मोन इंसुलिन-जैसे ग्रोथ फैक्टर-1 का स्तर बढ़ाता है, जिससे हड्डियों और मुलायम ऊतकों का आकार बढ़ सकता है। दुर्लभ मामलों में पिट्यूटरी के बाहर के ट्यूमर भी अत्यधिक ग्रोथ हार्मोन या संबंधित हार्मोन के उत्पादन को बढ़ा सकते हैं। अधिकांश मामले वंशानुगत नहीं होते।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:461:"Most cases of acromegaly occur sporadically, so there are few established preventable risk factors. A family history of certain rare genetic conditions can increase susceptibility to pituitary tumors or excessive growth hormone production. Some inherited syndromes, including multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1 and related disorders, are associated with an increased risk. The condition can occur in adults of either sex and is usually diagnosed in middle age.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1115:"एक्रोमेगाली के अधिकांश मामले स्वतः विकसित होते हैं, इसलिए इसके कुछ ही स्पष्ट रोकथाम योग्य जोखिम कारक ज्ञात हैं। कुछ दुर्लभ आनुवंशिक स्थितियों का पारिवारिक इतिहास पिट्यूटरी ट्यूमर या अत्यधिक ग्रोथ हार्मोन उत्पादन की संभावना बढ़ा सकता है। मल्टीपल एंडोक्राइन नियोप्लासिया टाइप 1 जैसी कुछ वंशानुगत स्थितियां बढ़े हुए जोखिम से जुड़ी हैं। यह रोग किसी भी लिंग के वयस्कों में हो सकता है और अक्सर मध्यम आयु में इसका निदान होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:384:"Acromegaly is diagnosed by evaluating growth hormone activity and related hormone levels. An IGF-1 blood test is commonly used because it reflects growth hormone activity over time. A growth hormone suppression test may be used to confirm excessive growth hormone production. Imaging, particularly MRI of the pituitary gland, can help identify a pituitary tumor when one is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:147:"ग्रोथ हार्मोन जांच और एमआरआई द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:366:"Acromegaly cannot usually be prevented because it is most often caused by a benign pituitary tumor that develops without a known preventable cause. Early recognition and treatment can help reduce complications. People with symptoms such as enlargement of the hands or feet, changes in facial features, excessive sweating, or headaches should seek medical evaluation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1006:"एक्रोमेगाली से आमतौर पर बचाव संभव नहीं होता क्योंकि यह प्रायः पिट्यूटरी ट्यूमर के कारण होती है, जिसका कोई ज्ञात रोकथाम योग्य कारण नहीं होता। ग्रोथ हार्मोन की अधिकता की जल्दी पहचान और उपचार से हृदय, हड्डियों, जोड़ों, दृष्टि और मेटाबॉलिज्म से जुड़ी जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद मिल सकती है। उपचार के बाद नियमित फॉलो-अप से हार्मोन स्तर और संबंधित स्वास्थ्य समस्याओं की निगरानी की जाती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:419:"Acromegaly generally requires planned endocrine evaluation and ongoing treatment. Seek prompt medical assessment when symptoms are progressing or complications involving the heart, joints, vision, breathing, or other organs are suspected. Emergency assessment is appropriate for severe headache with sudden vision changes, chest pain, severe breathing difficulty, or other acute neurological or cardiovascular symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:307;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:320;s:10:"disease_id";i:372;s:11:"overview_en";s:671:"Gigantism is a rare disorder in which excessive growth hormone is produced during childhood or adolescence, while the growth plates are still open. This causes unusually rapid growth and excessive height. Most cases are associated with a growth hormone-producing tumor in the pituitary gland. Children with gigantism may grow much faster and taller than expected for their age, sometimes accompanied by enlargement of the hands and feet, coarse facial features, headaches, excessive sweating, or joint discomfort. Because the condition occurs before growth plates close, early diagnosis is important to limit complications associated with prolonged excess growth hormone.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:229:"जाइगैन्टिज्म बचपन में अत्यधिक ग्रोथ हार्मोन स्राव के कारण होने वाली दुर्लभ स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:632:"Gigantism is usually caused by excessive production of growth hormone by a benign tumor of the pituitary gland. The excess growth hormone increases production of insulin-like growth factor 1, which stimulates growth of bones and other tissues. Rarely, other tumors or inherited conditions can contribute. Excess growth hormone stimulates the liver and other tissues to produce insulin-like growth factor 1, which promotes growth of bones and soft tissues. A pituitary adenoma is the usual source of excess hormone. Less commonly, growth hormone-releasing hormone from another tumor can stimulate excessive growth hormone production.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:132:"पिट्यूटरी ग्रंथि की असामान्यताएं मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:587:"Risk factors include conditions that affect growth hormone regulation and, in some cases, inherited genetic syndromes associated with pituitary tumors. A family history of certain endocrine disorders may increase risk. Gigantism remains rare because the underlying causes are uncommon. Risk is influenced primarily by disorders capable of producing excess growth hormone. A personal or family history of pituitary or endocrine tumors can be relevant, particularly when an inherited syndrome is present. Because gigantism is rare, most children with rapid growth do not have the disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1044:"जायगैन्टिज्म तब होता है जब हड्डियों की वृद्धि प्लेटें बंद होने से पहले शरीर में अत्यधिक ग्रोथ हार्मोन बनता है। इसका कारण अक्सर ग्रोथ हार्मोन बनाने वाला पिट्यूटरी ट्यूमर होता है। इसका जोखिम सामान्य जीवनशैली कारकों से अधिक उन स्थितियों से जुड़ा होता है जो ग्रोथ हार्मोन की अधिकता पैदा करती हैं। कुछ दुर्लभ आनुवंशिक स्थितियां पिट्यूटरी ट्यूमर और संबंधित हार्मोन विकारों की संभावना बढ़ा सकती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:639:"Diagnosis involves measuring growth hormone-related markers and evaluating abnormal growth patterns. Blood testing commonly measures insulin-like growth factor 1, and specialized testing may assess growth hormone suppression. Imaging, usually magnetic resonance imaging of the pituitary gland, can identify a tumor. Evaluation may include growth charts, physical examination, blood levels of insulin-like growth factor 1, and growth hormone testing. An oral glucose tolerance test may be used to determine whether growth hormone suppresses normally. Pituitary MRI is commonly used after biochemical evidence suggests excess growth hormone.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:959:"जायगैन्टिज्म के मूल्यांकन में ग्रोथ हार्मोन और इंसुलिन-लाइक ग्रोथ फैक्टर-1 (IGF-1) की जांच, वृद्धि के पैटर्न और शारीरिक संकेतों का आकलन शामिल होता है। हार्मोन की अधिकता का संदेह होने पर ग्रोथ हार्मोन के असामान्य नियंत्रण की पुष्टि के लिए अतिरिक्त जांच की जा सकती है। मस्तिष्क की इमेजिंग, आमतौर पर MRI, पिट्यूटरी ट्यूमर या अन्य संरचनात्मक कारणों की पहचान में मदद कर सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:658:"Gigantism cannot usually be prevented because it most often results from a pituitary disorder that develops independently of lifestyle. Early recognition of unusually rapid growth, enlarged hands or feet, headaches, or other related symptoms can help identify excessive growth hormone production sooner. There is no routine lifestyle measure known to prevent pituitary adenomas that cause gigantism. Parents and healthcare professionals can monitor unusually rapid growth and investigate growth that consistently exceeds expected patterns. Early assessment may allow treatment before excessive growth and hormone-related complications become more pronounced.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:90:"समय पर उपचार बेहतर परिणाम देता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:421:"Gigantism requires specialist endocrine assessment because excessive growth hormone during childhood can affect bones, joints, and the cardiovascular system. Seek prompt evaluation when unusually rapid growth, headaches, vision changes, or other concerning symptoms develop. Emergency assessment is appropriate for sudden severe headache, major vision changes, loss of consciousness, or other acute neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:308;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:321;s:10:"disease_id";i:373;s:11:"overview_en";s:402:"Growth hormone deficiency occurs when the body does not produce enough growth hormone. In children, it can result in slower growth and shorter stature, while in adults it may affect body composition, bone health, muscle mass, energy, and quality of life. The condition may result from problems affecting the pituitary gland, hypothalamus, genetic conditions, injury, tumors, or other medical disorders.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:172:"ग्रोथ हार्मोन की कमी में शरीर पर्याप्त ग्रोथ हार्मोन नहीं बनाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:346:"Growth hormone deficiency may result from abnormalities of the pituitary gland or hypothalamus. Causes include congenital or genetic disorders, pituitary tumors, surgery or radiation affecting the brain, head injury, infections, inflammation, and other conditions affecting hormone production. In some people, no specific cause can be identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:151:"पिट्यूटरी विकार और हार्मोनल असामान्यताएं इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:349:"Risk factors include genetic or congenital disorders, diseases affecting the pituitary or hypothalamus, brain tumors, head injury, surgery or radiation involving the brain, and certain inflammatory or infectious conditions. Children with unexplained poor growth may require evaluation for growth hormone deficiency and other causes of short stature.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"आनुवंशिक स्थितियां और पिट्यूटरी रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:395:"Diagnosis requires assessment of growth patterns, medical history, physical development, and other hormone-related findings. Blood testing may measure growth hormone-related markers such as insulin-like growth factor 1, while stimulation testing may be used because growth hormone levels naturally fluctuate. Imaging of the pituitary region and other tests may help identify an underlying cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:159:"हार्मोन जांच और वृद्धि मूल्यांकन द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:387:"There is no established way to prevent all cases of growth hormone deficiency, particularly when it results from genetic or congenital conditions. Protecting children from serious head injury, receiving appropriate care for conditions affecting the brain or pituitary gland, and obtaining timely evaluation of unexplained growth problems may help identify and manage the condition early.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:99:"शीघ्र पहचान बेहतर विकास में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:423:"Growth hormone deficiency generally requires planned endocrine assessment and follow-up, particularly in children with impaired growth. Seek prompt evaluation when growth is significantly delayed or other pituitary hormone problems are suspected. Emergency assessment is appropriate for sudden severe headache, altered consciousness, severe vomiting, or other symptoms suggesting an acute pituitary or neurological problem.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:309;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:322;s:10:"disease_id";i:374;s:11:"overview_en";s:544:"Diabetes insipidus is a disorder of water balance characterized by excessive urination and intense thirst. It occurs when the body does not produce enough antidiuretic hormone, does not respond properly to the hormone, or, in some cases, has excessive water intake that produces similar symptoms. Unlike diabetes mellitus, diabetes insipidus is not primarily a disorder of blood sugar regulation. The amount of urine can be very large and dilute, and inadequate fluid replacement can lead to dehydration and disturbances in blood sodium levels.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:210:"डायबिटीज इन्सिपिडस में हार्मोन असंतुलन के कारण अत्यधिक प्यास और पेशाब होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:576:"Diabetes insipidus results from inadequate production or release of antidiuretic hormone, reduced response of the kidneys to this hormone, or other disturbances in the mechanisms that regulate water balance. Central forms may result from damage involving the hypothalamus or pituitary gland after injury, surgery, infection, tumors, inflammation, or other disorders. Nephrogenic forms occur when the kidneys cannot respond appropriately to antidiuretic hormone and may be related to kidney disease, genetic conditions, high blood calcium, or certain medicines such as lithium.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:149:"एंटीडाययूरेटिक हार्मोन की कमी या प्रतिरोध इसका कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:452:"Risk factors depend on the type of diabetes insipidus. Central disease may be associated with head injury, brain or pituitary surgery, tumors, infections, inflammation, autoimmune conditions, or inherited disorders. Nephrogenic disease may be associated with chronic kidney problems, inherited abnormalities, high blood calcium, and medicines that interfere with the kidney response to antidiuretic hormone. Some cases have no clearly identified cause.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:136:"मस्तिष्क चोट और अंतःस्रावी विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:551:"Diagnosis involves assessing excessive urination and thirst while determining the cause of the water-balance abnormality. Tests may include measurement of urine volume and concentration, blood sodium and osmolality, urine osmolality, and other laboratory studies. A supervised water-deprivation test may be used in selected cases, sometimes followed by administration of a medicine that mimics antidiuretic hormone. Additional imaging or hormone evaluation may be needed when a central cause involving the hypothalamus or pituitary gland is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:147:"वॉटर डिप्रिवेशन टेस्ट और हार्मोन जांच से निदान होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:541:"Diabetes insipidus cannot always be prevented because some forms result from inherited conditions or unavoidable damage to the brain or kidneys. Preventing head injuries and obtaining appropriate treatment for conditions affecting the pituitary gland or kidneys may reduce the risk of some acquired cases. People taking medicines that can affect kidney function or water balance should have appropriate medical follow-up. Persistent excessive thirst or urination should be evaluated rather than assumed to be ordinary increased fluid intake.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1142:"डायबिटीज इंसिपिडस के कई मामलों को रोका नहीं जा सकता क्योंकि वे मस्तिष्क या गुर्दों को प्रभावित करने वाली स्थितियों के कारण होते हैं। बचाव के उपाय इसके मूल कारण पर निर्भर करते हैं। सिर की अनावश्यक चोट से बचना, दवाओं का केवल चिकित्सकीय निर्देश के अनुसार उपयोग करना और पिट्यूटरी ग्रंथि या गुर्दों को प्रभावित करने वाली स्थितियों का उचित प्रबंधन कुछ जोखिमों को कम कर सकता है। ज्ञात कारण वाले लोगों को नियमित चिकित्सकीय फॉलो-अप रखना चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:409:"Diabetes insipidus requires medical assessment because inadequate control of water balance can cause severe dehydration and electrolyte abnormalities. Seek prompt care for excessive thirst and urination with worsening weakness, dizziness, confusion, or inability to maintain adequate fluid intake. Emergency assessment is needed for severe dehydration, confusion, fainting, seizures, or loss of consciousness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:310;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:323;s:10:"disease_id";i:375;s:11:"overview_en";s:390:"Hyperprolactinemia is an abnormally elevated level of the hormone prolactin in the blood. Elevated prolactin can interfere with normal reproductive hormone function and may cause menstrual irregularities, infertility, reduced libido, erectile dysfunction, or unexpected milk production. Symptoms and effects depend on the degree and duration of prolactin elevation and its underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:182:"हाइपरप्रोलैक्टिनेमिया में प्रोलैक्टिन हार्मोन का स्तर बढ़ जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:389:"Hyperprolactinemia may result from pregnancy or breastfeeding, medicines that increase prolactin, pituitary prolactin-secreting tumors such as prolactinomas, hypothyroidism, and some disorders affecting the kidneys or liver. Temporary increases can also occur with physical or emotional stress, exercise, sleep, or other physiological factors. In some people, no clear cause is identified.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:133:"पिट्यूटरी ट्यूमर और हार्मोनल विकार इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:414:"Risk depends largely on the underlying cause. Factors may include use of medicines known to increase prolactin, pituitary disorders such as prolactinomas, thyroid disease, pregnancy, breastfeeding, and conditions affecting kidney or liver function. Persistent hormonal or reproductive symptoms may warrant evaluation, particularly when accompanied by visual symptoms or other signs suggesting a pituitary disorder.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:127:"अंतःस्रावी विकार और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:447:"Diagnosis generally begins with a blood test measuring prolactin. Because prolactin levels can vary and may be temporarily elevated, testing may sometimes be repeated under appropriate conditions. Healthcare professionals review medicines and associated symptoms and may check thyroid function and other laboratory values. Pituitary imaging, usually with MRI, may be considered when prolactin remains elevated or a pituitary disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:147:"रक्त प्रोलैक्टिन जांच और इमेजिंग से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:430:"Many causes of hyperprolactinemia cannot be prevented. Reviewing medicines with a healthcare professional before making changes, managing thyroid and other systemic diseases, and seeking evaluation for persistent menstrual, fertility, sexual, or unexpected milk-production symptoms can help identify the condition early. People with symptoms suggesting a pituitary disorder should follow recommended testing and medical follow-up.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:128:"नियमित निगरानी और उपचार जटिलताओं को कम करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:366:"Hyperprolactinemia generally requires planned medical evaluation to identify the underlying cause. Seek prompt assessment when persistent menstrual changes, infertility, sexual dysfunction, breast discharge, headaches, or visual problems occur. Emergency evaluation is appropriate for sudden severe headache, sudden vision loss, or other acute neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:311;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:324;s:10:"disease_id";i:376;s:11:"overview_en";s:507:"Pheochromocytoma is a rare tumor that develops from specialized cells of the adrenal glands and can cause excessive release of epinephrine and norepinephrine. These hormones affect heart rate, metabolism and blood pressure. The tumor usually develops in the adrenal gland but can occasionally occur outside it. Episodes may cause severe or recurring headaches, sweating, rapid or pounding heartbeat and high blood pressure. Most pheochromocytomas are not cancerous, although a small number can be malignant.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:147:"फिओक्रोमोसायटोमा अधिवृक्क ग्रंथि का दुर्लभ ट्यूमर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:487:"Pheochromocytoma develops from abnormal growth of cells in adrenal gland tissue that produce catecholamine hormones. A tumor may occur in one adrenal gland, both glands or, less commonly, in tissue outside the adrenal glands. Most cases occur without a clearly identified cause. Some pheochromocytomas occur as part of inherited conditions and may run in families. Hereditary forms can be associated with syndromes such as multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 and other genetic disorders.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:139:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन और अधिवृक्क ट्यूमर इसके कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:451:"Risk factors include having a family history of pheochromocytoma or an inherited syndrome associated with adrenal or endocrine tumors. People with certain hereditary conditions may have a higher likelihood of developing one or more tumors. Pheochromocytoma can occur at any age but is most commonly diagnosed during early to middle adulthood. Close relatives of people with hereditary disease may also need evaluation because some cases are inherited.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:575:"फियोक्रोमोसाइटोमा का जोखिम कुछ आनुवंशिक सिंड्रोम और जीन परिवर्तन से बढ़ सकता है, जिनमें मल्टीपल एंडोक्राइन नियोप्लासिया टाइप 2, वॉन हिप्पेल-लिंडाउ रोग और न्यूरोफिब्रोमेटोसिस टाइप 1 जैसी वंशानुगत स्थितियां शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:538:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and physical examination, particularly when episodes of headache, sweating, palpitations or high blood pressure suggest excess catecholamine production. Blood or urine testing can measure catecholamines and related substances such as metanephrines. Imaging studies may then be used to locate the tumor, including CT or MRI of the abdomen and, in selected cases, specialized nuclear imaging such as an MIBG scan. Genetic evaluation may be considered when the history suggests an inherited condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:109:"हार्मोन जांच और इमेजिंग से निदान होता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:485:"There is no established way to prevent most pheochromocytomas because many develop without a preventable cause. When a hereditary syndrome is present, genetic counseling and appropriate screening of affected families can help identify tumors earlier. Close relatives of people with inherited pheochromocytoma may benefit from evaluation and periodic testing. People who have previously been treated successfully should continue follow-up testing because the tumor can sometimes return.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:138:"शीघ्र निदान और उपचार गंभीर जटिलताओं को रोक सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:489:"Pheochromocytoma requires specialist medical assessment because excess catecholamine release can cause severe blood-pressure and cardiovascular complications. Seek prompt care for recurrent severe headaches, sweating, palpitations, or marked blood-pressure elevation. Emergency assessment is needed for severe chest pain, severe headache with neurological symptoms, very high blood pressure with symptoms, fainting, severe shortness of breath, or other signs of a cardiovascular emergency.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:312;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:325;s:10:"disease_id";i:377;s:11:"overview_en";s:390:"Adrenal insufficiency is a condition in which the adrenal glands do not produce enough hormones needed for normal body function. It may result from problems affecting the adrenal glands themselves or from disorders involving the pituitary or other parts of the hormone-regulating system. Symptoms can develop gradually and may include fatigue, weakness, weight loss, and low blood pressure.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:210:"अधिवृक्क अपर्याप्तता में अधिवृक्क ग्रंथियां पर्याप्त हार्मोन नहीं बनाती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:390:"Adrenal insufficiency can result from inadequate hormone production by the adrenal glands or from problems with the pituitary or hypothalamus that prevent appropriate stimulation of the glands. Autoimmune disease and damage to the adrenal glands are important causes. Other causes may include infections, certain medicines, bleeding, tumors, or other disorders affecting hormone production.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:172:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग और अधिवृक्क ग्रंथि की क्षति इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:390:"Risk factors for adrenal insufficiency depend on whether the problem originates in the adrenal glands, pituitary gland, or another part of the hormone-regulating system. Autoimmune disorders and chronic illnesses may increase risk. Certain infections, prolonged use of some medicines, previous surgery, bleeding, tumors, or other conditions affecting hormone production may also contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:145:"ऑटोइम्यून विकार और पुरानी बीमारियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:376:"Diagnosis of adrenal insufficiency is based on symptoms, medical history, physical examination, and blood tests measuring adrenal hormones. Testing may show low cortisol or abnormal electrolyte levels. An ACTH stimulation test can assess adrenal response. Depending on the suspected cause, additional hormone tests, antibody testing, and imaging such as CT or MRI may be used.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1206:"एड्रिनल इंसफिशिएंसी का मूल्यांकन लक्षणों, चिकित्सकीय इतिहास और एड्रिनल हार्मोन मापने वाली रक्त जाँच से किया जाता है। जाँच में कोर्टिसोल का स्तर कम तथा सोडियम या पोटैशियम के स्तर असामान्य मिल सकते हैं। ACTH stimulation test से यह देखा जा सकता है कि एड्रिनल ग्रंथियाँ adrenocorticotropic hormone के प्रति कैसी प्रतिक्रिया देती हैं। संभावित कारण के अनुसार ACTH, रेनिन, एल्डोस्टेरोन या एंटीबॉडी की जाँच तथा एड्रिनल ग्रंथियों में असामान्यता देखने के लिए CT जैसे इमेजिंग परीक्षण भी किए जा सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:377:"Adrenal insufficiency cannot always be prevented because it may result from autoimmune disease or other conditions that cannot be avoided. Early diagnosis and appropriate treatment can reduce the risk of complications. People taking medicines that may affect adrenal function should follow medical guidance and should not change long-term treatment without professional advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:120:"समय पर निदान और उपचार जटिलताओं को कम करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:449:"Adrenal insufficiency requires ongoing medical care and appropriate hormone replacement. Seek prompt medical attention for worsening weakness, vomiting, diarrhea, dehydration, dizziness, low blood pressure, or inability to take prescribed medication. Emergency assessment is required for suspected adrenal crisis with severe weakness, repeated vomiting, severe abdominal pain, confusion, fainting, difficulty breathing, or severe low blood pressure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:313;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:326;s:10:"disease_id";i:378;s:11:"overview_en";s:368:"An adrenal adenoma is a usually benign growth that develops in one of the adrenal glands. Many adrenal adenomas do not cause symptoms and are discovered during imaging performed for another reason. Some adenomas produce hormones, which can lead to conditions such as excess cortisol or aldosterone and related symptoms such as high blood pressure or metabolic changes.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:167:"एड्रिनल एडेनोमा अधिवृक्क ग्रंथि का सामान्यतः सौम्य ट्यूमर है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:354:"Adrenal adenomas develop from cells of the adrenal gland and are usually benign. Some are nonfunctioning and do not produce excess hormones, while others produce hormones such as cortisol or aldosterone. The exact reason an individual develops an adrenal adenoma is often unclear. Certain genetic conditions can increase the likelihood of adrenal tumors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:158:"हार्मोनल असामान्यताएं और आनुवंशिक कारक योगदान दे सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:348:"Risk depends on the type of adrenal adenoma and whether it produces hormones. Some benign adrenal tumors are associated with genetic syndromes, while others occur without an identifiable risk factor. Hormone-producing adenomas may be detected because of high blood pressure, abnormal potassium levels, Cushing syndrome, or another hormonal problem.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:148:"पारिवारिक इतिहास और अंतःस्रावी विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:345:"An adrenal adenoma may be discovered incidentally during CT or MRI performed for another medical reason. Evaluation may include imaging to determine the size and appearance of the mass and blood or urine tests to determine whether it produces hormones. Additional endocrine testing is selected according to symptoms and suspected hormone excess.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:122:"इमेजिंग और हार्मोन जांच से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:398:"There is no established lifestyle method for preventing adrenal adenomas. People with known genetic conditions associated with adrenal tumors may require appropriate medical surveillance. When an adrenal mass is discovered, evaluation of its size, appearance, and hormone production can help identify tumors that require closer monitoring or treatment. Follow-up should be based on clinical advice.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:140:"नियमित निगरानी जटिलताओं की शीघ्र पहचान में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:423:"Adrenal adenomas usually require medical evaluation to determine whether the lesion produces hormones or requires further monitoring. Seek prompt assessment when new symptoms suggest hormone excess, significant abdominal or flank pain, or unexplained changes in blood pressure or blood glucose. Emergency care is appropriate for severe abdominal pain, fainting, severe blood-pressure abnormalities, or other acute symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:314;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:327;s:10:"disease_id";i:379;s:11:"overview_en";s:332:"Insulin resistance occurs when the body's cells respond less effectively to insulin, the hormone that helps glucose move from the blood into cells. The pancreas may initially produce more insulin to compensate. Over time, insulin resistance can contribute to higher blood glucose levels, prediabetes, and eventually type 2 diabetes.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:188:"इंसुलिन प्रतिरोध में शरीर की कोशिकाएं इंसुलिन का उचित जवाब नहीं देतीं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:331:"Insulin resistance develops through a combination of metabolic, genetic, and lifestyle factors. Excess body fat, particularly abdominal fat, physical inactivity, and genetic susceptibility can contribute. It is also associated with conditions such as prediabetes, type 2 diabetes, polycystic ovary syndrome, and metabolic syndrome.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:153:"मोटापा, निष्क्रियता और चयापचय विकार इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:291:"Risk is increased by overweight or obesity, especially abdominal obesity, physical inactivity, a family history of diabetes, prediabetes, increasing age, polycystic ovary syndrome, and a history of gestational diabetes. Certain metabolic conditions and some medicines may also increase risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:153:"मोटापा, खराब आहार और निष्क्रिय जीवनशैली जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:368:"Insulin resistance does not have one single diagnostic test in routine practice. Healthcare professionals may assess blood glucose, HbA1c, fasting insulin, lipid levels, blood pressure, waist circumference, and other metabolic findings. The results are interpreted together with medical history and examination to identify prediabetes, diabetes, or metabolic syndrome.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:144:"रक्त शर्करा और इंसुलिन जांच द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:374:"Regular physical activity, maintaining a healthy weight, and eating a balanced diet can help improve insulin sensitivity and reduce the risk of progression to prediabetes and type 2 diabetes. Avoiding tobacco, getting adequate sleep, and managing blood pressure and cholesterol can also support metabolic health. People at increased risk should follow recommended screening.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:131:"स्वस्थ आहार और नियमित व्यायाम बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:369:"Insulin resistance generally requires planned medical assessment and long-term management of metabolic risk factors. Seek professional care when associated with increasing blood glucose, prediabetes, obesity, or other metabolic abnormalities. Urgent medical assessment is appropriate for symptoms suggesting severe hyperglycemia or another acute metabolic complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:315;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:328;s:10:"disease_id";i:380;s:11:"overview_en";s:410:"Hypoglycemia occurs when blood glucose falls below the level needed for normal body function. It can cause sweating, shakiness, hunger, weakness, dizziness, palpitations, irritability, confusion, and difficulty concentrating. Severe hypoglycemia can cause seizures, loss of consciousness, or other serious complications. It is particularly important in people who use insulin or certain medicines for diabetes.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:189:"हाइपोग्लाइसीमिया में रक्त शर्करा का स्तर असामान्य रूप से कम हो जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:457:"Common causes of hypoglycemia include insulin and certain glucose-lowering medicines, especially when medication effects exceed the available glucose. It may also occur after missed or delayed meals, prolonged or unusually intense physical activity, alcohol consumption without adequate food intake, or illness. Less common causes include hormonal disorders, severe liver or kidney disease, certain tumors, and other conditions affecting glucose regulation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:158:"मधुमेह उपचार, हार्मोनल विकार और उपवास इसके कारण हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:429:"Risk is increased in people who use insulin or certain glucose-lowering medicines, particularly when medication doses, meals, and physical activity are not well balanced. Irregular meals, prolonged or intense exercise, alcohol use, kidney or liver disease, hormonal disorders, and previous episodes of hypoglycemia can also increase risk. Older adults and people with complex medical conditions may require additional monitoring.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:120:"मधुमेह और अंतःस्रावी विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:467:"Diagnosis involves documenting low blood glucose together with symptoms that are compatible with hypoglycemia and improvement after glucose is restored. Blood glucose may be measured with a glucose meter or laboratory testing depending on the situation. When episodes are unexplained or recurrent, additional evaluation may be required to determine whether medicines, hormonal disorders, organ disease, dietary factors, or another underlying condition is responsible.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:103:"रक्त शर्करा जांच से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:452:"People at risk of hypoglycemia should follow prescribed medication and meal plans and monitor blood glucose when advised. Meals should not be skipped when medication depends on regular food intake, and physical activity should be planned appropriately. People who have been advised to do so may carry a rapid source of glucose and should learn to recognize early symptoms. Excessive alcohol intake should be avoided, particularly without adequate food.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:131:"नियमित भोजन और ग्लूकोज निगरानी बचाव में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:342:"Hypoglycemia can become dangerous when blood glucose falls substantially. Seek prompt medical attention for recurrent or unexplained episodes. Emergency assistance is needed for severe confusion, seizures, inability to safely swallow or take glucose, loss of consciousness, or symptoms that do not improve promptly with appropriate treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:316;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:329;s:10:"disease_id";i:381;s:11:"overview_en";s:624:"Influenza is a contagious respiratory illness caused by influenza viruses. It commonly develops suddenly and may cause fever, chills, cough, sore throat, muscle aches, headache, and marked fatigue. Some people, particularly young children, may also experience vomiting or diarrhea. Most healthy people recover without serious complications, but influenza can lead to pneumonia and other severe problems in older adults, young children, pregnant people, and individuals with certain chronic conditions or weakened immunity. Seasonal vaccination and appropriate infection-control measures help reduce illness and transmission.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:129:"इन्फ्लुएंजा एक संक्रामक वायरल श्वसन संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:555:"Influenza is caused by infection with influenza viruses, particularly influenza A and influenza B viruses responsible for seasonal outbreaks. The viruses spread mainly through respiratory particles released when an infected person coughs, sneezes, talks, or breathes. Transmission can also occur when people touch contaminated surfaces and then touch their mouth, nose, or eyes. Influenza viruses continually change through genetic variation, which contributes to the appearance of different circulating strains and the need for updated seasonal vaccines.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:136:"इन्फ्लुएंजा वायरस इस संक्रमण के लिए जिम्मेदार हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:525:"The risk of influenza is increased during periods when influenza viruses are circulating widely. Older adults, young children, pregnant people, and individuals with chronic heart, lung, kidney, metabolic, or neurological conditions may have a greater risk of serious complications. Weakened immunity can also increase risk. Close contact with infected people, crowded indoor environments, and inadequate ventilation can facilitate transmission. Lack of seasonal vaccination may increase susceptibility to circulating strains.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:126:"भीड़भाड़ और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:635:"Influenza can often be diagnosed clinically from symptoms and the pattern of illness during periods of active community transmission. Rapid influenza diagnostic tests may provide results quickly, although their ability to detect infection varies. Molecular tests, including rapid molecular assays and other laboratory methods, can provide more sensitive confirmation when testing is indicated. Testing is particularly useful when the result may affect treatment, infection-control decisions, or evaluation of people at higher risk of complications. The diagnosis should also consider other respiratory infections with similar symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:174:"क्लिनिकल मूल्यांकन और प्रयोगशाला जांच द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:562:"Annual influenza vaccination is an important measure for reducing the risk of influenza and its complications. Good hand hygiene, covering coughs and sneezes, improving indoor ventilation, and avoiding close contact with people who are ill can reduce transmission. People with influenza should stay home when sick when possible and follow local guidance about returning to normal activities. Higher-risk individuals should seek medical advice promptly when significant influenza symptoms develop because antiviral treatment may be most useful when started early.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:105:"टीकाकरण और स्वच्छता बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:393:"Influenza is often self-limited, but some people develop serious complications. Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening symptoms, dehydration, persistent high fever, or significant weakness, particularly in people at higher risk of complications. Emergency care is needed for severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, confusion, fainting, bluish lips or skin, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:317;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:330;s:10:"disease_id";i:382;s:11:"overview_en";s:386:"Respiratory syncytial virus infection is a common viral respiratory illness that usually causes mild, cold-like symptoms. These may include runny nose, congestion, cough, sneezing, fever, reduced appetite, and wheezing. RSV can sometimes cause more serious illness, including bronchiolitis or pneumonia, particularly in infants, older adults, and people with certain medical conditions.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:178:"आरएसवी संक्रमण श्वसन तंत्र को प्रभावित करने वाला वायरल संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:398:"RSV infection is caused by respiratory syncytial virus. The virus spreads mainly through respiratory particles and through contact with contaminated surfaces followed by touching the eyes, nose, or mouth. Infection can occur when an infected person coughs, sneezes, or has close contact with another person. RSV commonly spreads in homes, schools, childcare settings, and other shared environments.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:118:"रेस्पिरेटरी सिंशियल वायरस इस रोग का कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:360:"Severe RSV illness is more likely in very young infants, older adults, and people with certain chronic medical conditions or weakened immune systems. Risk may also be affected by underlying heart or lung disease. Crowded settings and close contact with infected people increase exposure to the virus, particularly during periods when RSV is circulating widely.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:180:"शिशु, बुजुर्ग और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा वाले लोगों में जोखिम अधिक होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:429:"RSV infection is often diagnosed from symptoms and clinical examination. Testing may be used when confirmation is important, particularly in people at higher risk of severe illness or in healthcare settings. Molecular tests such as PCR can detect RSV genetic material, while some rapid antigen tests can also identify infection. The clinician may also assess breathing and oxygen levels when respiratory symptoms are significant.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:153:"क्लिनिकल जांच और वायरल परीक्षण द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:398:"RSV prevention includes reducing close contact with people who are sick, improving hand hygiene, cleaning frequently touched surfaces, and avoiding touching the face with unwashed hands. Staying home when ill can reduce spread. Vaccination or preventive antibody products may be recommended for certain infants, older adults, or other higher-risk groups according to current public health guidance.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:153:"हाथों की स्वच्छता और संक्रमण नियंत्रण बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:427:"Respiratory syncytial virus infection is usually mild but can cause bronchiolitis or pneumonia, particularly in infants, older adults, and people with underlying conditions. Seek prompt care for worsening cough, wheezing, poor fluid intake, or increasing breathing difficulty. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing problems, bluish skin or lips, marked lethargy, dehydration, or inability to maintain oxygenation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:318;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:331;s:10:"disease_id";i:383;s:11:"overview_en";s:306:"Swine flu generally refers to influenza caused by influenza A viruses that can infect humans, including the H1N1 virus associated with the 2009 pandemic. The illness usually resembles other forms of influenza and may cause fever, cough, sore throat, body aches, headache, fatigue, and respiratory symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:159:"स्वाइन फ्लू इन्फ्लुएंजा A (H1N1) वायरस से होने वाला श्वसन रोग है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:371:"Swine flu is caused by influenza A viruses that are capable of infecting humans. These viruses spread mainly through respiratory droplets and smaller particles released when an infected person coughs, sneezes, talks, or breathes. Transmission can also occur through close contact with contaminated secretions. Different influenza strains can circulate at different times.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:90:"H1N1 इन्फ्लुएंजा वायरस इसका कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:361:"The risk of influenza complications varies with the circulating virus and individual health. Young children, older adults, pregnant people, and individuals with certain chronic medical conditions or weakened immune systems may have greater risk of serious illness. Crowded settings and close contact with infected people can increase the chance of transmission.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:126:"भीड़भाड़ और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:374:"Diagnosis is often based on influenza-like symptoms together with knowledge of circulating influenza viruses and local transmission. Rapid influenza tests or molecular tests may be used when confirmation is clinically useful, particularly for people at higher risk of complications or those who are seriously ill. Testing methods and availability vary by healthcare setting.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:171:"क्लिनिकल मूल्यांकन और प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:383:"Annual influenza vaccination is an important way to reduce the risk of influenza and its complications. Hand hygiene, good indoor ventilation, covering coughs and sneezes, avoiding close contact with people who are ill, and staying home when sick can reduce transmission. People at increased risk of complications should follow current medical advice about vaccination and treatment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:121:"टीकाकरण और श्वसन स्वच्छता बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:364:"Swine flu can range from a mild respiratory illness to severe influenza with complications. Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening fever, breathing symptoms, dehydration, or significant weakness. Emergency care is needed for severe difficulty breathing, chest pain, confusion, fainting, bluish lips or skin, severe dehydration, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:319;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:332;s:10:"disease_id";i:384;s:11:"overview_en";s:346:"Avian influenza is an infection caused by influenza A viruses that primarily affect birds but can occasionally infect humans and other animals. Human infections are uncommon but can sometimes cause severe respiratory illness. Most human infections occur after close or prolonged contact with infected birds, animals, or contaminated environments.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:740:"एवियन इन्फ्लुएंजा या बर्ड फ्लू इन्फ्लुएंजा वायरस से होने वाला संक्रमण है जो मुख्य रूप से पक्षियों को प्रभावित करता है। मनुष्यों में संक्रमण असामान्य है, लेकिन संक्रमित पक्षियों, पोल्ट्री, पशुओं या दूषित वातावरण के संपर्क के बाद हो सकता है और कभी-कभी गंभीर श्वसन रोग पैदा कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:352:"Avian influenza is caused by influenza A viruses that naturally circulate among birds. Certain strains can occasionally cross the species barrier and infect humans, usually following exposure to infected poultry, wild birds, other infected animals, or contaminated environments. Human-to-human transmission is uncommon for most avian influenza viruses.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:558:"एवियन इन्फ्लुएंजा मुख्य रूप से पक्षियों में फैलने वाले इन्फ्लुएंजा A वायरस के कारण होता है। संक्रमित पशुओं या दूषित सामग्री के निकट संपर्क के दौरान वायरस आंख, नाक, मुंह या श्वसन मार्ग से शरीर में प्रवेश कर सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:331:"Risk is mainly associated with close or prolonged contact with infected birds or animals, contaminated environments, or surfaces containing infectious material. People working with poultry or other potentially infected animals may have greater exposure. Risk can vary according to the circulating virus and local animal infections.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:1138:"एवियन इन्फ्लुएंजा के संक्रमण का जोखिम मुख्य रूप से संक्रमित पक्षियों, पोल्ट्री या दूषित वातावरण के निकट या लंबे समय तक संपर्क से जुड़ा होता है। पोल्ट्री के साथ काम करने वाले या संक्रमित जानवरों को संभालने वाले लोगों में संपर्क अधिक हो सकता है। दूषित सतहों या सामग्री के संपर्क से भी जोखिम हो सकता है। मनुष्यों में संक्रमण असामान्य है और जोखिम वायरस के प्रकार, संपर्क की स्थिति तथा सार्वजनिक स्वास्थ्य परिस्थितियों पर निर्भर करता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:382:"Diagnosis of avian influenza requires laboratory testing because symptoms can resemble other respiratory infections. Testing may involve molecular methods such as polymerase chain reaction on respiratory specimens. A detailed history of contact with birds, animals, contaminated environments, and relevant travel or outbreak exposure is important when evaluating possible infection.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:114:"प्रयोगशाला जांच द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:332:"Reducing contact with sick or dead birds and animals, avoiding contaminated environments, using appropriate protective equipment when exposure cannot be avoided, and practicing good hand hygiene can reduce risk. People working with poultry or infected animals should follow public-health and occupational infection-control guidance.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:662:"बीमार या मृत पक्षियों और पशुओं के निकट संपर्क से बचें तथा संभावित रूप से दूषित सामग्री को उचित सुरक्षा के बिना न संभालें। प्रकोप के दौरान स्थानीय स्वास्थ्य अधिकारियों की सलाह का पालन करें। हाथों की स्वच्छता और सुरक्षित भोजन प्रबंधन भी महत्वपूर्ण हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:429:"Avian influenza requires prompt medical assessment when infection is suspected because some strains can cause severe respiratory disease. Seek urgent evaluation for fever or respiratory symptoms following relevant exposure to infected birds or animals. Emergency care is needed for severe breathing difficulty, chest pain, confusion, bluish skin or lips, rapidly worsening pneumonia, or other signs of severe respiratory illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:320;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:333;s:10:"disease_id";i:385;s:11:"overview_en";s:492:"Measles is a highly contagious viral infection that commonly causes fever, cough, runny nose, red or watery eyes, and a characteristic widespread rash. The illness can cause complications involving the lungs, ears, brain, or other organs, particularly in young children and people with weakened immunity. Measles spreads readily through respiratory particles and can remain infectious in indoor environments after an infected person has left. Vaccination provides highly effective protection.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:180:"खसरा एक अत्यधिक संक्रामक वायरल रोग है जिसमें बुखार और दाने होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:477:"Measles is caused by the measles virus, which spreads primarily through respiratory particles from infected people. The virus enters the respiratory tract and replicates before spreading through the body. It can cause widespread immune and inflammatory effects that produce the characteristic fever and rash. Because the virus is highly contagious, infection can spread rapidly among people who are not immune. Infection usually results in long-lasting immunity after recovery.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:87:"खसरा वायरस इस संक्रमण का कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:475:"The greatest risk is lack of immunity to measles. Unvaccinated or incompletely vaccinated people are vulnerable to infection when exposed. Risk of severe complications is higher among young children, pregnant people, adults with certain health conditions, and people with weakened immune systems. International travel or exposure during outbreaks can increase the likelihood of encountering the virus. High population immunity substantially limits transmission and outbreaks.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:83:"टीकाकरण की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:489:"Measles is suspected when a person has fever and the characteristic respiratory symptoms followed by a widespread rash, particularly when there has been a known exposure or inadequate immunity. Laboratory testing is used to confirm many suspected cases, often with molecular testing or serologic methods. Because measles is highly contagious, suspected cases may require prompt public health notification and appropriate infection-control measures while diagnostic evaluation is completed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:162:"क्लिनिकल मूल्यांकन और प्रयोगशाला जांच से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:503:"Vaccination is the most effective way to prevent measles. Maintaining recommended vaccination according to the local immunization schedule helps protect both individuals and communities. During outbreaks or after significant exposure, public health authorities may recommend additional measures for susceptible people. Good respiratory hygiene and avoiding close contact with infected individuals can reduce transmission, although vaccination provides much stronger protection than these measures alone.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:92:"टीकाकरण सबसे प्रभावी बचाव उपाय है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:415:"Measles requires medical assessment because complications can include pneumonia and inflammation of the brain. Seek prompt medical care for suspected measles, particularly in infants, pregnant people, or those with weakened immune systems. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, dehydration, seizures, confusion, unusual sleepiness, severe headache, or other signs of serious complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:321;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:334;s:10:"disease_id";i:386;s:11:"overview_en";s:376:"Mumps is a contagious viral infection that primarily affects the salivary glands, especially the parotid glands. It commonly causes painful swelling near the cheeks and jaw, fever, headache, muscle aches, fatigue, and reduced appetite. Although many people recover without complications, mumps can occasionally affect the brain, reproductive organs, hearing, or other tissues.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:209:"कण्ठमाला एक वायरल संक्रमण है जो मुख्य रूप से लार ग्रंथियों को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:397:"Mumps is caused by the mumps virus, a member of the paramyxovirus family. The virus spreads mainly through respiratory droplets and secretions from an infected person. Transmission can occur through coughing, sneezing, talking, or close personal contact. A person can spread the virus before and shortly after symptoms become apparent, which allows infection to circulate among susceptible people.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:87:"कण्ठमाला वायरस इस रोग का कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:418:"The main risk factor for mumps is lack of immunity to the virus. People who have not received recommended vaccination or who have not developed immunity after vaccination are more susceptible. Close contact in households, schools, colleges, healthcare settings, and other crowded environments can increase transmission. Outbreaks are more likely where vaccination coverage is low or exposure to infected people occurs.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:140:"बिना टीकाकरण वाले व्यक्तियों में जोखिम अधिक होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:429:"Mumps is often diagnosed from characteristic symptoms, exposure history, vaccination status, and local outbreak information. Laboratory confirmation is recommended in many suspected cases and may involve molecular testing of a buccal or oral specimen. Blood testing can sometimes provide additional evidence. Other infections that cause swelling of the salivary glands may need to be considered when the presentation is atypical.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:156:"क्लिनिकल जांच और प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:458:"The most effective prevention of mumps is vaccination with the recommended measles, mumps, and rubella vaccine. Maintaining vaccination according to public-health recommendations reduces individual and community transmission. During outbreaks, avoiding close contact with infected people and following public-health isolation guidance can reduce spread. Good respiratory hygiene and staying away from others while contagious can also help limit transmission.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:121:"एमएमआर टीकाकरण कण्ठमाला से बचाव में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:386:"Mumps usually requires supportive care and medical assessment when symptoms are significant or complications are suspected. Seek prompt care for severe headache, persistent vomiting, testicular or abdominal pain, or worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is needed for severe neurological symptoms, difficulty breathing, altered consciousness, or other signs of serious complications.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:322;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:335;s:10:"disease_id";i:387;s:11:"overview_en";s:795:"Rubella is a contagious viral infection that commonly causes a mild rash, fever, swollen lymph nodes, and other symptoms. It spreads mainly through respiratory droplets when an infected person coughs or sneezes. Rubella is particularly important during pregnancy because infection can seriously affect a developing baby. Rubella is often mild, and some infected people have few noticeable symptoms. When symptoms occur, they may include a low-grade fever, sore throat, headache, tiredness, and swollen lymph nodes followed by a fine rash that begins on the face and spreads downward. The illness usually resolves without serious complications in otherwise healthy people, but infection during pregnancy can result in congenital rubella syndrome and severe problems affecting the developing baby.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:178:"रूबेला एक संक्रामक वायरल संक्रमण है जो लाल दाने के लिए जाना जाता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:673:"Rubella is caused by the rubella virus. The virus spreads from person to person through respiratory droplets released when an infected individual coughs, sneezes, or talks. A person can spread the infection before and after the rash appears, making transmission possible even when symptoms are not obvious. The rubella virus enters through the respiratory tract and multiplies in the body before spreading through the bloodstream. Infected people can transmit the virus even when symptoms are mild. The virus can cross the placenta during pregnancy and infect the developing fetus, which accounts for the serious congenital complications associated with maternal infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:93:"रूबेला वायरस इस संक्रमण का कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:605:"Risk factors include lack of vaccination, exposure to a person with rubella, and living or traveling in areas where rubella continues to circulate. Pregnant people who are not immune are at particular risk of complications if they become infected. The greatest concern is among people who are not immune and are exposed to circulating rubella virus. Lack of vaccination is the major preventable risk factor. International travel or residence in communities with incomplete vaccination coverage can increase the chance of exposure. Pregnancy substantially increases the potential consequences of infection.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:83:"टीकाकरण की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:669:"Rubella is diagnosed using the medical history, symptoms, physical examination, and laboratory testing. Blood tests can detect rubella-specific antibodies, while molecular tests may detect viral genetic material. Testing is particularly important during pregnancy or when confirmation is needed for public health purposes. Because the symptoms can resemble other viral infections, laboratory confirmation is useful when rubella is suspected. Testing may include detection of rubella-specific IgM antibodies or changes in IgG antibodies over time. Molecular testing can also help confirm infection. Public health authorities may recommend testing in suspected outbreaks.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:150:"क्लिनिकल जांच और रक्त परीक्षण द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:668:"Rubella can largely be prevented through vaccination. Maintaining recommended immunization and avoiding exposure to infected people help reduce transmission. People planning pregnancy should discuss immunity with a healthcare professional because vaccination is generally given before pregnancy rather than during pregnancy. Maintaining high vaccination coverage is the principal public-health method for preventing rubella. People should follow recommended immunization schedules and check immunity before pregnancy when appropriate. Anyone suspected of having rubella should follow public-health and infection-control advice to reduce exposure to susceptible people.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:115:"एमएमआर टीकाकरण रूबेला से बचाव में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:388:"Rubella is usually a mild infection but is particularly important to assess during pregnancy because fetal infection can cause serious complications. Seek prompt medical advice for suspected infection during pregnancy or significant worsening symptoms. Emergency assessment is appropriate for severe breathing difficulty, neurological symptoms, fainting, or another acute medical problem.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:323;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:336;s:10:"disease_id";i:388;s:11:"overview_en";s:366:"Chickenpox is a highly contagious infection caused by the varicella-zoster virus. It commonly causes an itchy rash that develops into fluid-filled blisters and then scabs. Fever, tiredness, headache, and loss of appetite may also occur. Most cases are mild, but complications can be more serious in adults, infants, pregnant people, and those with weakened immunity.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:209:"चेचक एक अत्यधिक संक्रामक वायरल रोग है जिसमें खुजली वाले फफोले और दाने होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:347:"Chickenpox is caused by infection with the varicella-zoster virus. The virus spreads very easily from an infected person, mainly through respiratory droplets and airborne particles or through contact with fluid from chickenpox blisters. A person can spread the infection before the rash is fully recognized and until the lesions have crusted over.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:102:"वैरीसेला-जोस्टर वायरस चेचक का कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:342:"The risk of chickenpox is highest in people who have not had the infection or vaccination and who are exposed to an infected person. Adults, infants, pregnant people, and individuals with weakened immune systems are at greater risk of serious complications if infection occurs. Crowded settings and close contact can make transmission easier.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:125:"बिना टीकाकरण वाले लोगों में जोखिम अधिक होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:396:"Chickenpox is often diagnosed from its characteristic itchy rash and the pattern in which the lesions develop. A healthcare professional may consider the symptoms, exposure history, and physical examination. Laboratory testing is not usually necessary for typical cases, but tests such as molecular or antibody testing can help confirm the diagnosis when the presentation is unusual or uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:136:"क्लिनिकल जांच द्वारा सामान्यतः निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:393:"Vaccination is the main way to prevent chickenpox and can also reduce the severity of illness when infection occurs. Avoiding close contact with people who have active chickenpox can reduce transmission. People with chickenpox should stay away from others who are susceptible, particularly pregnant people, newborns, and those with weakened immune systems, until they are no longer contagious.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:92:"टीकाकरण सबसे प्रभावी बचाव उपाय है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:375:"Chickenpox is usually self-limited but can cause serious complications in adults, pregnant people, infants, and people with weakened immune systems. Seek prompt medical assessment when symptoms are severe or complications are suspected. Emergency care is needed for difficulty breathing, severe dehydration, confusion, severe headache, seizures, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:324;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:337;s:10:"disease_id";i:389;s:11:"overview_en";s:501:"Shingles is a painful skin condition caused by reactivation of the varicella-zoster virus, the same virus that causes chickenpox. After chickenpox, the virus remains inactive in nerve tissue and can reactivate years later. Shingles usually produces pain, burning, tingling, or increased sensitivity followed by a localized blistering rash. The rash commonly occurs on one side of the body or face. Symptoms usually resolve over several weeks, although nerve pain can persist after the skin has healed.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:220:"दाद एक दर्दनाक त्वचा रोग है जो वैरीसेला-जोस्टर वायरस के पुनः सक्रिय होने से होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:476:"Shingles occurs when dormant varicella-zoster virus becomes active again within a sensory nerve. The exact reason for reactivation is not always known. The immune system normally keeps the virus under control, and reduced immune function can make reactivation more likely. After reactivation, the virus travels along a nerve toward the skin and produces the characteristic localized pain and rash. Previous chickenpox infection is required for the virus to remain in the body.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:1043:"शिंगल्स वैरिसेला-जोस्टर वायरस के दोबारा सक्रिय होने के कारण होता है, यही वायरस चिकनपॉक्स का कारण बनता है। चिकनपॉक्स के शुरुआती संक्रमण के बाद वायरस तंत्रिका ऊतक में निष्क्रिय रह सकता है और वर्षों बाद फिर सक्रिय हो सकता है। इसके दोबारा सक्रिय होने का सटीक कारण हमेशा ज्ञात नहीं होता। बढ़ती उम्र और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा तंत्र शिंगल्स के दोबारा सक्रिय होने तथा जोखिम बढ़ने से जुड़े महत्वपूर्ण कारक हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:502:"The main risk factor is previous infection with varicella-zoster virus. Risk increases substantially with advancing age because immune control of the virus may weaken over time. People with weakened immune systems because of certain illnesses or treatments also have greater risk. Severe physical or psychological stress may be associated with reactivation in some individuals. Shingles can occur in people without an obvious risk factor, so absence of these factors does not eliminate the possibility.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:922:"जिस व्यक्ति को पहले चिकनपॉक्स हो चुका है, उसमें बाद में शिंगल्स हो सकता है क्योंकि वैरिसेला-जोस्टर वायरस शरीर में बना रह सकता है और फिर सक्रिय हो सकता है। उम्र बढ़ने के साथ तथा प्रतिरक्षा तंत्र को कमजोर करने वाली स्थितियों या दवाओं के कारण जोखिम बढ़ता है। इनमें कुछ कैंसर, HIV संक्रमण, अंग प्रत्यारोपण और स्टेरॉयड जैसी प्रतिरक्षा-दमनकारी दवाएं शामिल हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:505:"Shingles is usually diagnosed from the characteristic pattern of localized pain followed by a one-sided blistering rash. A physical examination is generally sufficient when the presentation is typical. Laboratory testing may be considered when the diagnosis is uncertain, the rash is atypical, or the affected person has unusual symptoms. A sample from a blister can be tested for varicella-zoster virus. Eye, ear, neurological, or widespread involvement requires particularly careful clinical assessment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:123:"क्लिनिकल मूल्यांकन द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:522:"Vaccination against varicella-zoster virus can reduce the risk of chickenpox and later shingles, while shingles vaccination can reduce the risk of shingles and its complications in eligible people. Recommendations vary according to age and health status. Maintaining general health and appropriate management of conditions that weaken immunity may also be beneficial. People with an active rash should avoid direct contact with individuals who are particularly vulnerable to varicella infection until lesions have crusted.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:534:"दाद और इसकी जटिलताओं से बचाव का मुख्य उपाय टीकाकरण है। पुरानी बीमारियों की उचित देखभाल और चिकित्सक से अनुशंसित टीकाकरण के बारे में सलाह लेना रोग तथा पोस्टहर्पेटिक न्यूराल्जिया के जोखिम को कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:360:"Shingles should be medically assessed, particularly when the rash is extensive, severe, recurrent, or involves the face or eye. Seek prompt care for a rash near the eye, ear, or face, severe pain, or signs of infection. Emergency assessment is appropriate for vision loss, severe neurological symptoms, facial weakness, confusion, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:325;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:338;s:10:"disease_id";i:390;s:11:"overview_en";s:393:"Tuberculous pleurisy is inflammation of the pleural lining around the lungs caused by infection with Mycobacterium tuberculosis. It may occur when tuberculosis affects the tissues around the lungs and can cause chest pain, fever, cough, or difficulty breathing. Diagnosis generally requires clinical assessment together with imaging and laboratory evaluation of pleural fluid or other samples.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:174:"ट्यूबरकुलस प्लूरिसी फेफड़ों की झिल्ली में तपेदिक संबंधी सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:352:"Tuberculous pleurisy is caused by infection with Mycobacterium tuberculosis. The infection can involve the pleural tissues around the lungs and produce inflammation and accumulation of fluid in the pleural space. It may occur as part of tuberculosis affecting other parts of the body or as a manifestation of tuberculosis infection involving the chest.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"माइकोबैक्टीरियम ट्यूबरकुलोसिस संक्रमण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:392:"Risk of tuberculous pleurisy is increased by exposure to tuberculosis and conditions that weaken the immune system. Close contact with a person who has infectious tuberculosis, living or working in settings where tuberculosis transmission is more likely, and certain chronic illnesses can increase exposure or susceptibility. Previous or untreated tuberculosis infection can also be relevant.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:139:"तपेदिक संपर्क और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:431:"Diagnosis of tuberculous pleurisy may involve medical history, physical examination, chest imaging, and laboratory testing. Chest X-ray or other imaging can identify pleural fluid or inflammation. Analysis of pleural fluid may provide evidence of tuberculosis, and additional microbiological or molecular tests can be performed when appropriate. Testing for tuberculosis elsewhere in the body may also help establish the diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:204:"प्लूरल फ्लूइड जांच, इमेजिंग और प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:423:"Tuberculous pleurisy can be reduced by preventing tuberculosis infection and limiting its spread. Measures include appropriate evaluation and treatment of people with active tuberculosis, good ventilation, and following public health guidance after exposure. People at increased risk may benefit from screening and preventive treatment for latent tuberculosis infection. Vaccination policies vary by country and population.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:1215:"ट्यूबरकुलस प्ल्यूरिसी Mycobacterium tuberculosis संक्रमण से जुड़ी होती है, इसलिए तपेदिक संक्रमण और सक्रिय TB को रोकने से इसका जोखिम कम किया जा सकता है। TB के संपर्क में आए लोगों को चिकित्सकीय सलाह के अनुसार जाँच और follow-up की आवश्यकता हो सकती है। latent TB infection का उपचार सक्रिय बीमारी को रोकने में मदद कर सकता है, जबकि सक्रिय TB का समय पर उपचार दूसरों तक संक्रमण फैलने को कम करता है। जिन देशों में इसकी सिफारिश की जाती है वहाँ BCG टीका कुछ सुरक्षा दे सकता है, हालांकि इसकी प्रभावशीलता अलग-अलग हो सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:377:"Tuberculous pleurisy requires medical evaluation and appropriate tuberculosis treatment. Seek prompt care for persistent fever, chest pain, worsening cough, night sweats, weight loss, or increasing shortness of breath. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, coughing up significant blood, confusion, fainting, or rapidly worsening respiratory symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:326;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:339;s:10:"disease_id";i:391;s:11:"overview_en";s:556:"Acute sinobronchitis refers to an acute inflammatory illness involving the nasal and sinus passages together with the bronchial airways. It commonly develops after a respiratory infection and may cause nasal congestion, facial pressure, cough, mucus production, sore throat, fatigue, and other upper or lower respiratory symptoms. Most cases are associated with viral respiratory infections and improve with supportive care. Symptoms can overlap with other respiratory illnesses, so persistent, severe, or worsening symptoms may require medical evaluation.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:170:"एक्यूट साइनोब्रोंकाइटिस साइनस और ब्रोंकियल नलिकाओं की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:529:"Acute sinobronchitis is most commonly associated with respiratory viruses that initially infect the upper airways and may produce inflammation extending into the bronchial passages. Viral infections such as those responsible for the common cold and influenza-like illnesses can cause the condition. Irritation from smoke, air pollutants, or other respiratory exposures may worsen inflammation and coughing. Bacterial infection can occur in some respiratory illnesses, but symptoms alone do not always establish a bacterial cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:136:"वायरल या बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:539:"Risk of acute sinobronchitis may increase with exposure to people with respiratory infections, crowded indoor environments, frequent contact with young children, smoking or secondhand smoke, and other sources of airway irritation. Existing respiratory conditions may make symptoms more troublesome. Seasonal circulation of respiratory viruses also affects exposure risk. Most people with respiratory infections recover without complications, although age and underlying health conditions can influence the severity and duration of illness.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:117:"धूम्रपान और श्वसन संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:580:"Diagnosis is generally based on the pattern of respiratory symptoms and examination findings. A clinician may assess the nose, throat, breathing, cough, and other signs of respiratory infection. Laboratory testing is not routinely necessary in uncomplicated cases, although testing for specific respiratory viruses may be considered when the result would affect management or infection-control decisions. Persistent fever, severe symptoms, significant breathing difficulty, or an atypical course may require additional evaluation to exclude pneumonia or another serious condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:125:"क्लिनिकल जांच और इमेजिंग से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:545:"Prevention focuses largely on reducing transmission of respiratory infections and limiting airway irritants. Regular hand hygiene, avoiding close contact with people who are acutely ill, improving ventilation in crowded indoor settings, and covering coughs and sneezes can reduce exposure. Avoiding tobacco smoke and other respiratory irritants may reduce airway irritation. Vaccination against preventable respiratory infections, when recommended, can also reduce the likelihood of certain infections that may cause similar respiratory illness.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:150:"स्वच्छता और श्वसन उत्तेजकों से बचाव रोकथाम में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:384:"Acute sinobronchitis generally requires routine or prompt medical assessment when symptoms are severe, persistent, or worsening. Seek care for prolonged fever, significant facial or chest pain, dehydration, or worsening respiratory symptoms. Emergency assessment is appropriate for severe breathing difficulty, confusion, bluish lips or skin, chest pain, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:327;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:340;s:10:"disease_id";i:392;s:11:"overview_en";s:525:"Laryngotracheitis is inflammation involving the larynx and trachea, commonly occurring as part of a viral respiratory infection. It may cause hoarseness, a barking or harsh cough, noisy breathing, sore throat, fever, and other upper respiratory symptoms. The condition is particularly recognized in young children, in whom swelling of the upper airway can cause breathing difficulty. Most cases are mild and improve as the underlying infection resolves, but significant breathing difficulty requires prompt medical attention.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:141:"लैरिंगोट्रेकाइटिस स्वरयंत्र और श्वासनली की सूजन है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:466:"Laryngotracheitis is usually caused by a viral respiratory infection. Viruses can infect the upper airway and produce swelling around the larynx and trachea. Parainfluenza viruses are common causes, while other respiratory viruses can produce a similar illness. The characteristic cough and breathing symptoms result partly from inflammation and narrowing of the upper airway. Secondary bacterial infection is uncommon but can produce a more severe clinical illness.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:108:"वायरल संक्रमण इसका सबसे सामान्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:497:"Laryngotracheitis is particularly common in young children because their upper airways are narrower, so relatively modest swelling can produce noticeable breathing symptoms. Exposure to respiratory viruses, attendance at childcare or school, and close contact with infected individuals increase exposure. Seasonal viral circulation also affects risk. Children with certain underlying airway or respiratory problems may experience more significant symptoms when an infection causes airway swelling.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:93:"छोटे बच्चों में जोखिम अधिक होता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:563:"Diagnosis is usually based on the characteristic barking cough, hoarseness, and symptoms of upper-airway inflammation. A clinician evaluates breathing effort, respiratory rate, oxygenation when appropriate, and the presence of noisy breathing at rest or during activity. Routine laboratory tests and imaging are often unnecessary in uncomplicated cases. Severe, unusual, or rapidly worsening symptoms may require further assessment to distinguish laryngotracheitis from bacterial airway infection, foreign-body aspiration, or other causes of respiratory distress.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:136:"क्लिनिकल जांच द्वारा सामान्यतः निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:517:"Because laryngotracheitis is usually caused by respiratory viruses, prevention involves reducing exposure and transmission. Hand hygiene, avoiding close contact during acute illness, improving indoor ventilation, and covering coughs and sneezes can help. Children with respiratory infections should be kept home from school or childcare when appropriate according to local guidance. Vaccination against preventable respiratory infections can reduce the risk of some illnesses that may produce similar airway symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:153:"हाथों की स्वच्छता और संक्रमण नियंत्रण बचाव में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:405:"Laryngotracheitis can cause significant airway narrowing, particularly in children. Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening cough, noisy breathing, fever, or difficulty breathing. Emergency care is needed for stridor at rest, severe breathing difficulty, bluish lips or skin, inability to speak or cry normally because of breathing difficulty, marked exhaustion, or rapidly worsening airway symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:328;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:341;s:10:"disease_id";i:393;s:11:"overview_en";s:502:"Viral pneumonia is an infection and inflammation of the lungs caused by a virus. It can produce cough, fever, fatigue, shortness of breath, chest discomfort, and reduced oxygen levels in more serious cases. Different respiratory viruses can cause pneumonia, and symptoms may overlap with bacterial pneumonia or other respiratory conditions. Most mild cases improve with supportive care, while older adults, young children, and people with certain underlying conditions may develop more serious illness.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:162:"वायरल निमोनिया वायरस द्वारा होने वाला फेफड़ों का संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:489:"Viral pneumonia can be caused by several respiratory viruses, including influenza viruses, respiratory syncytial virus, adenoviruses, coronaviruses, and others. The virus infects respiratory tissues and triggers inflammation that interferes with normal gas exchange. Some viruses can cause pneumonia directly, while others may predispose the lungs to additional infection. The specific virus involved varies according to age, season, location, circulating strains, and individual exposure.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:118:"श्वसन वायरस इस संक्रमण के लिए जिम्मेदार हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:461:"Risk of viral pneumonia is influenced by age, immune status, underlying heart or lung disease, and exposure to respiratory viruses. Young children, older adults, pregnant people, and individuals with weakened immunity may have increased risk of severe disease from some viruses. Smoking and other factors that impair respiratory defenses can also increase vulnerability. Risk varies considerably according to the specific virus and the health of the individual.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:148:"कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा और पुरानी बीमारियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:519:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, and assessment of breathing and oxygenation. Depending on severity and clinical circumstances, chest imaging may be used to identify lung inflammation or pneumonia. Tests such as molecular assays or other respiratory testing may identify a causative virus when confirmation is clinically useful. Blood tests and additional investigations may be performed in more serious cases or when bacterial pneumonia, complications, or another diagnosis needs to be considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:151:"छाती की इमेजिंग और प्रयोगशाला जांच से निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:523:"Prevention depends on the virus involved and includes measures that reduce respiratory infection transmission. Vaccination against preventable respiratory viruses, when recommended, can reduce the risk of severe infection. Hand hygiene, good indoor ventilation, covering coughs and sneezes, and avoiding close contact with people who are acutely ill can reduce exposure. People with respiratory symptoms should follow appropriate infection-control guidance, particularly around individuals at higher risk of severe illness.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:128:"टीकाकरण और स्वच्छता जोखिम कम करने में सहायक हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:409:"Viral pneumonia requires medical assessment when symptoms are significant or worsening because respiratory function can deteriorate. Seek prompt care for persistent fever, worsening cough, dehydration, chest pain, or increasing shortness of breath. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, bluish lips or skin, confusion, fainting, severe chest pain, or rapidly worsening oxygen levels.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:329;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:342;s:10:"disease_id";i:394;s:11:"overview_en";s:383:"Bacterial pneumonia is an infection of the lungs caused by bacteria. It can cause inflammation and fluid or pus in the air sacs, making breathing more difficult. Common symptoms include cough, fever, chills, chest discomfort, shortness of breath, fatigue, and sometimes mucus production. Severity varies from mild illness to a potentially serious infection requiring hospitalization.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:568:"बैक्टीरियल निमोनिया फेफड़ों का जीवाणु संक्रमण है जिसमें बैक्टीरिया वायुकोषों और आसपास के ऊतकों में सूजन पैदा करते हैं। यह हल्के संक्रमण से लेकर गंभीर श्वसन रोग तक हो सकता है, विशेषकर कमजोर स्वास्थ्य वाले लोगों में।";s:9:"causes_en";s:404:"Bacterial pneumonia can be caused by several types of bacteria, including Streptococcus pneumoniae and other respiratory pathogens. Bacteria may reach the lungs after inhalation of infected respiratory particles or aspiration of material from the mouth or stomach. Pneumonia can also develop after another respiratory infection or when the immune system is unable to control bacterial growth effectively.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:629:"बैक्टीरियल निमोनिया कई प्रकार के जीवाणुओं से हो सकता है, जिनमें स्ट्रेप्टोकोकस निमोनिए शामिल है। जीवाणु श्वसन बूंदों या स्राव के माध्यम से फेफड़ों तक पहुंच सकते हैं या मुंह अथवा पेट की सामग्री के श्वसन मार्ग में जाने से संक्रमण हो सकता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:400:"Risk is higher in older adults, young children, and people with weakened immune systems or chronic heart, lung, kidney, or metabolic conditions. Smoking, recent respiratory infection, hospitalization, aspiration risk, and close exposure to infected individuals may also increase risk. People living in healthcare or long-term-care settings can have additional exposure to certain bacterial pathogens.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:635:"बुजुर्गों और छोटे बच्चों तथा पुरानी फेफड़ों या हृदय की बीमारी, मधुमेह, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, धूम्रपान, निगलने में कठिनाई या हाल के श्वसन संक्रमण वाले लोगों में जोखिम अधिक हो सकता है। अस्पताल में भर्ती रहने से कुछ जीवाणुओं का संपर्क भी बढ़ सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:402:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, and assessment of breathing and vital signs. Chest imaging, usually a chest X-ray, can help identify lung infection. Blood tests and sputum testing may be used in selected cases to identify bacterial infection or assess severity. Additional testing may be needed for people who are severely ill, hospitalized, or at increased risk of complications.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:588:"निदान लक्षणों, शारीरिक जांच और श्वसन की स्थिति के आकलन पर आधारित होता है। छाती का एक्स-रे फेफड़ों के संक्रमण की पहचान में मदद कर सकता है, जबकि आवश्यकता के अनुसार रक्त, बलगम या अन्य जांचों से कारण और गंभीरता का आकलन किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:421:"Good hand hygiene, avoiding tobacco smoke, maintaining recommended vaccinations, managing chronic medical conditions, and reducing exposure to respiratory infections can lower pneumonia risk. Staying up to date with recommended pneumococcal and influenza vaccination is particularly important for eligible people. People who are ill should follow appropriate respiratory hygiene and seek care when symptoms become severe.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:654:"अनुशंसित टीकाकरण, हाथों की स्वच्छता, श्वसन शिष्टाचार, धूम्रपान से बचना और पुरानी बीमारियों का अच्छा नियंत्रण बैक्टीरियल निमोनिया का जोखिम कम कर सकते हैं। अधिक जोखिम वाले लोगों को उचित टीकों और बचाव के उपायों के बारे में चिकित्सक से सलाह लेनी चाहिए।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:387:"Bacterial pneumonia requires prompt medical assessment and may require antibiotic treatment. Seek care for persistent fever, worsening cough, chest pain, dehydration, or increasing shortness of breath. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, bluish lips or skin, confusion, fainting, severe chest pain, coughing up significant blood, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:330;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:343;s:10:"disease_id";i:395;s:11:"overview_en";s:340:"Fungal pneumonia is a lung infection caused by fungi. Different fungi can cause different forms of pneumonia, including infections acquired from environmental exposure and infections that occur more readily in people with weakened immune systems. Symptoms may include fever, cough, fatigue, shortness of breath, chills, or chest discomfort.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:160:"फंगल निमोनिया फफूंद के कारण होने वाला फेफड़ों का संक्रमण है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:359:"Fungal pneumonia can result from inhaling fungal spores from the environment. Examples include Histoplasma, Aspergillus, and other disease-causing fungi. Some fungi are associated with particular geographic regions or environmental exposures, while others mainly cause serious lung infections in people with weakened immune systems or underlying lung disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:126:"विभिन्न फंगल संक्रमण इस रोग का कारण बन सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:395:"Risk varies according to the fungus involved. Important factors can include a weakened immune system, cancer treatment, organ or stem-cell transplantation, long-term corticosteroid or other immunosuppressive treatment, chronic lung disease, and exposure to environments containing disease-causing fungal spores. Geographic location and occupational or recreational exposure may also affect risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:111:"कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम को काफी बढ़ाती है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:357:"Diagnosis depends on the suspected fungus and clinical circumstances. Evaluation may include a medical history, physical examination, chest imaging, and laboratory testing of blood, urine, sputum, respiratory samples, or tissue. Because fungal pneumonia can resemble bacterial or viral pneumonia, identifying the specific cause may require targeted testing.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:134:"इमेजिंग और फंगल परीक्षण द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:350:"Prevention depends on the fungus and the person's risk. Avoiding heavy exposure to environments containing fungal spores, particularly soil or material contaminated with bird or bat droppings, may reduce the risk of some infections. People with weakened immune systems should follow healthcare guidance about reducing exposure to environmental fungi.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:153:"संक्रमण स्रोतों से बचाव और प्रतिरक्षा बनाए रखना सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:424:"Fungal pneumonia requires medical assessment because it can be serious, particularly in people with weakened immune systems or underlying lung disease. Seek prompt care for persistent fever, worsening cough, chest pain, or increasing shortness of breath. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, confusion, bluish lips or skin, coughing up significant blood, or rapidly worsening respiratory symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:331;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:344;s:10:"disease_id";i:396;s:11:"overview_en";s:492:"Legionnaires disease is a serious form of pneumonia caused by Legionella bacteria. Infection usually occurs when a person breathes contaminated water droplets or mist from systems in which the bacteria have multiplied. Symptoms can include fever, cough, shortness of breath, muscle aches, headache, and fatigue, and some people may also develop gastrointestinal symptoms. The illness can become severe, particularly in older adults and people with chronic diseases or weakened immune systems.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:180:"लीजियोनेयर्स रोग लेजियोनेला जीवाणु से होने वाला गंभीर निमोनिया है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:534:"Legionnaires disease is caused mainly by Legionella pneumophila and related Legionella bacteria. These organisms can multiply in water systems when temperature, stagnant water, inadequate disinfection, and other environmental conditions allow bacterial growth. Infection generally occurs after inhaling contaminated water droplets or mist from showers, cooling systems, hot tubs, fountains, or other water-containing equipment. Person-to-person transmission is uncommon, and most infections are associated with environmental exposure.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:188:"दूषित जल प्रणालियों में पाए जाने वाले लेजियोनेला जीवाणु इसका कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:443:"Risk is higher in people over 50 years of age, current or former smokers, and people with chronic lung disease, diabetes, kidney disease, cancer, or weakened immunity. Recent hospitalization and residence in long-term care facilities can increase exposure opportunities. The risk of disease is also influenced by exposure to contaminated water systems, cooling equipment, hot tubs, or other environments where Legionella bacteria can multiply.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:990:"Legionella के संपर्क में आने वाले अधिकांश स्वस्थ लोगों में बीमारी नहीं होती। 50 वर्ष से अधिक आयु, वर्तमान या पूर्व धूम्रपान, COPD जैसी पुरानी फेफड़ों की बीमारी, मधुमेह, किडनी रोग या अन्य दीर्घकालिक बीमारियों वाले लोगों में Legionnaires disease का जोखिम अधिक होता है। कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, हाल में अस्पताल में भर्ती होना या सर्जरी, long-term care facility में रहना और प्रतिरक्षा दबाने वाली दवाएँ लेना भी जोखिम बढ़ा सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:499:"Diagnosis generally involves evaluation of pneumonia together with testing specifically directed at Legionella when the clinical situation warrants it. Chest imaging can demonstrate pneumonia, while laboratory testing may include a urinary antigen test and testing of respiratory specimens by culture or molecular methods. The choice of testing depends on illness severity, exposure history, local public health considerations, and whether an outbreak or healthcare-associated exposure is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:169:"मूत्र एंटीजन परीक्षण और श्वसन नमूनों द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:562:"Prevention focuses on controlling Legionella growth in water systems. Building owners and facility managers should maintain and disinfect plumbing systems, cooling equipment, hot tubs, and other water systems according to appropriate safety procedures. Avoiding conditions that allow stagnant water and bacterial growth can reduce contamination. During recognized outbreaks or exposures, people at increased risk should follow public health recommendations. Healthcare facilities and long-term care settings should maintain appropriate water-management programs.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:125:"जल प्रणालियों का उचित रखरखाव बचाव में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:431:"Legionnaires disease requires prompt medical assessment and appropriate treatment because it can cause severe pneumonia and systemic illness. Seek urgent care for high fever, worsening cough, shortness of breath, confusion, gastrointestinal symptoms, or significant weakness. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, confusion, fainting, bluish lips or skin, severe dehydration, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:332;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:345;s:10:"disease_id";i:397;s:11:"overview_en";s:333:"Pulmonary edema occurs when excess fluid builds up in the lungs, making it difficult for oxygen to move into the blood. It can develop suddenly and cause severe shortness of breath, rapid breathing, coughing, and a feeling of suffocation. Acute pulmonary edema can be a medical emergency and requires prompt assessment and treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:266:"फुफ्फुसीय शोफ एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें फेफड़ों में द्रव जमा हो जाता है और सांस लेने में कठिनाई होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:368:"The most common cause of pulmonary edema is increased pressure in the blood vessels of the lungs due to heart problems, particularly left-sided heart failure. Other causes include heart attack, severe high blood pressure, abnormal heart valves, kidney failure, pneumonia, severe infections, inhalation of toxins or smoke, certain medicines, and high-altitude exposure.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"हृदय रोग, गुर्दा रोग और फेफड़ों की चोट इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:338:"Risk factors include heart failure or other heart disease, uncontrolled high blood pressure, kidney disease, previous heart attack, abnormal heart valves, severe infections, exposure to certain toxins, and conditions that cause rapid fluid accumulation. The risk also depends on the underlying condition responsible for the fluid buildup.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:157:"हृदय विफलता, गुर्दा विकार और उच्च रक्तचाप जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:350:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, physical examination, oxygen measurements, and medical history. A chest X-ray or other imaging may show fluid in the lungs. Blood tests, electrocardiography, echocardiography, and additional investigations may be used to determine whether heart disease, infection, kidney problems, or another condition is responsible.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:196:"छाती की इमेजिंग, रक्त जांच और ऑक्सीजन मूल्यांकन द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:372:"Preventing pulmonary edema focuses on controlling its underlying causes. People with heart failure or high blood pressure should follow prescribed treatment and monitor their condition. Managing kidney disease, limiting excess dietary sodium when advised, avoiding smoking, and seeking prompt care for worsening breathlessness can help reduce the risk of serious episodes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:171:"हृदय और गुर्दा रोगों का उचित नियंत्रण जोखिम कम करने में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:406:"Pulmonary edema is a medical emergency because fluid in the lungs can rapidly impair oxygen exchange. Seek emergency medical attention for severe shortness of breath, inability to speak in full sentences, coughing up blood or frothy sputum, blue or gray lips or skin, severe chest pain, confusion, fainting, or rapidly worsening breathing. Do not delay emergency assessment while attempting home treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:333;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:346;s:10:"disease_id";i:398;s:11:"overview_en";s:296:"Pulmonary hypertension means abnormally high pressure in the lung circulation, which can strain the right side of the heart. Pulmonary arterial hypertension is one particular form. Symptoms can include breathlessness, fatigue, chest discomfort, dizziness, or fainting, especially during activity.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:612:"पल्मोनरी हाइपरटेंशन ऐसी स्थितियों का समूह है जिसमें फेफड़ों की रक्त वाहिकाओं में दबाव असामान्य रूप से बढ़ जाता है। इससे हृदय के दाहिने हिस्से पर दबाव पड़ सकता है और सांस फूलना, थकान, सीने में असुविधा या व्यायाम सहनशीलता कम हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:392:"Pulmonary hypertension is classified into five groups: pulmonary arterial hypertension; disease related to the left side of the heart; lung disease or low oxygen; obstruction of pulmonary arteries, including chronic clot-related disease; and conditions with unclear or multiple mechanisms. These groups have different causes and should not all be described as pulmonary arterial hypertension.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:600:"पल्मोनरी हाइपरटेंशन के कई कारण हो सकते हैं, जैसे हृदय या फेफड़ों के रोग, फेफड़ों की धमनियों में पुराने रक्त के थक्के, संयोजी ऊतक के रोग, कुछ आनुवंशिक स्थितियां तथा कुछ दवाएं या विषैले पदार्थ। कुछ मामलों में स्पष्ट कारण नहीं मिलता।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:314:"Risk depends on the form of pulmonary hypertension. Associated factors can include heart or chronic lung disease, low oxygen levels, previous pulmonary blood clots, connective tissue disease such as scleroderma, and certain inherited conditions or exposures. A factor relevant to one form may not apply to another.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:637:"जोखिम पल्मोनरी हाइपरटेंशन के प्रकार पर निर्भर करता है। पुरानी फेफड़ों या हृदय की बीमारी, संयोजी ऊतक के रोग, पुराने रक्त के थक्के, कुछ आनुवंशिक स्थितियां, नींद से संबंधित श्वसन विकार और कुछ दवाओं या विषैले पदार्थों का संपर्क जोखिम बढ़ा सकता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:341:"Evaluation includes medical history, examination, and tests of heart and lung function. Echocardiography assesses heart function and the likelihood of pulmonary hypertension. Right-heart catheterization directly measures pressures when indicated. Further investigations identify the underlying cause and help distinguish the different forms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:623:"जांच में चिकित्सीय इतिहास, शारीरिक परीक्षण, रक्त जांच, छाती की इमेजिंग, ईसीजी और इकोकार्डियोग्राफी शामिल हो सकती है। आवश्यकता होने पर राइट-हार्ट कैथेटराइजेशन द्वारा फेफड़ों की धमनी का दबाव सीधे मापा जाता है और निदान की पुष्टि की जाती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:310:"Pulmonary hypertension cannot always be prevented. Possible risk-reduction measures depend on the underlying cause and individual circumstances. People with relevant heart, lung, inherited, or other associated conditions can discuss appropriate assessment and risk reduction with their healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:703:"पल्मोनरी हाइपरटेंशन के सभी प्रकारों को रोका नहीं जा सकता। धूम्रपान से बचना, हृदय और फेफड़ों के रोगों का नियंत्रण, उचित परिस्थितियों में रक्त के थक्कों की रोकथाम और उपचार तथा लगातार सांस की समस्या होने पर जांच कराना जटिलताओं को कम करने और जल्दी पहचान में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:443:"Pulmonary hypertension requires medical evaluation and ongoing specialist management because it can place increasing strain on the right side of the heart. Seek prompt care when shortness of breath is new or worsening, chest pain develops, dizziness or fainting occurs, or palpitations become persistent. Emergency assessment is needed for severe chest pain, severe breathing difficulty, fainting, bluish skin, or sudden neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:334;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:347;s:10:"disease_id";i:399;s:11:"overview_en";s:387:"Empyema is a collection of infected pus in the pleural space, the thin area between the lungs and the inner chest wall. It usually develops as a complication of pneumonia or another infection in the chest. Empyema can cause fever, chest pain, cough, shortness of breath, and fatigue. Because infected fluid can interfere with normal lung expansion, prompt medical treatment is important.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:190:"एम्पायमा फेफड़ों के आसपास की प्लूरल गुहा में मवाद जमा होने की स्थिति है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:365:"Empyema most commonly develops when a bacterial infection spreads from the lung or another nearby structure into the pleural space. Pneumonia is a frequent cause, but empyema can also follow a lung abscess, chest surgery, chest injury, or infection involving the bloodstream. Different bacteria may be responsible, and the specific organism can influence treatment.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:159:"जीवाणु संक्रमण और फेफड़ों के संक्रमण इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:395:"Risk increases with pneumonia, lung infections, weakened immunity, chronic lung disease, and conditions that make it difficult to clear respiratory infections. Recent chest surgery, chest injury, aspiration, or other infections within the chest can also increase risk. Older adults and people with significant underlying illnesses may be more vulnerable to complications from pleural infections.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:169:"निमोनिया, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा और छाती के संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:422:"Diagnosis involves the medical history, physical examination, and imaging of the chest. A chest X-ray may show pleural fluid, while ultrasound or CT scanning can provide more detailed information about the amount and location of fluid. A sample of pleural fluid may be removed with a needle and examined for bacteria, cells, and chemical characteristics. Culture testing can help identify the organism and guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:1045:"एम्पाइमा का निदान चिकित्सकीय इतिहास, शारीरिक परीक्षण और फेफड़ों के आसपास संक्रमित द्रव की पहचान करने वाली जाँचों से किया जाता है। छाती का X-ray, अल्ट्रासाउंड या CT स्कैन pleural space में मौजूद द्रव को दिखा सकता है और उसकी मात्रा तथा स्थिति समझने में मदद कर सकता है। संक्रमण की पुष्टि और उपचार की दिशा तय करने के लिए सुई द्वारा pleural fluid का नमूना लेकर उसमें बैक्टीरिया, कोशिकाओं और अन्य विशेषताओं की जाँच की जा सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:446:"Empyema cannot always be prevented, but treating pneumonia and other respiratory infections promptly may reduce the risk of complications. Following prescribed treatment and seeking medical attention when respiratory symptoms become severe or fail to improve are important. Preventive measures such as appropriate vaccination, avoiding smoking, and managing chronic lung conditions can also help reduce the risk of serious respiratory infections.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:132:"श्वसन संक्रमणों का समय पर उपचार बचाव में सहायक है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:406:"Empyema requires prompt medical assessment and treatment because infected fluid around the lung can cause serious infection and breathing problems. Seek urgent care for fever, chest pain, worsening cough, shortness of breath, or increasing weakness. Emergency assessment is needed for severe breathing difficulty, confusion, fainting, bluish lips or skin, severe chest pain, or rapidly worsening infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:335;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:348;s:10:"disease_id";i:400;s:11:"overview_en";s:563:"Respiratory failure occurs when the lungs cannot provide enough oxygen to the blood or cannot adequately remove carbon dioxide from the body. It may develop suddenly or gradually and can result from conditions affecting the lungs, airways, breathing muscles, or nervous system. Symptoms may include severe shortness of breath, rapid breathing, confusion, bluish or gray skin coloration, extreme sleepiness, and difficulty speaking because of breathlessness. Acute respiratory failure is a medical emergency and may require immediate oxygen or ventilatory support.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:300:"श्वसन विफलता एक गंभीर स्थिति है जिसमें फेफड़े पर्याप्त ऑक्सीजन और कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड का आदान-प्रदान नहीं कर पाते।";s:9:"causes_en";s:600:"Respiratory failure can result from many conditions that interfere with oxygen exchange or carbon dioxide removal. Severe pneumonia, asthma or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, pulmonary edema, acute respiratory distress syndrome, airway obstruction, and blood clots in the lungs can impair lung function. Weakness of the breathing muscles, overdose of sedating medicines, stroke, spinal cord injury, and other neurological conditions can also prevent adequate ventilation. Acute illness may cause sudden respiratory failure, while chronic lung or neuromuscular disease can cause a gradual form.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:192:"गंभीर फेफड़ों के रोग, संक्रमण और पुरानी बीमारियां इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:517:"Risk factors for respiratory failure include severe lung disease, pneumonia, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, severe asthma, heart failure, neuromuscular disorders, chest injuries, obesity, sleep-related breathing disorders, and conditions affecting the brain or spinal cord. Older age and serious systemic illness may increase vulnerability. Sedating medicines or drug overdose can suppress breathing. People with chronic respiratory disease may be at increased risk during infections or other acute illnesses.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:185:"पुरानी फेफड़ों की बीमारी, गंभीर संक्रमण और धूम्रपान जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:496:"Respiratory failure is diagnosed by assessing breathing, oxygen levels, and carbon dioxide levels. Pulse oximetry provides a quick estimate of blood oxygen saturation, while an arterial blood gas can directly measure oxygen, carbon dioxide, and blood acidity. A physical examination helps identify signs of airway obstruction or lung disease. Chest imaging and other tests may determine the underlying cause. The severity and speed of onset determine how urgently respiratory support is required.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:202:"धमनीय रक्त गैस जांच, ऑक्सीजन मॉनिटरिंग और इमेजिंग द्वारा निदान किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:548:"Respiratory failure cannot always be prevented because it can result from severe illness or injury. Preventive measures include managing chronic lung and heart conditions, avoiding tobacco smoke, keeping recommended vaccinations up to date, reducing exposure to respiratory infections, and following treatment plans for conditions such as asthma or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Avoiding misuse or overdose of sedating medicines can also reduce risk. Early treatment of serious respiratory symptoms can prevent deterioration in some cases.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:124:"श्वसन रोगों का समय पर उपचार जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:392:"Respiratory failure is a medical emergency when acute or when chronic respiratory disease suddenly worsens. Seek emergency medical attention for severe difficulty breathing, inability to speak normally because of breathlessness, bluish lips or skin, confusion, extreme drowsiness, fainting, or loss of consciousness. Acute respiratory failure may require hospital or intensive-care treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:51:53";}i:336;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:349;s:10:"disease_id";i:2;s:11:"overview_en";s:559:"Tension headache is a common type of headache characterized by pain or pressure that is often felt across the forehead, around the head, or at the back of the head and neck. The pain is commonly described as pressing or tightening rather than throbbing and is usually mild to moderate in intensity. Episodes may last from part of a day to several days. Stress, poor sleep, muscle tension, prolonged screen use, fatigue, and other factors may contribute. Frequent or changing headaches should be evaluated to determine whether another condition is responsible.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:521:"टेंशन सिरदर्द सिरदर्द का सबसे सामान्य प्रकार है जिसमें सिर के चारों ओर दबाव, जकड़न या हल्का से मध्यम दर्द महसूस होता है। यह कभी-कभी या लंबे समय तक रह सकता है और दैनिक गतिविधियों को प्रभावित कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:471:"Tension headaches are thought to involve increased sensitivity or tension in pain pathways involving the head and neck. Stress, emotional strain, fatigue, inadequate sleep, prolonged concentration, and muscle tension may contribute to attacks. Long periods of computer or screen use, poor posture, jaw clenching, and irregular meals may also be associated with headaches in some people. The exact mechanism is not completely understood and may differ between individuals.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:284:"मांसपेशियों में तनाव, तनाव, चिंता, गलत मुद्रा, नींद की कमी और आंखों पर दबाव टेंशन सिरदर्द के सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:485:"Tension headaches may be more common with ongoing psychological stress, inadequate sleep, fatigue, prolonged concentration, poor posture, and sustained muscle tension in the neck or shoulders. Irregular meals, dehydration, excessive or prolonged screen use, and jaw clenching may contribute in some people. Frequent use of pain medicines can also contribute to medication-overuse headache, which is a separate but potentially overlapping problem. Individual triggers vary considerably.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:265:"तनावपूर्ण जीवनशैली, लंबे समय तक स्क्रीन का उपयोग, खराब नींद की आदतें और मानसिक दबाव जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:597:"Tension headache is usually diagnosed from the patient's description of the headache and a clinical examination. The healthcare professional considers the location, quality, duration, frequency, associated symptoms, and possible triggers. A neurological examination may be performed to look for signs of another disorder. Imaging is generally not required for a typical tension headache when the history and examination are reassuring. Additional investigation may be considered when headaches are new, unusually severe, progressively changing, or associated with concerning neurological symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:397:"निदान चिकित्सा इतिहास, लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन और शारीरिक परीक्षण के आधार पर किया जाता है। अन्य रोगों को बाहर करने के लिए इमेजिंग परीक्षण किए जा सकते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:563:"Tension headaches may be reduced by maintaining regular sleep, meals, hydration, physical activity, and breaks during prolonged computer or screen work. Good posture and attention to neck and shoulder positioning may help reduce muscle strain. Stress-management techniques, relaxation exercises, and addressing jaw clenching or other individual triggers may also be useful. Pain medicines should be used according to medical advice, because frequent use can contribute to medication-overuse headaches. Recurrent or changing headaches should be medically reviewed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:302:"तनाव का प्रबंधन, सही मुद्रा बनाए रखना, पर्याप्त नींद लेना और नियमित व्यायाम टेंशन सिरदर्द को रोकने में मदद करते हैं.";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:310:"Tension headaches usually do not require emergency care. Seek urgent medical attention for a sudden, extremely severe headache, a new headache with weakness, numbness, confusion, fainting, seizures, vision changes, fever with a stiff neck, or a headache that is substantially different from your usual pattern.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:337;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:350;s:10:"disease_id";i:3;s:11:"overview_en";s:561:"Cluster headache is a neurological disorder characterized by repeated attacks of extremely severe pain, usually around or behind one eye or on one side of the head. Attacks often begin suddenly and may last from several minutes to a few hours. They can occur repeatedly during periods known as cluster periods, sometimes at similar times each day. The affected eye may become red or watery, and the eyelid may swell or droop. A blocked or runny nose on the same side may also occur. Because the pain can be severe and recurrent, medical evaluation is important.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:406:"क्लस्टर सिरदर्द एक गंभीर न्यूरोलॉजिकल विकार है जिसमें आंख के आसपास या सिर के एक तरफ अत्यधिक दर्द होता है और यह कई सप्ताह या महीनों तक समूहों में हो सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:554:"The precise cause of cluster headache is not fully understood. The condition appears to involve abnormal activity in brain regions and biological systems that regulate pain and circadian rhythms. The hypothalamus is thought to play an important role because attacks often occur at predictable times and may follow seasonal or daily patterns. During an active cluster period, alcohol can trigger an attack in susceptible people, and other individual triggers may also exist. Cluster headaches are not caused simply by stress or ordinary tension headaches.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:310:"सटीक कारण अज्ञात है, लेकिन यह हाइपोथैलेमस की असामान्यताओं और ट्राइजेमिनल तंत्रिका की सक्रियता से जुड़ा माना जाता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:552:"Cluster headache is more common in men than women and often begins in adulthood, although it can occur in anyone. A family history may increase susceptibility. Smoking has been associated with cluster headache, although the relationship is complex and smoking does not explain all cases. Alcohol can trigger attacks during an active cluster period in susceptible individuals. Attacks may also follow circadian or seasonal patterns. A person who experiences recurrent severe one-sided headaches with autonomic symptoms should receive medical evaluation.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:203:"धूम्रपान, शराब का सेवन, पारिवारिक इतिहास और पुरुष लिंग प्रमुख जोखिम कारक हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:595:"Cluster headache is diagnosed primarily from the characteristic pattern of attacks, including severe unilateral pain around or behind the eye, relatively short duration, repeated attacks, and associated symptoms such as tearing, nasal congestion, eyelid swelling, or restlessness. A detailed history and neurological examination are important. Imaging such as MRI may be recommended in some people, particularly when the headache pattern is new, unusual, or associated with findings that could suggest another neurological condition. There is no single blood test that confirms cluster headache.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:308:"निदान विशिष्ट लक्षणों, सिरदर्द के पैटर्न, न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण और आवश्यकता पड़ने पर इमेजिंग के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:596:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent cluster headaches because their underlying cause is not fully understood. People who experience cluster periods may identify individual triggers that reliably provoke attacks and can discuss avoidance strategies with a healthcare professional. Alcohol is a well-known trigger for some people during an active cluster period. Maintaining a consistent sleep schedule may also be useful because attacks can follow circadian patterns. Preventive medicines may be prescribed for people with frequent attacks, but treatment should be individualized by a clinician.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:282:"क्लस्टर अवधि के दौरान शराब से बचना, धूम्रपान छोड़ना और चिकित्सकीय उपचार का पालन करना हमलों को कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:296:"Seek urgent medical attention for a new or unusually severe headache, especially when accompanied by weakness, numbness, confusion, fainting, seizures, vision loss, fever with a stiff neck, or other neurological symptoms. Severe or rapidly changing headache patterns should be medically assessed.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:338;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:351;s:10:"disease_id";i:4;s:11:"overview_en";s:450:"A stroke occurs when blood flow to part of the brain is interrupted or when a blood vessel in the brain ruptures and causes bleeding. Without adequate blood flow, brain cells are deprived of oxygen and nutrients and can begin to die within minutes. Stroke can cause sudden problems with movement, speech, vision, balance, or understanding and may result in permanent disability. It is a medical emergency requiring immediate evaluation and treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:398:"स्ट्रोक तब होता है जब मस्तिष्क के किसी भाग में रक्त प्रवाह रुक जाता है या कम हो जाता है, जिससे मस्तिष्क की कोशिकाओं को ऑक्सीजन और पोषक तत्व नहीं मिल पाते।";s:9:"causes_en";s:500:"There are two main types of stroke. Ischemic stroke occurs when a blood vessel supplying the brain becomes blocked, commonly by a blood clot or buildup of fatty plaque. Hemorrhagic stroke occurs when a blood vessel in the brain ruptures and causes bleeding. Conditions affecting blood vessels, abnormal clotting, certain heart conditions, and other disorders can contribute to stroke. A transient ischemic attack causes temporary stroke-like symptoms and can signal increased risk of a future stroke.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:241:"धमनियों का अवरुद्ध होना, रक्त के थक्के या मस्तिष्क में रक्तस्राव स्ट्रोक के मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:489:"Major stroke risk factors include high blood pressure, smoking, diabetes, high cholesterol, heart disease, atrial fibrillation, obesity, physical inactivity, and previous stroke or transient ischemic attack. Increasing age and certain family or genetic factors can also increase risk. Risk may be influenced by alcohol use and other health conditions. Managing blood pressure, blood sugar, cholesterol, heart disease, and tobacco exposure is important for reducing preventable stroke risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:233:"उच्च रक्तचाप, मधुमेह, धूम्रपान, मोटापा, उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल और हृदय रोग जोखिम को बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:460:"Stroke diagnosis requires urgent medical assessment because treatment depends on the type and timing of the event. Healthcare professionals evaluate the onset and pattern of symptoms and perform a neurological examination. Brain imaging, usually CT or MRI, helps determine whether bleeding or an area of damaged brain tissue is present. Blood tests, heart evaluation, and imaging of the blood vessels may also be used to identify the cause and guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:261:"निदान में न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, सीटी स्कैन, एमआरआई, रक्त परीक्षण और रक्त वाहिकाओं की जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:560:"Many strokes can be prevented by controlling conditions that damage blood vessels. Regular monitoring and treatment of high blood pressure, diabetes, and high cholesterol are important. Avoiding tobacco, maintaining a healthy weight, exercising regularly, following a heart-healthy eating pattern, and limiting excessive alcohol can reduce risk. People with atrial fibrillation or other cardiovascular conditions should follow their healthcare professional’s treatment plan. Recognizing warning signs and seeking emergency care immediately is also essential.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:353:"रक्तचाप को नियंत्रित रखना, स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाना, धूम्रपान से बचना और पुरानी बीमारियों का प्रबंधन स्ट्रोक की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:315:"Stroke is a medical emergency. Seek emergency care immediately for sudden weakness or numbness, especially on one side of the body, facial drooping, trouble speaking or understanding speech, sudden vision problems, severe dizziness, loss of balance, or a sudden severe headache. Do not wait for symptoms to improve.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:339;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:352;s:10:"disease_id";i:5;s:11:"overview_en";s:387:"Transient ischemic attack (TIA) is a temporary interruption of blood flow to part of the brain. It can cause sudden stroke-like symptoms such as weakness, numbness, difficulty speaking, vision changes, or problems with balance. Unlike a completed stroke, the symptoms of a TIA resolve without permanent brain damage, but a TIA is an important warning sign that a future stroke may occur.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:367:"ट्रांज़िएंट इस्केमिक अटैक (TIA) मस्तिष्क में रक्त प्रवाह का अस्थायी रुकना है, जिससे स्ट्रोक जैसे लक्षण होते हैं लेकिन स्थायी क्षति नहीं होती।";s:9:"causes_en";s:434:"A transient ischemic attack commonly occurs when a small blood clot temporarily blocks blood flow through an artery supplying the brain. Narrowed arteries caused by atherosclerosis can also reduce blood flow and contribute to a TIA. Abnormal heart rhythms and other cardiovascular conditions may allow blood clots to form and travel to the brain. Identifying the underlying cause is important for reducing the risk of a future stroke.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:232:"छोटे रक्त के थक्कों या संकरी धमनियों के कारण रक्त प्रवाह का अस्थायी अवरोध मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:411:"High blood pressure, smoking, diabetes, heart disease, and high cholesterol are important risk factors for transient ischemic attack. Other factors may include increasing age, obesity, physical inactivity, certain heart rhythm disorders, and a history of vascular disease. A previous TIA or stroke also indicates increased risk. Managing these factors can reduce the likelihood of future cerebrovascular events.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:206:"उच्च रक्तचाप, धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, हृदय रोग और उच्च कोलेस्ट्रॉल जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:474:"Diagnosis of a transient ischemic attack involves assessing the symptoms and determining whether they were caused by temporary disruption of blood flow to the brain. Neurological evaluation is performed, and imaging studies such as brain imaging and examination of blood vessels may be used. Blood tests and cardiovascular assessment can help identify conditions such as diabetes, abnormal cholesterol levels, or heart rhythm problems that may have contributed to the event.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:258:"निदान में न्यूरोलॉजिकल मूल्यांकन, इमेजिंग जांच, रक्त परीक्षण और हृदय संबंधी मूल्यांकन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:523:"Preventing future transient ischemic attacks and strokes involves controlling cardiovascular risk factors. Blood pressure, cholesterol, and diabetes should be appropriately managed, and smoking should be avoided. A healthy diet, regular physical activity, and maintaining a healthy weight can support vascular health. Medicines prescribed to prevent blood clots or control other risk factors should be taken as directed. Prompt medical evaluation after TIA symptoms is important because the risk of stroke may be increased.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:287:"हृदय संबंधी जोखिम कारकों का शीघ्र उपचार और स्वस्थ जीवनशैली भविष्य में TIA और स्ट्रोक की रोकथाम में मदद करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:299:"A transient ischemic attack requires urgent medical assessment because it can precede a stroke. Seek emergency care immediately for sudden weakness or numbness, facial drooping, difficulty speaking, vision changes, severe dizziness, or loss of balance, even if the symptoms have already disappeared.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:340;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:353;s:10:"disease_id";i:6;s:11:"overview_en";s:374:"Epilepsy is a neurological disorder characterized by a tendency to have recurrent unprovoked seizures. Seizures result from abnormal bursts of electrical activity in the brain and can cause changes in awareness, movement, sensation, behavior, or consciousness. Epilepsy has many forms and causes, and seizure symptoms vary depending on which parts of the brain are involved.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:318:"मिर्गी एक दीर्घकालिक न्यूरोलॉजिकल विकार है जिसमें मस्तिष्क की असामान्य विद्युत गतिविधि के कारण बार-बार दौरे पड़ते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:439:"Epilepsy can result from genetic factors, abnormalities in brain development, previous brain injury, stroke, brain tumors, infections affecting the brain, or other neurological conditions. In some people, the cause cannot be identified despite evaluation. A person may also develop epilepsy after a significant head injury or another condition that damages brain tissue. The cause can influence the type of seizures and treatment approach.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:256:"आनुवंशिक कारण, मस्तिष्क की चोट, संक्रमण, स्ट्रोक और विकास संबंधी विकार मिर्गी का कारण बन सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:439:"Risk factors include a family history of epilepsy, previous traumatic brain injury, stroke, brain infection, brain tumors, abnormalities present from birth, and other neurological disorders. Seizure risk can also be influenced by conditions affecting the developing brain. The presence of one risk factor does not necessarily mean that a person will develop epilepsy, and many people with epilepsy have no clearly identifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:220:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, मस्तिष्क की चोट, संक्रमण और न्यूरोलॉजिकल विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:508:"Epilepsy is diagnosed from the history and characteristics of seizures together with neurological assessment and appropriate testing. An electroencephalogram can detect abnormal electrical activity in the brain and help classify seizures. Brain MRI or other imaging may identify structural abnormalities. Blood tests and additional studies may be used to identify possible metabolic or other causes. Diagnosis generally requires distinguishing epileptic seizures from other events that can resemble seizures.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:260:"निदान में न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, ईईजी, एमआरआई, सीटी स्कैन और चिकित्सा इतिहास का मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:534:"Not all epilepsy can be prevented, but reducing the risk of brain injury can help prevent some cases. Using seat belts, helmets and appropriate safety equipment, preventing falls, and following road and workplace safety measures can reduce traumatic brain injury. Preventing or promptly treating certain infections and managing cardiovascular risk factors may also reduce some causes of brain injury. People with epilepsy can reduce seizure-related risks by taking prescribed medicines consistently and following their treatment plan.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:282:"दवाओं का नियमित सेवन, दौरे के ट्रिगर्स से बचाव और पर्याप्त नींद लेना दौरे को नियंत्रित करने में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:241:"Seek emergency medical care for a seizure lasting longer than usual or continuing for several minutes, repeated seizures without recovery between them, serious injury during a seizure, difficulty breathing afterward, or a first-ever seizure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:48:51";}i:341;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:354;s:10:"disease_id";i:7;s:11:"overview_en";s:391:"Parkinson disease is a progressive neurological disorder that primarily affects movement. It commonly causes tremors, muscle stiffness, slowed movements, changes in posture, and balance problems. Symptoms may begin gradually and can become more noticeable over time. Some people may also experience changes in speech, sleep, mood, or other non-movement functions as the condition progresses.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:367:"पार्किंसन रोग एक प्रगतिशील न्यूरोलॉजिकल विकार है जो शरीर की गति को प्रभावित करता है और कंपन, जकड़न तथा संतुलन संबंधी समस्याएं पैदा करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:369:"Parkinson disease is primarily associated with the loss or dysfunction of dopamine-producing nerve cells in a region of the brain involved in controlling movement. The exact reason these nerve cells become damaged is not fully understood. A combination of genetic susceptibility and environmental factors may contribute to the development of the disease in some people.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:252:"मस्तिष्क में डोपामिन बनाने वाली तंत्रिका कोशिकाओं का नष्ट होना पार्किंसन रोग का मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:401:"Increasing age is an important risk factor for Parkinson disease. A family history of the condition may increase risk, particularly when certain genetic factors are present. Exposure to some environmental toxins has also been associated with increased risk. The condition occurs more often in men than women. Having a risk factor does not mean that a person will necessarily develop Parkinson disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:265:"बढ़ती उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास, पर्यावरणीय विषाक्त पदार्थों का संपर्क और पुरुष लिंग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:486:"Diagnosis of Parkinson disease is based mainly on the medical history, neurological examination, characteristic movement symptoms, and their progression over time. Doctors may assess tremor, muscle stiffness, slowed movement, posture, balance, walking pattern, and other neurological findings. The response to certain medications may provide additional information. Other tests or imaging studies may be used when needed to help exclude other conditions that can cause similar symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:295:"निदान चिकित्सा इतिहास, न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, लक्षणों की प्रगति और दवाओं की प्रतिक्रिया के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:457:"There is no established way to completely prevent Parkinson disease because its exact cause is not fully understood. Regular physical activity, a balanced diet, and maintaining general health may support physical function and overall well-being. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to environmental toxins may also be appropriate. Early medical evaluation of persistent movement symptoms can help with timely diagnosis, treatment, and management of complications.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:285:"नियमित व्यायाम, स्वस्थ आहार और समय पर उपचार जटिलताओं को कम करने और जीवन की गुणवत्ता सुधारने में मदद करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:339:"Seek urgent medical attention for sudden or rapidly worsening confusion, severe difficulty moving, repeated falls with significant injury, fainting, severe swallowing or breathing difficulty, or a sudden major change in symptoms. Medication-related complications or inability to take essential medicines may also require prompt assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:342;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:355;s:10:"disease_id";i:8;s:11:"overview_en";s:445:"Alzheimer disease is a progressive brain disorder that gradually damages memory, thinking, reasoning, and other cognitive abilities. As the disease progresses, a person may have increasing difficulty performing familiar everyday activities and may develop changes in communication, behavior, or judgment. The course varies between individuals, but symptoms generally become more significant over time as brain cells and connections are affected.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:345:"अल्जाइमर रोग एक प्रगतिशील मस्तिष्क विकार है जो धीरे-धीरे स्मृति, सोचने की क्षमता और दैनिक कार्य करने की क्षमता को प्रभावित करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:477:"Alzheimer disease is associated with abnormal changes in the brain, including the accumulation of certain proteins and degeneration of nerve cells and their connections. These changes interfere with communication between brain cells and eventually contribute to loss of brain function. Genetic factors can influence susceptibility, while aging and other biological factors may also contribute. The exact cause in an individual person is often a combination of multiple factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:239:"मस्तिष्क में असामान्य प्रोटीन जमाव और तंत्रिका कोशिकाओं का क्षय अल्जाइमर रोग से जुड़ा है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:483:"Advanced age is the strongest known risk factor for Alzheimer disease. Having a family history of the condition or certain genetic factors can increase susceptibility. Cardiovascular conditions and factors that affect blood vessel health may also be associated with increased risk. Other potentially relevant factors include physical inactivity and some lifestyle-related health conditions. Having a risk factor does not mean that a person will necessarily develop Alzheimer disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:193:"बढ़ती उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास, हृदय रोग और आनुवंशिक कारक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:527:"Diagnosis of Alzheimer disease involves evaluating memory, thinking, behavior, and the ability to perform everyday activities. Cognitive testing and neurological examination can help identify patterns of impairment. Brain imaging may be used to assess brain structure and exclude other causes of symptoms. Laboratory assessments may also be performed to identify potentially treatable conditions that can cause or worsen cognitive problems. The diagnosis is based on the overall clinical assessment and available test findings.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:278:"निदान में संज्ञानात्मक परीक्षण, न्यूरोलॉजिकल मूल्यांकन, मस्तिष्क इमेजिंग और प्रयोगशाला जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:485:"There is no guaranteed method for preventing Alzheimer disease, but maintaining overall brain and cardiovascular health may be beneficial. Regular physical activity, a balanced diet, adequate sleep, and continued mental and social activity can support general health. Managing conditions such as high blood pressure, diabetes, and other cardiovascular risk factors is also important. Regular medical care can help identify and manage health problems that may affect cognitive function.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:333:"मानसिक गतिविधि बनाए रखना, नियमित व्यायाम, स्वस्थ आहार और हृदय संबंधी जोखिम कारकों का नियंत्रण जोखिम कम करने में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:308:"Seek urgent medical attention for a sudden change in confusion, consciousness, behavior, or ability to function, particularly when it develops over hours or days. Falls with significant injury, seizures, severe difficulty breathing or swallowing, or other acute changes should also receive prompt assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:343;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:356;s:10:"disease_id";i:9;s:11:"overview_en";s:456:"Dementia is a group of disorders characterized by a decline in memory, thinking, language, problem-solving, or other mental abilities severe enough to interfere with everyday life. It is not a normal part of aging. Different forms of dementia affect the brain in different ways and can produce changes in behavior, movement, communication, and the ability to perform familiar activities. Symptoms and progression vary according to the underlying condition.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:364:"डिमेंशिया ऐसी स्थितियों का समूह है जिसमें मस्तिष्क की क्षति या बीमारी के कारण स्मृति, तर्क क्षमता, संचार और दैनिक कार्य प्रभावित होते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:521:"Dementia can result from several different diseases and brain disorders. Common forms include Alzheimer disease, vascular dementia, Lewy body dementia, and frontotemporal disorders. Alzheimer disease is associated with abnormal protein deposits and loss of nerve-cell connections, while vascular dementia is related to problems affecting blood supply to the brain. Other neurological disorders, brain injuries, infections, metabolic conditions, and certain medications or substances can also cause dementia-like symptoms.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:282:"अल्जाइमर रोग, रक्त वाहिका संबंधी विकार, न्यूरोलॉजिकल रोग और मस्तिष्क की चोट डिमेंशिया के सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:467:"Increasing age is the strongest known risk factor for dementia, although dementia is not an inevitable consequence of aging. Other factors associated with increased risk include a family history of dementia, smoking, uncontrolled diabetes, high blood pressure, excessive alcohol use, cardiovascular disease, and certain neurological conditions. Risk varies according to the type of dementia, and some causes of cognitive decline may be treatable or partly reversible.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:200:"बढ़ती उम्र, हृदय रोग, धूम्रपान, मधुमेह और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:485:"Dementia is diagnosed through a combination of medical history, assessment of symptoms, physical examination, and testing of memory and other cognitive abilities. Healthcare professionals may use blood tests to look for contributing conditions and may recommend brain imaging such as CT or MRI. Depending on the situation, neurological, genetic, or mental health evaluations may also be used. The evaluation aims to identify the type and possible underlying cause of cognitive decline.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:287:"निदान में संज्ञानात्मक मूल्यांकन, न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, मस्तिष्क इमेजिंग और प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:531:"There is no proven way to prevent every form of dementia, particularly those caused by age-related or genetic changes. However, maintaining a healthy lifestyle may help address some modifiable risk factors. Managing blood pressure, diabetes, and cardiovascular health, avoiding tobacco, limiting excessive alcohol use, remaining physically active, and maintaining social and mental activity may support overall brain health. Early evaluation of persistent cognitive changes can also help identify treatable contributing conditions.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:343:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाना, पुरानी बीमारियों को नियंत्रित रखना और मानसिक गतिविधियों में भाग लेना डिमेंशिया के जोखिम को कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:308:"Dementia usually progresses gradually, so a sudden change in confusion, alertness, behavior, or physical function should receive urgent medical assessment. Seek emergency care for severe breathing difficulty, seizures, significant injury after a fall, loss of consciousness, or other sudden serious symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:344;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:357;s:10:"disease_id";i:10;s:11:"overview_en";s:408:"Meningitis is inflammation of the protective membranes surrounding the brain and spinal cord. It can be caused by infections and, depending on the cause, may become life-threatening and require urgent treatment. Symptoms can include fever, severe headache, neck stiffness, sensitivity to light, nausea, vomiting, confusion, or changes in consciousness. The severity and course depend on the underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:390:"मेनिन्जाइटिस मस्तिष्क और रीढ़ की हड्डी को ढकने वाली झिल्लियों की सूजन है। यह संक्रमण के कारण हो सकता है और समय पर उपचार न मिलने पर जानलेवा हो सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:416:"Bacterial, viral, fungal, and parasitic infections can cause meningitis. The specific organism responsible influences how quickly the illness develops, its severity, and the treatment required. Bacterial meningitis can become severe rapidly, while some viral forms may be less severe. Infections can reach the membranes surrounding the brain and spinal cord through the bloodstream or from nearby sites of infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:214:"बैक्टीरिया, वायरस, फंगस या परजीवी संक्रमण मेनिन्जाइटिस के सबसे सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:442:"Young age can increase the risk of certain forms of meningitis, particularly in infants and children. A weakened immune system can make a person more susceptible to infection. Crowded living conditions can facilitate the spread of some infectious organisms. Lack of recommended vaccination can also increase the risk of vaccine-preventable forms of meningitis. Certain infections, medical conditions, and exposures may create additional risk.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:245:"कम उम्र, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, भीड़भाड़ वाले स्थानों में रहना और टीकाकरण की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:482:"Diagnosis of meningitis requires prompt medical evaluation when symptoms suggest inflammation of the membranes surrounding the brain and spinal cord. A physical and neurological examination is performed, and a lumbar puncture may be used to examine cerebrospinal fluid for evidence of infection and inflammation. Blood tests can help identify infection, while brain imaging may be performed when clinically appropriate to evaluate complications or other possible causes of symptoms.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:238:"निदान में शारीरिक परीक्षण, लम्बर पंचर, रक्त परीक्षण और मस्तिष्क की इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:443:"Vaccination is an important way to prevent several serious forms of meningitis. Good hygiene practices, including regular handwashing and avoiding close contact with people who have certain infections, can reduce transmission. Prompt evaluation and treatment of relevant infections may also reduce complications. People at increased risk should discuss recommended vaccinations and other preventive measures with their healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:241:"टीकाकरण, अच्छी स्वच्छता और संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार मेनिन्जाइटिस की रोकथाम में मदद करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:293:"Meningitis can become life-threatening quickly and requires urgent medical assessment. Seek emergency care for severe headache with fever and a stiff neck, confusion, extreme drowsiness, seizures, sensitivity to light, repeated vomiting, a rapidly spreading rash, or rapidly worsening illness.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:345;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:358;s:10:"disease_id";i:11;s:11:"overview_en";s:410:"Encephalitis is inflammation of the brain that can cause a serious illness affecting the nervous system. Symptoms may include fever, headache, confusion, unusual behavior, seizures, sensitivity to light, weakness, difficulty speaking, or loss of consciousness. Encephalitis can progress rapidly and may require urgent hospital treatment. Recovery varies according to the cause and severity of the inflammation.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:437:"एन्सेफलाइटिस मस्तिष्क ऊतक की सूजन है जो प्रायः वायरल संक्रमण के कारण होती है। यह मस्तिष्क की कार्यक्षमता को प्रभावित कर सकती है और गंभीर जटिलताएं उत्पन्न कर सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:432:"Encephalitis may be caused by infections, particularly viruses, or by an abnormal immune response in which the immune system attacks brain tissue. Several viruses can cause encephalitis, including some transmitted by mosquitoes or ticks. Less commonly, bacterial, fungal, or parasitic infections can be involved. Autoimmune encephalitis occurs when immune-system activity causes inflammation without a direct infection of the brain.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:279:"हर्पीस सिम्प्लेक्स वायरस, मच्छरों से फैलने वाले वायरस और ऑटोइम्यून प्रतिक्रियाएं इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:451:"Risk depends on the underlying cause. Exposure to viruses and other infectious organisms can increase risk, including exposure through mosquito or tick bites or contact with infected people. Travel or residence in areas where certain mosquito- or tick-borne infections occur may also increase risk. People with certain immune-system disorders may be susceptible to autoimmune encephalitis. Age and overall health can influence the severity of illness.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:174:"कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, वायरल संपर्क, बचपन और अधिक आयु जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:425:"Encephalitis is diagnosed using the symptoms, neurological examination, and tests designed to identify inflammation or infection of the brain. Evaluation may include brain imaging with CT or MRI, analysis of cerebrospinal fluid obtained by lumbar puncture, blood tests, and an electroencephalogram to assess brain electrical activity. Additional antibody or infectious-disease testing may be performed to determine the cause.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:244:"निदान में न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, एमआरआई, ईईजी, स्पाइनल फ्लूइड जांच और रक्त परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:469:"Prevention depends on the cause. Recommended vaccinations can protect against some infections associated with encephalitis. Avoiding mosquito and tick bites through appropriate clothing, repellents, and environmental precautions can reduce exposure to certain infectious causes. Good hygiene can reduce transmission of some viruses. People should seek urgent medical attention for severe headache, confusion, seizures, or other rapidly developing neurological symptoms.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:196:"टीकाकरण, मच्छरों से बचाव और संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार जोखिम को कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:265:"Encephalitis can be a medical emergency. Seek immediate medical attention for new confusion, severe drowsiness, seizures, loss of consciousness, unusual behavior, severe headache with fever, weakness, difficulty speaking, or rapidly worsening neurological symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:346;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:359;s:10:"disease_id";i:12;s:11:"overview_en";s:374:"A brain tumor is an abnormal growth of cells in or around the brain. Brain tumors may be benign or malignant and can affect brain function depending on their type, size, location, and rate of growth. Symptoms vary and may include headaches, seizures, changes in vision, weakness, difficulty with speech or movement, personality changes, or problems with memory and thinking.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:466:"ब्रेन ट्यूमर मस्तिष्क के भीतर कोशिकाओं की असामान्य वृद्धि है। यह सौम्य या कैंसरयुक्त हो सकता है और अपने आकार तथा स्थान के अनुसार मस्तिष्क की कार्यक्षमता को प्रभावित कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:374:"The exact cause of most brain tumors is unknown. Brain tumors develop when cells acquire genetic changes that cause them to grow or divide abnormally. Certain inherited genetic conditions can increase susceptibility, and exposure to high doses of ionizing radiation is an established risk factor. Most brain tumors, however, cannot be linked to a specific preventable cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:285:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन, विकिरण का संपर्क और कुछ वंशानुगत स्थितियां ब्रेन ट्यूमर के विकास में योगदान दे सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:369:"Risk factors include exposure to high doses of ionizing radiation, certain inherited genetic syndromes, and a family history of particular brain tumors or related genetic conditions. Some tumors are more common with increasing age, while others occur more often in children or younger adults. Having a risk factor does not mean that a person will develop a brain tumor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:207:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, विकिरण का संपर्क और कुछ आनुवंशिक सिंड्रोम जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:429:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and neurological examination to assess symptoms and brain function. Imaging studies such as magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) or computed tomography (CT) can identify a mass and show its location and characteristics. When appropriate, a biopsy may be performed to examine tumor cells and determine the tumor type and grade. Additional laboratory or molecular tests may help guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:240:"निदान में न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, एमआरआई, सीटी स्कैन, बायोप्सी और प्रयोगशाला जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:417:"There is no reliable way to prevent most brain tumors because their causes are often unknown. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to high-dose ionizing radiation and following appropriate medical guidance when radiation imaging or treatment is required may reduce avoidable exposure. People with known inherited conditions associated with brain tumors may benefit from appropriate medical monitoring and genetic counseling.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:260:"अनावश्यक विकिरण से बचाव और न्यूरोलॉजिकल लक्षणों की समय पर जांच प्रारंभिक पहचान में मदद कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:287:"Seek urgent medical attention for a new seizure, sudden or rapidly worsening weakness or numbness, difficulty speaking, severe or rapidly worsening headache, repeated vomiting with neurological symptoms, confusion, loss of consciousness, or significant changes in vision or coordination.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:347;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:360;s:10:"disease_id";i:13;s:11:"overview_en";s:367:"A concussion is a type of mild traumatic brain injury caused by a blow, bump, or jolt to the head or by a force that makes the brain move rapidly within the skull. Symptoms can include headache, dizziness, confusion, difficulty concentrating, memory problems, nausea, sensitivity to light or noise, and changes in sleep or mood. Loss of consciousness is not required.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:353:"कंकशन सिर पर चोट, झटका या आघात के कारण होने वाली हल्की मस्तिष्कीय चोट है जो अस्थायी रूप से मस्तिष्क की कार्यक्षमता को प्रभावित करती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:388:"A concussion can occur after a direct blow to the head or when a sudden impact causes the head and brain to move rapidly. Falls, vehicle crashes, sports injuries, assaults, and other accidents can cause concussions. The brain can be affected even when there is no visible external injury. Repeated head injuries before recovery may increase the risk of prolonged or more serious problems.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:217:"सिर पर सीधा आघात, गिरना, खेल संबंधी चोटें और वाहन दुर्घटनाएं इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:384:"Risk factors include participation in contact or collision sports, activities with a high risk of falls, previous concussion, and situations where protective equipment or safety measures are inadequate. Children and adolescents may require particular attention because their brains are still developing. Returning to activities before recovery can increase the risk of another injury.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:240:"संपर्क वाले खेलों में भाग लेना, पहले कंकशन होना और जोखिमपूर्ण गतिविधियां जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:442:"Concussion is diagnosed primarily from the circumstances of the injury, symptoms, and neurological examination. Healthcare professionals assess memory, concentration, balance, coordination, and other neurological functions. CT or MRI is not required for every concussion but may be used when there are signs suggesting a more serious brain injury, such as severe worsening headache, repeated vomiting, seizures, or neurological abnormalities.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:285:"निदान लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन, न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण और आवश्यकता पड़ने पर इमेजिंग जांच के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:458:"Concussion risk can be reduced by using appropriate protective equipment, following sports-safety rules, improving playing and training techniques, using seat belts, preventing falls, and making homes and work areas safer. Helmets can reduce the risk of some head injuries but cannot prevent every concussion. Anyone suspected of having a concussion should stop the activity and be medically assessed before returning to sports or other high-risk activities.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:237:"सुरक्षा उपकरण, सीट बेल्ट, हेलमेट और सुरक्षा नियमों का पालन कंकशन की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:298:"Seek emergency medical care after a head injury for worsening or severe headache, repeated vomiting, increasing drowsiness, confusion, unusual behavior, seizures, loss of consciousness, weakness or numbness, difficulty speaking, unequal pupils, or clear fluid or blood coming from the nose or ears.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:348;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:361;s:10:"disease_id";i:14;s:11:"overview_en";s:394:"Multiple sclerosis is a chronic disease in which the immune system attacks structures within the central nervous system, particularly the protective myelin surrounding nerve fibers. This can interfere with communication between the brain, spinal cord, and body. Symptoms vary widely and may include vision problems, numbness, weakness, balance difficulties, fatigue, or changes in coordination.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:479:"मल्टीपल स्क्लेरोसिस एक दीर्घकालिक ऑटोइम्यून रोग है जिसमें प्रतिरक्षा तंत्र तंत्रिका रेशों की सुरक्षात्मक परत पर हमला करता है, जिससे मस्तिष्क और शरीर के बीच संचार प्रभावित होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:445:"Multiple sclerosis results from an abnormal immune response directed against components of the central nervous system. The precise trigger is unknown. Genetic susceptibility interacts with environmental factors such as certain viral exposures, low vitamin D status, smoking, and other factors that may influence immune function. Different patterns of inflammation and nervous-system injury produce the wide range of symptoms seen in the disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:306:"ऑटोइम्यून प्रतिक्रियाएं, आनुवंशिक प्रवृत्ति और पर्यावरणीय कारक मल्टीपल स्क्लेरोसिस के विकास में योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:426:"Risk factors for multiple sclerosis include a family history of the disease, certain genetic backgrounds, female sex, younger adult age, smoking, and some environmental or geographic factors. Low vitamin D status and previous infection with Epstein-Barr virus have also been associated with increased risk. These factors influence susceptibility but do not by themselves establish that someone will develop multiple sclerosis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:221:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, महिला लिंग, विटामिन D की कमी और कुछ वायरल संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:462:"Diagnosis of multiple sclerosis involves evidence that symptoms or neurological abnormalities are separated in time and location within the central nervous system while excluding other explanations. MRI of the brain and spinal cord is commonly used to identify characteristic lesions. Cerebrospinal fluid testing, evoked potential studies, blood tests, and other investigations may be used when needed to support the diagnosis or rule out alternative conditions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:276:"निदान में न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, एमआरआई, स्पाइनल फ्लूइड विश्लेषण और इवोक्ड पोटेंशियल परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:477:"There is no established way to completely prevent multiple sclerosis. Avoiding smoking and maintaining adequate vitamin D through appropriate diet, safe sunlight exposure, or supplementation when medically indicated may support general health. People with a family history or neurological symptoms should discuss concerns with a healthcare professional. Early diagnosis and appropriate treatment can reduce disease activity and help prevent disability in people who develop MS.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:316:"सामान्य स्वास्थ्य बनाए रखना, पर्याप्त विटामिन D स्तर और नियमित चिकित्सा निगरानी जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:306:"Seek urgent medical attention for sudden or rapidly worsening weakness, significant new vision loss, severe difficulty walking, loss of coordination, difficulty speaking or swallowing, breathing problems, or other new neurological symptoms that are severe or substantially different from previous symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:349;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:362;s:10:"disease_id";i:15;s:11:"overview_en";s:504:"Hydrocephalus is a condition in which too much cerebrospinal fluid accumulates in or around the brain, causing enlargement of the brain spaces and potentially harmful pressure on brain tissue. It can occur before birth, during infancy, in childhood, or later in adulthood. Symptoms vary with age and cause and may include headache, vomiting, vision problems, balance difficulties, changes in thinking or memory, and problems with bladder control. Untreated hydrocephalus can cause permanent brain damage.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:427:"हाइड्रोसेफेलस ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें मस्तिष्क के भीतर सेरेब्रोस्पाइनल द्रव अत्यधिक मात्रा में जमा हो जाता है, जिससे दबाव बढ़ता है और मस्तिष्क को नुकसान हो सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:560:"Hydrocephalus develops when cerebrospinal fluid cannot flow normally, is not adequately absorbed into the bloodstream, or is produced in excessive amounts. Causes include congenital developmental abnormalities, genetic conditions, infections during pregnancy, bleeding in or around the brain, head injury, tumors, meningitis, encephalitis, and other disorders affecting cerebrospinal fluid circulation. Normal pressure hydrocephalus is a form that generally occurs in older adults and can develop after certain brain injuries, bleeding, infections, or surgery.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:328:"सेरेब्रोस्पाइनल द्रव के प्रवाह में अवरोध, जन्मजात दोष, संक्रमण, मस्तिष्क की चोट या ट्यूमर हाइड्रोसेफेलस का कारण बन सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:503:"Risk factors depend on the type of hydrocephalus. Congenital forms may be associated with genetic conditions or developmental abnormalities of the brain and spinal cord. In children, previous infections of the central nervous system, bleeding around birth, tumors, or head injury can increase risk. In adults, head trauma, brain bleeding, meningitis, brain surgery, or other conditions affecting cerebrospinal fluid circulation may contribute. Older age is associated with normal pressure hydrocephalus.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:241:"समय से पूर्व जन्म, जन्मजात असामान्यताएं, मस्तिष्क संक्रमण और सिर की चोटें जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:502:"Diagnosis involves assessment of symptoms, medical history, neurological function, and brain imaging. Ultrasound may be useful in infants before the skull bones have fully joined. CT and MRI scans can show enlargement of the brain ventricles, identify abnormalities, and help determine a possible cause. In suspected normal pressure hydrocephalus, additional tests may evaluate cerebrospinal fluid and determine whether symptoms are likely to improve after fluid removal or other diagnostic procedures.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:236:"निदान में न्यूरोलॉजिकल परीक्षण, शिशुओं में अल्ट्रासाउंड, सीटी स्कैन और एमआरआई शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:512:"Not all hydrocephalus can be prevented because some forms result from genetic or developmental conditions. Protecting infants and children from head injury and obtaining prompt treatment for infections that affect the brain or spinal cord may reduce the risk of some acquired cases. Appropriate prenatal care can help identify certain developmental problems. People with conditions that may cause bleeding or injury to the brain should receive timely medical care and follow recommended treatment and monitoring.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:304:"न्यूरोलॉजिकल रोगों का समय पर उपचार, संक्रमण की रोकथाम और प्रसवपूर्व देखभाल कुछ कारणों को कम करने में मदद कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:284:"Seek urgent medical attention for rapidly worsening headache, repeated vomiting, increasing drowsiness or confusion, seizures, loss of consciousness, sudden worsening of balance or walking, or significant changes in vision or behavior. Acute symptoms may require emergency evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:350;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:363;s:10:"disease_id";i:16;s:11:"overview_en";s:465:"A cataract is a clouding of the normally clear lens inside the eye. As the lens becomes cloudy, less light reaches the retina and vision may become blurred, dim, or less sharp. Cataracts usually develop gradually and are most common with increasing age, although they can also occur after eye injury, surgery, certain diseases, or prolonged exposure to factors that damage the lens. Cataracts may affect one or both eyes but do not spread from one eye to the other.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:390:"मोतियाबिंद एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें आंख का प्राकृतिक लेंस धुंधला हो जाता है, जिससे दृष्टि धुंधली हो जाती है और धीरे-धीरे देखने की क्षमता कम हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:483:"Most cataracts develop as part of the aging process as proteins in the lens break down and clump together, making the lens increasingly cloudy. Cataracts can also develop after an eye injury or eye surgery and may be associated with diabetes, inflammation inside the eye, certain medicines such as long-term corticosteroids, radiation exposure, or other conditions. Congenital cataracts may be present at birth or develop during childhood because of genetic or developmental factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:354:"बढ़ती उम्र मोतियाबिंद का सबसे सामान्य कारण है। आंख की चोट, मधुमेह, लंबे समय तक स्टेरॉयड का उपयोग और आनुवंशिक कारक भी योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:449:"Older age is the most important risk factor for cataracts. Other factors include diabetes, a family history of cataracts, previous eye injury or eye surgery, long-term use of corticosteroids or certain other medicines, smoking, radiation exposure, and prolonged ultraviolet light exposure. Some inflammatory eye diseases and other medical conditions can also increase risk. Risk generally increases as the lens is exposed to these factors over time.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:232:"अधिक उम्र, मधुमेह, धूम्रपान, अत्यधिक धूप का संपर्क और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:439:"Cataracts are diagnosed through an eye examination and assessment of vision. An eye care professional may test visual acuity and examine the lens and other structures of the eye using a slit lamp or other instruments. The pupils may be dilated so that the back of the eye can be examined and other causes of vision loss can be assessed. Additional tests may be used when another eye condition is suspected or when surgery is being planned.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:235:"निदान व्यापक नेत्र परीक्षण, दृष्टि परीक्षण और स्लिट-लैम्प जांच के माध्यम से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:514:"Not all cataracts can be prevented, especially those related to aging. Measures that may help reduce risk include protecting the eyes from ultraviolet light with appropriate sunglasses and a wide-brimmed hat, avoiding smoking, protecting the eyes from injury, and controlling medical conditions such as diabetes. A healthy diet containing fruits, vegetables, leafy greens, nuts, and whole grains may support overall eye health. Regular eye examinations can help detect cataracts and other causes of vision changes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:354:"आंखों को पराबैंगनी किरणों से बचाना, धूम्रपान से बचना, मधुमेह को नियंत्रित रखना और नियमित नेत्र जांच जोखिम को कम करने में मदद कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:298:"Cataracts usually develop gradually and do not normally require emergency care. Seek urgent eye assessment for sudden vision loss, severe eye pain, marked redness, flashes or a sudden increase in floaters, or a curtain-like shadow over part of the vision, as these may indicate another eye problem.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:351;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:364;s:10:"disease_id";i:17;s:11:"overview_en";s:434:"Glaucoma is a group of eye diseases that damage the optic nerve, which is essential for carrying visual information from the eye to the brain. Increased pressure inside the eye is a common contributing factor, although glaucoma can also occur when eye pressure is not markedly elevated. Damage may develop gradually without noticeable symptoms at first and can eventually cause permanent vision loss if it is not detected and treated.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:378:"ग्लूकोमा आंखों के रोगों का एक समूह है जिसमें ऑप्टिक नर्व को नुकसान पहुंचता है, अक्सर आंख के अंदर दबाव बढ़ने के कारण, जिससे दृष्टि हानि हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:382:"Glaucoma may develop when fluid inside the eye does not drain properly, causing increased intraocular pressure and damage to the optic nerve. Genetic factors can contribute to susceptibility. Some forms may occur because of abnormalities in the structure or development of the eye, while other forms can be associated with injury, inflammation, medications, or other eye conditions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:254:"आंख के भीतर बढ़ा हुआ दबाव, आंख के द्रव के निकास में समस्या और आनुवंशिक कारक इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:423:"Older age, a family history of glaucoma, diabetes, and elevated eye pressure can increase the risk of developing glaucoma. Prolonged or inappropriate use of corticosteroid medicines may also increase risk in some people. Other eye conditions, previous eye injury, and certain structural characteristics of the eye can contribute to risk. Regular examinations are particularly important for people with several risk factors.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:279:"बढ़ती उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास, मधुमेह, आंखों का उच्च दबाव और लंबे समय तक स्टेरॉयड का उपयोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:427:"Diagnosis of glaucoma involves a comprehensive eye examination. Eye pressure may be measured using tonometry, while the optic nerve is examined for signs of damage. Visual field testing can identify areas of reduced peripheral vision, and imaging studies may assess the optic nerve and retinal structures. Additional examinations may be performed to determine the type and severity of glaucoma and to monitor changes over time.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:265:"निदान में आंखों के दबाव की जांच, ऑप्टिक नर्व परीक्षण, विजुअल फील्ड परीक्षण और इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:412:"Glaucoma-related vision loss cannot always be prevented, but early detection and treatment can help protect remaining vision. Regular comprehensive eye examinations are important, particularly for people at increased risk. Following prescribed treatment and attending follow-up appointments can help control eye pressure and monitor optic nerve health. Prompt evaluation of new visual symptoms is also important.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:254:"नियमित नेत्र जांच और समय पर उपचार ग्लूकोमा से होने वाली दृष्टि हानि को रोकने में महत्वपूर्ण हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:260:"Sudden severe eye pain, marked eye redness, blurred or reduced vision, halos around lights, severe headache, nausea, or vomiting can indicate acute glaucoma and require emergency eye care. Any sudden or significant change in vision should be assessed promptly.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:352;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:365;s:10:"disease_id";i:18;s:11:"overview_en";s:367:"Conjunctivitis, commonly called pink eye, is inflammation or swelling of the conjunctiva, the clear tissue covering the white part of the eye and lining the inside of the eyelids. It may cause redness, watering, irritation, itching, discharge, or discomfort. Conjunctivitis can result from viruses, bacteria, allergies, dry eyes, or exposure to irritating substances.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:261:"कंजंक्टिवाइटिस या पिंक आई आंख की कंजंक्टिवा की सूजन है, जिससे लालिमा, जलन और आंख से स्राव हो सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:426:"Conjunctivitis has several possible causes. Viral and bacterial infections are common and can spread easily, particularly among children. Allergic conjunctivitis occurs when the eyes react to substances such as pollen, mold, or animal dander. Irritation from chemicals, smoke, foreign material, or other environmental factors can also cause inflammation. Dry eyes may make the eyes more vulnerable to irritation and infection.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:257:"वायरल संक्रमण, बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण, एलर्जी और उत्तेजक पदार्थ कंजंक्टिवाइटिस के सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:443:"Risk depends on the type of conjunctivitis. Close contact with a person who has viral or bacterial conjunctivitis increases the chance of infection. Children in group settings may be exposed more easily. Allergies, exposure to pollen or other allergens, dry eyes, and contact with irritating substances can increase the risk of noninfectious conjunctivitis. Newborns can develop serious eye infections from bacteria acquired during childbirth.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:253:"संक्रमित व्यक्तियों के संपर्क में आना, एलर्जी, खराब स्वच्छता और दूषित वस्तुएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:461:"Conjunctivitis is usually diagnosed from the eye symptoms and an examination of the eyes. The healthcare provider looks for redness, swelling, discharge, irritation, and other changes in the conjunctiva. The medical history helps distinguish infectious, allergic, and irritant causes. In some cases, especially when symptoms are severe, persistent, recurrent, or unusual, additional testing may be needed to identify an infectious cause or another eye disorder.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:313:"निदान आमतौर पर लक्षणों और नेत्र परीक्षण के आधार पर किया जाता है। कुछ मामलों में प्रयोगशाला जांच की आवश्यकता हो सकती है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:477:"Good hand hygiene can reduce the spread of infectious conjunctivitis. Avoid touching or rubbing the eyes and do not share towels, cosmetics, eye drops, or other personal items that contact the eyes. Clean hands should be used when applying eye medicines or contact lenses. People with symptoms should follow medical advice about limiting close contact and preventing transmission. Avoiding known allergens and eye irritants can help prevent allergic or irritant conjunctivitis.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:245:"हाथों की स्वच्छता बनाए रखना, आंखों को रगड़ने से बचना और संक्रमण से बचाव जोखिम को कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:273:"Seek urgent eye assessment for severe eye pain, significant sensitivity to light, reduced or blurred vision, marked swelling, injury or chemical exposure, or rapidly worsening symptoms. These features may indicate a condition more serious than uncomplicated conjunctivitis.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:353;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:366;s:10:"disease_id";i:19;s:11:"overview_en";s:460:"Dry eye syndrome occurs when the eyes do not produce enough tears or when tears evaporate too quickly or do not provide adequate protection for the eye surface. Tears are important for keeping the eyes moist, comfortable, and protected. Dry eye can cause burning, irritation, a gritty sensation, redness, blurred vision, or excessive watering. Symptoms may be temporary or persistent and can be influenced by environmental conditions and other health problems.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:328:"ड्राई आई सिंड्रोम तब होता है जब आंखें पर्याप्त आंसू नहीं बनातीं या आंसू बहुत जल्दी सूख जाते हैं, जिससे असुविधा और जलन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:428:"Dry eye may result from reduced tear production, excessive tear evaporation, or problems with the quality of the tear film. Aging, inflammation of the eyelids, certain eye conditions, previous eye procedures, and some systemic diseases can contribute. Environmental factors such as dry air, wind, smoke, and prolonged visual tasks may worsen symptoms. Some medicines can also affect tear production or contribute to eye dryness.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:305:"बढ़ती उम्र, आंसुओं का कम बनना, पर्यावरणीय कारक, लंबे समय तक स्क्रीन का उपयोग और कुछ दवाएं ड्राई आई का कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:438:"The risk of dry eye tends to increase with age. Other factors include prolonged screen use or activities that reduce blinking, exposure to wind or dry environments, contact lens use, eyelid inflammation, and previous eye or facial surgery. Medical conditions such as Sjogren syndrome, rheumatoid arthritis, and certain other disorders can also be associated with dry eye. Some medicines and hormonal changes may influence tear production.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:244:"अधिक उम्र, ऑटोइम्यून रोग, कॉन्टैक्ट लेंस का उपयोग और अत्यधिक स्क्रीन उपयोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:440:"Diagnosis of dry eye is based on symptoms, examination of the eyes, and assessment of the tear film. An eye care professional may examine the eyelids, conjunctiva, and cornea with a slit lamp. Tests can evaluate tear production, tear stability, or the condition of the eye surface. The Schirmer test is one method used to measure tear production, although additional tests may be needed because dry eye can have several contributing causes.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:234:"निदान में आंसू उत्पादन, आंसू की गुणवत्ता और विस्तृत नेत्र परीक्षण का मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:483:"Dry eye cannot always be prevented, particularly when it is related to aging, medical conditions, or changes in tear production. Limiting exposure to smoke, wind, and very dry air may reduce irritation. Taking regular breaks during prolonged screen use can encourage normal blinking. Proper contact lens care and attention to eyelid hygiene may also help. People with persistent symptoms should have their eyes evaluated so that contributing conditions can be identified and managed.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:293:"स्क्रीन उपयोग के दौरान विराम लेना, आंखों को नम रखना और शुष्क वातावरण से बचाव लक्षणों को रोकने में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:226:"Dry eye syndrome usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt eye assessment for sudden vision changes, significant eye pain, marked redness, light sensitivity, or symptoms following an eye injury or chemical exposure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:354;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:367;s:10:"disease_id";i:20;s:11:"overview_en";s:390:"Macular degeneration is a condition that damages the macula, the central part of the retina responsible for sharp, detailed vision. It can cause blurred or distorted central vision and difficulty reading, recognizing faces, or performing tasks requiring fine detail. Age-related macular degeneration is the most common form and may develop gradually or progress more rapidly in some people.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:330:"मैक्यूलर डिजनरेशन एक नेत्र रोग है जो रेटिना के केंद्रीय भाग को प्रभावित करता है और धीरे-धीरे केंद्रीय दृष्टि को कम कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:387:"Macular degeneration results from changes and damage involving the macula and the tissues that support it. In age-related disease, abnormal deposits and changes in retinal cells can impair vision. Some people develop abnormal blood vessels that leak fluid or blood beneath the retina. The exact mechanisms are complex and involve aging, genetic susceptibility, and environmental factors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:279:"रेटिना में उम्र संबंधी परिवर्तन, आनुवंशिक कारक और असामान्य रक्त वाहिका वृद्धि इस रोग में योगदान देते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:391:"Risk factors include increasing age, family history of macular degeneration, cigarette smoking, cardiovascular risk factors, and certain dietary and lifestyle factors. Genetic susceptibility can influence the likelihood of developing the disease. Having disease in one eye also increases the importance of monitoring the other eye. Smoking is a particularly important modifiable risk factor.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:200:"बढ़ती उम्र, धूम्रपान, मोटापा, पारिवारिक इतिहास और हृदय रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:412:"Macular degeneration is diagnosed through a comprehensive eye examination that includes examination of the retina and macula. Visual acuity testing and retinal imaging such as optical coherence tomography can identify structural changes. Fluorescein angiography or other imaging may be used when abnormal blood vessels are suspected. An Amsler grid may help detect changes in central vision between examinations.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:216:"निदान में रेटिना परीक्षण, ऑप्टिकल कोहेरेंस टोमोग्राफी और इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:468:"The risk of macular degeneration may be reduced by not smoking, eating a balanced diet rich in vegetables and other nutrient-dense foods, maintaining healthy blood pressure and cholesterol levels, exercising regularly, and protecting overall cardiovascular health. Regular eye examinations are important, particularly with increasing age or a family history. People with existing disease should follow their eye specialist’s monitoring and treatment recommendations.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:248:"स्वस्थ आहार, धूम्रपान से बचाव और नियमित नेत्र जांच रोग की प्रगति को कम करने में मदद कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:280:"Seek prompt eye assessment for sudden or rapidly worsening central vision loss, new distortion of straight lines, a new blind or blurred area in central vision, or other sudden changes in sight. Sudden vision changes should not be assumed to be part of usual macular degeneration.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:355;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:368;s:10:"disease_id";i:21;s:11:"overview_en";s:377:"Diabetic retinopathy is an eye condition caused by damage to the small blood vessels in the retina after prolonged or poorly controlled diabetes. It may begin without noticeable symptoms and can progress to blurred vision, floaters, bleeding, retinal detachment, or vision loss. Regular eye examinations can detect retinal changes early and help prevent severe vision problems.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:332:"डायबिटिक रेटिनोपैथी मधुमेह की एक जटिलता है जो रेटिना की रक्त वाहिकाओं को नुकसान पहुंचाती है और दृष्टि हानि का कारण बन सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:387:"Diabetic retinopathy develops when persistently high blood glucose damages the blood vessels that supply the retina. The damaged vessels may leak fluid or blood, or they may become blocked, causing areas of the retina to receive too little oxygen. In advanced disease, abnormal new blood vessels can grow and bleed. Longer duration of diabetes and poor glucose control increase the risk.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:215:"लंबे समय तक उच्च रक्त शर्करा स्तर रेटिना की रक्त वाहिकाओं को नुकसान पहुंचाते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:376:"Risk factors include having diabetes for many years, consistently high blood glucose levels, high blood pressure, abnormal cholesterol levels, pregnancy in someone with diabetes, smoking, and kidney disease. The risk generally increases as diabetes continues over time. Poor control of blood glucose, blood pressure, and cholesterol can accelerate retinal blood-vessel damage.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:248:"अनियंत्रित मधुमेह, उच्च रक्तचाप, गुर्दे की बीमारी और लंबे समय तक मधुमेह रहना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:390:"Diabetic retinopathy is diagnosed through a comprehensive eye examination. An eye specialist examines the retina and optic nerve for leaking blood vessels, swelling, abnormal vessel growth, and other retinal changes. Dilated retinal examination, retinal photography, optical coherence tomography, and sometimes fluorescein angiography may be used to assess the severity and guide treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:216:"निदान में विस्तारित नेत्र परीक्षण, रेटिना इमेजिंग और दृष्टि मूल्यांकन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:431:"The risk of diabetic retinopathy can be reduced by keeping blood glucose, blood pressure, and cholesterol within recommended ranges. Regular comprehensive dilated eye examinations are important even when vision seems normal. Taking prescribed diabetes medicines, following recommended lifestyle measures, avoiding smoking, and promptly addressing changes in vision can help reduce the risk of severe retinal damage and vision loss.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:232:"रक्त शर्करा नियंत्रण, रक्तचाप प्रबंधन और नियमित नेत्र जांच महत्वपूर्ण रोकथाम उपाय हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:281:"Seek urgent eye assessment for sudden vision loss, a sudden increase in floaters, flashes of light, dark areas or a curtain-like shadow across the vision, or rapidly worsening visual changes. These symptoms may indicate bleeding or retinal complications requiring prompt treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:356;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:369;s:10:"disease_id";i:22;s:11:"overview_en";s:381:"Retinal detachment occurs when the retina separates from the tissues that support it at the back of the eye. It is a serious eye condition that can cause sudden flashes of light, a sudden increase in floaters, a shadow or curtain across the field of vision, or loss of vision. Prompt medical treatment is important because prolonged separation can permanently damage retinal cells.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:336:"रेटिनल डिटैचमेंट एक गंभीर नेत्र स्थिति है जिसमें रेटिना अपनी आधारभूत परत से अलग हो जाती है, जिससे स्थायी दृष्टि हानि हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:409:"Retinal detachment may occur when a retinal tear or hole allows fluid to pass underneath the retina and separate it from the underlying tissue. It can also develop when scar tissue pulls on the retina or when fluid accumulates beneath it without a tear. Aging-related changes in the vitreous, eye injury, previous eye surgery, severe nearsightedness, and certain retinal disorders can increase susceptibility.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:259:"आंख की चोट, रेटिना में फटना, अत्यधिक निकट दृष्टि दोष और उम्र संबंधी परिवर्तन इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:399:"Risk factors include increasing age, severe nearsightedness, previous cataract or other eye surgery, previous retinal detachment in either eye, significant eye injury, and a family history of retinal detachment. Certain retinal disorders and conditions that cause abnormal blood-vessel growth or scarring can also increase risk. The presence of some risk factors does not mean detachment will occur.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:234:"पूर्व नेत्र शल्यक्रिया, गंभीर मायोपिया, पारिवारिक इतिहास और आंख की चोट जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:401:"Retinal detachment is diagnosed through an urgent dilated eye examination. An ophthalmologist examines the retina for tears, holes, bleeding, or separation from the underlying tissue. Ultrasound imaging of the eye may be used when the retina cannot be seen clearly, such as when there is significant bleeding or clouding of the eye. The extent and location of the detachment guide treatment decisions.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:205:"निदान विस्तृत रेटिना परीक्षण और विशेष इमेजिंग जांच के माध्यम से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:434:"Some retinal detachments cannot be prevented, but prompt treatment of retinal tears or holes can prevent certain detachments from developing. People at increased risk should follow recommended eye examinations. Wearing appropriate eye protection during activities that could cause eye injury can reduce trauma-related risk. Sudden flashes, a new shower of floaters, or a curtain-like shadow in vision require immediate eye evaluation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:332:"रेटिना में फटने का समय पर उपचार और उच्च जोखिम वाले व्यक्तियों में नियमित निगरानी रेटिनल डिटैचमेंट को रोकने में मदद कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:295:"Retinal detachment is an eye emergency. Seek immediate ophthalmic or emergency medical care for sudden flashes of light, a sudden increase in floaters, a dark curtain or shadow across the field of vision, or sudden loss or distortion of vision. Prompt treatment can help protect remaining sight.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 01:53:42";}i:357;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:370;s:10:"disease_id";i:23;s:11:"overview_en";s:425:"Color blindness is a condition in which a person has difficulty distinguishing certain colors or perceiving colors in the usual way. The most common forms involve difficulty distinguishing red and green, while less common forms affect blue and yellow or cause very limited color vision. Color vision deficiency is often inherited, but it can also result from eye disease, neurological conditions, aging, or certain medicines.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:328:"कलर ब्लाइंडनेस एक दृष्टि विकार है जिसमें व्यक्ति कुछ रंगों, विशेषकर लाल और हरे रंग, के बीच अंतर करने में कठिनाई अनुभव करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:412:"Inherited color vision deficiency usually results from genetic changes affecting the light-sensitive cone cells of the retina or the visual pathways that process color information. The condition may be present from birth and is more common in males for some inherited forms. Acquired color vision changes can result from retinal or optic-nerve disease, brain disorders, eye injury, aging, or certain medications.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:255:"रेटिना की रंग-संवेदनशील कोशिकाओं को प्रभावित करने वाले आनुवंशिक दोष इसका सबसे सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:393:"The main risk factor for inherited color blindness is a family history of color vision deficiency. Some inherited forms are associated with genes located on the X chromosome and therefore occur more frequently in males. Acquired color vision problems may be associated with aging, diabetes, eye disease, neurological disease, eye injury, or medicines that affect the retina or visual pathways.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:201:"पुरुष लिंग, पारिवारिक इतिहास, कुछ नेत्र रोग और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ा सकती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:421:"Color blindness is diagnosed with color vision tests that require a person to identify or arrange colored patterns. Ishihara-type plates are commonly used to detect red-green color deficiency, while other tests can assess different types and severity of color vision loss. An eye examination may be recommended when color vision changes develop later in life or when an acquired eye or neurological disorder is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:244:"निदान इशिहारा प्लेट जैसे रंग दृष्टि परीक्षणों और विशेष नेत्र जांच के माध्यम से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:497:"Inherited color blindness cannot currently be prevented because it results from genetic factors. Acquired color vision changes may sometimes be reduced by preventing or treating underlying eye and neurological conditions and by avoiding unnecessary exposure to substances that can damage vision. Regular eye examinations can help detect other eye problems. People with known color vision deficiency can use labels, technology, and other visual aids when accurate color identification is important.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:293:"वंशानुगत कलर ब्लाइंडनेस को आमतौर पर रोका नहीं जा सकता, लेकिन शीघ्र पहचान अनुकूलन और प्रबंधन में सहायता करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:306:"Color blindness usually does not require urgent medical care. Seek prompt eye assessment if color vision changes suddenly, particularly when accompanied by blurred vision, eye pain, flashes, new floaters, or other changes in sight, because sudden changes may indicate another eye or neurological condition.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:358;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:371;s:10:"disease_id";i:24;s:11:"overview_en";s:382:"Uveitis is inflammation of the uvea, the middle layer of the eye that includes the iris, ciliary body, and choroid. It can cause eye redness, pain, light sensitivity, blurred vision, floaters, or reduced vision. Uveitis may affect one or both eyes and can develop suddenly or gradually. Without appropriate treatment, inflammation may damage structures of the eye and impair vision.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:265:"यूवाइटिस आंख की मध्य परत (यूविया) की सूजन है, जिससे दर्द, लालिमा और दृष्टि संबंधी समस्याएं हो सकती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:420:"Uveitis can result from infections, autoimmune or inflammatory diseases, eye injuries, and other conditions. Sometimes no specific cause is identified. Inflammatory disorders affecting other parts of the body can trigger inflammation inside the eye. Infections such as certain viral, bacterial, parasitic, or fungal infections can also cause uveitis. The cause often depends on the type and location of the inflammation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:204:"ऑटोइम्यून रोग, संक्रमण, आंख की चोट और सूजन संबंधी विकार इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:397:"Risk factors include having an autoimmune or inflammatory disorder, certain infections, previous eye injury or surgery, and in some cases a family or genetic susceptibility to inflammatory disease. Exposure to certain infections may also increase risk. Because uveitis has many possible causes, risk factors vary considerably according to the underlying condition and the part of the eye involved.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:204:"ऑटोइम्यून स्थितियां, संक्रमण, धूम्रपान और पूर्व नेत्र सूजन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:416:"Uveitis is diagnosed through a detailed eye examination, usually by an ophthalmologist. The examination may identify inflammatory cells, redness, swelling, or other changes inside the eye. Visual acuity, pressure measurement, slit-lamp examination, and retinal examination are commonly used. Blood tests, imaging, or other investigations may be needed when an infection or systemic inflammatory disease is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:235:"निदान में नेत्र परीक्षण, इमेजिंग जांच, प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण और मूल कारणों की जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:447:"Uveitis cannot always be prevented because many cases are related to autoimmune conditions or causes that cannot be controlled. Preventing infections through appropriate hygiene, vaccination, and other recommended measures may reduce some infectious causes. People with inflammatory diseases should follow their treatment plans and seek prompt medical attention for eye pain, redness, light sensitivity, floaters, or unexplained changes in vision.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:250:"संक्रमण और सूजन संबंधी रोगों का समय पर उपचार यूवाइटिस की जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:236:"Uveitis requires prompt medical assessment because untreated inflammation can threaten vision. Seek urgent eye care for eye pain, marked redness, light sensitivity, blurred or reduced vision, new floaters, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:359;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:372;s:10:"disease_id";i:25;s:11:"overview_en";s:337:"A corneal ulcer is an open sore or area of damage on the cornea, the clear front surface of the eye. It can cause eye pain, redness, discharge, sensitivity to light, blurred vision, and other visual problems. Corneal ulcers can progress rapidly in some cases and may cause permanent scarring or vision impairment if treatment is delayed.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:331:"कॉर्नियल अल्सर कॉर्निया पर बनने वाला घाव है जो दर्द, लालिमा, स्राव और दृष्टि हानि का कारण बन सकता है यदि समय पर उपचार न किया जाए।";s:9:"causes_en";s:414:"Bacterial, viral, fungal, and parasitic infections are common causes of corneal ulcers. Eye injuries can damage the protective surface of the cornea and allow infection to develop. Improper contact lens use, including wearing lenses for too long or failing to maintain proper hygiene, can also increase risk. Other eye-surface disorders or conditions that reduce the normal protection of the cornea may contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:360:"बैक्टीरियल, वायरल, फंगल या परजीवी संक्रमण इसके सामान्य कारण हैं। आंख की चोट और गलत तरीके से कॉन्टैक्ट लेंस का उपयोग भी योगदान कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:373:"Improper contact lens use is an important risk factor for corneal ulcers. Eye trauma, poor eye hygiene, and conditions that weaken the immune system can also increase risk. Previous eye disease or damage to the corneal surface may make infection more likely. People who wear contact lenses should follow appropriate cleaning, storage, replacement, and wearing instructions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:242:"कॉन्टैक्ट लेंस का गलत उपयोग, आंख की चोट, खराब स्वच्छता और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:456:"Diagnosis of a corneal ulcer usually involves a detailed eye examination, including slit-lamp examination of the cornea. Special staining may be used to make an ulcer or area of corneal damage easier to identify. When infection is suspected, a sample from the affected area may be examined or sent for laboratory testing to help identify the organism responsible. The findings help determine appropriate treatment and assess the severity of corneal damage.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:258:"निदान में स्लिट-लैम्प परीक्षण, कॉर्नियल स्टेनिंग और कॉर्नियल नमूनों की प्रयोगशाला जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:430:"Proper contact lens hygiene can reduce the risk of corneal ulcers. Contact lenses should be handled, cleaned, stored, and replaced according to professional instructions, and they should not be used inappropriately. Protecting the eyes from injury, maintaining good eye hygiene, and seeking prompt treatment for eye infections can also reduce risk. New eye pain, redness, discharge, or vision changes should be evaluated promptly.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:336:"कॉन्टैक्ट लेंस की उचित स्वच्छता, आंखों के संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार और आंखों की सुरक्षा कॉर्नियल अल्सर की रोकथाम में मदद करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:287:"A corneal ulcer can threaten vision and requires urgent eye care. Seek immediate assessment for significant eye pain, redness, light sensitivity, blurred or reduced vision, discharge, a visible white spot on the cornea, or rapidly worsening symptoms, especially in a contact lens wearer.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:360;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:373;s:10:"disease_id";i:26;s:11:"overview_en";s:339:"Otitis media is an infection or inflammation of the middle ear, the space behind the eardrum. It commonly occurs after a cold, respiratory infection, or blockage of the eustachian tube. Symptoms may include ear pain, pressure, fever, irritability, reduced hearing, or fluid behind the eardrum. Children are affected more often than adults.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:322:"ओटाइटिस मीडिया मध्य कान का संक्रमण या सूजन है, जो बच्चों में अधिक सामान्य है और अक्सर सर्दी या श्वसन संक्रमण के बाद होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:382:"Otitis media commonly develops when the eustachian tube becomes swollen or blocked during a cold, respiratory infection, or allergy. This prevents normal drainage and ventilation of the middle ear, allowing fluid to accumulate. Viruses are a common cause, and bacteria can also infect the trapped fluid. Repeated infections may occur when the eustachian tubes do not drain normally.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:211:"मध्य कान को प्रभावित करने वाले बैक्टीरियल या वायरल संक्रमण इसके मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:347:"Risk factors include young age, frequent colds or respiratory infections, exposure to tobacco smoke, attending group child care, seasonal allergies, and structural problems affecting the eustachian tubes. Bottle feeding while lying down may also increase risk in infants. A history of repeated ear infections can make further episodes more likely.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:253:"कम उम्र, बार-बार सर्दी होना, एलर्जी, तंबाकू के धुएं का संपर्क और डे-केयर में रहना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:352:"Otitis media is diagnosed from symptoms and an examination of the ear. A healthcare professional uses an otoscope to look for a red, swollen, or bulging eardrum and fluid behind it. Pneumatic otoscopy or tympanometry may help determine whether fluid is present. Hearing testing may be recommended when infections are recurrent or hearing loss persists.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:209:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण और ओटोस्कोप द्वारा कान की जांच के माध्यम से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:421:"Some cases of otitis media can be reduced by preventing respiratory infections and limiting exposure to tobacco smoke. Keeping vaccinations up to date, including recommended influenza and pneumococcal vaccines, can reduce certain infections associated with ear disease. Breastfeeding during infancy may also lower risk. Children with recurrent infections may need evaluation for contributing factors and persistent fluid.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:208:"टीकाकरण, अच्छी स्वच्छता, स्तनपान और तंबाकू के धुएं से बचाव जोखिम कम कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:312:"Seek prompt medical assessment for severe or worsening ear pain, high fever, significant swelling behind the ear, dizziness, new hearing loss, facial weakness, severe headache, or symptoms that are rapidly worsening. Infants who appear very unwell or unusually difficult to wake should receive urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:361;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:374;s:10:"disease_id";i:27;s:11:"overview_en";s:425:"Otitis externa, commonly called swimmer’s ear, is inflammation or infection of the outer ear and ear canal. It may develop suddenly or persist as a chronic problem. Bacterial infection is a common cause, particularly after water remains in the ear canal, although fungi and other causes are possible. Symptoms can include ear pain, itching, redness, swelling, drainage and discomfort when the outer ear is touched or moved.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:253:"ओटाइटिस एक्सटर्ना या स्विमर्स ईयर बाहरी कान नली का संक्रमण है, जिससे दर्द, खुजली और सूजन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:490:"Otitis externa commonly develops when bacteria enter and multiply in the ear canal, especially when moisture remains after swimming. Swimming in contaminated water can increase exposure to bacteria. Scratching the ear or damaging the skin with cotton swabs, fingernails or other objects can make infection more likely. Foreign objects may also injure the ear canal. Less commonly, fungal infection or an allergic reaction to substances placed in the ear can cause external ear inflammation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:190:"बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण, अत्यधिक नमी और कान नली की चोट इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:392:"Risk factors include frequent swimming, exposure to contaminated water, moisture trapped in the ear canal and repeated irritation or injury to the canal skin. Cleaning the ears with cotton swabs or inserting other objects can damage the protective skin and increase risk. People with chronic skin conditions or allergies affecting the ear may also develop recurrent external ear inflammation.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:226:"बार-बार तैरना, आर्द्र वातावरण, कान की चोट और गलत तरीके से कान साफ करना जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:490:"Otitis externa is usually diagnosed from symptoms and examination of the outer ear and ear canal. The healthcare provider looks for redness, swelling, scaling, discharge or other signs of inflammation and infection. Pain when the outer ear is moved may support the diagnosis. Ear drainage may occasionally be tested when an infection does not improve or when the cause is uncertain. The examination also helps distinguish otitis externa from middle-ear disease and other causes of ear pain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:163:"निदान लक्षणों और बाहरी कान नली की जांच के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:509:"Keep the ears dry after swimming or bathing and avoid swimming in polluted water. Do not insert cotton swabs, fingernails or other objects into the ear canal because they can damage the skin. People who frequently develop swimmer’s ear may be advised by a healthcare provider about appropriate ear-drying measures. Hair sprays and dyes should be kept out of the ear canal. If an external ear infection develops, complete the recommended treatment to reduce the chance of persistent or more severe infection.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:270:"कानों को सूखा रखना, कान में वस्तुएं डालने से बचना और स्वच्छता बनाए रखना संक्रमण से बचाव में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:270:"Seek prompt medical assessment for severe or rapidly worsening ear pain, fever, swelling around the ear, discharge that is worsening, hearing loss, dizziness, or facial weakness. People with diabetes or weakened immune systems may require particularly prompt evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:362;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:375;s:10:"disease_id";i:28;s:11:"overview_en";s:470:"Tinnitus is the perception of sound in one or both ears when there is no corresponding outside source. It is commonly described as ringing but may also sound like buzzing, hissing, roaring, humming, whistling or other noises. Tinnitus may be temporary or persistent and can occur with hearing loss or other ear problems. Persistent or recurrent tinnitus may interfere with concentration or sleep and can sometimes indicate an underlying medical or ear-related condition.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:297:"टिनिटस ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें व्यक्ति को बिना बाहरी ध्वनि के कानों में घंटी, भनभनाहट या अन्य आवाजें सुनाई देती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:505:"Tinnitus can occur with many ear and hearing disorders. Possible causes include hearing loss, ear infections, earwax or foreign objects in the ear, Ménière disease and problems involving the eustachian tube. Certain medicines can also cause ear noises. Tinnitus may occur with head injury, temporomandibular joint problems, thyroid disorders, diabetes, anemia, high blood pressure or allergies. In uncommon cases, persistent tinnitus may be associated with a tumor, aneurysm or another vascular problem.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:300:"सुनने की क्षमता में कमी, तेज आवाज का संपर्क, कान के रोग, दवाएं और न्यूरोलॉजिकल स्थितियां टिनिटस का कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:507:"Risk factors include hearing loss, repeated exposure to loud sounds, ear infections, earwax buildup, head injury and disorders affecting the inner or middle ear. Some medicines can increase the likelihood of tinnitus. Smoking, alcohol and caffeine may make tinnitus more noticeable in some people. Other associated conditions include temporomandibular joint disorder, diabetes, thyroid disease and obesity. Older adults and people with significant hearing impairment may also experience tinnitus more often.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:196:"बढ़ती उम्र, तेज आवाज का संपर्क, कान के संक्रमण और हृदय रोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:551:"Evaluation of tinnitus begins with a medical history and examination of the ears and hearing. Audiometry may be performed to determine whether hearing loss is present. Depending on the pattern of symptoms, additional testing may include CT or MRI of the head or tests of blood vessels. Particular attention is given to tinnitus that is persistent in one ear, pulsatile, associated with hearing loss or accompanied by dizziness or other neurological symptoms. Finding and treating an underlying cause may reduce or eliminate the tinnitus in some cases.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:200:"निदान में श्रवण परीक्षण, चिकित्सा इतिहास की समीक्षा और कान की जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:551:"Protecting hearing from excessive noise can reduce the risk of noise-related tinnitus. Use appropriate hearing protection around loud machinery, concerts and other intense sounds, and avoid prolonged exposure to loud music. Prompt treatment of ear conditions and avoiding unnecessary injury to the ear canal may also help. Limiting factors that make tinnitus worse, such as smoking, alcohol or excessive caffeine, may be useful for people who already experience tinnitus. Regular management of underlying health and hearing problems is also important.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:190:"तेज आवाज से श्रवण की सुरक्षा और कान के रोगों का उपचार जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:268:"Seek urgent medical assessment for tinnitus that begins suddenly, especially when it occurs in one ear with sudden hearing loss, severe dizziness, weakness, or other neurological symptoms. Pulsing tinnitus that matches the heartbeat should also be medically evaluated.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:363;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:376;s:10:"disease_id";i:29;s:11:"overview_en";s:539:"Hearing loss is partial or complete inability to hear sounds in one or both ears. It may develop gradually or occur suddenly and can result from problems in the outer or middle ear, damage to the inner ear or auditory nerve, certain diseases, medications, injuries or prolonged exposure to loud sound. Conductive hearing loss occurs when sound cannot reach the inner ear normally, while sensorineural hearing loss results from damage to the inner ear or nerve pathways. Some forms can be treated or reversed, while others may be permanent.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:290:"श्रवण हानि ध्वनियों को सुनने की क्षमता में आंशिक या पूर्ण कमी है और यह एक या दोनों कानों को प्रभावित कर सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:571:"Hearing loss has many possible causes. Conductive loss can result from earwax buildup, fluid behind the eardrum, foreign objects, a damaged eardrum or problems with the small bones of the middle ear. Sensorineural loss can result from aging, prolonged loud-noise exposure, infections such as meningitis or mumps, certain medicines, Ménière disease, head injury and other disorders affecting the inner ear or auditory nerve. Hearing loss can also be present at birth because of genetic conditions, birth defects or infections passed from mother to baby during pregnancy.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:238:"बढ़ती उम्र, तेज आवाज का संपर्क, संक्रमण, आनुवंशिक विकार और कान की चोट इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:526:"Risk factors include increasing age, repeated exposure to loud music or workplace noise, certain infections, head or ear injuries, some medicines that can damage hearing, genetic conditions and a family history of hearing loss. Ear infections and conditions that block the ear canal or middle ear can contribute to conductive hearing loss. Smoking and certain medical conditions may also contribute to age-related hearing changes. The risk from noise increases with both the loudness of the sound and the duration of exposure.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:234:"अधिक उम्र, लंबे समय तक तेज आवाज का संपर्क, पारिवारिक इतिहास और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:553:"Evaluation of hearing loss begins with a medical history and examination of the ears. A healthcare provider may use an otoscope to look for earwax, infection, fluid or abnormalities of the eardrum. Audiometric testing measures the type and degree of hearing loss and can distinguish conductive from sensorineural problems. Tympanometry may evaluate middle-ear function. CT or MRI may be used when a tumor, fracture or another structural problem is suspected. Additional evaluation by an audiologist or ear, nose and throat specialist may be appropriate.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:188:"निदान में श्रवण परीक्षण, ऑडियोमेट्री और विस्तृत कान परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:562:"Some forms of hearing loss can be prevented by protecting the ears from excessive noise. Avoid prolonged exposure to loud music, machinery and other intense sounds, and use appropriate earplugs or earmuffs in noisy environments. Keep personal listening devices at safer volume levels and take breaks from prolonged listening. Promptly treating ear problems and avoiding insertion of objects into the ear canal can reduce some preventable causes. People exposed to occupational noise should follow workplace hearing-protection and hearing-testing recommendations.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:308:"श्रवण सुरक्षा उपकरणों का उपयोग, तेज आवाज से बचाव और कान के रोगों का समय पर उपचार श्रवण हानि को रोकने में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:288:"Sudden hearing loss, particularly in one ear, requires urgent medical assessment because early treatment may be important. Seek prompt care for rapidly worsening hearing, hearing loss with severe dizziness, neurological symptoms, significant ear pain, or symptoms following a head injury.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:364;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:377;s:10:"disease_id";i:30;s:11:"overview_en";s:581:"Meniere disease is a disorder of the inner ear that can cause repeated episodes of vertigo, fluctuating hearing loss, ringing in the ear, and a feeling of pressure or fullness in the affected ear. Episodes can vary in frequency and severity and may interfere with daily activities. Attacks of Meniere disease may begin suddenly and can last from several minutes to several hours. Hearing may fluctuate, particularly at lower frequencies, and tinnitus or ear pressure may accompany vertigo. Repeated attacks can affect balance, confidence, work, driving, and other daily activities.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:278:"मेनीयर रोग आंतरिक कान का एक विकार है जिसमें चक्कर आना, श्रवण हानि, टिनिटस और कान में भरेपन का अनुभव होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:654:"The exact cause of Meniere disease is not known. The condition is associated with abnormal buildup or regulation of fluid in the inner ear. Factors that may contribute include abnormal fluid balance, immune-related mechanisms, genetic susceptibility, viral infections, allergies, or other environmental influences. Abnormal regulation of the fluid within the inner-ear structures is one leading explanation for Meniere disease. Increased pressure or altered fluid composition may interfere with the structures responsible for hearing and balance. The precise mechanism remains uncertain, and several biological factors may contribute in different people.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:174:"आंतरिक कान में असामान्य द्रव संचय को इसका मुख्य कारण माना जाता है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:600:"Risk factors may include a family history of Meniere disease, certain immune or allergy-related conditions, migraine, and possible abnormalities affecting inner-ear fluid regulation. The condition can occur at any age but is most often diagnosed in adults. A family history can increase susceptibility, suggesting that genetic factors may play a role. Some people with migraine, autoimmune disorders, allergies, or other inner-ear problems may have overlapping risk factors. Stress, fatigue, and dietary or fluid-related factors are sometimes reported as triggers for attacks, although triggers vary.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:211:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, ऑटोइम्यून विकार, एलर्जी और वायरल संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:634:"Diagnosis is based on the pattern of repeated vertigo episodes together with hearing symptoms, tinnitus, or a feeling of fullness in the ear. Hearing tests are commonly performed. Additional tests or imaging may be used to exclude other conditions that can cause similar symptoms. Hearing assessment can document sensorineural hearing loss and provide a baseline for future comparison. Vestibular testing may be used in selected cases to evaluate balance-system function. MRI or other investigations may be recommended when symptoms are unusual or when conditions such as a brain tumor or other inner-ear disorder need to be excluded.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:195:"निदान में श्रवण परीक्षण, संतुलन परीक्षण और लक्षणों का मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:678:"Because the exact cause of Meniere disease is unknown, there is no proven way to prevent it completely. People with the condition may reduce symptom triggers by following their healthcare professional's recommendations, taking prescribed treatment, and identifying factors that appear to worsen episodes. People who experience recurrent attacks can keep a symptom diary to identify personal triggers and discuss them with their clinician. Following prescribed treatment, maintaining regular sleep, and managing conditions such as migraine or allergies may help some individuals. Avoiding known personal triggers is more useful than assuming that one trigger applies to everyone.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:221:"नमक का सेवन कम करना, तनाव प्रबंधन और समय पर उपचार हमलों को कम करने में मदद कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:287:"Seek urgent medical attention for a sudden change in hearing, severe or prolonged vertigo, fainting, new weakness or numbness, difficulty speaking, severe headache, or other neurological symptoms. New symptoms that differ substantially from previous episodes should be assessed promptly.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:365;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:378;s:10:"disease_id";i:31;s:11:"overview_en";s:379:"Labyrinthitis is inflammation of the inner ear structures involved in hearing and balance. It can cause sudden dizziness or vertigo, problems with balance, nausea, vomiting, and sometimes hearing loss or ringing in the ear. Symptoms may begin abruptly and can be severe. The condition is often associated with an infection or another inflammatory process affecting the inner ear.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:361:"लैबिरिन्थाइटिस आंतरिक कान की संरचनाओं की सूजन है जो संतुलन और श्रवण के लिए जिम्मेदार होती हैं, जिससे चक्कर और श्रवण समस्याएं हो सकती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:393:"Labyrinthitis may occur after a viral infection and less commonly after a bacterial infection. Inflammation can affect the delicate inner-ear structures responsible for hearing and balance. In some cases, the symptoms may be related to another inflammatory or autoimmune condition. Bacterial infection involving nearby ear structures can be more serious and requires prompt medical assessment.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:221:"वायरल संक्रमण इसका सबसे सामान्य कारण है, हालांकि बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण भी हो सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:388:"Risk factors may include a recent viral respiratory infection, another ear infection, or inflammation affecting the inner ear. People with conditions that increase susceptibility to infection may have a higher risk of complications. Certain inflammatory or autoimmune disorders can also be associated with inner-ear inflammation. A history of ear disease may contribute to susceptibility.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:196:"हाल का श्वसन संक्रमण, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा और कान के संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:418:"Labyrinthitis is diagnosed from the pattern of dizziness, balance problems, hearing symptoms, and medical history together with an examination. The ears and nervous system are assessed to look for other causes of vertigo. Hearing tests may be performed when hearing loss is present. Additional balance testing or brain imaging may be needed when symptoms are severe, unusual, or suggest another neurological condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:238:"निदान लक्षणों, श्रवण मूल्यांकन, संतुलन परीक्षण और चिकित्सा इतिहास के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:412:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent labyrinthitis, but reducing the risk of infections may help. Good hand hygiene, avoiding close contact with people who have contagious respiratory infections, and keeping recommended vaccinations up to date can reduce some infectious triggers. Prompt treatment of significant ear infections and medical assessment of sudden hearing loss or severe vertigo are also important.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:193:"संक्रमण की रोकथाम और कान व श्वसन रोगों का समय पर उपचार जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:269:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe or sudden dizziness accompanied by weakness, numbness, difficulty speaking, double vision, severe headache, inability to walk safely, fainting, or other neurological symptoms. Sudden hearing loss also requires prompt assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:366;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:379;s:10:"disease_id";i:32;s:11:"overview_en";s:387:"Earwax impaction occurs when earwax builds up and blocks the ear canal. Earwax is normally produced by glands in the ear and helps protect the ear canal by trapping dust and other particles. Normally it moves outward naturally. When too much wax accumulates or becomes difficult to remove, it can cause hearing loss, a feeling of fullness, ear discomfort, ringing, itching, or dizziness.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:355:"ईयरवैक्स इम्पैक्शन तब होता है जब अत्यधिक कान का मैल जमा होकर कान की नली को अवरुद्ध कर देता है, जिससे असुविधा और सुनने में कठिनाई होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:362:"Earwax impaction can occur when the ear produces a large amount of wax or when wax cannot move naturally out of the ear canal. Using cotton swabs, hearing aids, earplugs, or other objects can push wax deeper into the canal. Narrow or unusually shaped ear canals can also make wax accumulation more likely. Repeated attempts to clean the ears can worsen blockage.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:217:"कान के मैल का अधिक बनना, संकरी कान नली और गलत सफाई विधियां अवरोध का कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:349:"People who use hearing aids or earplugs may be more likely to develop earwax blockage. Narrow or unusually shaped ear canals can interfere with normal wax removal. Frequent use of cotton swabs or other objects inside the ear canal can push wax deeper and increase the risk of impaction. Older adults may also be more prone to harder or drier earwax.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:220:"कॉटन स्वैब का उपयोग, श्रवण यंत्र और प्राकृतिक रूप से संकरी कान नली जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:353:"Earwax impaction is diagnosed by examining the ear canal with an otoscope or another lighted instrument. The healthcare provider can usually see the accumulated wax and determine whether it is blocking the canal. Hearing tests may be performed when hearing loss persists after the wax is removed or when another cause of hearing difficulty is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:175:"निदान ओटोस्कोप द्वारा कान की नली की जांच के माध्यम से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:406:"The ears usually clean themselves naturally, so routine insertion of cotton swabs or other objects into the ear canal is not recommended. Avoid pushing objects into the ears because this can compact wax and injure the ear canal or eardrum. People who repeatedly develop earwax blockage, especially those using hearing aids, should ask a healthcare professional about safe methods of prevention and removal.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:203:"कान में वस्तुएं डालने से बचें और आवश्यकता होने पर विशेषज्ञ से कान साफ करवाएं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:279:"Earwax impaction usually does not require emergency care. Seek medical assessment for sudden or severe hearing loss, significant ear pain, drainage, bleeding, dizziness, or symptoms after inserting an object into the ear. Do not attempt to remove impacted wax with sharp objects.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:367;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:380;s:10:"disease_id";i:33;s:11:"overview_en";s:410:"Otosclerosis is an abnormal growth of bone in the middle ear that can cause progressive hearing loss. The abnormal bone interferes with normal movement of the small bones that transmit sound through the middle ear. The condition commonly begins in early or middle adulthood and may affect one or both ears. Some people also experience tinnitus or dizziness. Hearing loss can gradually worsen without treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:354:"ओटोस्क्लेरोसिस एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें मध्य कान में असामान्य हड्डी वृद्धि ध्वनि संचरण में बाधा डालती है और श्रवण हानि का कारण बनती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:346:"The exact cause of otosclerosis is not known. The condition appears to involve abnormal remodeling and growth of sponge-like bone within the middle ear. It may run in families, indicating that genetic factors contribute in some people. The abnormal bone can interfere with movement of the stapes and reduce transmission of sound to the inner ear.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:220:"मध्य कान की स्टेप्स हड्डी के आसपास असामान्य हड्डी पुनर्निर्माण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:361:"A family history of hearing loss or otosclerosis is an important risk factor. Otosclerosis commonly begins during early to middle adulthood and occurs more often in women. Pregnancy may influence the course of the condition in some people. Genetic factors appear to contribute because familial cases are recognized. The disease may involve one ear or both ears.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:218:"पारिवारिक इतिहास, महिला लिंग, हार्मोनल कारक और कुछ वायरल संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:426:"Diagnosis involves a hearing evaluation and examination of the ears. Audiometry or other audiology testing can determine the type and severity of hearing loss and help identify a conductive component. A temporal-bone CT scan may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain or when other causes of hearing loss need to be excluded. The clinical history and progression of hearing loss are also considered when making the diagnosis.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:217:"निदान में श्रवण परीक्षण, ऑडियोमेट्री और आवश्यकता पड़ने पर इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:475:"There is no established way to prevent otosclerosis because its exact cause is unknown and inherited factors can contribute. People with a family history of the condition should seek evaluation if hearing loss develops. Regular hearing assessments can help detect progressive hearing changes. Once diagnosed, appropriate monitoring and treatment can help address hearing loss and reduce its impact, although treatment does not necessarily prevent the underlying bone changes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:253:"श्रवण में परिवर्तन की समय पर जांच और उचित चिकित्सा देखभाल जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:277:"Otosclerosis usually develops gradually and does not require emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for sudden or rapidly worsening hearing loss, severe dizziness, significant ear pain, or new neurological symptoms, as these may indicate another condition requiring evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:368;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:381;s:10:"disease_id";i:34;s:11:"overview_en";s:384:"Sinusitis is inflammation or swelling of the tissue lining the sinuses, the air-filled spaces around the nose and face. It can cause nasal congestion, facial pressure or pain, thick nasal discharge, reduced sense of smell, headache, and difficulty breathing through the nose. Sinusitis may occur for a short period or become recurrent or persistent, depending on its underlying cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:275:"साइनसाइटिस साइनस की परत में सूजन है, जिससे नाक बंद होना, चेहरे में दर्द और सांस लेने में कठिनाई हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:462:"Viral respiratory infections are a common cause of sinusitis and may lead to temporary inflammation and blockage of the sinus passages. Bacterial infections can sometimes develop after or alongside a respiratory infection. Allergies can cause swelling of the nasal tissues and interfere with normal sinus drainage. Structural problems such as a deviated nasal septum or nasal polyps can also obstruct drainage and contribute to recurrent or persistent sinusitis.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:252:"वायरल संक्रमण, बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण, एलर्जी और नाक की संरचनात्मक समस्याएं इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:484:"Allergies and asthma can increase the likelihood of sinus inflammation and symptoms. Nasal polyps and other structural problems that interfere with normal drainage can also increase risk. Smoking and exposure to tobacco smoke may irritate the nasal passages and contribute to sinus problems. Frequent respiratory infections can increase the opportunity for sinus inflammation to develop. Individual risk depends on the combination of underlying conditions and environmental exposures.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:217:"एलर्जी, अस्थमा, नाक के पॉलिप्स, धूम्रपान और बार-बार श्वसन संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:444:"Diagnosis of sinusitis is based on the symptoms, duration of illness, and physical examination. A healthcare professional may examine the nose and surrounding areas for signs of inflammation or infection. Nasal endoscopy can provide a closer view of the nasal passages and sinus openings when symptoms are persistent or recurrent. Imaging studies may be used when complications are suspected or when structural problems need further evaluation.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:244:"निदान में शारीरिक परीक्षण, नाक की एंडोस्कोपी, इमेजिंग जांच और लक्षणों का मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:482:"Managing allergies and other conditions that cause nasal inflammation can help reduce the risk of recurrent sinusitis. Avoiding smoking and exposure to tobacco smoke may protect the nasal passages. Good hand hygiene can reduce the spread of respiratory infections, while appropriate treatment of respiratory infections may help prevent complications. People with recurrent symptoms should discuss possible underlying structural or inflammatory causes with a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:314:"एलर्जी का प्रबंधन, धूम्रपान से बचाव, स्वच्छता बनाए रखना और संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार साइनसाइटिस की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:272:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe headache, swelling or redness around the eyes, vision changes, confusion, stiff neck, severe facial swelling, persistent vomiting, or rapidly worsening illness. These symptoms may indicate a complication requiring prompt treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:369;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:382;s:10:"disease_id";i:35;s:11:"overview_en";s:438:"Allergic rhinitis is a group of symptoms affecting the nose and often the eyes after exposure to substances that trigger an allergic response. Common triggers include pollen, dust, mold and animal dander. Seasonal allergic rhinitis, commonly called hay fever, is often caused by pollen from trees, grasses or ragweed. Symptoms can include sneezing, itching, runny or stuffy nose, watery eyes, reduced sense of smell and throat irritation.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:279:"एलर्जिक राइनाइटिस नाक की एलर्जी संबंधी प्रतिक्रिया है, जिससे छींक, नाक बहना, खुजली और नाक बंद होना होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:471:"Allergic rhinitis occurs when the immune system reacts to an allergen such as pollen, mold, dust or animal dander. The allergic response causes release of chemicals such as histamine, leading to inflammation and increased mucus production in the nasal passages. Seasonal symptoms are commonly triggered by airborne pollen from trees, grasses and ragweed. Allergies often run in families, so inherited susceptibility can contribute to the development of allergic rhinitis.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:193:"परागकण, धूल के कण, फफूंदी और पशुओं के बाल जैसे एलर्जन इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:476:"Risk factors include a personal or family history of allergies, repeated exposure to pollen, dust mites, mold or animal dander, and living or working in environments where these allergens are common. Seasonal exposure is particularly important for hay fever. The amount of pollen in the air can influence symptoms, with higher pollen levels often occurring on hot, dry and windy days. People with other allergic conditions may also be more likely to develop allergic rhinitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:231:"एलर्जी का पारिवारिक इतिहास, अस्थमा और एलर्जन के लगातार संपर्क में रहना जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:493:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history and physical examination. The healthcare provider may ask when symptoms occur, whether they vary by season and whether they are associated with exposure to pets, dust or other allergens. Allergy testing can identify specific triggers. Skin testing is commonly used, while blood tests measuring allergy-related antibodies may be used when skin testing is not appropriate. An eosinophil count may also provide supporting information in some cases.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:193:"निदान लक्षणों, एलर्जी परीक्षण और चिकित्सा इतिहास के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:523:"Symptoms can sometimes be prevented or reduced by avoiding the allergens that trigger them. During pollen season, people with hay fever may benefit from staying indoors when pollen levels are high, keeping windows closed and using air conditioning when possible. Reducing exposure to known household allergens can also help. Identifying triggers through allergy testing may make avoidance strategies more effective. People with persistent symptoms should discuss appropriate preventive treatment with a healthcare provider.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:283:"ज्ञात एलर्जनों से बचाव और स्वच्छ वातावरण बनाए रखना एलर्जिक राइनाइटिस के लक्षणों को कम करने में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:282:"Allergic rhinitis is usually not an emergency. Seek emergency care for severe difficulty breathing, throat or tongue swelling, fainting, or other signs of a serious allergic reaction. Prompt medical assessment is also appropriate when symptoms are severe or significantly worsening.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:370;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:383;s:10:"disease_id";i:36;s:11:"overview_en";s:453:"Nasal polyps are soft, sac-like growths that develop on the lining of the nose or sinuses. They are usually noncancerous and are associated with long-term inflammation of the nasal and sinus tissues. Small polyps may cause no symptoms, while larger growths can block the nasal passages and contribute to congestion, runny nose, reduced sense of smell, reduced sense of taste, snoring and recurrent sinus problems. Polyps can return even after treatment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:233:"नासल पॉलिप्स नाक या साइनस की परत पर बनने वाली नरम, दर्दरहित और गैर-कैंसरयुक्त वृद्धि हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:432:"The exact reason some people develop nasal polyps is not known. They appear to be associated with long-term inflammation of the nose and sinuses. Conditions linked with increased likelihood include allergies, asthma, chronic sinus infections, aspirin sensitivity, cystic fibrosis and hay fever. The inflammation causes swelling of the nasal lining, and persistent inflammation may contribute to the development and growth of polyps.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:289:"एलर्जी, अस्थमा, संक्रमण या प्रतिरक्षा विकारों के कारण होने वाली दीर्घकालिक सूजन पॉलिप्स बनने का कारण बनती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:383:"Risk factors include asthma, chronic sinus infections, allergic rhinitis or hay fever, aspirin sensitivity and cystic fibrosis. Repeated or long-lasting inflammation of the nasal and sinus passages can increase the likelihood of developing polyps. Some people are more prone to recurrent polyps after treatment, particularly when the underlying inflammatory condition remains active.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:203:"अस्थमा, पुरानी साइनसाइटिस, एलर्जी और एस्पिरिन संवेदनशीलता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:502:"Nasal polyps are diagnosed by examining the nose and reviewing symptoms such as persistent congestion, runny nose and reduced smell. An ear, nose and throat specialist may use a nasal endoscope to examine areas that cannot be seen easily during a routine examination. CT scanning of the sinuses may help determine the size and location of polyps and identify associated sinus disease. The appearance of a polyp and the clinical history generally help distinguish it from other causes of nasal blockage.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:200:"निदान में नाक की जांच, एंडोस्कोपी, एलर्जी परीक्षण और इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:466:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent nasal polyps. Managing allergies, asthma and chronic sinus inflammation may help reduce nasal inflammation and the likelihood of recurrent blockage. Medicines such as nasal steroid sprays or antihistamines may be recommended to control inflammation in appropriate patients. Treating sinus infections promptly may also help. People who have recurrent polyps may require ongoing medical follow-up to reduce the chance of regrowth.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:219:"एलर्जी और दीर्घकालिक सूजन को नियंत्रित करना नासल पॉलिप्स के जोखिम को कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:271:"Nasal polyps usually do not require emergency care. Seek prompt medical assessment for significant or rapidly worsening difficulty breathing through the nose, persistent heavy bleeding, severe facial pain or swelling, vision changes, or other rapidly developing symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:371;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:384;s:10:"disease_id";i:37;s:11:"overview_en";s:385:"A deviated septum occurs when the nasal septum, the wall of bone and cartilage separating the two sides of the nose, is shifted away from the center. A mild deviation may cause no symptoms, while a more pronounced deviation can narrow one nasal passage and make breathing difficult. It may contribute to mouth breathing, snoring, recurrent nasal problems, or repeated sinus infections.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:348:"डेविएटेड सेप्टम तब होता है जब नाक के दोनों हिस्सों को विभाजित करने वाली दीवार टेढ़ी हो जाती है, जिससे सांस लेने में कठिनाई हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:341:"A deviated nasal septum may be present from birth or may develop after an injury to the nose. Trauma can bend or displace the bone and cartilage that form the septum. Normal growth of the facial structures can also contribute to deviation. In some people, the septum becomes increasingly uneven over time without a clearly identified injury.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:166:"जन्मजात असामान्यताएं और नाक की चोट इसके सबसे सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:385:"Risk of a deviated septum is increased by injuries to the nose, including injuries from falls, sports, accidents, or other trauma. A septal deviation may also be present from birth or become more noticeable as the nose and facial structures develop. People with significant deviation may be more likely to experience nasal obstruction or problems associated with reduced nasal airflow.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:169:"जन्मजात दोष, चेहरे की चोट और पूर्व नाक की चोटें जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:366:"A deviated septum is usually diagnosed by examining the nose and asking about symptoms such as difficulty breathing through the nose, congestion, nosebleeds, or recurrent sinus problems. The inside of the nose may be examined directly or with nasal endoscopy. Imaging may sometimes be used when additional information about the nasal structures or sinuses is needed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:183:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण और नाक की एंडोस्कोपी के माध्यम से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:419:"A deviated septum present from birth or caused by normal development cannot usually be prevented. Preventing nasal injuries can reduce the chance of developing a traumatic deviation. Wearing appropriate protective equipment during contact sports and activities with a risk of facial injury can help protect the nose. Persistent nasal blockage or repeated nasal problems should be evaluated by a healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:221:"चेहरे को चोट से बचाना और खेलों के दौरान सुरक्षा उपकरणों का उपयोग जोखिम कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:296:"A deviated septum usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt assessment for significant difficulty breathing, persistent or heavy nosebleeds, severe facial pain or swelling, or symptoms following a significant nasal injury. Sudden major changes in breathing should be assessed promptly.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:372;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:385;s:10:"disease_id";i:38;s:11:"overview_en";s:461:"Epistaxis, commonly called a nosebleed, occurs when blood vessels inside the nose break and bleed. Most nosebleeds start in the front part of the nasal septum, where many small blood vessels are close to the surface. Dry air, nose picking, irritation, injury, allergies, infections, or forceful nose blowing can trigger bleeding. Most episodes are minor and stop with simple first aid, but heavy, recurrent, or prolonged bleeding may require medical evaluation.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:256:"एपिस्टैक्सिस या नकसीर तब होती है जब नाक के भीतर की रक्त वाहिकाएं फट जाती हैं और रक्तस्राव होता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:444:"Common causes of epistaxis include dry or irritated nasal passages, nose picking, forceful nose blowing, minor injury, respiratory infections, allergies, and exposure to dry or heated air. Nasal sprays and medicines that affect blood clotting can also increase bleeding. Less commonly, repeated nosebleeds may be associated with structural problems in the nose, bleeding disorders, uncontrolled high blood pressure, or other medical conditions.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:264:"शुष्क हवा, चोट, संक्रमण, एलर्जी, उच्च रक्तचाप और रक्त के थक्के बनने की समस्याएं इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:404:"Risk factors for epistaxis include dry weather or indoor heating, frequent nose picking or rubbing, allergies, colds and other nasal infections, nasal trauma, and regular use of certain nasal sprays. Medicines that reduce blood clotting can make bleeding more likely or prolonged. Children and older adults may be particularly prone to nosebleeds because of differences in nasal tissue and blood vessels.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:226:"शुष्क जलवायु, नाक कुरेदना, रक्त पतला करने वाली दवाएं और उच्च रक्तचाप जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:440:"Epistaxis is usually diagnosed from the history of the bleeding and an examination of the nose. A clinician may look for the bleeding site, irritation, injury, inflammation, or an abnormal blood vessel. If nosebleeds are frequent, severe, prolonged, or associated with easy bruising or other bleeding, blood tests may be used to check blood counts and clotting. Further nasal examination may be needed for recurrent or unexplained bleeding.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:178:"निदान शारीरिक परीक्षण और मूल कारणों की जांच के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:434:"Nosebleeds can often be reduced by keeping the inside of the nose moist, especially during dry weather. Saline nasal spray or a suitable nasal moisturizer may help. Avoid picking or rubbing the nose and blow the nose gently. Managing allergies and nasal irritation can also reduce episodes. People taking medicines that affect clotting should use them only as directed and discuss repeated bleeding with their healthcare professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:178:"नाक को नम बनाए रखना और चोट से बचाव नकसीर की रोकथाम में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:301:"Seek emergency medical care for heavy nosebleeding that does not stop with appropriate first aid, bleeding that is causing weakness or fainting, significant blood loss, difficulty breathing, or bleeding after a serious injury. People taking blood-thinning medicines may need prompt medical assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:373;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:386;s:10:"disease_id";i:39;s:11:"overview_en";s:408:"The common cold is a mild infection of the upper respiratory tract, usually caused by viruses. It commonly produces a runny or blocked nose, sneezing, sore throat, cough, and mild tiredness. Symptoms generally develop gradually and improve within several days to about one or two weeks. Many different viruses can cause colds, so having one cold does not provide lasting protection against future infections.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:348:"सामान्य सर्दी एक हल्का वायरल संक्रमण है जो नाक और गले को प्रभावित करता है तथा छींक, नाक बंद होना, गले में खराश और खांसी का कारण बनता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:391:"The common cold is caused by viruses that infect the nose and throat. Rhinoviruses are frequent causes, but several other respiratory viruses can produce similar symptoms. The viruses spread through respiratory droplets, close personal contact, and by touching contaminated surfaces and then touching the nose, mouth, or eyes. Transmission is easier when people are in close contact indoors.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:169:"राइनोवायरस और अन्य श्वसन वायरस सामान्य सर्दी के मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:406:"Risk factors include close contact with people who have respiratory infections, frequent exposure to crowded indoor environments, and touching the nose, mouth, or eyes with unwashed hands. Children may experience frequent colds because they encounter many viruses while developing immunity. Seasonal changes and spending more time indoors can also increase opportunities for respiratory virus transmission.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:242:"संक्रमित व्यक्तियों के संपर्क में आना, खराब स्वच्छता और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:429:"A common cold is usually diagnosed from the symptoms and a physical examination. Typical features include nasal congestion or discharge, sneezing, sore throat, cough, and mild systemic symptoms. Laboratory testing is generally unnecessary for an uncomplicated cold. Testing may be considered when symptoms are unusual, severe, prolonged, or when another respiratory infection such as influenza or COVID-19 needs to be considered.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:183:"निदान आमतौर पर लक्षणों और चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:380:"Good hand hygiene can reduce the spread of viruses that cause colds. Wash hands regularly and avoid touching the eyes, nose, and mouth with unwashed hands. Avoid close contact with people who are ill when possible, and cover coughs and sneezes. Cleaning frequently touched surfaces and improving ventilation in shared indoor spaces can also reduce exposure to respiratory viruses.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:282:"बार-बार हाथ धोना, बीमार व्यक्तियों से दूरी बनाए रखना और प्रतिरक्षा मजबूत रखना सर्दी से बचाव में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:263:"A common cold usually does not require urgent medical care. Seek prompt assessment for difficulty breathing, chest pain, confusion, severe dehydration, persistent high fever, severe worsening symptoms, or symptoms that improve and then become significantly worse.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:374;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:387;s:10:"disease_id";i:40;s:11:"overview_en";s:374:"Hay fever, also called pollen allergy or seasonal allergic rhinitis, occurs when the immune system reacts to airborne allergens such as pollen. It commonly causes sneezing, a runny or blocked nose, itching of the eyes, nose or throat, watery eyes, coughing, and postnasal drainage. Symptoms may occur during seasons when trees, grasses, or weeds release pollen into the air.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:285:"हे फीवर या मौसमी एलर्जिक राइनाइटिस एक एलर्जी स्थिति है जो परागकण जैसे वायुजनित एलर्जनों से उत्पन्न होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:409:"Hay fever is caused by an allergic reaction to pollen and other airborne allergens. When a susceptible person breathes in an allergen, the immune system releases chemicals that produce inflammation and allergy symptoms. Common triggers include pollen from trees, grasses, and weeds. Mold, dust, and animal dander can also cause allergic rhinitis, although pollen is the typical trigger for seasonal hay fever.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:185:"परागकण, फफूंदी के बीजाणु और अन्य मौसमी एलर्जन हे फीवर का कारण बनते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:384:"The likelihood of hay fever is higher in people who have allergies or a family history of allergic conditions. Repeated exposure to pollen and other environmental allergens can trigger symptoms. Seasonal pollen levels, geographic location, and outdoor exposure influence when symptoms occur. People with other allergic diseases may also be more likely to experience allergic rhinitis.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:211:"एलर्जी का पारिवारिक इतिहास और मौसमी एलर्जनों का बार-बार संपर्क जोखिम बढ़ाता है।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:382:"Hay fever is usually diagnosed from the pattern of symptoms, their seasonal timing, and a physical examination. The healthcare provider may examine the nose, eyes, throat, and other areas affected by allergies. When the specific allergen is unclear or symptoms are difficult to control, allergy testing may be performed using skin tests or blood tests to identify relevant triggers.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:187:"निदान लक्षणों, एलर्जी इतिहास और एलर्जी परीक्षण के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:402:"Hay fever symptoms can be reduced by limiting exposure to pollen and other known allergens. During periods of high pollen, keeping windows closed, reducing outdoor exposure, and changing clothes after spending time outside may help. Showering can remove pollen from the skin and hair. Saline nasal rinsing may also help clear allergens, but sterile, distilled, or properly treated water should be used.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:200:"परागकण स्तर की निगरानी और एलर्जनों से बचाव लक्षणों को रोकने में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:301:"Hay fever usually does not require emergency care. Seek emergency medical attention for severe difficulty breathing, throat or tongue swelling, fainting, or other signs of a serious allergic reaction. Seek medical assessment if symptoms become unusually severe or are not responding to usual measures.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:375;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:388;s:10:"disease_id";i:41;s:11:"overview_en";s:403:"Chronic rhinosinusitis is long-lasting inflammation of the nose and sinuses that persists for weeks or months and may repeatedly return. Common symptoms include nasal blockage, facial pressure or pain, reduced sense of smell, nasal discharge, postnasal drainage, and cough. Nasal polyps, allergies, infection, structural problems, and other inflammatory conditions can contribute to persistent symptoms.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:315:"क्रॉनिक राइनोसाइनुसाइटिस नाक और साइनस की दीर्घकालिक सूजन है जो उपचार के बावजूद 12 सप्ताह या उससे अधिक समय तक बनी रहती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:414:"Chronic rhinosinusitis involves ongoing inflammation of the lining of the nose and sinuses. It may be associated with nasal polyps, allergies, repeated infections, impaired sinus drainage, or structural narrowing of the nasal passages. Asthma and other inflammatory conditions can occur alongside chronic sinus disease. In some people, the exact combination of factors causing persistent inflammation is not clear.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:258:"एलर्जी, संक्रमण, नासल पॉलिप्स या प्रतिरक्षा विकारों के कारण लगातार सूजन इस स्थिति का कारण बनती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:391:"Risk factors include nasal polyps, allergies, asthma, repeated respiratory infections, structural abnormalities of the nose or sinuses, exposure to cigarette smoke and other irritants, and certain inflammatory disorders. Problems with normal sinus drainage can promote persistent inflammation. Some people have a greater susceptibility because of underlying immune or respiratory conditions.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:203:"अस्थमा, एलर्जी, धूम्रपान, नासल पॉलिप्स और प्रतिरक्षा की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:434:"Diagnosis is based on persistent nasal and sinus symptoms together with examination of the nose and surrounding structures. Nasal endoscopy may allow direct examination of the nasal passages and sinus openings. CT imaging of the sinuses may be used when symptoms persist, complications are suspected, or surgery is being considered. Allergy testing or other investigations may be appropriate when an underlying condition is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:199:"निदान में नाक की एंडोस्कोपी, इमेजिंग जांच और लक्षणों का मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:493:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent chronic rhinosinusitis, but controlling contributing conditions may reduce symptoms and recurrence. Managing allergies and asthma, avoiding cigarette smoke and other nasal irritants, practicing good hand hygiene, and treating respiratory infections appropriately can help. Adequate hydration and following prescribed nasal treatments may support normal nasal and sinus function. Persistent symptoms should be evaluated rather than repeatedly self-treated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:317:"एलर्जी का प्रबंधन, धूम्रपान से बचाव और नाक के संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार क्रॉनिक राइनोसाइनुसाइटिस के जोखिम को कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:271:"Seek prompt medical assessment for severe or rapidly worsening headache, swelling or redness around the eyes, vision changes, confusion, stiff neck, severe facial swelling, or other rapidly worsening symptoms. These may indicate a complication requiring urgent treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:376;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:389;s:10:"disease_id";i:42;s:11:"overview_en";s:359:"Dental caries, commonly called tooth decay or cavities, is damage to the hard tissues of a tooth caused by acids produced when bacteria in dental plaque break down sugars and starches. Over time, repeated acid exposure can weaken enamel and create a cavity. Untreated decay may progress into deeper layers of the tooth, causing pain, infection, or tooth loss.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:375:"डेंटल कैरीज़ या दांतों में कीड़ा लगना एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें मुंह के बैक्टीरिया द्वारा उत्पन्न अम्ल दांतों की संरचना को नुकसान पहुंचाते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:402:"Dental caries develops when plaque bacteria use sugars and other fermentable carbohydrates from food and drinks to produce acids. Frequent consumption of sugary or starchy foods and drinks increases acid exposure. Poor oral hygiene allows plaque to remain on the teeth. Reduced saliva, inadequate fluoride exposure, and certain medicines or medical conditions can also increase the risk of tooth decay.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:268:"खराब मौखिक स्वच्छता, मीठे खाद्य पदार्थ, बैक्टीरियल प्लाक और बार-बार खाने की आदत इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:406:"Risk factors include frequent sugary snacks or drinks, poor brushing and flossing habits, inadequate fluoride exposure, dry mouth, previous cavities, and difficulty maintaining oral hygiene. Children and older adults may have increased risk for different reasons. Certain medicines can reduce saliva, while exposed tooth roots, dental appliances, and deep grooves in teeth can make cleaning more difficult.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:247:"अधिक चीनी का सेवन, दांतों की अपर्याप्त सफाई, मुंह का सूखना और फ्लोराइड की कमी जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:387:"Dental caries is diagnosed by a dentist through examination of the teeth and gums. The dentist may look for visible cavities, discoloration, softened enamel, or areas where plaque accumulates. Dental instruments can help identify weakened areas. X-rays may be used when decay is suspected between teeth or beneath existing restorations and cannot be fully assessed by visual examination.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:201:"निदान दंत परीक्षण, दृश्य निरीक्षण और डेंटल एक्स-रे के माध्यम से किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:403:"Dental caries can often be prevented by brushing teeth twice daily with fluoride toothpaste and cleaning between the teeth regularly. Limit frequent consumption of sugary foods and drinks, particularly between meals. Fluoride from toothpaste, drinking water, or professionally applied products helps strengthen enamel. Regular dental examinations allow early detection and treatment of developing decay.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:313:"नियमित ब्रशिंग, फ्लॉसिंग, फ्लोराइड का उपयोग और मीठे खाद्य पदार्थों को सीमित करना डेंटल कैरीज़ को रोकने में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:278:"Seek urgent dental or medical care for severe tooth or facial pain with swelling, fever, difficulty swallowing or breathing, rapidly spreading facial swelling, or swelling around the eye or neck. These symptoms may indicate a serious dental infection requiring prompt treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:06:31";}i:377;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:390;s:10:"disease_id";i:43;s:11:"overview_en";s:428:"Gingivitis is inflammation of the gums, usually causing redness, swelling, tenderness, and bleeding during brushing or flossing. It is an early form of gum disease and commonly develops when plaque, a sticky film of bacteria, accumulates along the gumline. Gingivitis is generally reversible with appropriate oral hygiene and professional dental care, but untreated inflammation can progress to more serious periodontal disease.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:257:"जिंजिवाइटिस मसूड़ों की बीमारी का प्रारंभिक रूप है जिसमें मसूड़ों में सूजन, लालिमा और जलन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:442:"The most common cause of gingivitis is buildup of dental plaque along the teeth and gumline. Plaque contains bacteria that can irritate and inflame gum tissue. If plaque is not removed regularly, it can harden into tartar, which is more difficult to remove with routine brushing. Hormonal changes, certain medicines, smoking, poor nutrition, some infections, and conditions that affect immune function can also contribute to gum inflammation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:571:"जिंजिवाइटिस मुख्यतः दांतों की सतह और मसूड़ों की रेखा पर जमा होने वाले प्लाक के कारण होता है, जिससे सूजन शुरू होती है। खराब मौखिक स्वच्छता, धूम्रपान, हार्मोनल परिवर्तन, कुछ दवाएं और कुछ रोग मसूड़ों की सूजन बढ़ा सकते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:434:"Risk increases with inadequate brushing or flossing, plaque and tartar buildup, smoking or tobacco use, dry mouth, and certain medications. Hormonal changes during puberty, menstruation, pregnancy, or menopause may make gums more sensitive. Diabetes and some immune-system disorders can increase susceptibility. Poor nutrition, crowded teeth, ill-fitting dental appliances, and difficulty maintaining oral hygiene can also contribute.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:231:"धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, खराब मौखिक स्वच्छता, हार्मोनल परिवर्तन और कुछ दवाएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:463:"Gingivitis is usually diagnosed during a dental examination. A dentist or dental professional examines the gums for redness, swelling, bleeding, tenderness, and plaque or tartar buildup. The depth of spaces around the teeth may be measured to determine whether periodontal disease is present. Dental X-rays may be used when deeper gum disease or bone loss is suspected. The examination also helps identify contributing factors and determine appropriate treatment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:614:"निदान सामान्यतः दंत परीक्षण के दौरान किया जाता है। दंत चिकित्सक मसूड़ों में लालिमा, सूजन, दर्द, रक्तस्राव और प्लाक के जमाव की जांच करते हैं तथा आवश्यकता होने पर मसूड़ों की जेब और अन्य पीरियोडॉन्टल रोग के संकेतों का मूल्यांकन करते हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:483:"Good oral hygiene is the main way to prevent gingivitis. Brush the teeth regularly with fluoride toothpaste and clean between the teeth with floss or another appropriate interdental cleaner. Regular dental examinations and professional cleanings help remove plaque and tartar that routine brushing cannot eliminate. Avoiding tobacco, managing conditions such as diabetes, maintaining a balanced diet, and seeking dental care when gums bleed or remain swollen can further reduce risk.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:253:"अच्छी मौखिक स्वच्छता, नियमित दंत सफाई और धूम्रपान छोड़ना जिंजिवाइटिस की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:249:"Gingivitis usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt dental assessment for severe or persistent gum swelling, significant bleeding, severe pain, pus or drainage, fever, facial swelling, or symptoms that are rapidly worsening or spreading.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:378;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:391;s:10:"disease_id";i:44;s:11:"overview_en";s:384:"Periodontitis is a serious form of gum disease in which inflammation and infection damage the tissues and bone that support the teeth. It usually develops from untreated gingivitis and long-term buildup of bacterial plaque and tartar. As the supporting tissues are damaged, gums may pull away from the teeth and pockets can form. Advanced disease can cause loose teeth and tooth loss.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:377:"पीरियोडोंटाइटिस मसूड़ों का गंभीर संक्रमण है जो दांतों को सहारा देने वाली हड्डी और ऊतकों को नुकसान पहुंचाता है और दांत गिरने का कारण बन सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:379:"Periodontitis usually develops when bacterial plaque accumulates around the teeth and causes persistent inflammation of the gums. If plaque is not removed, it can harden into tartar and contribute to deeper infection. Smoking, certain medical conditions, hormonal changes, some medicines, and genetic susceptibility can increase the likelihood or severity of periodontal disease.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:199:"अनुपचारित जिंजिवाइटिस और लंबे समय तक प्लाक का जमा रहना इसके मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:419:"Risk factors include inadequate oral hygiene, smoking or tobacco use, diabetes, a family history of gum disease, increasing age, hormonal changes, stress, and some medicines that affect the gums or saliva. Previous gingivitis and difficulty cleaning around crowded teeth, dental appliances, or restorations can also increase risk. Regular dental care helps identify periodontal disease before significant damage occurs.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:240:"धूम्रपान, मधुमेह, खराब मौखिक स्वच्छता, आनुवंशिक कारक और प्रतिरक्षा विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:374:"Periodontitis is diagnosed through a dental examination of the gums and supporting tissues. A dentist may measure the depth of spaces between the gums and teeth, check for bleeding, gum recession, tooth mobility, and plaque or tartar. Dental X-rays may be used to assess bone loss around the teeth. The findings help determine the extent and severity of periodontal disease.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:176:"निदान में दंत परीक्षण, पीरियोडोंटल जांच और डेंटल इमेजिंग शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:398:"Good oral hygiene is the main way to reduce the risk of periodontitis. Brush teeth twice daily with fluoride toothpaste and clean between the teeth every day. Professional dental examinations and cleanings help remove tartar that cannot be removed by brushing alone. Avoiding tobacco, controlling diabetes, and seeking care for persistent gum bleeding or swelling can also help prevent progression.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:294:"उचित मौखिक स्वच्छता, नियमित दंत देखभाल और अन्य बीमारियों का नियंत्रण पीरियोडोंटाइटिस को रोकने में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:237:"Seek prompt dental assessment for rapidly worsening gum swelling or pain, pus around the teeth, loose teeth, significant bleeding, fever, or facial swelling. Emergency care is needed if swelling causes difficulty breathing or swallowing.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:379;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:392;s:10:"disease_id";i:45;s:11:"overview_en";s:417:"A tooth abscess is a collection of pus caused by a bacterial infection in or around a tooth. It can develop when untreated tooth decay, a cracked tooth, or damage to the tooth allows bacteria to reach the inner tissues. An abscess may cause severe toothache, sensitivity, swelling, fever, or a bad taste in the mouth. Dental treatment is needed because an abscess does not usually resolve without treating its source.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:304:"टूथ एब्सेस दांत या उसके आसपास होने वाला बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण है जिसमें मवाद भर जाती है और गंभीर दर्द तथा सूजन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:329:"A tooth abscess most commonly results from bacteria entering the inner part of a tooth through untreated decay, cracks, fractures, or other damage. The infection can spread from the pulp through the root into surrounding tissues and form an abscess. Gum disease can also cause an abscess around the supporting tissues of a tooth.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:221:"अनुपचारित दांतों की सड़न, मसूड़ों की बीमारी और दांत की चोट एब्सेस का कारण बन सकती है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:357:"Risk factors include untreated cavities, poor oral hygiene, gum disease, frequent consumption of sugary foods and drinks, dry mouth, and previous dental injury. Delayed dental treatment can allow a small infection to become more extensive. People with weakened immune defenses may also have a greater risk of developing complications from dental infections.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:219:"खराब मौखिक स्वच्छता, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा और अनुपचारित दंत समस्याएं जोखिम बढ़ाती हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:392:"A tooth abscess is diagnosed through dental examination and assessment of symptoms such as tooth pain, swelling, tenderness, and sensitivity. The dentist may gently examine the affected tooth and surrounding tissues. Dental X-rays can help identify infection around the root or bone and determine how far the infection has spread. Additional tests may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:210:"निदान दंत परीक्षण, इमेजिंग जांच और लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:393:"Preventing tooth decay and gum disease reduces the risk of tooth abscesses. Brush twice daily with fluoride toothpaste, clean between the teeth, and limit frequent sugary foods and drinks. Regular dental examinations allow cavities and damaged teeth to be treated before infection develops. Seek prompt dental care for persistent toothache, swelling, broken teeth, or other signs of infection.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:240:"दांतों की सड़न का समय पर उपचार और अच्छी मौखिक स्वच्छता टूथ एब्सेस की रोकथाम में मदद करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:310:"A tooth abscess can spread beyond the tooth and requires prompt dental treatment. Seek urgent care for severe tooth pain with swelling, fever, pus, difficulty opening the mouth, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for difficulty breathing or swallowing or rapidly spreading facial or neck swelling.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:380;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:393;s:10:"disease_id";i:46;s:11:"overview_en";s:357:"Oral thrush is a fungal infection of the mouth caused by an overgrowth of Candida yeast. It can produce creamy white patches on the tongue, inner cheeks, gums, palate, or throat. The affected areas may be sore or may bleed slightly when the patches are removed. Some people experience a burning sensation, altered taste, or difficulty eating and swallowing.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:321:"ओरल थ्रश मुंह का फंगल संक्रमण है जो कैंडिडा यीस्ट की अत्यधिक वृद्धि के कारण होता है और सफेद धब्बे तथा असुविधा पैदा करता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:391:"Oral thrush develops when Candida yeast grows excessively in the mouth. Normally, small amounts of Candida can live in the mouth without causing illness, but changes in the local environment or immune defenses can allow overgrowth. Antibiotic use can alter normal mouth bacteria, while inhaled corticosteroids, dentures, dry mouth, diabetes, and weakened immune function can also contribute.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:317:"प्रतिरक्षा में कमी, एंटीबायोटिक उपयोग या खराब मौखिक स्वच्छता के कारण कैंडिडा फंगस की अत्यधिक वृद्धि इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:363:"Risk factors include recent antibiotic use, use of inhaled corticosteroids, diabetes, dry mouth, wearing dentures, poor oral hygiene, smoking, and weakened immune function. Infants and older adults may be more susceptible. Conditions or treatments that reduce the body’s ability to control Candida can make oral thrush more likely or cause recurrent infections.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:257:"मधुमेह, कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा, नकली दांतों का उपयोग और लंबे समय तक एंटीबायोटिक उपचार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:397:"Oral thrush is usually diagnosed by examining the mouth and identifying characteristic white patches and areas of inflammation. A healthcare professional may gently examine or remove a patch to assess the underlying tissue. Laboratory testing is not always necessary, but a sample may be examined when the diagnosis is uncertain, the infection is recurrent, or treatment does not work as expected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:222:"निदान मुंह की जांच और आवश्यकता होने पर प्रयोगशाला परीक्षणों के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:416:"Oral thrush risk can be reduced through good oral hygiene, regular dental care, and appropriate cleaning of dentures. People using inhaled corticosteroids should follow instructions for rinsing the mouth after use. Avoiding unnecessary antibiotics, controlling diabetes, treating dry mouth, and stopping smoking can also help. Persistent or recurrent symptoms should be evaluated to identify contributing conditions.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:276:"मौखिक स्वच्छता बनाए रखना, मधुमेह को नियंत्रित रखना और दवाओं का सही उपयोग ओरल थ्रश से बचाव में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:236:"Oral thrush usually does not require emergency care. Seek medical assessment if symptoms are severe, persistent, recurrent, or associated with difficulty swallowing, significant pain, fever, or signs that the infection may be spreading.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:381;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:394;s:10:"disease_id";i:47;s:11:"overview_en";s:405:"A mouth ulcer is a small, painful sore that develops on the lining of the mouth, including the inside of the lips or cheeks, tongue, gums, or other soft tissues. Many mouth ulcers are minor and heal on their own within one to two weeks. They can be triggered by accidental injury, irritation, stress, illness, or nutritional deficiencies. Persistent or unusual ulcers require dental or medical assessment.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:244:"माउथ अल्सर मुंह के अंदर बनने वाला दर्दनाक घाव है जो खाने और बोलने में परेशानी पैदा कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:411:"Mouth ulcers can result from minor trauma such as biting the cheek, sharp teeth, braces, dentures, or burns from hot food. Other possible triggers include stress, hormonal changes, infections, certain medicines, and nutritional deficiencies. Some people develop recurrent ulcers without an identifiable cause. Persistent or multiple ulcers may sometimes occur with underlying inflammatory or systemic disorders.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:251:"छोटी चोटें, तनाव, पोषण की कमी, संक्रमण और कुछ चिकित्सीय स्थितियां माउथ अल्सर का कारण बन सकती हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:366:"Risk factors include previous mouth ulcers, accidental biting or other oral injury, dental appliances, sharp teeth, emotional stress, hormonal changes, and nutritional deficiencies. Certain medicines and foods may trigger ulcers in susceptible people. Poorly fitting dentures and other sources of repeated irritation can also increase the chance of developing sores.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:205:"तनाव, विटामिन की कमी, हार्मोनल परिवर्तन और प्रतिरक्षा विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:441:"Most mouth ulcers are diagnosed by examining the sore and reviewing the person’s history. A clinician or dentist may assess its size, location, appearance, duration, and recurrence. Testing is generally unnecessary for a typical short-lived ulcer. Blood tests or other investigations may be considered when ulcers are frequent, severe, persistent, associated with other symptoms, or suggest an underlying nutritional or systemic condition.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:218:"निदान आमतौर पर चिकित्सकीय परीक्षण और लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:425:"Some mouth ulcers cannot be completely prevented, but avoiding known triggers may reduce recurrences. Protect the mouth from injury, maintain good oral hygiene, and use care when eating very hot or hard foods. Dental problems and poorly fitting appliances should be corrected. A balanced diet helps prevent nutritional deficiencies. Seek evaluation for ulcers that do not heal within a reasonable period or repeatedly return.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:232:"संतुलित आहार, तनाव प्रबंधन और मुंह की चोट से बचाव माउथ अल्सर की रोकथाम में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:309:"Most mouth ulcers heal without urgent treatment. Seek dental or medical assessment for an ulcer that persists beyond the expected healing period, repeatedly returns, becomes unusually large or painful, bleeds without an obvious cause, or is accompanied by unexplained weight loss or other concerning symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:382;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:395;s:10:"disease_id";i:48;s:11:"overview_en";s:418:"Temporomandibular joint disorder, or TMJ disorder, refers to conditions affecting the jaw joints and the muscles used for chewing. It may cause jaw pain, tenderness, clicking or popping, difficulty opening the mouth, headaches, or discomfort while chewing. Symptoms can be temporary or persistent. Causes are often multifactorial and may include jaw injury, muscle tension, arthritis, or excessive strain on the joint.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:383:"टेम्पोरोमैंडिबुलर जॉइंट (TMJ) विकार जबड़े के जोड़ और आसपास की मांसपेशियों को प्रभावित करता है, जिससे दर्द, क्लिक की आवाज और चबाने में कठिनाई होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:375:"TMJ disorders may be related to injury of the jaw or joint, inflammation, arthritis, muscle tension, or changes in the structures within the joint. Teeth clenching or grinding can place additional strain on the jaw muscles and joints. Stress may contribute to muscle tension and clenching. In many people, several factors contribute rather than one single identifiable cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:237:"जबड़े की चोट, दांत पीसना, गठिया और तनाव के कारण मांसपेशियों में तनाव इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:411:"Risk factors include jaw injury, arthritis, teeth grinding or clenching, prolonged jaw strain, stress, and certain structural problems affecting the jaw joint. Previous TMJ symptoms may increase the chance of recurrence. Some people are more susceptible because of differences in joint structure or muscle function. Persistent symptoms should be assessed rather than assuming that pain is caused only by stress.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:147:"दांत पीसना, तनाव, जबड़े की चोट और गठिया जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:373:"TMJ disorder is diagnosed from symptoms and examination of the jaw, muscles, teeth, and range of movement. A clinician or dentist may listen for clicking or other joint sounds and assess pain, tenderness, and difficulty opening or closing the mouth. Imaging such as X-ray, CT, or MRI may be considered when structural joint problems or other causes need further evaluation.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:224:"निदान में शारीरिक परीक्षण, दंत मूल्यांकन और आवश्यकता पड़ने पर इमेजिंग जांच शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:380:"There is no single way to prevent all TMJ disorders, but reducing excessive strain on the jaw may help. Avoid prolonged chewing of gum or very hard foods when symptoms are present. Managing stress and avoiding unnecessary jaw clenching can reduce muscle strain. Protecting the jaw from injury and seeking dental care for persistent grinding or bite-related problems may also help.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:264:"तनाव प्रबंधन, जबड़े पर अत्यधिक दबाव से बचाव और दांत पीसने का उपचार TMJ विकारों को रोकने में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:293:"Seek prompt medical or dental assessment for severe or rapidly worsening jaw pain, significant difficulty opening or closing the mouth, major swelling, facial weakness, trauma-related symptoms, or inability to eat or drink adequately. Sudden neurological symptoms require emergency assessment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:383;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:396;s:10:"disease_id";i:49;s:11:"overview_en";s:421:"Leukoplakia is a condition in which thickened white patches develop on the lining of the mouth. The patches usually cannot be easily scraped away and may result from chronic irritation. Tobacco use is an important risk factor, although leukoplakia can occur for other reasons. Most patches are not cancer, but some may contain abnormal cells or have a risk of becoming cancerous, so persistent lesions should be examined.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:276:"ल्यूकोप्लाकिया मुंह के अंदर बनने वाले मोटे सफेद धब्बों की स्थिति है जिन्हें आसानी से हटाया नहीं जा सकता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:414:"The exact cause of leukoplakia is not always known. Long-term irritation of the mouth can contribute, particularly from tobacco products, rough teeth, poorly fitting dental appliances, or other sources of repeated injury. Alcohol use may increase risk, especially when combined with tobacco. Certain infections or immune problems can produce similar white patches and may need to be distinguished from leukoplakia.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:205:"तंबाकू का उपयोग, लगातार जलन, शराब का सेवन और कुछ संक्रमण इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:392:"Tobacco smoking and other tobacco use are major risk factors for leukoplakia. Heavy alcohol use may add to the risk, particularly when combined with tobacco. Chronic irritation from rough teeth, dentures, or other dental problems can also contribute. Increasing age and certain immune-related conditions may be associated with a greater likelihood of developing persistent oral white patches.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:209:"धूम्रपान, तंबाकू चबाना, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन और लगातार मौखिक जलन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:415:"Leukoplakia is usually identified by examination of the mouth. A dentist or clinician may inspect the patch and check whether it can be removed by gentle scraping. Persistent or suspicious lesions may require a biopsy to examine the cells under a microscope and determine whether abnormal or precancerous changes are present. Additional evaluation may be needed when another condition could explain the white patch.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:232:"निदान में मुंह की जांच और कैंसर संबंधी परिवर्तनों को बाहर करने के लिए बायोप्सी शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:420:"Avoiding tobacco products is one of the most important ways to reduce the risk of leukoplakia. Limiting excessive alcohol use may also reduce risk. Good oral hygiene and regular dental examinations can help identify persistent irritation or abnormal patches early. Dental problems that repeatedly injure the mouth should be corrected. Any white patch that persists should be assessed by a dental or medical professional.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:254:"तंबाकू और शराब से बचना तथा अच्छी मौखिक स्वच्छता बनाए रखना ल्यूकोप्लाकिया के जोखिम को कम करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:309:"Leukoplakia should be assessed by a dentist or healthcare professional because some lesions can contain precancerous changes. Seek prompt evaluation for a persistent white patch, a lesion that grows or changes, develops pain or bleeding, or is associated with difficulty swallowing or unexplained weight loss.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:384;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:397;s:10:"disease_id";i:50;s:11:"overview_en";s:380:"Oral cancer is a malignant growth that develops in tissues of the mouth. It can affect the lips, tongue, gums, inner cheeks, floor of the mouth, palate, or other oral structures. Depending on its location and stage, it may cause a persistent sore, lump, pain, bleeding, difficulty chewing or swallowing, changes in speech, or a persistent change in the appearance of oral tissues.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:329:"ओरल कैंसर मुंह के ऊतकों में विकसित होने वाला घातक कैंसर है जो होंठ, जीभ, मसूड़ों या अन्य मौखिक संरचनाओं को प्रभावित कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:466:"Tobacco use is a major contributor to oral cancer, particularly when tobacco is smoked or chewed. Excessive alcohol consumption can further increase risk, especially when combined with tobacco use. Infection with certain types of human papillomavirus (HPV) is also associated with some oral cancers. Prolonged sun exposure can increase the risk of cancers affecting the lips. These factors may contribute to cellular changes that eventually lead to malignant growth.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:274:"तंबाकू का उपयोग, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन, HPV संक्रमण और होंठों पर लंबे समय तक धूप का संपर्क इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:467:"Smoking and other forms of tobacco use increase the risk of oral cancer. Heavy alcohol consumption, particularly together with tobacco use, can further increase risk. Certain HPV infections are also associated with oral cancer. Prolonged sun exposure can contribute to cancers of the lips. Poor oral health and inadequate dental care may also be associated with increased risk. Risk varies among individuals depending on the combination and duration of these factors.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:248:"धूम्रपान, तंबाकू चबाना, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन, HPV संक्रमण और खराब मौखिक स्वास्थ्य जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:490:"Diagnosis of oral cancer begins with examination of the mouth, including areas that appear abnormal or have persistent sores, lumps, discoloration, or other changes. A biopsy is generally needed to determine whether abnormal tissue contains cancer cells. Imaging studies may be used to assess the size and location of a tumor and whether it has spread to nearby or distant structures. Additional laboratory tests may be performed as part of the diagnostic evaluation and treatment planning.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:214:"निदान में मौखिक परीक्षण, बायोप्सी, इमेजिंग जांच और प्रयोगशाला परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:475:"Avoiding tobacco products is one of the most important ways to reduce the risk of oral cancer. Limiting excessive alcohol consumption can also lower risk, particularly when combined with avoiding tobacco. Maintaining good oral hygiene and attending regular dental examinations can help identify persistent abnormalities early. Protecting the lips from excessive sun exposure and discussing appropriate prevention measures with healthcare professionals may also be beneficial.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:316:"तंबाकू और अत्यधिक शराब से बचना, मौखिक स्वच्छता बनाए रखना और नियमित दंत जांच ओरल कैंसर के जोखिम को कम करने में मदद करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:306:"Seek prompt medical or dental evaluation for a persistent mouth or tongue ulcer, unexplained bleeding, a growing lump, persistent pain, difficulty swallowing or speaking, unexplained numbness, or a persistent white or red patch. Emergency assessment is needed for severe difficulty breathing or swallowing.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:385;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:398;s:10:"disease_id";i:51;s:11:"overview_en";s:374:"Pharyngitis is inflammation of the throat, often causing a sore or scratchy throat and pain when swallowing. It is commonly caused by viral infections such as those responsible for colds and influenza, although bacteria such as group A Streptococcus can also cause it. Symptoms may include fever, swollen throat tissues, cough, or swollen neck glands depending on the cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:270:"फैरिंजाइटिस गले के पीछे स्थित फैरिंक्स की सूजन है, जिससे गले में खराश, निगलने में कठिनाई और जलन होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:433:"Most cases of pharyngitis are caused by viruses, including common respiratory viruses. Bacterial infections, particularly group A Streptococcus, are another important cause. Irritation from smoking, polluted air, allergies, dry air, or stomach acid reaching the throat can also produce throat inflammation without an infection. Identifying the cause is important because treatment differs between infectious and noninfectious causes.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:220:"वायरल संक्रमण, बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण, एलर्जी और उत्तेजक पदार्थ इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:420:"Risk factors include close contact with people who have respiratory infections, crowded indoor environments, frequent exposure to children, and poor hand hygiene. Tobacco smoke and other environmental irritants can also increase throat irritation. People with frequent exposure to respiratory infections may have repeated episodes. Certain underlying conditions can contribute to recurrent or persistent throat symptoms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:249:"संक्रमित व्यक्तियों के संपर्क में आना, धूम्रपान, एलर्जी और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:401:"Pharyngitis is diagnosed from symptoms and examination of the throat. A clinician may look for redness, swelling, tonsil changes, and swollen lymph nodes and assess for other signs of respiratory infection. When bacterial infection is suspected, a rapid strep test or throat culture may be performed. Testing helps distinguish infections that may benefit from antibiotics from those caused by viruses.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:280:"निदान लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन, गले की जांच और आवश्यकता पड़ने पर प्रयोगशाला परीक्षणों के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:401:"Good hand hygiene and avoiding close contact with people who are sick can reduce the spread of infectious causes of pharyngitis. Cover coughs and sneezes and avoid sharing utensils or drinking containers. Avoiding tobacco smoke and other throat irritants can reduce noninfectious irritation. Prompt evaluation of persistent or severe symptoms can help identify infections requiring specific treatment.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:274:"अच्छी स्वच्छता, धूम्रपान से बचाव और श्वसन संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार फैरिंजाइटिस की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:286:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe difficulty breathing or swallowing, drooling, inability to swallow fluids, rapidly increasing throat or neck swelling, severe dehydration, confusion, or rapidly worsening illness. Persistent or severe symptoms may also require prompt evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:386;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:399;s:10:"disease_id";i:52;s:11:"overview_en";s:386:"Tonsillitis is inflammation of the tonsils, the tissues located at the back of the throat. It is commonly caused by viral infections, although bacteria such as group A Streptococcus can also cause it. Symptoms may include sore throat, painful swallowing, fever, swollen tonsils, and swollen lymph nodes in the neck. Some cases improve without specific treatment, depending on the cause.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:292:"टॉन्सिलाइटिस टॉन्सिल्स की सूजन है, जिससे गले में दर्द, बुखार, टॉन्सिल्स की सूजन और निगलने में कठिनाई हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:388:"Tonsillitis is most often caused by viruses that produce respiratory infections. Bacterial tonsillitis can occur, particularly from group A Streptococcus. The infection spreads through respiratory droplets and close contact with an infected person. Less commonly, other microorganisms may be involved. Determining whether the cause is viral or bacterial helps guide appropriate treatment.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:161:"वायरल और बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण टॉन्सिलाइटिस के मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:392:"Risk factors include close contact with infected people, exposure to crowded environments, and frequent contact with school-age children, who commonly spread respiratory infections. Poor hand hygiene can increase transmission. People who have had tonsillitis previously may experience recurrent episodes. Smoking and exposure to tobacco smoke may also irritate the throat and worsen symptoms.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:203:"बार-बार संक्रमण का संपर्क, बचपन की उम्र और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:385:"Tonsillitis is diagnosed through the symptoms and examination of the throat and tonsils. A clinician may look for enlarged or red tonsils, white patches, fever, and swollen neck lymph nodes. When streptococcal infection is suspected, a rapid strep test or throat culture may be used. Other testing is generally unnecessary unless symptoms are severe, recurrent, prolonged, or atypical.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:232:"निदान में गले की जांच, चिकित्सा इतिहास और आवश्यकता होने पर थ्रोट स्वैब परीक्षण शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:402:"Good hand hygiene helps reduce the spread of infections that cause tonsillitis. Avoid sharing utensils, cups, or personal items with someone who is ill, and cover coughs and sneezes. Avoiding tobacco smoke can reduce throat irritation. People with recurrent tonsillitis should discuss the pattern with a healthcare professional, who can determine whether further evaluation or treatment is appropriate.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:263:"स्वच्छता बनाए रखना और संक्रमित व्यक्तियों से दूरी बनाए रखना टॉन्सिलाइटिस के जोखिम को कम कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:311:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe difficulty breathing or swallowing, drooling, inability to drink, rapidly increasing throat or neck swelling, severe one-sided throat pain, difficulty opening the mouth, or rapidly worsening illness. These symptoms may indicate a complication requiring prompt treatment.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:387;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:400;s:10:"disease_id";i:53;s:11:"overview_en";s:462:"Laryngitis is inflammation and irritation of the larynx, or voice box, and commonly causes hoarseness or temporary loss of the voice. The vocal cords become swollen and do not vibrate normally, changing the sound of the voice. Laryngitis often occurs with an upper respiratory infection and usually improves when the underlying illness resolves. In some cases it can be related to allergies, irritation, reflux, bacterial infection or excessive use of the voice.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:266:"लैरिंजाइटिस स्वरयंत्र (लैरिंक्स) की सूजन है जिससे आवाज बैठना, आवाज खोना और गले में असुविधा हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:518:"The most common form of laryngitis is caused by a viral infection, often occurring with an upper respiratory infection. Other possible causes include bacterial infection, allergies, bronchitis, gastroesophageal reflux disease, throat injury, exposure to irritants or chemicals and overuse or strain of the voice. Smoking and other inhaled irritants can also contribute to persistent inflammation. In children, certain serious infections involving the upper airway can cause swelling and potentially obstruct breathing.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:228:"वायरल संक्रमण, आवाज का अत्यधिक उपयोग, धूम्रपान और एसिड रिफ्लक्स इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:539:"Risk factors include frequent upper respiratory infections, exposure to cigarette smoke or other respiratory irritants, allergies, gastroesophageal reflux, heavy or prolonged use of the voice and exposure to chemicals that irritate the throat. People who use their voices extensively for work may be more likely to develop voice strain. Smoking is particularly important in people with persistent hoarseness because it increases exposure to airway irritants and is associated with conditions that can also cause long-lasting voice changes.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:215:"धूम्रपान, आवाज का अत्यधिक उपयोग, श्वसन संक्रमण और एसिड रिफ्लक्स जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:552:"Laryngitis is usually diagnosed from symptoms and a physical examination, particularly when hoarseness occurs with a respiratory infection. The healthcare provider may examine the throat and ask about recent illness, allergies, reflux, smoking and voice use. Persistent hoarseness, especially when it lasts for several weeks or occurs in a smoker, may require evaluation by an ear, nose and throat specialist. Flexible examination of the throat and upper airway can be used to inspect the vocal cords and identify other causes of persistent hoarseness.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:261:"निदान लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन, गले की जांच और आवश्यकता पड़ने पर लैरिंगोस्कोपी के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:584:"The risk of laryngitis can be reduced by washing the hands regularly and avoiding close contact with people who have upper respiratory infections when possible. Avoiding cigarette smoke and other inhaled irritants can help protect the larynx. People who use their voices heavily should avoid excessive voice strain and allow adequate rest. Managing conditions such as allergies and reflux may also reduce irritation. Stopping smoking is especially important for protecting the voice box and reducing the risk of serious smoking-related conditions that may cause persistent hoarseness.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:263:"धूम्रपान से बचना, आवाज को आराम देना और संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार लैरिंजाइटिस की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:264:"Laryngitis usually does not require emergency care. Seek prompt medical assessment for significant or worsening difficulty breathing or swallowing, coughing up blood, severe throat or neck swelling, persistent voice changes, or symptoms that are rapidly worsening.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:388;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:401;s:10:"disease_id";i:54;s:11:"overview_en";s:358:"Strep throat is an infection of the throat and tonsils caused by group A Streptococcus bacteria. It commonly causes sudden sore throat, pain when swallowing, fever, swollen or tender lymph nodes in the neck, and red or swollen tonsils. Some people develop white patches or pus on the tonsils. Strep throat is more common in children but can occur at any age.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:364:"स्ट्रेप थ्रोट गले का एक बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण है जो स्ट्रेप्टोकोकस बैक्टीरिया के कारण होता है और गंभीर गले के दर्द तथा बुखार का कारण बनता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:369:"Strep throat is caused by group A Streptococcus bacteria. The bacteria spread from person to person through respiratory droplets and contact with infected saliva or nasal secretions. Transmission is more likely during close contact with an infected person. People with strep throat can spread the infection, particularly before effective antibiotic treatment has begun.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:174:"ग्रुप ए स्ट्रेप्टोकोकस बैक्टीरिया का संक्रमण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:375:"Children and adolescents are more likely than adults to develop strep throat. Close contact with an infected person is the main way the infection spreads. Crowded settings such as schools and childcare facilities can increase opportunities for transmission. Having contact with someone who has a group A streptococcal infection also increases the chance of becoming infected.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:236:"संक्रमित व्यक्तियों के निकट संपर्क, स्कूल में रहना और कमजोर प्रतिरक्षा जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:369:"Strep throat is diagnosed using symptoms and an examination of the throat and neck. Because viruses can cause similar symptoms, laboratory testing is often used to confirm group A Streptococcus infection. A rapid strep test can provide results quickly, while a throat culture may be used when needed. Testing helps determine whether antibiotic treatment is appropriate.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:178:"निदान में गले की जांच, रैपिड स्ट्रेप टेस्ट और थ्रोट कल्चर शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:416:"Good hand hygiene and avoiding close contact with people who have strep throat can reduce transmission. Do not share drinking glasses, eating utensils, or other personal items with an infected person. Covering coughs and sneezes and washing hands regularly are important. People diagnosed with strep throat should follow medical advice about treatment and staying home until they are no longer considered contagious.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:263:"हाथों की स्वच्छता और संक्रमित व्यक्तियों से दूरी बनाए रखना स्ट्रेप थ्रोट की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:302:"Seek urgent medical attention for severe difficulty breathing or swallowing, drooling, inability to drink fluids, significant neck swelling, severe dehydration, confusion, or rapidly worsening illness. Prompt assessment is particularly important when symptoms are severe or complications are suspected.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:389;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:402;s:10:"disease_id";i:55;s:11:"overview_en";s:583:"Vocal cord nodules are small, usually noncancerous growths that develop on the vocal cords because of repeated or excessive voice use. They can cause hoarseness, a rough or breathy voice, vocal fatigue, and difficulty speaking for long periods. Nodules are commonly associated with gradual voice changes rather than sudden loss of the voice. Affected people may feel that speaking requires greater effort, and the voice may become rough, weak, or strained. Continuing activities that repeatedly traumatize the vocal cords can prevent healing and may make the nodules more persistent.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:297:"वोकल कॉर्ड नोड्यूल्स स्वर रज्जुओं पर बनने वाली सौम्य गांठें हैं जो लंबे समय तक आवाज के अत्यधिक उपयोग से होती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:658:"Vocal cord nodules are most often caused by repeated or excessive use of the voice. Frequent shouting, prolonged speaking, singing, or speaking loudly can repeatedly irritate and traumatize the vocal cords. Smoking, respiratory irritation, and other factors that strain the voice can also contribute. Vocal cord nodules result from repeated collision and irritation of the vocal cords during forceful or prolonged voice use. Over time, repeated trauma causes localized swelling and tissue changes. Poor voice technique can increase the force of vocal-cord contact, while reflux, allergies, smoking, or respiratory infections may further irritate the tissues.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:198:"बार-बार आवाज पर दबाव, अत्यधिक बोलना, गाना और चिल्लाना इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:557:"Risk is increased by occupations or activities requiring frequent or prolonged speaking, singing, shouting, or loud voice use. Poor vocal technique, smoking, dehydration, and repeated irritation of the throat can further increase stress on the vocal cords. Teachers, singers, performers, public speakers, coaches, call-center workers, and others who use their voices extensively may have greater exposure to repetitive vocal trauma. Children who frequently shout may also develop nodules. Smoking and persistent throat irritation can increase vulnerability.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:218:"पेशेवर रूप से आवाज का उपयोग, धूम्रपान और अनुपचारित एसिड रिफ्लक्स जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:595:"Diagnosis is based on symptoms, voice history, and examination of the vocal cords. A healthcare professional may use laryngoscopy to directly view the vocal cords and identify nodules or other abnormalities. Voice evaluation may also be performed to assess vocal function and technique. Flexible or rigid laryngoscopy allows direct examination of the vocal cords and can identify the location and appearance of nodules. A speech-language pathologist may assess voice quality, breathing, pitch, and vocal technique. Persistent hoarseness should be evaluated to exclude other vocal-cord disorders.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:187:"निदान में लैरिंगोस्कोपी और आवाज की कार्यक्षमता का मूल्यांकन शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:596:"Vocal cord nodules may be prevented by using the voice properly, avoiding unnecessary shouting, taking regular vocal breaks, staying adequately hydrated, and addressing persistent throat irritation. People who rely heavily on their voices may benefit from professional voice training. People who use their voices professionally can reduce risk by learning efficient vocal techniques and avoiding speaking over loud background noise. Adequate hydration, rest during periods of heavy voice use, treatment of persistent throat irritation, and avoiding tobacco smoke can help protect the vocal cords.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:279:"आवाज की उचित देखभाल, पर्याप्त जल सेवन और अत्यधिक आवाज के उपयोग से बचाव नोड्यूल्स की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:270:"Vocal cord nodules usually develop gradually and are not an emergency. Seek prompt assessment for sudden or rapidly worsening voice changes, difficulty breathing or swallowing, coughing up blood, unexplained neck swelling, or persistent hoarseness that does not improve.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:390;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:403;s:10:"disease_id";i:56;s:11:"overview_en";s:355:"Throat cancer is cancer that develops in parts of the throat, including the pharynx, larynx, vocal cords, or nearby tissues. Symptoms can include persistent hoarseness, difficulty or pain with swallowing, a persistent sore throat, cough, a neck lump, or unexplained weight loss. The exact symptoms depend on where the cancer begins and how advanced it is.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:327:"थ्रोट कैंसर गले, स्वरयंत्र या आसपास की संरचनाओं को प्रभावित करने वाला घातक ट्यूमर है जो बोलने और निगलने में बाधा डाल सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:406:"Throat cancer develops when cells in the throat acquire abnormal changes that allow them to grow and divide uncontrollably. Tobacco use is an important cause, and long-term heavy alcohol use also increases risk. Human papillomavirus, particularly HPV-16, is associated with an increasing proportion of some throat cancers. The risk is especially high when tobacco and heavy alcohol exposure occur together.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:285:"तंबाकू का उपयोग, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन, HPV संक्रमण और लंबे समय तक उत्तेजक पदार्थों का संपर्क इसके प्रमुख कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:376:"Risk factors include smoking cigarettes and using other tobacco products, heavy or long-term alcohol consumption, and infection with certain types of human papillomavirus. Risk also increases with age, and throat cancer occurs more often in men than women. A history of prolonged exposure to tobacco and alcohol can substantially increase the likelihood of developing disease.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:217:"धूम्रपान, तंबाकू चबाना, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन, HPV संक्रमण और खराब पोषण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:420:"Diagnosis begins with a medical history and examination of the mouth, throat, neck, and lymph nodes. Persistent symptoms such as hoarseness, swallowing difficulty, or a neck lump may require examination by a specialist. Tests may include visualization of the throat and larynx with specialized instruments, imaging studies, and a biopsy. A biopsy is used to examine abnormal tissue and confirm whether cancer is present.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:198:"निदान में शारीरिक परीक्षण, एंडोस्कोपी, बायोप्सी और इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:465:"The risk of throat cancer can be reduced by avoiding tobacco products and limiting or avoiding heavy alcohol use. Avoiding combined tobacco and heavy alcohol exposure is particularly important because the two factors can increase risk together. Prevention also includes reducing exposure to HPV through appropriate vaccination and safer health practices. Persistent hoarseness, swallowing problems, or other concerning throat symptoms should be medically evaluated.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:318:"तंबाकू और शराब से बचना, मौखिक स्वच्छता बनाए रखना और नियमित स्वास्थ्य जांच थ्रोट कैंसर के जोखिम को कम करने में मदद करती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:285:"Seek prompt medical evaluation for persistent throat pain, difficulty swallowing, a neck lump, persistent hoarseness, unexplained weight loss, coughing up blood, or symptoms that progressively worsen. Emergency care is needed for severe difficulty breathing or an inability to swallow.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:391;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:404;s:10:"disease_id";i:57;s:11:"overview_en";s:399:"A peritonsillar abscess is a collection of infected material in the tissues around a tonsil, usually developing as a complication of tonsillitis. It commonly causes severe throat pain, often worse on one side, along with fever, difficulty swallowing, muffled speech, difficulty opening the mouth, drooling, and swelling. Severe swelling can obstruct the airway and requires urgent medical attention.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:349:"पेरिटॉन्सिलर एब्सेस टॉन्सिल्स के पास बनने वाली मवाद की थैली है जो अक्सर अनुपचारित टॉन्सिलाइटिस की जटिलता के रूप में विकसित होती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:382:"Peritonsillar abscess usually develops when an infection from the tonsils spreads into the surrounding tissues. Group A beta-hemolytic streptococcal bacteria are a common cause. The condition is often associated with untreated or inadequately treated tonsillitis. Once an abscess forms, infected material collects around the tonsil and can spread into nearby tissues if not treated.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:168:"टॉन्सिल्स से फैलने वाला बैक्टीरियल संक्रमण इसका मुख्य कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:366:"A recent or ongoing episode of tonsillitis increases the risk of a peritonsillar abscess. The condition is most common in older children, adolescents, and young adults. Repeated throat infections may also increase risk. Although antibiotics have made the condition less common, infection can still progress when tonsillitis is not appropriately evaluated or treated.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:190:"पुरानी टॉन्सिलाइटिस, धूम्रपान और खराब मौखिक स्वच्छता जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:396:"Diagnosis is usually based on the symptoms and examination of the throat. The healthcare provider may see swelling on one side of the throat and displacement of the uvula away from the affected area. Needle aspiration can help confirm and drain an abscess. CT imaging or fiberoptic endoscopy may be used when the diagnosis is uncertain or when airway obstruction or deeper infection is suspected.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:217:"निदान गले की जांच, इमेजिंग परीक्षण और लक्षणों के मूल्यांकन के आधार पर किया जाता है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:412:"Prompt evaluation and appropriate treatment of tonsillitis, particularly bacterial tonsillitis, may reduce the risk of a peritonsillar abscess. People with severe or worsening throat pain, difficulty swallowing, drooling, voice changes, or swelling should seek medical care promptly. Completing prescribed treatment and following healthcare advice can help prevent an untreated throat infection from progressing.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:277:"गले के संक्रमण का समय पर उपचार और मौखिक स्वच्छता बनाए रखना पेरिटॉन्सिलर एब्सेस की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:302:"A peritonsillar abscess can obstruct the airway and requires urgent medical treatment. Seek emergency care for severe one-sided throat pain and swelling, difficulty swallowing saliva, drooling, muffled or altered voice, difficulty opening the mouth, difficulty breathing, or rapidly worsening symptoms.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:392;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:405;s:10:"disease_id";i:58;s:11:"overview_en";s:360:"Dysphagia means difficulty or discomfort when swallowing food, liquids, or saliva. A person may feel that food is stuck in the throat or chest, cough or choke while eating, or need extra time and effort to swallow. Severe dysphagia can make it difficult to obtain enough food and fluids and may increase the risk of dehydration, poor nutrition, and aspiration.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:354:"डिस्फेजिया भोजन, तरल पदार्थ या लार निगलने में कठिनाई की स्थिति है जो न्यूरोलॉजिकल, मांसपेशीय या संरचनात्मक विकारों के कारण हो सकती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:429:"Dysphagia can result from problems involving the brain, nerves, muscles, throat, or esophagus. Neurologic conditions such as stroke and Parkinson disease can interfere with swallowing. Other causes include gastroesophageal reflux disease, narrowing or other disorders of the esophagus, head or spinal cord injury, and cancers of the head, neck, or esophagus. Anxiety or stress can also contribute to some swallowing difficulties.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:284:"न्यूरोलॉजिकल रोग, गले के विकार, मांसपेशियों की समस्याएं और अन्नप्रणाली की बीमारियां इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:339:"Dysphagia can occur at any age but is more common in older adults. Risk is increased by neurologic disorders, stroke, head or spinal cord injuries, diseases affecting the muscles involved in swallowing, and disorders of the esophagus such as reflux. Cancers affecting the head, neck, or esophagus can also interfere with normal swallowing.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:235:"स्ट्रोक, पार्किंसन रोग, बढ़ती उम्र, गले का कैंसर और न्यूरोमस्कुलर विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:424:"Evaluation of dysphagia begins with a medical history and examination to determine whether the difficulty involves the mouth, throat, or esophagus. Depending on the symptoms, testing may include a swallowing assessment, barium swallow or modified barium swallow study, endoscopy, or other imaging. A speech-language pathologist may evaluate swallowing function and help identify problems with the movement of food or liquid.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:242:"निदान में निगलने की जांच, एंडोस्कोपी, इमेजिंग परीक्षण और न्यूरोलॉजिकल मूल्यांकन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:458:"Dysphagia cannot always be prevented because it may result from conditions such as stroke, neurologic disease, injury, or cancer. Managing underlying diseases and seeking medical attention when swallowing problems persist can reduce complications. People with swallowing difficulties may be advised to modify food texture, eat slowly, use recommended swallowing techniques, and follow guidance from a healthcare professional to reduce choking and aspiration.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:294:"मूल रोगों का समय पर उपचार और नियमित चिकित्सा निगरानी डिस्फेजिया से जुड़ी जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:314:"Seek prompt medical assessment for new or worsening difficulty swallowing, especially when it causes choking, coughing during meals, repeated aspiration, dehydration, or unexplained weight loss. Emergency care is needed for inability to swallow saliva, severe breathing difficulty, or suspected airway obstruction.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:12:39";}i:393;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:406;s:10:"disease_id";i:103;s:11:"overview_en";s:518:"Peptic ulcer disease occurs when an open sore develops in the lining of the stomach or the first part of the small intestine. The most common causes are Helicobacter pylori infection and prolonged use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs. Symptoms may include burning or aching upper abdominal pain, indigestion, nausea, bloating, or early fullness, although some ulcers cause no symptoms until complications occur. Bleeding, perforation, or blockage can occur in severe cases and requires urgent medical attention.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:434:"पेप्टिक अल्सर रोग एक ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें पेट, अन्नप्रणाली के निचले भाग या छोटी आंत के ऊपरी भाग की परत में घाव बन जाते हैं, जिससे दर्द और पाचन संबंधी समस्याएं होती हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:534:"The two major causes of peptic ulcers are Helicobacter pylori infection and prolonged or frequent use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs. H. pylori can damage protective mechanisms in the stomach and duodenum, allowing acid to injure the lining. Medicines such as ibuprofen, naproxen, and aspirin may also reduce protective substances in the digestive tract. Smoking can interfere with healing and increase complications. Excess stomach acid can contribute in some conditions, although acid itself is not the usual primary cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:236:"हेलिकोबैक्टर पाइलोरी संक्रमण और लंबे समय तक NSAID दवाओं का उपयोग इसके सबसे सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:494:"Risk factors for peptic ulcer disease include H. pylori infection and regular use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs. Risk may be higher with increasing age, previous ulcer disease, smoking, heavy alcohol use, and certain medical conditions. Taking several medicines that irritate the digestive tract or combining medicines without medical guidance can increase risk. Some people have no obvious risk factors. A history of ulcer complications increases the importance of medical follow-up.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:227:"H. pylori संक्रमण, धूम्रपान, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन, तनाव और लंबे समय तक NSAID उपयोग जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:529:"Peptic ulcer disease is evaluated using the patient history, symptoms, medication use, and physical examination. Testing for H. pylori may involve a breath test, stool test, or other laboratory methods. Upper gastrointestinal endoscopy can directly examine the stomach and duodenum and may allow tissue sampling or treatment of bleeding. Imaging or other tests may be used in selected cases. Black stools, vomiting blood, severe abdominal pain, fainting, or signs of shock can indicate a complication requiring urgent assessment.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:226:"निदान में चिकित्सा इतिहास, एंडोस्कोपी, H. pylori परीक्षण, रक्त जांच और मल परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:579:"Preventing peptic ulcers involves reducing avoidable risk factors, particularly unnecessary or prolonged use of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs. When these medicines are medically necessary, a healthcare professional can determine whether protective treatment or an alternative is appropriate. H. pylori infection should be tested for and treated when indicated. Avoiding smoking can support healing and reduce complications. People with previous ulcers should follow their treatment plan and seek medical attention promptly if bleeding or severe abdominal symptoms develop.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:323:"अनावश्यक NSAID उपयोग से बचना, धूम्रपान छोड़ना, शराब सीमित करना और H. pylori संक्रमण का उपचार पेप्टिक अल्सर की रोकथाम में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:299:"Seek prompt medical assessment for persistent or worsening abdominal pain, vomiting, unexplained weight loss, or symptoms that may indicate complications. Emergency care is required for vomiting blood, black or bloody stools, severe sudden abdominal pain, fainting, or signs of significant bleeding.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:21:53";}i:394;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:407;s:10:"disease_id";i:109;s:11:"overview_en";s:375:"Hepatitis B is an infection of the liver caused by hepatitis B virus. It can be short-term or become chronic and cause ongoing liver inflammation. Some people have few or no symptoms, while others develop fatigue, nausea, abdominal discomfort, dark urine, jaundice, or loss of appetite. Chronic hepatitis B can cause liver scarring, cirrhosis, liver failure, or liver cancer.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:298:"हेपेटाइटिस बी एक वायरल संक्रमण है जो यकृत को प्रभावित करता है और तीव्र तथा दीर्घकालिक यकृत रोग का कारण बन सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:433:"Hepatitis B is caused by infection with hepatitis B virus. The virus is transmitted through infected blood and certain body fluids, including through sexual contact, sharing contaminated needles or other injection equipment, and from an infected mother to her baby during childbirth. Infection can also occur through exposure to contaminated medical or personal equipment when appropriate infection-control measures are not followed.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:163:"हेपेटाइटिस बी वायरस (HBV) का संक्रमण इस रोग का प्रत्यक्ष कारण है।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:459:"Risk factors include being born to a person with hepatitis B, unprotected sex with an infected person, sharing needles or injection equipment, occupational exposure to infected blood, and living in or frequently traveling to areas where hepatitis B is common. People receiving certain types of medical treatment or dialysis may also have increased exposure risk. Household exposure to infected blood or contaminated personal items can also transmit the virus.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:309:"असुरक्षित यौन संपर्क, संक्रमित सुइयों का उपयोग, संक्रमित रक्त का संपर्क और मां से बच्चे में संक्रमण जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:428:"Hepatitis B is diagnosed with blood tests that detect hepatitis B surface antigen, antibodies, and other markers of infection. Additional blood tests can assess liver inflammation and function. Testing can help determine whether an infection is acute, chronic, or resolved and whether a person has immunity. Imaging or other liver assessments may be recommended when chronic infection has caused or may have caused liver damage.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:248:"निदान में HBV मार्कर रक्त परीक्षण, लिवर फंक्शन टेस्ट और आवश्यकता होने पर इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:457:"Hepatitis B can be prevented effectively through vaccination. Avoiding contact with infected blood and body fluids, not sharing needles or injection equipment, practicing safer sex, and using sterile medical and tattoo equipment reduce transmission risk. Pregnant people should be tested so that appropriate measures can be taken to protect newborns when the mother has hepatitis B. People with known infection should receive appropriate medical monitoring.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:337:"हेपेटाइटिस बी टीकाकरण, सुरक्षित यौन व्यवहार, सुइयों को साझा करने से बचाव और रक्त की उचित जांच संक्रमण की रोकथाम में मदद करते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:323:"Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening jaundice, severe abdominal pain, persistent vomiting, unusual bleeding or bruising, abdominal swelling, confusion, or rapidly worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for vomiting blood, black stools, severe confusion, loss of consciousness, or signs of acute liver failure.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:395;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:408;s:10:"disease_id";i:113;s:11:"overview_en";s:370:"Gallstones are hard deposits that form inside the gallbladder. They may be very small or as large as a golf ball and may consist mainly of cholesterol or pigment containing bilirubin. Many people have gallstones without symptoms. Problems occur when a stone blocks a bile duct, causing abdominal pain and sometimes inflammation, infection, jaundice, nausea, or vomiting.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:332:"गॉलब्लैडर में बनने वाले कठोर जमाव को पित्त पथरी कहा जाता है, जो पित्त के प्रवाह को रोककर दर्द और पाचन समस्याएं पैदा कर सकते हैं।";s:9:"causes_en";s:403:"Gallstones form when substances in bile become unbalanced and crystallize inside the gallbladder. Cholesterol stones are the most common type, while pigment stones can develop when there is too much bilirubin in bile, including in conditions that cause increased breakdown of red blood cells. Poor emptying of the gallbladder and other changes in bile composition can also contribute to stone formation.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:261:"अधिक कोलेस्ट्रॉल, अधिक बिलीरुबिन और गॉलब्लैडर का ठीक से खाली न होना पित्त पथरी के सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:428:"Risk factors include being over age 40, being overweight, having a family history of gallstones, and certain ethnic backgrounds. Other factors include diabetes, pregnancy-related changes in gallbladder emptying, liver cirrhosis, diseases that cause increased destruction of red blood cells, rapid weight loss, very low-calorie diets, weight-loss surgery, long-term intravenous nutrition, and use of some birth control medicines.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:214:"महिला लिंग, मोटापा, तेजी से वजन घटना, मधुमेह और पारिवारिक इतिहास जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:453:"Gallstones are commonly evaluated with abdominal ultrasound, which can detect stones in the gallbladder. Depending on the symptoms and suspected complications, other tests may include CT scanning, endoscopic ultrasound, magnetic resonance cholangiopancreatography, a gallbladder radionuclide scan, or ERCP. Blood tests such as bilirubin, liver function tests, complete blood count, and pancreatic enzyme tests may help identify inflammation or blockage.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:245:"निदान में पेट का अल्ट्रासाउंड, सीटी स्कैन, रक्त परीक्षण और पित्त प्रणाली की इमेजिंग शामिल है।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:442:"Some risk factors for gallstones cannot be changed, but maintaining a healthy weight may lower risk. Avoiding very rapid weight loss and extremely low-calorie diets is important because rapid weight reduction can promote gallstone formation. A balanced eating pattern and regular physical activity can support healthy weight management. People planning major weight-loss treatment should discuss gallstone risk with their healthcare provider.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:281:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखना, संतुलित आहार लेना और तेजी से वजन घटाने से बचना पित्त पथरी की रोकथाम में मदद कर सकता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:314:"Gallstones may cause intermittent symptoms but can also lead to serious complications. Seek prompt medical assessment for persistent or severe upper abdominal pain, fever, jaundice, repeated vomiting, or worsening symptoms. Severe pain with fever, jaundice, or significant deterioration requires urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:27:48";}i:396;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:409;s:10:"disease_id";i:161;s:11:"overview_en";s:453:"Erectile dysfunction is a condition in which a man has persistent difficulty getting or keeping an erection firm enough for sexual activity. Occasional erection problems are common, but ongoing erectile dysfunction can be associated with an underlying medical condition and should not simply be considered a normal part of aging. Erectile function depends on coordinated activity involving the brain, nerves, hormones, blood vessels, and penile tissues.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:334:"इरेक्टाइल डिस्फंक्शन ऐसी स्थिति है जिसमें व्यक्ति संतोषजनक यौन गतिविधि के लिए पर्याप्त इरेक्शन प्राप्त या बनाए नहीं रख पाता।";s:9:"causes_en";s:472:"Erectile dysfunction can result from conditions that interfere with blood flow, nerve function, hormones, or the structures involved in an erection. Diabetes, cardiovascular disease, high blood pressure, nerve disorders, certain medicines, and some injuries can contribute. Psychological factors such as anxiety or relationship stress may also play a role. In some people, several physical and psychological factors occur together rather than there being one single cause.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:267:"रक्त वाहिकाओं के रोग, मधुमेह, हार्मोनल असंतुलन, मनोवैज्ञानिक कारण और कुछ दवाएं इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:491:"Risk increases with age, although erectile dysfunction is not an inevitable consequence of aging. Diabetes, high blood pressure, cardiovascular disease, obesity, smoking, and other conditions that affect blood vessels or nerves can increase risk. Certain medicines, injuries, hormonal disorders, and psychological stress may also contribute. Lifestyle factors that adversely affect cardiovascular health can influence erectile function because normal erections depend on adequate blood flow.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:198:"मधुमेह, उच्च रक्तचाप, धूम्रपान, मोटापा, तनाव और बढ़ती उम्र जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:491:"Diagnosis begins with a medical and sexual history and a physical examination. A healthcare professional may ask about the timing and pattern of erection difficulties, medications, medical conditions, and other symptoms. Depending on the findings, blood tests may evaluate glucose, cholesterol, hormones, or other conditions. Additional tests may be used when a vascular, neurological, or structural cause is suspected. Identifying an underlying condition is an important part of evaluation.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:287:"निदान में चिकित्सा इतिहास, शारीरिक परीक्षण, रक्त जांच, हार्मोन परीक्षण और मनोवैज्ञानिक मूल्यांकन शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:514:"Not every case of erectile dysfunction can be prevented, but maintaining cardiovascular and overall health may reduce risk. Regular physical activity, maintaining a healthy weight, avoiding tobacco, limiting excessive alcohol use, and managing conditions such as diabetes and high blood pressure can support normal blood vessel and nerve function. Reviewing medicines and addressing psychological or relationship factors with a healthcare professional may also be helpful when they contribute to erection problems.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:336:"हृदय स्वास्थ्य बनाए रखना, धूम्रपान से बचना, नियमित व्यायाम करना और पुरानी बीमारियों का प्रबंधन जोखिम को कम करने में मदद करता है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:330:"Erectile dysfunction is generally not an emergency, but persistent symptoms should be medically evaluated because they may be associated with vascular, hormonal, neurological, medication-related, or other health conditions. Seek prompt care for sudden symptoms accompanied by significant pain, injury, or other concerning changes.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:397;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:410;s:10:"disease_id";i:163;s:11:"overview_en";s:513:"Male infertility refers to difficulty achieving a pregnancy because of factors affecting male reproductive function. Problems may involve sperm production, sperm movement or quality, the reproductive tract, hormone regulation, sexual function, or the ability of sperm to reach the egg. Infertility is usually considered when a couple has not achieved pregnancy after a period of regular unprotected intercourse. Male and female factors can occur separately or together, and sometimes no clear cause is identified.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:352:"पुरुष बांझपन वह स्थिति है जिसमें शुक्राणुओं के उत्पादन, कार्य या परिवहन में समस्या के कारण संतान उत्पन्न करने की क्षमता कम हो जाती है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:482:"Male infertility can result from problems involving the testicles, sperm production, sperm transport, hormones, or sexual function. Causes may include genetic disorders, previous infections such as mumps, high fevers, testicular injury, hormonal abnormalities, blockages in the reproductive ducts, and certain medical conditions. Lifestyle and environmental factors can also affect fertility. In some men, testing does not identify a specific cause even though fertility is reduced.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:303:"कम शुक्राणु संख्या, असामान्य शुक्राणु कार्य, हार्मोनल विकार, संक्रमण और आनुवंशिक स्थितियां इसके सामान्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:512:"Risk factors include previous problems affecting the testicles, reproductive tract infections, significant injury, certain genetic or hormonal disorders, and conditions that interfere with sperm production or transport. Exposure to some environmental factors, heat, toxins, or certain medicines may also affect fertility. Smoking, excessive alcohol use, obesity, and other lifestyle factors may contribute. Increasing age can also be associated with gradual changes in sperm production and reproductive function.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:289:"धूम्रपान, अत्यधिक शराब सेवन, मोटापा, विषैले पदार्थों का संपर्क, संक्रमण और हार्मोनल असंतुलन जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:506:"Evaluation of male infertility usually begins with a detailed medical, reproductive, and sexual history and a physical examination. Semen analysis is an important test because it assesses sperm number, movement, and characteristics. Additional tests may include hormone measurements, urine testing, genetic testing, or imaging when indicated. The evaluation is directed toward identifying potentially treatable causes involving sperm production, sperm transport, hormones, or other reproductive structures.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:275:"निदान में वीर्य विश्लेषण, हार्मोन परीक्षण, शारीरिक परीक्षण, आनुवंशिक जांच और इमेजिंग परीक्षण शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:547:"Not all causes of male infertility can be prevented, particularly genetic and some medical causes. However, protecting the testicles from injury, preventing sexually transmitted infections, avoiding tobacco and excessive alcohol use, maintaining a healthy weight, and managing medical conditions may support reproductive health. Avoiding unnecessary exposure to reproductive toxins and discussing potentially fertility-affecting medicines with a healthcare professional may also be appropriate. Early evaluation can help identify treatable causes.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:335:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाना, विषैले पदार्थों से बचना, रोगों का उपचार और समय पर चिकित्सकीय सहायता प्रजनन क्षमता को बेहतर बना सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:368:"Male infertility generally requires planned medical evaluation rather than emergency care. Seek assessment when pregnancy has not occurred after an appropriate period of trying or when there are concerns about sperm production, sexual function, testicular health, or previous reproductive problems. Sudden severe testicular pain or swelling requires urgent evaluation.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:31:18";}i:398;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:411;s:10:"disease_id";i:166;s:11:"overview_en";s:400:"Benign prostatic hyperplasia is a noncancerous enlargement of the prostate gland that becomes more common with aging. An enlarged prostate can press on the urethra and interfere with the normal flow of urine. Symptoms may include difficulty starting urination, a weak or interrupted stream, frequent or urgent urination, nighttime urination, and a feeling that the bladder has not emptied completely.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:424:"बेनाइन प्रोस्टेटिक हाइपरप्लासिया (BPH) प्रोस्टेट ग्रंथि का गैर-कैंसरयुक्त बढ़ना है जो आमतौर पर वृद्ध पुरुषों में होता है और मूत्र संबंधी लक्षण उत्पन्न कर सकता है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:429:"Benign prostatic hyperplasia develops as the prostate changes with age and is influenced by male reproductive hormones. The prostate contains glandular and muscular tissue that can gradually increase in size over time. Although the prostate enlarges, the severity of urinary symptoms does not always correspond directly to its size. The condition is different from prostate cancer and does not itself mean that cancer is present.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:198:"उम्र के साथ होने वाले हार्मोनल परिवर्तन प्रोस्टेट बढ़ने का मुख्य कारण हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:402:"The main risk factor for benign prostatic hyperplasia is increasing age. A family history of the condition may increase susceptibility. Metabolic conditions such as obesity and diabetes have been associated with urinary symptoms and prostate enlargement. Cardiovascular disease and physical inactivity may also be associated with increased risk. Symptoms generally become more common as men grow older.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:195:"बढ़ती उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास, मोटापा और मेटाबोलिक विकार जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:415:"Diagnosis is based on urinary symptoms, medical history, and physical examination, including a digital rectal examination when appropriate. Urinalysis can help exclude infection or other causes of urinary symptoms. Depending on the situation, tests may include prostate-specific antigen measurement, urinary flow testing, measurement of urine remaining after urination, or imaging of the prostate and urinary tract.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:248:"निदान में चिकित्सा इतिहास, प्रोस्टेट परीक्षण, PSA जांच, मूत्र परीक्षण और इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:461:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent benign prostatic hyperplasia because prostate enlargement is strongly related to aging. Maintaining a healthy weight, exercising regularly, managing diabetes and cardiovascular risk factors, and limiting excessive fluid intake before bedtime may help reduce urinary symptoms. People with persistent or worsening urinary symptoms should be evaluated so that other causes can be excluded and appropriate treatment considered.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:268:"स्वस्थ वजन बनाए रखना, नियमित व्यायाम और नियमित स्वास्थ्य जांच जटिलताओं को कम करने में मदद कर सकते हैं।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:417:"Benign prostatic hyperplasia usually develops gradually but can cause urinary retention and other urinary complications. Seek prompt medical assessment for worsening difficulty urinating, blood in the urine, fever or chills with urinary symptoms, significant lower abdominal pain, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed if you cannot urinate at all or develop severe pain or other signs of serious infection.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}i:399;a:15:{s:2:"id";i:412;s:10:"disease_id";i:167;s:11:"overview_en";s:440:"Prostate cancer is a malignant tumor that develops in the prostate gland, a small gland in the male reproductive system. It is one of the most common cancers affecting men. Some prostate cancers grow slowly and may cause few symptoms initially, while others can be more aggressive. Symptoms, when present, may include urinary changes, difficulty urinating, or blood in the urine or semen, although these findings can also have other causes.";s:11:"overview_hi";s:337:"प्रोस्टेट कैंसर प्रोस्टेट ग्रंथि में विकसित होने वाला घातक ट्यूमर है और पुरुषों में पाए जाने वाले सामान्य कैंसरों में से एक है।";s:9:"causes_en";s:434:"Prostate cancer develops when cells in the prostate acquire genetic changes that allow them to grow and multiply abnormally. Aging is associated with an increasing likelihood of these cellular changes. Hormonal influences may contribute to tumor development, and inherited genetic factors can increase susceptibility in some families. The exact combination of factors responsible for an individual case may not always be identifiable.";s:9:"causes_hi";s:300:"आनुवंशिक परिवर्तन, बढ़ती उम्र, हार्मोनल प्रभाव और पारिवारिक इतिहास प्रोस्टेट कैंसर के विकास में योगदान करते हैं।";s:15:"risk_factors_en";s:460:"Older age is an important risk factor for prostate cancer. Having a close family history of prostate cancer can increase risk, particularly when certain inherited genetic changes are present. Some genetic factors may substantially increase susceptibility. Obesity and other health factors have also been associated with prostate cancer risk or with more advanced disease. Individual risk varies, and having a risk factor does not mean that cancer will develop.";s:15:"risk_factors_hi";s:196:"अधिक उम्र, पारिवारिक इतिहास, मोटापा और कुछ आनुवंशिक कारक जोखिम बढ़ाते हैं।";s:12:"diagnosis_en";s:449:"Evaluation for prostate cancer may include a prostate-specific antigen (PSA) blood test and a digital rectal examination. If findings are concerning, imaging such as magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) may be used to assess the prostate. A prostate biopsy is used to obtain tissue for microscopic examination and establish a diagnosis. Additional imaging or laboratory tests may be performed to determine the extent of disease when cancer is confirmed.";s:12:"diagnosis_hi";s:270:"निदान में PSA परीक्षण, डिजिटल रेक्टल परीक्षण, प्रोस्टेट बायोप्सी, एमआरआई और अन्य इमेजिंग जांच शामिल हैं।";s:13:"prevention_en";s:448:"There is no guaranteed way to prevent prostate cancer. Maintaining a healthy weight, eating a balanced diet, staying physically active, and avoiding tobacco can support overall health. Men should discuss prostate cancer risk and appropriate screening with their healthcare professional, particularly when they have a family history or other risk factors. Awareness of urinary or other persistent symptoms can also support timely medical evaluation.";s:13:"prevention_hi";s:340:"स्वस्थ जीवनशैली अपनाना, नियमित जांच और पारिवारिक इतिहास की जानकारी प्रारंभिक पहचान और जटिलताओं को कम करने में सहायता कर सकती है।";s:15:"urgency_note_en";s:378:"Prostate cancer requires medical evaluation and appropriate follow-up. Seek prompt assessment for persistent urinary changes, blood in the urine or semen, unexplained weight loss, persistent bone or back pain, weakness, or worsening symptoms. Emergency care is needed for severe pain, sudden neurological symptoms, inability to urinate, or other signs of a serious complication.";s:15:"urgency_note_hi";N;s:10:"updated_at";s:19:"2026-10-01 02:33:09";}}}s:13:"disease_diets";a:3:{s:3:"ddl";s:587:"CREATE TABLE `disease_diets` (
  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `disease_id` int(11) NOT NULL,
  `diet_type` enum('recommended','avoid') NOT NULL,
  `item_en` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `item_hi` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,
  `notes_en` text DEFAULT NULL,
  `notes_hi` text DEFAULT NULL,
  `sort_order` int(11) DEFAULT 0,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  KEY `idx_diet_disease` (`disease_id`),
  CONSTRAINT `disease_diets_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`disease_id`) REFERENCES `diseases` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=2249 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_general_ci";s:7:"columns";a:8:{i:0;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:2:"id";s:4:"Type";s:7:"int(11)";s:9:"Collation";N;s:4:"Null";s:2:"NO";s:3:"Key";s:3:"PRI";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:14:"auto_increment";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:1;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:10:"disease_id";s:4:"Type";s:7:"int(11)";s:9:"Collation";N;s:4:"Null";s:2:"NO";s:3:"Key";s:3:"MUL";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:2;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:9:"diet_type";s:4:"Type";s:27:"enum('recommended','avoid')";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:2:"NO";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:3;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:7:"item_en";s:4:"Type";s:12:"varchar(255)";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:2:"NO";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:4;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:7:"item_hi";s:4:"Type";s:12:"varchar(255)";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:5;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:8:"notes_en";s:4:"Type";s:4:"text";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:6;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:8:"notes_hi";s:4:"Type";s:4:"text";s:9:"Collation";s:18:"utf8mb4_general_ci";s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";N;s:5:"Extra";s:0:"";s:10:"Privileges";s:31:"select,insert,update,references";s:7:"Comment";s:0:"";}i:7;a:9:{s:5:"Field";s:10:"sort_order";s:4:"Type";s:7:"int(11)";s:9:"Collation";N;s:4:"Null";s:3:"YES";s:3:"Key";s:0